n\nwpt-pr: 61217\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-square-notch-mixed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-square-notch-superellipse.html.ini"], "git_node": "0abe08c125b653ba968b9749a1299d357ddc6d6c", "git_parents": ["9fe96d42792d79b2466956942650a3d36871fbb4"], "node": "ad232bd8dd1585bec6df288061308236ab879e8a", "parents": ["811db5e79b048bb3c8b29620efeff070ae826d9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniil Sakhapov \u003csakhapov@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054932 [wpt PR 61281] - Fix scroll marker updates during Find on Page, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix scroll marker updates during Find on Page\n\nFind on Page (and other targeted scrolls that do not target a scroll\nmarker) failed to update the active scroll marker if it was\npreviously pinned. This occurred because targeted scrolls avoided\nunpinning the scroll marker group.\n\nThis CL centralizes the scroll marker group pin state updates in\nPerformBubblingScrollIntoViewWithResult. When a scroll-into-view\noccurs, we now check if the target element matches any scroll marker's\ntarget. If it does, we pin that marker. If it does not, we unpin the\ngroup, allowing automatic updates to resume.\n\nLegacy, incomplete pinning logic in Element is removed.\n\nTAG=agy\n\nChange-Id: Id761ab0e0cd56bd1e434d83bd98a9932a4734fe6\nBug: 529411428\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8003639\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniil Sakhapov \u003csakhapov@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662136}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1b9c8e03dddb9d9ef3de6f3f008eeb2dcc048cb0\nwpt-pr: 61281\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-markers-nested-scrollers.html"], "git_node": "8368628258aca506cd6d224ebb2494279fe9397f", "git_parents": ["0abe08c125b653ba968b9749a1299d357ddc6d6c"], "node": "b0726f3c231b09bad370791728e1dbd5e4130cee", "parents": ["ad232bd8dd1585bec6df288061308236ab879e8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054932 [wpt PR 61281] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61281\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-marker-in-display-none-column-crash.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-markers/scroll-markers-nested-scrollers.html.ini"], "git_node": "9bd9fe201479ad07567ab93cf3611beb46f5f364", "git_parents": ["8368628258aca506cd6d224ebb2494279fe9397f"], "node": "7f90b7dfa81cf1db56ab33bf0de5d4fa99d2ad8a", "parents": ["b0726f3c231b09bad370791728e1dbd5e4130cee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055231 [wpt PR 61291] - [WebInstallAPI] Rename `id` to `manifestId`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebInstallAPI] Rename `id` to `manifestId`\n\n* Align `InstallParams` dictionary with `\u003cinstall\u003e` element attributes\n* Use `manifestId` instead of `id`\n\nBug: 333795265\nChange-Id: Id5acd954bb0393c0e97899a98c1d0eaa799f727b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8086669\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Luke Deng \u003clukedeng@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dibyajyoti Pal \u003cdibyapal@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Lia Hiscock \u003cliahiscock@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662153}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 08e168922e0c0d42250335a40e679fa5123489df\nwpt-pr: 61291\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-install/navigator-install-bad-inputs.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "ba47ba667ee2d62b3a6563f4dc34d514c098d4a5", "git_parents": ["9bd9fe201479ad07567ab93cf3611beb46f5f364"], "node": "ed01fb1efbf5a76dd9f8229db3122558f0d73df2", "parents": ["7f90b7dfa81cf1db56ab33bf0de5d4fa99d2ad8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055231 [wpt PR 61291] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61291\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/web-install/navigator-install-bad-inputs.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "55ce8245ede8d4e65f4744b9ae05265e30940627", "git_parents": ["ba47ba667ee2d62b3a6563f4dc34d514c098d4a5"], "node": "d94f8051a395be05343fed1d2fca536b65f3c60f", "parents": ["ed01fb1efbf5a76dd9f8229db3122558f0d73df2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055013 [wpt PR 61286] - [masonry] Add base test suite for gap decorations for grid lanes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[masonry] Add base test suite for gap decorations for grid lanes\n\nThis CL adds the base test suite for grid lanes gap decorations. They\ndon't cover special cases with `rule-break` or `rule-inset` etc, those\nwill be added later. This test suite just covers the base test cases for\nthe stacking axis and the grid axis, including with spanners, alignment,\nmanually placed items, dense packing, fill-reverse, track-reverse\n\nSince its not implemented yet, they are marked as failing\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: I4158d68cc1c3588d15a407ab72686c157e11fb28\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8072382\nReviewed-by: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662145}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4bf3e0de36a98413094d0d4860c44b2bde8d62ee\nwpt-pr: 61286\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-gaps/grid-lanes/column-gap-decorations-001.html", "test