ive.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/shared-storage-writable-permissions-policy-default.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/shared-storage-writable-permissions-policy-self.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/shared-storage-writable-service-worker-fetch.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/shared-storage-writable-service-worker-iframe.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/shared-storage-writable-service-worker-img.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/shared-storage-writable-setters.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/shared-storage/verify-get-undefined.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prerender/restrictions_shared_storage.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prerender/restrictions_shared_storage_worklet.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "f9111ca4cf01311be84435fad364b4532d93bb97", "git_parents": ["6232198068f136ecc5aa843ff3cf252addd5f6aa"], "node": "2a3c1f0b89e4f3429ba47b97e01bfcd22b7e7091", "parents": ["b17087a30b9b2787bc77acf4d0ced89314c2aceb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moonira \u003cmoonira@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055037 [wpt PR 61290] - Fix if() tests with valid argument grammar, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix if() tests with valid argument grammar\n\nif() function that contains a condition that passes the generic argument\ngrammar, but fails to parse as an \u003cif-condition\u003e should be valid, but\ncondition should be skipped as if tthey were false.\n\nBug: 534464220\nChange-Id: I17490cb0c9873da41d5618e854b871f3929251e2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8090871\nCommit-Queue: Munira Tursunova \u003cmoonira@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Daniil Sakhapov \u003csakhapov@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip J\u00e4genstedt \u003cfoolip@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662170}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e69af49d58318da252132e0279a773b82ee6bb00\nwpt-pr: 61290\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/if-conditionals.html"], "git_node": "c9e1a25c5c6e591316662403f085efbcec6e4df8", "git_parents": ["f9111ca4cf01311be84435fad364b4532d93bb97"], "node": "9528d4faa25f1947eb386bac4d5f550abc3867c3", "parents": ["2a3c1f0b89e4f3429ba47b97e01bfcd22b7e7091"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sangbaek Park \u003csangbaekpark@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055076 [wpt PR 61292] - Media Capabilities: Add robust WPT for encryptionScheme plumbing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMedia Capabilities: Add robust WPT for encryptionScheme plumbing\n\nPreviously, WPT tests for mediaCapabilities.decodingInfo()\nencryptionScheme plumbing succeeded even if the plumbing was\nmissing or incomplete. This was because the tests only validated\nthat the returned object has supported/smooth/powerEfficient as\nbooleans using the standard Clear Key system (which supports both\ncenc and cbcs).\n\nTo make these tests fail when the plumbing is missing or broken:\n1. Define a helper function in WPT that queries decodingInfo() with a\n   specific encryptionScheme, and asserts that the negotiated\n   configuration matches the expected scheme and support status.\n2. Run test cases covering different valid encryption schemes ('cenc',\n   'cbcs', 'cbcs-1-9'), as well as unrecognized ('foobar') and null\n   schemes. If the plumbing is missing, unrecognized schemes will be\n   incorrectly supported, and valid schemes will negotiate as null\n   instead of their expected scheme, causing the tests to fail.\n3. Remove the obsolete and non-assertive tests that only checked\n   that the result type was a boolean.\n\nBug: 498284510\nChange-Id: I88b3c01f7b3f200312b948f18714707ca2aa7c32\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8076778\nReviewed-by: Xiaohan Wang \u003cxhwang@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Sangbaek Park \u003csangbaekpark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662185}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dc97e7bed3096ac9e0e591ab5fa22e7fb8844ead\nwpt-pr: 61292\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/media-capabilities/decodingInfoEncryptedMedia.https.html"], "git_node": "68dc0bc6b17933d8dbf9d1e691da3a5ee08fb9e2", "git_parents": ["c9e1a25c5c6e591316662403f085efbcec6e4df8"], "node": "59ea3d032f2905ef79d66a1a84d56dae824c26a2", "parents": ["9528d4faa25f1947eb386bac4d5f550abc3867c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Sneddon \u003cgsnedders@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055114 [wpt PR 61299] - Increase Safari and STP chunks to avoid timeouts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nIncrease Safari and STP chunks to avoid timeouts\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e9c1387e87ea0ee46adff0cfaabadb158d3e3df9\nwpt-pr: 61299\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/safari_stable.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/safari_technology_preview.yml"], "git_node": "16fad72006371dd73490e48d191c2894f9c8a311", "git_parents": ["68dc0bc6b17933d8dbf9d1e691da3a5ee08fb9e2"], "node": "cff973b1728d537a726f0b7263a23a5c320f1dbb", "parents": ["59ea3d032f2905ef79d66a1a84d56dae824c26a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055097 [wpt PR 61295] - [wpt] Fix failing image decoder test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wpt] Fix failing image decoder test\n\nTest was just missing a tracks.ready wait\n\nR=tguilbert\n\nBug: 515679398\nChange-Id: Ie8d0ec4d35cd39c3087b226af4481588ea45080e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8093160\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662218}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3d44aebd35c499395df6e10acb6a5cb5e4050707\nwpt-pr: 61295\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/image-decoder-animated-zero-delay.https.any.js"], "git_node": "5e273b98fb401e3a221117cb018254917c113482", "git_parents": ["16fad72006371dd73490e48d191c2894f9c8a311"], "node": "24daba36b5384d0d000fd15c96b839f97c8ec9db", "parents": ["cff973b1728d537a726f0b7263a23a5c320f1dbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055102 [wpt PR 61297] - [html-in-canvas] Fire canvas paint events in reverse tree order, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[html-in-canvas] Fire canvas paint events in reverse tree order\n\nThis is a followup to https://crrev.com/1660605 which fires canvas\npaint events in reverse tree order. Previously, the code only sorted\nonly based on depth. A comprehensive test has been added for the new\nbehavior. This change aligns the implementation with the spec PR:\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11588/changes/4b5772d93ea052e950594d768341ee1a8e91abe2\n\nBug: 527969910\nChange-Id: I05134de6c70569527cb4d4105ce08d2d710198fa\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8093150\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip J\u00e4genstedt \u003cfoolip@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662264}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 92e281600ba335aabc8ed12896e58795625c0f27\nwpt-pr: 61297\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/lint.ignore"], "git_node": "4a0831787d0b42ec42388c03ddf718a2e9920531", "git_parents": ["5e273b98fb401e3a221117cb018254917c113482"], "node": "f87addcf2a0b861f5a1020903eb3f0ed9061c60c", "parents": ["24daba36b5384d0d000fd15c96b839f97c8ec9db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055102 [wpt PR 61297] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61297\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/onpaint-post-tree-order.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "021f3caf3e5bdc14d4b56c729dc8b5c4aaeba00c", "git_parents": ["4a0831787d0b42ec42388c03ddf718a2e9920531"], "node": "45a6f4971749e27991404fa654e3668030a09b7c", "parents": ["f87addcf2a0b861f5a1020903eb3f0ed9061c60c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marcos C\u00e1ceres \u003ccaceres_m@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053981 [wpt PR 61188] - [digital-credentials] Test get() from an opaque origin, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[digital-credentials] Test get() from an opaque origin (#61188)\n\nnavigator.credentials.get({ digital }) from a document with an opaque origin must\nbe rejected with a SecurityError. Covers opaque origins via a sandbox attribute, a\nContent-Security-Policy: sandbox header, a sandboxed srcdoc, and nesting up to three\nlevels (sandbox flags propagate); non-opaque controls (allow-same-origin, srcdoc,\nblob:); a top-level page made opaque via a CSP sandbox header; and a data: document\n(not a secure context, so the API is absent).\n\nAsserts SecurityError per working-group agreement; the spec PR\nw3c-fedid/digital-credentials#535 is being updated from NotAllowedError.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c158a06b7d745c6fcf5e38b674e31ee26f7a3edc\nwpt-pr: 61188\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-combinations.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-top-level-allow-same-origin.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-top-level-allow-same-origin.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-top-level.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-top-level.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/support/dc-nest.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/support/dc-report-get-blob-in-sandbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/support/dc-report-get-csp-sandbox.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/support/dc-report-get-csp-sandbox.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/support/dc-report-get.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/support/dc-report-get.js"], "git_node": "028aa838ecf7d01ba838a7507453c80010db3a76", "git_parents": ["021f3caf3e5bdc14d4b56c729dc8b5c4aaeba00c"], "node": "a4a7b41cad10d3f86c3c2d452a02097b5bb7879f", "parents": ["45a6f4971749e27991404fa654e3668030a09b7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053981 [wpt PR 61188] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61188\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-combinations.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-top-level-allow-same-origin.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/digital-credentials/get-opaque-origin-top-level.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "355f4f38186abd9111612e221c889a6e576d77dd", "git_parents": ["028aa838ecf7d01ba838a7507453c80010db3a76"], "node": "4edd87bcb44b4324d9fa9afc5144595057d77f29", "parents": ["a4a7b41cad10d3f86c3c2d452a02097b5bb7879f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mahesh Bharadwaj Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054264 [wpt PR 61225] - WebAudio: Fix loopStart ignored when loopEnd is default 0, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebAudio: Fix loopStart ignored when loopEnd is default 0\n\nWhen loopStart is set on an AudioBufferSourceNode but loopEnd is left\nat its default value of 0, the loop falls back to the entire buffer\ninstead of looping from loopStart to the end of the buffer.\n\nThis patch fixes the logic to treat loopEnd=0 as the buffer duration\nwhen loopStart \u003e 0, aligning with the spec and user expectations.\n\nBug: 40918221\nChange-Id: I5cf2ede6cff1be5031d4d1d39c52c383ee14342d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7830628\nCommit-Queue: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Michael Wilson \u003cmjwilson@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662294}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 85aeda55206d82bdf3eaf45706e8735360857e79\nwpt-pr: 61225\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiobuffersourcenode-interface/audiobuffersource-playbackrate-negative.html"], "git_node": "30852b0b90a0d9ec08e2bbf1dfcd829e2d11f41e", "git_parents": ["355f4f38186abd9111612e221c889a6e576d77dd"], "node": "6cb532950269f1c069061d79dd2cea4f45746448", "parents": ["4edd87bcb44b4324d9fa9afc5144595057d77f29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054264 [wpt PR 61225] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61225\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audiobuffersourcenode-interface/audiobuffersource-playbackrate-negative.html.ini"], "git_node": "213b6c3755e5eb230a740619520d08c7fce54867", "git_parents": ["30852b0b90a0d9ec08e2bbf1dfcd829e2d11f41e"], "node": "248cfa1d7ea738c84b693c307275ee1cfcf5e8cd", "parents": ["6cb532950269f1c069061d79dd2cea4f45746448"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mingmingtasd \u003cmingming1.xu@intel.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055107 [wpt PR 61298] - WebNN: Remove constant tensor both on renderer and services side, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebNN: Remove constant tensor both on renderer and services side\n\nThe constant tensor feature allows tensors to be created with\ninitial data and used as graph constants. But due to no backend\nsupports constant tensors now, we should remove it to simplify.\n\nThis CL removes the constant tensor support from the renderer\nside and all WebNN backends on services side.\n\nMojom interface changes:\n- Remove the `tensor_data` parameter from the\n  WebNNContext::CreateTensor() method.\n- Remove `id_to_constant_tensor_operand_map` from the GraphInfo\n  struct.\n- Remove the BigBuffer import from webnn_context.mojom.\n- Remove the `graph_constant` field from the TensorUsage struct.\n\nBackend implementation changes:\n- Remove constant tensor handling from all backend contexts\n  (CoreML, ORT, TFLite, LiteRT).\n- Remove the `constant_tensor_operands` parameter from\n  BuildGraph() and CreateGraphImpl().\n\nBlink renderer changes:\n- Remove the MLContext::createConstantTensor() implementation.\n- Update createTensor() to call CreateTensor() without the\n  tensor data parameter.\n- Remove kGraphConstant dispatch checks from input/output\n  tensor validation.\n- Remove kGraphConstant from the MLTensorUsageFlags enum since\n  no code path can produce it.\n\nTests and fuzzers are updated to drop constant tensor references.\n\nBug: 502249078,508864477\nChange-Id: Ie0e5af6f3af578b011b66a37ad900ce2304280ab\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7947968\nReviewed-by: Reilly Grant \u003creillyg@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Hu, Ningxin \u003cningxin.hu@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rafael Cintron \u003crafael.cintron@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Xu, Mingming1 \u003cmingming1.xu@intel.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alex Gough \u003cajgo@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662328}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4830edb033cb486fd0cd6f85b5e937cfc718704d\nwpt-pr: 61298\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webnn/conformance_tests/tensor.https.any.js"], "git_node": "1039d1204c617fe1af1babcdf52aac1142633516", "git_parents": ["213b6c3755e5eb230a740619520d08c7fce54867"], "node": "91452a1f732757b6d3c5fd50d67e55e92902e201", "parents": ["248cfa1d7ea738c84b693c307275ee1cfcf5e8cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Minseong Kim \u003cjja08111@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055194 [wpt PR 61306] - [css-overflow] Pin fonts for text-overflow string values WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-overflow] Pin fonts for text-overflow string values WPTs\n\nThe text-overflow-string-* tests relied on the platform's fonts. So, the\nadvance width of the ellipsis differed across platforms and the\ncontainer widths were not deterministic.\n\nThis CL pins a bundled font per script so the ellipsis has known,\nplatform-independent advances.\n- Latin strings uses monospace with a width expressed in `ch`.\n- Hebrew and bidi strings use the bundled `mplus-1p-regular` font.\n- The emoji string uses a new subset of Noto Color Emoji.\n\nBug: 41492459\nChange-Id: I76bac02be8b435537db01906acd1d719db6ca8ea\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8062288\nReviewed-by: Andreu Botella \u003cabotella@igalia.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Minseong Kim \u003cjja08111@gmail.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662490}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 82e703d8ad0f5e132c1609743989df73f2b95aae\nwpt-pr: 61306\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-007-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/reference/text-overflow-string-008-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-007.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-008.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fonts/noto/color-emoji/LICENSE.txt", "testing/web-platform/tests/fonts/noto/color-emoji/NotoColorEmoji-subset.ttf", "testing/web-platform/tests/fonts/noto/color-emoji/README.md", "testing/web-platform/tests/fonts/noto/color-emoji/subset.sh"], "git_node": "adea2c16d02242c9432c468a3df6ff834ce34a8b", "git_parents": ["1039d1204c617fe1af1babcdf52aac1142633516"], "node": "7f51ebfbe605a25c1254aa0e7d05e90e73fbcefa", "parents": ["91452a1f732757b6d3c5fd50d67e55e92902e201"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055194 [wpt PR 61306] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61306\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-ui/text-overflow-string-005.html.ini"], "git_node": "40b75832b9681287879154ad29f977c28d3b748e", "git_parents": ["adea2c16d02242c9432c468a3df6ff834ce34a8b"], "node": "801450d4ce4dc9a4277cb217a017e311008c23b0", "parents": ["7f51ebfbe605a25c1254aa0e7d05e90e73fbcefa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yao Xiao \u003cyaoxia@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055196 [wpt PR 61307] - [Topics] Delete all Topics-specific web tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Topics] Delete all Topics-specific web tests\n\nThis CL removes all web tests related to the Topics API.\n\nI2D&R:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/_R85yctz4Rs\n\nBug: 461709147\nChange-Id: Ia2300ee4e9fe3ebe559be6c2a1f3660792874ee5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8093782\nReviewed-by: Josh Karlin \u003cjkarlin@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yao Xiao \u003cyaoxia@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662590}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e9fbe38094ee7d4369620ad81b40b96251ab6afb\nwpt-pr: 61307\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/WEB_FEATURES.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/browsing-topics-permissions-policy-default.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/browsing-topics-permissions-policy-none.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/browsing-topics-permissions-policy-none.tentative.https.sub.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/browsing-topics-permissions-policy-self.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/browsing-topics-permissions-policy-self.tentative.https.sub.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/document-api-insecure-context.tentative.http.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/document-api.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/fetch-topics-header-not-visible-in-service-worker.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/fetch-topics-insecure-context.tentative.http.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/fetch-topics.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/fetch-without-topics-flag.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/iframe-topics-attribute-insecure-context.tentative.http.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/iframe-topics-attribute.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/img-topics-attribute.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/check-topics-request-header-in-img.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/check-topics-request-header-notify-parent.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/check-topics-request-header.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/document-api-notify-parent.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/empty.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/fetch-topics-header-not-visible-in-service-worker-helper.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/fetch-topics.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/header-util.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/intercept-request.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/load_img.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/permissions-policy-util.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/pixel.png", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/resources/topics-not-allowed-for-service-worker-fetch-helper.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/browsing-topics/topics-not-allowed-for-service-worker-fetch.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "b0439468538bf9f9db0c5f0d0905f5a3efd87c4c", "git_parents": ["40b75832b9681287879154ad29f977c28d3b748e"], "node": "ed4345cd4c0e3922fcb8d9e531e265f82bb4dc02", "parents": ["801450d4ce4dc9a4277cb217a017e311008c23b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yi S \u003cratsunny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1994965 [wpt PR 55505] - html: dynamic import entry should not be cached for HTTP error, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHTML: dynamic import entry should not be cached for HTTP error\n\nThis PR added and adjusted some WPT tests for the proposed change in\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/10327, which clarifies that the failed module fetches\n(HTTP/Network/MIME errors) should not be cached in the module map.\n\nBackground\nIn the current spec, the module map caches the module fetches\nregardless of the fetch result. This means that if a module fetch\nfails due to an HTTP error (e.g., 404 Not Found), subsequent\ndynamic imports of the same module will immediately fail with\nthe same error without attempting to fetch the module again.\n\nThis behavior can lead to issues where transient errors (like a\ntemporary network glitch or a server hiccup) cause a module to\nbe permanently unavailable for the duration of the page session.\n\nThe proposed change in whatwg/html#10327 aims to address this by\nspecifying that only successful module fetches should be cached.\nThis means that if a module fetch fails, subsequent dynamic imports\nwill attempt to fetch the module again, allowing developers\nto recover from transient errors more gracefully.\n\nSpec references\n- whatwg/html#6768\n- whatwg/html#10327\n\nThese tests pass on a Chromium prototype implementation in\nhttps://chromium-review.googlesource.com/7039725\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 855402fbf3ebf818d11f4dae1f4bf41068a19853\nwpt-pr: 55505\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/css-module/repeated-import.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/json-module/repeated-imports.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/dynamic-imports-fetch-error.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/repeated-imports.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/resources/status-changing-script.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-a.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-b.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/serve-custom-response.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/serve-json-then-js.py"], "git_node": "f4d3668145578dbe856a0fad798f610dae4ea4dd", "git_parents": ["b0439468538bf9f9db0c5f0d0905f5a3efd87c4c"], "node": "7cdaaf2852465d0cb952d12c75827e3ae63c00c3", "parents": ["ed4345cd4c0e3922fcb8d9e531e265f82bb4dc02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1994965 [wpt PR 55505] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 55505\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/css-module/repeated-import.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/json-module/repeated-imports.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/repeated-imports.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html.ini"], "git_node": "e6c7b6d0f22fb6c6f9d80acca10b7dc01549fa31", "git_parents": ["f4d3668145578dbe856a0fad798f610dae4ea4dd"], "node": "74292fe7b4dbda426b72261796c02fae34b409b3", "parents": ["7cdaaf2852465d0cb952d12c75827e3ae63c00c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoav Weiss \u003cyoav.weiss@shopify.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055192 [wpt PR 61305] - Dont cache failed module fetch extra tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nConcurrent module script imports result in a single fetch (#61305)\n\nEnsure the test validates the microtask case\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 48340cb389d4134422f1799c579f7da80c0e286f\nwpt-pr: 61305\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module-fetch-tester.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/concurrent-failed-imports.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/concurrent-failed-imports.any.js"], "git_node": "669b9d4b49dbd92eb949f1eb265363fc9e37793d", "git_parents": ["e6c7b6d0f22fb6c6f9d80acca10b7dc01549fa31"], "node": "2e79585dc1cecbb8c4132308b436f49327854fa3", "parents": ["74292fe7b4dbda426b72261796c02fae34b409b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055192 [wpt PR 61305] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61305\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/concurrent-failed-imports.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/concurrent-failed-imports.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/modulepreload-referrerpolicy.html.ini"], "git_node": "9721e8472591dfac8a6240793455ca2008107543", "git_parents": ["669b9d4b49dbd92eb949f1eb265363fc9e37793d"], "node": "ce38e680cca6e3e08f15d5f510dc069b24d79247", "parents": ["2e79585dc1cecbb8c4132308b436f49327854fa3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055290 [wpt PR 61313] - Resolve scroll-animations spec mismatch per CSS WG issue 13500, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnsure the `scroll-timeline` and `view-timeline` shorthands serialize to an empty string when the longhands don't match the base property's length. Solve scroll-animations spec mismatch per CSS WG issue 13500 (https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13500). (#61313)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9b281717c580296f7a2080e5a26968f6d822c796\nwpt-pr: 61313\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/css/scroll-timeline-shorthand.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/css/view-timeline-shorthand.html"], "git_node": "3075df7ef379e4858e78225b8f8a5ddbe428a669", "git_parents": ["9721e8472591dfac8a6240793455ca2008107543"], "node": "68af93534c5737b97b7ff28346f1e4ad7e35dc86", "parents": ["ce38e680cca6e3e08f15d5f510dc069b24d79247"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055290 [wpt PR 61313] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61313\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/view-timeline-shorthand.html.ini"], "git_node": "d180230057e2a55830b4264e45b29f4dc7d5ecc0", "git_parents": ["3075df7ef379e4858e78225b8f8a5ddbe428a669"], "node": "571a33453b62e00241f790df046719b5db70dd66", "parents": ["68af93534c5737b97b7ff28346f1e4ad7e35dc86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055297 [wpt PR 61316] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314104., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=314104. (#61316)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bae042a878d87767e9fb190acb333790716eff9a\nwpt-pr: 61316\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/css/timeline-offset-keyframes-with-scroll-timeline.html"], "git_node": "e9c32de3f46a81a1e1192dbf3a0d4069453b2a56", "git_parents": ["d180230057e2a55830b4264e45b29f4dc7d5ecc0"], "node": "51a477d2fceb93d3afeb4e1451e65406159010d8", "parents": ["571a33453b62e00241f790df046719b5db70dd66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055297 [wpt PR 61316] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61316\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/timeline-offset-keyframes-with-scroll-timeline.html.ini"], "git_node": "8df1901998e1a5ba71c8ccded4349a8155ef8237", "git_parents": ["e9c32de3f46a81a1e1192dbf3a0d4069453b2a56"], "node": "8af6b24895a2fac65a230037b7a244d894e7aa11", "parents": ["51a477d2fceb93d3afeb4e1451e65406159010d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055293 [wpt PR 61314] - View timeline insets account for scroll-padding by default, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nView timeline insets account for scroll-padding by default. This matches the resolution for CSS WG issue 11644 (https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11644). (#61314)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0684405ec9c5c9a789d912c2dff3980a7980690a\nwpt-pr: 61314\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-snapport.html"], "git_node": "627f05905789d011c93bd82037d4a57ac42aa3e1", "git_parents": ["8df1901998e1a5ba71c8ccded4349a8155ef8237"], "node": "344bbe4287deb62171b80ecbd82251c91a50b92a", "parents": ["8af6b24895a2fac65a230037b7a244d894e7aa11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055325 [wpt PR 61317] - Clamp resolution of no-render LoAFs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nClamp resolution of no-render LoAFs\n\nBug: 514439436\nChange-Id: I875813bdc78560b59795508e4fe37d020973790a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8040052\nReviewed-by: Yoav Weiss (@Shopify) \u003cyoavweiss@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662777}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 37d9cf353594dde3010f4d057166879d47dd6c5e\nwpt-pr: 61317\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-duration-clamping.html"], "git_node": "505ae96f1af0ee74eba4aa2afbe11514923df524", "git_parents": ["627f05905789d011c93bd82037d4a57ac42aa3e1"], "node": "49fcfdf1593baf8562bfbca369fa5f1b162cd1c8", "parents": ["344bbe4287deb62171b80ecbd82251c91a50b92a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054004 [wpt PR 61198] - Use committed origin when deciding whether to dispatch navigate event, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nUse committed origin when deciding whether to dispatch navigate event\n\nThe committed origin can be opaque in sandboxed iframes, and is also\npre-redirect.\n\nBug: 511774376\nChange-Id: Ia5f4257a907274f24abb32186ae0e074eb488716\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8041464\nReviewed-by: Charlie Reis \u003ccreis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nate Chapin \u003cjaphet@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662779}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6b36dd68e58ad84a5d7f90a075ef5f4d0aaf14f0\nwpt-pr: 61198\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/cross-window/cross-document-history-traversal-from-sandboxed-opaque-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/cross-window/resources/sandboxed-opaque-origin-step2.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/cross-window/resources/sandboxed-opaque-origin.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/navigation-api/navigate-event/cross-window/resources/sandboxed-opaque-origin.html.headers"], "git_node": "19925ba522211178d2bb9b10dc08f051b4e856bb", "git_parents": ["505ae96f1af0ee74eba4aa2afbe11514923df524"], "node": "bf6e9e33de714777d5b554d9bffdcce5a80bc332", "parents": ["49fcfdf1593baf8562bfbca369fa5f1b162cd1c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054004 [wpt PR 61198] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61198\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/navigation-api/navigate-event/cross-window/cross-document-history-traversal-from-sandboxed-opaque-origin.html.ini"], "git_node": "085ed6574ca2223dfcbfba31391858d9aac192f7", "git_parents": ["19925ba522211178d2bb9b10dc08f051b4e856bb"], "node": "8881edf011ea53ca82b49f1e14775464d16d5cfe", "parents": ["bf6e9e33de714777d5b554d9bffdcce5a80bc332"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antoine Quint \u003cgraouts@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055346 [wpt PR 61319] - Ensure the scroll-timeline shorthand serializes to an empty string when its longhands don't match the base property's length, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnsure the scroll-timeline shorthand serializes to an empty string when its longhands don't match the base property's length. Solves scroll-animations spec mismatch per CSS WG issue 13500 (https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13500). (#61319)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5ef40c7e6f0328764731e64882efa446c739b9d3\nwpt-pr: 61319\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/css/scroll-timeline-shorthand.html"], "git_node": "0d75334a0a934ddf294b9abc9b929b96f8ee1109", "git_parents": ["085ed6574ca2223dfcbfba31391858d9aac192f7"], "node": "fe62956b19c886db41dad6250830e285a392e791", "parents": ["8881edf011ea53ca82b49f1e14775464d16d5cfe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055346 [wpt PR 61319] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61319\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/scroll-timeline-shorthand.html.ini"], "git_node": "0cfbe41d30fffdfd0e90134fc47f3ad326fd31a6", "git_parents": ["0d75334a0a934ddf294b9abc9b929b96f8ee1109"], "node": "7bfbb1950619b0391013dd511c915bff4cc9a711", "parents": ["fe62956b19c886db41dad6250830e285a392e791"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055400 [wpt PR 61323] - [OpaqueRange] Support multi-node geometry in text controls, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[OpaqueRange] Support multi-node geometry in text controls\n\nMove value offset mapping into TextControlElement so geometry APIs\ncorrectly handle inner editors with multiple Text nodes and line breaks.\n\nPreviously, BuildValueGeometryContext() only used the first Text node,\nproducing incorrect rects for multiline content or editors with multiple\ntext nodes.\n\nSplit multiline-and-mutations WPT into separate multiline and mutations\ntest files and added multi-line selection and newline edge case\ncoverage.\n\nLow-Coverage-Reason: COVERAGE_UNDERREPORTED\nBug: 482337697\nChange-Id: I36bd9d17fc66f215e2ee04e9fcc7a9bad2b079c2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7870745\nReviewed-by: Ana Sollano Kim \u003cansollan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1662846}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 437665fdcf646504415938f6acce1831ffd44dbd\nwpt-pr: 61323\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-geometry-multiline-and-mutations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-geometry-multiline.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-geometry-mutations.html"], "git_node": "7b0ee7c8402cad2357a2b6acb1ece7a6a670639c", "git_parents": ["0cfbe41d30fffdfd0e90134fc47f3ad326fd31a6"], "node": "dce8d39008644fb5165db1374bf52f84d060e9cf", "parents": ["7bfbb1950619b0391013dd511c915bff4cc9a711"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055400 [wpt PR 61323] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61323\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-geometry-multiline-and-mutations.html.ini", "testing