node": "d6a8baf801c93a81872bbab1bd5d42cfacc444a5", "git_parents": ["c1694335e5bbb85599d54b370406278502a2cec1"], "node": "f32ba685d958964538c5bdeb7b4d84428d1c5282", "parents": ["0357f6dd19337c10e2c7348255ffca810fd4725a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056002 - [loong64] Part 7: Enable jit::Disassemble on loong64. r=jandem\n\nWith all the previous parts in place, we can now enable jit::Disassemble\non loong64, thus enabling disnative(), disblic(), and wasmDis()\naltogether.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312862\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/Disassemble.cpp"], "git_node": "6ead593e7b6098e87b42d089bab31bef434226f1", "git_parents": ["d6a8baf801c93a81872bbab1bd5d42cfacc444a5"], "node": "d69876a056294b9ebecf2e2b5c67b9f8c5e305cf", "parents": ["f32ba685d958964538c5bdeb7b4d84428d1c5282"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erich Gubler \u003cerichdongubler@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055567 - chore(rust): update `cfg_aliases` 0.2.1 \u2192 0.2.2 r=supply-chain-reviewers\n\nThis preempts a supply chain change that would be forced with an update to wgpu crates anyway. See also: \u003chttps://github.com/gfx-rs/wgpu/pull/9885\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312535\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/README.md", "third_party/rust/cfg_aliases/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "1736aebae6187b153b1eba7278723195dfe7425f", "git_parents": ["6ead593e7b6098e87b42d089bab31bef434226f1"], "node": "9a03257d13d7d1b4ba5651dca8b931478e6774ed", "parents": ["d69876a056294b9ebecf2e2b5c67b9f8c5e305cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "DrSeed Lu \u003cdr.seed.lu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053182 - Deemphasize the selected tab border in inactive windows in the open tabs sidebar panel r=kcochrane,nsharpley,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nThe open tabs panel shows the selected tab of every window with a full\nstrength border. For windows other than the current one, the border is now\nshown at about 60% opacity, so the current window stays the focus.\n\nThe panel marks each non-current window's tab list and pinned buttons, and\nthe selected border colours are mixed down to 60% for those. This covers both\nthe pinned buttons and the regular rows, in normal and high contrast mode.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312714\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-opentabs.css", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-opentabs.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-tab-list.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-tab-row.css", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_opentabs_sidebar.js"], "git_node": "1dba15fe7f0add7e3c94ea375928627407f8d62d", "git_parents": ["1736aebae6187b153b1eba7278723195dfe7425f"], "node": "360f162274af88dd8d68d9482caa019c19633426", "parents": ["9a03257d13d7d1b4ba5651dca8b931478e6774ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051682 - Update neqo to v0.30.1 r=necko-reviewers,supply-chain-reviewers,kershaw\n\nUpdate the vendored neqo crates to v0.30.1 and adapt neqo_glue to the API:\n\n- The slow start exit stats are now a single SlowStartExitStats struct,\n  and SlowStartExitReason::CongestionEvent carries a CongestionTrigger.\n- Surface the new WebTransportEvent::Draining variant as a new\n  WebTransportEventExternal::Draining FFI event. Http3Session ignores it\n  for now, preserving the previous behavior.\n- The WebTransport and CONNECT-UDP client methods moved into ClientSession\n  extension traits, and the server-side event and session types moved into\n  the webtransport and connect_udp modules. neqo_glue and http3server are\n  updated to import them from their new locations.\n\nAlso bound the per-pass receive loop in neqo_http3conn_process_input to\n50 MB so a misbehaving or malicious peer cannot make us buffer datagrams\nunboundedly. Nothing is lost when the cap is hit: buffered events are\ndelivered to the upper layer right after, and the level-triggered poll\nre-fires RecvData to read the rest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309777\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/Cargo.toml", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs", "netwerk/test/http3server/Cargo.toml", "netwerk/test/http3server/src/main.rs", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "third_party/rust/mtu/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/mtu/build.rs", "third_party/rust/mtu/src/bindings/openbsd.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-bin/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/neqo-bin/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/neqo-bin/benches/main.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-bin/build.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-bin/src/client/http3.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-bin/src/server/mod.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/src/codec.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/src/datagram.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/src/header.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/src/hex.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-common/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/benches/common.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/benches/streams_simulated.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/benches/streams_walltime.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/src/client_events.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/src/conn_params.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/src/connect_udp.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/src/connection.rs", "third_party/rust/neqo-http3/src/c