WidgetMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/sports/WorldCupMatchesRepositoryTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/sports/client/AppServicesWorldCupMatchesClientTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/sports/ui/SportsWidgetTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/sports/util/LocalizedCountryNameTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/ui/WordmarkTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/settingssearch/DefaultFenixSettingsIndexerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/config/detekt-baseline.xml"], "git_node": "a91ad60e864c5c29d3882a0d0954efc6ec1eb914", "git_parents": ["02e9b8be663aa257a150c340a91541fd4d78284d"], "node": "969978a0a07af2f1aa0bc578d7cc03546883f930", "parents": ["e01c15577d621b1d64838a628217fe1006bc40d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051571 - Add a new aboutaddons-themes-picker component to manage built-in and AMO-hosted Nova themes from about:addons. r=willdurand,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309609\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/locales-preview/nova-aboutAddons.ftl", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.css", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.html", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/aboutaddons-themes-picker.css", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/aboutaddons-themes-picker.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/addon-list.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/theme-preview.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_html_themes_picker.js"], "git_node": "1311f6380009012a2ccaf9c6b03e70da135f881b", "git_parents": ["a91ad60e864c5c29d3882a0d0954efc6ec1eb914"], "node": "0312ada1975e0b6fc63826bb8d08ba24f594ded4", "parents": ["969978a0a07af2f1aa0bc578d7cc03546883f930"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054642: Fix favicons for ai-grouped-chip-container added via mentions panel r=flozia\n\n**Issue:** When we added context chips via the mentions menu (typing @ in the smartbar instead of adding via the + button), the favicons were lost and it displayed the default one.\n\n**Root cause:** The icon was never passed as an attribute when we got mentions.\n\n**Solution: ** Add the icon as an attribute. We wrap it around `getIconForUrl` replicating what happens in the smartbar input.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312599\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs"], "git_node": "0eb7ac8bd403371355ebd49b9e1866858e83ac8b", "git_parents": ["1311f6380009012a2ccaf9c6b03e70da135f881b"], "node": "bef7cce36ff4123238a9533d8032068b17508145", "parents": ["0312ada1975e0b6fc63826bb8d08ba24f594ded4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055191 - Stop running WebCodecs camera tests on Chrome and custom-car on Linux r=perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nThe linux.*.* subtest branch for browsertime-webcodecs applied one list\nto every app, so Chrome and custom-car picked up the camera-source\nvariants. Those variants rely on Firefox's fake camera device, which\nChromium does not honor, so getUserMedia finds no video input device and\nthe benchmark fails.\n\nGate the Linux subtest list by app, matching the non-Linux branch:\nFirefox keeps the camera variants while Chrome and custom-car run the\nnon-camera variants only, until bug 2044846 supplies a Chromium fake\ncamera.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312775\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/desktop.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.rst"], "git_node": "8feabbb8ed864d8d001d10a658aad4d87a574f07", "git_parents": ["0eb7ac8bd403371355ebd49b9e1866858e83ac8b"], "node": "f600c141e5f1d4e1ae187737718aaf9599553f84", "parents": ["bef7cce36ff4123238a9533d8032068b17508145"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055887 - Make pref.general.disable_button.default_browser work again. r=mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312763\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/main.js"], "git_node": "a38058c5fe714fa3c6c69d10471fa2a3ef0bbd7b", "git_parents": ["8feabbb8ed864d8d001d10a658aad4d87a574f07"], "node": "529723e49f5bfb77832c14c33847aae4d14cd44f", "parents": ["f600c141e5f1d4e1ae187737718aaf9599553f84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053103 - Add TimeDuration::ToTicksAtRate for exact tick-rate conversion r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nAdds an integer/rational conversion from a TimeDuration to a count of\narbitrary-rate ticks, rounded to the nearest tick with no floating point.\nUnlike ToMicroseconds()/ToSeconds(), which multiply by a precomputed double\ntick factor, this is computed directly from the platform tick count and the\nplatform's native rational rate, so it is exact for durations representable at\nthe target rate and unbiased (nearest, no drift) otherwise. The GCD-reduced\n64-bit mul/div decomposition avoids 128-bit arithmetic (portable to 32-bit and\nto Windows, whose runtime lacks __udivti3). Implemented for the mach (darwin),\nPOSIX (nanosecond) and Windows (QPC) backends, with a gtest in TestTimeStamp.cpp.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311215\n", "files": ["mozglue/misc/RoundedMulDiv.h", "mozglue/misc/TimeStamp.h", "mozglue/misc/TimeStamp_darwin.cpp", "mozglue/misc/TimeStamp_posix.cpp", "mozglue/misc/TimeStamp_windows.cpp", "mozglue/misc/moz.build", "xpcom/tests/gtest/TestTimeStamp.cpp"], "git_node": "9ec8ebfa9435113bad2db379a8d35dc2e1f6b018", "git_parents": ["a38058c5fe714fa3c6c69d10471fa2a3ef0bbd7b"], "node": "18a3f566ec41712c6df684bade37d6a8139ab18a", "parents": ["529723e49f5bfb77832c14c33847aae4d14cd44f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053103 - Use TimeDuration::ToTicksAtRate in VideoTrackEncoder r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nReplace UsecsToFrames(absoluteEndTime.ToMicroseconds(), mTrackRate) at both the\nper-frame and end-of-stream sites with the exact ToTicksAtRate conversion. This\nremoves the lossy TimeDuration -\u003e double-microseconds step that mis-rounds on\nclocks whose tick factor is not exactly representable (e.g. the Apple Silicon\n125/3 mach timebase), which produced off-by-one-tick frame durations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311214\n", "files": ["dom/media/encoder/TrackEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "9191fcdec0825e7036af0e3b78437f13d48d5b17", "git_parents": ["9ec8ebfa9435113bad2db379a8d35dc2e1f6b018"], "node": "f1fbe46426b9d3b02df2d3b6ef78b9c578cc0ff5", "parents": ["18a3f566ec41712c6df684bade37d6a8139ab18a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053103 - Add VP8 tests for track tick duration conversion r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311895\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestVideoTrackEncoder.cpp"], "git_node": "353142276109ed844258542973717a9f5eff5d3e", "git_parents": ["9191fcdec0825e7036af0e3b78437f13d48d5b17"], "node": "38ace240f2ef3b0f3512fadbb752feee8a9157ce", "parents": ["f1fbe46426b9d3b02df2d3b6ef78b9c578cc0ff5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ed Lee \u003cedilee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056383 - update mots for machine learning peers, includes, groups r=shtrom\n\nadd new people and update outdated meta into new submodules\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313099\n", "files": ["mots.yaml"], "git_node": "98c342573b2b9716ac14fac45b5b0a6300905ec3", "git_parents": ["353142276109ed844258542973717a9f5eff5d3e"], "node": "b09f6a2d864a4520398b38bcf9e47c8800a28070", "parents": ["38ace240f2ef3b0f3512fadbb752feee8a9157ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050294 - Update libcubeb to 4274d032. r=cubeb-reviewers,kinetik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313012\n", "files": ["media/libcubeb/moz.yaml", "media/libcubeb/test/test_loopback.cpp"], "git_node": "e7e36cb922b6bbc45a9aacf4414d54fa0c701fa0", "git_parents": ["98c342573b2b9716ac14fac45b5b0a6300905ec3"], "node": "a770d4688dd2eeff1c89c927357a2c540e720948", "parents": ["b09f6a2d864a4520398b38bcf9e47c8800a28070"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Artur Iunusov \u003caiunusov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048490 - Schedule queued workers on their owning thread r=dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307742\n", "files": ["dom/workers/RuntimeService.cpp", "dom/workers/RuntimeService.h", "dom/workers/WorkerPrivate.h"], "git_node": "c397cea0200ad80253935bb4135d5d834fb8acd1", "git_parents": ["e7e36cb922b6bbc45a9aacf4414d54fa0c701fa0"], "node": "f6b1bd01c42279cf264619102ef0044792bb376b", "parents": ["a770d4688dd2eeff1c89c927357a2c540e720948"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2054642: Fix favicons for ai-grouped-chip-container added via mentions panel r=flozia\" for causing bc failures @ browser_aiwindow_smartbar_inline_mentions.js\n\nThis reverts commit 0eb7ac8bd403371355ebd49b9e1866858e83ac8b.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs"], "git_node": "ad7319dc2b3b6cb9d608c20a8a01ae28b2fb3a31", "git_parents": ["c397cea0200ad80253935bb4135d5d834fb8acd1"], "node": "450d79a89e62095044c49ab47eaaa6659cd84ab9", "parents": ["f6b1bd01c42279cf264619102ef0044792bb376b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McDonough \u003cemcdonough@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1856162 Part 1 - Allow scaling a PDF beyond its normal page-size. r=dholbert\n\nThis will only happen when printing a single page-per-sheet, and when the page\nis smaller than the sheet. This also does not let you zoom the PDF up past the\nsize of the sheet being used.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D284747\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsPageFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsPageSequenceFrame.h", "layout/printing/nsPrintJob.cpp"], "git_node": "659144b819cfb23ebfdbec162e30af511b0c235d", "git_parents": ["ad7319dc2b3b6cb9d608c20a8a01ae28b2fb3a31"], "node": "738c4e7760a0bd32152e2121ae35e3325c51546d", "parents": ["450d79a89e62095044c49ab47eaaa6659cd84ab9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McDonough \u003cemcdonough@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1856162 Part 2 - Add tests for printing PDFs with scale factors greater than 100% r=layout-reviewers,dholbert\n\nThis tests that scaling a PDF above 100% will work up to the maximum of the\nsheet size.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312832\n", "files": ["layout/base/tests/chrome/printpreview_helper.xhtml"], "git_node": "67a857787dcab7275ddf8086ea12b5eb2a2fb20d", "git_parents": ["659144b819cfb23ebfdbec162e30af511b0c235d"], "node": "ca0ba2e53ef70f1c2fb25ef997cabf17dd3a2814", "parents": ["738c4e7760a0bd32152e2121ae35e3325c51546d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McDonough \u003cemcdonough@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038941 - Initial addition of gfx/fontations_glue, vendor skrifa + read-font + font-types r=supply-chain-reviewers,jfkthame,sylvestre\n\nThis also required a minor bump for once_cell.\n\ngfx/fontations_glue does absolutely nothing yet, it's just there to pull\nskrifa into a sensible place until we begin the actual work of integrating it.\n\nThis adds the configure option `--enable-fontations` which will enable\nbuilding the local crate and pull in skrifa. Doing so defines MOZ_FONTATIONS\nin C/C++.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311205\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "gfx/fontations_glue/Cargo.toml", "gfx/fontations_glue/lib.rs", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/font-types/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/font-types/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/font-types/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/font-types/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/font-types/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/font-types/LICENSE-APACHE", "third_party/rust/font-types/LICENSE-MIT", "third_party/rust/font-types/README.md", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/bbox.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/fixed.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/fword.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/glyph_id.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/int24.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/lib.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/longdatetime.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/matrix.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/name_id.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/offset.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/point.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/raw.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/serde_test.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/tag.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/uint24.rs", "third_party/rust/font-types/src/version.rs", "third_party/rust/once_cell/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/once_cell/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/once_cell/CHANGELOG.md", "third_party/rust/once_cell/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/once_cell/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/once_cell/Cargo.toml.orig"