aa73175c6915b09a039c84adaec3ca2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055101 - Add screenshot taking functionality to GVE for testing purposes r=geckoview-reviewers,nalexander\" for causing android lint failure\n\nThis reverts commit c40dbc22106dc9ff42faf4c970aeafd9ad61bf74.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview_example/GeckoViewActivity.java", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/res/menu/actions.xml", "mobile/android/geckoview_example/src/main/res/values/strings.xml"], "git_node": "13c061cb99dbcc14676f53374d2701cb7edf6989", "git_parents": ["9729eaf9ca67cf27f20e0cfdf9a464d03afc459f"], "node": "92048b0a9cebada2cbdc46b5fe2bce15b64e1918", "parents": ["129f0ebb969c5919a6ffb02be59c2ff57befaaab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055676 - Throw an error if a debugger hook breaks the promise invariant. r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312708\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI-inl.h", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI.h", "js/src/debugger/Debugger.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-08.js"], "git_node": "9c547a2d5b554cce5dcb09be6ae3689e31561a37", "git_parents": ["13c061cb99dbcc14676f53374d2701cb7edf6989"], "node": "b1515c9ed4d8eaa0297dfd883e22d4555cca4215", "parents": ["92048b0a9cebada2cbdc46b5fe2bce15b64e1918"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055125: Only send accessibility info to the parent process if accessibility is in use there. r=eeejay\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312224\n", "files": ["accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.h", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.h", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp"], "git_node": "10ee7ff2027272355e41e5a25bcbf405bdea442e", "git_parents": ["9c547a2d5b554cce5dcb09be6ae3689e31561a37"], "node": "c9a760703f8633266a92874a8fbe93825b07e1e3", "parents": ["b1515c9ed4d8eaa0297dfd883e22d4555cca4215"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055541 - Part 1: Hold the seek-resume clock to the audible position. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nResuming after a seek advanced the reported clock on the system clock while the\naudio stream restarted, then re-anchored the reported position forward to\nwall-clock time when it switched to the audio clock. On a device with a large\noutput latency the audio only becomes audible well after the stream starts, so\nthe reported clock, and the video that follows it, ended up ahead of the audible\naudio by the resume gap and stayed there.\n\nFor example, seeking to 10s on a device with 200ms of output latency:\n\n  1. the stream restarts at 10s, but the speakers stay silent for 200ms;\n  2. before this change the reported clock jumped to about 10.2s during that\n     silence, so the video ran about 200ms ahead of the sound;\n  3. after this change the clock stays at 10s until the audio is actually heard,\n     then advances together with it.\n\nOn a seek resume, follow the audio stream's own position instead: hold the\nreported position at the seek target until the stream produces audio, then track\nit, on both the recreated-stream and reused-stream paths.\n\nA seek resume that begins while muted has no audio stream to follow, so playback\nadvances on the system clock. Drop the hold in that case so a later unmute takes\nthe normal system-clock handoff and the reported clock never jumps backwards.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312951\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediasink/AudioSinkWrapper.cpp", "dom/media/mediasink/AudioSinkWrapper.h"], "git_node": "2d1ed548605c35e744dfe8164a5b4f7a1be92b77", "git_parents": ["10ee7ff2027272355e41e5a25bcbf405bdea442e"], "node": "11bdc4eea17f00dcb7b2ab6f443f6389c5c21a82", "parents": ["c9a760703f8633266a92874a8fbe93825b07e1e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055541 - Part 2: Drain pending events in the AudioSinkWrapper gtest callback helper. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe AudioSinkWrapper gtests advance playback by hand and must pump the owner\nthread's event queue to observe asynchronously dispatched work (stream event\nlisteners, promise continuations). DriveCallback left that to each caller, which\nhad to follow it with a bare ProcessPending().\n\nDrain the queue inside DriveCallback after a callback runs, bundling the\nProcessPending() with the call that needs it so the tests read cleaner, and drop\nthe now-redundant ProcessPending() calls in the fixture helpers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312952\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestAudioSinkWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "67aa8218e86a81f52953c620e89dcc9e3f23a3ae", "git_parents": ["2d1ed548605c35e744dfe8164a5b4f7a1be92b77"], "node": "d47f7ea5b99d824d68350d076dd1bf55d7b38c89", "parents": ["11bdc4eea17f00dcb7b2ab6f443f6389c5c21a82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055541 - Part 3: Model output latency in MockCubeb and add seek-resume clock coverage. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nMockCubeb reported its play cursor as equal to its write cursor, so a test\ncould not exercise a backend whose played position lags the written frames by\nthe output device's latency, as real backends do. Add a settable output latency\nso the reported play cursor lags the write cursor, letting tests reproduce\noutput-latency-dependent playback-clock behaviour without real audio hardware.\n\nBuilding on that, add gtest coverage for the seek-resume playback clock: it\nasserts the reported position never leads the audible audio after a seek resume,\nrun across both the reused-stream and freshly-created-stream paths.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312953\n", "files": ["dom/media/MockCubeb.cpp", "dom/media/MockCubeb.h", "dom/media/gtest/TestAudioSinkWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "aef2d149f8ae65586d17e6bc64e185b68453588e", "git_parents": ["67aa8218e86a81f52953c620e89dcc9e3f23a3ae"], "node": "9ef40d56c30da9ba7d4f49b61a24e200856c2211", "parents": ["d47f7ea5b99d824d68350d076dd1bf55d7b38c89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055541 - Part 4: Document the AudioSinkWrapper playback clock. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nThe playback clock in AudioSinkWrapper selects between the audio-stream clock,\nthe system clock, and a held constant depending on the playback mode, and those\nmodes have grown to include seek resume on recreated and reused streams, unmute,\nand a seek while muted.\n\nAdd a docs page that lays out the clock model, the two invariants it must\nsatisfy, and each playback mode with the clock source it uses and why, so the\nbehaviour can be reviewed and maintained as a whole rather than reconstructed\nfrom the branches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312954\n", "files": ["dom/media/docs/AudioSinkWrapper.md", "dom/media/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "8875648eceb93d394623517add29e488583725e7", "git_parents": ["aef2d149f8ae65586d17e6bc64e185b68453588e"], "node": "c6f303a9cfc477dbed831948e97f4260e4d6dcc6", "parents": ["9ef40d56c30da9ba7d4f49b61a24e200856c2211"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Norisz Fay \u003cnfay@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055676 - Throw an error if a debugger hook breaks the promise invariant. r=mgaudet\" for causing bc and xpcshell failures\n\nThis reverts commit 9c547a2d5b554cce5dcb09be6ae3689e31561a37.\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI-inl.h", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI.h", "js/src/debugger/Debugger.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-08.js"], "git_node": "6ef37b3f695a4f183be257c76e95537c1dea50aa", "git_parents": ["8875648eceb93d394623517add29e488583725e7"], "node": "3212eab9050a2daa15f487f46d7dd887119d409d", "parents": ["c6f303a9cfc477dbed831948e97f4260e4d6dcc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055125: Only send accessibility info to the parent process if accessibility is in use there. r=eeejay\" for causing DocAccessible related failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 10ee7ff2027272355e41e5a25bcbf405bdea442e.\n", "files": ["accessible/base/NotificationController.cpp", "accessible/base/nsAccessibilityService.h", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.cpp", "accessible/generic/DocAccessible.h", "accessible/generic/LocalAccessible.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.cpp", "accessible/ipc/DocAccessibleParent.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp"], "git_node": "82725615de2b9102dc9c8cc303a619226cc92a7f", "git_parents": ["6ef37b3f695a4f183be257c76e95537c1dea50aa"], "node": "e9fa3a1dea1762b61c02048ec7c1fd4bb3948e8f", "parents": ["3212eab9050a2daa15f487f46d7dd887119d409d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2052047 - Add setting for tracker count. r=urlbar-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,mconley,flod,daleharvey\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6df634b802fcf109a7eaf3bd8981df8670bbe715.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/preferences/config/privacy.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/tests/etp/browser_etp_status.js", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_trust_panel_icon.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl"], "git_node": "b2ded3e21639ad5e78120c8212c8779a10a3375b", "git_parents": ["82725615de2b9102dc9c8cc303a619226cc92a7f"], "node": "7f737141927aa474d8333ed494d7fbb95c95b493", "parents": ["e9fa3a1dea1762b61c02048ec7c1fd4bb3948e8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2052046 - Allow tracker count to be controlled by an experiment. r=urlbar-reviewers,daisuke\"\n\nThis reverts commit e905a96b2184e11785ba241bb079c063983096c1.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_trust_panel_icon.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "317e1d5ed61d212ce180e16b7ae744477ac39f56", "git_parents": ["b2ded3e21639ad5e78120c8212c8779a10a3375b"], "node": "7cc3131d516e765ce25b230a277f39ae3c125a33", "parents": ["7f737141927aa474d8333ed494d7fbb95c95b493"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2051545 - Highlight blocked trackers in the address bar. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,flod,daleharvey,dao\" for causing failures on browser_tab_groups.\n\nThis reverts commit 18e028f6758e6572975faa1a3bcd118ff7994c2c.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-trustPanel.js", "browser/base/content/navigator-toolbox.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/controlcenter/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_trust_panel.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_trust_panel_icon.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css", "tools/lint/rejected-words.yml"], "git_node": "aaab2276cc325b2412924e5f1d88ae4399483d1b", "git_parents": ["317e1d5ed61d212ce180e16b7ae744477ac39f56"], "node": "5f8411901e3e170d5e56cadbfedea673915a7b94", "parents": ["7cc3131d516e765ce25b230a277f39ae3c125a33"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056392 - Remove ipc/ipdl from ruff exclude list, r=ipc-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313086\n", "files": ["ipc/ipdl/ipdl/__init__.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/ast.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/checker.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/cxx/ast.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/cxx/cgen.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/cxx/code.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/exporter.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/lower.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/parser.py", "ipc/ipdl/ipdl/type.py", "pyproject.toml"], "git_node": "58421fff610457880c3e8781e469af73dfa70efc", "git_parents": ["aaab2276cc325b2412924e5f1d88ae4399483d1b"], "node": "221ca807dd576490d11b62bb04a5360f8ac013c6", "parents": ["5f8411901e3e170d5e56cadbfedea673915a7b94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alin lastun \u003calastun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049319 - Save hasAlreadyUsedVpn flag when user triggers IP Protection toggle r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour,mavduevskiy\n\nIntroduce IPProtectionPreferencesMiddleware to intercept user-initiated Toggle actions\n   and persistently record VPN usage on the current device\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310793\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtection.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPreferencesMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/IPProtectionFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionRepositoryMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "022753f3d4cdf825f7e1944b0098b6d09c94028e", "git_parents": ["58421fff610457880c3e8781e469af73dfa70efc"], "node": "df1cf8b167406a42518769c4032417bae9932175", "parents": ["221ca807dd576490d11b62bb04a5360f8ac013c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tooru Fujisawa \u003carai_a@mac.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055676 - Throw an error if a debugger hook breaks the promise invariant. r=mgaudet\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312708\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI-inl.h", "js/src/debugger/DebugAPI.h", "js/src/debugger/Debugger.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/Debugger-onNewPromise-08.js"], "git_node": "727cc9daba27ab2235c16beb04f1c0da0157b370", "git_parents": ["022753f3d4cdf825f7e1944b0098b6d09c94028e"], "node": "44d3095a4a773612002f03aa88ff256d3309d2ad", "parents": ["df1cf8b167406a42518769c4032417bae9932175"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1910169 - Part 0: Fix Translations first-use header r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit fixes the issue where the Translations\nfirst-use header reverts when you switch the language\nwhile the Full-Page Translations Panel is open.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298900\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/content/fullPageTranslationsPanel.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_panel_firstrun.js"], "git_node": "2518df5d97b160165119815fc04680d7f021a4d9", "git_parents": ["727cc9daba27ab2235c16beb04f1c0da0157b370"], "node": "5409a638cbee9a232ba86550d5c558380dceb7b8", "parents": ["44d3095a4a773612002f03aa88ff256d3309d2ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1845783 - Part 1: Refactor find-bar state lookup in TranslationsParent r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit refactors the way that the FindBar's open state is queried\nwithin TranslationsParent to make things easier for the transition into\ntranslating iframes within subsequent commits.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297026\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "060c6ec2b74ec2840eecfe50e69d15f160f09428", "git_parents": ["2518df5d97b160165119815fc04680d7f021a4d9"], "node": "7d482f17c1d1bb61a8e1572c01d5c9a93448a49f", "parents": ["5409a638cbee9a232ba86550d5c558380dceb7b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1845783 - Part 2: Refactor document translation startup in TranslationsParent r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit refactors the way that full-page translation is started\nwithin TranslationsParent to make things easier for the transition\ninto translating iframes within subsequent commits.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297027\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f30de4f2c547002683065e08eaada87c8aa4e266", "git_parents": ["060c6ec2b74ec2840eecfe50e69d15f160f09428"], "node": "a33ed5042e1a7b94f6b0341ae07ab955c367ae0b", "parents": ["7d482f17c1d1bb61a8e1572c01d5c9a93448a49f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1845783 - Part 3: Make Translations actors available in sub frames r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit updates the actor management for the TranslationsParent\nand TranslationsChild actors to ensure that they are loaded into\nsub frames of the page, instead of only the main frame.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297028\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_actor_availability.js", "toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f8cd826361f412e27298bc13d0536cc0794a5357", "git_parents": ["f30de4f2c547002683065e08eaada87c8aa4e266"], "node": "8f466b5aec54fef15e46338e3d6d4bfb5449a063", "parents": ["a33ed5042e1a7b94f6b0341ae07ab955c367ae0b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1845783 - Part 4: Translate \u003ciframe\u003e in full-page translation r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit reworks the full-page translation algorithms to enable\ntranslating iframe content and attributes, in addition to the main\npage's top-level content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297029\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsEngineParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/content/translations-document.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/content/translations-engine.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f5b4b05a19b4833f3de7c4c66abff48f0b48e0b4", "git_parents": ["f8cd826361f412e27298bc13d0536cc0794a5357"], "node": "23239b926efa310a3bc6acc0f11debaebfd896b6", "parents": ["8f466b5aec54fef15e46338e3d6d4bfb5449a063"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1845783 - Part 5: Add iframe test page r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit adds a new test page that can be used specifically to\ntest the translation of iframes for full-page translation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297030\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/translations-tester-iframe-es.html"], "git_node": "7aaf95335c07d467920dee8a1910e9b880ea446c", "git_parents": ["f5b4b05a19b4833f3de7c4c66abff48f0b48e0b4"], "node": "edab10adaeee547784fb4fa9dc89d1453af601de", "parents": ["23239b926efa310a3bc6acc0f11debaebfd896b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1845783 - Part 6: Add full-page translation iframe tests r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit introduces several new test cases to ensure that the\nbehavior of translating iframes within full-page tranlation is\nworking as expected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297031\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_full.toml", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_intersection_iframe_content_eager.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_intersection_iframe_find_bar.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_intersection_iframe_lazy.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_intersection_iframe_mutations_lazy.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/head.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_iframe.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/shared-head.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/translations-test.mjs"], "git_node": "ec0a46baa88c26f77a4281ecdc03aa4504ad61c6", "git_parents": ["7aaf95335c07d467920dee8a1910e9b880ea446c"], "node": "a1d154b216fae354c0e595bdd5901a80d99f43aa", "parents": ["edab10adaeee547784fb4fa9dc89d1453af601de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038279 - Part 7: Allow about:* subframe translations r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit adds the ability for `\u003ciframe\u003e` content that is\nloaded from `about:blank` or `about:srcdoc` to translate as\nsub-frame content while still restricting offering full-page\ntranslation for these as top-level pages.\n\nThis fixes the particular `\u003ciframe\u003e` issue in Bug 2038279,\nwhich is not addressed by the rest of this stack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D299444\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_actor_availability.js", "toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "abe5019cb0e29c44ad4baaa09be1bafbde69c121", "git_parents": ["ec0a46baa88c26f77a4281ecdc03aa4504ad61c6"], "node": "c6855fb208c4578441c8c7cf78fab36650b27ee2", "parents": ["a1d154b216fae354c0e595bdd5901a80d99f43aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 1: Improve langTagsMatch r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit improves the reasoning behind the `TranslationsUtils.langTagsMatch()`\nfunction to consider canonicalization as one of the steps. This lets us further\nunify the lang-tag matching code throughout the Translations component.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302536\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/TranslationsUtils.mjs"], "git_node": "528f45f5d326593c3a3b3f7be4735594fc6bc4f6", "git_parents": ["abe5019cb0e29c44ad4baaa09be1bafbde69c121"], "node": "2c25750e8056f8bc854dd3cb267a306dc43d1fd9", "parents": ["c6855fb208c4578441c8c7cf78fab36650b27ee2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 2: Remove obviously unneeded code r=gregtatum,nika,translations-reviewers\n\nThis patch removes code that will become obviously unneeded\nonce we move the page-text extraction code to native C++,\nand then rework the TranslationsChild to be lazily initialized.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302537\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/ActorManagerParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "beb7457cf5744edc385842ff3c664d6e51d65a4f", "git_parents": ["528f45f5d326593c3a3b3f7be4735594fc6bc4f6"], "node": "5441527fb976b85901e884c041472e58431ea099", "parents": ["2c25750e8056f8bc854dd3cb267a306dc43d1fd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 3: DocumentLanguageMetadata Interfaces r=saschanaz\n\nThis commit defines the WebIDL and IPDL interfaces used to request\nDocumentLanguageMetadata through the WindowGlobal parent/child pair.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302538\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/WindowGlobalActors.webidl", "dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalMessageUtils.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "dom/ipc/moz.build"], "git_node": "0b4d19d2071b66d5b636a496dc9939051d434eb8", "git_parents": ["beb7457cf5744edc385842ff3c664d6e51d65a4f"], "node": "bd20487780f85970985e9491cd851d5553ff6128", "parents": ["5441527fb976b85901e884c041472e58431ea099"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 4: Implement Native Page-Text Extraction r=hsivonen,saschanaz\n\nThis commit implements document-language metadata requests in\nWindowGlobalChild. Each request waits for the document load event or a\ntimeout, extracts the HTML lang attribute and a text sample, then may\nretry sampling based on how much text was sampled, controlled by prefs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302539\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsGlobalWindowInner.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalChild.h", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "5f106f6c85f470bc9a5e0636ca67b0aecfc2ff1c", "git_parents": ["0b4d19d2071b66d5b636a496dc9939051d434eb8"], "node": "d7669f9215a50534ddba67415edb2fc56804d9fd", "parents": ["bd20487780f85970985e9491cd851d5553ff6128"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 5: Use document language metadata in TranslationsParent r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers,saschanaz\n\nThis commit updates TranslationsParent to consume document-language metadata payload\nfrom WindowGlobal instead of asking TranslationsChild to extract page text.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302540\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/translations.d.ts"], "git_node": "04e24f4e3104791fae7fc3d822943759f44938f8", "git_parents": ["5f106f6c85f470bc9a5e0636ca67b0aecfc2ff1c"], "node": "597dec780f10e5cc2efa244fc71b287c93f54f79", "parents": ["d7669f9215a50534ddba67415edb2fc56804d9fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 6: Lazily create Translations sub-frame actors r=gregtatum,translations-reviewersnika\n\nUpdates the TranslationsParent code so that sub-frame actors are\ncreated lazily only when translation is requested, instead of\neagerly at page load.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310702\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "4001da955d96242f0c83f02cadfe33963d477a43", "git_parents": ["04e24f4e3104791fae7fc3d822943759f44938f8"], "node": "ab85a33a3f1203a40445a1c11167a862ab17b86a", "parents": ["597dec780f10e5cc2efa244fc71b287c93f54f79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 7: Rework Translations offer decisions r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit reworks the full-page translation offer logic to use the\nnew document-language metadata API, and improves readability by letting\nthe logic map directly to conditions in a decision matrix.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302541\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/content/fullPageTranslationsPanel.js", "toolkit/components/translations/TranslationsTelemetry.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/actors/TranslationsParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/translations/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/translations/translations.d.ts"], "git_node": "4ebb802e96c49276fdbe8b8bbb8afbfac023b898", "git_parents": ["4001da955d96242f0c83f02cadfe33963d477a43"], "node": "4f267cafa35e4135c38cff8dd412f80ac4024d5c", "parents": ["ab85a33a3f1203a40445a1c11167a862ab17b86a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1840857 - Part 8: Update Test Expectations r=gregtatum,translations-reviewers\n\nThis commit updates all of the test cases and expectations to conform\nto the new language-identification behavior, and updated decision-making\nabout when to offer full-page translation to the user.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302542\n", "files": ["browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_ai_feature_mid_translation.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_language_id_behavior.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_panel_auto_translate_error_view.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_panel_auto_translate_revisit_view.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_panel_settings_unsupported_lang.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_auto_translate.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_basics.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_open_panel.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_panel_auto_offer.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_panel_auto_offer_settings.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_retranslate.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_switch_languages.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_translation_failure.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_translation_request.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_full_page_telemetry_unsupported_lang.js", "browser/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_select_telemetry_multi_page.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_actor_availability.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_actor_detected_langs.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/browser_translations_actor_empty_langs.js", "toolkit/components/translations/tests/browser/shared-head.js"], "git_node": "b2e8d9111d7c1e044c14bd5262d752586b033d9f", "git_parents": ["4ebb802e96c49276fdbe8b8bbb8afbfac023b898"], "node": "d55f6f1cc4dda91e18ffbf4a6e6f0bd66f1d3ae9", "parents": ["4f267cafa35e4135c38cff8dd412f80ac4024d5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053617 - Implement remaining \"last visited\" string logic for urlbar result explanations. r=daisuke,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nThis implements the \"{n} days ago\", \"{n} weeks ago\", and \"{n} months ago\" logic\nfrom the content spec [1]. The spec isn't entirely clear on whether a week means\na calendar week or seven days, or whether a month means a calendar month or ~30\ndays.\n\nCommon usage of these words is the calendar meaning IMO, so that's what I've\nimplemented.\n\nI forgot or didn't realize that `Intl.RelativeTimeFormat` returns localized\nstrings like \"{n} days ago\". We don't need separate l10n strings for those\nafter all. Sorry for the churn.\n\n[1] https://docs.google.com/document/d/1OS54nHYSCsngEp0ybRZ6-8TQ-HSVOec5jbaVHLer_oY/edit?tab=t.k6aje44ao6nu\n\nDepends on D311478\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311787\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/SportsSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/UrlbarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_result_explanations.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/browser/browser_quicksuggest_sports.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarUtils_formatDate.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl"], "git_node": "cc76e132b048d103be1ade7c3f58bd68348387db", "git_parents": ["b2e8d9111d7c1e044c14bd5262d752586b033d9f"], "node": "114f368311406d30f9f343877571cabed4670a43", "parents": ["d55f6f1cc4dda91e18ffbf4a6e6f0bd66f1d3ae9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaditya Dhingra \u003cadhingra@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052887 - Move detekt to top level as a plugin r=geckoview-reviewers,android-reviewers,nalexander,ahochheiden\n\nUpdate the temporary detekt ktlint aliases with top-level detekt plugin. With current implementation, the mach instances are overwriting and corrupting the same objdir causing failures even without touching code. This is not caught by try as it runs subproject linters sequentially.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311097\n", "files": ["build.gradle", "gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/build.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/fenix/build.gradle", "mobile/android/focus-android/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/build.gradle", "mobile/android/focus-android/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectExtension.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/src/main/java/org/mozilla/conventions/ProjectPlugin.kt", "settings.gradle"], "git_node": "d4be754c39b634b1a2ea04b8dedae2b91ee61da5", "git_parents": ["cc76e132b048d103be1ade7c3f58bd68348387db"], "node": "2843bcafd9cc156775335c3a4d492ea433baf3ec", "parents": ["114f368311406d30f9f343877571cabed4670a43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056155 - Handle uninitialized storage in uiBusy/isLoggedIn r=dimi\n\nSince LoginManagerStorage.create() became asynchronous (bug 2042808),\nthis._storage the  synchronous uiBusy and isLoggedIn getters could threw a\nTypeError during a small window before the storage has bneen set.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312993\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/unit/test_module_LoginManager.js"], "git_node": "0665c3d10124001fc6b44d17c0ed2dc6e93b79cc", "git_parents": ["d4be754c39b634b1a2ea04b8dedae2b91ee61da5"], "node": "fec71d8cf2bdaf17945c6ca4f7a9acf2aa94b843", "parents": ["2843bcafd9cc156775335c3a4d492ea433baf3ec"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784627208, "git_changesets": ["28f8fb9edd7492f82da0a17c091d1353fcc1a2a6", "b334aa7a9c96a4763d834e5e781ee38c5cc9ea4e", "7812a95acdb9ed484d7813719bf4ab35e20b568e", "4e683092a9461dee6b550bacad6005df2d21e796", "54e504827b1989d0f8e056138ae14bda3a71628a", "146d248ceefc80f74468a5c8fa87d52953418b68", "0ef4ee9246a7cd0faf699600900928112fe30e46", "fc0a203a4c482e24ff0d950f5f3d85a3da051bf8", "e2561a2503b49666b122b4a398ca48a4d2e18ac0", "997ffd1b0f3390294a0fea96eb70bd6077e7dbce", "2593b1bad3a186ad2e8ecad35a4d349331f6fba7", "a2c4cb631990dc3ffce82aeec00211228015ef42", "cd7f1e552efbfa00f27940c7f61464d570913d23", "5e81661c86bca5f9c64e07475931c77c4c963da9", "2e51a9704a75bf262b7cc688f858446d85cf4e96", "4067426afb5e83eec2228b8df2ffc8