.com/D311370\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ml/jar.mn", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/README.md", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama-module-dev.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama-module.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama/LICENSE", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama/README.md", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama/build.sh", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama/diff.patch", "toolkit/components/ml/vendor/wllama/moz.yaml", "toolkit/content/license.html", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "12e253825393b23a9c17f8ceb2136dfdadc98aeb", "git_parents": ["28c225ed1898982a757575599f4cc037284635a2"], "node": "a77f7b4927ab176837b78d219d5adb0f780dd8d1", "parents": ["61c090c8c6c3b99abd3521f484dd899a5ff6ce3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Pollet \u003cvpollet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053830 - Part 4: Rename the wllama-text-generation task to llama-text-generation r=gregtatum,ai-platform-reviewers,flozia\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311371\n", "files": ["browser/components/genai/LinkPreviewModel.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/aboutinference/content/aboutInference.js", "toolkit/components/ml/content/ModelHub.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_cache.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_engine_e2e.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "01339ac9c32f73cfd6a5d9e1686b50a8ff65883f", "git_parents": ["12e253825393b23a9c17f8ceb2136dfdadc98aeb"], "node": "4b9dce46afe8cb26e3a4f2f334ce0377b874fc6e", "parents": ["a77f7b4927ab176837b78d219d5adb0f780dd8d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055458 - Don't trigger read barrier for assertion in NukeRemovedCrossCompartmentWrapper r=spidermonkey-reviewers,mgaudet\n\nThe read barrier can end up causing an assertion to fail because the CCW isn't\nin the wrapper map, but this is expected when calling\nNukeRemovedCrossCompartmentWrapper. The barrier isn't necessary to assert the\npointers are different.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313160\n", "files": ["js/src/proxy/BaseProxyHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "73e34a3371f221d839262613ff2a7ec9f028194d", "git_parents": ["01339ac9c32f73cfd6a5d9e1686b50a8ff65883f"], "node": "648f25e97c42a5531f040bb86c4a2006ac63fbd7", "parents": ["4b9dce46afe8cb26e3a4f2f334ce0377b874fc6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "MoHan Zhang \u003cmzhang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037171 - Load chat prompts and model+params from v2 records and add get_skill tool r=simonf,bjohns\n\nTeach PromptLoader to assemble the chat system prompt from modular v2 records\nin the ai-window-prompts Remote Settings collection. The chat params record\ncarries an ordered `modules` manifest ([{name, version}]) that drives assembly:\nbuildChatSystemPrompt reads the major-CHAT_PARAMS_MAJOR_VERSION params record\nfor the engine's model (falling back to generic), then for each manifest entry\nloads the module record at the named major version, concatenating in manifest\norder. Per-model records win over the generic fallback. There is no hardcoded\nmodule order and no v1 fallback: when the manifest is absent, or omits or can't\nresolve a required core module, buildChatSystemPrompt throws. loadPrompt's CHAT\nbranch returns the assembled body with the params version.\n\nChat is fully v2 on this branch -- there is no v1 fallback. identity and\nresponse-rules are required; if either is missing (or a manifest omits one)\nbuildChatSystemPrompt throws (clientReason \"promptLoadFailure\") rather than\nserve a partial prompt. The remaining modules are optional and are skipped\nwhen no record is published. Non-chat features are untouched and keep reading\ntheir legacy v1 records.\n\nChat model selection and inference parameters resolve from v2 as well, so the\nwhole chat runtime -- prompt and model+params -- comes from v2 with no v1/v2\nsplit. selectFeatureConfig and resolveChatModelChoice read the per-model\nkind:\"params\" records (model, model_choice_id, parameters, service_type,\npurpose) instead of the legacy v1 main-config; selectMainConfig is unchanged\nbecause a params record is a superset of the old chat config minus prompts.\nParams records version independently of the prompt at CHAT_PARAMS_MAJOR_VERSION\n(8) and carry the module manifest; the manifest is the source of truth for\nper-module versions, so adding it is an additive minor bump (8.0 -\u003e 8.1) that\nolder clients ignore. Non-chat features still resolve model+params from their\nv1 records. This relies on the v2 records (modules, skills, and params) being\npublished to the ai-window-prompts collection and the packaged dump regenerated\nbefore it rides to release -- the same dependency the v2 prompt path already has.\n\nChat `prompt_version` telemetry now reports the assembled prompt's version\n(`Conversation.systemPromptVersion`, i.e. the params/manifest version) at the\nfeedback-modal, tool-call, and manage-tabs sites, instead of the hardcoded\n`FEATURE_MAJOR_VERSIONS[CHAT]` major that no longer reflects the shipped chat\nprompt now that model+params version at CHAT_PARAMS_MAJOR_VERSION.\n\nNew PromptLoader exports: buildChatSystemPrompt, buildBrowserContextPrompt,\ngetSkillPrompt. The get_skill tool is always registered; when no skill\nrecords are published the {skill_list} placeholder renders empty and a\nget_skill call returns an \"Unknown skill\" error, so the model has nothing\nto look up. Because skill prompts are Remote Settings content, the tool\ndispatches without securityProperties and sets no trust flags (same trust\nlevel as the system prompt itself). ChatConversation.injectRealTimeContext\ncollapses to a thin wrapper around buildBrowserContextPrompt with a\nidentical to the previous turn's, we skip writing, so the prompt cache\nprefix stays stable across turns where the active tab hasn't changed.\nloadPrompt returns the same {prompt, version} shape the rest of the engine\nalready expects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D303489\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Chat.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/PromptLoader.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_get_page_content.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_prompt_loader_browser_context.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_prompt_loader_build_conversation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_prompt_loader_chat_system_prompt.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_prompt_loader_get_skill_prompt.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_tools_get_page_content.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_tools_get_skill.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_PromptLoader_buildConversation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Utils_RemoteSettings_ChatModelChoice.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-window/ai-window.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatConversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatConversation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatModelChoice.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatSwitchModel.js"], "git_node": "ab3d94761bab36103a2707915dbcc1b5b79b482e", "git_parents": ["73e34a3371f221d839262613ff2a7ec9f028194d"], "node": "d6fed30421c6f60e565c855115d2ed1987fca1bc", "parents": ["648f25e97c42a5531f040bb86c4a2006ac63fbd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056372: Add barriers to component core instances. r=jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313230\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/components/bug2056372.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmComponent.h"], "git_node": "5d20d2ac7c964b889f5a77b86044e69b2708272e", "git_parents": ["ab3d94761bab36103a2707915dbcc1b5b79b482e"], "node": "d337b07b4da55899bb836afedbcac10799004daf", "parents": ["d6fed30421c6f60e565c855115d2ed1987fca1bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042193 - Move per-window state in RenderBackend into a dedicated WindowState struct. r=gw\n\nIntroduces a private `WindowState` struct that owns the fields previously\nheld directly on `RenderBackend`: `result_tx`, `notifier`, `sampler`,\n`resource_cache`, `chunk_pool`, `tile_caches`, `frame_config`,\n`default_compositor_kind`, `debug_flags`, `recycler`, `frame_publish_id`,\nand the cfg-gated `capture_config` / `loaded_resource_sequence_id`.\n\n`RenderBackend` now holds:\n- `windows: FastHashMap\u003cWindowId, WindowState\u003e` (always one entry today,\n  keyed by `WINDOW_ID_DEFAULT`)\n- `document_to_window: FastHashMap\u003cDocumentId, WindowId\u003e`, populated and\n  cleared at `AddDocument` / `DeleteDocument` / `ClearNamespace` /\n  `documents.clear()` sites.\n\nNo behavior change. This is foundation work so that a later step can let\nmultiple windows share a single render backend thread, with a fixed pool\nof threads round-robining over windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302353\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs"], "git_node": "3bd9941eb3f52fd64b1486a391c0bce2358f69b1", "git_parents": ["5d20d2ac7c964b889f5a77b86044e69b2708272e"], "node": "a8282230fd2e702826864bb967d437b63daab25f", "parents": ["d337b07b4da55899bb836afedbcac10799004daf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042193 - Introduce RenderBackendId and route per-window state through it. r=gw\n\nAdds a public `RenderBackendId(u32)` type in `webrender_api`. Each\n`RenderApi` / `RenderApiSender` now carries the id of the window it\ntargets, and `AddDocument` carries that id so the backend can install\nthe document under the right window.\n\n`RenderBackend::new` is reduced to the global-only state. The\nper-window state (`WindowState`) is installed via a new\n`register_window(WindowRegistration)` method called directly from the\nspawn closure in `renderer::init`. `register_window` also takes over\n`sampler.register()`. `unregister_window` mirrors it and is exposed\nvia a new `ApiMsg::UnregisterWindow(RenderBackendId)` variant.\n\nWindows are now keyed by `RenderBackendId`; the placeholder\n`WINDOW_ID_DEFAULT` from the previous step is gone. Run-loop\nshutdown drains all registered windows so it tolerates having zero\nor many of them. No behavior change for the existing one-window\ncase: a fresh id is allocated per webrender instance and registered\nbefore the backend's message loop starts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302354\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_api.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "19e86ad5e6b76b26b856e8ea043d380b51d7480f", "git_parents": ["3bd9941eb3f52fd64b1486a391c0bce2358f69b1"], "node": "92921aef4bbf15562b67946b54d4c87d7c825679", "parents": ["a8282230fd2e702826864bb967d437b63daab25f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042193 - Add RenderBackendPool and let multiple windows share a backend thread. r=gw\n\nAdds a `RenderBackendPool` that owns a configurable number of\n(render-backend, scene-builder, low-priority-scene-builder) thread\ntriples and assigns windows to them round-robin. A new\n`WebRenderOptions::render_backend_pool` lets callers supply a shared\npool; when each rende backend has its own pool of size 1, which is\nfunctionally equivalent to the previous one-backend-per-window setup.\n\nDefault behavior is preserved: one window per backend, scene builders\n1:1 with backend threads.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302355\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/debugger.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_api.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend_pool.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtest.rs"], "git_node": "edfc3055ca4641d7e4edf8ef76872195b82f7c85", "git_parents": ["19e86ad5e6b76b26b856e8ea043d380b51d7480f"], "node": "a7f1793a7983deadf4d26370c4c05f1fe2722789", "parents": ["92921aef4bbf15562b67946b54d4c87d7c825679"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042193 - Plumb the WebRender render-backend pool into Gecko. r=gw\n\nAdds the FFI surface for `RenderBackendPool` and wires it into the GPU\nprocess so Gecko can opt in to a shared pool of WebRender backend\nthreads. The behavior is gated behind the new pref\n`gfx.webrender.render-backend-thread-count`:\n\n- `0` (default): each window keeps its own private backend thread,\n  identical to the previous behavior.\n- `N \u003e= 1`: `RenderThread` constructs a single shared pool of N backend\n  threads at startup and every window assigned to it round-robins to\n  one of those threads.\n\nNew FFI:\n- `wr_render_backend_pool_new(size, size_of_op, enclosing_size_of_op)`\n  allocates a fresh font namespace and builds a `RenderBackendPool`\n  whose scene builders all share that namespace; this keeps font-key\n  lookups consistent across windows on the same pool.\n- `wr_render_backend_pool_delete` for shutdown.\n- `wr_window_new` gains a new `render_backend_pool` argument forwarded\n  to `WebRenderOptions::render_backend_pool`.\n\nThe opaque pool struct nests its `Arc\u003cRenderBackendPool\u003e` + font\nnamespace inside a private inner type so cbindgen exports the outer\n`WrRenderBackendPool` as a true forward declaration, matching the\nexisting `WrChunkPool` pattern.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302356\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderThread.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderThread.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/init.rs", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "a613fa40d1163705f794c023abb9f6e3b4dc1fa1", "git_parents": ["edfc3055ca4641d7e4edf8ef76872195b82f7c85"], "node": "ec63d071e3da4edbc537083401f54f29ef2645ad", "parents": ["a7f1793a7983deadf4d26370c4c05f1fe2722789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042193 - Improve the logic that records scene build times for telemetry. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe previous version took the first recorded scene build time in the list of transactions (there is usually only one but it's still an odd/arbitrary choice) and sent it to telemetry with millisecond resolution. The new version walks all all timings and sends the worst one with nano-second resolution.\n\nThis may change a bit what we observe in telemetry. I don't think that picking the worst time will actuall change much in practice because we rarely oor never have multiple scene builds, but the higher resolution should make the signal look a bit different and hopefully more useful.\nSince we were truncating at the millisecond granularity, the signal on telemetry will probably look about half a millisecond worse on average even though real timings won't actually have changed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302865\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs"], "git_node": "b3c2aa56cb94040838929e7336cc41abc16302c9", "git_parents": ["a613fa40d1163705f794c023abb9f6e3b4dc1fa1"], "node": "2bbccc6a0e73a9f769137794f6a9e0ef7cc17a1b", "parents": ["ec63d071e3da4edbc537083401f54f29ef2645ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042193: apply code formatting via Lando\n\n# ignore-this-changeset\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderThread.cpp"], "git_node": "a8674405815aea57c440a9c7cf0170b99f92dc4b", "git_parents": ["b3c2aa56cb94040838929e7336cc41abc16302c9"], "node": "4a5b3b102f0349b1361faf3c5ada0797043cca4a", "parents": ["2bbccc6a0e73a9f769137794f6a9e0ef7cc17a1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "SaaSha Pina \u003csaasha@heysparkbox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1988226 - Create --icon-size-xxlarge that points to --size-item-xlarge. r=jules\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311612\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/UITour.css", "browser/themes/shared/controlcenter/panel.css", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/privatebrowsing/aboutPrivateBrowsing.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/commonDialog.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-figma-primitives.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/icon.tokens.json"], "git_node": "260340749e50a9eeef38b8dad589930bd00927f3", "git_parents": ["a8674405815aea57c440a9c7cf0170b99f92dc4b"], "node": "d9cc4a346d602f2c9aa381edeb70a61461d4690b", "parents": ["4a5b3b102f0349b1361faf3c5ada0797043cca4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021718 - Add CumulativeAverage\u003cT\u003e template to mfbt r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nSeveral media classes maintain running averages with local formulas.\nAdd CumulativeAverage\u003cT\u003e, which uses the online mean recurrence without\nan overflow-prone sum or a growing mean * count product.\n\nReject integral T because division truncates and unsigned counts corrupt\nnegative deltas. For built-in floating types, scale operands only when\ntheir direct difference would overflow; otherwise retain the more\naccurate single-difference update.\n\nAdd mfbt unit coverage for normal values, finite extremes, subnormals,\nreset, and user-defined arithmetic types.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286540\n", "files": ["mfbt/CumulativeAverage.h", "mfbt/moz.build", "mfbt/tests/TestCumulativeAverage.cpp", "mfbt/tests/moz.build", "testing/cppunittest.toml"], "git_node": "e88a7963ca58e719389c71bb1cf66354853568c6", "git_parents": ["260340749e50a9eeef38b8dad589930bd00927f3"], "node": "e0f83d7ae72e4ffc2ca6914c64bfbf2ad07b7758", "parents": ["d9cc4a346d602f2c9aa381edeb70a61461d4690b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021718 - Use CumulativeAverage for MediaFormatReader mMeanRate r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nReplace MediaFormatReader's local running-average class with\nCumulativeAverage\u003cdouble\u003e. A double accumulator avoids narrowing frame\nrates before the update and matches the double videoRate debug field;\nthe decoder hint remains explicitly converted to float.\n\nThis preserves mean(1 / duration), including the existing duplicate\nfirst-frame accounting. The variable-rate correctness issue is tracked\nby Bug 2055649.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286541\n", "files": ["dom/media/MediaFormatReader.cpp", "dom/media/MediaFormatReader.h"], "git_node": "9061a992d57211866439b5b898a2583854b38827", "git_parents": ["e88a7963ca58e719389c71bb1cf66354853568c6"], "node": "422892a8c0b184e8b05b9eaca68b434e8e6b761e", "parents": ["e0f83d7ae72e4ffc2ca6914c64bfbf2ad07b7758"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021718 - Extract FFmpegDecodeStats from FFmpegVideoDecoder r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nMove DecodeStats out of FFmpegVideoDecoder so its slow-decode and reset\nbehavior can be tested directly.\n\nCompile it through ffvpx/moz.build so the symbols are available on all\nplatforms, including Windows and Android, which use mozffvpx only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286542\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecodeStats.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecodeStats.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.h", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/ffvpx/moz.build"], "git_node": "54ad10795ac5122275daa6c1704881f752f47a29", "git_parents": ["9061a992d57211866439b5b898a2583854b38827"], "node": "13b647ffebedf08c0124ef2c0d4e26150971e555", "parents": ["422892a8c0b184e8b05b9eaca68b434e8e6b761e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021718 - Add gtest for FFmpegDecodeStats r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nCover the late-frame threshold, transition to slow decoding, reset after\nsustained on-time playback, and rejection of zero-duration samples.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286543\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestFFmpegDecodeStats.cpp", "dom/media/gtest/moz.build", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecodeStats.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecodeStats.h"], "git_node": "1171455b2183dc5774ee62eebbdd27d6675b8695", "git_parents": ["54ad10795ac5122275daa6c1704881f752f47a29"], "node": "184a26e2a0888ec8c15039b176b4fe2c3a8969c6", "parents": ["13b647ffebedf08c0124ef2c0d4e26150971e555"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021718 - Use CumulativeAverage in FFmpegVideoDecoder DecodeStats r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nReplace DecodeStats' product-based running averages with\nCumulativeAverage\u003cdouble\u003e. The online recurrence avoids the growing\nmean * frame-count intermediate while retaining double precision.\n\nUse CumulativeAverage::count() in place of the duplicate decoded-frame\ncounter.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D286544\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecodeStats.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegDecodeStats.h"], "git_node": "259fd4fd2a5fa81d40aa0be6dd75186e8c532106", "git_parents": ["1171455b2183dc5774ee62eebbdd27d6675b8695"], "node": "e03b43ec08084c7e23dba7025fc1de73123ddd54", "parents": ["184a26e2a0888ec8c15039b176b4fe2c3a8969c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056361 - Consolidate verbatim-duplicated shard/label/bootstrap helpers in ui/efficiency navigation factories r=aaronmt\n\nPure refactor, no behavior change. Extracts loadShard(), toDisplayLabel(),\nand the near-identical XGraphBootstrap.ensureInitialized() implementations\n(previously duplicated across the reachability/pairs/interaction/behavior\nnavigation generator domains) into single shared implementations under\nnavigation/planning/. No package moves, no public API changes. Verified via\ngrep that no duplicate definitions remain; full local UI test suite run to\nconfirm no regressions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313061\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/behavior/BehaviorCaseFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/behavior/BehaviorCaseGenerator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/behavior/BehaviorGraphBootstrap.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/behavior/BehaviorShardData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/interaction/InteractionShardData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/interaction/InteractionTestPlanner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/pairs/NavigationPairCaseFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/pairs/NavigationPairGraphBootstrap.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/pairs/NavigationPairShardData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/DisplayLabels.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/NavigationGraphBootstrap.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/NavigationTestPlanner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/ShardUtils.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/NavigationCaseFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/NavigationShardData.kt"], "git_node": "7e2b7494d3a3b018e25876f61b509f1ff124b0b0", "git_parents": ["259fd4fd2a5fa81d40aa0be6dd75186e8c532106"], "node": "d9e0e66e8769a00058658294f05c3b5ee5806e10", "parents": ["e03b43ec08084c7e23dba7025fc1de73123ddd54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056374 - Split dev-tool output computation from emission in ui/efficiency navigation generators r=aaronmt\n\nBehavior-preserving refactor of the framework's local dev-tools (Navigation/\nInteraction/Behavior case generators + the reachability plan logger). Each\nnow returns a plain DevToolReport (list of lines, no side effects) via a new\nbuild*Report() function; a thin log*() wrapper emits it through a new shared\nlogReport() helper. The three boilerplate-printing tools share a new\nbuildBoilerplateReport() helper for their identical header/separator/\nper-item/separator shape.\n\nEarly groundwork for eventually hooking these dev-tools into something\nother than logcat (a dev-tools UI, possibly an MCP surface for AI agents) -\nnot committed to in this diff, just why the split is shaped this way.\n\nNo file moves/renames here; that's deferred to land with the P2b-4\nnavigation/ reorg. All public function signatures unchanged, so examples/\ncall sites are unaffected. Full local UI test suite run to confirm no\nregressions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313071\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/behavior/BehaviorCaseGenerator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/interaction/InteractionCaseGenerator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/DevToolReport.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/NavigationCaseGenerator.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/planning/NavigationTestPlannerLogger.kt"], "git_node": "378be15efd69b39a107cb8ced54ce627a897953d", "git_parents": ["7e2b7494d3a3b018e25876f61b509f1ff124b0b0"], "node": "aeaa774904b8a21c0ff8f41b138362f6b2503d52", "parents": ["d9e0e66e8769a00058658294f05c3b5ee5806e10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056405 - Move ui/efficiency's reachability generator files into the new generation/ package structure r=aaronmt\n\nPure move/rename, no logic changes. First of four per-domain diffs for P2b-4\n(pairs, interaction, behavior to follow in separate diffs). Drops the\nredundant \"Navigation\" prefix now that the package name disambiguates:\n\nnavigation/reachability/NavigationCase.kt        -\u003e generation/reachability/ReachabilityCase.kt\nnavigation/reachability/NavigationCaseFactory.kt -\u003e generation/reachability/ReachabilityCaseFactory.kt\nnavigation/reachability/NavigationShardData.kt   -\u003e generation/reachability/ReachabilityShardData.kt\nnavigation/reachability/BaseNavigationShardTest.kt -\u003e generation/reachability/BaseReachabilityShardTest.kt\nnavigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard01-20.kt -\u003e generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard01-20.kt\n\nUpdates arm-experimental-api-tests.yml's Flank package path in the same\ndiff (standing gotcha: any diff moving reachability/ or pairs/ shards must\nupdate this or CI silently stops running them).\n\nConfirmed via grep this move is self-contained - nothing outside\nnavigation/reachability/ imports it. Deliberately left ShardUtils,\nNavigationTestPlanner, and toDisplayLabel imported from their current\nnavigation.planning location; promoting those (used by all four domains)\nis a separate diff, not bundled here. Verified locally: builds and runs\nclean with the old files removed.\n\nThis is P2b-4 (MTE-5686), Phase 2b (MTE-5652).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313095\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/BaseReachabilityShardTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/ReachabilityCase.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/ReachabilityCaseFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/ReachabilityShardData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard01.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard02.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard03.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard04.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard05.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard06.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard07.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard08.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard09.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard10.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard11.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard12.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard13.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard14.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard15.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard16.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard17.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard18.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard19.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/reachability/shards/ReachabilityShard20.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/BaseNavigationShardTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/NavigationCase.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/NavigationCaseFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/NavigationShardData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard01.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard02.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard03.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard04.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard05.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard06.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard07.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard08.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard09.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard10.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard11.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard12.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard13.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard14.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard15.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard16.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard17.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard18.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard19.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/reachability/shards/NavigationReachabilityShard20.kt", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-tae-tests.yml", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm64-v8a-detect-leaks.yml", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm64-v8a.yml"], "git_node": "831f643561190fcc12aff6f9082532b91b633717", "git_parents": ["378be15efd69b39a107cb8ced54ce627a897953d"], "node": "215a4688c80426fccde6c0e518dea2a37a96c696", "parents": ["aeaa774904b8a21c0ff8f41b138362f6b2503d52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056411 - Move ui/efficiency's pairs generator files into the new generation/ package structure r=aaronmt\n\nPure move/rename, no logic changes. Second of four per-domain diffs for\nP2b-4 (reachability landed first; interaction and behavior to follow).\nDrops the redundant \"Navigation\" prefix, keeping \"Pair\" singular to match\nwhat the classes already used:\n\nnavigation/pairs/NavigationPairCase.kt          -\u003e generation/pairs/PairCase.kt\nnavigation/pairs/NavigationPairCaseFactory.kt   -\u003e generation/pairs/PairCaseFactory.kt\nnavigation/pairs/NavigationPairShardData.kt     -\u003e generation/pairs/PairShardData.kt\nnavigation/pairs/BaseNavigationPairShardTest.kt -\u003e generation/pairs/BasePairShardTest.kt\nnavigation/pairs/shards/NavigationPairShard01-20.kt -\u003e generation/pairs/shards/PairShard01-20.kt\n\nNo Flank config change - pairs shards aren't wired into CI yet (separate,\nalready-tracked gap, P3-3).\n\nAlso: removed a stale unused import of NavigationPairCaseFactory from\nexamples/NavigationRegistryLoggingTest.kt (would have become a broken\nreference otherwise), and updated two KDoc comments in\nnavigation/planning/{DisplayLabels,ShardUtils}.kt that named the old\nclass by its pre-move name (comment-only, no code change).\n\nConfirmed via grep this move is self-contained aside from the one stale\nimport above. ShardUtils/NavigationTestPlanner/toDisplayLabel/\nNavigationGraphBootstrap promotion out of navigation.planning remains a\nseparate diff, same as the reachability move. Verified locally: builds\nand runs clean with the old files removed.\n\nThis is P2b-4 (MTE-5686), Phase 2b (MTE-5652).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313098\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/examples/NavigationRegistryLoggingTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/BasePairShardTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/PairCase.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/PairCaseFactory.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/PairShardData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/shards/PairShard01.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/shards/PairShard02.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/shards/PairShard03.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/shards/PairShard04.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/shards/PairShard05.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/generation/pairs/shards/PairShard06.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/s