 iframe's parent matches the browsing context, r=NeilDeakin,credential-management-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312950\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7a2abdbf091719a781cdcfdb7ea01dce2a48b9ff", "git_parents": ["f189951e3efb03f5846869170f8cfe79fa6e34d8"], "node": "a65d3c8dd83c746fd6df9da64c9e91d74086b37e", "parents": ["81e16b8b160978895af87d9470e428747b0f3331"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054776 - Validate form history entries in FormHistoryParent. r=NeilDeakin,credential-management-reviewers\n\nMove the form history entry checks into FormHistory and apply them in\nFormHistoryParent for the submit, autocomplete search and remove paths,\nin addition to the existing checks in FormHistoryChild.\n\nThe checks are applied by the actor that receives these messages.\nFormHistory.update is intentionally left unchanged so in-process callers\nsuch as the search bar continue to manage their own history directly.\nAutocomplete results are still scoped by fieldname only, so form history\nvisibility across origins is unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313170\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/satchel/FormHistory.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/FormHistoryChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/satchel/FormHistoryParent.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "c4147681c178b9a2f8093d623e990578d710a70a", "git_parents": ["7a2abdbf091719a781cdcfdb7ea01dce2a48b9ff"], "node": "3f967c44c0d474064771a9dd450c340bdd2669a8", "parents": ["a65d3c8dd83c746fd6df9da64c9e91d74086b37e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052520 - Don't suggest importing logins when Firefox already has a saved login for the origin. r=credential-management-reviewers,mtigley\n\nThe \"Import your login from Chrome\" autocomplete suggestion was shown even\nwhen Firefox already had a saved login for the site, if that login had an\nempty username. The import gate reused the display-filtered autocomplete\nmatch list, which deliberately drops empty-username logins on username\nfields, so the existing login was invisible to the \"no saved logins\" check.\n\nMove the existing-login awareness into the importable descriptor:\ngetImportableLogins() now receives the full deduped set of saved logins for\nthe origin and only returns an \"import\" state when that set is empty. Both\ncall sites pass the unfiltered logins list. The now-redundant !logins.length\nguard in the result builder is removed since the descriptor authoritatively\ngates the import row.\n\nAlso add a regression test covering the empty-username case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313168\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginAutoComplete.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/LoginManagerParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/passwordmgr/test/browser/browser_autocomplete_import.js"], "git_node": "e03e67513b50fd2788fa1dcc19392cfd223de340", "git_parents": ["c4147681c178b9a2f8093d623e990578d710a70a"], "node": "b15b08c4d0826dabf4eb8fd9b76e54bf64ebfa8d", "parents": ["3f967c44c0d474064771a9dd450c340bdd2669a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052797 - P1. Implement Passport capture doorhanger r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,credential-management-reviewers,mtigley,bolsson,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310577\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/popup-notifications.inc.xhtml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/content/editPassport.xhtml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_passport_capture_doorhanger.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/fixtures/autocomplete_passport_basic.html", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/fixtures/autocomplete_passport_combined_date.html", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/fixtures/autocomplete_passport_split_name.html", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/confirmationHints.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/formAutofill.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/formautofill-notification.css", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/PassportRecord.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "97acb53c83656c1a6edb46f0e36854613eeb83e5", "git_parents": ["e03e67513b50fd2788fa1dcc19392cfd223de340"], "node": "4646f3a848c2eafffdeaba9ae7db4d752b27f884", "parents": ["b15b08c4d0826dabf4eb8fd9b76e54bf64ebfa8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052797 - P2. Merge promptToSave{Address,CreditCard,Passport} into a single config-driven promptToSave r=NeilDeakin,credential-management-reviewers\n\nThe three doorhanger entry points were near-identical. Replace them with a\nsingle promptToSave(type, ...) driven by a per-type config table so adding a\nnew data type only requires a new entry. The update-vs-add decision and the\noptional edit sub-flow are preserved for each type.\n\nThe per-type confirmation-hint l10n ids are folded into the same config table\n(replacing the separate messageIdMap and the storageType field), so a new type\nis described in exactly one place.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310609\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/android/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillPrompter.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7030386410140c6025f263370104d38879d3a113", "git_parents": ["97acb53c83656c1a6edb46f0e36854613eeb83e5"], "node": "d4e2e7ff6ce0018551f02f51ea6ed932500ebe69", "parents": ["4646f3a848c2eafffdeaba9ae7db4d752b27f884"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Train \u003caaron.train@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041220 - Scroll Quit Firefox menu item into view before clicking to fix intermittent SettingsDeleteBrowsingDataOnQuitTest failures r=jajohnson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313294\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/MainMenuSelectors.kt"], "git_node": "4296aea7ed85100c8010b0a35a9a18801a347568", "git_parents": ["7030386410140c6025f263370104d38879d3a113"], "node": "455283040b855325a0ad54390400f73e13eb9d8d", "parents": ["d4e2e7ff6ce0018551f02f51ea6ed932500ebe69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "KS \u003ckshampur@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051202 - Fix macOS CaR builds failing due to vpython changes r=aglavic\n\nThis patch addresses a few things. First, recent upstream changes to\ndepot_tools/vpython created an issue in resolving package dependencies\ndue to  looking for packages pinned in chrome's artifact registry and\ninternal pypi. Here chrome AR is explicitly used to grab the packages\nand transitive dependencies.\n\nSecondly, vpython is overridden by using `uv` to provide a guaranteed\naarch64 mac python version since the current internal toolchains are x64\nand system python is too old. This prevents gclient sync from fetching\nx64 dependencies due to the x64 python triggering rosetta.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313254\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/misc.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-custom-car.sh"], "git_node": "ab1b35537a232073fa2addaf30255ef0c7c20b25", "git_parents": ["4296aea7ed85100c8010b0a35a9a18801a347568"], "node": "1027b7c3d6e285d1484a684c80467a45c31c1326", "parents": ["455283040b855325a0ad54390400f73e13eb9d8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Matthew Tighe \u003cmatthewdtighe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052276 - Enable S2S by default r=android-reviewers,nalexander\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310116\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/nimbus.fml.yaml"], "git_node": "97fad1b3575bb9a84105bc055c0d6d80cefa35d0", "git_parents": ["ab1b35537a232073fa2addaf30255ef0c7c20b25"], "node": "8cb34566d9841770c07280735f38b751aa9d4fec", "parents": ["1027b7c3d6e285d1484a684c80467a45c31c1326"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ted Campbell \u003ctcampbell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043618 - Cleanup timing of EdgeToEdgeFragmentLifecycleCallbacks r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nWe had previously delayed registration until after the SplashScreen as\ndismissed, but fragments may be rendering underneath already. Instead, do this\n_before_ the `setContent` call. This must happen after call `setupTheme`. Since\nwe explicitly do `setupTheme` early, we no longer have to worry about timing of\nthe splash-screen toggling themes.\n\nNote that for ExternalAppBrowserActivity the `setupTheme` is a no-op, but we\nalso do not set the SplashScreenTheme on that activity so a switch isn't needed.\n\nSimplify the EdgeToEdgeFragmentLifecycleCallbacks.register method since we now\ncan assume it happens before any fragments are added to activity.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313149\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/e2e/EdgeToEdgeFragmentLifecycleCallbacks.kt"], "git_node": "99bc1e118eb1983682b211fc4c7f806c30597531", "git_parents": ["97fad1b3575bb9a84105bc055c0d6d80cefa35d0"], "node": "f874dad9e1e56de6691e662dac32297d8f7e99c6", "parents": ["8cb34566d9841770c07280735f38b751aa9d4fec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Ritter \u003ctom@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1983119: Remove all security events from legacy telemetry r=chutten\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D261142\n", "files": ["dom/metrics.yaml", "dom/security/metrics.yaml", "modules/libpref/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Events.yaml"], "git_node": "7e0a7b92c817018775e4b8176b8913b4de2a9feb", "git_parents": ["99bc1e118eb1983682b211fc4c7f806c30597531"], "node": "079851c7394830b1e1ebbc607891b1fac6ff81bb", "parents": ["f874dad9e1e56de6691e662dac32297d8f7e99c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048353 - Improve worker shutdown support in CookieStoreNotificationWatcher r=manuel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311765\n", "files": ["dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreNotificationWatcherWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "74e007f613c15ee7aec92992f0abfd3b7e2254d7", "git_parents": ["7e0a7b92c817018775e4b8176b8913b4de2a9feb"], "node": "c73c5600a962e0b4cdf6d558b7d20b77a237a7d1", "parents": ["079851c7394830b1e1ebbc607891b1fac6ff81bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055730 [wpt PR 61346] - Reflect the \u003cfieldset checkable\u003e attribute., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nReflect the \u003cfieldset checkable\u003e attribute.\n\nThis is conditioned on MenuElements being enabled.\n\nThis aligns with how I specified the checkable attribute's reflection on\nthe menu-elements branch in\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/3373ac0401fb3e8546d976d0e079bb63b780bf48\nwhich uses a nullable DOMString, similar to HTMLLinkElement.crossOrigin.\n\nBug: 406566432\nChange-Id: I8127ea3c00e9d11db62c8897e86aa4f45a1bdc6d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8102343\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663189}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a6d7bef6711c5d46187eeb2ac57bf909d9390061\nwpt-pr: 61346\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/html-menu-elements.tentative.idl"], "git_node": "e5a0f50131fcd873feba9e0ec2109ae4adc32cec", "git_parents": ["74e007f613c15ee7aec92992f0abfd3b7e2254d7"], "node": "d6c130167e7d77599283f292c721c2b7d1aae651", "parents": ["c73c5600a962e0b4cdf6d558b7d20b77a237a7d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055730 [wpt PR 61346] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61346\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/idlharness.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "db881a77cc33eecf0a1c93146f9de4a92745a525", "git_parents": ["e5a0f50131fcd873feba9e0ec2109ae4adc32cec"], "node": "37e6d7a5178defc02fe55a692360b7a51f0034f8", "parents": ["d6c130167e7d77599283f292c721c2b7d1aae651"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jingyun Liu \u003cjingyun@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055732 [wpt PR 61347] - Remove classifier API related code now that the API is deprecated., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove classifier API related code now that the API is deprecated.\n\nRemove:\n- blink, IDL\n- browser, unittests\n- wpt tests\n\nBug: 527960113\nChange-Id: I521dcc530b42af9d11779b018ce01aae2cadd0b2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8091535\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dave Tapuska \u003cdtapuska@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jingyun Liu \u003cjingyun@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mustafa Emre Acer \u003cmeacer@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663256}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9eac15a0cd90ec22099204d418fb8fed83a88565\nwpt-pr: 61347\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/classifier/classifier-abort.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/classifier/classifier-availability.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/classifier/classifier-classify-post-abort.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/classifier/classifier-classify.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/classifier/classifier-create-available.tentative.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/ai/classifier/classifier-create.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "4c3ef769b07345466ca63bcc04a65373d60f6586", "git_parents": ["db881a77cc33eecf0a1c93146f9de4a92745a525"], "node": "8600247f69142183e861e8923d6b206de75ec73d", "parents": ["37e6d7a5178defc02fe55a692360b7a51f0034f8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Lee \u003cjonathan-j-lee@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055739 [wpt PR 61351] - Fix sequential focus starting point for slot elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix sequential focus starting point for slot elements (#61351)\n\nThis patch fixes the resulting sequential focus starting point in the\ncase that the currently focused element is being slotted and then gets\nremoved. Without this patch, sequential focus gets reset to the start of\nthe document, and with this patch it goes to the next element it would\nhave gone to if the element never got removed.\n\nThis fix makes us match the behavior in firefox and safari.\n\nAlso fixed a crash in FixupRemovedNodeAcrossShadowBoundary by checking\nif the node being removed is immediately before the range boundary.\n\nFixed: 512749482\nChange-Id: I9a997ea269ebcac69270a5bc9bf63957148e79a2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7853014\nCommit-Queue: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1658892}\n\nCo-authored-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 2671397aa7fcbd68a00b6fe82cff36d6468facf6\nwpt-pr: 61351\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/sequential-focus-navigation-starting-point.tentative.html"], "git_node": "992256c10d46b8aabf053d7a0ab140a71e0abd2c", "git_parents": ["4c3ef769b07345466ca63bcc04a65373d60f6586"], "node": "f50fc566c5c88ff1b744fe1bbee46383cf781d79", "parents": ["8600247f69142183e861e8923d6b206de75ec73d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mahesh Bharadwaj Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055432 [wpt PR 61327] - [WebAudio] Implement AudioWorkletNode lifetime fix (part 2 of 2), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Implement AudioWorkletNode lifetime fix (part 2 of 2)\n\nThis CL implements the spec-compliant lifetime logic for\nAudioWorkletNode.\n\nSpecifically:\n- We track the active source flag of the processor.\n- In AudioWorkletHandler::Process(), we check if there are active\n  connected inputs. If the active source flag is false and there are no\n  active inputs, we terminate the processor early and skip JS execution.\n- We resolve a thread-safety hazard by pre-binding a WeakPtr to the\n  handler on the main thread and copying it on the audio thread.\n- We refactor the cleanup and input connection checks into private\n  helpers for better readability and style.\n- We pass nullptr to inputs when they are disconnected to remain spec-\n  compliant (0 channels in JS).\n- We fix a boundary-stopping delay in AudioScheduledSourceHandler to\n  ensure source nodes finish immediately when scheduled to stop on a\n  quantum boundary, resolving a 1-quantum lag in downstream\n  disconnection.\n- We fix a DCHECK failure in AudioScheduledSourceHandler by restricting\n  zeroing to strictly less than quantum end.\n- We make the zero-output-processor.js test processor robust against\n  0-channel inputs when disconnected.\n- We remove the expected failure baseline for the WPT test as it now\n  passes completely.\n\nBug: 41435286\nTest: third_party/blink/web_tests/external/wpt/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletnode-lifetime.https.html\nChange-Id: I6499feddbb119c3220781bfd8561dc241ffcf37b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8093149\nCommit-Queue: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Michael Wilson \u003cmjwilson@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663226}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 465597159515e4768fd8296900985cf5f7de3ef5\nwpt-pr: 61327\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/processors/zero-output-processor.js"], "git_node": "98c6e5cff7b099f7d7a3f826792d28bbe70225e8", "git_parents": ["992256c10d46b8aabf053d7a0ab140a71e0abd2c"], "node": "0a6e8c207f5b7aa1b9c64a627fe6eaf63ec58144", "parents": ["f50fc566c5c88ff1b744fe1bbee46383cf781d79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055432 [wpt PR 61327] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61327\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-audioworklet-interface/audioworkletprocessor-unconnected-outputs.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "49514e8ea7812975b15f03004ccdb3abcc919b58", "git_parents": ["98c6e5cff7b099f7d7a3f826792d28bbe70225e8"], "node": "7a616f20f64d260c6122e61ba74a7b3de2e3ea5d", "parents": ["0a6e8c207f5b7aa1b9c64a627fe6eaf63ec58144"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055734 [wpt PR 61348] - [compression-dictionary] Check that invalid URLs neither trigger any load/error event nor any fetch request., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Check that invalid URLs neither trigger any load/error event nor any fetch request.\n\n\"create a link request\" for an invalid URL returns null per\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/#create-a-link-request\n\nso \"load a compression dictionary\" should return early per\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11620\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: Id2f37d8c578a585200b88574ef1262048b98ded3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8084469\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663433}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fe2e38df0b44dee73701b8fa7b4e3b56ccd8dced\nwpt-pr: 61348\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-element-invalid-url.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "e04ab1d4da910195e2f2a3192af50af1cb82664c", "git_parents": ["49514e8ea7812975b15f03004ccdb3abcc919b58"], "node": "134f5e7b7aa52a92769becd4dbbc4c2f2233e4d6", "parents": ["7a616f20f64d260c6122e61ba74a7b3de2e3ea5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055740 [wpt PR 61352] - [compression-dictionary] Align crossorigin handling with the spec PR., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Align crossorigin handling with the spec PR.\n\nPer https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11620, if crossorigin is\n\"No Cors\" we should default to Anonymous. Currently, Chromium departs\nfrom the spec and always forces request's mode to \"cors\" and request's\ncredentials to \"omit\". This CL aligns Chromium's behavior on the spec PR\nunder a runtime flag and adds corresponding WPT test.\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: I30835aebc9df79b59e74747b0729efbc6df69457\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8098207\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663435}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: babeec89975126bd1a6d29b75f6285dc23ae64fd\nwpt-pr: 61352\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-element-crossorigin.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/dummy", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/empty.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/fetch-options-worker.js"], "git_node": "34154a585254eebf7e5c3ff68e53dae77d18462f", "git_parents": ["e04ab1d4da910195e2f2a3192af50af1cb82664c"], "node": "31ce33ef3d3674d2cf1d4243214d83c8e50aa8c4", "parents": ["134f5e7b7aa52a92769becd4dbbc4c2f2233e4d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Lulejian \u003cjlulejian@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055752 [wpt PR 61353] - [Extensions][WPT] Remove check for nonexistent `dataTypes` property., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Extensions][WPT] Remove check for nonexistent `dataTypes` property.\n\nbrowser.browsingData.settings().dataTypes does not exist, it was\nmistakenly added in a previous commit.\n\nBug: 527385398\nChange-Id: I727866f2296e3a98c38cd0a1f39619a978b11e36\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8109018\nCommit-Queue: Justin Lulejian \u003cjlulejian@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Oliver Dunk \u003coliverdunk@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Justin Lulejian \u003cjlulejian@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Oliver Dunk \u003coliverdunk@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663468}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e9ef0755e1a01a5e819ef4050c0aaffbd8345257\nwpt-pr: 61353\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/web-extensions/resources/browsingData/background.js"], "git_node": "012cf22a365dddeb41c7375f01807efae2b9276c", "git_parents": ["34154a585254eebf7e5c3ff68e53dae77d18462f"], "node": "232387bcab0186a017e53a6f4820dfc25ccac419", "parents": ["31ce33ef3d3674d2cf1d4243214d83c8e50aa8c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055755 [wpt PR 61355] - Invalidate when EffectiveAppearance changes., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInvalidate when EffectiveAppearance changes.\n\nIt's possible for EffectiveAppearance to change when there are no other\nstyle changes, for example when a new author style is added but that\nstyle doesn't change the CSS computed style.  Since EffectiveAppearance\nis what affects rendering (rather than appearance), we should invalidate\nfor it instead of appearance.\n\nFixed: 534166365\nChange-Id: I41309adba32b25feb5a8a5537f81da15a6a0ce0c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8103430\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663476}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3eb52783facf7e3abd55fc943521f6134015cb97\nwpt-pr: 61355\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/appearance-invalidate-author-styling-001-notref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/appearance-invalidate-author-styling-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/appearance-invalidate-author-styling-001.html"], "git_node": "6c0b8c68400659362f8b10d91bfe2a1621c55fae", "git_parents": ["012cf22a365dddeb41c7375f01807efae2b9276c"], "node": "2a4da3eb963c47e6e1fa87b62533285bf2bb9c68", "parents": ["232387bcab0186a017e53a6f4820dfc25ccac419"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055759 [wpt PR 61357] - [OpaqueRange] Introduce NodeRange interface, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[OpaqueRange] Introduce NodeRange interface\n\nAdd NodeRange between AbstractRange and Range/StaticRange. Under the\nOpaqueRange flag, startContainer/endContainer move from AbstractRange to\nNodeRange, allowing OpaqueRange to inherit from AbstractRange without\nexposing internal DOM containers.\n\nKeep startContainer/endContainer on AbstractRange behind the inverse\nLegacyAbstractRange flag until OpaqueRange ships. Add the C++ NodeRange\nparent unconditionally so the inheritance chain stays stable.\n\nRelevant discussions: https://github.com/whatwg/dom/pull/1470\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11478#issuecomment-4622847878\n\nSignoff from Blink API Owners on change:\nhttps://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/otEJ9AacRg4\n\nLow-Coverage-Reason: COVERAGE_UNDERREPORTED\nBug: 421421332\nChange-Id: Ica8f37cc536044269f1e252b63c38e7c8b55e758\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7904930\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dan Clark \u003cdaniec@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663534}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dc365f114ff5e1fb18a90b0aa1539eb1f036a4ce\nwpt-pr: 61357\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-basic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-disconnect.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-range-updates.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/ranges/tentative/OpaqueRange-supported-elements.html"], "git_node": "4eede831c443fae52359b28db8a157c371daad3c", "git_parents": ["6c0b8c68400659362f8b10d91bfe2a1621c55fae"], "node": "49fae0ee190ebc2e3bcf9e9e55a2dc7f14b75997", "parents": ["2a4da3eb963c47e6e1fa87b62533285bf2bb9c68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055771 [wpt PR 61359] - Handle values of \u003cfieldset checkable\u003e attribute more consistently., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHandle values of \u003cfieldset checkable\u003e attribute more consistently.\n\nThis tries to be more consistent at implementing the spec concepts that:\n * the missing value default is the None state\n * the empty value default is the Multiple state\n * the invalid value default is the Multiple state\n\nThis aligns with how I specified the checkable attribute's reflection on\nthe menu-elements branch in\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/commit/3373ac0401fb3e8546d976d0e079bb63b780bf48\n\nThe tests were initially AI-generated but I then duplicated them to test\nboth empty string and invalid values.  The empty string dynamic change\ntests fail without this CL.  The others help to test the spec prose\naround missing value default and invalid value default.\n\nBug: 406566432\nChange-Id: I59ded48c8973e6337efc75e5743e711d1eeb58a2\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8102282\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663573}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 36f4a331ced5bddb747fb49d00499e0978ef2d97\nwpt-pr: 61359\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/menu/tentative/checkable.html"], "git_node": "538feadbfe271c767ff314a80df0b59dfb5d84ad", "git_parents": ["4eede831c443fae52359b28db8a157c371daad3c"], "node": "c7857e334c24fd5044cda63d466247f24725405a", "parents": ["49fae0ee190ebc2e3bcf9e9e55a2dc7f14b75997"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055771 [wpt PR 61359] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61359\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/menu/tentative/checkable.html.ini"], "git_node": "eaff099756888ead95119af1825540b18b0a10e0", "git_parents": ["538feadbfe271c767ff314a80df0b59dfb5d84ad"], "node": "caf0bf01ed2e36eea830a6d6d3b48ca08031f348", "parents": ["c7857e334c24fd5044cda63d466247f24725405a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "youennf \u003cyouennf@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054002 [wpt PR 61196] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318954, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318954 (#61196)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f0b30d60daf6a64a3b087d66732c54c8e5273dbd\nwpt-pr: 61196\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-video-element-loadedmetadata-event.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-videoDetectorTest.html"], "git_node": "2e175175de73dd026faba964add4e5279d22ddec", "git_parents": ["eaff099756888ead95119af1825540b18b0a10e0"], "node": "a2ef2586dc2e89465b6bcb22559d19933655a71c", "parents": ["caf0bf01ed2e36eea830a6d6d3b48ca08031f348"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054002 [wpt PR 61196] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61196\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCRtpParameters-codec.html.ini"], "git_node": "ce545e342e46d2095c57e26d7ea080327f240d33", "git_parents": ["2e175175de73dd026faba964add4e5279d22ddec"], "node": "f1f5db64a83212b8a7fcdf4b7a98e53c92dd5039", "parents": ["a2ef2586dc2e89465b6bcb22559d19933655a71c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055514 [wpt PR 61336] - Add WPT test coverage for 16-bit high-bit-depth video frame encoding, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd WPT test coverage for 16-bit high-bit-depth video frame encoding\n\nAdds `video-encoder-hbd.https.any.js` WebPlatformTest to test encoding\n16-bit high-bit-depth (HBD) and alpha VideoFrame inputs directly from\nUint16Array buffers without going through Canvas.\n\nTest coverage details:\n- Tests 9 high-bit-depth input formats: I420P10, I422P10, I444P10,\n  I420P12, I422P12, I444P12, I420AP10, I422AP10, I444AP10.\n- Exercises 8-bit conversion encoding for 8-bit profiles (AV1 Main 8-bit,\n  VP8, VP9 Profile 0, VP9 Profile 1, H.264 Baseline) and 10-bit HBD\n  encoding for high-bit-depth profiles (VP9 Profile 2, VP9 Profile 3).\n- Re-decodes output chunks via VideoDecoder and verifies RGBA channels\n  (including alpha) using VideoFrame.copyTo({ format: 'RGBA' }).\n- Includes capability checks via VideoEncoder and VideoDecoder\n  isConfigSupported() with assert_implements_optional().\n\nFixed: 529852980\nChange-Id: Ib42c3c97a04c0733ecbb4d5d3da0b94e6b9c082a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8093249\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Eugene Zemtsov \u003ceugene@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663682}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dedb54ae802f84675709a5951f42eafb668dcbb5\nwpt-pr: 61336\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webcodecs/video-encoder-hbd.https.any.js"], "git_node": "1bd9a1d139720dbfa9223f8008a4dd5b615eeff4", "git_parents": ["ce545e342e46d2095c57e26d7ea080327f240d33"], "node": "1c392cf72a0c2edaeeb7241ed3583f07220b4b02", "parents": ["f1f5db64a83212b8a7fcdf4b7a98e53c92dd5039"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055514 [wpt PR 61336] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61336\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webcodecs/video-encoder-hbd.https.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "65f975a24f10120ccd6ddadd331c06a386f07c8e", "git_parents": ["1bd9a1d139720dbfa9223f8008a4dd5b615eeff4"], "node": "17b9822f451a29a13aebde08d05f5dc18e92a392", "parents": ["1c392cf72a0c2edaeeb7241ed3583f07220b4b02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055736 [wpt PR 61350] - [compression-dictionary] Make sure link element are processed after changes to crossorigin attribute, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Make sure link element are processed after changes to crossorigin attribute\n\nThis is currently not specified but is proposed at\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11620\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: Ia6f60eee7f0e5a3af9fb4bda9b0d0a483a3e5950\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8027613\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663692}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9fb9c273ff8ed6dda31c3326cc87d0624404ee3a\nwpt-pr: 61350\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-timing-002.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "07b1f73795d2773131fe65726b3ee8b9b0943fc3", "git_parents": ["65f975a24f10120ccd6ddadd331c06a386f07c8e"], "node": "c004bb1d83e42a1b4b47f27bc982c8ee2da44653", "parents": ["17b9822f451a29a13aebde08d05f5dc18e92a392"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055736 [wpt PR 61350] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61350\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-timing-002.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "e5e0cbf4c391c48abd08ac1addb75aa85dc1e0e9", "git_parents": ["07b1f73795d2773131fe65726b3ee8b9b0943fc3"], "node": "2153619266f4ebc99602d201e95b2b1b12a08dc5", "parents": ["c004bb1d83e42a1b4b47f27bc982c8ee2da44653"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055729 [wpt PR 61345] - Add missing check-scheme action in WS stash responder, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd missing check-scheme action in WS stash responder\n\nstash_responder_wsh.py handled put/purge/take but not check-scheme,\nso a mixed-content test sending that action hit an UnboundLocalError and\ntimed out. This CL adds the missing branch and removes expected.txt\nbaselines and test expectation entries.\n\nBug: 504770562\nChange-Id: Ic687ec7f02a13de48fa56aaaed7d92c7036012fc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8105315\nReviewed-by: Carlos IL \u003ccarlosil@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663729}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7df1411ef080cddaa8dacc510ffa505afe253577\nwpt-pr: 61345\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/websockets/handlers/stash_responder_wsh.py"], "git_node": "3da5ae5521cb5ace7a855936ec80641db0a73730", "git_parents": ["e5e0cbf4c391c48abd08ac1addb75aa85dc1e0e9"], "node": "70ec02de5dd05d589758c1535c6cf4d00ef8ea38", "parents": ["2153619266f4ebc99602d201e95b2b1b12a08dc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055842 [wpt PR 61364] - Custom elements: test the active custom element constructor map, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCustom elements: test the active custom element constructor map\n\nAdd coverage for how the active custom element constructor map is\nconsulted and restored across re-entrant construction:\n\n- Directly constructing a custom element whose definition lives only in\n  the global registry resolves against the global registry, even while\n  an upgrade or a scoped createElement() construction is in progress.\n- Re-entrant createElement() with a different registry for the same\n  constructor restores the outer registry, so the outer super() still\n  resolves correctly.\n- Re-entrant createElement() for the same element constructs two\n  independent elements (create an element does not push onto the\n  construction stack).\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/12691.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d3dbfff737c17ee648d6f459f795c158be21bb26\nwpt-pr: 61364\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/createElement-reentrant-construction.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/registries/constructor-direct-call-fallback-registry.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/registries/constructor-reentry-createElement.window.js"], "git_node": "59b619c678d28cca64ef9a32e3923ce611a27da0", "git_parents": ["3da5ae5521cb5ace7a855936ec80641db0a73730"], "node": "56f81a4d5119a80bcb684adbc2b332225631ff90", "parents": ["70ec02de5dd05d589758c1535c6cf4d00ef8ea38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055842 [wpt PR 61364] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61364\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/constructor-direct-call-fallback-registry.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/constructor-reentry-createElement.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "7563721be6fbb6f3ea69a840b27d1926721c41bd", "git_parents": ["59b619c678d28cca64ef9a32e3923ce611a27da0"], "node": "b61d3ae07cba7c2be26db3cf536463ae91b0ac95", "parents": ["56f81a4d5119a80bcb684adbc2b332225631ff90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054231 [wpt PR 61212] - Create nodes in the passed document's realm, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCreate nodes in the passed document's realm\n\nTest that DOM node creation uses the relevant realm of the document the\nnode is created for, rather than the realm running the algorithm. This\ncovers elements, shadow roots, and the other node types, exercised via\nadoption, innerHTML, attachShadow(), importNode(), cloneNode(), Range,\nand the createX() factory methods invoked cross-realm.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/dom/issues/977.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 33933167af8e8d0711fc64d96afc4b69c6943a40\nwpt-pr: 61212\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/attach-shadow-realm-after-adoption.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/create-element-realm-after-adoption.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/node-creation-realm.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/node-realm-adoption-after-frame-removal.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/node-realm-mixed-across-adoption.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/node-realm-preserved-across-adoption.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/node-realm-preserved-across-frameless-adoption.html"], "git_node": "e3eb3b4bc3de2844b011147f7b0b9e3da77524ba", "git_parents": ["7563721be6fbb6f3ea69a840b27d1926721c41bd"], "node": "c3e4dc3d6b8faa214fb6496b34bb1645d1d5343b", "parents": ["b61d3ae07cba7c2be26db3cf536463ae91b0ac95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054231 [wpt PR 61212] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61212\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/node-realm-adoption-after-frame-removal.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/node-realm-mixed-across-adoption.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/node-realm-preserved-across-adoption.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/node-realm-preserved-across-frameless-adoption.html.ini"], "git_node": "506b44407a3e3013790242c9cd799ab978f85430", "git_parents": ["e3eb3b4bc3de2844b011147f7b0b9e3da77524ba"], "node": "fc3340e5bf4d113cc7a5ce05176dd38694cea847", "parents": ["c3e4dc3d6b8faa214fb6496b34bb1645d1d5343b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054276 [wpt PR 61229] - [compression-dictionary] Add tentative tests to verify that link headers in subresources do not trigger dictionary fetches, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Add tentative tests to verify that link headers in subresources do not trigger dictionary fetches\n\nHandling of link rel=compression-dictionary header from subresources is\ncurrently not defined in specifications. It is implemented in Chromium\n(with discussions to try to restrict it) but not in WebKit or Firefox.\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/11619#issuecomment-49381925637\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 363c89482493a3b62ffed9166207b6607758633c\nwpt-pr: 61229\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/common/empty.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/common/empty.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-header-in-subresources.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "d536a45a66ad32800685b410fc4b4e9de9c0e1b6", "git_parents": ["506b44407a3e3013790242c9cd799ab978f85430"], "node": "89e57c433c79ee6a552a7574281849f0b937f9ae", "parents": ["fc3340e5bf4d113cc7a5ce05176dd38694cea847"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055851 [wpt PR 61363] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316174, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=316174 (#61363)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d3ed97f7b225e4aa3051c532bf13380027e2550e\nwpt-pr: 61363\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-pannernode-interface/panner-non-finite-distance-params.html"], "git_node": "c3a92d427e49092c9c9166492032cef683f53fc9", "git_parents": ["d536a45a66ad32800685b410fc4b4e9de9c0e1b6"], "node": "a24df4325e136bd55b6e25bb1d2b27e180f2726c", "parents": ["89e57c433c79ee6a552a7574281849f0b937f9ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055901 [wpt PR 61368] - Canvas2D: Respect EXIF orientation for cross-origin CSSImageValue, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCanvas2D: Respect EXIF orientation for cross-origin CSSImageValue\n\nEnforce kRespectImageOrientation for any source that would taint the\norigin, including CSS image values.\n\nThe IsImageBitmap() || IsImageElement() checks which previously gated\nthe WouldTaintOrigin() check had been introduced to fix a CHECK failure\nin SVGImage::CheckLoaded(); see https://crrev.com/c/2521049. However, in\nhttps://crrev.com/c/5892795 we removed the call to CheckLoaded() on this\npath, so the image type gates are no longer needed.\n\nFixed: 517655953\nChange-Id: I1e1838c3af56264fb49c4086c9cf6ae28fe84d15\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8102890\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Colin Blundell \u003cblundell@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663972}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f87b5bbcba4c385266f9d5c29023b6957bbd7a2d\nwpt-pr: 61368\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-canvas-css-image-value.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-images/image-orientation/reference/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-canvas-css-image-value-ref.sub.html"], "git_node": "108b4904380eadd554933decea4e553bbaf30926", "git_parents": ["c3a92d427e49092c9c9166492032cef683f53fc9"], "node": "6058acddfe3c6ffc1bc5563f839011f5578e41f9", "parents": ["a24df4325e136bd55b6e25bb1d2b27e180f2726c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055901 [wpt PR 61368] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61368\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-images/image-orientation/image-orientation-none-cross-origin-canvas-css-image-value.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "61ffa7085b0e9de3fbf026fb54b48b50c7e07af9", "git_parents": ["108b4904380eadd554933decea4e553bbaf30926"], "node": "da33d8eb548c538d6e8eb45691c8cf71354993cf", "parents": ["6058acddfe3c6ffc1bc5563f839011f5578e41f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Palak Agarwal \u003cagpalak@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055959 [wpt PR 61375] - audio-preferred captures in getDisplayMedia, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\naudio-preferred captures in getDisplayMedia\n\nThis CL comprises mostly of changes in blink to plumb the audioSelection\nconstraint from JS to StreamControls to MediaStreamRequest.\n\nThis includes:\n- Adding audio_selection_preferred to StreamControls mojom and C++ structs.\n- Parsing the audioSelection constraint in Blink.\n- Adding GetDisplayMediaAudioSelection runtime feature.\n\nBug: 535514300\nChange-Id: If34715999d061df52d0b8b1cce0b2046308674ad\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8107082\nReviewed-by: Arthur Sonzogni \u003carthursonzogni@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jeremy Roman \u003cjbroman@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Evan Liu \u003cevliu@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Palak Agarwal \u003cagpalak@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664045}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 95bb127374794c6ac9f362ef757fffa2fb112c2f\nwpt-pr: 61375\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/screen-capture/getdisplaymedia.https.html"], "git_node": "50d0e94669ddf7da7985f511e6604be309bf2f24", "git_parents": ["61ffa7085b0e9de3fbf026fb54b48b50c7e07af9"], "node": "f3e1bdf2d406a73513c0e9176551f1a7276cb676", "parents": ["da33d8eb548c538d6e8eb45691c8cf71354993cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055959 [wpt PR 61375] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61375\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/screen-capture/getdisplaymedia.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "2e69b1108bf5671e735eb2daffbf606cccc7d59e", "git_parents": ["50d0e94669ddf7da7985f511e6604be309bf2f24"], "node": "da2128b10b837251a05a3d38632cc136dded6cb2", "parents": ["f3e1bdf2d406a73513c0e9176551f1a7276cb676"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055960 [wpt PR 61376] - Clamp outermost-main-frame mismatches in the network service, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nClamp outermost-main-frame mismatches in the network service\n\nInitial empty documents in opener-retaining popups can inherit their\ncreating subframe's URLLoaderFactory while correctly identifying as an\noutermost main frame. Clamp the renderer-provided value to the\nbrowser-derived factory value instead of reporting a bad message, and\nrecord the occurrence in UMA.\n\nBug: 535676050\nChange-Id: Ibf7af1974d06ebe67d11d5d5d0029b6733e763f3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8112401\nReviewed-by: Crisrael Lucero \u003ccrisrael@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Tsuyoshi Horo \u003choro@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664069}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a4c4a710cf6b92886cd8105713e3886e751985aa\nwpt-pr: 61376\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/api/basic/fetch-in-popup-from-iframe.html"], "git_node": "c2665b348a9902cdbfa4c016ee3036e5284196ff", "git_parents": ["2e69b1108bf5671e735eb2daffbf606cccc7d59e"], "node": "d17a7a843b57a52785b96cbd5425c63f50012172", "parents": ["da2128b10b837251a05a3d38632cc136dded6cb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055962 [wpt PR 61377] - [css-mixins] Allow @mixin definitions without a parameter list, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Allow @mixin definitions without a parameter list\n\nAccept a bare \u003cdashed-ident\u003e prelude, so `@mixin --foo {}` is valid and\nequivalent to `@mixin --foo() {}`. Previously, a \u003cfunction-token\u003e was\nrequired, even though @apply already allowed omitting the parentheses.\n\nSpec change: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14151\nIssue: https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/13015\n\nChange-Id: Ib2ccf89e5f374facd6d45d0d9bd994d9d0ef9c3c\nFixed: 496172417\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8111117\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664074}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4778049f6c52369cddf9a02442563951e283c2c2\nwpt-pr: 61377\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-basic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-cssom.tentative.html"], "git_node": "91eb6bae61a50266b4dd2767298b5178b04ae112", "git_parents": ["c2665b348a9902cdbfa4c016ee3036e5284196ff"], "node": "8c76fbe25c44af4366bf8324e4ac6c188654620d", "parents": ["d17a7a843b57a52785b96cbd5425c63f50012172"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055962 [wpt PR 61377] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61377\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-cssom.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "690b41f8a4ad0de78cf4cf624fba4c36b4a493c5", "git_parents": ["91eb6bae61a50266b4dd2767298b5178b04ae112"], "node": "57e1c67fc364a877ca3dffe76d756e0daa35d569", "parents": ["8c76fbe25c44af4366bf8324e4ac6c188654620d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joone Hur \u003cjoonehur@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055972 [wpt PR 61378] - Support Long Animation Frames in Web Workers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport Long Animation Frames in Web Workers\n\nExtend the Long Animation Frame API to Web Workers so that a long task\nblocking a worker's event loop is reported as a \"long-animation-frame\"\nentry, observable from inside the worker via PerformanceObserver.\n\nRun with --enable-blink-features=LongAnimationFrameWorker.\n\nBug: 534893134\nTest: external/wpt/long-animation-frame/loaf-congested-moment-worker.html\nBinary-Size: Size increase from adding Long Animation Frame support for dedicated workers.\nCompile-Size: Size increase is unavoidable.\nChange-Id: Id8ca8fbde43a34b02c4b7f611e9a748655e63917\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8094995\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joone Hur \u003cjoonehur@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664161}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: eebb679e5316ba7ea154c2a5d12fc8a305c06aca\nwpt-pr: 61378\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-congested-moment-worker.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-window-only.worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/resources/loaf-congested-moment-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/resources/utils-worker.js"], "git_node": "428f27447431ea36ee5351821a6d34a515c960c7", "git_parents": ["690b41f8a4ad0de78cf4cf624fba4c36b4a493c5"], "node": "0ac2ec5fb72cf184d4bd24f1950bbe01e659498e", "parents": ["57e1c67fc364a877ca3dffe76d756e0daa35d569"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Anne van Kesteren \u003cannevk@annevk.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055923 [wpt PR 61370] - Add NULL character parsing tests for MathML and foreign fragments, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd NULL character parsing tests for MathML and foreign fragments\n\nU+0000 NULL coverage was SVG-heavy. Add tests for NULL in MathML foreign\ncontent (including CDATA and annotation-xml with/without\nencoding=\"text/html\"), and for fragment parsing with NULL at foreign and\nintegration-point context nodes.\n\nSee https://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/4015.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e45db0ba200746d562a15aac953e51f37954d870\nwpt-pr: 61370\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat"], "git_node": "af244b6da1785eacf837b59686bd2feb5e327769", "git_parents": ["428f27447431ea36ee5351821a6d34a515c960c7"], "node": "c87027fc82cec110984111150e7920b1bd5362ec", "parents": ["0ac2ec5fb72cf184d4bd24f1950bbe01e659498e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055760 [wpt PR 61358] - Apply anchor positioning scroll adjustment per axis, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nApply anchor positioning scroll adjustment per axis\n\nWith single-axis scroll containers, one inset axis of an anchored\nelement can be scroll adjusted while the other is not. Scroll adjustment\nis compensated on the compositor for the default anchor's scrolling\ncontext only, so for each axis, apply it only when the anchor queried by\nan inset and the default anchor have the same nearest scroll container\nfor that axis.\n\nFixed: 522362440\nBug: 440038212\nChange-Id: I584672f48c14a7666dc0f6faa57e5717622d85ea\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7934709\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Free Debreuil \u003cfreedebreuil@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664172}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 766be7e40accf3b97ef447fb7ba29fb344915d00\nwpt-pr: 61358\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-scroll-single-axis-default-anchor.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-scroll-single-axis-mixed-anchor.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-scroll-single-axis.html"], "git_node": "cfbbad007354cc2b5f81635f51e663aa98953785", "git_parents": ["af244b6da1785eacf837b59686bd2feb5e327769"], "node": "cd27e4ed96406fb87e0a70648f9c435a978096f5", "parents": ["c87027fc82cec110984111150e7920b1bd5362ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055760 [wpt PR 61358] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61358\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-scroll-single-axis-default-anchor.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-scroll-single-axis-mixed-anchor.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-scroll-single-axis.html.ini"], "git_node": "14ab7978226214b29d4cf6a904792b87bbfcd7b4", "git_parents": ["cfbbad007354cc2b5f81635f51e663aa98953785"], "node": "61107b845161b9f802c801018418dc963da2109d", "parents": ["cd27e4ed96406fb87e0a70648f9c435a978096f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Marcos C\u00e1ceres \u003ccaceres_m@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055706 [wpt PR 61341] - [digital-credentials] Test concurrent-request rejection is queued as a task, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[digital-credentials] Test concurrent-request rejection is queued as a task (#61341)\n\nAdds a subtest to concurrent-requests.https.html asserting that the concurrency rejection in \"prepare credential requests\" is queued on the DOM manipulation task source (a microtask scheduled in the same tick runs before the rejection reaction), rather than settled synchronously.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9c1395d9af3bb045d287c5adb31f93cf22cf988f\nwpt-pr: 61341\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/digital-credentials/concurrent-requests.https.html"], "git_node": "92b93bc1e843d9eb7f5c4cb956194660dbe5f68f", "git_parents": ["14ab7978226214b29d4cf6a904792b87bbfcd7b4"], "node": "4915a8e7f9c4d56cca89e9aa3671259a4c40f66c", "parents": ["61107b845161b9f802c801018418dc963da2109d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055706 [wpt PR 61341] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61341\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/digital-credentials/concurrent-requests.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "dc08dbc7b804a697e138ba05e61d4b74537fbc48", "git_parents": ["92b93bc1e843d9eb7f5c4cb956194660dbe5f68f"], "node": "cb33aa0dc5cd34d9dc727ddbc7597586fdb8e2db", "parents": ["4915a8e7f9c4d56cca89e9aa3671259a4c40f66c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055214 [wpt PR 61309] - Add test to verify that link rel=compression-dictionary fetches can be blocked via connect-src, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd test to verify that link rel=compression-dictionary fetches can be blocked via connect-src\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 49a6294ddb9565714cba508f21a436450725d85d\nwpt-pr: 61309\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src.tentative.https.html.headers"], "git_node": "644f99dfe5c1b03b9cdd573ea96804d45a54f0dc", "git_parents": ["dc08dbc7b804a697e138ba05e61d4b74537fbc48"], "node": "16d0f1fdd9b52aa4d3af5b38e6ab1d7feef8f3a2", "parents": ["cb33aa0dc5cd34d9dc727ddbc7597586fdb8e2db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055214 [wpt PR 61309] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61309\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "8bde29f380f3fcbbd82a620ddb6ca6199c9dd88d", "git_parents": ["644f99dfe5c1b03b9cdd573ea96804d45a54f0dc"], "node": "d0af4ff170c701f2986c88a0a764a61d377a3f81", "parents": ["16d0f1fdd9b52aa4d3af5b38e6ab1d7feef8f3a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Simon W\u00fclker \u003csimon.wuelker@arcor.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055988 [wpt PR 61382] - script: Mark document tree as dirty when web fonts are removed, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd web platform test\n\nSigned-off-by: Simon W\u00fclker \u003csimon.wuelker@arcor.de\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8ffdd886a64cf6c1ba24cd422b2944f5d0359c92\nwpt-pr: 61382\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/remove-loaded-font-face-rule-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-fonts/remove-loaded-font-face-rule.html"], "git_node": "d3bc5507a4ab322e5d5f5743297f5d6c402b49df", "git_parents": ["8bde29f380f3fcbbd82a620ddb6ca6199c9dd88d"], "node": "d8b8db284b48235b8e5e5b1e1c8a2be2ad371cab", "parents": ["d0af4ff170c701f2986c88a0a764a61d377a3f81"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055996 [wpt PR 61386] - script: Halt \"update the rendering\" for `Document` if rAF blocks rendering, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Halt \"update the rendering\" for `Document` if rAF blocks rendering\n\nA `requestAnimationFrame` can do things that put a `Document` in\nrender blocking mode during the process of \"update the rendering.\" If\nthat happens we should just bail out of the rendering update for the\n`Document` until it is time to render. This prevents a panic due to an\nassertion failure.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 56d37a3588d33e2c36529203eccc7001e74a7497\nwpt-pr: 61386\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/render-blocking/render-blocking-during-update-the-rendering-crash.html"], "git_node": "e3e0460bf36519c7aeae0528786dff5e1b980b11", "git_parents": ["d3bc5507a4ab322e5d5f5743297f5d6c402b49df"], "node": "6b01f4f8b90a0534114dbdaf99ef47bbb709fa5c", "parents": ["d8b8db284b48235b8e5e5b1e1c8a2be2ad371cab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim van der Lippe \u003ctvanderlippe@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054521 [wpt PR 61252] - script: Parse vtt payload for track elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Parse vtt payload for track elements\n\nThis uses the payload retrieved by the fetch to construct the\nlist of cues to be added to the track.\n\nPart of #46288\n\nTesting: new passing WPT tests\n\nSigned-off-by: Tim van der Lippe \u003ctvanderlippe@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 37cd7ff74eb974fd41600bf7bc01d37576abf8b5\nwpt-pr: 61252\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/resources/header-empty-after.vtt", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/resources/header-invalid-equal.vtt", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/resources/header-newlines-after.vtt", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/resources/header-too-short.vtt", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/embedded-content/media-elements/track/track-element/track-webvtt-header-checks.html"], "git_node": "f1fae5b3949493b23767011b9374a53d975ea4f4", "git_parents": ["e3e0460bf36519c7aeae0528786dff5e1b980b11"], "node": "0285b917c1756131b51c5f50c7d62140cecb9d16", "parents": ["6b01f4f8b90a0534114dbdaf99ef47bbb709fa5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055926 [wpt PR 61372] - layout: Implement block-axis centering for buttons, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Implement block-axis centering for buttons\n\nMark `\u003cbutton\u003e` elements and `\u003cinput\u003e` that lay out as buttons with a\nnew `FragmentFlags::IS_BUTTON` flag. Then, if they contain a block\nformatting context, center their contents in the block axis.\n\nThis is done similarly as for `vertical-align` on table cells: we wrap\nthe contents inside a `PositioningFragment`, which is then shifted to\nappear at the correct place. But unlike table cells, this is done before\ncaching the layout results, not afterwards.\n\nIn the future, when we implement `align-content` for block containers,\nwe should probably switch to that.\n\nCo-authored-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e4ea1706fa708c3ac4523c534a65160d1ab20db8\nwpt-pr: 61372\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-003.html"], "git_node": "061ab86cd4fdc7c32eb4ced2edba72fa816da691", "git_parents": ["f1fae5b3949493b23767011b9374a53d975ea4f4"], "node": "10e73b6f5cea6a6b8ac32e9f74c97cd0b810ffd9", "parents": ["0285b917c1756131b51c5f50c7d62140cecb9d16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055926 [wpt PR 61372] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61372\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/rendering/widgets/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "9c526345a69f90cd30c4b5eacec7ee4a30cbd225", "git_parents": ["061ab86cd4fdc7c32eb4ced2edba72fa816da691"], "node": "05be7e2331c5bbbb708f9a69f2b2a34f09a90967", "parents": ["10e73b6f5cea6a6b8ac32e9f74c97cd0b810ffd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056120 [wpt PR 61401] - [HiC] Fix issues with shadow dom canvas children, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[HiC] Fix issues with shadow dom canvas children\n\nRecursively mark shadow dom content as a canvas child when it's slotting\nstatus changes (flat tree parent changes). This corrects problems with\nprivacy preserving painting and painting in general, particularly for\nforms.\n\nThis approach was chosen over a style-based version for a couple of\nreasons:\n* There is a significant chunk of code that depends on the\n  DidChangeCanvasSubtree method, so it would need to stay in some form.\n  There's less use in moving to style if we still need this DOM status\n  tracking.\n* The style based relied on suppressing autofill data at the getter\n  stage, rather than on setting. I think a setter approach is more\n  robust to future changes.\n\nAdd tests for declarative slotting, custom elements, and privacy for\nvisited links and cross-origin image. The privacy tests cover things\nprotected by style setting (visited links) and paint flags (images).\nAlso a test for video correctly updating it's compositor read-back\nneeds, and lots of form control unit tests for autofill privacy.\n\nFixed: 501661601, 503553618\nChange-Id: I261f0c55c3e7204ff919f3e64a9655c6f93e47e4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7899615\nCommit-Queue: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664517}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 466ab94ab6b91d4051a59a2e8295ad331916ce01\nwpt-pr: 61401\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element-multiple-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element-multiple.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/canvas-in-custom-element-images-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/support/CanvasWidgetWithImages.https.sub.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-slotted-color-ignored.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/resources/CanvasWidget.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slot-canvas-child.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted-moveBefore.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted.tentative.html"], "git_node": "7405f75f68793c67483cf15998ce4e6782fbeab4", "git_parents": ["9c526345a69f90cd30c4b5eacec7ee4a30cbd225"], "node": "863f9c88004339fba85fc2f0e4c7fcf83c9affa4", "parents": ["05be7e2331c5bbbb708f9a69f2b2a34f09a90967"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056120 [wpt PR 61401] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61401\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element-multiple.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/canvas-in-custom-element.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/canvas-in-custom-element-images-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/visited-link-slotted-color-ignored.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slot-canvas-child.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted-moveBefore.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/shadow-dom-slotted.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "636d7220c38f67bb1ac116736c507376b3666e4b", "git_parents": ["7405f75f68793c67483cf15998ce4e6782fbeab4"], "node": "ca04aa91568ccb381b67b33b79ee2af1f66ccab9", "parents": ["863f9c88004339fba85fc2f0e4c7fcf83c9affa4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Henrik Skupin \u003cmail@hskupin.info\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056153 [wpt PR 61402] - Bump marionette dependency to 3.7.1, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBump marionette dependency to 3.7.1 (#61402)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c937f9d271eb35913c3b5b0635fa7fd5f8c88eec\nwpt-pr: 61402\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wptrunner/requirements_firefox.txt"], "git_node": "d9ddcf882ef78bb89858f42c7eddd097f75e605c", "git_parents": ["636d7220c38f67bb1ac116736c507376b3666e4b"], "node": "64a0e6a2765ec78a7c287b2d504cd721456a5abc", "parents": ["ca04aa91568ccb381b67b33b79ee2af1f66ccab9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "eri \u003ceri@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056210 [wpt PR 61407] - [jpegxl] Add fuzzy matching to jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[jpegxl] Add fuzzy matching to jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest (#61407)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 678ccf0d22a4097d74ecb383051297d2b24b824b\nwpt-pr: 61407\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/jpegxl/cmyk-basic-conversion-reftest.html"], "git_node": "83d50528eb3357e3fda38998e6e2d2153aaab11f", "git_parents": ["d9ddcf882ef78bb89858f42c7eddd097f75e605c"], "node": "f7ee6fea5211ff07c25328806670ccf3fdbb12f3", "parents": ["64a0e6a2765ec78a7c287b2d504cd721456a5abc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055925 [wpt PR 61371] - [mathml] Fix the target navigation test for mathml a element, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[mathml] Fix the target navigation test for mathml a element\n\nThere is a typo that use a undeclared variable in the test.\n\nBug: 510487697\nChange-Id: Ia90187aca1ec72319ad638dc8942c5215b1b3c43\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8103445\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664600}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 745d25af49c47728fcf1a5b7995e8cb56feb6dca\nwpt-pr: 61371\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/href-navigation.html"], "git_node": "4843dd5863ed7124c6c6c8f3b1a10777b387bbb9", "git_parents": ["83d50528eb3357e3fda38998e6e2d2153aaab11f"], "node": "ad3f206f82e6827df8a09480d62e4a41fd670fe5", "parents": ["f7ee6fea5211ff07c25328806670ccf3fdbb12f3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056215 [wpt PR 61409] - [mathml] Add the `ping` attribute of the mathml a element, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[mathml] Add the `ping` attribute of the mathml a element\n\nThe actual implementation of the ping behavior was added previously to\nMathMLAnchorElement.[1]\n\nThis change only adds the dom interface to access the ping attribute and\ntests its behavior.\n\nThe `ping` attribute for the mathml anchor element serves the same\npurpose and behaves as the HTML and SVG anchor elements.\nSee the spec details in [2] [3].\n\n[1] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7940188\n[2] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#ping\n[3] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#hyperlink-auditing\n\nBug: 510487697\nChange-Id: I334ce3f74cc28a49b79bb35d027385aee732af6c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8084280\nReviewed-by: Rob Buis \u003crbuis@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664601}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1791612486c6a2a68524ba6046798819bcfd356f\nwpt-pr: 61409\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-ping.html"], "git_node": "74b51e1ff64a4370f19865961885a8b599937cab", "git_parents": ["4843dd5863ed7124c6c6c8f3b1a10777b387bbb9"], "node": "6b1ff9340377663e1de13ddfd751779ca6f49e08", "parents": ["ad3f206f82e6827df8a09480d62e4a41fd670fe5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056215 [wpt PR 61409] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61409\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-ping.html.ini"], "git_node": "5d6b6133a2f6e8a162dc525e916f9cc589ce5ec0", "git_parents": ["74b51e1ff64a4370f19865961885a8b599937cab"], "node": "c6094d8a856b429af59a75603311eb381044e936", "parents": ["6b1ff9340377663e1de13ddfd751779ca6f49e08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Psychpsyo (Cameron) \u003c60073468+Psychpsyo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056000 [wpt PR 61388] - script: Implement forwarddelete command, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: Implement forwarddelete command\n\nSigned-off-by: Psychpsyo (Cameron) \u003c60073468+Psychpsyo@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: beed4bd81b71e115e053dba4beb4b36954f67b50\nwpt-pr: 61388\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/editing/crashtests/forwarddelete-after-editable-slot-element-outside-body.html"], "git_node": "5c13a2dcb2a8142f09f4de5f30e80c6d9d73bc82", "git_parents": ["5d6b6133a2f6e8a162dc525e916f9cc589ce5ec0"], "node": "14072620139bc613eb3b031e291c5aab04e82066", "parents": ["c6094d8a856b429af59a75603311eb381044e936"], "tags": []}, {"author": "tannal \u003cmtan@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056206 [wpt PR 61406] - [mathml] Add WPT tests for attributeStyleMap on MathMLElement, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[mathml] Add WPT tests for attributeStyleMap on MathMLElement\n\nBug: 527954011\nChange-Id: I258de8455c422dc0aec2a8fb76b6964f721f9013\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8010506\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664605}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 030897f81a3297054a93fd3aa0b40264419bf4f5\nwpt-pr: 61406\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/attributeStyleMap-getter-setter.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/attributeStyleMap-getter.html"], "git_node": "0c93332e687c04d4d1e44782ea28fc30a4500259", "git_parents": ["5c13a2dcb2a8142f09f4de5f30e80c6d9d73bc82"], "node": "1672c47c327944b365de022d2ec282d8abd5758a", "parents": ["14072620139bc613eb3b031e291c5aab04e82066"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056110 [wpt PR 61400] - layout: Avoid setting FragmentFlags for HTML elements on pseudo-elements, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Avoid setting FragmentFlags for HTML elements on pseudo-elements\n\nFor example, a `::before` originated by a `\u003cbutton\u003e` was marked with\n`FragmentFlags::IS_BUTTON`, so its contents were wrongly centered\nvertically, as if it was another `\u003cbutton\u003e`.\n\nOr a `::before` originated by the body element used to be marked with\n`FragmentFlags::IS_BODY_ELEMENT_OF_HTML_ELEMENT_ROOT`, so if the body\npropagated its background to the viewport, we would also avoid painting\nthe background of that `::before`.\n\nThe exception is the `\u003cbr\u003e` element. Layout logic expects the flag to\nappear both on the element itself, and on its `::before`.\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8695dbbad76933e55492c53d966a9e2df71184c2\nwpt-pr: 61400\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-color-body-propagation-010.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-color-root-propagation-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/button-layout/centering-004.html"], "git_node": "414a09d0bd5c3c2b19ee9405bf607887bb30f5fa", "git_parents": ["0c93332e687c04d4d1e44782ea28fc30a4500259"], "node": "dd37ad6b9dc952a6bf838dd8370447761d25fa5b", "parents": ["1672c47c327944b365de022d2ec282d8abd5758a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053646 [wpt PR 61162] - [wdspec] update get_element_tag_name tests to assert qualified name, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[wdspec] update get_element_tag_name tests to assert qualified name\n\n--\n[wdspec] additional test cases for get_element_tag_name based on tagname wpt test\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 323ae4aead996a3429a6d672059c318e413de9bd, ff372ea4a4b10d75830d4bad6445b2904d00a537\nwpt-pr: 61162\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/get_element_tag_name/get.py"], "git_node": "1a4cf57b13ecb7f7d523c447f35b0315ee7c1e2e", "git_parents": ["414a09d0bd5c3c2b19ee9405bf607887bb30f5fa"], "node": "1d65ab303e23b7f34077c9cfd85a68e5d1bf27bb", "parents": ["dd37ad6b9dc952a6bf838dd8370447761d25fa5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053646 [wpt PR 61162] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61162\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/get_element_tag_name/get.py.ini"], "git_node": "82f1ba4bcc10046cf62d8b0ff3684c6779d6b6d4", "git_parents": ["1a4cf57b13ecb7f7d523c447f35b0315ee7c1e2e"], "node": "c9945b4c823ef7877150a99b932439ca5e641d5b", "parents": ["1d65ab303e23b7f34077c9cfd85a68e5d1bf27bb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056221 [wpt PR 61410] - Skip invisible descendants in background-clip text masks, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSkip invisible descendants in background-clip text masks\n\nFully transparent self-painting descendants should not leave glyphs\nin an ancestor's text mask.\n\nBug: 534893146\nChange-Id: I3352447d2aea4f19ba4e853a9173dfd3d019574d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8119590\nCommit-Queue: Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664641}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e50823ceeb7f91dedbabb86a4fa528748ab0e0cc\nwpt-pr: 61410\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-text-stacking-context-child-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-backgrounds/background-clip/clip-text-stacking-context-child.html"], "git_node": "fc058a7de43f6038ac0d840c541a492d40e2349e", "git_parents": ["82f1ba4bcc10046cf62d8b0ff3684c6779d6b6d4"], "node": "767a4faa5ec4ccfedcc7e16b0c5aff7b693b1dc7", "parents": ["c9945b4c823ef7877150a99b932439ca5e641d5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056245 [wpt PR 61412] - corner-shape: always serialize as superellipse(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncorner-shape: always serialize as superellipse()\n\nThis matches the spec and consistent with other props.\n\nBug: 524886862\nChange-Id: I524dac94e150cc8ea4f915a435aaf4017408c721\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8024710\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664650}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0edf5e9196498403b31b167a4816fcef9751a93d\nwpt-pr: 61412\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-block-start-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-shape-interpolation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-top-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/corner-shape/corner-top-left-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/nested/group-children-animations.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/geolocation-element/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/install/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/usermedia/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html"], "git_node": "56424142820037dbfa17e2a635473aa44005a730", "git_parents": ["fc058a7de43f6038ac0d840c541a492d40e2349e"], "node": "b20a72f1bfb0ac6ab2f6bca4a587b69fae5b7d90", "parents": ["767a4faa5ec4ccfedcc7e16b0c5aff7b693b1dc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056258 [wpt PR 61413] - [compression-dictionary] Add WPT test to ensure imagesrcset attribute is ignored., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Add WPT test to ensure imagesrcset attribute is ignored.\n\nsource set option is mentioned on [1] but really only used for [2], so\nit shouldn't interfer with rel=compression-dictionary.\n\n[1] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#create-link-options-from-element\n[2] https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/links.html#link-type-preload:link-options-source-set\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: I528c8b9a08859505863d647ef442414df521cfd7\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8124456\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664656}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 753696c188f12591469913adbf8e85ad692359b0\nwpt-pr: 61413\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-imagesrcset.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "20b65ff663a3cc11f8eca873e10635a6939e0513", "git_parents": ["56424142820037dbfa17e2a635473aa44005a730"], "node": "fbba7cf49c8cb0dbb047d3a143837f3535ab97b8", "parents": ["b20a72f1bfb0ac6ab2f6bca4a587b69fae5b7d90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056294 [wpt PR 61417] - \u003cmeta referrer\u003e should only apply when document is active, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n\u003cmeta referrer\u003e should only apply when document is active\n\nNote that referrer is a bit quirky, see the note in the spec:\nhttps://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/semantics.html#meta-referrer\n\nThis quirks makes it so that the ExecutionContext is updated directly\ninstead of the document, which is what other meta types do.\n\nBug: 536526176\nChange-Id: I38947b9849544e5b5f6fbf98250d319028d633ef\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8125036\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664718}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ecacb90aaf63b558905264b8fc901ae7b33ac3c0\nwpt-pr: 61417\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/referrer-policy/generic/meta-referrer-domparser.html"], "git_node": "bc6870a60366305c2dcc0911719fca59ef798ae6", "git_parents": ["20b65ff663a3cc11f8eca873e10635a6939e0513"], "node": "38a7b3a7c03778c1207a894c835d3c7a622f0de6", "parents": ["fbba7cf49c8cb0dbb047d3a143837f3535ab97b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joone Hur \u003cjoonehur@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056182 [wpt PR 61404] - Add scriptCount to Long Animation Frame timing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd scriptCount to Long Animation Frame timing\n\nIntroduce the `scriptCount` member on\n`PerformanceLongAnimationFrameTiming`. It reports the number of\ntop-level JavaScript entry points observed within the entry's interval,\ncounted regardless of each entry point's individual duration.\n\nTest: external/wpt/long-animation-frame/loaf-script-count.tentative.html\nBug: 534893134\nChange-Id: Ia3e03132ab9254c4ed7b3d944f188d7683210e89\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8115510\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Joone Hur \u003cjoonehur@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664728}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 073a34f030ad68af980d7a627e829900b003961b\nwpt-pr: 61404\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/long-animation-frame/loaf-script-count.tentative.html"], "git_node": "edbdf1eb1f1bb1e50544e0e40557c52ec95ac45f", "git_parents": ["bc6870a60366305c2dcc0911719fca59ef798ae6"], "node": "ae867c78007c50fc9a91fa397f71830101439f08", "parents": ["38a7b3a7c03778c1207a894c835d3c7a622f0de6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Awogbemila \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056237 [wpt PR 61411] - Implement scroll-axis-lock: none support for compositor scrolls, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement scroll-axis-lock: none support for compositor scrolls\n\nThis CL implements the scroll-axis-lock: none CSS property for\ncompositor-threaded scrolling (touch and wheel). This property allows\nfree diagonal scrolling without triggering axis locking (railing).\n\nTo support this, we introduce unconstrained scroll deltas alongside the\nstandard constrained deltas in the input pipeline. The unconstrained\ndeltas capture the user's raw scroll intent before railing is applied.\n\nWe retain the standard constrained deltas because they are still\nnecessary for correct scroll chaining. For example, on a horizontal-only\nscroller, a vertical scroll with a tiny horizontal component should not\nconsume the vertical delta if it fails to scroll. Using constrained\ndeltas allows the vertical delta to correctly chain to the parent\nscroller, whereas using unconstrained deltas would consume the delta and\nblock chaining.\n\nDesign doc:\nhttps://docs.google.com/document/d/1BvcEKG7Q4wOJhWIsdiymV9--hhxHK9Pb97rXHrs29ec/edit?tab=t.0#heading=h.q9bcgay8f2df\n\nBug: 479472367\nChange-Id: I936e2439c09589f4359dd72fce860d5aa2501869\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8012210\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Vladimir Levin \u003cvmpstr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Robert Flack \u003cflackr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David A \u003cawogbemila@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Dave Tapuska \u003cdtapuska@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664747}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4fa69bf9efab8291e72ff2f1c2e8b7628f6ac827\nwpt-pr: 61411\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock.html"], "git_node": "91bd782dc68d7e63026234ad82f8c280e916a5dd", "git_parents": ["edbdf1eb1f1bb1e50544e0e40557c52ec95ac45f"], "node": "661dae07d41f6f540b021d733f2646654f4b3932", "parents": ["ae867c78007c50fc9a91fa397f71830101439f08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056237 [wpt PR 61411] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61411\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/scroll-axis-lock.html.ini"], "git_node": "7234f35f8b9b39ac5cbc7fb99d7d92e4af9559fa", "git_parents": ["91bd782dc68d7e63026234ad82f8c280e916a5dd"], "node": "e9450797e5e6382e487de486d95a9c7d72458654", "parents": ["661dae07d41f6f540b021d733f2646654f4b3932"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056398 [wpt PR 61427] - [css-mixins] Test that @layer is dropped inside mixins, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Test that @layer is dropped inside mixins\n\nBlink already drops @layer inside mixins per the CSSWG resolution [0],\nbut existing tests only checked the mixin stayed valid, not that @layer\nwas dropped.\n\nAdd test cases asserting @layer is dropped at every depth inside a\nmixin, each keeping a sibling \"color: green\" rule to confirm only the\n@layer, not its container, was removed.\n\n[0] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/12417\n\nBug: 440050694\nChange-Id: I08c354d23e25f33ba0b843292bb931009570319d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8114962\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664819}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 55394a9b50ea93a00b8d229a9def5eff7555c3d6\nwpt-pr: 61427\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-parsing.html"], "git_node": "be76b29836a851008dc6c66fbc84191707808219", "git_parents": ["7234f35f8b9b39ac5cbc7fb99d7d92e4af9559fa"], "node": "f91f640b335e1c57b7156fed9f3396d1c52fb2a6", "parents": ["e9450797e5e6382e487de486d95a9c7d72458654"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056398 [wpt PR 61427] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61427\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-parsing.html.ini"], "git_node": "318963765b4349d6b39164885d4742026ecd60ad", "git_parents": ["be76b29836a851008dc6c66fbc84191707808219"], "node": "e16418cb5e236f04ba618856b8ba2c2be1ce3367", "parents": ["f91f640b335e1c57b7156fed9f3396d1c52fb2a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056279 [wpt PR 61415] - [compression-dictionary] Use nonce attribute as a fetch parameter., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Use nonce attribute as a fetch parameter.\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: I46785fd36a4ec78df54bbb462a92a32ec923aab5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8098863\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664828}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6f4b88171a950b6088e92446a51d0b3087226243\nwpt-pr: 61415\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src-nonce.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src-nonce.tentative.https.html.headers"], "git_node": "29af79036929f1967e7b5c4d6e8689b9ce629179", "git_parents": ["318963765b4349d6b39164885d4742026ecd60ad"], "node": "7f0089822b60b2aab880cd72244fbb604d0a53cf", "parents": ["e16418cb5e236f04ba618856b8ba2c2be1ce3367"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056279 [wpt PR 61415] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61415\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src-nonce.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "5a1135e36e218d06af31fc41c0d727bb9d6773ad", "git_parents": ["29af79036929f1967e7b5c4d6e8689b9ce629179"], "node": "0a8180e13e710581fb305a1f4d20012da745173d", "parents": ["7f0089822b60b2aab880cd72244fbb604d0a53cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056367 [wpt PR 61421] - Propagate attr() taint through interpolable custom property transitions, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nPropagate attr() taint through interpolable custom property transitions\n\nFor custom property transitions, we were calculating is_attr_tainted\nonly in discrete transition cases. This allowed the flag to be laundered\naway in interpolable transitions.\n\nThis CL factors is_attr_tainted computation onto the common path and\npropagates it through the pipeline for interpolable transitions.\n\nFixed: 517746687\nChange-Id: I07a965b29838567d746fa48cb270c74c2bbdd6aa\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8102417\nReviewed-by: Kevin Ellis \u003ckevers@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664831}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 68b620f668ddf3fa5fe2167e0f1e9d71ebc65f22\nwpt-pr: 61421\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/attr-security-transition-interpolated.html"], "git_node": "f40bcfa6e8507191f022ce22513779bd203d693d", "git_parents": ["5a1135e36e218d06af31fc41c0d727bb9d6773ad"], "node": "fbbb170226153b58b9f08d26f9d76762b7d114ea", "parents": ["0a8180e13e710581fb305a1f4d20012da745173d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056285 [wpt PR 61416] - [compression-dictionary] Align handling of referrer and referrerpolicy with the spec PR., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Align handling of referrer and referrerpolicy with the spec PR.\n\nhttp://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/11620 follows what is done for\nrel=\"prefetch\", which does not override referrer and takes into account\nthe referrerpolicy attribute. Align Chromium with that behavior under\na runtime flag and add corresponding WPT tests.\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: Ia9f845dd8a1bd9c950c5ac302fba0f2d5eaf246c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8118407\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664847}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 69eb56728c4e02228dee97a3463df937a0d35ef1\nwpt-pr: 61416\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-referrer-and-referrerpolicy.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/fetch-options-worker.js"], "git_node": "27557fd5d6997c775d5583a8391e2fd818394f1e", "git_parents": ["f40bcfa6e8507191f022ce22513779bd203d693d"], "node": "f05a6d7f721cf0a58d3fa52528e0ca9fa443f563", "parents": ["fbbb170226153b58b9f08d26f9d76762b7d114ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056185 [wpt PR 61405] - Enable InitiatorUrl for ResourceTiming on static resources from CSS files, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEnable InitiatorUrl for ResourceTiming on static resources from CSS files\n\nBug: 40919714\nChange-Id: I5822ce4abf58b5304acbb7e1b8d43fb5aef561d0\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8066304\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Guohui Deng \u003cguohuideng@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664854}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6e795c4b6af805908b9608b49b2b46149b8c1221\nwpt-pr: 61405\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/resources/nested-dynamic-initiator.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/resources/nested-initiator.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/stylesheet-dynamic.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/stylesheet-static.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/tentative/stylesheet-initiated.html"], "git_node": "44b48361e9711b5182610ec211fbf1e98634718f", "git_parents": ["27557fd5d6997c775d5583a8391e2fd818394f1e"], "node": "2abd76580760a182abcd9838424a779f743ae3ac", "parents": ["f05a6d7f721cf0a58d3fa52528e0ca9fa443f563"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056185 [wpt PR 61405] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61405\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/stylesheet-dynamic.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/tentative/initiator-url/stylesheet-static.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/resource-timing/tentative/stylesheet-initiated.html.ini"], "git_node": "5859747e45130f8d5274ad343134b2ad84841bd2", "git_parents": ["44b48361e9711b5182610ec211fbf1e98634718f"], "node": "32c9e223bf5afd94c62f5b7132f480f48e389933", "parents": ["2abd76580760a182abcd9838424a779f743ae3ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056381 [wpt PR 61422] - [compression-dictionary] Add WPT test to ensure integrity attribute is ignored., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Add WPT test to ensure integrity attribute is ignored.\n\nSee https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#attr-link-integrity\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: I2454f5305b855b21ca40c2177fabb7ecbf2e9a2e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8117450\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1664905}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5fed9e8740e582a1099eca1400f86671c2ba26a0\nwpt-pr: 61422\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-integrity.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/fetch-options-worker.js"], "git_node": "4b6addc9bf9ef63ff9e298a0c9af79e32a523f56", "git_parents": ["5859747e45130f8d5274ad343134b2ad84841bd2"], "node": "525b937ded335781ffbed6e1e307f7ead8b04b3e", "parents": ["32c9e223bf5afd94c62f5b7132f480f48e389933"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056389 [wpt PR 61424] - Migrate MSE preload/play-then-seek-back coverage to WPT, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMigrate MSE preload/play-then-seek-back coverage to WPT\n\nAdd the missing preload=none error case and post-seek assertions to\nexternal/wpt/media-source/, then drop the internal tests.\n\nBug: 485677942\nChange-Id: I5eb945ab23b7775a40602c4b80e005ea850d110b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8123434\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Brian Sheedy \u003cbsheedy@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1665110}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: fdd9d8bc59b8b5dbe53cfcf7ce64b885871f204c\nwpt-pr: 61424\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/mediasource-play-then-seek-back.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/mediasource-preload.html"], "git_node": "e4886b531c8b1d47d583d07f336ee46f5406fc77", "git_parents": ["4b6addc9bf9ef63ff9e298a0c9af79e32a523f56"], "node": "855a8b702119a8d433c5568a9b6d651807abeb5f", "parents": ["525b937ded335781ffbed6e1e307f7ead8b04b3e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056389 [wpt PR 61424] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61424\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-preload.html.ini"], "git_node": "585529e6342510e53570f2f347cc9e3773ed94ef", "git_parents": ["e4886b531c8b1d47d583d07f336ee46f5406fc77"], "node": "a4bfb0e5518daed4d0b60a824ddcf54798b02e79", "parents": ["855a8b702119a8d433c5568a9b6d651807abeb5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexander Cooper \u003calcooper@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056421 [wpt PR 61430] - [WebXR] Detect all frame owners in DOM Overlay, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebXR] Detect all frame owners in DOM Overlay\n\nProcessOverlayHitTest downcasts the hit element to HTMLFrameElementBase\nto decide whether to walk the content frame subtree for cross-origin\ncontent. That base class only covers \u003ciframe\u003e and \u003cframe\u003e; content\nembedded via \u003cobject\u003e, \u003cembed\u003e, or \u003cfencedframe\u003e owns a content frame\nthrough HTMLFrameOwnerElement instead, so the cast returned null and\nthe cross-origin check was skipped.\n\nCast to HTMLFrameOwnerElement instead so every frame-owning element is\nsubject to the same origin check. Extend the ar_dom_overlay WPT with\nan \u003cobject\u003e variant of the existing cross-origin iframe test.\n\nTAG=agy\n\nFixed: 524418836\nChange-Id: I43830c7a669820dbb56c3a1792d9f7c6813d1c1e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8120459\nReviewed-by: Brian Sheedy \u003cbsheedy@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alexander Cooper \u003calcooper@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1665189}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4809b72f863e05ab1df710d3390547dd86694239\nwpt-pr: 61430\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webxr/dom-overlay/ar_dom_overlay.https.html"], "git_node": "5b80e629792cbec649e51189b8e2da5590bc0881", "git_parents": ["585529e6342510e53570f2f347cc9e3773ed94ef"], "node": "7ea4d5a1e8dc2caa0780e11f261bcb96bdbec0cc", "parents": ["a4bfb0e5518daed4d0b60a824ddcf54798b02e79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056421 [wpt PR 61430] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61430\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webxr/dom-overlay/ar_dom_overlay.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "2d471a2bdae6189536238ce7cd81ae4f4e1f1793", "git_parents": ["5b80e629792cbec649e51189b8e2da5590bc0881"], "node": "fe3e64269e058f37a991eef9bbcfb8153acbe0d5", "parents": ["7ea4d5a1e8dc2caa0780e11f261bcb96bdbec0cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jose Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056385 [wpt PR 61423] - ContainerTiming: tests for pre-paint attribution tracker, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nContainerTiming: tests for pre-paint attribution tracker\n\nSplit out of the pre-paint attribution tracker implementation CL to keep\nthat change focused on production code.\n\nAdds:\n- Unit tests for the ContainerTimingPaintAttributionTracker and for\n  ContainerTiming aggregation/caching under both flag states.\n- pre_paint_tree_walk_test.cc coverage for the container-timing dirty-bit\n  propagation and the ShouldInheritContainerTimingRoot cache.\n- display_lock_context_test.cc coverage for the container-timing\n  interaction with display locking.\n- container_timing_test_utils.h, shared by blink_unittests and\n  blink_perf_tests via unit_test_support.\n- WPTs for container timing roots with containertiming-ignore reporting\n  their own paints, plus a virtual test suite running the existing\n  container-timing WPTs with ContainerTimingPrepaintTraversal enabled.\n\nAll Container Timing Web Platform Tests pass with both the legacy\nimplementation and the prepaint optimization.\n\nBug: 489959278\nChange-Id: Iaad076cafb821c7807edb739db764b34072ed0bc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7979158\nCommit-Queue: Jos\u00e9 Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Michal Mocny \u003cmmocny@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1665238}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f64f3e13f0c456553639fd5c30a438204cc5dfe3\nwpt-pr: 61423\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-img-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-and-ignore-on-text-itself.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-img.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-text.html"], "git_node": "504b066de86eab2a5dea3cf72dfb8c778e41a961", "git_parents": ["2d471a2bdae6189536238ce7cd81ae4f4e1f1793"], "node": "7dbe84b86398298c555dc7e682e29559652cc5a8", "parents": ["fe3e64269e058f37a991eef9bbcfb8153acbe0d5"], "tags": []}, {"author