ps://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/ios/+log/e5683b9378..c3df8a6ea5\n    * src/third_party: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/third_party/+log/4cb40bab0b..acd7a3d156\n    * src/tools: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/tools/+log/2c58d1da16..bdb323cddd\n    DEPS diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/bb2a96f843..71f564d373/DEPS\n\n    BUG=None\n\n    Change-Id: I211a009b535ee8fb5b55733233cd63bb0443abfd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/483260\n    Bot-Commit: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: chromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cchromium-webrtc-autoroll@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48033}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/DEPS", "third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor"], "git_node": "9c2d156a09903bff8c80c28bb0d8995da93db453", "git_parents": ["110c251dcab1726fba5bbbc3937d6631b6759c76"], "node": "d7a08898cb211c01bc3c1e83c9172296ac97b98c", "parents": ["3696bbcc28aea78fa7ed8c30c7cf52dd2b232228"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from ef8d997c72\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ef8d997c72f85a058bf0bcb0525793ac2b4776ee\n    [SCReAM] Self-contain Application-Limited detection via fixed-window acked rate\n\n    Previously, SCReAM v2 did not autonomously monitor the actual received (acked) bitrate on the channel to evaluate if a session was truly Application-Limited.\n\n    With this CL, ScreamV2 tracks the received (acked) transfer rate over a fixed 100ms window and evaluates is_application_limited internally by checking if the received rate is less than 0.9 times the target rate. When periodic padding or probing bursts are transmitted, the receive rate scales up close to the target rate and automatically unfreezes the reference window so BWE can adapt upwards to full link capacity. In addition, leaving ALR when the receive rate is close to the target rate ensures that RTT and feedback hold time estimates are updated faster.\n\n    In addition, ReceivedRateWindow and AlrThreshold parameters have been exposed via field trials in ScreamV2Parameters to allow runtime configuration.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:447037083\n    Change-Id: I1ba1a6f098944e79431e46a8547149f2b084c610\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482680\n    Commit-Queue: Per Kjellander \u003cperkj@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Bj\u00f6rn Terelius \u003cterelius@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48034}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_feedback.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_network_controller_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_parameters.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/congestion_controller/scream/scream_v2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/analyze_bwe.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/log_scream_simulation.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_tools/rtc_event_log_visualizer/log_scream_simulation.h"], "git_node": "39c7d6b40c869530c88807ccdb14ad11eb71ca92", "git_parents": ["9c2d156a09903bff8c80c28bb0d8995da93db453"], "node": "5043da32c818be2733ff6d1ee1643a177bc2ebd8", "parents": ["d7a08898cb211c01bc3c1e83c9172296ac97b98c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from ed794b0fea\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ed794b0fea213577ef6258ece6ffa2055d11c1a0\n    Don't initialize jvm in PeerConnectionFactory if it is already initialized.\n\n    Goal is to fix PeerConnectionFactoryTest.NativeToJavaPeerConnectionFactory flakiness on Android (https://ci.chromium.org/ui/tests/p/webrtc/clusters/testname-v4/58398f78c8a0f7acb3962fe872b81723):\n\n    # Fatal error in: ../../modules/utility/source/jvm_android.cc, line 218\n    # last system error: 0\n    # Check failed: !g_jvm\n\n    Change-Id: I3c90a5af0bb9c2089aa26b8cc99bb595eca56d62\n    Bug: None\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482940\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48035}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/utility/include/jvm_android.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/utility/source/jvm_android.cc"], "git_node": "957136a74a4d560ccfea654b1dc6b8a077dc70c3", "git_parents": ["39c7d6b40c869530c88807ccdb14ad11eb71ca92"], "node": "6405098acec89d1a7cd4898a4399ef81500be118", "parents": ["5043da32c818be2733ff6d1ee1643a177bc2ebd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from ca896656ed\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/ca896656edeb2eb663868b5b14efd6eba9372199\n    Validate RTP header extension IDs in ParseExtmap\n\n    Bug: b/522284100\n    Change-Id: Ib782e02e6b33b1b703a2551f9f4c178cdfafefda\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/483240\n    Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Mirko Bonadei \u003cmbonadei@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48036}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "abe83c9f6cdee0245519a5e64d02c3f5bde33e94", "git_parents": ["957136a74a4d560ccfea654b1dc6b8a077dc70c3"], "node": "a145e5a3b7cc10eabb394e04e9808f4e23bbfd5c", "parents": ["6405098acec89d1a7cd4898a4399ef81500be118"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from d57bda1bb6\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/d57bda1bb6222d9606f683fdfc50f0fbe0033f8b\n    Reland \"Make RtpHeaderExtensionId(int) explicit\"\n\n    This reverts commit 031d798a20cc5d9c867598a38632accb20c6effe.\n\n    Reason for revert: Revised constructor deprecation approach\n\n    Original change's description:\n    \u003e Revert \"Make RtpHeaderExtensionId(int) explicit\"\n    \u003e\n    \u003e This reverts commit 9cb2a61b06bacaeb9a7abedc1d00517d7f79548d.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Reason for revert: Suspected downstream failures.\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Failure Link: https://fusion2.corp.google.com/invocations/abc66f5c-f5bc-4767-8ff8-e67efeaa0f7c/targets/%2F%2Fbuzz%2Ftest%2Fpclf%2Ftests:absolute_capture_time_test_experiments_launched;config=a544fae14671853db631fbeeb923d84e665cd2045db88e266d17af360c6b5925/tests?q=status:failed%20OR%20status:broken%20OR%20status:cancelled%20OR%20status:running%20OR%20status:timed_out%20OR%20status:tool_failure%20label:buildbucket-8678846321400548705\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Original change's description:\n    \u003e \u003e Make RtpHeaderExtensionId(int) explicit\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Make RtpHeaderExtensionId(int) constructor explicit to prevent\n    \u003e \u003e implicit conversions. Added a deprecated template constructor to\n    \u003e \u003e allow implicit conversion downstream to avoid breaking them. Also\n    \u003e \u003e added explicit constructor for uint8_t to avoid matching the template\n    \u003e \u003e in WebRTC.\n    \u003e \u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Bug: webrtc:514817938\n    \u003e \u003e Change-Id: I5f8a03dc2ffb6d6d76164e734e1627f07727da49\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482540\n    \u003e \u003e Commit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48017}\n    \u003e\n    \u003e Bug: webrtc:514817938\n    \u003e No-Presubmit: true\n    \u003e No-Tree-Checks: true\n    \u003e No-Try: true\n    \u003e Change-Id: I367b804a5f3af448f1ce49b8f178a079edab1612\n    \u003e Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482800\n    \u003e Auto-Submit: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    \u003e Bot-Commit: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    \u003e Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    \u003e Commit-Queue: rubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com \u003crubber-stamper@appspot.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    \u003e Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48018}\n\n    Bug: webrtc:514817938\n    Change-Id: I476b96e2bdf869a27abe5dd46f4f67693d82d5cd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482820\n    Commit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48037}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/rtp_header_extension_id.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/rtp_header_extension_id_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/payload_type_picker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/rtp_rtcp/source/rtp_rtcp_impl2_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0096.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0138.patch"], "git_node": "cfe1d98295f2b652d5cd419099154a925aed94a6", "git_parents": ["abe83c9f6cdee0245519a5e64d02c3f5bde33e94"], "node": "3acb02ba354d315600904089b839656ac7a6b818", "parents": ["a145e5a3b7cc10eabb394e04e9808f4e23bbfd5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 (MOZ) - upstream d57bda1bb6 deprecated implicit conversion of RtpHeaderExtensionId\n", "files": ["media/webrtc/signaling/gtest/audioconduit_unittests.cpp"], "git_node": "da7cd5b6dc1b188b9b50443f23c1411b98bfc8d7", "git_parents": ["cfe1d98295f2b652d5cd419099154a925aed94a6"], "node": "e9d39ce4f2824f9ddc3d403ac05ae06513d5cd04", "parents": ["3acb02ba354d315600904089b839656ac7a6b818"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from a66df29015\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/a66df290150d59e82295555508b97eeb450e850e\n    Fix Multiple SSL clocks issue when running PeerConnectionIntegrationTestWithFakeClock.\n\n    This is needed because reference deletion of DtlsTransport and OpenSSLStreamAdapter is queued asynchronously on the network_thread.\n\n    # Fatal error in: ../../rtc_base/openssl_stream_adapter.cc, line 1121\n    # last system error: 0\n    # Check failed: g_clock_for_testing == clock\n    # Multiple SSL clocks for testing is not implemented*** SIGABRT received at time=1781709018 on cpu 4 ***\n\n    https://ci.chromium.org/ui/tests/p/webrtc/clusters?interval=24h&selectedMetrics=human-cls-failed-presubmit%2Ccritical-failures-exonerated%2Cfailures&orderBy=critical-failures-exonerated&orderDir=desc&q=PeerConnectionIntegrationTestWithFakeClock\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: Ie1068ddd338fbfb33883761fa19d0495162eddff\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/483460\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Jeremy Leconte \u003cjleconte@google.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48038}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/rtc_base/openssl_stream_adapter.cc"], "git_node": "f9ca2df178d495ee6b18d2dfc6ea3311f262136f", "git_parents": ["da7cd5b6dc1b188b9b50443f23c1411b98bfc8d7"], "node": "b8286939adea88983915cbe5cfeb64e68eeef2d3", "parents": ["e9d39ce4f2824f9ddc3d403ac05ae06513d5cd04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3c141cd8a3\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3c141cd8a38f2f9cdb2f55915d068f5e7376074c\n    Update WebRTC code version (2026-06-18T04:06:56).\n\n    Bug: None\n    Change-Id: I0d25ec14de073caf931ecc194a5ba1da63a83c35\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/483600\n    Bot-Commit: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: webrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com \u003cwebrtc-version-updater@webrtc-ci.iam.gserviceaccount.com\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48039}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/call/version.cc"], "git_node": "caf69adf102d9cdda8dc4bd6e9b57ee1f302754e", "git_parents": ["f9ca2df178d495ee6b18d2dfc6ea3311f262136f"], "node": "cf7b5da29a064fe3d93898f030a86234121d1bbd", "parents": ["b8286939adea88983915cbe5cfeb64e68eeef2d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 2bd5f8f65c\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/2bd5f8f65cf336b7a135d1e0139203eddd75e8ba\n    Remove all untagged Subscribe methods\n\n    Bug: webrtc:465197113\n    Change-Id: Iafb4042dcc1c9e41ff8d222af8bb68b9011e0b0a\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482720\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Auto-Submit: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48040}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/p2p/base/port_interface.h"], "git_node": "c6973dd91dcc733fcdd818f1d60b0b63d5b7e27d", "git_parents": ["caf69adf102d9cdda8dc4bd6e9b57ee1f302754e"], "node": "0baad6398b003e355a2c33a54147ca06e4d8e00f", "parents": ["cf7b5da29a064fe3d93898f030a86234121d1bbd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 6d313ff83e\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/6d313ff83e12492d68be4e56b59150937e0230ae\n    snap: cache early dtls packets in race condition\n\n    If SCTP is negotiated after the DTLS handshake has been completed there exists a race condition with SNAP wherein the answerer can start opening  channels (and send data) before the answer with the sctp-init arrives at the offerer.\n\n    Cache a limited amount of decrypted and authenticated packets and replay them after receiving the answer. This problem also exists for non-snap but is mitigated by the symmetric open on both sides so the loss in one direction does not matter much.\n\n    Note: doing a \"half-open\" on the offerer socket does not work as it can not send acknowledgements of received packets due to the missing peer verification tag.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:426480601\n    Change-Id: Ic8ee193b6ca8774943e19e37073814af144ce7d4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/478160\n    Reviewed-by: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: Philipp Hancke \u003cphilipp.hancke@googlemail.com\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Victor Boivie \u003cboivie@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48041}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/sctp/dcsctp_transport.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/sctp/dcsctp_transport.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/sctp/sctp_transport_internal.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0084.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0094.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0096.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0101.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0103.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/data_channel_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sctp_transport_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/test/pc/sctp/fake_sctp_transport.h"], "git_node": "bb35967c8e825427ad49735d5b272d65eab381c7", "git_parents": ["c6973dd91dcc733fcdd818f1d60b0b63d5b7e27d"], "node": "dc9a108d8bdb9069a226ab05151fb93747a6bf08", "parents": ["0baad6398b003e355a2c33a54147ca06e4d8e00f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 65ae614737\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/65ae614737f3a0824c0ab6a1c49a357723900bb1\n    Rename StopDecodeTimer to UpdateDecodeTimeEstimate in VCMTiming.\n\n    Renamed to better reflect that it is used to provide a measured decode duration, rather than stopping a timing state.\n\n    Bug: b/493549134\n    Change-Id: Iecd4a327fb28de7e2d95efc6808cbd5e285c82f5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/483360\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48042}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/generic_decoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/timing.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/timing.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/timing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0087.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/frame_decode_timing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/timing/simulator/rendering_tracker.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "9497b39220528c2b563e7a2535263a20a1e3c803", "git_parents": ["bb35967c8e825427ad49735d5b272d65eab381c7"], "node": "5e9fe7ac5b99d8bf2e094826c51cb861c3d177e2", "parents": ["dc9a108d8bdb9069a226ab05151fb93747a6bf08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from eff99934d9\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/eff99934d9b7977586ae82c98376a45dbe710d91\n    Allow SDP munging in peerconnection_unittests\n\n    Configure peerconnection_unittests to allow specific munging types\n    (such as kVideoCodecsFmtp, kAudioCodecsRemoved, etc.) under the\n    WebRTC-NoSdpMangleAllowForTesting field trial, as these tests\n    explicitly perform SDP munging to verify behavior.\n\n    Specifically allow CCFB munging (kAudioCodecsRtcpFb and\n    kVideoCodecsRtcpFb) in tests that negotiate CCFB and use\n    PeerConnectionTestWrapper, due to CCFB negotiation asymmetry.\n\n    Refactored CreatePeerConnection helpers in tests to use overloading\n    instead of default arguments.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:414284082\n    Change-Id: I2cb72fce127dcde8e334408e3a704d8b618058d5\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/482360\n    Commit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48043}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0096.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/congestion_control_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/media_session.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_bundle_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_crypto_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_data_channel_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_encodings_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_header_extension_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_ice_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_interface_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_jsep_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_rtp_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_signaling_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/peer_connection_simulcast_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/pranswer_switch_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/rtc_stats_integrationtest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_munging_detector_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/pc/sdp_offer_answer_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "59ac695b7bc2b402c63baadc3fc0d4f811dd9e8d", "git_parents": ["9497b39220528c2b563e7a2535263a20a1e3c803"], "node": "0879251ff4001748dc6800f7462f8113e2abc9fd", "parents": ["5e9fe7ac5b99d8bf2e094826c51cb861c3d177e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from edb60993da\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/edb60993da28bdb3e5bf347da9035a4c5f447983\n    Reassign ownership of WebRTC documentat