an@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 4078717fde\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/4078717fdea29d41b388fa6f3af04074dcbc6ce4\n    Update how complete frames are reported to DefaultVideoJitterTiming.\n\n    Add FrameInfo struct and move logic that decides whether to update the TimestampExtrapolator from VideoStreamBufferController to DefaultVideoJitterTiming.\n\n    Bug: b/493549134\n    Change-Id: I4efcd328b36c8f408cae19d3c403414195c85da0\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/485600\n    Reviewed-by: Rasmus Brandt \u003cbrandtr@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Commit-Queue: \u00c5sa Persson \u003casapersson@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48093}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/video/timing/video_jitter_timing_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/default_video_jitter_timing.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/default_video_jitter_timing.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/default_video_jitter_timing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/timing.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/timing.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/modules/video_coding/timing/timing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0057.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0059.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/frame_decode_timing_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_buffer_controller_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "f3df84d4fd59e31e3ee1236f09bc76aa0a95938a", "git_parents": ["89a9567975f892b1501a4b0e3aa10921d5c68bd4"], "node": "a918e415784205353b6b75f408f21db74d24316b", "parents": ["af732216883db89e43c0e992f06a41676ef9b485"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 3a7e6b27eb\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/3a7e6b27ebb2f9fae32538904d5dda32b32e6ca8\n    Generate keyframes only for requested SSRCs\n\n    Add WebRTC-Video-PerSsrcKeyframes field trial that enables the existing\n    functionality (guarded by x-google-per-layer-pli FMTP parameter) to\n    generate keyframes per SSRC.\n\n    There is a small difference to x-google-per-layer-pli implementation:\n    unlike in x-google-per-layer-pli, SEA doesn't force separate encoders\n    when the functionality enabled by the field trial. It would be better to\n    let multistream/SVC encoders decide how to handle per-stream keyframe\n    requests.\n\n    Also fixed an issue in VideoStreamEncoder::SendKeyFrame where a new\n    keyframe request always overrode the previous non-executed one.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:527515375, b/527798266\n    Change-Id: I05b1cedf09adcbec3471b255b1676a114ea037fd\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/485561\n    Commit-Queue: Sergey Silkin \u003cssilkin@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Erik Spr\u00e5ng \u003csprang@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48094}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/experiments/field_trials.py", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/engine/simulcast_encoder_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0027.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0068.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0102.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0131.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/BUILD.gn", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_impl.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_send_stream_impl_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/video/video_stream_encoder_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "ccd294f95182c30e16891c5084ace26696046cda", "git_parents": ["f3df84d4fd59e31e3ee1236f09bc76aa0a95938a"], "node": "5848f20b1e06c5b1d2899188cf5a1fbc38cf77a0", "parents": ["a918e415784205353b6b75f408f21db74d24316b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from df5d5ee522\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/df5d5ee522b02ce53fb3d90be42dd5e10ccbd38e\n    Remove special handling of -1 in bandwidth modifiers\n\n    This is nonstandard, and appears unused.\n\n    Bug: webrtc:502249086\n    Change-Id: I5b35b43e8ca1d55802e377511d6afa151459bbe4\n    Reviewed-on: https://webrtc-review.googlesource.com/c/src/+/485820\n    Commit-Queue: Harald Alvestrand \u003chta@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Reviewed-by: Danil Chapovalov \u003cdanilchap@webrtc.org\u003e\n    Cr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#48095}\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/README.mozilla.last-vendor", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/webrtc_sdp_unittest.cc"], "git_node": "658513a5e842817e7c934277656734a66caa2bfa", "git_parents": ["ccd294f95182c30e16891c5084ace26696046cda"], "node": "7219dd437119ec33cf9e4ce40a54573dd6226cde", "parents": ["5848f20b1e06c5b1d2899188cf5a1fbc38cf77a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Froman \u003cmfroman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049872 - Vendor libwebrtc from 085d29eb6a\n\nUpstream commit: https://webrtc.googlesource.com/src/+/085d29eb6a38fd418f7b3f71994ccf547d941b06\n    Roll chromium_revision 35ac7eab8b..870545d8b5 (1651839:1653577)\n\n    Change log: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+log/35ac7eab8b..870545d8b5\n    Full diff: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/+/35ac7eab8b..870545d8b5\n\n    Changed dependencies\n    * fuchsia_version: version:32.20260611.1.1..version:32.20260625.4.1\n    * src/build: https://chromium.googlesource.com/chromium/src/build/+log/0cd0da38e2..8edf031b7f\n    * src/buildtools/linux