e02260beb0fd6d\nmr -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nms -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nmy -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nnb-NO -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nne-NP -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nnl -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nnn-NO -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\noc -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\npa-IN -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\npl -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\npt-BR -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\npt-PT -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nrm -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nro -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nru -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nsk -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nsl -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nson -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nsq -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nsr -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nsv-SE -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nta -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nte -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nth -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\ntl -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\ntr -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\ntrs -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nuk -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nur -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nuz -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nvi -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nwo -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nxh -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nzam -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nzh-CN -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\nzh-TW -\u003e cbeced2b93e116c0932e19ee95e02260beb0fd6d\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "12196160355ba9888e67f41450ad31095c68cbba", "git_parents": ["c67d0e1e803a8d7fb5a84c553a1cc5c22d97d761"], "node": "2e66e0e17b8b1e0c7c0528439bbd03b863438a15", "parents": ["fcc67e7aa36545fa5f5129795c0c508820cd666a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teh \u003cjteh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053730: Fix handling of the enter key when assigning keys in about:keyboard. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs\n\n1. Map the enter key code correctly.\n  Previously, the key code was invalid, which caused severe breakage when enter was assigned.\n2. Don't allow unmodified enter to be assigned.\n  This is very likely to cause confusion at best, brokenness at worst, given the broad usage of the enter key in various different contexts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313139\n", "files": ["browser/components/customkeys/CustomKeysParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/customkeys/tests/browser/browser_aboutKeyboard.js"], "git_node": "31e9253b7d96f02c23a21501cbee83a43d21c167", "git_parents": ["12196160355ba9888e67f41450ad31095c68cbba"], "node": "7c1e4259cc7c3621696fe41cca8c4593bb84e7cc", "parents": ["2e66e0e17b8b1e0c7c0528439bbd03b863438a15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046954 - Sandbox - Fix RDD Vulkan sandbox policy for display server access. r=jld,sandbox-reviewers\n\nEnable brokered socket/connect syscalls in the RDD sandbox and add narrow\nMAY_CONNECT rules for Wayland and X11 display sockets so EGL can connect\nfor EGL_MESA_image_dma_buf_export during Vulkan video decode.\n\nOn XWayland, both the Wayland socket and the X11 socket (/tmp/.X11-unix/X*)\nare now allowed since EGL may connect via either path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306340\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/common/test/SandboxTestingChildTests.h", "security/sandbox/linux/SandboxFilter.cpp", "security/sandbox/linux/broker/SandboxBrokerPolicyFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "5ec2f029d26ae5d65e4af3ad8c5e0ca3e838f0ab", "git_parents": ["31e9253b7d96f02c23a21501cbee83a43d21c167"], "node": "468d16e93a0c418f64f1e7c6dd3be1277b351d6b", "parents": ["7c1e4259cc7c3621696fe41cca8c4593bb84e7cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055213 - Fix WebCompat Reporter design issues. r=android-reviewers,rebecatudor273\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312459\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/ui/BrokenSiteReasonListItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/ui/ReadOnlyUrlField.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/ui/WebCompatReporter.kt"], "git_node": "ab3a1acf75b65f7fcc2c5960960a917ef95c8dad", "git_parents": ["5ec2f029d26ae5d65e4af3ad8c5e0ca3e838f0ab"], "node": "825fab3156edd1eb87556481c66b79e6d3feaea7", "parents": ["468d16e93a0c418f64f1e7c6dd3be1277b351d6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054503 - Add happy_eyeballs_h3_discovery_by_resolver telemetry, r=necko-reviewers,sunil\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312043\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HappyEyeballsConnectionAttempt.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/happy_eyeballs_glue/src/lib.rs", "netwerk/protocol/http/happy_eyeballs_glue/src/metrics.rs", "netwerk/protocol/http/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "c5b85ebbe5e11676569dc48bb0cde3e349c4e165", "git_parents": ["ab3a1acf75b65f7fcc2c5960960a917ef95c8dad"], "node": "c7e72f94f367f855f5b2728a13f73fe8a744c335", "parents": ["825fab3156edd1eb87556481c66b79e6d3feaea7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055834 - Reconcile interned data stores when loading a WebRender capture. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThe interner (scene builder thread) and the data store (render backend\nthread) are serialized independently and at slightly different points when\nsaving a capture, so the data store snapshot can lag the interner by a scene\nbuild. An item interned on the last frame is then present in the interner's\nmap but its insertion has not been applied to the saved data store.\n\nWhen such a capture is loaded, the scene is rebuilt: re-interning that item\nreturns the existing handle without emitting a new insertion, so the data\nstore slot stays empty and frame building panics with \"Bad datastore lookup\".\n\nReconstruct the missing data store slots from the interned keys on load\n(StoreData: From\u003cKey\u003e) so the loaded frame is self-consistent. Only empty\nslots are filled, so consistent captures are unaffected.\n\nA better fix would be to overhaul wrench captures with some synchorization so that\nscenes/frames/resources are captured in the right order and ensure that no transaction\nraces with the capture, but I don't have the badwidth for that right now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313178\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs"], "git_node": "4ea4efd965e74bd7bde6c2b5d88a624ff972ee4a", "git_parents": ["c5b85ebbe5e11676569dc48bb0cde3e349c4e165"], "node": "6c729ce4766e32817db680a0b05776570bafce39", "parents": ["c7e72f94f367f855f5b2728a13f73fe8a744c335"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055834 - Call begin_frame before loading external textures in a WebRender capture. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nRenderer::load_capture creates GL textures for external texture-backed images\nbefore calling device.begin_frame(), which trips the\ndebug_assert!(self.inside_frame) in Device::create_texture for captures that\ncontain such images.\n\nMove begin_frame() ahead of the external image loading loop.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313180\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs"], "git_node": "de2a9b4f88bccafc8aac890b8230c7a2f21bcf0b", "git_parents": ["4ea4efd965e74bd7bde6c2b5d88a624ff972ee4a"], "node": "22a25825689800e5c1332d17960925fc0f87ca1e", "parents": ["6c729ce4766e32817db680a0b05776570bafce39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055834 - Serialize scene-spatial-tree in WebRender capture sequences. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nSceneBuilderThread::save_capture_sequence serialized the interners and scene\nbut omitted the scene spatial tree, while the capture load path\n(RenderBackend) requires scene-spatial-tree-*.ron. As a result no capture\nsequence could be replayed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313186\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs"], "git_node": "3b7c6dc29c79ddb3bedc0cfe0f23fa4cea61f53f", "git_parents": ["de2a9b4f88bccafc8aac890b8230c7a2f21bcf0b"], "node": "d6951e414d1c053efce0020af056fd8c65bb8e40", "parents": ["22a25825689800e5c1332d17960925fc0f87ca1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053260 - Set the same limit to WebGL buffer sizes as WebGPU. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nUncoditionally, just like in WebGPU.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310999\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLBuffer.cpp"], "git_node": "e8cfa05986c6d825badf78cb339c5c23e2e1509a", "git_parents": ["3b7c6dc29c79ddb3bedc0cfe0f23fa4cea61f53f"], "node": "10c145d3f4b29d332d8002f9feacbb3788a28901", "parents": ["d6951e414d1c053efce0020af056fd8c65bb8e40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053261 - Allow overlapping vertex groups. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe code was previously assuming that the vertex stride is always larger than the vertex size which is not necessarily true per spec. This patches fixes that by computing the number of times the stride fits in the buffer after having removed the size of the last element (following a similar logic to what the (much better) webgpu spec describes to validate the equivalent API.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310994\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLContext.h"], "git_node": "87adcb2b303543f1b76816e3787efae96273a62a", "git_parents": ["e8cfa05986c6d825badf78cb339c5c23e2e1509a"], "node": "a96f15b9b73248f38dec7c4412ac22f0d9d82afe", "parents": ["10c145d3f4b29d332d8002f9feacbb3788a28901"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053615 - Show the Bookmarked explanation for bookmark-type suggestions r=urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312711\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderBookmarkKeywords.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderInputHistory.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderTopSites.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_result_explanations.js"], "git_node": "3657b09ce87e60034f2ae05ee24932becf692a87", "git_parents": ["87adcb2b303543f1b76816e3787efae96273a62a"], "node": "bd3d3ce2c712e92ca0e1180e44392673255a9a4e", "parents": ["a96f15b9b73248f38dec7c4412ac22f0d9d82afe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055856 - Update gfx SanityTest to load with a resource:// URL in a content process. r=Gijs,gfx-reviewers,aosmond\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312717\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_all_files_referenced.js", "dom/security/nsContentSecurityUtils.cpp", "toolkit/components/gfx/SanityTest.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/gfx/content/gfxFrameScript.js", "toolkit/components/gfx/content/sanitytest.html", "toolkit/components/gfx/jar.mn"], "git_node": "2b41cf04a5cc0f3f5d899763c80d4296a4f98f99", "git_parents": ["3657b09ce87e60034f2ae05ee24932becf692a87"], "node": "a946e0b47e0c41316b7074acc6ee24dd05520482", "parents": ["bd3d3ce2c712e92ca0e1180e44392673255a9a4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Eden Chuang \u003cechuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056219 - Isolate remoteDebugger_freeze_syncloop test resources per run to fix perma-fail in test-verify. r=dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\n\nThe test coordinates its owner frame, nav page and shared worker through\nprocess-global fixed names: the SharedWorker name, two BroadcastChannel names,\nand a single module-global timer in hang.sjs. When test-verify reruns the test\nmany times in one browser (and in chaos mode), stale frame/nav pages left in\nbfcache stay subscribed to the same-named BroadcastChannels and react to\ncommands meant for a later run, desyncing the freeze/thaw sequence; overlapping\nrequests to hang.sjs also clobbered its single timer and dropped a response,\nleaving the worker permanently parked in its sync XHR (the reported deadlock).\n\nScope every run with a unique token: the test generates it, threads it through\nthe frame and nav page URLs, and uses it to suffix the SharedWorker and both\nBroadcastChannel names. hang.sjs now keeps each pending timer in a set so\nconcurrent requests can't drop each other's response.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313109\n", "files": ["dom/workers/test/remoteDebugger_freeze_syncloop_frame.html", "dom/workers/test/remoteDebugger_freeze_syncloop_hang.sjs", "dom/workers/test/remoteDebugger_freeze_syncloop_nav.html", "dom/workers/test/test_remoteDebugger_freeze_syncloop.html"], "git_node": "10c93311a10423c9a6164638bf00eeee377bf551", "git_parents": ["2b41cf04a5cc0f3f5d899763c80d4296a4f98f99"], "node": "c3d90ce72c3443dd270dba4eb46faaf56c1ae8d6", "parents": ["a946e0b47e0c41316b7074acc6ee24dd05520482"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056154 - Extract search optimization model classes from the AwesomeBar concept r=android-reviewers,nalexander,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312967\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/Suggestions.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/optimizedsuggestions/FlightSuggestion.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/optimizedsuggestions/SportSuggestion.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/optimizedsuggestions/StockSuggestion.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/utils/FlightSuggestionDataProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/utils/SportSuggestionDataProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/utils/StockSuggestionDataProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/compose/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/compose/browser/awesomebar/internal/utils/SuggestionUtils.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/awesomebar/AwesomeBar.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/awesomebar/optimizedsuggestions/FlightSuggestionModel.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/concept/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/concept/awesomebar/optimizedsuggestions/SportSuggestionModel.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/optimizedsuggestions/CombinedSuggestionsDataSource.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/optimizedsuggestions/FlightSuggestion.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/optimizedsuggestions/SportSuggestions.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/optimizedsuggestions/StockSuggestion.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/FlightsOnlineSuggestionProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/SportsOnlineSuggestionProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/StocksOnlineSuggestionProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/FakeCombinedOnlineSuggestionDataSource.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/FlightsOnlineSuggestionProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/SportsOnlineSuggestionProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/awesomebar/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/awesomebar/provider/StocksOnlineSuggestionProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/fxsuggest/datasource/CombinedOnlineSuggestionDataSource.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/fxsuggest/parser/FlightsSuggestionParser.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/fxsuggest/parser/SportsSuggestionParser.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/fxsuggest/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/fxsuggest/parser/StocksSuggestionParser.kt"], "git_node": "075f29d6164833cfd46adea836a86a61dfab5ea7", "git_parents": ["10c93311a10423c9a6164638bf00eeee377bf551"], "node": "b15f598f1e5f89280f21de5f1a1b6f3f0db1335b", "parents": ["c3d90ce72c3443dd270dba4eb46faaf56c1ae8d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mugurell \u003cMugurell@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1934909 - Use UI context for measuring UI widgets r=android-reviewers,moyin\n\nAs per the official documentation from\nhttps://developer.android.com/develop/adaptive-apps/guides/support-connected-displays#use-the-right-context\n\n\"The activity context contains information about the display and is always\nadjusted for the display area in which the activity appears. This lets you\nget the correct information about the display density or window metrics of\nyour app. Always use the activity context (or another UI-based context) to\nget information about the current window or display.\"\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313228\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/Fragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/FragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/SettingsTest.kt"], "git_node": "1758f1b8531cfa6a5c924ea747385effb3038fc0", "git_parents": ["075f29d6164833cfd46adea836a86a61dfab5ea7"], "node": "a3bd54cfbb64520adcbe84cdc46830acfea1523c", "parents": ["b15f598f1e5f89280f21de5f1a1b6f3f0db1335b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056558 r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313362\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.cpp", "gfx/layers/ipc/CompositorBridgeParent.h", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderBridgeParent.cpp"], "git_node": "076f33aea8c3b2cc635b6ff289cb05dd42e185ed", "git_parents": ["1758f1b8531cfa6a5c924ea747385effb3038fc0"], "node": "3f94f37fa7f3f952f7acea8b49cc713f0bd605e1", "parents": ["a3bd54cfbb64520adcbe84cdc46830acfea1523c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056194 - Add accuracy guidance to profiler-analysis skill r=padenot,ai4dev-reviewers\n\nI've noticed that sometimes profiler-analysis skill gives some findings\nvery confidently without fully checking the source code. It might result in\nwasted engineering time and might be frustrating.\n\nThis patch adds a new accuracy section to the skill to make sure that\nthe agent always try to validate its assumption before presenting them.\nAnd if can't validate, it never presents as facts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312982\n", "files": [".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "fcb68c8f40cea6deb8a73d29df01b1a3fdfe13c4", "git_parents": ["076f33aea8c3b2cc635b6ff289cb05dd42e185ed"], "node": "3e649c150e70f9dd7ddec89c84ca5ad01b4eafa0", "parents": ["3f94f37fa7f3f952f7acea8b49cc713f0bd605e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055793 - Clear about:logging uploaded profiles before testing empty state. r=profiler-reviewers,canova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312695\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/tests/browser/browser_about_logging.js"], "git_node": "d4e0095e18607bf153b2349bbd4e9840b2fd4239", "git_parents": ["fcb68c8f40cea6deb8a73d29df01b1a3fdfe13c4"], "node": "56f885365bb4072f24fe866f31e154fc92f21d8c", "parents": ["3e649c150e70f9dd7ddec89c84ca5ad01b4eafa0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054499 - extension-popup-panel body border-radius should match panel border-radius when Nova is enabled. r=willdurand,desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305353\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/extension-popup-panel.css", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_popup_corners.js"], "git_node": "236586c73638a512b26abcdbfedecc7fad504fe6", "git_parents": ["d4e0095e18607bf153b2349bbd4e9840b2fd4239"], "node": "5d3eb76c3ecacbbbf6da25641475e4230c964806", "parents": ["56f885365bb4072f24fe866f31e154fc92f21d8c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052620 - Opening a downloaded file immediately from the pop-up should remove the blue dot from the menu. r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312978\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/snackbar/SnackbarBinding.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/snackbar/SnackbarBindingTest.kt"], "git_node": "17d9c56a2b5e0cd4e6a6003da8e598c7ae0a8260", "git_parents": ["236586c73638a512b26abcdbfedecc7fad504fe6"], "node": "af9b49b8fdf2cff01c5bcc791f6216cfcbaf0df9", "parents": ["5d3eb76c3ecacbbbf6da25641475e4230c964806"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo McArdle \u003cleo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049610 - [devtools] add mdn icon to links in compat/inactive tooltips r=devtools-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308214\n", "files": ["devtools/client/locales/en-US/tooltips.ftl", "devtools/client/shared/components/MdnLink.css", "devtools/client/shared/widgets/tooltip/css-compatibility-tooltip-helper.js", "devtools/client/shared/widgets/tooltip/inactive-css-tooltip-helper.js", "devtools/client/themes/tooltips.css", "devtools/server/actors/utils/inactive-property-helper.js", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2049610_devtools_mdn_icon_tooltips.py"], "git_node": "9770f4153cb800356c5161298ceb9148cb14d829", "git_parents": ["17d9c56a2b5e0cd4e6a6003da8e598c7ae0a8260"], "node": "69d38594e46eb679de854574bf0d4486bfce1bbf", "parents": ["af9b49b8fdf2cff01c5bcc791f6216cfcbaf0df9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge mozilla-central to autoland\n", "files": ["third_party/libwebrtc/api/sframe/sframe_decrypter_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/sframe/sframe_encrypter_interface.h", "third_party/libwebrtc/api/stats/OWNERS", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/adapted_video_track_source_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/adapted_video_track_source.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/video_adapter.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/video_adapter_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/video_broadcaster.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/video_broadcaster_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/video_common.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/base/video_common_unittest.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/video_adapter_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/video_broadcaster_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/media/video_common_gn/moz.build", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/07b9afe36a.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/0f95d45b269df107246f36b6d1f6ce3c399b0cce.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/9ee59b4ab3.no-op-cherry-pick-msg", "third_party/libwebrtc/moz-patch-stack/s0143.patch", "third_party/libwebrtc/stats/attribute.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/stats/rtc_stats.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/stats/rtc_stats_report.cc", "third_party/libwebrtc/stats/rtcstats_objects.cc"], "git_node": "bac9aef61216c8ca211394d49903cfd0195131f8", "git_parents": ["9770f4153cb800356c5161298ceb9148cb14d829", "3b3f727963c10fe58e6e72c15989ad0e35dbf832"], "node": "1769beea6a741e13f5f3e5a4f6660cf7a6c57da0", "parents": ["69d38594e46eb679de854574bf0d4486bfce1bbf", "20c76e79a48fcadf0bb99dc95fc0f85bc6f6c5f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Teow \u003cjteow@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054959 - Fix browser_urlbar_search.js and browser_urlbar_keyed_search.js failures when Nova is enabled - r=urlbar-reviewers,daisuke\n\nRun performance tests with browser.nova.enabled and fix the resulting failures.\nMove geometry measurement out of the perf-observed testFn into a new measureGeometry\nhelper so its style/layout reads aren't counted as reflows, and compute the reference\nrect's horizontal bounds from the .urlbar-background element's actual bounding rect\ninstead of the urlbar's inline margin, so the allowed paint region matches Nova's\nrendering.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312736\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/performance/browserNova.toml", "browser/base/content/test/performance/head.js", "browser/base/content/test/performance/moz.build"], "git_node": "14de91dffab6f8480f0615c8c298d872e19d0b08", "git_parents": ["bac9aef61216c8ca211394d49903cfd0195131f8"], "node": "a994c74ad5005d470f71dc1048a68f0cb0514d89", "parents": ["1769beea6a741e13f5f3e5a4f6660cf7a6c57da0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054941 - Add assertions guarding the BounceTrackingState OriginAttributes invariant against future per-site container association. r=bvandersloot\n\nThe assertions only hold for documents BTP actually tracks, so gate every\nlive-principal/channel OriginAttributes comparison on\nBounceTrackingState::ShouldTrackPrincipal (or an http(s) channel scheme). This\nexcludes the process-wide system principal singleton, whose OriginAttributes\nreport the default non-private values regardless of the window, and non-http(s)\ndocuments (about:, moz-extension:) which are not partitioned like the http(s)\ncontent BTP records bounces for.\n\nAlso make BrowsingContext::GetCurrentTopByBrowserId null-safe like its sibling\nGet(), since BounceTrackingState can query it while recording bounces on tab\nclose during shutdown, after the ClearOnShutdown map has been torn down.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313036\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingProtection.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.cpp"], "git_node": "9200c7e5e00f24e1d757c8e9160df1d65e868563", "git_parents": ["14de91dffab6f8480f0615c8c298d872e19d0b08"], "node": "dace39737831755298ca7ec00a33b9fd8bc35b6a", "parents": ["a994c74ad5005d470f71dc1048a68f0cb0514d89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "chloezhouny \u003cchloezhouny@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046612 - Add animated loading treatment to Smart Window Action Log processing states. r=echa\n\nWhile an Action Log is processing, ai-action-result renders a non-interactive role=\"status\" row instead of the expandable header: a shimmering gradient label (with trailing ellipsis) beside the full-color logo that spins and breathes. The chat-assistant-loader spinner is suppressed while an action log is in progress. Animations respect prefers-reduced-motion and forced-colors.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311938\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-action-result/ai-action-result.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-action-result/ai-action-result.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_content_loader_suppression.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_ai_action_result.js", "browser/themes/shared/icons/smart-window-filled.svg", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn"], "git_node": "747da0cf0a606d949dc94d33f66fdec934fabf95", "git_parents": ["9200c7e5e00f24e1d757c8e9160df1d65e868563"], "node": "117d5b9972598e707920035d95a74ed5e118fbdd", "parents": ["dace39737831755298ca7ec00a33b9fd8bc35b6a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056518 - Update the \"profiler-cli stop\" instruction in the profiler-analysis skill r=padenot,florian,ai4dev-reviewers\n\nThere were some cases where it would stop the profiler-cli and then\ndoesns't start again even though the user has requested to dive into the\nissue further. Let's try softening this wording a bit to see if it'll\nhelp for those cases.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313192\n", "files": [".agents/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md", ".claude/skills/profiler-analysis/SKILL.md"], "git_node": "fa49781771ae4b3a692df8df262a71bd04b28a29", "git_parents": ["747da0cf0a606d949dc94d33f66fdec934fabf95"], "node": "ae54b4bd6189796658e6567ffd78043440ef50b7", "parents": ["117d5b9972598e707920035d95a74ed5e118fbdd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047140 [Linux] Move source side of D&D operation to extra class nsDragSessionSource r=emilio\n\nNo code changes, only extract source D&D part to a new class.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312056\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/moz.build", "widget/gtk/nsDragService.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsDragService.h", "widget/gtk/nsDragServiceGtk.h", "widget/gtk/nsDragServiceWayland.h", "widget/gtk/nsDragSessionSource.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsDragSessionSource.h", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp"], "git_node": "8e4638905a5c54d268fbe7428f012d3ff999ccf2", "git_parents": ["fa49781771ae4b3a692df8df262a71bd04b28a29"], "node": "fb6dbf22433d390aa8bf504cc4672283d6e33fa1", "parents": ["ae54b4bd6189796658e6567ffd78043440ef50b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047140 [Linux] Keep D&D source GtkWidget live until D&D operations is finished r=emilio\n\nRecently we delete source GtkWidget while the D&D is still live. That may lead to various issues/crashes as\nGtk still renders and uses the widget surface etc.\n\nThe early delete was introduced as a hack for mem leak in Bug 219521. Let's fix that better.\n\nAlso fix logging build errors.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312259\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsDragService.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsDragService.h", "widget/gtk/nsDragServiceGtk.h", "widget/gtk/nsDragServiceWayland.h", "widget/gtk/nsDragSessionSource.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsDragSessionSource.h", "widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp"], "git_node": "f221d1f0da416d7b5088a345c82de1959ec929b6", "git_parents": ["8e4638905a5c54d268fbe7428f012d3ff999ccf2"], "node": "fad4e1cc59400fb1adf07d3b888c166e052acb14", "parents": ["fb6dbf22433d390aa8bf504cc4672283d6e33fa1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056463 - Add test_forbid_moduleloaderbase_include. r=linter-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313152\n", "files": ["tools/lint/test/python.toml", "tools/lint/test/test_forbid_moduleloaderbase_include.py"], "git_node": "407568a8942234887ddb6c9d316c133283ad8a08", "git_parents": ["f221d1f0da416d7b5088a345c82de1959ec929b6"], "node": "719283fff0e2f9d9665fc04e0680b71d8ebc16e6", "parents": ["fad4e1cc59400fb1adf07d3b888c166e052acb14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018164 - Verify more Client IPC. r=asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310602\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.h"], "git_node": "465d674a01a462998fd0370683ae965b023dc9f0", "git_parents": ["407568a8942234887ddb6c9d316c133283ad8a08"], "node": "720314dc5dd8a69f1c56cfcd230a34a6a994e728", "parents": ["719283fff0e2f9d9665fc04e0680b71d8ebc16e6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kycn \u003c35106533+kycn@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056517 - Record FREEZER, DEPENDENCY_DIED, INITIALIZATION_FAILURE in app_exit_info.process_exited. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nSurfaces system-driven exit reasons that TRACKED_REASONS previously dropped.\nUser-triggered reasons remain excluded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313194\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/ApplicationExitInfoMetrics.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/perf/ApplicationExitInfoMetricsTest.kt"], "git_node": "61d5ef5de78744b520de33588c4c12b994b289ac", "git_parents": ["465d674a01a462998fd0370683ae965b023dc9f0"], "node": "5590be080049fd9fe0d9cbf78603df45a3a9cba7", "parents": ["720314dc5dd8a69f1c56cfcd230a34a6a994e728"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056503. Pass --forward to patch during vendoring so an already-applied patch fails instead of being silently reversed. r=tjr\n\nimport_local_patches applies each patch with `patch --batch`, which assumes\n-R and applies the reverse of any patch that looks already-applied or reversed.\nAfter a local patch is upstreamed, re-vendoring the newer revision makes the\nforward patch look already-applied, so patch silently un-applies it (exit 0, no\nreject) and the upstreamed change is reverted with no error reported. --forward\nmakes patch skip such a patch and exit nonzero, which ensure_exit_code=0 turns\ninto a hard failure. Verified against Apple/BSD patch (exit 1 + reject) and, from\nthe GNU patch source, GNU patch (exit 1, \"N out of M hunks ignored\").\n\nThis bug almost made me undo an upstreamed patch while I was vendoring in a new\nrevision of libyuv but I just happened to remember that I upstreamed a patch\nsince the last update and it should have failed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313169\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/vendor/test_vendor_manifest.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/vendor/vendor_manifest.py"], "git_node": "00137948431291415c7671984dc005a94f7c95e1", "git_parents": ["61d5ef5de78744b520de33588c4c12b994b289ac"], "node": "44b3bcee86efaf988325692b08e52d0f564b2d2c", "parents": ["5590be080049fd9fe0d9cbf78603df45a3a9cba7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1949093 [Linux] Merge gfx test utilities to one binary r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311502\n", "files": ["browser/installer/package-manifest.in", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/artifacts.py", "toolkit/xre/gfxtest/gfxtest.cpp", "toolkit/xre/gfxtest/glxtest.cpp", "toolkit/xre/gfxtest/moz.build", "toolkit/xre/gfxtest/v4l2test.cpp", "toolkit/xre/gfxtest/vaapitest.cpp", "toolkit/xre/gfxtest/vulkantest.cpp", "toolkit/xre/glxtest/glxtest.cpp", "toolkit/xre/glxtest/moz.build", "toolkit/xre/moz.build", "widget/gtk/GfxInfo.cpp", "widget/gtk/GfxInfoUtils.h", "widget/gtk/moz.build", "widget/gtk/v4l2test/moz.build", "widget/gtk/v4l2test/v4l2test.cpp", "widget/gtk/vaapitest/moz.build", "widget/gtk/vaapitest/vaapitest.cpp", "widget/gtk/vulkantest/moz.build", "widget/gtk/vulkantest/vulkantest.cpp"], "git_node": "1ec6c168263f1c00dce04e41801c4ae5511f3eec", "git_parents": ["00137948431291415c7671984dc005a94f7c95e1"], "node": "bb1a373caf402eaa8ccc8294a09382585bf51bbe", "parents": ["44b3bcee86efaf988325692b08e52d0f564b2d2c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "stransky \u003cstransky@redhat.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1650672 [Linux] Use libnotify only if the notification daemon is running r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312700\n", "files": ["toolkit/system/gnome/nsAlertsIconListener.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsAppShell.h"], "git_node": "f18a08cd59a4c299c1f9bd6ed0d735647ca58d5b", "git_parents": ["1ec6c168263f1c00dce04e41801c4ae5511f3eec"], "node": "0b47413c2e637febe76470f5b511bad40ba71593", "parents": ["bb1a373caf402eaa8ccc8294a09382585bf51bbe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrej Glavic \u003caglavic@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2015141 - Add ability to run mozperftest in CI with arm64 android emulators. r=perftest-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310708\n", "files": ["python/mozperftest/mozperftest/system/android.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/test_android.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/test_utils.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/utils.py", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/android-emulator.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "f50115f9470684b55b9b6f8abea6e5642c7f785f", "git_parents": ["f18a08cd59a4c299c1f9bd6ed0d735647ca58d5b"], "node": "e4eb010225290602a310c00be4d06eb7da4f6ebd", "parents": ["0b47413c2e637febe76470f5b511bad40ba71593"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego Escalante \u003cdescalante@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044157 - Don't zoom shape function twice for clip paths. r=longsonr,boris,firefox-svg-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313295\n", "files": ["layout/svg/CSSClipPathInstance.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-shape-transition-with-zoom.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-shape-hittest.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/clip-path/animations/clip-path-shape-interpolation-with-zoom.html"], "git_node": "d8d8c2379535c65ac72e3253c3d3d387d9b3dff0", "git_parents": ["f50115f9470684b55b9b6f8abea6e5642c7f785f"], "node": "270076d3c18cc6e563f92b960899f0828cff9f5e", "parents": ["e4eb010225290602a310c00be4d06eb7da4f6ebd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056302 - Add Moloco as a new marketing partner in Adjust. r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313043\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/AdjustMetricsService.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/AdjustThirdPartySharingController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallReferrerHandlingService.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallReferrerWorker.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/AdjustMetricsServiceTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallReferrerHandlingServiceTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/metrics/InstallReferrerWorkerTest.kt"], "git_node": "6bbc6ea02fc25558e61e702c3f775556dff0a72f", "git_parents": ["d8d8c2379535c65ac72e3253c3d3d387d9b3dff0"], "node": "25e4d28e1dbc170be915791b17a39901dd4e7bd9", "parents": ["270076d3c18cc6e563f92b960899f0828cff9f5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055222. Add qcms_profile_create_cicp_with_intent. r=jrmuizel\n\njxl encodes the transfer function, the primaries and the rendering intent, so it'd be good to receive them all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312281\n", "files": ["gfx/qcms/qcms.h", "gfx/qcms/src/c_bindings.rs", "gfx/qcms/src/iccread.rs"], "git_node": "d7a477db28f44db3cd4a4b42b10016f31660d370", "git_parents": ["6bbc6ea02fc25558e61e702c3f775556dff0a72f"], "node": "9dfd46bfc5807295d6b58e5b85dfedf7d26bc789", "parents": ["25e4d28e1dbc170be915791b17a39901dd4e7bd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055224. Recognize common JXL color spaces via CICP enums instead of synthesizing an ICC. r=saschanaz\n\nHaving jxl-rs synthesize an ICC profile just so we can build a qcms input\nprofile from it is inefficient. Instead recognize the common color spaces\nfrom their CICP enum values and build the qcms profile directly, keeping the\nICC path only for what CICP can't represent (grayscale, CMYK, embedded ICC,\ncustom color points).\n\nPQ and HLG transfer functions are excluded (we want the icc for those): for\nPQ and HLG jxl-rs bakes HDR tone mapping into the ICC's A2B0 LUT, which qcms\nuses. We currently don't do any tonemapping for these transfer functions and\nthe result is not good.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312282\n", "files": ["image/decoders/nsJXLDecoder.cpp", "image/rust/jxl/src/decoder.rs", "image/rust/jxl/src/ffi.rs"], "git_node": "89fffee6c7eb11329176fa748fc7f1a4448ab8b3", "git_parents": ["d7a477db28f44db3cd4a4b42b10016f31660d370"], "node": "54167ec23d5b0de4b00969a1b92c0f520e21c08b", "parents": ["9dfd46bfc5807295d6b58e5b85dfedf7d26bc789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1989252 - Don't show unavailable quickactions in action mode. r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312081\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProviderQuickActions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/QuickActionsLoaderDefault.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderActionsSearchMode.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_general.js"], "git_node": "dd6f2fcf8197aef374c3d2887e6ed1334963f851", "git_parents": ["89fffee6c7eb11329176fa748fc7f1a4448ab8b3"], "node": "05ac32723be1e8475fa36e517b959b5bf2e5d74a", "parents": ["54167ec23d5b0de4b00969a1b92c0f520e21c08b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Bucher \u003cmanuel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053008 - Increase timeout factor in antitracking mochitest to fix timeouts r=bvandersloot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312772\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_PBMCookieBehavior.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_blockingCookies.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_blockingIndexedDb.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_blockingLocalStorage.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_blockingMessaging.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_blockingSessionStorage.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_blockingSharedWorkers.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_partitionedCookies.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/test/browser/browser_referrerDefaultPolicy.js"], "git_node": "8481157d1f1395a137c90bd667a6321217315dd6", "git_parents": ["dd6f2fcf8197aef374c3d2887e6ed1334963f851"], "node": "d563089bdcc5e237eeacefabbab72b6324795658", "parents": ["05ac32723be1e8475fa36e517b959b5bf2e5d74a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Krist Baliev \u003ckbaliev@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056575: CPM panel background color should be consistent with other panels. r=mtigley,credential-management-reviewers DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313234\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/megalist.css"], "git_node": "332efedb0d24da598f54524a18f2af0e7a120d94", "git_parents": ["8481157d1f1395a137c90bd667a6321217315dd6"], "node": "826304f74080ee0ec826338f32bd09faa7feb339", "parents": ["d563089bdcc5e237eeacefabbab72b6324795658"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046918: Move FastTransform to webrender_api crate r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nSigned-off-by: Nico Burns \u003cnico@nicoburns.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306261\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/util.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/fast_transform.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "7cc0eba7dca72a87ea62dcc93671e678f39378c9", "git_parents": ["332efedb0d24da598f54524a18f2af0e7a120d94"], "node": "4b17c5ef983afc7212139d1ce3553795f2b05ca8", "parents": ["826304f74080ee0ec826338f32bd09faa7feb339"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046918 - Address servo-tidy lints. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313181\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/fast_transform.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/key_types.rs"], "git_node": "29ac9a8c7d38f4f5be36c5e9dc46838805a2d72f", "git_parents": ["7cc0eba7dca72a87ea62dcc93671e678f39378c9"], "node": "03ce48ce4c4bf47d75b335267ced09a0e8a66d5a", "parents": ["4b17c5ef983afc7212139d1ce3553795f2b05ca8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2018164 - Verify more Client IPC. r=asuth\" for causing build bustages @ClientHandleParent.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 465d674a01a462998fd0370683ae965b023dc9f0.\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.h"], "git_node": "76979dfd1f56f3bbfc78739c108084f7eb19aeca", "git_parents": ["29ac9a8c7d38f4f5be36c5e9dc46838805a2d72f"], "node": "dbe376a6b7cdb648ab0a47c91b020ae60cea4373", "parents": ["03ce48ce4c4bf47d75b335267ced09a0e8a66d5a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056633 - Don't allow \u003cinput\u003e / \u003ctextarea\u003e to be affected by multicol styles. r=layout-reviewers,jfkthame\n\nMatches other browsers and our previous behavior, in general it doesn't\nmake sense to split an input into columns.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313434\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-multicol/textarea-text-overflow-ellipsis-crash.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/textarea-multicol-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/widgets/textarea-multicol.html"], "git_node": "694b65b487a4b09ba14a23d26da095833160c4bc", "git_parents": ["76979dfd1f56f3bbfc78739c108084f7eb19aeca"], "node": "f5a67dd06bc52c16dbde62317e85bd33c3ce8dfd", "parents": ["dbe376a6b7cdb648ab0a47c91b020ae60cea4373"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kevin Gosse \u003ckrix33@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054036 - Return DV_E_FORMATETC from nsDataObj::QueryGetData for unsupported formats. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311521\n", "files": ["widget/windows/nsDataObj.cpp"], "git_node": "7dfbf9f9f3905721307b0c763063c7a4a1705e8a", "git_parents": ["694b65b487a4b09ba14a23d26da095833160c4bc"], "node": "485c17cd26c2444e3b1be5b770348a671b32c22a", "parents": ["f5a67dd06bc52c16dbde62317e85bd33c3ce8dfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055206 - Part 1: Do not attempt to refresh while in background r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nFirefox on android might be running but in the background.\nWhile in this state, doing network requests are forbidden.\n\nSo if we do happen to do a scheudled rotation, we will fail and enter the \"Catastropic, cannot continue\" state.\nGiven that we do know when we are backgrounded and will re-fetch once we are back in foreground, we should skip any rotation while in background.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313027\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPLifecycleHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js"], "git_node": "416f31aa6168b2e7f34bcb491d6165a394c770f0", "git_parents": ["7dfbf9f9f3905721307b0c763063c7a4a1705e8a"], "node": "694665909b02854f70aeba726194a949810baa31", "parents": ["485c17cd26c2444e3b1be5b770348a671b32c22a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055206 - Part 2: Add individual timouts per fetch r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nWe do have a single 30s timeout for the roation. However a single very very slow fetch request may take that time for itself. So we should have a more aggressive per_request timeout, so we can retry multiple times\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313028\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "a3d207d23cd997584dbeddaede525806d141f68e", "git_parents": ["416f31aa6168b2e7f34bcb491d6165a394c770f0"], "node": "259c76e6cc8cbef7a84985af8789c35f8f98fd69", "parents": ["694665909b02854f70aeba726194a949810baa31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055206 - Part 3: A forced rotation should reset the Proxy-Manager timer r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nRN we do only reschedule the Roation if we get a new Pass from a rotation.\n\nThis is a bit off, given we might skip a rotation while in background, or have an early rotation when fastly rejects the token, it does not make sense to keep the old rotation.\n\nSo whenever we have a new token, we should take it's expiration as the new rotation time.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313029\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js"], "git_node": "b4c4d0bb1f5a38f580874cc809eb0c861c37c6b4", "git_parents": ["a3d207d23cd997584dbeddaede525806d141f68e"], "node": "e6f9c9b39be8696be8469fa7c52b476e145366a0", "parents": ["259c76e6cc8cbef7a84985af8789c35f8f98fd69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikki Sharpley \u003cnsharpley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056253 - Show all devices in connected devices section of account menu r=skhamis\n\nMerge lists of devices with \"send tab to device\" capability and devices with remote tabs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313025\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_sync.js"], "git_node": "4b00f94fe792ee163a9457fdb760647dedf6d61f", "git_parents": ["b4c4d0bb1f5a38f580874cc809eb0c861c37c6b4"], "node": "f61f880b39e09cda3eef98eb7a98327e78edcef5", "parents": ["e6f9c9b39be8696be8469fa7c52b476e145366a0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "KS \u003ckshampur@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049826 - Run navigation benchmark regularly on nightly as release r=perftest-reviewers,fbilt\n\nrecently evidence was found that this benchmark can pick up on\nimprovements (e.g. Bug 2052301 where Linux NaR PGO was updated)\n\nwe should run this regularly and see how the data looks over time\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312815\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/desktop.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.rst"], "git_node": "d726f7df31cd821b9e47785ad5c7ba56382c9f69", "git_parents": ["4b00f94fe792ee163a9457fdb760647dedf6d61f"], "node": "3908e4ef783d0e91d39a0577f1ef5bb5ab90360b", "parents": ["f61f880b39e09cda3eef98eb7a98327e78edcef5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054792 - Don't auto-compact uidensity when RFP window sizing is active. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jsudiaman,tjr\n\ngUIDensity auto-compact (bug 2044082) toggles uidensity=compact on resize,\nshrinking the chrome by ~6px. RFP window-size protections (letterboxing and the\nmaxInner* rounding enabled by resistFingerprinting) quantize the content area to\na fixed, deterministic size, so reclaiming chrome space inflates the content\npast the rounded dimensions and races with the size updates.\n\nBail out of auto-compact when privacy.resistFingerprinting[.pbmode] or\nprivacy.resistFingerprinting.letterboxing is set, and observe those prefs so the\nresolved density re-evaluates when they toggle.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312764\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser.js"], "git_node": "8c9946b42c4beacb9859c71e0ee83703584f7d33", "git_parents": ["d726f7df31cd821b9e47785ad5c7ba56382c9f69"], "node": "36d1c3770289e1e5b051810fe1093f14590aeaa5", "parents": ["3908e4ef783d0e91d39a0577f1ef5bb5ab90360b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054792 - Make the RFP window-rounding tests robust to Nova's chrome geometry. r=tjr\n\nTwo RFP window-rounding tests made assumptions about chrome size that break\nwhen browser.nova.enabled changes the chrome geometry:\n\n1. browser_dynamical_window_rounding.js captured the browser container size once\n   and compared later-read content against a rounding of that stale value, so\n   under Nova (where the content area sits in a flex #browser whose size lags the\n   window resize by a frame) the check trailed a full case behind. Re-read the\n   container inside the waitForCondition loop and wait for the rounding to reach a\n   fixed point on every platform. This also lets us drop the Linux-only\n   redo-resize hack, which compared the content container against the requested\n   outer width -- under Nova the container can never equal that width, so the hack\n   looped forever and timed out.\n\n2. browser_roundedWindow_newWindow.js asserted the opened window's spoofed\n   screen/inner size equalled a re-derived round(min(maxInner, avail - chrome)).\n   That derivation assumes the content area always reaches the maxInner clamp,\n   which only holds when the chrome is small enough; Nova's larger chrome leaves\n   the content just under the clamp, so the exact-equality check failed. RFP\n   actually collapses screen and screen.avail onto the content viewport, so assert\n   that invariant (screen == screen.avail == inner, positive) instead of a fragile\n   re-derived pixel size. This holds regardless of chrome geometry and still\n   catches RFP being disabled or spoofing breaking. The 200x100 stepping this test\n   incidentally depended on is covered by the browser_roundedWindow_open_*.js\n   window.open/resizeTo tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312765\n", "files": ["browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_dynamical_window_rounding.js", "browser/components/resistfingerprinting/test/browser/browser_roundedWindow_newWindow.js"], "git_node": "a2152ea74bfb38c237beb92fe93c0146ca9699b6", "git_parents": ["8c9946b42c4beacb9859c71e0ee83703584f7d33"], "node": "9dea084dfe972fb90bb109f959320dc5f4f88516", "parents": ["36d1c3770289e1e5b051810fe1093f14590aeaa5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055206 - Part 3: A forced rotation should reset the Proxy-Manager timer r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\" for causing xpc failures @test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js.\n\nThis reverts commit b4c4d0bb1f5a38f580874cc809eb0c861c37c6b4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055206 - Part 2: Add individual timouts per fetch r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\"\n\nThis reverts commit a3d207d23cd997584dbeddaede525806d141f68e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055206 - Part 1: Do not attempt to refresh while in background r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\"\n\nThis reverts commit 416f31aa6168b2e7f34bcb491d6165a394c770f0.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPLifecycleHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "bc3b2eb6f8239e9900cb8398fcc2e883255cde8b", "git_parents": ["a2152ea74bfb38c237beb92fe93c0146ca9699b6"], "node": "fb6bdae282c33c0a174ec70e57e39ff91a6f02b7", "parents": ["9dea084dfe972fb90bb109f959320dc5f4f88516"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1989252 - Don't show unavailable quickactions in action mode. r=daleharvey,urlbar-reviewers,mak\" for causing xpc failures @test_quickaction_telemetry.js.\n\nThis reverts commit dd6f2fcf8197aef374c3d2887e6ed1334963f851.\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProviderQuickActions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/QuickActionsLoaderDefault.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderActionsSearchMode.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-quickactions/browser_general.js"], "git_node": "0372164bf317a03f4b4387406af483fd48d0964a", "git_parents": ["bc3b2eb6f8239e9900cb8398fcc2e883255cde8b"], "node": "9619a95c6d24fb2d44609535313f8e05160c0653", "parents": ["fb6bdae282c33c0a174ec70e57e39ff91a6f02b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1650672 [Linux] Use libnotify only if the notification daemon is running r=emilio\" for causing xpc failures @test_dynamicLauncher.js.\n\nThis reverts commit f18a08cd59a4c299c1f9bd6ed0d735647ca58d5b.\n", "files": ["toolkit/system/gnome/nsAlertsIconListener.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsAppShell.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsAppShell.h"], "git_node": "779463c725d2d1b08620971a460fe7248e27e2f1", "git_parents": ["0372164bf317a03f4b4387406af483fd48d0964a"], "node": "8479a93d41b86b82e3f73bc22f65368685f0c176", "parents": ["9619a95c6d24fb2d44609535313f8e05160c0653"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056193 - Make smart window switcher clickable during first run r=pdahiya,desktop-theme-reviewers,sfoster\n\n**Cause**: When I made the window switcher button part of customizable UI another patch landed that touched the CSS for immersive view and first run. During a rebase I didn't notice this new CSS made the window switcher button unclickable as well via `pointer-events: none`.\n\n**Solution**: Adjust the new CSS so the window switcher button is clickable and the rest of the tabs toolbar stays with `pointer-events: none`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313050\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_firstrun.js", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css"], "git_node": "cc0d52be8653150aac748cf8304b7e5ced8b3862", "git_parents": ["779463c725d2d1b08620971a460fe7248e27e2f1"], "node": "90a25199ca89afc6c89bad37047f5f3fff951bc0", "parents": ["8479a93d41b86b82e3f73bc22f65368685f0c176"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056373 - Update browser icon moz-promo illustrations to look better in the dark theme. r=hjones,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313100\n", "files": ["toolkit/themes/shared/illustrations/kit-confetti.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/illustrations/kit-holding-lock.svg"], "git_node": "d714e9c2ef868d3283f7eef6b3426d1d5da35a81", "git_parents": ["cc0d52be8653150aac748cf8304b7e5ced8b3862"], "node": "9707bb8713cee932ff4b8a4035a30a7cca3ae020", "parents": ["90a25199ca89afc6c89bad37047f5f3fff951bc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054581 - Properly forward updating properties from MessageWrapper down through ExternalComponentWrapper down to wrapped message components. r=jbrown\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311935\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/ExternalComponentWrapper/ExternalComponentWrapper.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/MessageWrapper/MessageWrapper.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/ExternalComponentWrapper.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/MessageWrapper.test.jsx"], "git_node": "0ef390cc87b205f8e92842e0655c8aba8a71563c", "git_parents": ["d714e9c2ef868d3283f7eef6b3426d1d5da35a81"], "node": "1428baa5376dc41c6adc4c7679cb67f934676936", "parents": ["9707bb8713cee932ff4b8a4035a30a7cca3ae020"], "tags": []}, {"author": "giorga \u003cgiorga@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038713 - [WebCompat Reporter v3] Update \"Preview report\" bottom sheet. r=android-reviewers,petru\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308808\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/middleware/WebCompatReporterSubmissionMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/store/WebCompatReporterStore.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/ui/WebCompatReporter.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/ui/WebCompatReporterPreviewSheet.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/webcompat/middleware/WebCompatReporterSubmissionMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "6dd3d70900965a4088059ec6db863375a3d4ae9b", "git_parents": ["0ef390cc87b205f8e92842e0655c8aba8a71563c"], "node": "6103e800739443ad8ff3f663a7d405aec3abc6cd", "parents": ["1428baa5376dc41c6adc4c7679cb67f934676936"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055711 - Fix verifyENLocalesDefaultTopSitesListTest UI test r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI test was flaky because default shortcuts did not consistently appear on a cold start.\nThis is a known issue related to how home screen items load.\n\nTo fix this, I applied a workaround that is already being used in other home screen related UI tests and removed a previous loop that was ineffective.\n\nThe UI tests successfully passed 50x on Firebase \u2705\nAll Top sites related UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313444\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/TopSitesTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/robots/HomeScreenRobot.kt"], "git_node": "a6cc4809f2580a24fa550497afef4be361c56edd", "git_parents": ["6dd3d70900965a4088059ec6db863375a3d4ae9b"], "node": "f931b70abfb105ce226760f5da7db95a90202acc", "parents": ["6103e800739443ad8ff3f663a7d405aec3abc6cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Johns \u003cbjohns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052182 - added tabKeyByToken argument to groupTabs direct call (no confirmation) path r=cdipersio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312295\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/ManageTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_ManageTabs.js"], "git_node": "b7280e3b597b7ec1c4884cfc75e956d5ba877911", "git_parents": ["a6cc4809f2580a24fa550497afef4be361c56edd"], "node": "0ae32925b3e3811a6b2d7ebba56ccfa5e58419e0", "parents": ["f931b70abfb105ce226760f5da7db95a90202acc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056892 - Show the container icon/name/color in the tab preview r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sclements\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313452\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/main-popupset.inc.xhtml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab-hover-preview.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_preview.js", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tab-hover-preview.css"], "git_node": "8b32d772784c5b8b3ec9fbc9626d2fde28983fed", "git_parents": ["b7280e3b597b7ec1c4884cfc75e956d5ba877911"], "node": "b8e780986907a7bafe32878e8d9576fc4095288b", "parents": ["0ae32925b3e3811a6b2d7ebba56ccfa5e58419e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056345 - Patch frequent linux asan FATAL ERROR r=czhou\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313137\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aichat_content_message_event.js"], "git_node": "f806fadb1094a51a4cb9a9aae9f96d0ad99cd9ed", "git_parents": ["8b32d772784c5b8b3ec9fbc9626d2fde28983fed"], "node": "7c589e85c9e4e3756bac0faca8c131d6d4854e7e", "parents": ["b8e780986907a7bafe32878e8d9576fc4095288b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054303 - Minor tweaks to attribute selector matching. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nSee the discussion in bug 2052936. The comparators are relatively\nexpensive.\n\nCleanup a bit nsStyleUtil includes while at it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311685\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsJSEnvironment.cpp", "dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "dom/view-transitions/ViewTransition.cpp", "editor/spellchecker/EditorSpellCheck.cpp", "layout/style/FontFaceImpl.cpp", "layout/style/GeckoBindings.cpp", "layout/style/StyleColor.cpp", "layout/style/StyleColorInlines.h", "layout/style/nsStyleUtil.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleUtil.h", "layout/xul/nsXULPopupManager.cpp", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/nsRFPService.cpp"], "git_node": "f6fe253bcf235082591d3b46dfdad16c5a52ea18", "git_parents": ["f806fadb1094a51a4cb9a9aae9f96d0ad99cd9ed"], "node": "c38c0a17113bb0795b7268ac8b334cd15d381331", "parents": ["7c589e85c9e4e3756bac0faca8c131d6d4854e7e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikki Sharpley \u003cnsharpley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055860 - Remove icon from \"create a new profile\" button in app menu r=sthompson,desktop-theme-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313458\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "d08e15204722f504c27de33dbbd1efe4a1406a30", "git_parents": ["f6fe253bcf235082591d3b46dfdad16c5a52ea18"], "node": "afc080f15cc00068b3c5941c3e87b85d453fbf48", "parents": ["c38c0a17113bb0795b7268ac8b334cd15d381331"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1910797 - Don't remove a fragmented anonymous wrapper when removing its only child. r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nWe generally don't support plain removing last continuations, and\nremoving a previous continuation would incorrectly remove all the\nfollowing ones as well.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313460\n", "files": ["layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-flexbox/crashtests/fragmented-anon-box-remove.html"], "git_node": "b8113a102407e378a58c82248c0286bf23fe72f5", "git_parents": ["d08e15204722f504c27de33dbbd1efe4a1406a30"], "node": "fab66ffcf0020052a66485634feca79ddc869375", "parents": ["afc080f15cc00068b3c5941c3e87b85d453fbf48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018164 - Verify more Client IPC. r=asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310602\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.h", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.h"], "git_node": "51916ddc26d90e09b453a7a33161fc2dd3e2730f", "git_parents": ["b8113a102407e378a58c82248c0286bf23fe72f5"], "node": "109f286d718c7f0556d347a910e5e0a3500040ed", "parents": ["fab66ffcf0020052a66485634feca79ddc869375"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Conley \u003cmconley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054761. r=kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313213\n", "files": ["browser/components/mozcachedohttp/actors/MozCachedOHTTPParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/mozcachedohttp/test/unit/test_cache_behavior.js"], "git_node": "0d218990609f9e69c70d4036fa05c7363b155319", "git_parents": ["51916ddc26d90e09b453a7a33161fc2dd3e2730f"], "node": "d137c773a54716a0074736423186d7c73e4c3ef5", "parents": ["109f286d718c7f0556d347a910e5e0a3500040ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "RebecaTudor \u003crebecatudor273@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054435 - Fix navigation of \"Leave private tabs\" button from Unlock screen. r=android-reviewers,alastun\n\nIssue:\n When clicking the \"Leave private tabs\" button from Unlock screen, the app navigated back\n to the home fragment but incorrectly remained in Private mode UI. This occurred because\n only the AppStore was updated, while the BrowsingModeManager (which handles theme\n transitions and Activity recreation) was not notified of the change.\n\n Fix:\n Update BrowsingModeManager.mode to BrowsingMode.Normal correctly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313223\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/pbmlock/UnlockPrivateTabsFragment.kt"], "git_node": "4eddb46920f026331de2c260ea7a3853434105f9", "git_parents": ["0d218990609f9e69c70d4036fa05c7363b155319"], "node": "72153ab8971d17ca5d8933f5587f253cb3a5bc6f", "parents": ["d137c773a54716a0074736423186d7c73e4c3ef5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen Thompson \u003csthompson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047229 - Nova duotone icons trust-icon-insecure, security-broken r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton,jsudiaman,dao\n\nThese two SVG icons were drawn with a hardcoded `#F90D3F`-colored slash through them. The Acorn icon designers redrew these two icons as \"duotone,\" with one path colored by context-fill and the other path colored by context-stroke, allowing CSS to control the color of the slash.\n\nUsing these appropriately requires updating any CSS targeting them so that they specify at least `-moz-context-properties: fill, stroke` and set `stroke: var(--icon-color-critical)` so that the slash is colored by an appropriate design token.\n\nHowever, out of an abundance of caution, they will fall back to using `#F90D3F` if a `stroke` color is not set.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306524\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_parsable_css.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/split-view-footer.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_splitview_footer.js", "browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css", "browser/themes/shared/controlcenter/panel.css", "browser/themes/shared/identity-block/identity-block.css", "browser/themes/shared/identity-block/trust-icon-insecure.svg", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/fullscreen-and-pointerlock.css", "toolkit/components/aboutthirdparty/content/aboutThirdParty.css", "toolkit/components/prompts/content/adjustableTitle.js", "toolkit/components/prompts/content/commonDialog.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/icons/security-broken.svg"], "git_node": "a2edeb25c3a4f8d9b2b24c9e426f7bd26ef997bb", "git_parents": ["4eddb46920f026331de2c260ea7a3853434105f9"], "node": "ccdf32404fb083a72908c6ddc2713a3fcc0ecab1", "parents": ["72153ab8971d17ca5d8933f5587f253cb3a5bc6f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042302 - Make AutoHandlingUserInputStatePusher main-thread-only; r=masayuki\n\nThe user input state is only available on main thread, so AutoHandlingUserInputStatePusher\ncan also be main-thread-only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313184\n", "files": ["dom/base/UserActivation.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSContext.cpp"], "git_node": "4d27ff7f1514bab7dd1d5c6472d247e848f9c0e0", "git_parents": ["a2edeb25c3a4f8d9b2b24c9e426f7bd26ef997bb"], "node": "9bae1a09dc9eb7bdd87aab505b545cdf7672be91", "parents": ["ccdf32404fb083a72908c6ddc2713a3fcc0ecab1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042302 - Skip the paste confirmation popup if programmatic paste is initiated while handling a keyboard event that would trigger a paste command; r=masayuki,smaug\n\nWhen a page requests to read the clipboard programmatically and the clipboard\ndata originates from a different page, a paste popup is shown to obtain user\nconsent. However, if the programmatic paste is initiated while handling a\nkeyboard event that would trigger a paste command, it is not necessary to ask\nfor confirmation, since we know the page could already obtain the clipboard data\nfrom paste event.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308747\n", "files": ["dom/base/UserActivation.cpp", "dom/base/UserActivation.h", "dom/base/nsGlobalWindowCommands.cpp", "dom/events/GlobalKeyListener.cpp", "dom/events/GlobalKeyListener.h", "dom/events/KeyEventHandler.cpp", "dom/events/KeyEventHandler.h", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_document_command_paste_contextmenu_event_loop.js", "dom/events/test/clipboard/browser_document_command_paste_contextmenu_suppression_key.js", "dom/events/test/gtest/TestShortcutKeyDefinitions.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "editor/libeditor/EditorCommands.cpp", "widget/TextEventDispatcher.cpp", "widget/TextEvents.h", "widget/nsGUIEventIPC.h"], "git_node": "4559366a819949a8db0b02386410cd770aa4ff38", "git_parents": ["4d27ff7f1514bab7dd1d5c6472d247e848f9c0e0"], "node": "1b80daeaee984dc590b41aa87d99d464ecb2d801", "parents": ["9bae1a09dc9eb7bdd87aab505b545cdf7672be91"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056866: add taskgraph parameters for autoland backstop pushes r=taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313432\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test/params/autoland-onpush-backstop.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/update.sh"], "git_node": "82c61463f5e7af932199cce855997138a3b1f27e", "git_parents": ["4559366a819949a8db0b02386410cd770aa4ff38"], "node": "f9fd034e7b2f85562e16f49a069062626e8e57ce", "parents": ["1b80daeaee984dc590b41aa87d99d464ecb2d801"], "tags": []}, {"author": "R\u00e9mi Papilli\u00e9 \u003crpapillie@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056913 - Fix WebRender build with \"debugger\" feature enabled. r=nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313475\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs"], "git_node": "3e08fc5eecd5f0fc6e36aa96fe4029c7dca81edd", "git_parents": ["82c61463f5e7af932199cce855997138a3b1f27e"], "node": "fcb49ab17936126d62994fcba8af7c593530beb2", "parents": ["f9fd034e7b2f85562e16f49a069062626e8e57ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055224, Bug 2055222. Recognize common JXL color spaces via CICP enums instead of synthesizing an ICC. r=saschanaz\" for causing wr failures @hdr-alpha-reftest.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 89fffee6c7eb11329176fa748fc7f1a4448ab8b3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055222. Add qcms_profile_create_cicp_with_intent. r=jrmuizel\"\n\nThis reverts commit d7a477db28f44db3cd4a4b42b10016f31660d370.\n", "files": ["gfx/qcms/qcms.h", "gfx/qcms/src/c_bindings.rs", "gfx/qcms/src/iccread.rs", "image/decoders/nsJXLDecoder.cpp", "image/rust/jxl/src/decoder.rs", "image/rust/jxl/src/ffi.rs"], "git_node": "4841e0b11bb226bc902bad018668c392558f2487", "git_parents": ["3e08fc5eecd5f0fc6e36aa96fe4029c7dca81edd"], "node": "422ae612d943b7faa2da53dc9b7c24182464229f", "parents": ["fcb49ab17936126d62994fcba8af7c593530beb2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051555: In case of OOM, make an inline array. r=jpages\n\nFor both array and struct objects, an OOM can occur in between\nallocating the object and allocating its out-of-line data area. For\nstructs we don't really have a choice but to be aware of null data\npointers in obj_trace and obj_moved, but for arrays we can just convert\nthe failed array into an empty inline-storage array.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311827\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/bug2051555.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmGcObject-inl.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmGcObject.cpp"], "git_node": "7c457f55a9a6f36c8fa797580544f3535f1137d8", "git_parents": ["4841e0b11bb226bc902bad018668c392558f2487"], "node": "04c7f061d4ac9afdfab6d4e14162c6051aa383ef", "parents": ["422ae612d943b7faa2da53dc9b7c24182464229f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mimi \u003cmjung@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055012 - Adds crashCountInLastDay and crashCountInLast7Days to ASRouter targeting r=omc-reviewers,sachung\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312766\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/docs/targeting-attributes.md", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTargeting.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_targeting.js"], "git_node": "431a7aba79f70860248d3364f2388f48e8276ffc", "git_parents": ["7c457f55a9a6f36c8fa797580544f3535f1137d8"], "node": "29a581ace45d4937e4d5024765d01d7beb26fa86", "parents": ["04c7f061d4ac9afdfab6d4e14162c6051aa383ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luk\u00e1\u0161 Lipinsk\u00fd \u003c6032558+Mr-Tao@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056714 - Display \u010cesk\u00e1 televize captions in Picture-in-Picture. r=mconley\n\nThe \u010cesk\u00e1 televize players keep their active WebVTT tracks in hidden mode and render captions in page overlays. Picture-in-Picture therefore does not select the tracks.\n\nTreat hidden tracks as showing for videos in the standalone player document and on CT24 pages, as already done for TED and Vimeo.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313325\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/pictureinpicture/data/picture_in_picture_overrides.js"], "git_node": "75eb9e887d9086f8285d42a7eb772e58d1aea46d", "git_parents": ["431a7aba79f70860248d3364f2388f48e8276ffc"], "node": "31b81ee7f92a9af6c4755ff55c4a05d25cfe0c97", "parents": ["29a581ace45d4937e4d5024765d01d7beb26fa86"], "tags": []}, {"author": "t-p-white \u003ctowhite@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056500 - Fix continuous onboarding Compose previews rendering blank. r=android-reviewers,marcin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313166\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingScreen.kt"], "git_node": "2fb66fc843b3c9d96d7517b70cdb4483bbe6e243", "git_parents": ["75eb9e887d9086f8285d42a7eb772e58d1aea46d"], "node": "962b4593e878086b30ffe14e72c658c17d5fa241", "parents": ["31b81ee7f92a9af6c4755ff55c4a05d25cfe0c97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "t-p-white \u003ctowhite@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056508 - Update the continuous onboarding card background to use the surfaceBright colour token r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\n{F75814348}\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313172\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingScreen.kt"], "git_node": "48c6077d0cf5378771a2f76c276c642ee63e81ca", "git_parents": ["2fb66fc843b3c9d96d7517b70cdb4483bbe6e243"], "node": "ae2d2f0ce07232d434e6163d60bc59e4fd782b2c", "parents": ["962b4593e878086b30ffe14e72c658c17d5fa241"], "tags": []}, {"author": "t-p-white \