: "Bug 2055765 - Make `EventStateManager` store last `eMouseDown` and `eMouseUp` target and `HTMLInputElement` check them if the clear button is recreated r=edgar,emilio,webidl,saschanaz\n\n`click` event target must be the closest and connected inclusive common\nancestor of `mousedown` and `mouseup` event targets and the clear button\nof `HTMLInputElement` is recreated at a reframe. So, if clicking the\nclear button causes a reframe of the `\u003cinput\u003e`, the `click` event target\nis the common ancestor of the old button and the new button. So,\n`HTMLInputElement` cannot check whether the button is clicked only with\nthe event target.\n\nThis patch makes `EventStateManager` store the last `eMouseDown` and\n`eMouseUp` targets while dispatching mouse button events and click\nevents. Therefore, the `ePointerClick` handler of `HTMLInputElement`\ncan know the `eMouseDown` and `eMouseUp` target even after they are\ndisconnected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313368\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.h", "dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp", "dom/html/test/forms/mochitest.toml", "dom/html/test/forms/test_input_click_clear_button_without_focus.html"], "git_node": "5f12a06995c8d71fd2ea8c3e782e6079256ca786", "git_parents": ["75b78cd720003377b6f8c5d6ba31eca7be65ed33"], "node": "d8b26f2cab0a9ef6161b028adb27e4762101360b", "parents": ["8994598599ab62de1c0916a87c6e469ed02c785a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055831 - bump uv toolchain from 0.7.2 to 0.11.28. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\nI'm seeing errors when running against our pypi.pub.build.mozilla.org\nmirror like \"Failed to unzip wheel\" / \"Encountered an unexpected\nheader\", which appear to have been fixed some time after 0.7.2.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312710\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "6458280a8473e234efb4db5b1c6018c610b760b3", "git_parents": ["5f12a06995c8d71fd2ea8c3e782e6079256ca786"], "node": "e6a860fdbb48353127a6cbb53074eb6a4104d26f", "parents": ["d8b26f2cab0a9ef6161b028adb27e4762101360b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - pass use-uv and use-python through the test transforms. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThe values set in kind.yml were being dropped, so we've been using system\npython and pip instead of uv even though kind.yml tried to do the opposite.\nRevert those kind.yml to the reality to avoid breaking things for now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312740\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/__init__.py", "taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "c8e4399d360d79d760c2e609c08c678b9d7b7cfd", "git_parents": ["6458280a8473e234efb4db5b1c6018c610b760b3"], "node": "53a636746c203b7438f14c840d2d2ce004a0273d", "parents": ["e6a860fdbb48353127a6cbb53074eb6a4104d26f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - build dbus-python against the pinned 3.9 toolchain. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\nThe existing linux64-{2204,2404}-dbus-python wheels are built against\neach Ubuntu image's own system Python (3.10/3.12), which matches the\ntest venv's Python because `use-python: default` was not honored.\n\nAdd linux64-python3.9-dbus-python, built with use-python: \"3.9\" so it\ntargets the same interpreter the test venv actually uses when we move\nback to `use-python: default`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312741\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/python-wheels.yml"], "git_node": "73df45326acfd2e50f8c9c9327446fb9c56ffb20", "git_parents": ["c8e4399d360d79d760c2e609c08c678b9d7b7cfd"], "node": "0ed15061957ce7373cfd82a19d2923f9b754323e", "parents": ["53a636746c203b7438f14c840d2d2ce004a0273d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - pin pycairo to a Python-3.9-compatible version in wheel_requirements.txt. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\npycairo==1.29.0 requires Python \u003e=3.10, but this shared requirements\nfile is now also used to build a wheel against the pinned 3.9\ntoolchain (linux64-python3.9-dbus-python), where pip can't find a\nmatching pycairo release at all and the whole wheel build aborts\nbefore ever getting to the package being built.\n\nSplit it the same way build==1.4.4/1.5.0 already is, using pycairo\n1.28.0 (requires \u003e=3.9) below the 3.10 boundary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312742\n", "files": ["build/wheel_requirements.txt"], "git_node": "d49641f3fe73ee90da6e60ff2211b740d9155579", "git_parents": ["73df45326acfd2e50f8c9c9327446fb9c56ffb20"], "node": "8be4b5db8d8cd17d379809085135226a59d398e4", "parents": ["0ed15061957ce7373cfd82a19d2923f9b754323e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - fix Python.h discovery when building wheels against a fetched python. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\nlinux64-python3.9-dbus-python fetches the pinned python-3.9 toolchain\nto build against, but building pycairo (a transitive build dependency\nvia meson-python for wheel_requirements.txt) failed:\n\n  ../cairo/font.c:32:10: fatal error: Python.h: No such file or directory\n  cc ... -I/python/include/python3.9 ...\n\nbuild-cpython.sh makes the fetched python relocatable by patching\nsysconfig's build_time_vars at extraction time, but its\npython3.X-config script - which build backends like meson-python\nconsult to find headers - still has the unrelocated build-time prefix\nbaked in as plain text, since that script isn't Python code and never\ngets patched. The headers do exist in the fetched toolchain, just not\nwhere meson-python looked.\n\nAdd the real include directory to CPATH, which the compiler searches\nregardless of what -I flags the build backend guessed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312743\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-python-wheel.sh"], "git_node": "6ba86bdb339547602cba97be28b6148e3ac27cd2", "git_parents": ["d49641f3fe73ee90da6e60ff2211b740d9155579"], "node": "9f8619d5af539186930e30c81541b2824d7cd3d5", "parents": ["8be4b5db8d8cd17d379809085135226a59d398e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - mozharness: pass sys.executable to uv venv --python. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nTwo issues here:\n\n- if MOZ_PYTHON_HOME had a different python than sys.executable, we'd\n  create a venv for a different version, and \"activate\" it in the\n  current process by updating (amongst others) sys.path and\n  sys.executable.  The current process would end up with a mix of\n  potentially incompatible entries in sys.path, and a spawned subprocess\n  would use a different version of the interpreter and again\n  incompatible libraries in its sys.path, and hilarity would likely\n  ensue\n\n- when use-uv is set without a fetched python toolchain (`use-python:\n  system`), `MOZ_PYTHON_HOME` isn't set, and create_virtualenv() would\n  fall back to `Path(sys.executable).parents[1]` to guess where the\n  interpreter lives.  That assumes a Unix-style `prefix/bin/python3`\n  layout: going up two levels from `.../bin/python3` lands on `prefix`.\n  On Windows workers there's no bin/ subdir (python3.exe sits in\n  `C:\\mozilla-build\\python3`), so going up two levels overshoots by one,\n  and `uv venv --python=...` gets pointed at a directory with no\n  interpreter in it at all:\n\n    uv venv ... --python=c:\\mozilla-build --no-project\n    No interpreter found for directory `c:\\mozilla-build`\n\nPassing sys.executable directly fixes both issues (uv accepts a literal\ninterpreter path just as well as a prefix).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312744\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/python.py"], "git_node": "c23b8797bb0fec201412fe5983d0f4edb8eefea2", "git_parents": ["6ba86bdb339547602cba97be28b6148e3ac27cd2"], "node": "a04d57f0dbab60e1d29fe116b0383ab239a2e95c", "parents": ["9f8619d5af539186930e30c81541b2824d7cd3d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - run mozharness script with the fetched python. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nWhen `use-python` is not `system`, we need to use the fetched python to\nrun the configured mozharness script, not system python.  run-task takes\ncare of prepending its location to PATH, so use that.\n\nThis also fixes the mozharness_on_generic_worker function to look for\n`use-python` in the right place: we were previously using system python\non windows even when configured to use the fetched one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313239\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mozharness.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mozharness_test.py"], "git_node": "9c9d0f0d2656768887a7fd0bc982e8152005145e", "git_parents": ["c23b8797bb0fec201412fe5983d0f4edb8eefea2"], "node": "d65deeb35659189acc795257c427abd5e637c249", "parents": ["a04d57f0dbab60e1d29fe116b0383ab239a2e95c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for test tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThis was meant to have happened in bug 1888131.  Better late than never.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312746\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/misc.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/xpcshell.yml"], "git_node": "039b86140c7cf8e8d1269a6edf4b0d86c00d847f", "git_parents": ["9c9d0f0d2656768887a7fd0bc982e8152005145e"], "node": "b9fc38a565b55c9ba3e42763a0602a49b45c2e22", "parents": ["d65deeb35659189acc795257c427abd5e637c249"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for mochitest tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312747\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "305d67a75606ee8cbaec3802ea7003dc326916d0", "git_parents": ["039b86140c7cf8e8d1269a6edf4b0d86c00d847f"], "node": "11b46355e4f94173d6d8eaece2d7105e153f85c6", "parents": ["b9fc38a565b55c9ba3e42763a0602a49b45c2e22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for reftest tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312748\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "490256b4a299aa3d6bffcaf7d0b75f6305a338ed", "git_parents": ["305d67a75606ee8cbaec3802ea7003dc326916d0"], "node": "18ad2a6201850155682466891e0587439d424f0f", "parents": ["11b46355e4f94173d6d8eaece2d7105e153f85c6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for web-platform-tests tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312749\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "6c4b2f32e61c4a8eec63c472fd0df6aab4727e56", "git_parents": ["490256b4a299aa3d6bffcaf7d0b75f6305a338ed"],