for borders that can go further inside the primitive than classic borders (superellipse parameter \u003c 1). r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nWith the new corner-shape feature, the area where borders' corners are drawn\nneed to be expanded. The assumption that the corner always fits in a rect\nof the same size as the radii doesn't hold any more.\n\nThis adds the plumbing for the new parameter, actual usage will come in\nfollow-up commits.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313684\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/border_shared.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/border.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/gpu_types.rs"], "git_node": "7b839573c68b7bb24017523b8232e71f524ab1f7", "git_parents": ["209401ff949af22e3ea6697cb2b7668165df2d93"], "node": "958ea46444c4dfb411a12bf75813c8bfee994c4b", "parents": ["09cc5dd9f70c8f2adeb92ffb8d56bd524ce91759"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052937 - Make nsReadableUtils depend less on comparators. r=nika,xpcom-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nThis changes behavior for empty patterns, but the new behavior is\nconsistent with Find().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312808\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsAttrValue.cpp", "dom/filesystem/FileSystemSecurity.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "intl/unicharutil/util/nsUnicharUtils.h", "layout/base/nsCSSFrameConstructor.cpp", "storage/mozStorageAsyncStatement.cpp", "storage/mozStorageStatement.cpp", "toolkit/components/reputationservice/ApplicationReputation.cpp", "xpcom/base/nsMacUtilsImpl.cpp", "xpcom/docs/stringguide.md", "xpcom/string/nsReadableUtils.cpp", "xpcom/string/nsReadableUtils.h", "xpcom/string/nsStringFwd.h", "xpcom/string/nsTStringRepr.h"], "git_node": "1865eee9d6a3ee838e83503dfe7efe2de9d4bd03", "git_parents": ["7b839573c68b7bb24017523b8232e71f524ab1f7"], "node": "0a786aebd57aad5b9e3250082331f9eebab5127c", "parents": ["958ea46444c4dfb411a12bf758