62480b44398", "parents": ["dc7d8e0ce6704354ae99372fe533710e1f015330"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2007200, 2007206: apply code formatting via Lando\" for causing wpt lint failures & build bustages @ TestHttp3ConnectUDPStream.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 352ec53c7d9c8c0b49aa5cfc7a59122f7750edff.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2007200: Add wpt tests for WebTransport exportKeyingMaterial r=jib\"\n\nThis reverts commit a3d89ea678c8e133852841ed40e99e0d3ec1ba02.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2007200: Hook up WebTransport exportKeyingMaterial to necko/neqo r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 04e1ad930476951afda78acb021d086cdf83410c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2007200: Add WebTransport ExportKeyingMaterial backend r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7bcd930d5d79b328e36a44ea505d86db4baa689e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2007200: Implement exportKeyingMaterial() method r=saschanaz,webidl,tschuster,smaug\"\n\nThis reverts commit f882f45e31031cb9f8ad5170a64549ed713806d7.\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/WebTransport.webidl", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.cpp", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.h", "dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.cpp", "dom/webtransport/parent/WebTransportParent.h", "dom/webtransport/shared/PWebTransport.ipdl", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http2WebTransportSession.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3Session.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/Http3WebTransportSession.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/WebTransportSessionBase.h", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/WebTransportSessionProxy.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/webtransport/nsIWebTransport.idl", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/NeqoHttp3Conn.h", "netwerk/socket/neqo_glue/src/lib.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/idlharness.https.sub.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/export-keying-material.https.any.js"], "git_node": "78a5278d9691fdfcb099f561748e626d53df6f90", "git_parents": ["352ec53c7d9c8c0b49aa5cfc7a59122f7750edff"], "node": "daa7a7b4892e814fb53d8651a5e807db5d76d528", "parents": ["cb21b3eec5efd5f89b48e11a6e9d562480b44398"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2007206: Make WebTransportHash members required r=saschanaz,webidl\" for causing wpt lint failures & build bustages @ TestHttp3ConnectUDPStream.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 3c5fbcec304329d5df5aecd7b431ae9162d1a51f.\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/WebTransport.webidl", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.cpp"], "git_node": "db4186c1a4315ca79963edaa22bde0e126f0c119", "git_parents": ["78a5278d9691fdfcb099f561748e626d53df6f90"], "node": "d4293f3c24590d795f92964e2bd46a0cc1b2ca9f", "parents": ["daa7a7b4892e814fb53d8651a5e807db5d76d528"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bas Schouten \u003cbschouten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056070: Add a field to the eTLD+1 pageload event to distinguish the first daily visit. r=denispal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312922\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/metrics.yaml", "tools/performance/PageloadEvent.cpp", "tools/performance/PageloadEvent.h"], "git_node": "0fe805af7a19fa8924a0a54921fed77f76face98", "git_parents": ["db4186c1a4315ca79963edaa22bde0e126f0c119"], "node": "8c96346d5485dfd991c0a93b8730cf34eb188516", "parents": ["d4293f3c24590d795f92964e2bd46a0cc1b2ca9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julie De Lorenzo \u003cjdelorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053616:  Add regression tests for adding to tab group (new/existing group) navigation r=android-reviewers,aaronmt,calu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311352\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/TabDrawerSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/TabbedBrowsingTest.kt"], "git_node": "a2cb4b9e06fe1d98302f5e5bd7c5d91e3d9f9cfb", "git_parents": ["0fe805af7a19fa8924a0a54921fed77f76face98"], "node": "a356452ed3f1a9c38045f9dc71271304ac571240", "parents": ["8c96346d5485dfd991c0a93b8730cf34eb188516"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056894 - Set the number of render backend threads to 2. r=gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313453\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "2a9140aba53d427e04a99610b17a3ff8ef618a7e", "git_parents": ["a2cb4b9e06fe1d98302f5e5bd7c5d91e3d9f9cfb"], "node": "4e286d080ab83044ee9e84222830912e8c34967e", "parents": ["a356452ed3f1a9c38045f9dc71271304ac571240"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051959 - [IPC Urlbar] Phase 6: Search the selected search-mode engine on Enter instead of a stale heuristic. r=daleharvey\n\nIn an engine search mode, Enter navigated using the view's heuristic result.\nOn the message path a search-mode change re-queries asynchronously, so the\nauto-selected heuristic can still carry the previously-cycled engine when Enter\nfires, navigating to the wrong engine (surfacing as browser_searchModeSwitcher_basic\nreaching the real Wikipedia engine and tripping the harness's non-local-connection\nguard).\n\nMake the selected search-mode engine authoritative: when Enter would pick the\nheuristic in an engine search mode, search the current engine directly. The\none-off branch's engine-search (query URL + search recording + form history) is\nextracted into a shared helper the search-mode path reuses.\n\nOpening the engine's search URL directly skips the result-pick path that tags\nthe load with globalHistoryOptions.triggeringSearchEngine, which Places uses to\nrecord the visit source as a search. The shared helper now sets that tag, so\nsearch-mode Enter keeps annotating the visit. This also fixes a pre-existing\nbug: the one-off path already opened the URL directly and never set the tag, so\none-off searches were recorded as organic visits.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310464\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs"], "git_node": "db6ab8040e573ca09ee58e222d0fd44386a9eb1b", "git_parents": ["2a9140aba53d427e04a99610b17a3ff8ef618a7e"], "node": "afbb797eca799e4da4e0b7bef7e7b96dfca9ada3", "parents": ["4e286d080ab83044ee9e84222830912e8c34967e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056877: Share code to set-up prologue for GenerateCallablePrologue and GenerateJitEntryPrologue. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nFor all architectures except ARM64, `GenerateCallablePrologue` and\n`GenerateJitEntryPrologue` emitted the same code to set-up the prologue, but\nconfusingly used different `MacroAssembler` methods to make it more difficult\nto see that the same instructions are emitted.\n\nMove the code to create the prologue into `GenerateCommonPrologue` and call\nthat function from `GenerateCallablePrologue` and `GenerateJitEntryPrologue`.\n\nAdditionally for RISCV64, emit a smaller instruction sequence to create the\nprologue, matching what's used by Clang/GCC.\n\nBefore:\n```\naddi      sp, sp, -8\nsd        ra, 0(sp)\naddi      sp, sp, -8\nsd        fp, 0(sp)\nmv        fp, sp\n```\n\nAfter:\n```\naddi      sp, sp, -16\nsd        ra, 8(sp)\nsd        fp, 0(sp)\nmv        fp, sp\n```\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313442\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/lib/codegen-riscv64-test.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmFrameIter.cpp"], "git_node": "d122bda56578052cd70d6a2926464657527a20bb", "git_parents": ["db6ab8040e573ca09ee58e222d0fd44386a9eb1b"], "node": "7386f182252d643c9bf33ba53506abd298b5419c", "parents": ["afbb797eca799e4da4e0b7bef7e7b96dfca9ada3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "s-rosen \u003csimon.rosen17@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1875517 - Add a playback speed control to the Picture-in-Picture player. r=fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,kpatenio,bolsson,dao\n\nAdds a playback speed button to the Picture-in-Picture window, gated behind\nthe pref media.videocontrols.picture-in-picture.playback-speed.enabled.\nIt opens a panel, modeled on the existing subtitles settings panel, containing a live\nrate readout, a 0.25x-2.0x slider, and one-tap presets for 0.75x/1.0x/1.25x/1.5x/2.0x.\nThe \u003c and \u003e keys (with Shift key as a modifier) step through the standard presets.\n\nThe rate is applied to the originating video through new overridable\nPictureInPictureChildVideoWrapper methods (getPlaybackRate/setPlaybackRate)\nwith the usual fallback implementation. A ratechange listener on the\noriginating video keeps the panel in sync when the rate is changed from\nthe page, and the originating video's rate is carried into the PiP window\nwhen it opens (mirroring the existing volume flow).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306643\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "toolkit/actors/PictureInPictureChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/PictureInPicture.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/content/player.js", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/content/player.xhtml", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/tests/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/pictureinpicture/tests/browser_playbackRate.js", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/pictureinpicture/pictureinpicture.ftl", "toolkit/themes/shared/media/playback-speed-button.svg", "toolkit/themes/shared/minimal-toolkit.jar.inc.mn", "toolkit/themes/shared/pictureinpicture/player.css"], "git_node": "593c8d056e91a5d9f3612c28d371efbd6602aadb", "git_parents": ["d122bda56578052cd70d6a2926464657527a20bb"], "node": "b3575a3229cd04bd70ae7422eebe35cc4ece409f", "parents": ["7386f182252d643c9bf33ba53506abd298b5419c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nirmaladvani \u003cnirmaladvani@live.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2003174 - Remove unused media.benchmark prefs. r=gregp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313775\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "04e47e529c70a622681c650ee9d7a9429a274049", "git_parents": ["593c8d056e91a5d9f3612c28d371efbd6602aadb"], "node": "7fbf6f4558d5764f9cddd256b35f0114be49cf89", "parents": ["b3575a3229cd04bd70ae7422eebe35cc4ece409f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057164 - Skip Rust logins sync while Primary Password is locked r=bdk,sync-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313691\n", "files": ["services/sync/modules/engines/passwords.sys.mjs", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_rust_password_engine_mp_locked.js", "services/sync/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "998102077320135b93550730bc1442cc2a039ff9", "git_parents": ["04e47e529c70a622681c650ee9d7a9429a274049"], "node": "eb80b5c6362544ee50452b3ec3b08007d87babfd", "parents": ["7fbf6f4558d5764f9cddd256b35f0114be49cf89"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057280 - Render the Picture of the Day widget from the thumbnail instead of the high-res image r=Dre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313778\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay/PictureOfTheDay.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/PictureOfTheDay.test.jsx"], "git_node": "d58da1b06d8eb0cf9657371bb774b3f3411b9050", "git_parents": ["998102077320135b93550730bc1442cc2a039ff9"], "node": "cc85026a8c89a0f0d0fadfb8893cc4590bd18131", "parents": ["eb80b5c6362544ee50452b3ec3b08007d87babfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044710 - Allow ProfilingStackFrame::script() during minor GC r=jonco\n\nscript() returned null whenever JSContext::suppressProfilerSampling was set,\nbecause a script might be mid-relocation during a compacting GC. But that flag\nis also set by sites that don't move scripts (minor GC, debugger, JIT frame\nfixup, JitcodeGlobalTable mutations), so JS frames sampled during those windows\nlost line/column attribution.\n\nThe case that hurt us is minor GC during async resumption. Reading tenured\nscript data (filename, line/column via pc()) is safe there: the only\nnursery-movable field is the script's JSFunction, which is reached through\nfunction() and keeps the isProfilerSamplingEnabled() guard.\n\nSo script access is now opt-in. AutoSuppressProfilerSampling takes a\nProfilerScriptAccess option defaulting to Deny; only the minor GC site passes\nAllow. Compacting GC and everything else keep the default.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D304691\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Compacting.cpp", "js/src/gc/Nursery.cpp", "js/src/jit-test/tests/profiler/async-resume-frame-position-gc.js", "js/src/vm/GeckoProfiler-inl.h", "js/src/vm/GeckoProfiler.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.cpp", "js/src/vm/JSContext.h"], "git_node": "8c82a06aa7f5f9bc5ee08fe171a6101d7a7a45cb", "git_parents": ["d58da1b06d8eb0cf9657371bb774b3f3411b9050"], "node": "7d751d254c0a10716db4e94e63d11223b37ffd4f", "parents": ["cc85026a8c89a0f0d0fadfb8893cc4590bd18131"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050022: Smart Window Nova context chips, smarbar and ask dropdown fixes r=mlucks,desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\n**Issue 1:** For Nova, there was a 1px overlay between the rightmost context chip and the smartbar border.\n**Cause**: The smartbar has a rounded border that conflicts with the radius of the chip. It\u2019s not an issue we can fix with an overflow or an updated border radius.\n**Solution**: Add a mask to the inline-end edge of the context chips header. UX already had a look at a screenshot video.\n\n**Issue 2**: Animation/transition on context chips hover is gone.\n**Cause**: I wrongfully moved a CSS attribute to the wrong place to avoid a bug while working on other context chips task. The previous approach using margin-inline-end added some extra spacing for smaller chips.\n**Solution**: Use clip-path to crop the chip label on hover instead of margin. The mask-image was also updated to support that. UX already had a look at a screenshot video.\n\n**Issue 3**: Padding around the ask dropdown increased in the past 2 weeks.\n**Cause**: Panel-item style was updated to include margins on Jul 14 - so we no longer need the padding I added last month.\n**Solution**: Remove padding around the ask dropdown.\n\n**Issue 4**: Smartbar should have the same padding on top and bottom.\n**Solution**:  Update smartbar-button-container bottom padding\n\n**Issue 5**: The model picker and ask button have different chevron down sizes in the smartbar.\n**Solution**: Before the model picker, I changed the smartbar ask button chevron icon to a small size based on Figma. I\u2019m removing this change to use the mod-button default icon size.\n\n**Issue 6**: Smarbar has a 17px font size\n**Solution**: Change it to root font-size (15px on Mac) and increase the vertical padding around it.\n\n**Issue 7**: The pipe (|) in the smartbar ask button has a different color than it should\n**Solution**: Update the pipe color\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313243\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/input-cta/input-cta.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/website-chip-container/website-chip-container.css", "browser/components/multilineeditor/multiline-editor.css", "browser/themes/shared/smartbar.css"], "git_node": "fd77966dc7ccc70a64da5628a29b50b2e08516f6", "git_parents": ["8c82a06aa7f5f9bc5ee08fe171a6101d7a7a45cb"], "node": "f26ba89a16db8de5ffa70a8c7a4e73334d34f1bc", "parents": ["7d751d254c0a10716db4e94e63d11223b37ffd4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Train \u003caaron.train@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056978 - Migrate to gcloud storage in copy-artifacts-from-ftl.py r=jajohnson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313781\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/tests/copy-artifacts-from-ftl.py"], "git_node": "b0eeb14457c474a9f96466202c81bbdb8eccbce1", "git_parents": ["fd77966dc7ccc70a64da5628a29b50b2e08516f6"], "node": "fe2ff934f986b76042a0fac0e3da1102c9743683", "parents": ["f26ba89a16db8de5ffa70a8c7a4e73334d34f1bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053766 - Move the urlbar user-context helpers to UrlbarShared. r=daleharvey\n\nThe urlbar's content modules (UrlbarInput/SmartbarInput, UrlbarView, and\nUrlbarQueryContext) reach UrlbarProviderOpenTabs only for its stateless\nuser-context-id helpers, but the provider is parent-only (SQL, the providers\nmanager) and can't load in a privileged content process. Move that family --\nthe PRIVATE_USER_CONTEXT_ID sentinel plus getUserContextIdForOpenPagesTable,\nisNonPrivateUserContextId, and isContainerUserContextId -- to UrlbarShared,\nthe content-safe module both realms already import, and point every caller\nthere so UrlbarQueryContext can stop importing the provider once it moves to\na content module.\n\nWhile consolidating them, fold the recurring \"normalize a raw container id to\nthe id the open-pages table is keyed by\" pattern into a\nUrlbarShared.normalizedUserContextId helper and route the callers that need it\n(the query context's constructor, and later the parent controller) through it.\n\nBehavior-neutral: the helpers are pure and unchanged; only their home moves.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311718\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderInputHistory.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderOpenTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderPlaces.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderSemanticHistorySearch.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs"], "git_node": "d9470ae684bbcfed2ac7023327615674480e5aa1", "git_parents": ["b0eeb14457c474a9f96466202c81bbdb8eccbce1"], "node": "f237b03571bd13f3db1055d253c83d340bf56b59", "parents": ["fe2ff934f986b76042a0fac0e3da1102c9743683"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iulian moraru \u003cimoraru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2051707 - Add a redirector component and a test message for about:referrals r=omc-reviewers,jhirsch,sachung\" for causing bc failures on browser_aboutDialog_referrals.js.\n\nThis reverts commit c5d47982e77ff7e82e321eb7d03bbcb4abae0e8a.\n", "files": ["browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp", "browser/components/about/components.conf", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/PanelTestProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_aboutURLs.js", "browser/components/originattributes/test/browser/browser_firstPartyIsolation_aboutPages.js", "browser/components/referrals/tests/browser/browser_referralsAppMenu.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging