eb509f738ff3bd.\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "642bb59331d40b8361c0843e77726ab0f31ec7cd", "git_parents": ["60265b532094743fb0ac976004b5cfb8454f60c2"], "node": "a4c0025724e9b72fe2294b8d86b40cf89ebf392c", "parents": ["f45836b3bd85da6c40b8113377efe4be75d40c38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2006262 - Add helpers for parsing Animation.rangeStart/rangeEnd. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312634\n", "files": ["dom/animation/AnimationUtils.cpp", "dom/animation/AnimationUtils.h"], "git_node": "2ec55775e73a65a67ee32981060f09178be1686d", "git_parents": ["642bb59331d40b8361c0843e77726ab0f31ec7cd"], "node": "27cddfd6f2cb69b8c0527ceced2eba0f1da78e28", "parents": ["a4c0025724e9b72fe2294b8d86b40cf89ebf392c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Watt \u003cjwatt@jwatt.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2006262 - Implement Animation.rangeStart and Animation.rangeEnd. r=boris,webidl,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,emilio\n\nhttps://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations-2/#dom-animation-rangestart\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312635\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.cpp", "dom/animation/Animation.h", "dom/webidl/Animation.webidl", "layout/style/typedom/CSSNumericValue.cpp", "layout/style/typedom/CSSNumericValue.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/animation-range-normal-matches-cover.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/animation-range-scroll-timeline.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/intrinsic-iteration-duration.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/setting-timeline.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/change-animation-range-updates-play-state.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-get-set-range.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/interfaces/Animation/scroll-timeline-overallProgress.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/web-animations/interfaces/Animation/style-change-events.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/scroll-animations/view-timelines/view-timeline-on-display-none-element.html"], "git_node": "0ac20659add2125c8e1e09bd71dcbd966e848a2d", "git_parents": ["2ec55775e73a65a67ee32981060f09178be1686d"], "node": "99ad5d879b572bd15cadcf45db40b6e35b954d42", "parents": ["27cddfd6f2cb69b8c0527ceced2eba0f1da78e28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053766 - Move UrlbarQueryContext to its own content module. r=daleharvey\n\nUrlbarQueryContext lived in the system module UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs (moz-src:///),\nwhich a privileged content process can't resolve, yet urlbar content modules\nalready import it. Move the class to its own content module served at chrome://,\nmirroring UrlbarResult -- its wire-serialization partner, also a content .mjs --\nand re-point every importer, including the actor pair, both test heads, and the\ntypes/urlbar.ts alias that resolves the bare {UrlbarQueryContext} JSDoc\nreferences.\n\nBehavior-neutral relocation; the class is unchanged. Its UrlbarPrefs dependency\nstays a moz-src lazy getter, so the class is not yet loadable in a content\nprocess -- that is gated on Bug 2053759 making UrlbarPrefs content-importable,\nafter which the getter flips to chrome://.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311719\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarQueryContext.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/jar.mn", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/types/urlbar.ts", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "4572790828cc0ac748a8c6f40f793a45d496d76a", "git_parents": ["0ac20659add2125c8e1e09bd71dcbd966e848a2d"], "node": "346f931c3306736e2de009fcec89448e5fbbe174", "parents": ["99ad5d879b572bd15cadcf45db40b6e35b954d42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1624579 - Reset the search-mode preview through UrlbarInput's userTypedValue setter. r=daleharvey\n\nOn close after a search-mode preview, the view cleared\ngBrowser.userTypedValue directly. Route it through the input's\nuserTypedValue setter, which is gated on whether the instance is the\naddress bar: the chrome address bar still writes gBrowser.userTypedValue,\nwhile a content-process urlbar uses its local mirror. Behavior-neutral for\nthe address bar.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311708\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs"], "git_node": "9809f4956622290ee62c46bd0acac5c491ddc643", "git_parents": ["4572790828cc0ac748a8c6f40f793a45d496d76a"], "node": "c3f0538dae5212d95f4637ec11860cad2a969188", "parents": ["346f931c3306736e2de009fcec89448e5fbbe174"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1624579 - Only read per-tab query-context data in a browser window. r=mbeier\n\nUrlbarInput.#makeQueryContext and SmartbarInput.#makeQueryContext read the\nselected browser's userContextId, tab group, and current page off the chrome\nwindow's gBrowser, which a content-process urlbar can't reach. Gate those\nreads on being in a browser window (this.window.gBrowser): a content\n\u003cmoz-urlbar\u003e -- a pure-search instance with no per-tab state -- skips them and\nits context keeps the defaults, while the address bar fills them as before.\nSmartbarInput already did this; UrlbarInput now uses the same flow.\nUrlbarQueryContext declares userContextId and tabGroup defaults and documents\nthat currentPage, userContextId, and tabGroup are populated only in a browser\nwindow.\n\nBehavior-neutral for the chrome instances, where gBrowser is present.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311709\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarQueryContext.mjs"], "git_node": "c70f798183bec328f15af0932a23f7fc5f500c76", "git_parents": ["9809f4956622290ee62c46bd0acac5c491ddc643"], "node": "1940e0964868abdd78edfd21b7c08687e90c5d57", "parents": ["c3f0538dae5212d95f4637ec11860cad2a969188"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1624579 - Route urlbar page loads through the parent controller's LoadURL. r=mbeier\n\nUrlbarInput._loadURL and SmartbarInput._loadURL reached the chrome window\ndirectly to call openTrustedLinkIn against a XUL \u003cbrowser\u003e, neither of which\na content-process urlbar can touch. Split them: the child keeps the\ninput/view work (selection, revert, closing the view) and hands the load to\nthe new UrlbarParentController.loadURL over the controller seam, mirroring\nspeculativeConnect.\n\nThe parent resolves the target browser from a stable browserId (or the\nselected browser), supplies the params that reference the chrome window\n(targetBrowser, initiatingDoc), focuses the browser, and runs\nopenTrustedLinkIn. It returns whether the load threw without showing an\nerror page, so the child still reverts the input on failure. Only\nserializable params cross the wire; the \u003cbrowser\u003e and document are rebuilt\nparent-side.\n\nTo verify: the direct path returns the status synchronously (the view\ncloses without a turn delay), so the chrome address bar is behavior-neutral;\nthe message path round-trips it. Navigation, canonized-enter, enter-race,\nslow-query, and new-tab-reset browser tests pass with the message-passing\npref both off and on.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311710\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs"], "git_node": "ee1c3f8dc795f6281ffb6be867d7dac509e5bfae", "git_parents": ["c70f798183bec328f15af0932a23f7fc5f500c76"], "node": "9ad689ffd0cd9aa928db2c7ae6ef29cf1fa54465", "parents": ["1940e0964868abdd78edfd21b7c08687e90c5d57"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1624579 - Move #prepareAddressbarLoad to the parent controller. r=mak\n\nRouting the page load through UrlbarParentController.loadURL left\nwhere it still mutated a XUL \u003cbrowser\u003e and the chrome window (userTypedValue,\ninitialPageLoadedFromUserAction, authPromptAbuseCounter, SitePermissions,\ngInitialPages) -- none of which a content-process urlbar can touch.\n\nMove that bookkeeping into the parent's loadURL, running before\nopenTrustedLinkIn as it did before. The child keeps only the input-value\ndisplay update and hands the resulting value over the seam so the parent\ncan record it as browser.userTypedValue. The parent derives whether it\nserves the addressbar from its sapName, so nothing new crosses the wire\nbesides that value.\n\nTo verify: the direct path keeps its ordering and stays synchronous, so\nthe chrome address bar is behavior-neutral; on the message path the browser\nbookkeeping round-trips alongside the load, which is safe because it's\nbrowser/session state, not urlbar-input state read synchronously after\n_loadURL returns. Navigation, canonized-enter, enter-race, slow-query, and\nnew-tab-reset browser tests pass with the message-passing pref both off and\non.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312256\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs"], "git_node": "1e5a95bd1a6503c3f6cdf875dad5ef21fc5431b5", "git_parents": ["ee1c3f8dc795f6281ffb6be867d7dac509e5bfae"], "node": "efd1ffff38057e76ea6d6ec63d396c5b877e2c23", "parents": ["9ad689ffd0cd9aa928db2c7ae6ef29cf1fa54465"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Swarup Ukil \u003csukil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057061 - Apply text content changes on the frame holding the non-pseudo-element ComputedStyle. r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers,layout-reviewers\n\nThe table wrapper is the primary frame, but its child InnerTableFrame holds\nthe non-pseudo-element ComputedStyle, which our update in\nHandlePrimaryFrameStyleChange() missed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313790\n", "files": ["layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp", "layout/style/test/test_dynamic_change_causing_reflow_content.html"], "git_node": "589a93df90e7924d92b7a8bd03c773203ee70690", "git_parents": ["1e5a95bd1a6503c3f6cdf875dad5ef21fc5431b5"], "node": "dc7f12a8cbce5054d89f43168fc81a2944341621", "parents": ["efd1ffff38057e76ea6d6ec63d396c5b877e2c23"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784883703, "git_changesets": ["c5d47982e77ff7e82e321eb7d03bbcb4abae0e8a", "90340f5a087cb8b80260fc835df18a7e5ac072bb", "637798befc2a032719f170958f277064bd0b67ba", "d9a50b5bb120b89c4e2879df7e6ca877f44cd316", "c5bfddc3de051df543d521d1d2160eda46c9071a", "f28ee5e3ba5bb07338f2a1494885e6aab3ba808f", "aa2f03e31546dd75413410842f4ec5f9405fb310", "5d9e23f2d1cd