branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging b7b1868f2e31da0d089ccb869ec773fa5d9fd9ac with DEVEDITION_154_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "cd088da456a57601344907e0abed8bb5cd78ae13", "git_parents": ["0850dded7a18974407107de29b27299ca5ef9c2e"], "node": "d41d51ece25ea8730dcaa86f3c7bbe3025054cf1", "parents": ["5169a35684c8e8082c13769df5ca4bc94d398bae"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784907460, "git_changesets": ["cd088da456a57601344907e0abed8bb5cd78ae13"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "44956": {"changesets": [{"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055968 - Don't warn in nsCocoaWindow::UnlockNativePointer() when the pointer isn't natively locked; r=mstange\n\nUnlockNativePointer() can be called from nsCocoaWindow::DestroyNativeWindow()\nwhere the pointer may not be natively locked.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313760\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm"], "git_node": "807045cf3293ff3bc80dea5560819d7dc2db74f7", "git_parents": ["589a93df90e7924d92b7a8bd03c773203ee70690"], "node": "eb2dd5f2ff6bae828c03c63e8e6fe97c105f4226", "parents": ["dc7f12a8cbce5054d89f43168fc81a2944341621"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmhommey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057371 - Fetch a prebuilt mozcheck toolchain before trying to build from source. r=linter-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nUse bootstrap_toolchain, the same mechanism already used to locate or\nfetch clang-tidy, gn, cargo-vet, etc., to find a prebuilt mozcheck\nbinary for the host first. This also subsumes the previous manual\n$MOZ_FETCHES_DIR/mozcheck check used in CI. Only fall back to building\nfrom source with a plain `cargo` when no prebuilt binary is available.\n\nAlso remove the check for $MOZ_FETCHES_DIR/rustc/bin/cargo because it's\ndead code in practice as no task on CI is running this linter and has\na dependency on the rustc toolchain.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313916\n", "files": ["tools/lint/mozcheck/__init__.py"], "git_node": "17ba06295a57118e3855a37c646487a255791ad8", "git_parents": ["807045cf3293ff3bc80dea5560819d7dc2db74f7"], "node": "3b84a646e15e6d9d70e3e99144302b5fdd9d4c53", "parents": ["eb2dd5f2ff6bae828c03c63e8e6fe97c105f4226"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055039 - Make `test_queryCaretRect.html` check with dynamic data r=m_kato\n\nThe test checks the query result point relative to the root widget\nwith the fixed value. Therefore, if the widget is not at the top-left\ncorner of the top level widget, it fails to compare the expected values\nand Nova will make the situation. Therefore this patch computes the\nwindow offset in the top level window and add it to the expected\nvalues. Additionally, the test is not HiDPI environment aware.\nTherefore, this makes the test check `window.devicePixelRatio`.\n\nFinally, we don't treat CRLF on Windows separately. Therefore, we don't\nneed to have the CRLF version of the test anymore.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312454\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/chrome/chrome.toml", "dom/tests/mochitest/chrome/queryCaretRect.html", "dom/tests/mochitest/chrome/queryCaretRectUnix.html", "dom/tests/mochitest/chrome/queryCaretRectWin.html", "dom/tests/mochitest/chrome/test_queryCaretRect.html"], "git_node": "1fcbd16b26c0216affab3013841a409a2cef45d7", "git_parents": ["17ba06295a57118e3855a37c646487a255791ad8"], "node": "55a71de2cd5890f9506efe106b3e64de113bd43c", "parents": ["3b84a646e15e6d9d70e3e99144302b5fdd9d4c53"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056539 [wpt PR 61439] - Fix blank canvas output when chaining CSS filters with url() SVG filters, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix blank canvas output when chaining CSS filters with url() SVG filters\n\nCSS filter functions don't clip to bounds and never get a primitive\nsubregion, so their empty subregion was unioned into the next url()\nfilter's default subregion, producing an empty crop rect.\n\nBug: 533040707\nChange-Id: I4142fc547e708b5ba87d1432d26a2195d55dc583\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8083705\nReviewed-by: Stephen Chenney \u003cschenney@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Hyowon Kim \u003chyowon@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1665939}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3801d935087f3f608ad39fe127e4318507760e3c\nwpt-pr: 61439\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/filters/2d.filter.function-then-svg-reference.html"], "git_node": "a31fbe073822f829aa8a91d4dc92f16ca9826f36", "git_parents": ["1fcbd16b26c0216affab3013841a409a2cef45d7"], "node": "8fc0a25a688e6df62e0ed72129f040613641d730", "parents": ["55a71de2cd5890f9506efe106b3e64de113bd43c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jose Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056753 [wpt PR 61469] - ContainerTiming: WPT for inner img containertiming root without ignore, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nContainerTiming: WPT for inner img containertiming root without ignore\n\nBrackets nested-containertiming-and-ignore-on-img.html with the\nwithout-ignore case (2 entries instead of 1).\n\nBug: 489959278\nChange-Id: Id4899a493638a1727a83f69be9ec7b1089dba09c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7842319\nReviewed-by: Scott Haseley \u003cshaseley@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jos\u00e9 Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666047}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 05bdaad6d64b87a20a8f9920279d131f21421af4\nwpt-pr: 61469\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-on-img-without-ignore.html"], "git_node": "f1f4b9e6035014920ba6aa1a3b35d9e711e7859a", "git_parents": ["a31fbe073822f829aa8a91d4dc92f16ca9826f36"], "node": "51aac8c48ba38ad7c9f4fa5fb8031205e27cae22", "parents": ["8fc0a25a688e6df62e0ed72129f040613641d730"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056753 [wpt PR 61469] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61469\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/nested-containertiming-on-img-without-ignore.html.ini"], "git_node": "d7e79dbabc23c5a7976e65c5caf2f1ff1af5e863", "git_parents": ["f1f4b9e6035014920ba6aa1a3b35d9e711e7859a"], "node": "5d64b1cd7ff00ac418ed8c6f61c4342435ba7f5d", "parents": ["51aac8c48ba38ad7c9f4fa5fb8031205e27cae22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056834 [wpt PR 61477] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319562, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319562 (#61477)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7856365907179a472c81ffd97e8899c2f2b66c9a\nwpt-pr: 61477\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-scroll-snap/snap-after-relayout/multiple-aligned-targets/prefer-focused-element-scaled-ancestor.html"], "git_node": "0dc078e52f2f7ac58f2a7b551d5449ade03f0c87", "git_parents": ["d7e79dbabc23c5a7976e65c5caf2f1ff1af5e863"], "node": "4853cc48928e54c9627bc89dbc80dbacf5cebb78", "parents": ["5d64b1cd7ff00ac418ed8c6f61c4342435ba7f5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056832 [wpt PR 61476] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318659, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318659 (#61476)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d82f239e578a0ccc0b80694bac4a58ce588c871e\nwpt-pr: 61476\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/IndexedDB/idbobjectstore-put-unique-index-constraint-is-atomic.any.js"], "git_node": "9c3062bc12243d0fab6a0545754ff860badac885", "git_parents": ["0dc078e52f2f7ac58f2a7b551d5449ade03f0c87"], "node": "e479d6c086ef90fbe7c3eff24df993f10d3f07e8", "parents": ["4853cc48928e54c9627bc89dbc80dbacf5cebb78"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mahesh Bharadwaj Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056828 [wpt PR 61475] - [WebAudio] Reject incompatible ScriptProcessorNode configurations, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Reject incompatible ScriptProcessorNode configurations\n\nWhen WebAudioConfigurableRenderQuantum is enabled, a custom\nrenderSizeHint can result in a render quantum size that is not a\nmultiple of the ScriptProcessorNode's buffer size. This leads to\nout-of-bounds memory access in ScriptProcessorHandler::Process.\n\nThis CL adds validation in ScriptProcessorNode::Create to reject\nincompatible configurations by throwing a NotSupportedError\nDOMException.\n\nWe also update the WPT robustness test helper to support expected\ncreation failures (by returning null), and update the ScriptProcessor\nrobustness test to expect the exception for incompatible configs and\nassert against the actual clamped buffer size for clamped configs.\n\nBug: 521719869\nTest: external/wpt/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-scriptprocessornode-interface/scriptprocessor-rendersizehint.https.html\nChange-Id: I78a3d59dba2ca9d613922006e20611dac940ad2e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7922729\nReviewed-by: Michael Wilson \u003cmjwilson@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mahesh Kannan \u003ckmaheshb@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666384}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a4dfbb234b1faeb5912f213a802047092064ac50\nwpt-pr: 61475\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/resources/rendersizehint-robustness-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-scriptprocessornode-interface/scriptprocessor-rendersizehint.https.html"], "git_node": "2d71be951b3506a06f03fffdd5cd301b1b83f201", "git_parents": ["9c3062bc12243d0fab6a0545754ff860badac885"], "node": "7c38a98910ad9e9b988c724d5783700f26b17581", "parents": ["e479d6c086ef90fbe7c3eff24df993f10d3f07e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056828 [wpt PR 61475] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61475\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-analysernode-interface/test-analyser-resume-after-suspended.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webaudio/the-audio-api/the-scriptprocessornode-interface/scriptprocessor-rendersizehint.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "9468667d50b10768ab3687b54ae21d07f528fea3", "git_parents": ["2d71be951b3506a06f03fffdd5cd301b1b83f201"], "node": "c1372f4b787cc1ae4073907c6c9b1ec4f852ccc5", "parents": ["7c38a98910ad9e9b988c724d5783700f26b17581"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056941 [wpt PR 61480] - Expose RequestDestination \"compression-dictionary\", a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nExpose RequestDestination \"compression-dictionary\"\n\nCurrently, Chromium uses \"dictionary\" as an internal destination. Align\nChromium with spec PR [1], which uses string \"compression-dictionary\"\ninstead. This is a web-exposed behavior change, so do that under a\nruntime flag.  Also add a WPT test to check the new value, a more\ncomplex one is added in [2].\n\n[1] https://github.com/whatwg/fetch/pull/1854\n[2] https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8129944\n\nNO_IFTTT=Both files updated, but the IfThen labels were wrong.\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884\nChange-Id: I54b2047492ebc4d410351a83a10de8d0249b4b3a\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8086393\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Andrea Orru \u003candreaorru@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Josh Karlin \u003cjkarlin@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Takashi Toyoshima \u003ctoyoshim@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Benoit Lize \u003clizeb@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Matthew Denton \u003cmpdenton@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ben Kelly \u003cwanderview@meta.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666398}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 69f36b0704aafee6a79156bfe842a491f482093e\nwpt-pr: 61480\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/fetch-destination.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/resources/fetch-options-worker.js"], "git_node": "ffc23285a41d3bd7d1e6bf641b388d54d882ac55", "git_parents": ["9468667d50b10768ab3687b54ae21d07f528fea3"], "node": "ba10519f0fcdcd9477fd78a1abafe6efbe88b1a8", "parents": ["c1372f4b787cc1ae4073907c6c9b1ec4f852ccc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056941 [wpt PR 61480] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61480\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/fetch/compression-dictionary/fetch-destination.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "d8d35df0ed7a6b9b01cdc02084fdf2292d776b01", "git_parents": ["ffc23285a41d3bd7d1e6bf641b388d54d882ac55"], "node": "f0e2db776b6f1765d31e6a106d296c173fa69e44", "parents": ["ba10519f0fcdcd9477fd78a1abafe6efbe88b1a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056666 [wpt PR 61452] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=308486, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=308486 (#61452)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f3fd4942a169f21f904f7d6aac6b4d70c693d9ce\nwpt-pr: 61452\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/column-rule-width.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/outline-offset.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/outline-width.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/column-rule-width-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/outline-offset-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/outline-width-ref.html"], "git_node": "db10ce9824d9e4a7bf6a79ca4b9dfab492cbcd1f", "git_parents": ["d8d35df0ed7a6b9b01cdc02084fdf2292d776b01"], "node": "5e3cd2f936645ccf3ef9be154fefe450e6faf97d", "parents": ["f0e2db776b6f1765d31e6a106d296c173fa69e44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056666 [wpt PR 61452] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61452\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-viewport/zoom/outline-offset.html.ini"], "git_node": "2a077ee1e73db1de7b1dbb5df300f580892645f0", "git_parents": ["db10ce9824d9e4a7bf6a79ca4b9dfab492cbcd1f"], "node": "e6999a3d46cb746e052f004eab8c4a0147a9be4d", "parents": ["5e3cd2f936645ccf3ef9be154fefe450e6faf97d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnoamr@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056528 [wpt PR 61436] - Add empty #errors to html5tests .dat files as per README, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd empty #errors to html5tests .dat files as per README (#61436)\n\n* Add empty #errors to html5tests .dat filesas per README\n\nCo-authored-by: Jon Surrell \u003csirreal@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n\n* update plaintext invisible characters (#61438)\n\n---------\n\nCo-authored-by: Jon Surrell \u003csirreal@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 37cfee8549b687f1cb0bc8cf772a81ab86de657d\nwpt-pr: 61436\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/html5test-com.dat", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/plain-text-unsafe.dat", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/syntax/parsing/resources/processing-instructions.dat"], "git_node": "bae26c59bf02988e008d746367874593fc6ef0e0", "git_parents": ["2a077ee1e73db1de7b1dbb5df300f580892645f0"], "node": "e6357afa0dfd251275a89c3e91d69eac75facaf0", "parents": ["e6999a3d46cb746e052f004eab8c4a0147a9be4d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057000 [wpt PR 61484] - Hide masked content until all mask-image layers settle, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nHide masked content until all mask-image layers settle\n\nHide content with CSS masks while any mask-image layer is still loading,\nand reveal it once every layer settles, treating failed loads as\ntransparent black\n\nBug: 473987435\nChange-Id: I31e212600b42fe899e2ae42046ac26bc6eaf977c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7620503\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Helmut Januschka \u003chelmut@januschka.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666510}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f2c6f025f424107da538c212117e3fe5b3d34091\nwpt-pr: 61484\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-multi-layer-after-load-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-multi-layer-after-load.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-multi-layer-hidden-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-multi-layer-while-loading.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/mask-image/mask-image-multi-layer-while-loading-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-masking/mask-image/mask-image-multi-layer-while-loading.tentative.html"], "git_node": "e33fd07bab0bf075c7806deef1a1441eb0cca3a3", "git_parents": ["bae26c59bf02988e008d746367874593fc6ef0e0"], "node": "ef94f53ec91f19a06908415c788eaee2bd02c7cc", "parents": ["e6357afa0dfd251275a89c3e91d69eac75facaf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057000 [wpt PR 61484] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61484\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-multi-layer-after-load.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/mask-image/backdrop-filter-mask-image-multi-layer-while-loading.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-masking/mask-image/mask-image-multi-layer-while-loading.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "73e92bb98e246731b84c89ce8e1a653e0e93dbdc", "git_parents": ["e33fd07bab0bf075c7806deef1a1441eb0cca3a3"], "node": "39ddae30fc0fe53083d2bc127f9fc9874ea5df21", "parents": ["ef94f53ec91f19a06908415c788eaee2bd02c7cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giovanni Del Valle \u003cgdelvalle@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056838 [wpt PR 61478] - [Connection-Allowlist] Add connectionallowlist iframe attribute + IPC transport, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Connection-Allowlist] Add connectionallowlist iframe attribute + IPC transport\n\nThis is one in a series of CLs:\n\n1. https://crrev.com/c/7926080 - Rename AllowCSPFromHeaderValue to OriginOrWildcardHeaderValue\n2. https://crrev.com/c/7925634 - Add Connection-Allowlist embedded enforcement primitives\n3. https://crrev.com/c/7925636 - [You are here.]\n4. https://crrev.com/c/7933938 - Enforce Connection-Allowlist embedded enforcement handshake\n\nSecond CL for Connection-Allowlist embedded enforcement (after the\nnetwork primitives; WICG/connection-allowlists#1). Adds the renderer\nattribute and delivers it to the browser, with no enforcement yet:\n\n* New `ConnectionAllowlistEmbeddedEnforcement` runtime feature, kept\n  separate from `ConnectionAllowlist` so this piece can iterate\n  independently.\n* `connectionallowlist` iframe content attribute, with a reflecting\n  `connectionAllowlist` IDL attribute (flag-gated). The renderer\n  validates the value by parsing it -- the structured-field grammar\n  rejects header injection and other malformed input -- and sends the\n  raw structured-header value to the browser via IframeAttributes.\n* The browser receives it on FrameTreeNode\n  (`connection_allowlist_attribute()`).\n\nA browsertest verifies the attribute reaches the browser and that the\nIDL attribute reflects it. Enforcement of the delivered value (the\nnavigation handshake) follows in the next CL.\n\nBug: 522111613\nChange-Id: I3b12446776abc5c44bfef69b3249c4ea4771bc06\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7925636\nReviewed-by: Andrew Verge \u003caverge@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rakina Zata Amni \u003crakina@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike West \u003cmkwst@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Giovanni Del Valle \u003cgdelvalle@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666523}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7b4ab497613481693e03af107b93bd4d25cb223f\nwpt-pr: 61478\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/connection-allowlist/tentative/iframe-connectionallowlist-reflection.html"], "git_node": "c8c80887ae8b90058347d2e7100bcc2feec86462", "git_parents": ["73e92bb98e246731b84c89ce8e1a653e0e93dbdc"], "node": "608ca00633267e453c788ecf679ddeb6eeb79b39", "parents": ["39ddae30fc0fe53083d2bc127f9fc9874ea5df21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056838 [wpt PR 61478] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61478\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/connection-allowlist/tentative/iframe-connectionallowlist-reflection.html.ini"], "git_node": "70d031e356a1a2c52ac4d00345e824553da9fbd9", "git_parents": ["c8c80887ae8b90058347d2e7100bcc2feec86462"], "node": "000d995e570feaf0c22bbcee98c29131d2714d37", "parents": ["608ca00633267e453c788ecf679ddeb6eeb79b39"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056532 [wpt PR 61437] - [WebAudio] Enforce speaker-selection permissions policy in setSinkId, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebAudio] Enforce speaker-selection permissions policy in setSinkId\n\nEnforce the 'speaker-selection' permissions policy in\nAudioContext.setSinkId() on the renderer side, and ensure the browser\nside checks the policy before validating the device ID.\n\nPreviously, AudioContext.setSinkId() did not check the policy, leading\nto incorrect NotFoundError exceptions instead of NotAllowedError when\nthe policy was disabled and an invalid device ID was used.\n\nSimilarly, the browser-side AudioOutputAuthorizationHandler validated\nthe device ID before checking the policy, causing the same issue.\n\nWe now check the policy early in Blink, and defer the device ID\nvalidation in the browser until after the policy check.\n\nexternal/wpt/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-*\nTAG=agy\nCONV=4e2f1dcf-7770-427b-a524-e92369d8aaab\n\nBug: 40876498\nTest: Run run_wpt_tests.py with\nChange-Id: I990a01ad8472ce652619e21ab8b980c20fa8fb70\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8117150\nCommit-Queue: Hongchan Choi \u003chongchan@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Guido Urdaneta \u003cguidou@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666564}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: df282a958fef6d6926ef737e452d27c93b98610e\nwpt-pr: 61437\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/resources/permissions-policy-speaker-selection.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-allowed-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-allowed-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-disabled-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-disabled-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html.headers"], "git_node": "8a4b29b4a420e3bdfe27002c3249af3b3adc7430", "git_parents": ["70d031e356a1a2c52ac4d00345e824553da9fbd9"], "node": "ce3a879f80cc1bd7501705113ecb6fc66aa1689d", "parents": ["000d995e570feaf0c22bbcee98c29131d2714d37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056532 [wpt PR 61437] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61437\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-allowed-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/permissions-policy/speaker-selection-disabled-by-permissions-policy.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "8193ebe72346f529f0285e6e15638497d916511b", "git_parents": ["8a4b29b4a420e3bdfe27002c3249af3b3adc7430"], "node": "bd23fbea1ef557491f642355595799cddf74bd0d", "parents": ["ce3a879f80cc1bd7501705113ecb6fc66aa1689d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Gill \u003csammy.gill@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056683 [wpt PR 61455] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=302111, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=302111 (#61455)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 23354ce7c94088b1d61e5b20ef8141d7fc1b1936\nwpt-pr: 61455\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/border-width-keywords.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/column-rule-width-keywords.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/outline-width-keywords.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-viewport/zoom/reference/border-width-keywords-ref.ht