er and compositor. This preserves linear tiling when it is the only supported option and avoids EGL import failures on NVIDIA.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313910\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "a061350a23f050be24861637ed379dcf06160f2c", "git_parents": ["ccbb891c28908ecb558caa3e79e29ab004e6d9f5"], "node": "e2a1bf5f6a1a9730e96b8553d709cc25c70f1640", "parents": ["290bad82b433d51c626117dbe831d24539cdf7e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055416: Propagate reftype when redefining WasmNullConstant at uses. r=bvisness\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312488\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/regress/bug2055416.js", "js/src/jit/shared/Lowering-shared-inl.h"], "git_node": "3632c9752ede091d96511110977305ceb1d6ed10", "git_parents": ["a061350a23f050be24861637ed379dcf06160f2c"], "node": "0df97b76cfad792a2d661725273b2d3fd669b43b", "parents": ["e2a1bf5f6a1a9730e96b8553d709cc25c70f1640"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 1: Add MacroAssembler::testValueSet. r=jandem\n\nAdd `testValueSet` based on the arch-specific `branchTestValue` method.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312215\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/arm/MacroAssembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm64/MacroAssembler-arm64.cpp", "js/src/jit/loong64/MacroAssembler-loong64.cpp", "js/src/jit/mips64/MacroAssembler-mips64.cpp", "js/src/jit/riscv64/MacroAssembler-riscv64.cpp", "js/src/jit/wasm32/MacroAssembler-wasm32.cpp", "js/src/jit/x64/MacroAssembler-x64.cpp", "js/src/jit/x86/MacroAssembler-x86.cpp"], "git_node": "260915f55e6af228b60f8c795d5dc063ade1afe1", "git_parents": ["3632c9752ede091d96511110977305ceb1d6ed10"], "node": "3a6a12de55aa0202f4f94e407b404e902ff4439d", "parents": ["0df97b76cfad792a2d661725273b2d3fd669b43b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 2: Use MacroAssembler::testValueSet. r=jandem\n\nReplace `cmp64Set` now that `testValueSet` is available.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312216\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "32d174df81cf755f2f5206ebb0e7f829843d05ff", "git_parents": ["260915f55e6af228b60f8c795d5dc063ade1afe1"], "node": "4099ab1310242c5b932546820a47db2f4bbd61cf", "parents": ["3a6a12de55aa0202f4f94e407b404e902ff4439d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 3: Replace LNode::mirRaw() with LNode::mir(). r=jandem\n\nAnd add `MBinaryCache::jsop()` to return the `JSOp` of a binary cache.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312217\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.h"], "git_node": "2e4bffc5e04c3e4918d7e7d718d7c6920e4b9484", "git_parents": ["32d174df81cf755f2f5206ebb0e7f829843d05ff"], "node": "da6499b2da3f2c0b88b50d434347e168ed6f0f76", "parents": ["4099ab1310242c5b932546820a47db2f4bbd61cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 4: Add MacroAssembler::equalStrings. r=jandem\n\nAdd `equalStrings` in preparation of part 5.\n\nAlso slightly improve the codegen and support the empty string case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312218\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.cpp", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h"], "git_node": "4f993eb1feb35d3184531a3888a44e428a47ef16", "git_parents": ["2e4bffc5e04c3e4918d7e7d718d7c6920e4b9484"], "node": "5e8cfe134675b73cc42a2a068bd3f9681cd73078", "parents": ["da6499b2da3f2c0b88b50d434347e168ed6f0f76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 5: Add MStrictConstantCompareString. r=jandem\n\nAdd an instruction to compare a String against Value when strict-equality is used.\n\nUsed in part 9.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312219\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml"], "git_node": "a17c44a3d32116e60ac48fb1aef11d437ef46795", "git_parents": ["4f993eb1feb35d3184531a3888a44e428a47ef16"], "node": "05f21b526fc4de97d0d912a2be4acd9414a135ae", "parents": ["5e8cfe134675b73cc42a2a068bd3f9681cd73078"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 6: Add MStrictConstantCompareObject. r=jandem\n\nAdd an instruction to compare an Object against a Value when strict-equality\nsemantics are used.\n\nUsed in part 9.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312220\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml"], "git_node": "0f222aa9d77c79b22ff2d8d93611839d30b56185", "git_parents": ["a17c44a3d32116e60ac48fb1aef11d437ef46795"], "node": "56ff890401cd006419d57d1d69cd480b152fe739", "parents": ["05f21b526fc4de97d0d912a2be4acd9414a135ae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 7: Add TryBitwise to avoid creating a MBinaryCache. r=jandem\n\nAvoid creating Ion ICs for binary bitwise operations when neither input is a Value\nand both inputs can be truncated through `MTruncateToInt32`.\n\nThis optimisation is performed early instead of in `MBinaryCache::foldsTo`, because\n`MBinaryCache` adds resume points which can keep operands alive. For example in the\ntest case from bug 1997557, this leads to having extra `MBox` instructions, where\nthe `MBox` result is only kept alive for resume points. (`MBox` can't be recovered,\nso when it has resume point uses, it can't DCE'd.)\n\nAll except for one `MBinaryCache` instruction in SunSpider, where both operands\nare `MBox`, are elimated through this new optimisation.\n\nThis avoids 146 `MBinaryCache` instructions for `JSOp::BitAnd` when running\nSunSpider in JetStream 3. After this change there are still 67 `MBinaryCache`\nfor `JSOp::BitAnd` left. Adding support for `MPhi` can help to avoid one\nadditional `MBinaryCache`, but this isn't yet implemented.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312221\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/binary-bitwise-ic-fold.js", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "2b3e61e5fc2b1aada313d735dc66053677ba3003", "git_parents": ["0f222aa9d77c79b22ff2d8d93611839d30b56185"], "node": "994b80823f5f9231016fc870ce6c72753d972c69", "parents": ["56ff890401cd006419d57d1d69cd480b152fe739"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 8: Add TryCompare. r=jandem\n\nSimilar to part 7, avoid creating `MBinaryCache` for comparisons when neither operand is a Value.\n\nThis case doesn't occur in JetStream 3, but was mentioned in the description of bug 1997557.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312222\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/binary-compare-ic-fold.js", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "7f435e0ba63fbfc06cb8e371d1bb5a59be3f9d6b", "git_parents": ["2b3e61e5fc2b1aada313d735dc66053677ba3003"], "node": "ddbd66d4960bda4016da31c85c8d047d491f20df", "parents": ["994b80823f5f9231016fc870ce6c72753d972c69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andr\u00e9 Bargull \u003candre.bargull@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1997557 - Part 9: Add TryStrictConstantCompare. r=jandem\n\nAvoid creating `MBinaryCache` when a strict-constant-compare instruction can\nbe used.\n\nStrict-equality comparison against a String constant occurs multiple times and\nis therefore probably the most important case to optimise. Strict-equality\ncomparison against an Object constant only occurs in \"chai-wtb\", but because\nit's easy to support this case, also optimise for it. Strict-equality\ncomparison against an Int32, Undefined, or Null constant can be supported\nthrough existing `MStrictConstantCompareInt32` resp. `MCompare` instructions,\nso these cases are also supported.\n\nOverview how often `MBinaryCache` can be avoided in JetStream 3 test suites:\n\n`MStrictConstantCompareString`:\n- acorn-wtb: 1\n- typescript-lib: 1\n- ML: 2\n- babylon-wtb: 3\n- validatorjs: 7\n- esprima-next-wtb: 10\n- lebab-wtb: 13\n- babel-wtb: 18\n- postcss-wtb: 25\n- proxy-vue: 26\n- prettier-wtb: 27\n- jsdom-d3-startup: 45\n- OfflineAssembler: 67\n- babel-minify-wtb: 130\n\n`MStrictConstantCompareObject`:\n- chai-wtb: 1\n\n`MStrictConstantCompareInt32`:\n- typescript-lib: 4\n\n`MCompare(Undefined)`:\n- lebab-wtb: 1\n- babel-wtb: 1\n\n`MCompare(Null)`:\n- Doesn't occur in JetStream 3, only added for consistency with the `Undefined` case.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312223\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/warp/binary-strictcompare-ic-fold.js", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "40b0a02d713ff86ded88f414e8fe266ea7375a31", "git_parents": ["7f435e0ba63fbfc06cb8e371d1bb5a59be3f9d6b"], "node": "9bf60504ac3d2cffe0878c67616963bad5681ddb", "parents": ["ddbd66d4960bda4016da31c85c8d047d491f20df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandre Poirot \u003cpoirot.alex@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053052 - [devtools] Add minimal telemetry for Local Mode. r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313021\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/LocalModeMappings.sys.mjs", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox-options.js", "devtools/client/shared/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "8db8efdb3c34ccc26b9c4e121dc38cd927a4e7fc", "git_parents": ["40b0a02d713ff86ded88f414e8fe266ea7375a31"], "node": "9d83973e0dcab0f0cbd36f1238ce9ab5db03c994", "parents": ["9bf60504ac3d2cffe0878c67616963bad5681ddb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055831 - bump uv toolchain from 0.7.2 to 0.11.28. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\nI'm seeing errors when running against our pypi.pub.build.mozilla.org\nmirror like \"Failed to unzip wheel\" / \"Encountered an unexpected\nheader\", which appear to have been fixed some time after 0.7.2.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312710\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "9a083936284093686bcc023ae7f1427e17f4b567", "git_parents": ["8db8efdb3c34ccc26b9c4e121dc38cd927a4e7fc"], "node": "0e3062d70e82254974456db96ba05edb9083afa9", "parents": ["9d83973e0dcab0f0cbd36f1238ce9ab5db03c994"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - pass use-uv and use-python through the test transforms. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThe values set in kind.yml were being dropped, so we've been using system\npython and pip instead of uv even though kind.yml tried to do the opposite.\nRevert those kind.yml to the reality to avoid breaking things for now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312740\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/__init__.py", "taskcluster/kinds/browsertime/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "cc3d900c90d36cdb442092af856e141be9aa26fa", "git_parents": ["9a083936284093686bcc023ae7f1427e17f4b567"], "node": "2773104162c0294f12d0b6ce5fede8008044d4ad", "parents": ["0e3062d70e82254974456db96ba05edb9083afa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - let use-python be gated by test-platform. r=jlorenzo\n\nandroid-hw tests break if we use our own python, so we need to keep\nusing the system one there.  Allow that in the test transforms.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313708\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/__init__.py"], "git_node": "df6894eb7ce6401d9ecc0e9e8b164d187602151f", "git_parents": ["cc3d900c90d36cdb442092af856e141be9aa26fa"], "node": "0596d9ae80c73d5acff53137ecabe41d712f1d77", "parents": ["2773104162c0294f12d0b6ce5fede8008044d4ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - build dbus-python against the pinned 3.9 toolchain. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\nThe existing linux64-{2204,2404}-dbus-python wheels are built against\neach Ubuntu image's own system Python (3.10/3.12), which matches the\ntest venv's Python because `use-python: default` was not honored.\n\nAdd linux64-python3.9-dbus-python, built with use-python: \"3.9\" so it\ntargets the same interpreter the test venv actually uses when we move\nback to `use-python: default`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312741\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/python-wheels.yml"], "git_node": "4454775cb6c6b99e3f573e75d35e5a0190442a84", "git_parents": ["df6894eb7ce6401d9ecc0e9e8b164d187602151f"], "node": "7816f9c630242b034dcd3a35f4fe0584602e2471", "parents": ["0596d9ae80c73d5acff53137ecabe41d712f1d77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - pin pycairo to a Python-3.9-compatible version in wheel_requirements.txt. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\npycairo==1.29.0 requires Python \u003e=3.10, but this shared requirements\nfile is now also used to build a wheel against the pinned 3.9\ntoolchain (linux64-python3.9-dbus-python), where pip can't find a\nmatching pycairo release at all and the whole wheel build aborts\nbefore ever getting to the package being built.\n\nSplit it the same way build==1.4.4/1.5.0 already is, using pycairo\n1.28.0 (requires \u003e=3.9) below the 3.10 boundary.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312742\n", "files": ["build/wheel_requirements.txt"], "git_node": "64da1ebbf3af66ff9dc7b95afc2ce774563326da", "git_parents": ["4454775cb6c6b99e3f573e75d35e5a0190442a84"], "node": "6d566d3f77edbc0030745ad533fe32903a6b8919", "parents": ["7816f9c630242b034dcd3a35f4fe0584602e2471"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - fix Python.h discovery when building wheels against a fetched python. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,bhearsum,ahochheiden\n\nlinux64-python3.9-dbus-python fetches the pinned python-3.9 toolchain\nto build against, but building pycairo (a transitive build dependency\nvia meson-python for wheel_requirements.txt) failed:\n\n  ../cairo/font.c:32:10: fatal error: Python.h: No such file or directory\n  cc ... -I/python/include/python3.9 ...\n\nbuild-cpython.sh makes the fetched python relocatable by patching\nsysconfig's build_time_vars at extraction time, but its\npython3.X-config script - which build backends like meson-python\nconsult to find headers - still has the unrelocated build-time prefix\nbaked in as plain text, since that script isn't Python code and never\ngets patched. The headers do exist in the fetched toolchain, just not\nwhere meson-python looked.\n\nAdd the real include directory to CPATH, which the compiler searches\nregardless of what -I flags the build backend guessed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312743\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-python-wheel.sh"], "git_node": "96e2a7c1c87468dcc0c839d51ff6fb86265110b8", "git_parents": ["64da1ebbf3af66ff9dc7b95afc2ce774563326da"], "node": "038672812076826fd4f86024776f8bdce0824cd6", "parents": ["6d566d3f77edbc0030745ad533fe32903a6b8919"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - mozharness: pass sys.executable to uv venv --python. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nTwo issues here:\n\n- if MOZ_PYTHON_HOME had a different python than sys.executable, we'd\n  create a venv for a different version, and \"activate\" it in the\n  current process by updating (amongst others) sys.path and\n  sys.executable.  The current process would end up with a mix of\n  potentially incompatible entries in sys.path, and a spawned subprocess\n  would use a different version of the interpreter and again\n  incompatible libraries in its sys.path, and hilarity would likely\n  ensue\n\n- when use-uv is set without a fetched python toolchain (`use-python:\n  system`), `MOZ_PYTHON_HOME` isn't set, and create_virtualenv() would\n  fall back to `Path(sys.executable).parents[1]` to guess where the\n  interpreter lives.  That assumes a Unix-style `prefix/bin/python3`\n  layout: going up two levels from `.../bin/python3` lands on `prefix`.\n  On Windows workers there's no bin/ subdir (python3.exe sits in\n  `C:\\mozilla-build\\python3`), so going up two levels overshoots by one,\n  and `uv venv --python=...` gets pointed at a directory with no\n  interpreter in it at all:\n\n    uv venv ... --python=c:\\mozilla-build --no-project\n    No interpreter found for directory `c:\\mozilla-build`\n\nPassing sys.executable directly fixes both issues (uv accepts a literal\ninterpreter path just as well as a prefix).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312744\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/python.py"], "git_node": "941ec2f3c68ed1e5bd4f0a8ff1c788a14bad0a88", "git_parents": ["96e2a7c1c87468dcc0c839d51ff6fb86265110b8"], "node": "70eaa4c647a7e87d21e23daeaa27b1b72704e9a6", "parents": ["038672812076826fd4f86024776f8bdce0824cd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - mozharness: don't use uv venv --relocatable on mac. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\n`uv venv --relocatable` causes console scripts to have a #!/bin/sh\nwrapper that calls `realpath` (since\nhttps://github.com/astral-sh/uv/pull/8079).  That command is not\navailable on macOS 10.15 (AFAICT it was added in 13), so skip the\n`--relocatable` flag there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313703\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/base/python.py"], "git_node": "6b1f877147b01e2a39682370726e9e080f27e18d", "git_parents": ["941ec2f3c68ed1e5bd4f0a8ff1c788a14bad0a88"], "node": "3ca9dfcbdef3917c1982dc2779be5974ec2d29c3", "parents": ["70eaa4c647a7e87d21e23daeaa27b1b72704e9a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - run mozharness script with the fetched python. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nWhen `use-python` is not `system`, we need to use the fetched python to\nrun the configured mozharness script, not system python.  run-task takes\ncare of prepending its location to PATH, so use that.\n\nThis also fixes the mozharness_on_generic_worker function to look for\n`use-python` in the right place: we were previously using system python\non windows even when configured to use the fetched one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313239\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mozharness.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mozharness_test.py"], "git_node": "7fbb1a62a4f5d6e9494283a3fdf17aa0d57dddb4", "git_parents": ["6b1f877147b01e2a39682370726e9e080f27e18d"], "node": "7d1f01dafb0267cf53eacd429c468673e762b0ba", "parents": ["3ca9dfcbdef3917c1982dc2779be5974ec2d29c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1577227 - Add stats counters for IDB mozGetAll/mozGetAllKeys, and mark them as deprecated. r=dom-storage-reviewers,webidl,saschanaz,jari\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313037\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDeprecatedOperationList.inc", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/locales/en-US/chrome/dom/dom.properties", "dom/push/PushDB.sys.mjs", "dom/webidl/IDBIndex.webidl", "dom/webidl/IDBObjectStore.webidl"], "git_node": "b0c15252298550d4b2c7d1f7efb16b7d96ef2b40", "git_parents": ["7fbb1a62a4f5d6e9494283a3fdf17aa0d57dddb4"], "node": "368311ac493a8679b36661a7f1b8de54dfbaca76", "parents": ["7d1f01dafb0267cf53eacd429c468673e762b0ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047215 - Part 1: Close tabs from non-interacting windows with Manage Tabs Tool r=jlewis\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313064\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ToolUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ToolUI.js"], "git_node": "17c390739059a5aa1523396be040ee292629dac1", "git_parents": ["b0c15252298550d4b2c7d1f7efb16b7d96ef2b40"], "node": "60afe648bc59bf2435721d2ffb4cb927dafd783a", "parents": ["368311ac493a8679b36661a7f1b8de54dfbaca76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047215 - Part 2: Undo closing tabs from non-interacting windows with Manage Tabs Tool r=jlewis,cdipersio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313065\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/ManageTabs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_ManageTabs.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatConversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/TabManagementService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ToolUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_manage_tabs_tool.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatConversation.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_TabManagementService.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ToolUI.js"], "git_node": "1f3fe59d5fab396251459c20e4bb16a8761f280c", "git_parents": ["17c390739059a5aa1523396be040ee292629dac1"], "node": "5bfb906f1fd46eb3541d2cb7cb0ea2c39449c52a", "parents": ["60afe648bc59bf2435721d2ffb4cb927dafd783a"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784910802, "git_changesets": ["807045cf3293ff3bc80dea5560819d7dc2db74f7", "17ba06295a57118e3855a37c646487a255791ad8", "1fcbd16b26c0216affab3013841a409a2cef45d7", "a31fbe073822f829aa8a91d4dc92f16ca9826f36", "f1f4b9e6035014920ba6aa1a3b35d9e711e7859a", "d7e79dbabc23c5a7976e65c5caf2f1ff1af5e863", "0dc078e52f2f7ac58f2a7b551d5449ade03f0c87", "9c3062bc12243d0fab6a0545754ff860badac885", "2d71be951b3506a06f03fffdd5cd301b1b83f201", "9468667d50b10768ab3687b54ae21d07f528fea3", "ffc23285a41d3bd7d1e6bf641b388d54d882ac55", "d8d35df0ed7a6b9b01cdc02084fdf2292d776b01", "db10ce9824d9e4a7bf6a79ca4b9dfab492cbcd1f", "2a077ee1e73db1de7b1dbb5df300f580892645f0", "bae26c59bf02988e008d746367874593fc6ef0e0", "e33fd07bab0bf075c7806deef1a1441eb0cca3a3", "73e92bb98e246731b84c89ce8e1a653e0e93dbdc", "c8c80887ae8b90058347d2e7100bcc2feec86462", "70d031e356a1a2c52ac4d00345e824553da9fbd9", "8a4b29b4a420e3bdfe27002c3249af3b3adc7430", "8193ebe72346f529f0285e6e15638497d916511b", "8c2b4141c28b41cdfe86318420354aae1af8d2f2", "394866f1a69702d82626a4d9f429a93233252a21", "8ba6f490e25565d9caadefe2314b1c4359d90f64", "b05f8db0bff70627062822b0b3c51a9181583163", "e180d59f475caa6976030527d933e6eddfc01a7c", "5d0662e89f91b3bb7f01a141196b09c178d2f84e", "b779d099a1bc24d85c1b03da6ca4b87aae37951d", "9341113fd7a41e4e34f189801149cd3e1d3f132a", "8197f602d8b4721ac10e3c19e25c594930c6aca7", "db8b42f057dbaa6775601c75ca0ff88de093f3ff", "d0db7395837d69a195341bea6e6c375a58e1859a", "3535515119488be40534ff8c32572457e01636d6", "f9d543cc88e1ef5dde41665abb3e33d3568f6bc6", "a8d2e059be11c1e787f07e8fddb53efd82eece15", "ccbb891c28908ecb558caa3e79e29ab004e6d9f5", "a061350a23f050be24861637ed379dcf06160f2c", "3632c9752ede091d96511110977305ceb1d6ed10", "260915f55e6af228b60f8c795d5dc063ade1afe1", "32d174df81cf755f2f5206ebb0e7f829843d05ff", "2e4bffc5e04c3e4918d7e7d718d7c6920e4b9484", "4f993eb1feb35d3184531a3888a44e428a47ef16", "a17c44a3d32116e60ac48fb1aef11d437ef46795", "0f222aa9d77c79b22ff2d8d93611839d30b56185", "2b3e61e5fc2b1aada313d735dc66053677ba3003", "7f435e0ba63fbfc06cb8e371d1bb5a59be3f9d6b", "40b0a02d713ff86ded88f414e8fe266ea7375a31", "8db8efdb3c34ccc26b9c4e121dc38cd927a4e7fc", "9a083936284093686bcc023ae7f1427e17f4b567", "cc3d900c90d36cdb442092af856e141be9aa26fa", "df6894eb7ce6401d9ecc0e9e8b164d187602151f", "4454775cb6c6b99e3f573e75d35e5a0190442a84", "64da1ebbf3af66ff9dc7b95afc2ce774563326da", "96e2a7c1c87468dcc0c839d51ff6fb86265110b8", "941ec2f3c68ed1e5bd4f0a8ff1c788a14bad0a88", "6b1f877147b01e2a39682370726e9e080f27e18d", "7fbb1a62a4f5d6e9494283a3fdf17aa0d57dddb4", "b0c15252298550d4b2c7d1f7efb16b7d96ef2b40", "17c390739059a5aa1523396be040ee292629dac1", "1f3fe59d5fab396251459c20e4bb16a8761f280c"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "44957": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging b7b1868f2e31da0d089ccb869ec773fa5d9fd9ac with FIREFOX_154_0b2_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "4a3636b562d3b82230fc990b3c486221c55540ea", "git_parents": ["cd088da456a57601344907e0abed8bb5cd78ae13"], "node": "6faeec5b00cf1abc41384174cdb1461f71fdcc6c", "parents": ["d41d51ece25ea8730dcaa86f3c7bbe3025054cf1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1784912251, "git_changesets": ["4a3636b562d3b82230fc990b3c486221c55540ea"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "44958": {"changesets": [{"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054502 - Move UrlbarInput::_whereToOpen to UrlbarChildController::whereToOpen, route BrowserUtils.whereToOpenLink through UrlbarChild. r=mbeier\n\nFor a content-process \u003cmoz-urlbar\u003e (e.g. about:newtab), UrlbarInput can't compute\nwhere to open a picked result: _whereToOpen calls BrowserUtils.whereToOpenLink (a\nsystem module a content-web scope can't import) and reads gBrowser directly.\n\nMove the computation into UrlbarChildController.whereToOpen (with the\nisCanonizeKeyboardEvent helper it uses), which is content-safe: event modifiers,\nprefs, and a guarded gBrowser read for the empty-tab reuse (absent in a content\nprocess, so a content input skips reuse). Only the BrowserUtils.whereToOpenLink\ncall routes through the UrlbarChild actor, which is privileged and runs in the\ninput's own process, so the whole computation stays synchronous with the live\nevent passed straight through, preserving whereToOpenLink's sourceEvent handling.\n\nUrlbarInput and SmartbarInput drop their own _whereToOpen and\nbrowser_whereToOpen.js now drives the controller entry point instead of the\nremoved method. Behavior-neutral for the chrome address bar and search bars.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311856\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_whereToOpen.js"], "git_node": "7bd32bb6c4a2cd66a9ddecc3c4041bf619625d32", "git_parents": ["1f3fe59d5fab396251459c20e4bb16a8761f280c"], "node": "77556aa680c9a54ee7a3cc6c88b563b09fadc96f", "parents": ["5bfb906f1fd46eb3541d2cb7cb0ea2c39449c52a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054502 - Rename UrlbarChildController's #parent field to #parentController. r=daleharvey\n\nBehavior-neutral rename of the private field to mirror the public\n`parentController` getter and avoid confusion with the `UrlbarParent`\nactor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311964\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs"], "git_node": "8cf065ba3dfb53cad5be57f0f51816e1912dfb75", "git_parents": ["7bd32bb6c4a2cd66a9ddecc3c4041bf619625d32"], "node": "3262777ad01a8fe7f418e242c3559dbe5e29c8a7", "parents": ["77556aa680c9a54ee7a3cc6c88b563b09fadc96f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053751 - Move parent-only search recording out of urlbar content to the parent controller. r=Standard8\n\nBrowserSearchTelemetry and ASRouter are parent-process modules, recordSearch\nneeds the live \u003cbrowser\u003e and resolved engine, and the search-count prefs can\nonly be written in the parent -- so urlbar content code can't do any of this\ndirectly once it runs in a content process. Route it all to\nUrlbarParentController through the controller pair (directly in-process, or as\nactor messages on the message path), the same way engagement telemetry already\nreaches the parent recorder.\n\nThe content side ships the engine by name and, only for the new-tab case, a\nbrowserId; the parent resolves both (defaulting to its selected browser), bumps\nthe browser.search.totalSearches / widget.lastUsed prefs, fires the ASRouter\nonSearch trigger, and records the search telemetry.\n\nBehavior-neutral on the direct path. Exercised on both transports with the\nurlbar telemetry/search-mode and ASRouter onSearch tests.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312150\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs"], "git_node": "a5cddd5f8e3454adddc72220c989b6b12b0c2909", "git_parents": ["8cf065ba3dfb53cad5be57f0f51816e1912dfb75"], "node": "127a1f35265c56623a4f479693c9c4fa111bb8e2", "parents": ["3262777ad01a8fe7f418e242c3559dbe5e29c8a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1624579 - Focus the deferred-Enter load's browser in the parent controller. r=mak\n\nOn Enter keyup after a deferred load, the urlbar inputs focused the loaded\n\u003cbrowser\u003e directly and compared it against gBrowser.selectedBrowser --\nchrome-window reaches a content-process urlbar can't make.\n\nRoute it over the controller seam like the load itself: loadURL now returns\nthe id of the browser it loaded into, the child hands that id to the key up\nhandler through the _keyDownEnterDeferred promise, and a new\nUrlbarChildController.focusBrowser forwards to the parent, which focuses the\nbrowser only if it is still selected and reports back so the child can keep\nthe domain name visible. The direct path runs synchronously; the message\npath round-trips, mirroring LoadURL.\n\nBehavior-neutral for the chrome address bar. Verified with browser_enter.js\nand browser_autocomplete_enter_race.js under the message-passing pref both\noff and on.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312318\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs"], "git_node": "b3dbb3d234f65811517ed20b273b8f0a146027ed", "git_parents": ["a5cddd5f8e3454adddc72220c989b6b12b0c2909"], "node": "ead798fe6446594c80be59bc2ed23a7d355a037e", "parents": ["127a1f35265c56623a4f479693c9c4fa111bb8e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "t-p-white \u003ctowhite@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056840 - Make ContinuousOnboardingFeature a LifecycleAwareFeature. r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nConform to the idiomatic LifecycleAwareFeature/ViewBoundFeatureWrapper pattern.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313697\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/onboarding/continuous/ContinuousOnboardingFeatureTest.kt"], "git_node": "45e90fd46ac25bdb9844fdfada04e4d561deb243", "git_parents": ["b3dbb3d234f65811517ed20b273b8f0a146027ed"], "node": "6ccb0b3374452447959721aa70d872b7f73d8c76", "parents": ["ead798fe6446594c80be59bc2ed23a7d355a037e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051359 - Part 1: Add small size variant to ai-website-chip r=czhou\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312330\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-website-chip/ai-website-chip.stories.mjs"], "git_node": "f96d2801139b095e40748b8c99f387f37d27cf36", "git_parents": ["45e90fd46ac25bdb9844fdfada04e4d561deb243"], "node": "d81d3e34776a07f2d091fea16d3a66bb4a572522", "parents": ["6ccb0b3374452447959721aa70d872b7f73d8c76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051359 - Part 2: Support custom child items in smartwindow-panel-list r=czhou\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312331\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.mjs"], "git_node": "9fa2532b38cd325f2015e2ab45fc1def9d0f0da9", "git_parents": ["f96d2801139b095e40748b8c99f387f37d27cf36"], "node": "9c6c5a89c5de01fa69eb4db81feb2f2f128cf4f6", "parents": ["d81d3e34776a07f2d091fea16d3a66bb4a572522"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Zia \u003cfzia@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051359 - Part 3: Add citation component for assistant chat messages r=fluent-reviewers,czhou,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312332\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/chat-assistant-citations/chat-assistant-citations.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindowContent.ftl"], "git_node": "60533c0bf2859abc4861541357c247969031c76a", "git_parents": ["9fa2532b38cd325f2015e2ab45fc1def9d0f0da9"], "node": "8e40d12c576d957098a6ea6b323896802ad11116", "parents": ["9c6c5a89c5de01fa69eb4db81feb2f2f128cf4f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Naz\u0131m Can Alt\u0131nova \u003ccanaltinova@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044695 - Scope PerfSpewer's gecko-profiler recording to the per-compile runtime r=denispal\n\nThe gecko profiler's compile-time line/column recording was gated by a\nprocess-wide flag that every JSRuntime toggled through\n`GeckoProfilerRuntime::enable()`. When one runtime disabled the profiler\n(for example, a worker terminating mid-profile) it cleared the flag for\nthe whole process, so baseline code compiled elsewhere in that window\nended up with an empty `BaselineEntry::sourceInfo_`, and samples into it\nresolved to line 0 for the rest of the profile.\n\nPerfSpewer really has two independent consumers: jitdump/ETW output,\nwhich is genuinely process-wide (PerfMode), and sourceInfo_, which\nbelongs to the runtime being compiled. Instead of sharing one flag,\nPerfSpewer now snapshots the compiling runtime's profiler state at\nstartRecording and gates the gecko path on that, while\nPerfEnabled()/PerfSrcEnabled() go back to meaning only PerfMode. A\nworker disabling the profiler now only affects its own runtime.\n\nIC stubs, the Baseline interpreter, and wasm aren't tied to a runtime\nhere, so they no longer record source data in gecko-only sessions --\nnone of them fed the gecko profiler anyway.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310380\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIRGraph.cpp", "js/src/jit/PerfSpewer.cpp", "js/src/jit/PerfSpewer.h", "js/src/vm/GeckoProfiler.cpp"], "git_node": "31b42478aa299119bcebf047d5975cd5bd70f40b", "git_parents": ["60533c0bf2859abc4861541357c247969031c76a"], "node": "c734c2d2c8e2e9a80f90ee6b5a709f14009a345a", "parents": ["8e40d12c576d957098a6ea6b323896802ad11116"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056264 - Bug 2056264 - Apply proper Nova styling to moz-select's selected option r=desktop-theme-reviewers,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313968\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/widgets/moz-select/moz-select.css"], "git_node": "b973f67fc90788fc41a4af817a57b59adaf8551a", "git_parents": ["31b42478aa299119bcebf047d5975cd5bd70f40b"], "node": "8a47cdafc2f07ced44c97e57cb0d80d67790ab8b", "parents": ["c734c2d2c8e2e9a80f90ee6b5a709f14009a345a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert (Bug 2035575, Bug 2035579) for causing BR bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 2b0d3ea91668ce93f75ee7014bcbfc16b8bfe3d0.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2035579 - Wire rusttests through the build system to link in-tree native libraries r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit dbc812d13920733b2e2f95e6e920cc28e7541759.\n", "files": ["config/baseconfig.mk", "config/makefiles/rust.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "third_party/application-services/moz.yaml", "third_party/application-services/proguard-rules-consumer-jna.pro"], "git_node": "5f9b667c6b95b2faf3404dede7ad31a9bf088666", "git_parents": ["b973f67fc90788fc41a4af817a57b59adaf8551a"], "node": "6a6a7e2a62f1e669d9225415492f8f4ba5948a94", "parents": ["8a47cdafc2f07ced44c97e57cb0d80d67790ab8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055233 - Don't stop the InitMacApplication() runloop until first idle. r=Logan\n\nBefore the SDK update, macOS did the openURLs calls sync, before\napplicationDidFinishLaunching, so applicationDidFinishLaunching was a\nnice place to stop the app again.\n\nHowever those calls are just posted to the event loop, so this mechanism\nwas not working at all.\n\nBug 2036237 fixed the opening of these urls so that they went through\nthe remote service instead of getting dropped, but that still races with\nsession restore, which looks at whether the command line was empty for\nexample.\n\nThis is the lower risk fix, which fixes this mechanism to wait for those\nevents. In order to do that without arbitrary timeouts, we just wait for\nthe event loop to idle.\n\nThere's a (maybe better) long term fix, which is removing this startup\nurl mechanism stuff altogether, handle all the openURLs method in the\nremote service, and ensure session restore doesn't mess with them.\n\nBut that seems more annoying and risky, and this doesn't feel too\nterrible? And it seems we might need the eager initialization anyways\nfor accessibility, so...\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313704\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/MacApplicationDelegate.h", "toolkit/xre/MacApplicationDelegate.mm", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp"], "git_node": "aa48e8bd99bbd730c075215ad7c7afd04bd05bf3", "git_parents": ["5f9b667c6b95b2faf3404dede7ad31a9bf088666"], "node": "8bf265da09cd248228a3b68c60771726e2a2c735", "parents": ["6a6a7e2a62f1e669d9225415492f8f4ba5948a94"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056266 - Provide interfaces to variation data in skrifa fonts. r=AlaskanEmily,layout-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313275\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "gfx/fontations_glue/Cargo.toml", "gfx/fontations_glue/lib.rs"], "git_node": "d7362097f068fb1fc505a5854c837098664b8ec3", "git_parents": ["aa48e8bd99bbd730c075215ad7c7afd04bd05bf3"], "node": "05e12c78f052219562d93f620ae2e024c18ab53f", "parents": ["8bf265da09cd248228a3b68c60771726e2a2c735"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056256 - Add function to access font-wide metrics from a skrifa font. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313276\n", "files": ["gfx/fontations_glue/lib.rs"], "git_node": "e0d8a52fc9d422f539ab6f072bbbfafa09b08815", "git_parents": ["d7362097f068fb1fc505a5854c837098664b8ec3"], "node": "cd5bd43f237321ceb01c54d6b9f4b5437e690570", "parents": ["05e12c78f052219562d93f620ae2e024c18ab53f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049374 - Skip Vulkan AV1 decode with libavcodec 60. r=stransky\n\nlibavcodec 60 only understands VK_MESA_video_decode_av1, not\nVK_KHR_video_decode_av1. Return NOT_AVAILABLE so InitHWDecoderIfAllowed\nfalls through to VA-API instead of a false-positive Vulkan init.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313981\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp"], "git_node": "e39bfd8f2729c99e23643dce6f77fdc783b8cd24", "git_parents": ["e0d8a52fc9d422f539ab6f072bbbfafa09b08815"], "node": "7914e5bfd5e4081ccd8387d9d6ec4a4fcd9301f0", "parents": ["cd5bd43f237321ceb01c54d6b9f4b5437e690570"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053759 - Make it possible import UrlbarPrefs into non-chrome content. r=dao,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312735\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentPrefs.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarQueryContext.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarTelemetryUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/jar.mn", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "9eaa749a1e5145e8c53f233d4a1601cf4e2159b0", "git_parents": ["e39bfd8f2729c99e23643dce6f77fdc783b8cd24"], "node": "c5f7b1cac09eae93b7c8090cec5a416570c225a4", "parents": ["7914e5bfd5e4081ccd8387d9d6ec4a4fcd9301f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053759 - Use UrlbarContentPrefs in new functions in UrlbarChildController. r=dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313985\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs"], "git_node": "957a181c75272fea4c036d0c7666b58622cd862d", "git_parents": ["9eaa749a1e5145e8c53f233d4a1601cf4e2159b0"], "node": "1b2979c27f0befc0cbb2d78f35b4d2dc5e9e0c11", "parents": ["c5f7b1cac09eae93b7c8090cec5a416570c225a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057429 - Fix pullToRefreshPreferenceTest UI test r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI test was failing because it didn't scroll to the end of the \"Customize\" settings sub menu, and couldn't click the pull to refresh toggle.\n\nAdded a change to the way we do the scrolling, namely now we scroll to the end of the sub menu.\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 15x on Firebase using the main branch \u2705\nThe UI test successfully passed 15x on Firebase using the beta branch \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313943\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/robots/SettingsSubMenuCustomizeRobot.kt"], "git_node": "edfcb6b4bd6b8e14a4873c891b5c933b210dcc0d", "git_parents": ["957a181c75272fea4c036d0c7666b58622cd862d"], "node": "8951429cfc0dad5cdd59ae863ea37f951d5904dd", "parents": ["1b2979c27f0befc0cbb2d78f35b4d2dc5e9e0c11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044275 - Sort all UA rules in the same batch. r=keithamus\n\nThis is more consistent and allows specificity and rule source order to\nwork as intended.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307133\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/rule_collector.rs"], "git_node": "8e52451d956b7c3872ea67e7c3a067802ec31ce5", "git_parents": ["edfcb6b4bd6b8e14a4873c891b5c933b210dcc0d"], "node": "98246339b79d441b05f6db0b4f31d5588c7c5a11", "parents": ["8951429cfc0dad5cdd59ae863ea37f951d5904dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2053759 - Use UrlbarContentPrefs in new functions in UrlbarChildController. r=dao\" for causing multiple failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 957a181c75272fea4c036d0c7666b58622cd862d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053759 - Make it possible import UrlbarPrefs into non-chrome content. r=dao,urlbar-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9eaa749a1e5145e8c53f233d4a1601cf4e2159b0.\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarContentPrefs.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarQueryContext.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarTelemetryUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/jar.mn", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.modules.d.ts", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "8b7ecaf101f7b2136ef13d222343e103b0299814", "git_parents": ["8e52451d956b7c3872ea67e7c3a067802ec31ce5"], "node": "83bb1aee9bb1b6c61551161e222807951f460b19", "parents": ["98246339b79d441b05f6db0b4f31d5588c7c5a11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for test tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThis was meant to have happened in bug 1888131.  Better late than never.\n\nKeep using system python on android-hw though, as the scripts we run\nthere rely on it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312746\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/misc.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/xpcshell.yml"], "git_node": "48567aff7b6152b43dcd85c2fbbca7510b79ae4d", "git_parents": ["8b7ecaf101f7b2136ef13d222343e103b0299814"], "node": "0bc83ed42421aa5f426ebb29b1d025c17ea47ac3", "parents": ["83bb1aee9bb1b6c61551161e222807951f460b19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for mochitest tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312747\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "81f5fbdb3301101b8957fa8521c388883f7362f1", "git_parents": ["48567aff7b6152b43dcd85c2fbbca7510b79ae4d"], "node": "e977176f6a07c08f24720f5294e2e0f46ff4f191", "parents": ["0bc83ed42421aa5f426ebb29b1d025c17ea47ac3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for reftest tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312748\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/reftest/kind.yml"], "git_node": "7721791d09f0455b9de5504ad1f0d7dda970ea10", "git_parents": ["81f5fbdb3301101b8957fa8521c388883f7362f1"], "node": "8ccbd292653478d4ba2ea371e7c9d0b0a951a0e8", "parents": ["e977176f6a07c08f24720f5294e2e0f46ff4f191"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for web-platform-tests tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312749\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/web-platform-tests/kind.yml"], "git_node": "5106e9fe3aae0df7e31d87b27be7a5873a403fed", "git_parents": ["7721791d09f0455b9de5504ad1f0d7dda970ea10"], "node": "1b2d6671c2abbeeaf584058859e2d4c75d15e2c2", "parents": ["8ccbd292653478d4ba2ea371e7c9d0b0a951a0e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055820. Don't quantize f16 to u8 before the qcms tetrahedral CLUT. r=jrmuizel\n\nThe tetrahedral CLUT interpolation (which works in f32) was duplicated: it lived\nin tetra() for the CMYK path and was hand-inlined again in the RGB template path.\nFactor it out into a single tetra_interp() that both call.\n\ntetra_interp is #[inline(always)] on purpose: as an ordinary function it adds a\nper-pixel call that regresses the u8 CLUT path ~14% (measured via disassembly, a\nstandalone microbench, and a gtest); forcing the inline keeps the original\ncodegen. A nice side benefit of routing CMYK through it is that the C/M/Y grid\ncoordinates are now computed once instead of once per K-slice.\n\nWith the shared function in place, the f16 (HDR) path uses it directly: it now\ngoes f16 -\u003e f32 -\u003e u8 through the CLUT instead of the old f16 -\u003e u8 -\u003e f32 -\u003e u8,\nwhich quantized to 8 bits before color management and caused banding.\n\nAlso add a CLUT perf gtest (GfxQcmsPerf_Clut, using the A2B0-only\ndisplaycal-lut-stripped.icc); the qcms perf tests previously only covered the\nmatrix-shaper path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312705\n", "files": ["gfx/qcms/src/transform.rs", "gfx/tests/gtest/TestQcms.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "75cf81c81496713701c84e93d361ffe38ef571cc", "git_parents": ["5106e9fe3aae0df7e31d87b27be7a5873a403fed"], "node": "7dd466724a80ce7ee8ea987cdad4e75d4c7323d5", "parents": ["1b2d6671c2abbeeaf584058859e2d4c75d15e2c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053485 - Remove unicode-bidi: plaintext special-case. r=jfkthame,layout-reviewers\n\nIt was decided that the right way to fix this is using dir=auto. This\nseems green on try, so needs a wpt test at least. I know it used to\ncause some front-end issues in the urlbar but doesn't seem to be the\ncase anymore...\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311698\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "5d10653c61fb83dce37d916f201ff0123cd8d1c3", "git_parents": ["75cf81c81496713701c84e93d361ffe38ef571cc"], "node": "797a876c12a3aed9e152946985f3972fd3ac0397", "parents": ["7dd466724a80ce7ee8ea987cdad4e75d4c7323d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053485 - Add dir=auto to inputs that used to get this special treatment. r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313240\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "devtools/client/framework/components/DebugTargetInfo.js", "devtools/client/framework/test/node/components/__snapshots__/debug-target-info.test.js.snap", "devtools/client/webconsole/components/Input/ReverseSearchInput.js"], "git_node": "8d926b48dcee5afee3d3fdca59eee19e6d7f573c", "git_parents": ["5d10653c61fb83dce37d916f201ff0123cd8d1c3"], "node": "8e20b43fe86d1ed9e2f3878e5096613c7e483f07", "parents": ["797a876c12a3aed9e152946985f3972fd3ac0397"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053485 - Add a WPT for this behavior change. r=layout-reviewers,TYLin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313260\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/unicode-bidi-plaintext-scroll-direction.html"], "git_node": "7ab910c5e194cf4825e8b3c0efa200a305bd3f3e", "git_parents": ["8d926b48dcee5afee3d3fdca59eee19e6d7f573c"], "node": "08e9329e791434cbbf3eb239d88f2dd8d37a4b14", "parents": ["8e20b43fe86d1ed9e2f3878e5096613c7e483f07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055206 - Part 1: Do not attempt to refresh while in background r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313027\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPLifecycleHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js"], "git_node": "1339415bffa1c4135db0864dfe47daa674f611bb", "git_parents": ["7ab910c5e194cf4825e8b3c0efa200a305bd3f3e"], "node": "bd3e79f7447ee129658f8aacbe135f2748f607b8", "parents": ["08e9329e791434cbbf3eb239d88f2dd8d37a4b14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055206 - Part 2: Add individual timouts per fetch r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313028\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "0192f3a5a910754c78b1353ac9ef18ade15e83cc", "git_parents": ["1339415bffa1c4135db0864dfe47daa674f611bb"], "node": "f2b7efdf53f8a0159781798b5ca32cacd599785b", "parents": ["bd3e79f7447ee129658f8aacbe135f2748f607b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Streich \u003csstreich@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055206 - Part 3: A forced rotation should reset the Proxy-Manager timer r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313029\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js"], "git_node": "1933c839b1bcb97219a7b91d47394c56e55e0feb", "git_parents": ["0192f3a5a910754c78b1353ac9ef18ade15e83cc"], "node": "4abf1e09da2c657af4796e4b336889943373eccc", "parents": ["f2b7efdf53f8a0159781798b5ca32cacd599785b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055006 - Add IMEStyle to RFPTargetsDefault. r=masayuki,timhuang\n\nDisable custom IME styling for EditContext textformatupdate events if\n\"Suspected fingerprinters\" are blocked. By default this is only enabled\nin PBM; with strict ETP it is enabled in all windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312100\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/test_editcontext_resist_fingerprinting.html", "toolkit/components/resistfingerprinting/RFPTargetsDefault.inc"], "git_node": "62b6db05224263db18280e3a6e16b0c444393e5d", "git_parents": ["1933c839b1bcb97219a7b91d47394c56e55e0feb"], "node": "a5cc58e2614dec316668eb4923a17d907b841aec", "parents": ["4abf1e09da2c657af4796e4b336889943373eccc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056928 - Make legacy disabling pref work with new settings. r=mstriemer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313517\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_disable_buttons.js", "browser/components/preferences/config/about-firefox.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/downloads.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/passwords-autofill.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/privacy.mjs"], "git_node": "9970c0c6a28394197875ffb3d263cfd05551e02a", "git_parents": ["62b6db05224263db18280e3a6e16b0c444393e5d"], "node": "96c345bde7cff1697e9ad511c2a2e8d0280bf0a9", "parents": ["a5cc58e2614dec316668eb4923a17d907b841aec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056610 - Clean up a bit the select picker rules. r=keithamus\n\n* Move the listbox pseudos after the main listbox rule. We could\n   consider to use nesting nowadays...\n\n * Don't inherit background on something that's display: contents.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313989\n", "files": ["layout/style/res/forms.css"], "git_node": "e093941a5c7f5e618eb735546a2d5f8279aebf0a", "git_parents": ["9970c0c6a28394197875ffb3d263cfd05551e02a"], "node": "aa6bab4f0bc62372bb8cc29b6620249c4287c3cd", "parents": ["96c345bde7cff1697e9ad511c2a2e8d0280bf0a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056610 - Clean up some dead nsListControlFrame code. r=keithamus\n\nShould probably have been done in bug 2047603 or so.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313990\n", "files": ["layout/forms/nsListControlFrame.cpp", "layout/forms/nsListControlFrame.h"], "git_node": "63b8f4ddab42e4de647ae9df04ce7a141bb6ba17", "git_parents": ["e093941a5c7f5e618eb735546a2d5f8279aebf0a"], "node": "fa1eb404a8c1386432c6b436d966190884db05b5", "parents": ["aa6bab4f0bc62372bb8cc29b6620249c4287c3cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julien Cristau \u003cjcristau@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054116 - add a slack notification to desktop and android release mark-as-shipped. r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313976\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/release-mark-as-shipped/kind.yml"], "git_node": "0901632f59c1c2a9d5dbe7d34cfe1f89b01c38aa", "git_parents": ["63b8f4ddab42e4de647ae9df04ce7a141bb6ba17"], "node": "5d701c4ce7cab9d75146a07598dd19b14acfbaa9", "parents": ["fa1eb404a8c1386432c6b436d966190884db05b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033838 - [ci] Implement ability to clone from Git in Hg graphs, r=taskgraph-reviewers,hneiva\n\nAs part of the GeckoCI to Github migration, we are going to start making\ntasks clone from a corresponding push in Github rather than\nhg.mozilla.org.\n\nThis results in an identical Taskgraph diff.\n\nCo-authored-by: Heitor Neiva \u003chneiva@mozilla.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313503\n", "files": ["taskcluster/android_taskgraph/job.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/python.toml", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/test/test_transforms_job_common.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/common.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/hazard.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mach.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mozharness.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/mozharness_test.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/python_test.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/run_task.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/spidermonkey.py", "taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/job/toolchain.py"], "git_node": "da9c3ec76ae04b50939e82292150a5946119cbea", "git_parents": ["0901632f59c1c2a9d5dbe7d34cfe1f89b01c38aa"], "node": "b7c7e9be911cb7fb23eaa8df8c7059c1e0a0aba8", "parents": ["5d701c4ce7cab9d75146a07598dd19b14acfbaa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sarah Clements \u003csclements@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047224 - Sidebar & firefoxview image and string updates r=desktop-theme-reviewers,fxview-reviewers,kcochrane,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\n* Update assets for history empty state and synced tabs empty state and error states for sidebar and fxview\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312975\n", "files": ["browser/components/firefoxview/SyncedTabsController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/chats.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/firefox-view-synced-tabs-error-handler.sys.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/firefoxview.css", "browser/components/firefoxview/fxview-empty-state.css", "browser/components/firefoxview/helpers.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/history.mjs", "browser/components/firefoxview/recentlyclosed.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-history.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-panel-header.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/firefoxView.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-page-history.svg", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-tabs-devices-error.svg", "browser/themes/shared/sidebar/kit-tabs-devices.svg"], "git_node": "340cb855d6aadba359f9f2ceee1a4bf8e4657913", "git_parents": ["da9c3ec76ae04b50939e82292150a5946119cbea"], "node": "6ad3425b047c512b252e651bc0571c0f94cae892", "parents": ["b7c7e9be911cb7fb23eaa8df8c7059c1e0a0aba8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Federico Cucinotta \u003cgithub@fedec.online\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1418178 - Allow configuring the number of Ctrl-Tab previews with a pref. r=emilio,desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,dao\n\nAdd a hidden pref, browser.ctrlTab.maxPreviews (default 7, clamped to\n[4, 49]), controlling how many tab previews the ctrl-tab panel shows.\nPreviews wrap into rows of at most 7, as suggested in the earlier\nreview of D194909, and the preview buttons are rebuilt when the pref\nchanges. The XUL flex attribute is removed from the preview buttons\nbecause its flex-basis of 0 prevents flex wrapping; the equivalent\nflex styling with a content-based basis is applied in CSS instead.\n\nWrapped rows use a row-gap that offsets the pre-existing -10px\nmargin-top on .ctrlTab-preview-inner. Without it, a second row of\npreviews sat only a subpixel distance below the first, which rounded to\na 1px overlap on Windows and backed out an earlier version of this\npatch (browser_ctrlTab.js test_maxPreviews_pref).\n\nThis supersedes D194909, which its author invited commandeering of in\nbug 1418178 comment 33.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306290\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/browser-ctrlTab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_ctrlTab.js", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/ctrlTab.css"], "git_node": "0ae401a2dae6d893ae3cf1fc439fa457a57b63b6", "git_parents": ["340cb855d6aadba359f9f2ceee1a4bf8e4657913"], "node": "a96ea433642fcb2c2e98dcde091a60a03aebd3ee", "parents": ["6ad3425b047c512b252e651bc0571c0f94cae892"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055206 - Part 3: A forced rotation should reset the Proxy-Manager timer r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\" for causing xpc failures @test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js.\n\nThis reverts commit 1933c839b1bcb97219a7b91d47394c56e55e0feb.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055206 - Part 2: Add individual timouts per fetch r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\"\n\nThis reverts commit 0192f3a5a910754c78b1353ac9ef18ade15e83cc.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2055206 - Part 1: Do not attempt to refresh while in background r=ip-protection-reviewers,apopov\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1339415bffa1c4135db0864dfe47daa674f611bb.\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPLifecycleHelper.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/IPPProxyManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPPLifecycleHelper.js", "toolkit/components/ipprotection/tests/xpcshell/test_IPProxyManager.js"], "git_node": "dacd18953ae7744c9c100ae78bcb7d642a8fe5f1", "git_parents": ["0ae401a2dae6d893ae3cf1fc439fa457a57b63b6"], "node": "6ecde5a8ec896365d2264634995b782f7a296591", "parents": ["a96ea433642fcb2c2e98dcde091a60a03aebd3ee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055837 - use taskcluster-built python for test tasks. r=taskgraph-reviewers,bhearsum\" for causing gtest failures @ DesktopLauncherDownloaderTest\n\nThis reverts commit 48567aff7b6152b43dcd85c2fbbca7510b79ae4d.\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/test/kind.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/misc.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/test/xpcshell.yml"], "git_node": "9e4075982f41a99b48258ede097ba04b7b5e504b", "git_parents": ["dacd18953ae7744c9c100ae78bcb7d642a8fe5f1"], "node": "353a7b6c43a8d7b37635af941ae4c0ae8701813e", "parents": ["6ecde5a8ec896365d2264634995b782f7a296591"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056610 - Restore :not() selector for now, with a comment.\n\nTurns out this is green in main but not with\nhttps://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307133 which landed right\nbefore the previous patches. See the comment.\n", "files": ["layout/style/res/forms.css"], "git_node": "ae6e73297cd99dab7a92ab4db0324e5aca0c7832", "git_parents": ["9e4075982f41a99b48258ede097ba04b7b5e504b"], "node": "7c8a13628c7c6e00f64799aadffd86ed769a5bcf", "parents": ["353a7b6c43a8d7b37635af941ae4c0ae8701813e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031045: pre: add bz2 support to marannon r=releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThis is needed to test post-watershed versions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297798\n", "files": ["tools/update-verify/marannon/Cargo.lock", "tools/update-verify/marannon/Cargo.toml", "tools/update-verify/marannon/src/main.rs", "tools/update-verify/marannon/src/updater.rs"], "git_node": "9dde8c2458140500c1a0230eba044537e52034f3", "git_parents": ["ae6e73297cd99dab7a92ab4db0324e5aca0c7832"], "node": "f32f8fb020c2cfe4bba4526732f5bcb00dc07561", "parents": ["7c8a13628c7c6e00f64799aadffd86ed769a5bcf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031045: pre: add getNightlyDir helper function r=releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThis is needed to support the goal of running update integrity tests on an older release, and makes a good companion to the release versions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297799\n", "files": ["python/mozrelease/mozrelease/paths.py"], "git_node": "c5ed8b60ab810feb947c7ea9beec33b3ae0be7cf", "git_parents": ["9dde8c2458140500c1a0230eba044537e52034f3"], "node": "31d0595ac4abb3667750f848e0e4076b4e883929", "parents": ["f32f8fb020c2cfe4bba4526732f5bcb00dc07561"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031045: pre: add build platform -\u003e ftp platform mapping r=releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThese build platforms are *so* close to being the same as ftp ones, but alas, they are just different enough to need this.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297800\n", "files": ["python/mozrelease/mozrelease/platforms.py"], "git_node": "79d0e2695b4f42c64416cb63a90e1fad2c19653d", "git_parents": ["c5ed8b60ab810feb947c7ea9beec33b3ae0be7cf"], "node": "526264afe8458680153f4e98a94a17ddcebcb6f7", "parents": ["31d0595ac4abb3667750f848e0e4076b4e883929"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031045: run update integrity tests on one older release per platform r=releng-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,jcristau\n\nThis adds an additional `--from` test for each update integrity task. For releases, this is the first post-watershed release for each platform. For nightly this is something a little bit after that, for reasons explained in the comments. Try is slightly different as well.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D297801\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/update_integrity.py", "taskcluster/kinds/test-update-integrity/kind.yml"], "git_node": "d81f6096e62621dcb462322ce7cdd86e2af6e827", "git_parents": ["79d0e2695b4f42c64416cb63a90e1fad2c19653d"], "node": "b3f60c2e18708a6b4129089dcaa276796fa58cc2", "parents": ["526264afe8458680153f4e98a94a17ddcebcb6f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "lottiehope \u003clottie_hope@hotmail.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039171 - Support share text and subject in the native share sheet r=android-reviewers,rebecatudor273\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313975\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/share/ShareSheetLauncher.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/ShareUseCases.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessor.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/ShareSheetLauncherTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/ShareUseCasesTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/fake/FakeShareSheetLauncher.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/intent/HomeDeepLinkIntentProcessorTest.kt"], "git_node": "6dc242dfe85f816e03c9ed7c9db80efe46f17237", "git_parents": ["d81f6096e62621dcb462322ce7cdd86e2af6e827"], "node": "c947cee15a029f3596996a900a0684e62f3dd6a8", "parents": ["b3f60c2e18708a6b4129089dcaa276796fa58cc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Arnaud Bienner \u003cabienner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053492 - Add telemetry for quota usage drifts and underflow in OriginInfo's constructor and LockedUsage. r=janv\n\nThis will help to know how many bad values remain sticky once underflow occured.\nThis will also allow to find drifts between usage counters (which don't always end up with underflows)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313994\n", "files": ["dom/quota/OriginInfo.cpp", "dom/quota/OriginInfo.h"], "git_node": "f44c8b1f8c743fa645f7c1a016016c32617da6be", "git_parents": ["6dc242dfe85f816e03c9ed7c9db80efe46f17237"], "node": "7efcb3e6ec3ce0748b63866dab425dd72729304f", "parents": ["c947cee15a029f3596996a900a0684e62f3dd6a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulio Berra \u003cgiulio@freedom.press\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048884 - Fix webRequest frameId for worker-initiated requests. r=robwu,dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\n\nwebRequest events for requests initiated from a worker reported frameId\n0. importScripts() and module imports from a dedicated worker were not\nattributed to the frame that owns the worker.\n\nTwo changes:\n - ChannelFromScriptURL now propagates the worker's associated\n   BrowsingContext onto worker script channels, so a dedicated worker's\n   requests are attributed to its owning frame.\n - NormalizeFrameID now returns -1 (instead of 0) when the request is\n   not associated with any BrowsingContext.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311304\n", "files": ["dom/chrome-webidl/ChannelWrapper.webidl", "dom/workers/ScriptLoader.cpp", "netwerk/base/nsILoadInfo.idl", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/file_worker_importscripts.html", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/file_worker_importscripts_frame.html", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/mochitest-common.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_webrequest_worker.html", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_webrequest_worker_importscripts.html", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/worker_importscripts.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ChannelWrapper.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/webrequest/ChannelWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "d2dd144bf1e460582b7fe3d2847125787f0ed524", "git_parents": ["f44c8b1f8c743fa645f7c1a016016c32617da6be"], "node": "37b3f738a9bd8487e34b1f02e874b8711fe915a7", "parents": ["7efcb3e6ec3ce0748b63866dab425dd72729304f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040603 - part 1: Show assembler offsets in IONFLAGS=codegen output for arm32.  r=nbp.\n\nFor IONFLAGS=codegen, on arm32, best-effort printing of assembler buffer\noffsets is now done, with the format (as per other architectures) \"%06x \".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D301273\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/arm/Assembler-arm.cpp", "js/src/jit/arm/Assembler-arm.h", "js/src/jit/arm/disasm/Disasm-arm.cpp"], "git_node": "329d6f4d364e86e5dbca7fce5b7d32fc582b5bda", "git_parents": ["d2dd144bf1e460582b7fe3d2847125787f0ed524"], "node": "b80f86505ce5e6e015b63ba14a6f488029b4a389", "parents": ["37b3f738a9bd8487e34b1f02e874b8711fe915a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056301 - Add New Tab customize panel browser theme strings r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313090\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "031d3978f5a1a6311dfe873f0d27451ebc69428d", "git_parents": ["329d6f4d364e86e5dbca7fce5b7d32fc582b5bda"], "node": "5c274d9805b1e28daa0665c91e07eb217d5e722e", "parents": ["b80f86505ce5e6e015b63ba14a6f488029b4a389"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056300 - Integrate the compact theme-picker into the New Tab customize panel r=Dre\n\nEmbed the reusable toolkit `theme-picker` element (compact layout) in the New Tab customize panel so users can switch their Firefox theme directly from Firefox Home.\n\n- Render `\u003ctheme-picker layout=\"compact\" installsource=\"about:newtab\"\u003e` in ContentSection, gated on the browser-wide `browser.nova.enabled` pref. PrefsFeed reads and observes that pref and broadcasts it to content as `browserNovaEnabled`; CustomizeMenu threads it through to ContentSection.\n- Register the ThemePicker JSWindowActor for `about:newtab` and `about:home` so the element's remote controller can reach AddonManager/ThemesList via the parent in the content sandbox (about:home covers the startup-cache first tab).\n- Load the theme-picker / moz-visual-picker / moz-segmented-control element modules in the live-rendered page (render-activity-stream-html.js) and the about:home startup-cache template (page.html.template) so the custom element is defined on both normal and cached pages.\n- Add tests for the gate (ContentSection) and the pref observer/broadcast (PrefsFeed).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313091\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ContentSection/ContentSection.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/CustomizeMenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/_CustomizeMenu.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/css/activity-stream.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/css/nova/activity-stream.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ContentSection.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/CustomizeMenu.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/lib/PrefsFeed.test.js"], "git_node": "be9e02019a852000566bc87b17bc3cb6525d26e6", "git_parents": ["031d3978f5a1a6311dfe873f0d27451ebc69428d"], "node": "503206ab0dba7d5a15025e4d5a96f7310a91d945", "parents": ["5c274d9805b1e28daa0665c91e07eb217d5e722e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056304 - Add the full browser theme selection panel to the New Tab customize panel r=Dre\n\nWire the existing \"See more themes\" button in the customize panel's Appearance section to a new full theme selection sub-panel.\n\n- New ThemesManagementPanel (mirrors WidgetsManagementPanel): the box-button opens a sliding sub-panel with a back button (\"Firefox Themes\" title), the full-layout theme-picker (Light/Dark/Device chooser + all themes), and a moz-box-link out to the about:addons themes list.\n- Panel visibility state (showThemesPanel / toggleThemesPanel) lives in Base and is threaded through CustomizeMenu to ContentSection.\n- OPEN_ABOUT_ADDONS_THEMES action + AboutPreferences handler open addons://list/theme via BrowserAddonUI.openAddonsMgr.\n- Load the moz-box-link element module in the prerendered and startup-cache HTML; reuse the mgmt-panel slide styles for .themes-mgmt-panel.\n- Tests for the panel and appearance section; Karma coverage override for the Jest-tested panel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313092\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/Actions.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ContentSection/ContentSection.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/CustomizeMenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ThemesManagementPanel/ThemesManagementPanel.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/_CustomizeMenu.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/css/activity-stream.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/css/nova/activity-stream.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/karma.mc.config.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ContentSection.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/ThemesManagementPanel.test.jsx"], "git_node": "8497057983d0dee5bed4655ee750207500a6e459", "git_parents": ["be9e02019a852000566bc87b17bc3cb6525d26e6"], "node": "f028a7975d26e04eca28825edda85e5af47ed752", "parents": ["503206ab0dba7d5a15025e4d5a96f7310a91d945"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056040 - Crop the homepage tab thumbnail to only include the homepage content r=android-reviewers,adhingra\n\n- Capture the bounds of the homepage content in order to crop the thumbnail screenshot to those bounds so the tabs tray shows only the homepage content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313521\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/HomepageThumbnailIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt"], "git_node": "88d4d4a6d59dbb70a683d2cc0aea639723d2266f", "git_parents": ["8497057983d0dee5bed4655ee750207500a6e459"], "node": "03d94eb485d823b125453d409fd3ce7389a15e23", "parents": ["f028a7975d26e04eca28825edda85e5af47ed752"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emily McMinn \u003cemcminn@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051707 - Add a redirector component and a test message for about:referrals r=omc-reviewers,jhirsch,sachung\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311654\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutDialog_referrals.js", "browser/components/about/AboutRedirector.cpp", "browser/components/about/components.conf", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/PanelTestProvider.sys.mjs", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_aboutURLs.js", "browser/components/originattributes/test/browser/browser_firstPartyIsolation_aboutPages.js", "browser/components/referrals/tests/browser/browser_referralsAppMenu.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas.json", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/index.md", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser_sma_get_referral_code.js"], "git_node": "050513563241a754e83568cca3a8923058fd8a25", "git_parents": ["88d4d4a6d59dbb70a683d2cc0aea639723d2266f"], "node": "d682ccab121d8b872bd18a5989609eda554692b3", "parents": ["03d94eb485d823b125453d409fd3ce7389a15e23"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049782 - Add nsIAlertCallbacks to replace nsIObserver for Alerts Service r=nrishel,win-reviewers\n\nHaving this new interface should allow us to introduce more observer topics without fears on internal backwards compatibility.\n\nExisting callers can still use nsIObservers with the same behavior, while ideally we should slowly move them to this new approach.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308321\n", "files": ["dom/notification/NotificationParent.cpp", "dom/notification/NotificationUtils.cpp", "dom/notification/NotificationUtils.h", "toolkit/components/alerts/alert.js", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsAlertsService.cpp", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsIAlertsService.idl", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsXULAlerts.cpp", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsXULAlerts.h", "toolkit/components/alerts/test/chrome/chrome.toml", "toolkit/components/alerts/test/chrome/test_alerts_callbacks.html", "toolkit/system/gnome/nsAlertsIconListener.cpp", "toolkit/system/gnome/nsAlertsIconListener.h", "toolkit/system/gnome/nsSystemAlertsService.cpp", "widget/cocoa/MacOSNotificationCenter.mm", "widget/windows/ToastNotification.cpp", "widget/windows/ToastNotificationHandler.cpp", "widget/windows/ToastNotificationHandler.h"], "git_node": "31ffaa6370f203b2cf59f7eaaef19ba2b583a5d7", "git_parents": ["050513563241a754e83568cca3a8923058fd8a25"], "node": "1a2b8336498a55c2b6561b550a73fd89dc01d093", "parents": ["d682ccab121d8b872bd18a5989609eda554692b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049782 - Fall back to ShowAlert in AndroidAlerts r=nrishel\n\nUpdating AndroidAlerts is possible, but properly doing so requires GeckoView API change. For now we fall back to ShowAlert with nsIObserver.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312485\n", "files": ["widget/android/AndroidAlerts.cpp"], "git_node": "5bb68c92becfbd5d26647c78164a6e4e8aae7251", "git_parents": ["31ffaa6370f203b2cf59f7eaaef19ba2b583a5d7"], "node": "7bfcfbeccfc2fa0f690ec608976facbce2568bf4", "parents": ["1a2b8336498a55c2b6561b550a73fd89dc01d093"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049782 - Update Alerts Service mocks to use showAlertWithCallbacks r=extension-reviewers,nrishel,robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312486\n", "files": ["dom/notification/test/browser/browser_openwindow_without_window.js", "dom/notification/test/browser/browser_userContextId_openWindow.js", "dom/notification/test/browser/browser_userContextId_tag.js", "dom/notification/test/chrome/test_notification_system_principal.xhtml", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/MockAlertsService.js", "dom/notification/test/mochitest/test_notification_tag.html"], "git_node": "34420480d27ced14f466d93bf4d1079fabe71fc0", "git_parents": ["5bb68c92becfbd5d26647c78164a6e4e8aae7251"], "node": "82ccf39dce5d5fdb20db74af1bdad587a539b2a9", "parents": ["7bfcfbeccfc2fa0f690ec608976facbce2568bf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052574 - Track ignored notifications on Windows r=nrishel,win-reviewers\n\nWith the following code I can confirm that the new dismissed-from-forgeground event works.\n\n```js\nalerts = Cc[\"@mozilla.org/alerts-service;1\"].getService().QueryInterface(Ci.nsIAlertsService)\nalert = Cc[\"@mozilla.org/alert-notification;1\"].createInstance().QueryInterface(Ci.nsIAlertNotification)\nalert.initWithObject({ title: \"foo\", textClickable: true })\nalerts.showAlertWithCallbacks(alert, { onAlertDismissedFromForeground: () =\u003e console.log(\"dismissed-from-foreground\"), onAlertClick: () =\u003e console.log(\"click\"), onAlertFinished: () =\u003e console.log(\"closed\") })\n```\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310399\n", "files": ["dom/notification/NotificationParent.cpp", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsAlertsService.cpp", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsIAlertsService.idl", "toolkit/components/alerts/nsXULAlerts.cpp", "widget/windows/ToastNotificationHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "e29a6acf419201493c7e7bf6b618adb4835d1488", "git_parents": ["34420480d27ced14f466d93bf4d1079fabe71fc0"], "node": "585d4766f485a9f6647e9d306350309dd1f16ca2", "parents": ["82ccf39dce5d5fdb20db74af1bdad587a539b2a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046925 - Refactor NotificationObserver::Observe for clearer behavior for each topic r=asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306258\n", "files": ["dom/notification/NotificationParent.cpp", "dom/notification/NotificationParent.h"], "git_node": "873ba040d7b51dbf4fd957653821c8df4f7717b1", "git_parents": ["e29a6acf419201493c7e7bf6b618adb4835d1488"], "node": "76d33a02b27cb31f25c26bdecfc72550f8846f82", "parents": ["585d4766f485a9f6647e9d306350309dd1f16ca2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kagami Sascha Rosylight \u003ckrosylight@proton.me\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046221 - Part 2: Add telemetry to NotificationParent r=nrishel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D305800\n", "files": ["dom/notification/NotificationParent.cpp", "dom/notification/metrics.yaml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/notifications/resources/MockAlertsService.js", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/notifications/resources/SiteCategory.js", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/notifications/telemetry.sub.https.window.js"], "git_node": "ba85cfd8aba17362fea051a1836687dd313003c9", "git_parents": ["873ba040d7b51dbf4fd957653821c8df4f7717b1"], "node": "d1e1fd811b48ae0f3