as Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057470 - Add a debug option for initializing renderable textures with opaque pink. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313977\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/gui/debug_flags.rs", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "be67d8afb3e615815e5ed6cc24c64a99a9545635", "git_parents": ["457e5a67f09b2e93c6f9ac899df466ebfcef12f6"], "node": "3e49224be1e21c762d5a2aad12525d0e313265a8", "parents": ["82202bf232b0dc2723fc2b02a1099b992b2d514a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057470 - Enable the render target init debugging flag for wrench reftest. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nAlso add an option to enable it for other sub-commands.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313978\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/near-plane-clip.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/args.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/wrench.rs"], "git_node": "96f384b1e975444a52140b139aede8707493ed68", "git_parents": ["be67d8afb3e615815e5ed6cc24c64a99a9545635"], "node": "3f4061095ef119482c207822b36a98abe713aeac", "parents": ["3e49224be1e21c762d5a2aad12525d0e313265a8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Omar Gonzalez \u003cs9tpepper@apache.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054987 - make getting tab list part of getOpenTabs toolcall reusable for Smart Form Fill r=tliu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312195\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/head.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Tools_GetOpenTabs.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Tools_GetTabList.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "3a7232fbe284236ba3588e8b64f0b1aa35c78495", "git_parents": ["96f384b1e975444a52140b139aede8707493ed68"], "node": "2f21a43c0b2e00e36ea1680e386cfaf82a8d6a90", "parents": ["3f4061095ef119482c207822b36a98abe713aeac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kershaw Chang \u003ckershaw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057071 - Extend cors_authorization_header metric, r=necko-reviewers,sunil\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314389\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "e9e7627ba3787cd50355a2ed912f6396d0e00d37", "git_parents": ["3a7232fbe284236ba3588e8b64f0b1aa35c78495"], "node": "a3020847136ccd3726261111a70932807f31e059", "parents": ["2f21a43c0b2e00e36ea1680e386cfaf82a8d6a90"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057595 - Don't re-report the xpcshell harness abort as an unexpected exception. r=ahal\n\nUse a dedicated symbol for the abort the harness throws to unwind after a\nfailure it has already logged, instead of a generic NS_ERROR_ABORT\ndistinguished by the _quit flag. This removes the redundant \"Unexpected\nexception NS_ERROR_ABORT\" report (with stack) that followed an in-task\nassertion failure, and avoids masking a genuine NS_ERROR_ABORT thrown by\ntest code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314031\n", "files": ["testing/xpcshell/head.js", "testing/xpcshell/selftest.py"], "git_node": "9505ce1c580ebd8a394a4d941e21bb8e66c27a96", "git_parents": ["e9e7627ba3787cd50355a2ed912f6396d0e00d37"], "node": "56f259ad933ed55c262f5a49cefad6125fdafee9", "parents": ["a3020847136ccd3726261111a70932807f31e059"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057694 - unconditionally set the certificate transparency pref to enabled r=jschanck\n\nThis unifies the static pref list with what we're actually shipping in\npractice, and removes an early beta reference.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314166\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "f245131db4e7c43059f05961389d04b1a68394a7", "git_parents": ["9505ce1c580ebd8a394a4d941e21bb8e66c27a96"], "node": "883e11c2d1588478b375130629883dfe4b299bc7", "parents": ["56f259ad933ed55c262f5a49cefad6125fdafee9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058244 - Use Gradle's embedded Kotlin version for the build-logic plugin builds. r=ahochheiden\n\nThe conventions build applies kotlin-dsl, which compiles against Gradle's embedded Kotlin, but it was\nalso applying the serialization plugin at the version catalog's Kotlin version. That pulled a newer\nKotlin Gradle Plugin onto the build's classpath, so every configuration phase logged an eight-line\n\"Unsupported Kotlin plugin version\" warning. The apilint and nimbus plugin builds each hardcoded a\nKotlin version that matched neither the catalog nor Gradle's embedded Kotlin, so both had silently\ndrifted.\n\nGradle loads all three of these plugins into its own classloader against its own Kotlin runtime, so\ntracking embeddedKotlinVersion keeps the build logic aligned with what actually loads it, and removes\ntwo versions that have to be updated by hand. Our Android code is unaffected and still compiles with\nthe catalog version.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314466\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/conventions/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/nimbus-gradle-plugin/build.gradle.kts"], "git_node": "4140036a2c6d9807a0cf4294ef903501d7f0bef3", "git_parents": ["f245131db4e7c43059f05961389d04b1a68394a7"], "node": "20cc9fc3e3a04bcef2ddb0844d782ff967b3591e", "parents": ["883e11c2d1588478b375130629883dfe4b299bc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056412: Set RTCSctpTransport.maxChannels r=mjf\n\nAlso, fix a bug that was preventing our dcsctp-based DataChannel\nimplementation from availing itself of the full range of allowed stream\nids (was previously hard-capped at 2048).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313329\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.h", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannel.cpp", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannel.h", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannelDcSctp.cpp", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannelDcSctp.h", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannelUsrsctp.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCSctpTransport-maxChannels.html.ini"], "git_node": "07eda5c95318cc41920c8900bd03f5b133dfee18", "git_parents": ["4140036a2c6d9807a0cf4294ef903501d7f0bef3"], "node": "2632876bffce0c803361ffd817f6e988359c0d7c", "parents": ["20cc9fc3e3a04bcef2ddb0844d782ff967b3591e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2019353: Perform state-checking before comparison against last created description. r=dbaker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314158\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSession.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_setLocalAnswerInHaveLocalOffer.html", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_setLocalAnswerInStable.html", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_setLocalOfferInHaveRemoteOffer.html", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-setLocalDescription-answer.html.ini"], "git_node": "3deb3168f1468fb49a99b5775b688cbffe38ad9c", "git_parents": ["07eda5c95318cc41920c8900bd03f5b133dfee18"], "node": "11cf0f26521103e0081be8c9a0e0e89a9757140b", "parents": ["2632876bffce0c803361ffd817f6e988359c0d7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1814460: Surface RTCError for SCTP failures. r=mjf,webidl,saschanaz,dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\n\n*Lots* of hops involved in plumbing that error through.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312838\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannel.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannel.h", "dom/webidl/RTCError.webidl", "dom/webidl/RTCErrorEvent.webidl", "dom/workers/test/test_worker_interfaces.js", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannel.cpp", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannel.h", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannelDcSctp.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini"], "git_node": "23a9de79fb370ef187a2d8b0cc80f9d6a97c14a5", "git_parents": ["3deb3168f1468fb49a99b5775b688cbffe38ad9c"], "node": "ba21fba7a7fbec24eb4f23081b9c360330c10373", "parents": ["11cf0f26521103e0081be8c9a0e0e89a9757140b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058129 - Move gContainerCreation out of browser.js into its own module r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314349\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-sets.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js.globals", "browser/components/contextualidentity/content/ContainerCreationPanel.mjs", "browser/components/contextualidentity/jar.mn", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js"], "git_node": "0019a858e79ed44fce15d1f554e89df3ea622c18", "git_parents": ["23a9de79fb370ef187a2d8b0cc80f9d6a97c14a5"], "node": "6f802afd64e52ea6d50bdb4adcb87fdf0989677b", "parents": ["ba21fba7a7fbec24eb4f23081b9c360330c10373"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058197: ensure the patch instruction for firefox.exe is the last instruction in partial mars r=yjuglaret,releng-reviewers,hneiva,ahal\n\nThis ensures that Firefox cannot be run in the middle of an update being applied, reducing the chances of hitting https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1681745 and similar issues.\n\nI verified this locally by:\n* Running a `partials` task locally in a docker container with the existing code\n* Running again after injecting this new code\n* Unpacking one of the generated partials and diffing the `updatev3.manifest` contents, which showed the `firefox.exe` instruction moving to the bottom of the manifest as expected:\n\n```\nworker@a087bd0a695f:~$ diff -Naur artifacts-nofix/part/updatev3.manifest artifacts/part/updatev3.manifest\n--- artifacts-nofix/part/updatev3.manifest\t2026-07-27 16:54:46.958931475 +0000\n+++ artifacts/part/updatev3.manifest\t2026-07-27 17:26:03.533519742 +0000\n@@ -35,7 +35,6 @@\n patch \"gkcodecs.dll.patch\" \"gkcodecs.dll\"\n patch \"freebl3.dll.patch\" \"freebl3.dll\"\n patch \"firefox.exe.sig.patch\" \"firefox.exe.sig\"\n-patch \"firefox.exe.patch\" \"firefox.exe\"\n patch \"dxcompiler.dll.patch\" \"dxcompiler.dll\"\n patch \"desktop-launcher/desktop-launcher.exe.patch\" \"desktop-launcher/desktop-launcher.exe\"\n add \"dependentlibs.list\"\n@@ -61,3 +60,4 @@\n add \"browser/confused_fox.pdf\"\n add \"browser/blank.pdf\"\n remove \"chrome.manifest\"\n+patch \"firefox.exe.patch\" \"firefox.exe\"\n```\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314421\n", "files": ["tools/update-packaging/make_incremental_update.sh"], "git_node": "7d4a1fec9ceee2df1d7d4ac6a347c1b480856189", "git_parents": ["0019a858e79ed44fce15d1f554e89df3ea622c18"], "node": "1514c3e3fb70e8f7757ed8a60416c327d6d0410d", "parents": ["6f802afd64e52ea6d50bdb4adcb87fdf0989677b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057921 - Stop disabling overlay scrollbars on the root scroll container on mobile even with a ::-webkit-scrollbar style. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314287\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/scrolling/webkit-scrollbar-on-root-on-mobile.html"], "git_node": "0f4e0830528e7ad82a13c2aecea67da42fd73b1f", "git_parents": ["7d4a1fec9ceee2df1d7d4ac6a347c1b480856189"], "node": "dd86d83767183677f7d35a8f7d399f21f87bf8d8", "parents": ["1514c3e3fb70e8f7757ed8a60416c327d6d0410d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048354 \u2014 fix tab-audio-blocked-circle-12.svg to use play-circle-fill-12 for Nova r=tabbrowser-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,dao,sthompson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314419\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tab-audio-blocked-circle-12.svg"], "git_node": "53d25b6b87e71b77b41ad9f75955b6aa8b68567c", "git_parents": ["0f4e0830528e7ad82a13c2aecea67da42fd73b1f"], "node": "6eb74322204598f99abc855c14cd8cf59ca658d3", "parents": ["dd86d83767183677f7d35a8f7d399f21f87bf8d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pstanciu \u003cpstanciu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057470 - Enable the render target init debugging flag for wrench reftest. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causing wrench failure @ near-plane-clip.png\n\nThis reverts commit 96f384b1e975444a52140b139aede8707493ed68.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057470 - Add a debug option for initializing renderable textures with opaque pink. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\"\n\nThis reverts commit be67d8afb3e615815e5ed6cc24c64a99a9545635.\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxPlatform.cpp", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/device/gl.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/renderer/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/near-plane-clip.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/args.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/wrench.rs", "gfx/wr/wrshell/src/gui/debug_flags.rs", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "7697ddf217f5d01001ea78444578d1483422c669", "git_parents": ["53d25b6b87e71b77b41ad9f75955b6aa8b68567c"], "node": "310824cb776ea116dfcb9d59c81eee37fcf6a132", "parents": ["6eb74322204598f99abc855c14cd8cf59ca658d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1814460, Bug 2019353: Surface RTCError for SCTP failures. r=mjf,webidl,saschanaz,dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\" for causing mass failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 23a9de79fb370ef187a2d8b0cc80f9d6a97c14a5.\n\nThis reverts commit 3deb3168f1468fb49a99b5775b688cbffe38ad9c.\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannel.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannel.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSession.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsep/JsepSessionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_setLocalAnswerInHaveLocalOffer.html", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_setLocalAnswerInStable.html", "dom/media/webrtc/tests/mochitests/test_peerConnection_setLocalOfferInHaveRemoteOffer.html", "dom/webidl/RTCError.webidl", "dom/webidl/RTCErrorEvent.webidl", "dom/workers/test/test_worker_interfaces.js", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannel.cpp", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannel.h", "netwerk/sctp/datachannel/DataChannelDcSctp.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-close.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCPeerConnection-setLocalDescription-answer.html.ini"], "git_node": "315326a1e8a3d4b8d9d5944523f8dc6dd47e63c7", "git_parents": ["7697ddf217f5d01001ea78444578d1483422c669"], "node": "d00038d023f3776b49a0cbbb31ff8ec27eff477c", "parents": ["310824cb776ea116dfcb9d59c81eee37fcf6a132"], "tags": []}, {"author": "pstanciu \u003cpstanciu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057921 - Stop disabling overlay scrollbars on the root scroll container on mobile even with a ::-webkit-scrollbar style. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\" for causing reftest failures @ webkit-scrollbar-on-root-on-mobile.html\n\nThis reverts commit 0f4e0830528e7ad82a13c2aecea67da42fd73b1f.\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/scrolling/webkit-scrollbar-on-root-on-mobile.html"], "git_node": "ab3bfd4d1a4e6256cde453113f8fb58d3fa68c6c", "git_parents": ["315326a1e8a3d4b8d9d5944523f8dc6dd47e63c7"], "node": "027e6efbe932b10639145021551a9e3d7c7ad700", "parents": ["d00038d023f3776b49a0cbbb31ff8ec27eff477c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dre Grant \u003cdgrant@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057217 - Fix New Tab wallpaper flash when setting the Picture of the Day as wallpaper. r=thecount\n\nSetting a custom wallpaper (e.g. Picture of the Day) over an existing one briefly flashed the New Tab background to the base color: updateWallpaper swapped --newtab-wallpaper to the new URL before the image was decoded, so the background-color showed through while it loaded, and while the \"custom\" selection was in state before its uploaded URL had hydrated the background was cleared entirely.\n\nIn BaseContent.updateWallpaper: keep the current background while a \"custom\" wallpaper is selected but its uploaded URL is not yet in state; when replacing an already-painted wallpaper with a custom image, decode it first (keeping the current wallpaper visible) and only then swap it in, while initial/startup renders still apply synchronously so first paint and the startup cache are not delayed; a monotonic token ensures a newer selection supersedes an in-flight decode, and a failed decode keeps the current wallpaper.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313889\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx"], "git_node": "9ea48a2f8cd57067e44390a1e471a79918ae9580", "git_parents": ["ab3bfd4d1a4e6256cde453113f8fb58d3fa68c6c"], "node": "04d96e3aabb1518af0700ba13b45709cfde92172", "parents": ["027e6efbe932b10639145021551a9e3d7c7ad700"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olivia Hall \u003cohall@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054962 - Make debug Glean ID have permanence r=android-reviewers,kaya\n\nThis patch adds a way to persist a Glean debug view tag across app restarts so pings can be inspected after a restart. Before this patch, Glean keeps the debug view tag in memory only, so it is otherwise cleared on every launch.\n\nPersistence is set through Glean's existing debug intent to prevent accidental usage. This patch did not change the debug drawer.\n\n```adb shell am start -n \u003cpackage\u003e/mozilla.telemetry.glean.debug.GleanDebugActivity --es debugViewTag \u003ctag\u003e --ez persistDebugViewTag true\n```\n\n* The persisted tag is re-applied to Glean on startup.\n* A debug tag set without the persistDebugViewTag flag clears any persisted tag.\n* A launch with no debug tag (a normal restart) leaves persistence untouched.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314132\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/GleanHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/gleandebugtools/GleanDebugToolsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/gleandebugtools/GleanDebugToolsMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/gleandebugtools/GleanDebugToolsStorage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/ui/FenixOverlay.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/datachoices/DataChoicesMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/preference_keys.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivityTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/GleanDebugToolsStorageTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/debugsettings/GleanDebugToolsStoreTest.kt"], "git_node": "454ef5aba7f98800752b4e4caef38410846518be", "git_parents": ["9ea48a2f8cd57067e44390a1e471a79918ae9580"], "node": "c71a05740ad516dd46480079e8afeba8a650504c", "parents": ["04d96e3aabb1518af0700ba13b45709cfde92172"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2011747 - Order backdrop-filter sub-graph content before the tasks that sample it r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nWhen a backdrop-filter sub-graph is popped, pop_surface adds a replacement\npicture task that draws the content following the capture into the parent\nsurface's texture. For a chained parent (a CSS blur, drop-shadow or SVG filter)\nonly the chain root was made to depend on that task, but the tasks that sample\nthe texture are at the start of the chain, not the output end. Pass assignment\ncould therefore schedule the blur to read the texture before the replacement\ntask had drawn into it, and since nothing else samples that texture the content\nwas dropped entirely - a child with any backdrop-filter disappeared under an\nancestor blur.\n\nMake every task in the chain that samples the old parent task depend on the\nreplacement task as well.\n\nThis also makes the WPT css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-plus-filter-2.html\nreftest pass with WebRender, so drop its expectation file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314294\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-blurred-parent-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/backdrop-filter-in-blurred-parent.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-plus-filter-2.html.ini"], "git_node": "865c925ec74249b8802fa3c6d4bc37eba0bf38b5", "git_parents": ["454ef5aba7f98800752b4e4caef38410846518be"], "node": "4a03614ba69d89184d3e96fa06106a559ef3095e", "parents": ["c71a05740ad516dd46480079e8afeba8a650504c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harrison Oglesby \u003coglesby.harrison@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057263 - Enable private browsing mode context menu entry point to Google lens r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313785\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensImageUploader.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensFeatureTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/LensImageUploaderTest.kt"], "git_node": "86bdfed34ac36db65667c3dda84fbdabda8e3861", "git_parents": ["865c925ec74249b8802fa3c6d4bc37eba0bf38b5"], "node": "7dc5febc119711fd6c05ea6c47207142ac512923", "parents": ["4a03614ba69d89184d3e96fa06106a559ef3095e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Osmond \u003caosmond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058285 - Switch to SwizzleYFlipData for GL readback paths. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314477\n", "files": ["gfx/gl/GLReadTexImageHelper.cpp", "gfx/gl/GLReadTexImageHelper.h", "gfx/layers/opengl/CompositorOGL.cpp"], "git_node": "fa33a1de0d4c152ca318c8e4e0c07279d4972db6", "git_parents": ["86bdfed34ac36db65667c3dda84fbdabda8e3861"], "node": "0af6d683e7d5634ed3d0494186ba2881963199ea", "parents": ["7dc5febc119711fd6c05ea6c47207142ac512923"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Harvey \u003cdale@arandomurl.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057220 - Move UrlbarUtils functions to UrlbarShared. r=dao,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314086\n", "files": ["browser/components/downloads/DownloadsViewUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/places/InteractionsBlocklist.sys.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/config/search.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/search.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/search/browser_localSearchShortcuts_xul.js", "browser/components/urlbar/ActionsProviderContextualSearch.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/SmartbarMentionsPanelSearch.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarMuxerStandard.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderAutofill.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderHistoryUrlHeuristic.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderPlaces.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderTabToSearch.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarSearchOneOffs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarSearchUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarTokenizer.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/L10nCache.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarResult.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarTelemetryUtils.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/private/SportsSuggestions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/UrlbarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-autofill/browser_reintegration_telemetry.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-autofill/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_resultSpan.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_result_explanations.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_oneOffs_heuristicRestyle.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-updateResults/browser_appendSpanCount.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-updateResults/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarShared_formatDate.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarUtils_formatDate.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_autofill_originsAndQueries.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "4bfa4ce1e32f7250509b4d1ea3d29df60a09b7d6", "git_parents": ["fa33a1de0d4c152ca318c8e4e0c07279d4972db6"], "node": "f6a6ead113af19c544f127714f300d667b9d6bb7", "parents": ["0af6d683e7d5634ed3d0494186ba2881963199ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058185 - Record autofill backspaces through the parent controller. r=daleharvey\n\n`UrlbarShared` is a content module, so each realm importing it gets its own\ncopy. `_lastRecordAutofillBackspacePromise` lived on it while the write it\ntracks happens in the parent, which left the input writing the window realm's\ncopy and the tests awaiting the system realm's -- an await that never waited.\n\nRouting the call through the child controller puts the bookkeeping where its\nPlaces write already lives and takes another `UrlbarUtils` call out of\n`UrlbarInput`; the promise handle goes back to `UrlbarUtils`, recorded by\n`recordAutofillBackspace()` itself so no caller has to hold it.\n\nWorth verifying: the new actor message is the only part the direct path\ndoesn't exercise, so the message path is where a mistake would show. Both\npaths are green on browser-autofill.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314396\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarParentControllerProxy.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-autofill/browser_reintegration_telemetry.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-autofill/head.js"], "git_node": "47395fa791c9c22bdbab840406ea2318e29cfa80", "git_parents": ["4bfa4ce1e32f7250509b4d1ea3d29df60a09b7d6"], "node": "00e43543b807f2828c468edd79848766f3299fb1", "parents": ["f6a6ead113af19c544f127714f300d667b9d6bb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lando \u003clando@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Merge firefox-autoland to firefox-main\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_UrlbarUtils_formatDate.js", "devtools/client/aboutdebugging/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_af.toml", "devtools/client/framework/test/browser.toml", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "gfx/wr/servo-tidy.toml", "layout/reftests/abs-pos/select-1-dynamic.html", "layout/reftests/abs-pos/select-1-ref.html", "layout/reftests/abs-pos/select-1.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/boguskids-ref.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/boguskids.html", "layout/reftests/forms/select/dynamic-boguskids.html", "mozglue/misc/WindowsDllMain.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/declared/delete-invalid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/declared/delete-shorthand.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/declared/delete.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/inline/delete-invalid.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/inline/delete-shorthand.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/the-stylepropertymap/inline/delete.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/filter-effects/backdrop-filter-plus-filter-2.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCSctpTransport-constructor.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCSctpTransport-events.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCSctpTransport-maxChannels.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/simulcast/negotiation-encodings.https.html.ini", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "d5c0bb96ad84524b445ee72323a4c91176d20b4c", "git_parents": ["a3803eaf8ebda13b8e7177199bf553e6802dc1dc", "47395fa791c9c22bdbab840406ea2318e29cfa80"], "node": "64b39571ed7930978455ebbfbc5a3a6796ea0997", "parents": ["ffb33055e80b3bd79238fbb7e2bb0e1b3f7785ab", "00e43543b807f2828c468edd79848766f3299fb1"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785232342, "git_changesets": ["f86be70ef2f7b917c61d549c901063d8abdf8f26", "aee531ac41034bf427df0ca0acf5184014406c44", "cadda9dc89d6809edc674a2bf218af2dc3173adf", "8e8fb77ff1ba6a83c95db97a6422598209d478a2", "0e283f94bbe9842b0376f07e61d70762ce0fa4bb", "92784b528a229662921280b8bea8aee947319369", "776dade1716e580fb7431716597c8c8ccf2f8027", "606afcd16b12e5af8f537cedd6b563da36c068aa", "57bfc53adeaab2064e2075ecd6a20e15740f362a", "9246c5645b7b5ff6933dd46f2b7c388f76fc8f22", "e0c09cc29cb8a42b96f7a7c9c7174c899866ac13", "c40e53e386530673facd0a58f8640163b14afe14", "c2a54d55282b1863bf513e0a83c11f02726c4a0a", "40adcc963c5175b6315226775e28cc51aa6074b2", "a7af2fec73d438260f06c96c14e30b0ac67763b3", "7b98822f71a1f862dc937975d02183a60e867139", "065951ec4eaba333063ebf5c324b74548afb74a6", "aee0923dc2d7270eb361e519f44035f49a563b75", "40d485231a7f2c141429ed662c6a3cd63ffe8983", "16e8979074c60f9743260cc0cb96f6efac481929", "a61954fb585c3ebceaf72a361df5ab2fd8c5b9a4", "526646a68248dd69babf659527f8b5bed3065e85", "a83008e