ccaa14671ef"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785242790, "git_changesets": ["b76a04437cd19d8e600ac0e8a84ef30bdb2e826e"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "44979": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 44d12294c895576c9a489c0d7efa44b2ea0f7d71 with FIREFOX_153_0_1_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "6625d06aff5742bf828966e63ec8e170c25f0300", "git_parents": ["b76a04437cd19d8e600ac0e8a84ef30bdb2e826e"], "node": "5484bed3001ea9b0e31afe384c25e9509edf09d8", "parents": ["6075a5e37ddbdf738564b10f1e069cad98742854"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785242838, "git_changesets": ["6625d06aff5742bf828966e63ec8e170c25f0300"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "44980": {"changesets": [{"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056111 - Add remote.screenshot.use_readback pref to capture screenshots via WebRender r=jdescottes\n\nWebDriver and Marionette screenshots normally re-render the document through\nthe software drawSnapshot path, which does not reflect WebRender-specific\nrendering. When this pref is enabled, capture.canvas instead reads back the\nactual WebRender composited framebuffer via drawWindow with USE_WIDGET_LAYERS.\n\nReadback can only return the content area composited on screen, and its\ncoordinates are relative to the chrome window rather than the document, so with\nthe pref enabled every capture degrades to the whole content area of the\nforeground tab: full-document, clip and element captures all return the\nviewport. A capture with no content area to read back, such as one taken in\nchrome scope, keeps using drawSnapshot.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312921\n", "files": ["gfx/docs/DebuggingWebRenderScreenshots.md", "gfx/docs/index.md", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "remote/doc/Prefs.md", "remote/shared/Capture.sys.mjs", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_screenshot.py"], "git_node": "c900f6de3175424a72d23765300aa4a4292a4c1a", "git_parents": ["47395fa791c9c22bdbab840406ea2318e29cfa80"], "node": "cd2706487531f6166c6db07513a9c87b22210315", "parents": ["00e43543b807f2828c468edd79848766f3299fb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ansh \u003cansinha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040072 - Share the novaColorGroups between ColorsScreen and NovaColorsPreview r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311667\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/colors/src/main/java/mozilla/components/ui/colors/NovaColorGroups.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/colors/src/main/java/mozilla/components/ui/colors/NovaColorsPreview.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/samples/acorn-components/src/main/java/org/mozilla/samples/acorn/components/ui/ColorsScreen.kt"], "git_node": "d44ec8737d069da986543b1f052a8d64c3c7684c", "git_parents": ["c900f6de3175424a72d23765300aa4a4292a4c1a"], "node": "e184115c58e269f3c15cb71c5993354d26515f41", "parents": ["cd2706487531f6166c6db07513a9c87b22210315"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045119 - Check sizes of received shared memory objects on `mmap`-using platforms. r=afranchuk,sandbox-reviewers\n\nSee the added comments on the various `Platform::IsSafeToMap` methods\nfor more details.\n\nAlso modifies the Linux sandbox policies: all processes can read file\nseals and set shrink/grow seals.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306581\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/SharedMemoryHandle.cpp", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryPlatform.h", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryPlatform_android.cpp", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryPlatform_mach.cpp", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryPlatform_posix.cpp", "ipc/glue/SharedMemoryPlatform_windows.cpp", "security/sandbox/linux/SandboxFilter.cpp"], "git_node": "0112087d1a12b39a202934abc4176a9d9e470029", "git_parents": ["d44ec8737d069da986543b1f052a8d64c3c7684c"], "node": "db1a48a97feda281f9a1e3b445f1edbe433bf444", "parents": ["e184115c58e269f3c15cb71c5993354d26515f41"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045119 - Add test cases for tampering with a shared memory handle's size. r=afranchuk\n\nThis adds some affordances for testing which might have other uses:\n\n* A test fixture class which allows access to otherwise private operations,\n  to test what happens in situations normally disallowed by C++ types\n\n* A mock IPC actor that turns deserialization FatalError calls into\n  non-fatal logging, to test that invalid input is correctly rejected\n  without the overhead of gtest death tests\n\n* SerializeAndDeserialize is now factored out and type-generic\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306582\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/SharedMemoryHandle.h", "ipc/gtest/IPCTestUtils.h", "ipc/gtest/TestBigBuffer.cpp", "ipc/gtest/TestSharedMemory.cpp"], "git_node": "1485e9ce0da0ef41b8faf94fd0772bc174616dc5", "git_parents": ["0112087d1a12b39a202934abc4176a9d9e470029"], "node": "e49520a23c48f69722b04882d471a579f76efcf3", "parents": ["db1a48a97feda281f9a1e3b445f1edbe433bf444"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jed Davis \u003cjld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047332 - Fix the FreezeAndMapRW shared memory gtest. r=afranchuk\n\nThe original intent of that test, expressed in terms of the current API,\nis: what if you could transmute a ReadOnlyHandle into a MutableHandle?\nSo now there's a test-only method for that.\n\nBonus fix: reword the comment for Reprotect; I found the old one to be\nconfusing.  (It is also the case that you can't set bits in `max_prot`\nthat the object being mapped doesn't like, but it's FreezeAndMapRW that\ntests that part, not Reprotect.)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306583\n", "files": ["ipc/gtest/TestSharedMemory.cpp"], "git_node": "db8808c338598be41ce90f4bf6c9ac49e492e22d", "git_parents": ["1485e9ce0da0ef41b8faf94fd0772bc174616dc5"], "node": "2a8936e0faa74109d694095bf8dc5e2e59f038bf", "parents": ["e49520a23c48f69722b04882d471a579f76efcf3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "owlishDeveloper \u003cbugzeeeeee@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055683 - IPC improvement r=nika,geckoview-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314463\n", "files": ["mobile/android/components/geckoview/GeckoViewContentChannelParent.cpp"], "git_node": "b6b18b911126f6b241c3867015684ed0f0625562", "git_parents": ["db8808c338598be41ce90f4bf6c9ac49e492e22d"], "node": "3361c5f80b62ee047915909ae7ee5ed1eef94b18", "parents": ["2a8936e0faa74109d694095bf8dc5e2e59f038bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Harveer Singh \u003chsingh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052481 - Replace EARLY_BETA_OR_EARLIER with NIGHTLY_BUILD for dom.workers.throttling.enabled r=aiunusov,dom-worker-reviewers,asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314450\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "78c63883a325a85bbd8cb11bf000617687519b02", "git_parents": ["b6b18b911126f6b241c3867015684ed0f0625562"], "node": "a896b863606bd991f3ac042dd2f044a4ea39477b", "parents": ["3361c5f80b62ee047915909ae7ee5ed1eef94b18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057902 - skip tests with Nova design enabled if they fail: test_console_assert.html\n\nThis started to fail after test_cached_messages.html had been disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314531\n", "files": ["devtools/shared/webconsole/test/chrome/chrome.toml"], "git_node": "98dec3139efbdcda41eb21523a5fc8d73e90be37", "git_parents": ["78c63883a325a85bbd8cb11bf000617687519b02"], "node": "7c1fc9ee46a25bdd2de1307fff40c58d1ce26d66", "parents": ["a896b863606bd991f3ac042dd2f044a4ea39477b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049244 - Turn .browserContainer into a CSS grid. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,devtools-reviewers,sfoster,ochameau,dao,jdescottes.\n\nThis makes the element layout more explicit and easier to work with.\nAs the DevTools splitter is turned into a grid area resizer, we need to handle\nthe DevTools frame max size so it doesn't grow bigger than its grid \"cell\".\n\nWhen the toolbox is docked to the side, it doesn't change much to what we\nhad before: the max width is contrained by the browser container width, so\nwe keep the resize observer on it, and update the max width (alongside the\nsplitter attributes aria-value(min|max)).\n\nWhen the toolbox is docked to the bottom, now we need to account for the possible\nitems that will be displayed and taking some vertical space:\n- the notifications (in split view)\n- the RDM toolbar\n- the \"Find in page\" toolbar\n\nSo here, we need to know when the browser container size is updated (e.g. when\nthe browser, or the split view, or one of the sidebar are resized), but also\nwhen we get additional items in the browser container.\nSadly we can't just use a MutationObserver on top of the ResizeObserver: for some\nof those items they don't actually have their final height when they're added\ninto the DOM, which makes it tricky to reason about the available space.\nSo we're taking another approach and detect when the browser container grid lines\nsized are updated. We're using a reflow observer and a debounced method to react\nwhen reflow occurs, and then compute some string representation of the grid lines\nheight using `getGridFragments`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311100\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/static/browser_parsable_css.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/content-area.css", "devtools/client/framework/test/browser_toolbox_hosts_size.js", "devtools/client/framework/test/browser_toolbox_splitter_keyboard.js", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox-hosts.js", "devtools/client/responsive/responsive-browser.css", "devtools/client/themes/devtools-browser.css", "devtools/client/themes/splitters.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/tabbox.js", "toolkit/themes/shared/findbar.css"], "git_node": "47ff726537689d6fc00918b7d25c0c17f7708305", "git_parents": ["98dec3139efbdcda41eb21523a5fc8d73e90be37"], "node": "d2ba01e204b40bfcbb30e46de27018f458193012", "parents": ["7c1fc9ee46a25bdd2de1307fff40c58d1ce26d66"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038693 - [devtools] Use thick Nova borders for DevTools toolbox. r=devtools-reviewers,ochameau.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312253\n", "files": ["devtools/client/inspector/markup/test/events/helper_events_test_runner.js", "devtools/client/themes/devtools-browser.css", "devtools/client/themes/splitters.css"], "git_node": "80fca9d9b44ae98a609036941ad35989445e68ab", "git_parents": ["47ff726537689d6fc00918b7d25c0c17f7708305"], "node": "6c6ed67b3bb178bdee2dd8340dba0382bee5460a", "parents": ["d2ba01e204b40bfcbb30e46de27018f458193012"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sebastian Hengst \u003caryx.github@gmx-topmail.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057902 - skip tests with Nova design enabled if they fail: browser_browser_toolbox_fission_inspector.js\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314534\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/browser-toolbox/test/browser.toml"], "git_node": "b7d7f3c53355c049e23a3318b1d9d13ba6b62943", "git_parents": ["80fca9d9b44ae98a609036941ad35989445e68ab"], "node": "ca3cdf1601ca6483b10dac5af58b4c1018a6ed72", "parents": ["6c6ed67b3bb178bdee2dd8340dba0382bee5460a"], "tags": []}, {"au