398a3da"], "node": "f3480c4c58fffca0d7a6b98f9c3666920f7e220a", "parents": ["f6d89f4180509e5be7984b7813494063e9a4d84f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Link \u003cjlink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057305: Add an AVX2 implementation of convolve_horizontally r=lsalzman\n\nThe horizontal image convolution used by high-quality (Lanczos)\ndownscale-on-decode had only an SSE2 kernel, while the vertical pass already\nhad an AVX2 one (convolve_vertically_avx2). On AVX2 hardware this left the\nhorizontal pass running at half the SIMD width of the vertical pass, making it\nthe dominant cost of downscaling.\n\nAdd convolve_horizontally_avx2, a 256-bit widening of the SSE2 kernel: it\nproduces one output pixel per iteration and consumes eight filter taps at a\ntime, processing four taps in each of the __m256i's two 128-bit lanes exactly\nas the SSE2 kernel processes four taps in an __m128i, then combines the two\nlanes once per output pixel. The fixed-point arithmetic, rounding and\nsaturation are unchanged, so the result is bit-identical to the SSE2 kernel.\nDispatch prefers AVX2 when available, mirroring the vertical pass.\n\nAdd a gtest that checks the SSE2 and AVX2 kernels against a scalar reference\nacross a range of filter lengths, including every tail remainder (length mod\n8), filters shorter than one SIMD block, and per-output-pixel varying lengths.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314186\n", "files": ["gfx/2d/ConvolutionFilterAVX2.cpp", "gfx/2d/SkConvolver.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/TestConvolutionFilter.cpp", "gfx/tests/gtest/moz.build"], "git_node": "7c47a1a819b6dccbc80a0f6f6c9aac33c376c528", "git_parents": ["5b2b91dbfcc1d4a9ff02073d76affd85d710fafa"], "node": "076ae50a4a49c522b74daa9347b435e62ee642fc", "parents": ["f3480c4c58fffca0d7a6b98f9c3666920f7e220a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057308. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313983\n", "files": ["image/RasterImage.cpp", "image/RasterImage.h"], "git_node": "55dc289554151972f35cb8d8102e334a6e953ff2", "git_parents": ["7c47a1a819b6dccbc80a0f6f6c9aac33c376c528"], "node": "3744df357b9c444461f36554f45a4143e961729b", "parents": ["076ae50a4a49c522b74daa9347b435e62ee642fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053417 - P1. Add Glean telemetry for Form Autofill passports r=NeilDeakin,credential-management-reviewers\n\nAdd telemetry so we can measure how users interact with passport autofill:\nwhether passport fields are detected on a page, whether the autofill popup is\nshown and used, how the save/update capture doorhanger is handled, and what\nactions users take in the management UI.\n\n - Add a `passport` event category covering form interaction, capture\n   doorhanger and management events.\n - Add a PassportTelemetry class and wire it into\n   AutofillTelemetry.#getTelemetryByType. The shared, type-generic call sites\n   (FormAutofillSection, FormAutofillPrompter, editDialog) already pass the\n   passport dataType, but had no telemetry instance to route it to, so passport\n   events were silently dropped until now.\n - Record \"passport\" as a possible iframe_layout_detection category.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311072\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/formautofill/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/AutofillTelemetry.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "07dd472f969d8e47e0945a0823e0c6eabe8f8b2b", "git_parents": ["55dc289554151972f35cb8d8102e334a6e953ff2"], "node": "d731e1b19f7cb1afa2a09656f834be916b52efd5", "parents": ["3744df357b9c444461f36554f45a4143e961729b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053417 - P2. Add a browser test for Form Autofill passport telemetry r=NeilDeakin,credential-management-reviewers\n\nAdd end-to-end coverage for the passport telemetry added in P1, so the recorded\nevents and their extra keys stay correct as the passport code evolves. The test\ndrives a real passport form, the capture doorhanger and the management edit\ndialog, then asserts:\n\n - form events: detected, popup_shown, filled and submitted;\n - capture doorhanger events: show, save, cancel and disable;\n - management events: add, edit and show_entry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311789\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser_passport_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "4f1f441185fb677db92b88c74fdcebb556c16f5b", "git_parents": ["07dd472f969d8e47e0945a0823e0c6eabe8f8b2b"], "node": "36d820847126360fd8492bff12e54cfa0fc832a1", "parents": ["d731e1b19f7cb1afa2a09656f834be916b52efd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057921 - Stop disabling overlay scrollbars on the root scroll container on mobile even with a ::-webkit-scrollbar style. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314287\n", "files": ["layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/scrolling/webkit-scrollbar-on-root-on-mobile.html"], "git_node": "2bcc5c1a352d9ff8da42e285e6f7b50a698082fc", "git_parents": ["4f1f441185fb677db92b88c74fdcebb556c16f5b"], "node": "3a0ed263e80dcf52dba8dcbebfaeeb62f420f6b6", "parents": ["36d820847126360fd8492bff12e54cfa0fc832a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rolf Rando \u003crrando@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055930 - New engine architecture for Form Autofill model r=valentinp,credential-management-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,NeilDeakin,perftest-reviewers,dimi,mozperftest-reviewers,sparky,nordzilla\n\nFusion model approach improves weighted English f1 score (weighted on autofill field prevelance in the wild) from 93% to 98%. Raw multi-lingual accuracy improvement is 3%.\n\nA small change in the inference engine is made to support a windowed model. Non normalized embeddings for text is calculated per field, then results are windowed 3 items at a time (previous, current and next) and applied to a head model that emulates a transformers.js to allow for classification outputs.\n\nThe head model is fp32 for now, since it is small\n\nhttps://mozilla-hub.atlassian.net/wiki/spaces/FAAMT/pages/2832663088/Improving+Local+ML+Auto-Fill+Models\n\nNot that previously all tests were WASM. We've updated the tests to use best-onnx. The inputs for the legacy tests (which included 'aa' 'bb' prefixes) have been updated as well to provide a true comparison.\n\nWASM (linux) perf\n| Metric (11-field form) | Legacy (tinybert) | New (encoder + head) |\n|---|---|---|\n| One-time init | 277 ms | 403 ms (both engines, concurrent Promise.all) |\n| Per-form inference | 126 ms | 37 ms (encoder 33 + head 0.8) |\n| Memory | 248 MiB | 383 MiB |\n\nOnnx-Native perf\n| Metric (11-field form) | Legacy (tinybert) | New (encoder + head) |\n|---|---|---|\n| One-time init | 100 ms | 120 ms (both engines, concurrent Promise.all) |\n| Per-form inference | 34 ms | 13 ms (encoder 9.2 + head 0.36) |\n| Memory | 113 MiB | 146 MiB |\n\nPerf Run https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=71617\n\n{F75771378}\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312803\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/onnxruntime-web-fetch.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/linux.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/macosx.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/windows11-24h2-ref.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/perftest/windows11-24h2.yml", "testing/perfdocs/generated/mozperftest.rst", "toolkit/components/formautofill/shared/FormAutofillML.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/content/EngineProcess.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/content/backends/ONNXPipeline.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_autofill_perf.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "50e2f3f40d997aa00ff58db5808e211c0a57dbc6", "git_parents": ["2bcc5c1a352d9ff8da42e285e6f7b50a698082fc"], "node": "4ead97942d92a3a942fe53b04f01c7b26375b338", "parents": ["3a0ed263e80dcf52dba8dcbebfaeeb62f420f6b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mcarare \u003c48995920+mcarare@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053653 - Ensure the search overlay and suggestions occupy the full screen. r=jonalmeida\n\nSpecifically:\n- In `fragment_urlinput.xml`, changed the `searchViewContainer` height from `wrap_content` to `match_parent`.\n- In `SearchOverlay.kt`, wrapped the overlay content in a `Box` with `fillMaxSize` and moved the background color to this parent container.\n- Applied `fillMaxSize` to the `Column` containing the search suggestions list.\n- In `fragment_search_suggestions.xml`, replaced the `CoordinatorLayout` with a `LinearLayout` and configured the `ComposeView` to use `layout_weight=\"1\"` to ensure it expands to fill the available space.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311375\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/focus/activity/robots/SearchRobot.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/searchsuggestions/SearchSuggestionsViewModel.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/searchsuggestions/ui/SearchOverlay.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_search_suggestions.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_urlinput.xml"], "git_node": "5d38023bb83f8f056ef81b79f7637d889119bb5c", "git_parents": ["50e2f3f40d997aa00ff58db5808e211c0a57dbc6"], "node": "e6ce100c63f59dd6fd29fdf128bb9950df216f97", "parents": ["4ead97942d92a3a942fe53b04f01c7b26375b338"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057218 - Migrate verifyTheShareButtonTest UI test to the efficiency framework r=aaronmt\n\nConverted the verifyTheShareButtonTest UI test to the efficiency framework.\n\nThe new UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase (along with shareBookmarkTest and shareAllTabsFromACollectionTest).  [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=71287 | Try ]]\nAll efficiency UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=3696f43cec299581ed5741ac3bee47523fbd5d1d  | Try ]]\nThe updated legacy UI test successfully passed 25x on Firebase.  [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=71262  | Try ]]\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313737\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/helpers/Constants.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/ShareOverlayPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/BookmarksTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CollectionsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MainMenuTest.kt"], "git_node": "879be4e05a8d320acd227b5fbd25d3a215667560", "git_parents": ["5d38023bb83f8f056ef81b79f7637d889119bb5c"], "node": "c3b399437e926ab064b69ab9a7284ff1284a96b5", "parents": ["e6ce100c63f59dd6fd29fdf128bb9950df216f97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058044 - [devtools] Enable browser_aboutdebugging_devtoolstoolbox_contextmenu.js for nova r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nWe were using the \"about:devtools-toolbox\" browser element in order to select an element in about:debugging.\nI don't really know why this only fails with nova, it was plain wrong.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314500\n", "files": ["devtools/client/aboutdebugging/test/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/client/aboutdebugging/test/browser/browser_aboutdebugging_devtoolstoolbox_contextmenu.js"], "git_node": "335a20f8a2c30013a96c4e1fc247342f223871cb", "git_parents": ["879be4e05a8d320acd227b5fbd25d3a215667560"], "node": "a9ea0d9d47143e88b14c66a2d25b335c2ebedf5e", "parents": ["c3b399437e926ab064b69ab9a7284ff1284a96b5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Descottes \u003cjdescottes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058202 - [DevTools Release Tasks - Cycle 155] Remove backward compatibility code r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314403\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/toolbox.js", "devtools/client/fronts/style-rule.js", "devtools/client/inspector/rules/views/text-property-editor.js", "devtools/client/netmonitor/src/components/request-details/ResponsePanel.js", "devtools/server/actors/style-rule.js"], "git_node": "a2c88f92ed62389676163da399bf13efdc0ae65e", "git_parents": ["335a20f8a2c30013a96c4e1fc247342f223871cb"], "node": "fe75354f961ddff6fa562b2a95731e7ab765b2ed", "parents": ["a9ea0d9d47143e88b14c66a2d25b335c2ebedf5e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056818 - Do not reuse a captured touch target for a single-touch touchstart; r=masayuki\n\nA touchstart carrying a single touch is the start of a new touch session;\nTouchManager::PreHandleEvent() already relies on this by evicting any captured\ntouches when a touchstart has a single touch.\n\nHowever, TouchManager::SetupTarget() reused the captured target whenever the touch\nid was still present in the captuired list. This caused inconsistent\nbehavior and allowed the touchstart event to be dispatched to a stale target,\nwhich would later be removed from the captured list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313429\n", "files": ["dom/events/test/browser.toml", "dom/events/test/browser_touch_target_new_session.js", "layout/base/TouchManager.cpp"], "git_node": "eb353714f91a09fc1c446028f54921558fda5024", "git_parents": ["a2c88f92ed62389676163da399bf13efdc0ae65e"], "node": "c5c533edcece1a7e205d112709d316aef15819ab", "parents": ["fe75354f961ddff6fa562b2a95731e7ab765b2ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057308. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\" for causing lint failures @RasterImage.h.\n\nThis reverts commit 55dc289554151972f35cb8d8102e334a6e953ff2.\n", "files": ["image/RasterImage.cpp", "image/RasterImage.h"], "git_node": "6d6d2824858e9462d8f0587d0358c1d6a9af5b53", "git_parents": ["eb353714f91a09fc1c446028f54921558fda5024"], "node": "5247996049cdca3867806452ef9e1b426d57dee6", "parents": ["c5c533edcece1a7e205d112709d316aef15819ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056111 - Add remote.screenshot.use_readback pref to capture screenshots via WebRender r=jdescottes\" for causing marionette failures @nsAboutRedirector.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit c900f6de3175424a72d23765300aa4a4292a4c1a.\n", "files": ["gfx/docs/DebuggingWebRenderScreenshots.md", "gfx/docs/index.md", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "remote/doc/Prefs.md", "remote/shared/Capture.sys.mjs", "testing/marionette/harness/marionette_harness/tests/unit/test_screenshot.py"], "git_node": "ab4c62f327484254559c4770a152d2a985785cec", "git_parents": ["6d6d2824858e9462d8f0587d0358c1d6a9af5b53"], "node": "e0be5ab23dbda3b6df3482fd9c65f9a579c45c70", "parents": ["5247996049cdca3867806452ef9e1b426d57dee6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047483 - Hand off main-thread keyboard scrolling to an ancestor scroll container when the focused one is at the edge. r=botond,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306678\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.h", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.cpp", "layout/base/nsLayoutUtils.h", "layout/base/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/base/tests/test_keyboard_scroll_handoff.html", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior-keyboard-scroll-child-frame.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior-keyboard-scroll.html.ini"], "git_node": "ab7549d7e533bbbba0c271f1759cc893068422dd", "git_parents": ["ab4c62f327484254559c4770a152d2a985785cec"], "node": "701b5997e60bb1a31450227bcb55508526927d48", "parents": ["e0be5ab23dbda3b6df3482fd9c65f9a579c45c70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058115 - Touch down slightly off the document's left edge, not exactly on it. r=botond\n\nOn Nova, with a zero offset, the initial touch position converted to\nscreen coordinates ends up outside the document, so scrolling doesn't\nhappen at all.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314554\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_zoomed_pan.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml"], "git_node": "dc08fe5e170f787e6fd608a4ed7b504b896eb528", "git_parents": ["ab7549d7e533bbbba0c271f1759cc893068422dd"], "node": "baef265281feeaddb5791d6a0f35de297b2cbd9f", "parents": ["701b5997e60bb1a31450227bcb55508526927d48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Schedule the clang-tidy source-test tasks on tools/clang-tidy changes r=taskgraph-reviewers,linter-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nThe cpp(clang-tidy) and cpp(clang-tidy-external) tasks only matched C/C++/ObjC\nsource extensions, so a change to tools/clang-tidy/config.yaml (which decides\nwhich checks run) never scheduled them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314398\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/source-test/clang.yml"], "git_node": "9d547849fcfc4c2355d2a03a0db4745c03a7186a", "git_parents": ["dc08fe5e170f787e6fd608a4ed7b504b896eb528"], "node": "419424af83e9c56bbb4ec11a92530f4a981b47c1", "parents": ["baef265281feeaddb5791d6a0f35de297b2cbd9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Chevobbe \u003cnchevobbe@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057290 - [devtools] Fix addon manifest URL focus indicator in about:debugging. r=devtools-reviewers,bomsy.\n\nThe link parent element hides overflow, which clipped the \u003ca\u003e outline.\nThis patch moves the focus indicator to the parent element so it's not clipped anymore.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313787\n", "files": ["devtools/client/aboutdebugging/src/components/debugtarget/FieldPair.css"], "git_node": "958bc54ac3d6314d416e7e40bfab37559e281e5a", "git_parents": ["9d547849fcfc4c2355d2a03a0db4745c03a7186a"], "node": "95df5e91cc490f802cfe1b248d93f5da0370e602", "parents": ["419424af83e9c56bbb4ec11a92530f4a981b47c1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Johannes Salas Schmidt \u003cjoschmidt@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057310 - Parse bridged engine payloads in the Sync collection validator r=sync-reviewers,markh\n\n`transformAfterDecrypt(cleartext)` has a different signature in the old\nsynchronization engine than in the Sync Bridge - it used to return an object, but\nnow it returns a string. The validator then saw a server item with no `id`, so\nevery local login was reported as `serverMissing`.\n\nNow parse the cleartext into an object when it is a string, at the single point where\nserver items are collected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314350\n", "files": ["services/sync/modules/collection_validator.sys.mjs", "services/sync/tests/unit/test_password_validator.js"], "git_node": "519b072e42c0ebca58b87b03eca7ef350af90d3d", "git_parents": ["958bc54ac3d6314d416e7e40bfab37559e281e5a"], "node": "8836a7026f667a41433e9dd05823b59dad4a0d19", "parents": ["95df5e91cc490f802cfe1b248d93f5da0370e602"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057586 [wpt PR 61516] - Fix flakiness in dictionary-fetch-with-link-header-in-subresources.tentative.https.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix flakiness in dictionary-fetch-with-link-header-in-subresources.tentative.https.html\n\nThat's currently easy to reproduce with `run_wpt_tests.py --repeat=10`.\nUse `token()` to work around race conditions between dictionary\nregistrations and cache clearing between\n`compression_dictionary_promise_test`s. Also replace the use of\n`registerAltDictionaryAndWait` with actual dictionary ID check to\nmake waiting for dictionary availability more reliable.\n\nBug: 522338661, 40255884, 417529151\nChange-Id: Ic48a71611d48081438060143cafb26249352da2c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8139240\nReviewed-by: Patrick Meenan \u003cpmeenan@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1667868}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 74cfea54b2a74d8ad599e01885a6bdfea7515306\nwpt-pr: 61516\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-header-in-subresources.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "d4c7c30e568c628bc0cd78a817d537435df9bd6d", "git_parents": ["519b072e42c0ebca58b87b03eca7ef350af90d3d"], "node": "5d4776c1b530dce79956812e89d32445084bd336", "parents": ["8836a7026f667a41433e9dd05823b59dad4a0d19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "LongYinan \u003clynweklm@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057591 [wpt PR 61517] - Fix border-shape arc interpolation neutral keyframe list length, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix border-shape arc interpolation neutral keyframe list length\n\nCSSShapeInterpolationType::CreateNeutralValue() built the neutral\ninterpolable list for an arc segment with only two InterpolableLength\nentries in the radius block, but the canonical arc layout used by the\nreader (ShapeInterpolationReader::ReadArc) and the real-value writers\n(ConvertPath and MaybeConvertNeutral) has three: radius_x, radius_y and\nthe direction-agnostic radius. The neutral list was therefore one entry\nshorter per arc than the real value it animates against.\n\nCreateNeutralValue() is reached only from border-shape, through\nshape_interpolation_functions::CreateNeutralValue() and\nCSSBorderShapeInterpolationType::MaybeConvertNeutral(). clip-path,\noffset-path and shape-outside use MaybeConvertNeutral(), which already\nemits three lengths, so only border-shape was affected.\n\nMaybeMergeSingles() only compares the segment command structure\n(ShapesAreCompatible) and not the interpolable list length, so the\nshorter neutral list was merged with the longer real list. Sampling the\nanimation then reached InterpolableList::Interpolate() with mismatched\nlists: at the divergent index the neutral holds an InterpolableNumber\n(the arc-large flag) where the real value holds an InterpolableLength\n(the direction-agnostic radius), and InterpolableNumber::Interpolate()'s\nTo\u003cInterpolableNumber\u003e() downcast aborts the renderer (an always-on\nrelease CHECK; on DCHECK builds the length DCHECK in\nInterpolableList::AssertCanInterpolateWith fires first).\n\nThis is web-reachable with no flag (border-shape is shipped): animating a\nborder-shape whose shape() contains an arc, with an implicit (neutral)\nboundary keyframe, deterministically crashes the renderer.\n\nEmit three lengths so the neutral arc list matches the real value, and\nadd a crashtest.\n\nBug: 513192895\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 \u003cnoreply@anthropic.com\u003e\nChange-Id: I57fcda1f7981406f393b695e522fb1396611bcdb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8022742\nReviewed-by: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jason Leo \u003ccgqaq@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1667880}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a282b38dcc15c067c16bdbf79f5137f26abd2214\nwpt-pr: 61517\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/border-shape/crashtests/border-shape-shape-arc-animation-crash.html"], "git_node": "53dae563e45bc2844cde92585812ff6dff224ca6", "git_parents": ["d4c7c30e568c628bc0cd78a817d537435df9bd6d"], "node": "f3ce3f086ba0678c2bf92a76dddb647348746bd1", "parents": ["5d4776c1b530dce79956812e89d32445084bd336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikolaos Papaspyrou \u003cnikolaos@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057600 [wpt PR 61518] - cpu_performance: Ship the CPU Performance API, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncpu_performance: Ship the CPU Performance API\n\nThis CL enables CpuPerformance for Stable.\n\nI2S: https://groups.google.com/a/chromium.org/g/blink-dev/c/igPwzkxhQtk/m/Epzx3q7MBwAJ\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=8a29dc4d-cbb7-45d9-b0ec-f9ba0a26158a\n\nBug: 449760252\nChange-Id: Ia9da4f6940cc11813a552338a5068ec2799f3228\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8139880\nReviewed-by: Rick Byers \u003crbyers@chromium.org\u003e\nOwners-Override: Rick Byers \u003crbyers@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Nikolaos Papaspyrou \u003cnikolaos@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1667924}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6a009d73f0d315941b90cac13a9523a2a08c631b\nwpt-pr: 61518\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/cpu-performance/cpu-performance.https.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/cpu-performance/cpu-performance.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "b27f1ab69887d7084f075146f446f3470d1a8970", "git_parents": ["53dae563e45bc2844cde92585812ff6dff224ca6"], "node": "e30acc79f08048db842e059f1b90f09f0b1962a4", "parents": ["f3ce3f086ba0678c2bf92a76dddb647348746bd1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057600 [wpt PR 61518] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61518\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/cpu-performance/cpu-performance.https.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/cpu-performance/cpu-performance.tentative.https.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "6508360d30cd7fddce2fbc73d8fadb8760c5a2ca", "git_parents": ["b27f1ab69887d7084f075146f446f3470d1a8970"], "node": "60813b8cb6572d6a19ebc28d3ab3c4c66c05c638", "parents": ["e30acc79f08048db842e059f1b90f09f0b1962a4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057658 [wpt PR 61523] - Escape CSS syntax component identifiers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nEscape CSS syntax component identifiers\n\nMissing escape of custom identifiers used in syntax definition for\n@function parameter and return types.\n\nAlso added a test for escaped identifiers in @property syntax\ndescriptors.\n\nBug: 518094442\nChange-Id: Idf41c16dccabdcdf3350e2eb5dc3fa58e16e0f7b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8143363\nReviewed-by: Kevin Babbitt \u003ckbabbitt@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1668036}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e8882f5c298918441461db07556ac813716dbe58\nwpt-pr: 61523\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/functions/at-function-cssom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-properties-values-api/at-property-cssom.html"], "git_node": "ae52cac02fb7510fab138ee2e2f85650f1bd806e", "git_parents": ["6508360d30cd7fddce2fbc73d8fadb8760c5a2ca"], "node": "fb21687f38315f12a92cd2fb82d4274e05ae107a", "parents": ["60813b8cb6572d6a19ebc28d3ab3c4c66c05c638"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057658 [wpt PR 61523] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61523\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/functions/at-function-cssom.html.ini"], "git_node": "493c61393cc83a6cb9bbde7f9b466d40d6b13b1f", "git_parents": ["ae52cac02fb7510fab138ee2e2f85650f1bd806e"], "node": "bdaaec95228e6dff723fef7b792a073723ab5b8a", "parents": ["fb21687f38315f12a92cd2fb82d4274e05ae107a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Navoda Munasinha \u003cnavoda.munasinha@codimite.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057653 [wpt PR 61522] - Don't inherit table border-color onto cell borders (flagged), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDon't inherit table border-color onto cell borders (flagged)\n\nThe border/rules table attributes create borders on interior cells.\nBlink builds those cell borders with `border-color: inherit`, so a\nborder-color set on the \u003ctable\u003e via CSS cascades down onto the cell\nborders. This is wrong: border-color is not an inherited property per\nCSS Backgrounds 3, and it is an interop bug -- Gecko does not do this.\n\nThis adds a TableCellBorderColorInherit flag guarding that legacy\ninheritance. The flag defaults to \"stable\" (enabled), so the current\nbehavior is unchanged. When it is disabled, interior cell borders resolve\nto `currentColor` instead, following the cell's own color rather than\nthe table's border-color. The legacy `bordercolor` attribute path is\npreserved in both modes: when it is present the cell borders still\ninherit the table's (attribute-set) color.\n\nDefaulting to stable means no behavior change yet; the flag will be\nflipped off in a follow-up to launch the spec-compliant behavior. A new\nWPT asserts the flag-disabled behavior and runs via the disable-* virtual suite.\n\nBug: 40745409\nChange-Id: I7d5d9e9f527abd652ac3496feba484d7b95b5d2f\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8130161\nReviewed-by: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: David Baron \u003cdbaron@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1668070}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 90b8c2ee4d51620a97c3888e882eb4a7868be26b\nwpt-pr: 61522\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-border-color-not-inherited.html"], "git_node": "34156690cfad9c1bad70334576a3f7080315e6e5", "git_parents": ["493c61393cc83a6cb9bbde7f9b466d40d6b13b1f"], "node": "ff62e461a25ba73fe6c6504fd22dd0ad774c67b2", "parents": ["bdaaec95228e6dff723fef7b792a073723ab5b8a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yulun Wu \u003cyulun_wu@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055098 [wpt PR 61296] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318844, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=318844 (#61296)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: be52155b4e5c087ef2541da4be3e065433f79df8\nwpt-pr: 61296\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-in-multicol-relpos-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-in-multicol-relpos-content.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-with-relpos-block-content-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/outside-marker-with-relpos-block-content.html"], "git_node": "765572b6f7e663aaa0f0b366fa22bd1561a08bdf", "git_parents": ["34156690cfad9c1bad70334576a3f7080315e6e5"], "node": "ed7068725a28113a735065faf326066fb8dcb6d6", "parents": ["ff62e461a25ba73fe6c6504fd22dd0ad774c67b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057740 [wpt PR 61530] - layout: Use `f64` when blending table content sizes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Use `f64` when blending table content sizes\n\nIt seems that `f32` doesn't have enough precision to prevent hitting our\nfloating point error limit when blending content sizes during table\nlayout. This change makes more calculations use `f64` preventing a debug\nassertion from firing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 631dbaad495ee313b77383c268d339c2b1d1be05\nwpt-pr: 61530\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-tables/crashtests/table-content-size-blending-crash.html"], "git_node": "4d4eb0a47bda50aa68a51f1ed4afdb1691a6f6cf", "git_parents": ["765572b6f7e663aaa0f0b366fa22bd1561a08bdf"], "node": "ef5f65fe3e64baa466eaf2c36287e049bd61da28", "parents": ["ed7068725a28113a735065faf326066fb8dcb6d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050362 [wpt PR 60888] - wpt: Add missing message type to autoplay permission query., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nwpt: Add missing message type to autoplay permission query.\n\nSigned-off-by: Josh Matthews \u003cjosh@joshmatthews.net\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0c5e9f8e1569d66568e734a4388b2a31cf1c1390\nwpt-pr: 60888\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/permissions-policy/resources/permissions-policy-autoplay.html"], "git_node": "071d2ab21cabee92a05d81466e2bd3c5b0463776", "git_parents": ["4d4eb0a47bda50aa68a51f1ed4afdb1691a6f6cf"], "node": "62cbddf9abc2e6d4e903b822de08ec5a229726d9", "parents": ["ef5f65fe3e64baa466eaf2c36287e049bd61da28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050362 [wpt PR 60888] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 60888\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/embedde