85340293, "git_changesets": ["2d6a09b064082bfca4f19deec41b2870bcb28e0e"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "44989": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058762 - Update metadata for permissions/crashtests/permissions-query.any.js.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314854\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/permissions/crashtests/permissions-query.any.js.ini"], "git_node": "e9226a5eee5402f83199a7eff84e4959d12ad6e4", "git_parents": ["9d0c7d75f303b16930388cf1b8ef93d161d72c29"], "node": "a807d5fbceb92d3774ff4a280b34d66a32f5adcf", "parents": ["aea36f7c13cee7e70f5b27c073c11088c6e1725e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058763 - Update metadata for css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314856\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overscroll-behavior/overscroll-behavior.html.ini"], "git_node": "14f47542619728e623df5e6e3c1ccbdbd0359263", "git_parents": ["e9226a5eee5402f83199a7eff84e4959d12ad6e4"], "node": "1ab5a47f15209c0a60233ac8a23a487d6638a0ab", "parents": ["a807d5fbceb92d3774ff4a280b34d66a32f5adcf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053582 - Mask invalid values in SetCanBreakBefore. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman,shravanrn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314763\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h"], "git_node": "a2a26d27c6013b5e38e26e31038e63a820637223", "git_parents": ["14f47542619728e623df5e6e3c1ccbdbd0359263"], "node": "2e1b79f467352a1b46b3d9684eaa913db88797ce", "parents": ["1ab5a47f15209c0a60233ac8a23a487d6638a0ab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053582 - Pass glyph count in to GetDetailedGlyphs. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman,shravanrn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314764\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxFont.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFont.h", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.h", "layout/generic/nsTextFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsTextRunTransformations.cpp", "layout/mathml/nsMathMLChar.cpp", "layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp"], "git_node": "67319082a52e2f8180ff51c93cce8863ef5ffacd", "git_parents": ["a2a26d27c6013b5e38e26e31038e63a820637223"], "node": "ee2506a879f2375c703894f25de5d2c4e72c4975", "parents": ["2e1b79f467352a1b46b3d9684eaa913db88797ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053582 - Strengthen offset validation in gfxGraphiteShaper. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman,shravanrn\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314765\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxGraphiteShaper.cpp"], "git_node": "00adefbfbe6251e545322fde909f00b4954063b1", "git_parents": ["67319082a52e2f8180ff51c93cce8863ef5ffacd"], "node": "a882a80b25d5d661c9c09b37e85d1fd6f9a4d3a3", "parents": ["ee2506a879f2375c703894f25de5d2c4e72c4975"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alin lastun \u003calastun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052171 - Refactor microsurvey to use global state r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\n- Add a new global state (AppState.microsurvey) to save the survey data.\n   - If the survey ID is the same, the reducer does not change the state. This stops the app from reloading the UI again and again when we resume the fragment.\n   - Save the \"dismiss\" action globally when the user closes the survey.\n   - Delete duplicated code from BaseBrowserFragment and HomeFragment.\n   - The fragments now just look at the global state.\n   - In BaseBrowserFragment, we no longer check if the survey ID is new. We just build the container once. The reducer is what stops it from rebuilding for the same survey.\n   - In HomeFragment, Jetpack Compose connects to the new stable state. If the user closes the survey in one place, it disappears everywhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312042\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/appstate/AppState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/experiments/UninstallSurveyBottomSheetFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/HomeFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/messaging/state/MessagingReducer.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/microsurvey/MicrosurveyState.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/microsurvey/ui/MicrosurveyBottomSheetFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/messaging/state/MessagingReducerTest.kt"], "git_node": "b2d84630a534117fe93400178c50c4bcfadbefd0", "git_parents": ["00adefbfbe6251e545322fde909f00b4954063b1"], "node": "23848c14ef11618003fa965aaaffd927e230519c", "parents": ["a882a80b25d5d661c9c09b37e85d1fd6f9a4d3a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037102 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.1: Add PPrefetchRecord IPDL actor scaffolding r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,nika,kershaw\n\nPlumbing-only patch for Speculation Rules prefetch (M1, same-origin).\nAdds the PPrefetchRecord IPDL protocol, child/parent actor skeletons,\nand PWindowGlobal management. No behavior yet \u2014 Init/Cancel bodies and\nSpeculationRulesManager wiring follow in subsequent parts.\n\n- dom/ipc/PPrefetchRecord.ipdl (new): protocol definition\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchIPCTypes.ipdlh (new): shared IPDL types\n  (SpeculativePrefetchArgs) usable by PPrefetchRecord + PWindowGlobal\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchTypes.h (new): shared C++ enums (PrefetchState,\n  PrefetchAnonymizationPolicy, PrefetchSource) and ExchangeRecord\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.{h,cpp} (new): content-side actor; holds\n  URL + anon policy\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.{h,cpp} (new): parent-side actor; holds\n  prefetch record fields; empty RecvCancel/ActorDestroy\n- dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl: add 'manages PPrefetchRecord;' and\n  constructor message\n- dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.{h,cpp}: add AllocPPrefetchRecordParent\n- dom/ipc/moz.build: wire new sources\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302502\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PPrefetchRecord.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PrefetchIPCTypes.ipdlh", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchTypes.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "dom/ipc/moz.build"], "git_node": "b283608ec69b939a04ebfab2470c35c27cacc67e", "git_parents": ["b2d84630a534117fe93400178c50c4bcfadbefd0"], "node": "6e11118a126013ee2bd58101ad1efddc57a4b913", "parents": ["23848c14ef11618003fa965aaaffd927e230519c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.2: Add SpeculationRulesManager skeleton r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nEmpty DOM-side orchestrator class for Speculation Rules prefetch.\nHolds the active PrefetchRecordChild list; only RemoveRecord is\nimplemented for now. Document integration follows in Part 1.3;\nStartPrefetch / CancelPrefetch / GarbageCollect and rule parsing\nland in Part 6.\n\n- dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.{h,cpp} (new): skeleton class\n- dom/base/moz.build: wire new sources\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302503\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.h", "dom/base/moz.build"], "git_node": "cc7b215f7e4005d6b49748d057fa6aa28bad45a8", "git_parents": ["b283608ec69b939a04ebfab2470c35c27cacc67e"], "node": "d22342313972c09d6f749f1cff649770fa51ad95", "parents": ["6e11118a126013ee2bd58101ad1efddc57a4b913"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.3: Integrate SpeculationRulesManager with Document r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nAdds the lazy UniquePtr\u003cSpeculationRulesManager\u003e field on Document and\nwires PrefetchRecordChild::ActorDestroy to RemoveRecord via the\nWindow -\u003e Document chain. Records-list cleanup now happens automatically\non actor death (PWindowGlobal teardown, Send__delete__, content\nprocess crash).\n\nAlso adds a Source() accessor to PrefetchRecordParent to clear a\n-Wunused-private-field warning on mSource introduced in Part 1.1.\n\n- dom/base/Document.{h,cpp}: forward declaration, member, accessor,\n  include\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.cpp: wire ActorDestroy -\u003e RemoveRecord\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h: add Source() accessor\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302504\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.cpp"], "git_node": "1e50caebc3a9cfc907ceb0f6cee90f82718473a3", "git_parents": ["cc7b215f7e4005d6b49748d057fa6aa28bad45a8"], "node": "2e0fc7acec26dd880f732a7d1979c45ebc113e16", "parents": ["d22342313972c09d6f749f1cff649770fa51ad95"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.4: Add SpeculationRules MOZ_LOG module and prefs r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nLogging infrastructure and pref surface for Speculation Rules\nprefetch. No log calls yet.\n\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchLog.h (new): extern LazyLogModule\n  gSpeculationRulesLog + LOG_SPECRULES macros\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp: define gSpeculationRulesLog\n- dom/ipc/moz.build: export PrefetchLog.h\n\nPrefs added to modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml:\n- dom.speculation_rules.enabled (false): master switch\n- dom.speculation_rules.wait_timeout_ms (2000): navigation-wait timeout\n- dom.speculation_rules.max_records_per_document (20): records cap\n- dom.speculation_rules.max_body_bytes (5242880): body cap\n- dom.speculation_rules.record_expiry_ms (300000): record expiry\n- dom.speculation_rules.same_origin_only (true): same-origin gate\n\nEnable via: MOZ_LOG=SpeculationRules:5\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302505\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchLog.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/moz.build", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "4ea28edd5548351668dae252f0a3e4615b46e7d2", "git_parents": ["1e50caebc3a9cfc907ceb0f6cee90f82718473a3"], "node": "216561d64fb5b64bdd6a815aa49116f649c7538d", "parents": ["2e0fc7acec26dd880f732a7d1979c45ebc113e16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.5: Wire lifecycle log calls for prefetch actors and SpeculationRulesManager r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nAdds MOZ_LOG=SpeculationRules:5 visibility for the actor lifecycle and\nmanager bookkeeping wired up in Parts 1.1-1.4. Each log line carries\nthe relevant arguments (URL, anonymization policy, reason code, tag\ncount, remaining records).\n\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.cpp: log ctor + ActorDestroy\n- dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp: log RecvCancel + ActorDestroy\n- dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.cpp: log RemoveRecord\n- dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp: log AllocPPrefetchRecordParent\n  with deserialized URL + args\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302506\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp"], "git_node": "64fdd69b2a3f35144126516b7e973a79afe57086", "git_parents": ["4ea28edd5548351668dae252f0a3e4615b46e7d2"], "node": "c2766973b9e8e3eb2eaf7f0ee808ffb867abd44a", "parents": ["216561d64fb5b64bdd6a815aa49116f649c7538d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 2.1: Implement PrefetchRecordParent::Init() and streaming interfaces r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,kershaw\n\nImplements \"start a referrer-initiated navigational prefetch\":\nHTTPS gate, same-origin gate, conditional isolation setup,\nNS_NewChannelInternal with TYPE_OTHER, Sec-Purpose header, referrer\ninfo, and AsyncOpen. Adds nsIStreamListener/nsIRequestObserver/\nnsIInterfaceRequestor/nsIChannelEventSink as base classes with full\nQI. OnDataAvailable enforces the body-bytes cap via\ndom.speculation_rules.max_body_bytes pref. OnStartRequest fills\nthe redirect chain entry with response status and No-Vary-Search\nheader. AsyncOnChannelRedirect updates the redirect chain; cross-site\npartition check follows in Part 2.3.\n\nHelper functions added: IsCrossOriginToDocument,\nPopulateIsolatedPartitionKey, ConfigureSecPurpose,\nPrefetchIPAnonymizationPolicyRequiresAnonymity, AppendRedirectChainEntry,\nFillResponseOnLastEntry.\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html#start-a-referrer-initiated-navigational-prefetch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302507\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "e1eda86cd494ce45705cb43758c69d1cbaa2856c", "git_parents": ["64fdd69b2a3f35144126516b7e973a79afe57086"], "node": "b150add12928286df49d9763214d58905e921454", "parents": ["c2766973b9e8e3eb2eaf7f0ee808ffb867abd44a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 2.2: Add cross-site redirect partition-key check r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,valentin\n\nCompletes AsyncOnChannelRedirect: when a redirect crosses a site\nboundary (proposedPartitionKey != sourcePartitionKey), the prefetch\nis aborted if the referrer policy would leak too much source-page\ninformation. Strict policies (strict-origin-when-cross-origin,\nstrict-origin, same-origin, no-referrer, empty) are allowed;\nno-referrer-when-downgrade, origin, origin-when-cross-origin,\nand unsafe-url are rejected.\n\nNew helpers: ComputePartitionKeyForChannel (derives partition key\nfrom the redirected URL via OriginAttributes::SetPartitionKey),\nIsReferrerPolicySufficientlyStrict.\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html#list-of-sufficiently-strict-speculative-navigation-referrer-policies\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302508\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h"], "git_node": "e938bb5a14d65ee861b40ddc7d0e47e87ec22c3a", "git_parents": ["e1eda86cd494ce45705cb43758c69d1cbaa2856c"], "node": "35a72314a0f6a1ad2e9dace1e6312402ae5d32c9", "parents": ["b150add12928286df49d9763214d58905e921454"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 3.1: Implement RecvCancel, ActorDestroy safety net, and FirePrefetchStatusUpdated stub r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nImplements \"cancel and discard a prefetch record\": RecvCancel\nsets state=Canceled, aborts the channel, fires the prefetchstatusupdated\nfailure event stub, and notifies state-change waiters. ActorDestroy adds\na safety net that cancels the channel if the actor dies mid-flight\n(tab close, PWindowGlobal teardown, process crash).\n\n- PrefetchRecordParent: RecvCancel (idempotent guard, channel abort,\n  FirePrefetchStatusUpdated, NotifyPrefetchStateChanged); ActorDestroy\n  safety net; FirePrefetchStatusUpdated stub (BiDi wiring deferred)\n- WindowGlobalParent: NotifyPrefetchStateChanged stub (waiter logic\n  added in Part 4.2)\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html#prefetch-record-cancel-and-discard\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302509\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "7d01ece758957947ff5a7af6387435e5413a316a", "git_parents": ["e938bb5a14d65ee861b40ddc7d0e47e87ec22c3a"], "node": "afc3b868e30afff6fe42f7f1d102c8d2cae3353a", "parents": ["35a72314a0f6a1ad2e9dace1e6312402ae5d32c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 3.2: Implement OnStopRequest completion path and DedupePrefetchRecords r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nImplements \"complete a prefetch record\": OnStopRequest success path\nsets expiry (via dom.speculation_rules.record_expiry_ms pref), deduplicates\nsame-URL completed records, sets state=Completed, fires prefetchstatusupdated\nsuccess stub, and notifies state-change waiters. OnStopRequest failure path\nuses MarkCanceled and notifies waiters.\n\nAdds MarkCanceled() helper (extracted from RecvCancel) so both RecvCancel\nand DedupePrefetchRecords can share the cancel logic without code duplication.\n\nDedupePrefetchRecords marks older Completed records with the same URL as\nCanceled.\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html#prefetch-record-complete\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302510\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "ce0009f861369a57fc155b138644c52bcc23d308", "git_parents": ["7d01ece758957947ff5a7af6387435e5413a316a"], "node": "abf121c41272a15e6beb2c5c69aaaf26fe8b45ac", "parents": ["afc3b868e30afff6fe42f7f1d102c8d2cae3353a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041372 - [speculation-rules] Part 4.1: Implement navigation matching algorithms r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,kershaw\n\nImplements the synchronous navigation matching algorithms:\n\n- \"find a matching complete prefetch record\": iterates managed\n  actors, prefers exact URL match over No-Vary-Search equivalence,\n  checks expiry and conflicting credentials on every redirect chain hop.\n\n- \"prefetch record matches a URL\": exact URL equality first, then\n  No-Vary-Search variance from redirect chain[0]'s response header via\n  mozilla::net::ParseNoVarySearchHeader /\n  URLsAreEquivalentModuloVariationConfig (bug 2038006).\n\n- IsExpectedToMatch: pre-response variant using the rule's noVarySearchHint;\n  used by \"wait for a matching prefetch record\" to identify ongoing records\n  that might complete into a match.\n\n- \"conflicting credentials exist\": computes hypothetical partition\n  key for each redirect hop; same-site always returns false (M1); M2 will\n  add nsICookieManager cookie presence check for cross-site hops.\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html#find-a-matching-complete-prefetch-record\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302512\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h"], "git_node": "873c10649282de0309f61633b7d0fdf43b726946", "git_parents": ["ce0009f861369a57fc155b138644c52bcc23d308"], "node": "7b002118dccd24b0e42c47385081aee3f84f53ff", "parents": ["abf121c41272a15e6beb2c5c69aaaf26fe8b45ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041372 - [speculation-rules] Part 4.2: Implement async PrefetchMatchWaiter for the wait algorithm r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\n\nImplements \"wait for a matching prefetch record\": when navigation\narrives while a potentially matching prefetch is still ongoing,\nWaitForMatchingPrefetchRecord fast-paths to FindMatchingPrefetchRecord\n(sync), or registers a PrefetchMatchWaiter if ongoing records could\nsatisfy the URL.\n\nPrefetchMatchWaiter holds a MozPromise, an nsITimer for the\ndom.speculation_rules.wait_timeout_ms timeout, and an Atomic\u003cbool\u003e\nresolved flag to prevent double-resolution if the timer and a\nstate-change notification race.\nNotifyPrefetchStateChanged now iterates mPrefetchWaiters and calls\nOnRecordStateChanged on each.\n\nSpec: https://wicg.github.io/nav-speculation/prefetch.html#wait-for-a-matching-prefetch-record\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302513\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchMatchWaiter.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchMatchWaiter.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "dom/ipc/moz.build"], "git_node": "d67227677ad6401be9483227037777137316ea9d", "git_parents": ["873c10649282de0309f61633b7d0fdf43b726946"], "node": "e9eed82338e98694ec2339e7a21306252ce28e8f", "parents": ["7b002118dccd24b0e42c47385081aee3f84f53ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041381 - [speculation-rules] Part 5.1: Serve navigation from prefetch cache in DocumentLoadListener. r=necko-reviewers,cookie-reviewers,valentin\n\nHooks DocumentLoadListener::Open() to check for a matching prefetch record\nbefore opening the navigation channel to the network.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302514\n", "files": ["netwerk/cookie/PrefetchCookieCopier.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/PrefetchCookieCopier.h", "netwerk/cookie/moz.build", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.h"], "git_node": "c67d0357b8d7b02051c2df59a0d1530154912486", "git_parents": ["d67227677ad6401be9483227037777137316ea9d"], "node": "f7383ff051113ad7e139efb742f5a7b6be82f825", "parents": ["e9eed82338e98694ec2339e7a21306252ce28e8f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041381 - [speculation-rules] Part 5.2: Expose deliveryType=\"navigational-prefetch\" on PerformanceNavigationTiming r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,webidl,emilio,canova,saschanaz,kershaw,avandolder\n\nPropagates the activation signal from DocumentLoadListener (parent process)\nto PerformanceNavigationTiming (content process) via a new boolean on\nnsDOMNavigationTiming, which is already IPC-serialized in RedirectToRealChannelArgs.\n\nWhen a navigation is served from a speculation rules prefetch cache,\nperformance.getEntriesByType(\"navigation\")[0].deliveryType returns\n\"navigational-prefetch\" instead of the default empty string.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302516\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMNavigationTiming.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMNavigationTiming.h", "dom/performance/PerformanceMainThread.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceResourceTiming.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceResourceTiming.h", "dom/webidl/PerformanceResourceTiming.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp"], "git_node": "da473bf5d90f3ee0e954980afb5d5369d7a7dbf6", "git_parents": ["c67d0357b8d7b02051c2df59a0d1530154912486"], "node": "5b59eb009fead084354e0e40f96bc256e5941e3f", "parents": ["f7383ff051113ad7e139efb742f5a7b6be82f825"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041381 - [speculation-rules] Part 6: Integrate DOM speculation rules parser with PrefetchRecord Actors and SpeculationRules manager. r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302517\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.h", "dom/base/speculationrules/lib.rs"], "git_node": "ca0146509e5cb40a83c2ba54199e199e8f435b9f", "git_parents": ["da473bf5d90f3ee0e954980afb5d5369d7a7dbf6"], "node": "018164036aae9e4af3df9496233da936a21796ed", "parents": ["5b59eb009fead084354e0e40f96bc256e5941e3f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041381 - pass cookies storage info while creating channel in prefetch parent. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D302518\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "008ffa2ba87ae1c6d8673cac70ca725266e63166", "git_parents": ["ca0146509e5cb40a83c2ba54199e199e8f435b9f"], "node": "977e5579a7b0b9b2b3b15b9b036200b1211067c2", "parents": ["018164036aae9e4af3df9496233da936a21796ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2041381 - Enable Speculation Rules API (same-origin prefetch) for nightly. r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310767\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "8ccf29060abe0da46201895f718e22eef0f64a78", "git_parents": ["008ffa2ba87ae1c6d8673cac70ca725266e63166"], "node": "c813ad53980244c38bebbade6f49b333f6ad5308", "parents": ["977e5579a7b0b9b2b3b15b9b036200b1211067c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julian Seward \u003cjseward@acm.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058654.  r=jandem.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314845\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/arrays.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/defaultable.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/signal-null-check.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmSummarizeInsn.cpp"], "git_node": "469f25e72ab31369a3d1f1c91974308fbc213491", "git_parents": ["8ccf29060abe0da46201895f718e22eef0f64a78"], "node": "a3a2077f99ac95eee1e5a04647728ed3fcb64102", "parents": ["c813ad53980244c38bebbade6f49b333f6ad5308"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056496 - P1. Vendor application-services with autofill Store::shutdown() r=joschmidt\n\nBump the vendored application-services revision to aac41f82fd13 to pick up\nthe autofill Store::shutdown() API, which closes the store's rusqlite\nconnection synchronously (mirroring LoginStore) instead of only at GC during\nshutdown, past the late-write barrier.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314555\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/autofill.udl", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/db/mod.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/db/store.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/error.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/engine.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/tests/test_migrate_remote_address.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/autofill/src/sync/tests/test_reconcile.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/android/src/main/java/org/mozilla/experiments/nimbus/Nimbus.kt", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/metrics.yaml", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/evaluator.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/nimbus.udl", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/schema.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/stateful/dbcache.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/stateful/nimbus_client.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/targeting.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/tests/stateful/test_behavior.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/tests/stateful/test_evaluator.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/tests/stateful/test_nimbus.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/tests/stateful/test_targeting.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/src/tests/test_evaluator.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/tests/test_message_helpers.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/nimbus/tests/test_restart.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/places/src/db/db.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/places/src/storage/mod.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/src/client.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/src/service.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/remote_settings/src/storage.rs", "third_party/application-services/components/search/src/selector.rs", "third_party/application-services/docs/building.md", "third_party/application-services/docs/howtos/locally-published-components-in-fenix.md", "third_party/application-services/docs/howtos/locally-published-components-in-firefox-ios.md", "third_party/application-services/examples/cli-support/Cargo.toml", "third_party/application-services/examples/cli-support/src/fxa_creds.rs", "third_party/application-services/moz.yaml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustAutofill.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustBreachAlerts.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustContextId.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustFilterAdult.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustInitRustComponents.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustLogins.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustRelevancy.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustRemoteSettings.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustSearch.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustSuggest.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustTabs.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustTracing.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustViaduct.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/generated/RustWebextstorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/tests/generated/RustUniffiBindingsTests.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/tests/generated/RustUniffiBindingsTestsCollision.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/tests/generated/RustUniffiBindingsTestsExternalTypes.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/uniffi-js/GeneratedScaffolding.cpp"], "git_node": "a3df7349899442e3ffbd890058657f451de891eb", "git_parents": ["469f25e72ab31369a3d1f1c91974308fbc213491"], "node": "e145a8c588e85a55ae631440c30f708e93b4b315", "parents": ["a3a2077f99ac95eee1e5a04647728ed3fcb64102"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056496 - P2. Close the autofill store from a shutdown blocker and re-enable passport tests r=credential-management-reviewers,joschmidt\n\nThe Application Services autofill store's rusqlite connection was otherwise\nonly closed when its JS wrapper is garbage-collected at shutdown, which runs\nthe SQLite flush past the late-write barrier and crashes debug builds at\nLateWriteObserver.\n\nIntroduce RustAutofillStore, a new module owning the store's lifecycle: it\nopens the store lazily on first use and, on first open, registers an\nAsyncShutdown.profileChangeTeardown blocker calling the vendored\nStore::shutdown(), so the connection is closed before the late-write barrier.\nThere is one store per profile (addresses, credit cards and passports are\ncollections within it), so it is a singleton in the same shape as\nLoginManagerRustStorage: constructing it always hands back the shared\ninstance, and a second handler can never open a second connection to the\nsame file.\n\nRe-enable the Form Autofill passport tests that were disabled with\nskip-if = [\"true\"] for the LateWriteChecks crash.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314556\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/heuristics/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/test_rustStoreShutdown.js", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillStorageBase.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/RustAutofillStore.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/FormAutofillStorage.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/formautofill/default/PassportStorage.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "f6089b9bda53ae80ea8754a2029ede5a915e3747", "git_parents": ["a3df7349899442e3ffbd890058657f451de891eb"], "node": "baf3dc347e69681a2963d71a0dfa6c9f8afb588c", "parents": ["e145a8c588e85a55ae631440c30f708e93b4b315"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dimi \u003cdlee@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056496 - P3. Add signature `mode` to the quicksuggest mock Remote Settings server r=urlbar-reviewers,daisuke\n\nThe application-services bump pulls in a remote_settings client change that\nmakes the collection metadata signature's `mode` field (the signature type,\ne.g. \"p384ecdsa\") required when deserializing the server changeset response.\nThe quicksuggest test harness's mock server only emitted `signature` and\n`x5u`, so the Rust Suggest backend failed to ingest with \"missing field\n`mode`\" and returned no suggestions, failing ~34 quicksuggest tests across all\nplatforms. Emit `mode` to match real Remote Settings servers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314557\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/RemoteSettingsServer.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "03222beff2716358075de4ae8ec4214a9f10e6f2", "git_parents": ["f6089b9bda53ae80ea8754a2029ede5a915e3747"], "node": "d02a6a317ea2fd1d48273ae6908f13b32bd96d02", "parents": ["baf3dc347e69681a2963d71a0dfa6c9f8afb588c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Calixte Denizet \u003ccalixte.denizet@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058436 - Enable pdf digital signature verification by default for nightly only r=nkulatova\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314650\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/PdfJsOverridePrefs.js"], "git_node": "9d5253adaba4cab7f6d9515650b15002888d163f", "git_parents": ["03222beff2716358075de4ae8ec4214a9f10e6f2"], "node": "81a0c17c5890674224d975fea0a6f0ca01a55a27", "parents": ["d02a6a317ea2fd1d48273ae6908f13b32bd96d02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038819 - Convert toolkit/mozapps/dmgInstallHelper docs index to Markdown r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nThe sibling dmgInstallHelper.md is already Markdown; this converts the\nlast RST file in that documentation tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314841\n", "files": ["toolkit/mozapps/dmgInstallHelper/docs/index.md", "toolkit/mozapps/dmgInstallHelper/docs/index.rst"], "git_node": "b7d808f39dd6b41e7ea17750f1b0604f2b3d302f", "git_parents": ["9d5253adaba4cab7f6d9515650b15002888d163f"], "node": "a816c3870724d0d2b26c102543a7d1af30fd5f92", "parents": ["81a0c17c5890674224d975fea0a6f0ca01a55a27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2038819 - Rename the codespell lint fixture from .rst to .md\n\nThe RST documentation has been converted to Markdown, so the fixture\nshould use a file type that still exists in the tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314842\n", "files": ["tools/lint/test/files/codespell/ignore.md", "tools/lint/test/files/codespell/ignore.rst", "tools/lint/test/test_codespell.py"], "git_node": "968b6c33c1c1786b6517a9364d726b22b0967460", "git_parents": ["b7d808f39dd6b41e7ea17750f1b0604f2b3d302f"], "node": "5f224e1481d9acece86277599e4bd1c2d45f030e", "parents": ["a816c3870724d0d2b26c102543a7d1af30fd5f92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Manuel Bucher \u003cmanuel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054991 - Fix SEC_ERROR_CA_CERT_INVALID not recoverable in felt privacy r=crypto-reviewers,keeler\n\nAlso fix test that was checking for the visibility of the override button.\nThe previous error was overrideable: https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/4b4e59946a3db5ddf42ea730fc44c22a99877303/security/manager/ssl/NSSErrorsService.cpp#185,188\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314603\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutCertError_caInvalid.js", "toolkit/content/errors/cert-errors.mjs"], "git_node": "fc5694a02b1c03c2905232a2cf8cb9ddc3a64525", "git_parents": ["968b6c33c1c1786b6517a9364d726b22b0967460"], "node": "79dbdf4293d7e0dfd0a33ec743a6f865c4b991ed", "parents": ["5f224e1481d9acece86277599e4bd1c2d45f030e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Banner \u003cstandard8@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058536 - Ensure default engine changed notifications for search engines are only sent when something has changed. r=search-reviewers,scunnane\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314762\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/search/SearchService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/test_telemetry_default_changed_startup.js", "toolkit/components/search/tests/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "9dd18e56c4ceafd3fb7e94501049281dbbc5c7d2", "git_parents": ["fc5694a02b1c03c2905232a2cf8cb9ddc3a64525"], "node": "61494aa0b8cdeff65c8e4d644a797b6a139fe4c2", "parents": ["79dbdf4293d7e0dfd0a33ec743a6f865c4b991ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058512 - Update toolchain update policy documents to account for the 2-week release cycles. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nWe had a \"freeze\" policy for toolchains somehow only documented in the\nRust update policy. It used to be tied to the Soft-freezes, which were\ndiscontinued in February, but extended through the use of the string\nfreeze dates.\n\nThe general rule was that toolchains ought to be frozen 7 days before\nthe soft-freeze, which itself was 4-5 days before the merge day. That\nworked out fine when release cycles were 4 weeks, because it left a\nwindow of more than 2 weeks to update toolchains.\n\nBut with 2-week release cycles, the same rule would leave us with only\na 2-3 day window, which is too short.\n\nSo we take a middle ground, whereby we make the new toolchain freeze\nlast 7 days until merge day, leaving us with a 7-day window to update\ntoolchains within the 2-week release cycle framework.\n\nWhile here, remove the historic version data for rust releases, keeping\nthe relevant versions for the latest release and still maintained ESRs,\nand update with the new release schedule.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314661\n", "files": ["build/docs/toolchains-update-policy.md", "docs/writing-rust-code/update-policy.md"], "git_node": "c53dfb48f9fe2ca47ee7077311922ffd3366e915", "git_parents": ["9dd18e56c4ceafd3fb7e94501049281dbbc5c7d2"], "node": "bfc5fe3895c0ed885808946decb9b3acd46a307e", "parents": ["61494aa0b8cdeff65c8e4d644a797b6a139fe4c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alin lastun \u003calastun@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058401 - Fix VPN animation for Custom Tabs r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nMove `IPProtectionAction.ProxyActiveShown` dispatch to `onAnimationStarted` callback in `CustomTabBrowserToolbarMiddleware`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314832\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/CustomTabBrowserToolbarMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/CustomTabBrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "5283b464541d12a8c1c3762ed438e3eadb19879c", "git_parents": ["c53dfb48f9fe2ca47ee7077311922ffd3366e915"], "node": "244fd30095caf91c1fef7c7e535b35871475d544", "parents": ["bfc5fe3895c0ed885808946decb9b3acd46a307e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048977 - Add review-context.toml linter for AI code review context rules. r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib\n\nAdds a mozlint linter that validates review-context.toml, the file the\nbugbug code review agent reads to inject domain knowledge into the review\nprompt. The schema/grammar is vendored verbatim from bugbug so the tree\nvalidates against the same schema the agent uses at runtime; this will be\nreplaced by a pinned stdlib-only package once bugbug publishes one.\n\nExcludes the file from test-manifest-toml, which would otherwise try to\nparse it as a ManifestParser test manifest and fail.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307834\n", "files": ["pyproject.toml", "taskcluster/kinds/source-test/mozlint.yml", "tools/lint/python/review_context_schema.py", "tools/lint/python/review_context_toml.py", "tools/lint/review-context-toml.yml", "tools/lint/test-manifest-toml.yml"], "git_node": "2b87996cbb8bd4a70d2e5b5d7e832217d3483d87", "git_parents": ["5283b464541d12a8c1c3762ed438e3eadb19879c"], "node": "001ae97198539804b385c6ca3ab75b6e1d279502", "parents": ["244fd30095caf91c1fef7c7e535b35871475d544"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048977 - Add initial review-context.toml rules. r=Gijs,smaug\n\nLoads the desktop front-end and WebIDL implementation skills as review\ncontext for patches touching the matching files.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307835\n", "files": ["moz.build", "review-context.toml"], "git_node": "c865590a0ea60385775ba556d277ba032ed9bb26", "git_parents": ["2b87996cbb8bd4a70d2e5b5d7e832217d3483d87"], "node": "e485256313ffef294c232c2f16c7fc9d432bfd2b", "parents": ["001ae97198539804b385c6ca3ab75b6e1d279502"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Paul Adenot \u003cpaul@paul.cx\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048977 - Document review-context.toml authoring. r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307836\n", "files": ["docs/ai-agent-tools/code-review-context.md", "docs/ai-agent-tools/index.md"], "git_node": "52b14a5a420b6a6e47ea7f19009ce8abfb073b58", "git_parents": ["c865590a0ea60385775ba556d277ba032ed9bb26"], "node": "97bd4dbaac6365bfc4cdf47704bbcd5ea844ea7a", "parents": ["e485256313ffef294c232c2f16c7fc9d432bfd2b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056225 - Remove unimplemented  option from Services.scriptloader.loadSubScriptWithOptions. r=arai,webcompat-reviewers,ip-protection-reviewers,sstreich,dholbert,twisniewski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313208\n", "files": ["browser/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionPanel.sys.mjs", "browser/components/reportbrokensite/ReportBrokenSite.sys.mjs", "js/xpconnect/idl/mozIJSSubScriptLoader.idl"], "git_node": "664d8a16f7d7e0ab7cb65463681d90d4734b8d15", "git_parents": ["52b14a5a420b6a6e47ea7f19009ce8abfb073b58"], "node": "3d94e0af9df96501556c139b829e857f50542c5c", "parents": ["97bd4dbaac6365bfc4cdf47704bbcd5ea844ea7a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058405 - Don't handle form submission before the fields are identified. r=credential-management-reviewers,dimi\n\nFormAutofillHandler.fieldDetails throws until setIdentifiedFieldDetails() has\nbeen called, which only happens once the parent has round-tripped\nFormAutofill:OnFieldsDetected. A form submitted while that reply is in flight\nmade FormAutofillChild.formSubmitted call collectFormFilledData() and hit the\nthrowing getter.\n\nGuard formSubmitted() with the existing hasIdentifiedFields() predicate: when\nthe fields were never identified nothing was filled, so there is nothing to\ncapture. This covers the page-navigation and form-removal heuristics too, since\nboth funnel through formSubmitted().\n\nFormAutofill:GetFilledInfo had the same latent throw for subframes that have not\nbeen identified yet.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314592\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/address/browser.toml", "browser/extensions/formautofill/test/browser/address/browser_address_capture_before_fields_identified.js", "toolkit/components/formautofill/FormAutofillChild.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "6c5787611a445bf91f88273edcc0f7eca237c21c", "git_parents": ["664d8a16f7d7e0ab7cb65463681d90d4734b8d15"], "node": "4b21160c4fe71425a23aee0bb106bf5bacec678a", "parents": ["3d94e0af9df96501556c139b829e857f50542c5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058809 - Update sccache to 0.17.0 r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,glandium\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314836\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/fetch/toolchains.yml"], "git_node": "28cc1260439cee77d7ed6230e620d6ae0c5ca18b", "git_parents": ["6c5787611a445bf91f88273edcc0f7eca237c21c"], "node": "0f5932176168892ac1419a057186ca8f5d1a08ca", "parents": ["4b21160c4fe71425a23aee0bb106bf5bacec678a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2050584. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\" for causing gl failures in test_2_conformance2__extensions__ovr_multiview2_draw_buffers.html.\n\nThis reverts commit bd92d332234416ed6f648394941194d15a7a51ac.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.cpp"], "git_node": "056a65d0b2d56cf2edd6820479dbb8898fd0c72f", "git_parents": ["28cc1260439cee77d7ed6230e620d6ae0c5ca18b"], "node": "4d7a39462628599636c171c30bff0beece041a12", "parents": ["0f5932176168892ac1419a057186ca8f5d1a08ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2054991 - Fix SEC_ERROR_CA_CERT_INVALID not recoverable in felt privacy r=crypto-reviewers,keeler\" for causing mochitests failures in browser_error_registry.js.\n\nThis reverts commit fc5694a02b1c03c2905232a2cf8cb9ddc3a64525.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/about/browser_aboutCertError_caInvalid.js", "toolkit/content/errors/cert-errors.mjs"], "git_node": "d72c1ebe72b1ad1bd98b2849dc3f75e440cf2f38", "git_parents": ["056a65d0b2d56cf2edd6820479dbb8898fd0c72f"], "node": "26b784949ff22be31cec3e6cc663d6c0f628bf0f", "parents": ["4d7a39462628599636c171c30bff0beece041a12"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057724 - Sandbox - Allow /dev/udmabuf in RDD for Vulkan DMA-BUF export. r=jld,sandbox-reviewers\n\nNVIDIA EGL/Vulkan on Wayland opens /dev/udmabuf and issues UDMABUF_CREATE\n(ioctl type 'u', e.g. 0x40187542) against a sealed memfd, checking its seals\nvia fcntl(F_GET_SEALS). Without broker + seccomp access for both, the RDD\nprocess is killed and VideoBridge sees AbnormalShutdown; later reinits fail\nto create a decoder. X11 typically never hits this path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314604\n", "files": ["security/sandbox/linux/SandboxFilter.cpp", "security/sandbox/linux/broker/SandboxBrokerPolicyFactory.cpp"], "git_node": "acf7317ebe3994f16f87c9f22b71c2fcaecbb76b", "git_parents": ["d72c1ebe72b1ad1bd98b2849dc3f75e440cf2f38"], "node": "f441e5f2918b0001833cf5d27ee2bcfb5ce575c3", "parents": ["26b784949ff22be31cec3e6cc663d6c0f628bf0f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057417 - [efficiency] Convert MainMenuTest.verifyTheBookmarksMainMenuItemTest to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt,isabel_rios\n\nFaithful port of the legacy nav-\u003eclick-\u003everify smoke test: load a page, open the main menu, tap the\nBookmarks item, and verify the Bookmarks view opens. Reuses BrowserPage/MainMenuPage/BookmarksPage nav +\nMainMenuSelectors.BOOKMARKS_BUTTON; no new selectors. TestRail 3080137. Green, non-flaky (passed on try #1).\n\nParity note: the legacy test also returned to the browser and re-verified page content; that leg is omitted\nbecause the nav graph has no stateful BookmarksPage-\u003eBrowserPage return edge (logged as a harness gap for the\nstateful-nav / Pairs work).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313944\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MainMenuTest.kt"], "git_node": "0e06f964d8227ec78ab51c00c1a0591615d214ac", "git_parents": ["acf7317ebe3994f16f87c9f22b71c2fcaecbb76b"], "node": "1a74134215696c0726cc9280351d08c58cee7cb5", "parents": ["f441e5f2918b0001833cf5d27ee2bcfb5ce575c3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057419 - [efficiency] Convert expanded-toolbar main-menu/tab-tray smoke tests to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt,isabel_rios\n\nPorts two NavigationToolbarExpandedTest smoke tests into the efficiency ToolbarTest:\n- verifyTheExpandedToolbarMainMenuButtonTest: load a page, open the main menu, verify the\n  browser-view main-menu items (browserViewMainMenuItems group). TestRail 3333215.\n- verifyTheExpandedToolbarTabTrayButtonTest: load a page, open the tab tray, verify the open tab.\n  TestRail 3333214.\nBoth green, non-flaky (pass on try #1).\n\nAdds the shouldUseExpandedToolbar launch flag (BaseTest constructor arg + LaunchConfig field, defaulting\nto false so every existing subclass is unaffected) and sets it on ToolbarTest. The legacy class enables\nthis on its activity rule, so the flag is required for these ports to exercise the expanded toolbar\nrather than the default layout.\n\nAdds a BrowserPage -\u003e TabDrawerPage navigation edge: the tab counter is on the browser toolbar too,\nso this is generally reusable by any test that opens the tab tray from a loaded page. Uses the\nUIAutomator tab-counter variant to avoid Compose-sync hangs while GeckoView is active.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313945\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/NavigationToolbarExpandedTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/LaunchConfig.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/TabDrawerPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/MainMenuSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/ToolbarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/ToolbarTest.kt"], "git_node": "42c7e3fb491429fa85bf86952c5c1ccf08374627", "git_parents": ["0e06f964d8227ec78ab51c00c1a0591615d214ac"], "node": "456dbcef3a2abfe149de4184702569a5975884da", "parents": ["1a74134215696c0726cc9280351d08c58cee7cb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057411 - [efficiency] Convert recently-closed tabs delete/open smoke tests to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt,isabel_rios\n\nPorts two RecentlyClosedTabsTest smoke tests:\n- deleteRecentlyClosedTabsItemTest (TestRail 2195812)\n- openRecentlyClosedItemTest (TestRail 1065414)\nBoth green, non-flaky (pass on try #1).\n\nCapability build for the recently-closed screen (previously only the empty state was modeled):\n- RecentlyClosedTabsSelectors: add item-by-title (res-id title + text), item url (text-contains),\n  the delete/overflow button, and an always-present toolbar-title arrival signal. Move the empty-state\n  view out of requiredForPage into its own group so the page is reachable/assertable when populated.\n- RecentlyClosedTabsPage: verifyRecentlyClosedItem / openRecentlyClosedItem / deleteRecentlyClosedItem /\n  verifyEmptyRecentlyClosedList.\n- Tests reuse on.tabDrawer.closeTabWithTitle + the on.home.navigateToPage() re-sync idiom (from HomeTest)\n  to close the only tab and route to the recently-closed list.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313946\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/RecentlyClosedTabsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/RecentlyClosedTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/RecentlyClosedTabsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/RecentlyClosedTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "6fe590930dad672c4e37cbc5e325a047fd4a8181", "git_parents": ["42c7e3fb491429fa85bf86952c5c1ccf08374627"], "node": "50586dc73f23c30ef0d317b4f0b73e75d6071ed1", "parents": ["456dbcef3a2abfe149de4184702569a5975884da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057420 - [efficiency] Convert quick-settings page-connection smoke tests + trust-panel state capability r=aaronmt\n\nPorts two UnifiedTrustPanelTest smoke tests:\n- verifySecurePageConnectionFromQuickSettingsWithNoTrackersTest (TestRail 3186718)\n- verifyInsecurePageConnectionFromQuickSettingsWithTrackersTest (TestRail 3186721)\nBoth green, non-flaky (pass on try #1).\n\nShared capability (reused by these and the custom-tab connection variants still to convert):\n- UnifiedTrustPanelPage.verifyUnifiedTrustPanelItems(...): parameterized assertion of the full\n  trust-panel state (site identity, ETP banner + toggle on/off, trackers-blocked option, connection\n  security), mirroring the legacy helper; plus clickTheEnhancedTrackingProtectionOption().\n- UnifiedTrustPanelSelectors: ETP banner / toggle / trackers-blocked / connection-security / privacy-link.\n- Trust-panel nav edge now opens from secure, unsecure, OR unknown pages (the site-info button tag\n  varies with the page's security state). ToolbarSelectors gains UNSECURE/UNKNOWN site-information\n  buttons. Unblocks insecure-page trust-panel access generally.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313947\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/UnifiedTrustPanelTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/UnifiedTrustPanelPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/ToolbarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/UnifiedTrustPanelSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/UnifiedTrustPanelTest.kt"], "git_node": "8f99a978892cdfca93e57f5fb89853659e9fa5bd", "git_parents": ["6fe590930dad672c4e37cbc5e325a047fd4a8181"], "node": "326164407bf9a7ba570f761a3d364f8bd75a5d02", "parents": ["50586dc73f23c30ef0d317b4f0b73e75d6071ed1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057412 - [efficiency] Add custom-tab launch capability + convert verifyCustomTabMenuItemsTest r=aaronmt,isabel_rios\n\nCustom tabs run in their own activity (CustomTabActivity), launched by an intent rather than an in-app\nnav path. Adds that as a reusable harness capability:\n- CustomTabsPage.launchCustomTab(url, customMenuItem): fires createCustomTabIntent at IntentReceiverActivity\n  (FLAG_ACTIVITY_NEW_TASK), waits for the custom-tab toolbar, sets page state. No NavigationRegistry edge --\n  custom tabs are launch-reached (this removes the previous illegal empty-steps edge). Plus openMainMenu().\n- CustomTabsSelectors: device-level (UIAutomator) locators so they resolve across the activity switch --\n  redesigned-toolbar menu button (\"More options\"), close button (\"Return to previous app\"), and main-menu items.\n- PageContext gains on.customTabs.\n\nConverts CustomTabsTest.verifyCustomTabMenuItemsTest (TestRail 249644). Green, non-flaky.\nUnlocks the rest of the custom-tab family + the custom-tab connection variants (reuse the trust-panel verifier).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313948\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/CustomTabsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageContext.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CustomTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/CustomTabsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "f2caae15afd516ac4dc9bb4639ea306779802182", "git_parents": ["8f99a978892cdfca93e57f5fb89853659e9fa5bd"], "node": "88b299e4a39ce3ba80527b5675c01fa0d5ece63b", "parents": ["326164407bf9a7ba570f761a3d364f8bd75a5d02"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057416 - [efficiency] Convert CustomTabsTest.openCustomTabInFirefoxTest to ui/efficiency r=isabel_rios\n\nReuses the custom-tab launch capability: launch a custom tab, verify the close button, open the menu,\ntap \"Open in Firefox\", and confirm the page opens in the full browser with one open tab.\nTestRail 249645. Green, non-flaky.\n\nAdds ToolbarSelectors.TAB_COUNTER_WITH_COUNT(openTabs) so the legacy verifyTabCounter(\"1\") assertion\ncarries over. UIAutomator-backed rather than Compose: it is asserted on BrowserPage while GeckoView is\nactive, where Compose sync can hang.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313949\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/CustomTabsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/ToolbarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "42177aeb349f585e0dd2020b7c89fab1d12fca45", "git_parents": ["f2caae15afd516ac4dc9bb4639ea306779802182"], "node": "2a91cbfef4fbb926937b733b0a5d6322e47f16d9", "parents": ["88b299e4a39ce3ba80527b5675c01fa0d5ece63b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057415 - [efficiency] Add on-demand screen-dump dev tool (Compose + native/UIAutomator) r=isabel_rios\n\nScreenDump.dumpUiAutomator(): native View-hierarchy snapshot (res-id / text / content-desc / clickable)\ncomplementing the existing Compose dump. Needed to author UIAUTOMATOR_*/ESPRESSO_* selectors for legacy\nView screens (RecyclerViews, res-id widgets) that never appear in the Compose semantics tree \u2014 e.g. the\nrecently-closed screen dumps 0 Compose nodes but its res-ids (recently_closed_empty_view, etc.) show here.\n\nEffScreenDumpRunner (devtools): navigates to a page by PageContext property (instrumentation arg\neffdump.page) and emits both dumps, so selectors are authored from ground truth instead of stale legacy\nrobots. Graph-navigable pages only.\n\nThe TAE flank config (arm-tae-tests.yml) scans the whole efficiency.devtools package, so dumpPage is\ngated with assumeFalse(isTestLab()): skipped on Firebase, still runnable by hand from Android Studio or\nthe command line. @Ignore would have blocked the manual runs this tool exists for.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313950\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/EffScreenDumpRunner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ScreenDump.kt"], "git_node": "57592225ef4926d9ebcd574f4309960b88e9dc2c", "git_parents": ["42177aeb349f585e0dd2020b7c89fab1d12fca45"], "node": "4ecc6de891728d1d56277832e644d18d7cfef3da", "parents": ["2a91cbfef4fbb926937b733b0a5d6322e47f16d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057418 - [efficiency] Add Espresso in-process view-tree dump to ScreenDump/effdump r=aaronmt,isabel_rios\n\nScreenDump.dumpEspresso(): walks the foreground activity's View hierarchy via an Espresso root ViewAction,\nlogging id / class / text / hint / content-desc / clickable with nesting. Complements the Compose and\nUIAutomator dumps: Espresso sees id-less views and View classes/structure the accessibility (UIAutomator)\ntree omits -- validated on the recently-closed screen (id-less toolbar title, recently_closed_list\nRecyclerView, LibrarySiteItemView row, nesting). EffScreenDumpRunner now emits all three (compose /\nespresso / uiautomator), matching the framework's Espresso-first preference for res-ids on Views.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313951\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/EffScreenDumpRunner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ScreenDump.kt"], "git_node": "760cc9a46818ffbff876f53045917f4e2071f207", "git_parents": ["57592225ef4926d9ebcd574f4309960b88e9dc2c"], "node": "94425f15ddc300f9c4df9299c326f1c9d93e2d84", "parents": ["4ecc6de891728d1d56277832e644d18d7cfef3da"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057421 - [efficiency] Convert verifyClearCookiesAndSiteDataFromQuickSettingsInCustomTabsTest to ui/efficiency r=isabel_rios\n\nReuses the custom-tab launch capability + the trust-panel clear-cookies verify. Adds one edge: CustomTabsPage\n-\u003e UnifiedTrustPanelPage via the custom-tab toolbar \"Site information\" button (CustomTabsSelectors.SITE_INFO_BUTTON).\nTestRail 3186714. Green first try, non-flaky.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313952\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/UnifiedTrustPanelTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/UnifiedTrustPanelPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/CustomTabsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/UnifiedTrustPanelTest.kt"], "git_node": "dc7954f986ab8f11fa706e90e6cd75f4fbb0ddf7", "git_parents": ["760cc9a46818ffbff876f53045917f4e2071f207"], "node": "ce03521defc213b58d3b25b3de8fba86448d3b2a", "parents": ["94425f15ddc300f9c4df9299c326f1c9d93e2d84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057414 - [efficiency] Convert custom-tab back/forward-from-menu smoke tests to ui/efficiency r=aaronmt\n\nAdds web-content interaction to CustomTabsPage (clickWebContent / verifyWebContent), reusing the\ndevice-level BrowserPageSelectors.PAGE_CONTENT locator (GeckoView content is matched device-wide, so it\nworks inside a custom tab). Converts, reusing custom-tab launch + MENU_BACK / MENU_FORWARD:\n- verifyTheMainMenuBackButtonFromCustomTabTest (TestRail 3080096)\n- verifyTheMainMenuForwardButtonFromCustomTabTest (TestRail 3080097)\nBoth green first try.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313953\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/CustomTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "0659130c597b6224f96447562ff7401b3ff33b36", "git_parents": ["dc7954f986ab8f11fa706e90e6cd75f4fbb0ddf7"], "node": "2972b00b911d59cfdb35738b647ba159b982ac83", "parents": ["ce03521defc213b58d3b25b3de8fba86448d3b2a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057413 - [efficiency] Convert insecure-connection-in-custom-tab test + harden trust-panel website selectors r=isabel_rios\n\nConverts UnifiedTrustPanelTest.verifyInsecurePageConnectionFromQuickSettingsWithNoTrackersInCustomTabsTest\n(TestRail 3186711) -- pure reuse of custom-tab launch + the CustomTabsPage-\u003etrust-panel site-info edge +\nverifyUnifiedTrustPanelItems (no new capability).\n\nHardening: WEBSITE_TITLE / WEBSITE_URL now match the unique testTags (unified.trust.panel.website[.url])\n*and* the expected text, via a new COMPOSE_BY_TAG_AND_TEXT strategy. Text alone was ambiguous because the\nhost also renders in the address bar (gotcha A7); the tag alone would have stopped asserting which site\nthe panel describes. Matching both keeps the disambiguation and the content assertion, and fixes it for\nevery trust-panel test. Full UnifiedTrustPanelTest re-verified green (5 tests).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313954\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/UnifiedTrustPanelTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/Selector.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/UnifiedTrustPanelSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/UnifiedTrustPanelTest.kt"], "git_node": "ce7b780b459390d6658d32b53dd1a0b7ff2a4274", "git_parents": ["0659130c597b6224f96447562ff7401b3ff33b36"], "node": "24357325ee3dbc8aa68586f55d1760c5c06763d3", "parents": ["2972b00b911d59cfdb35738b647ba159b982ac83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057409 - [efficiency] Convert find-in-page-in-custom-tab smoke test to ui/efficiency r=isabel_rios\n\nAdds a CustomTabsPage -\u003e FindInPagePage nav edge (custom-tab menu -\u003e Find in page). Converts\nverifyTheFindInPageMenuItemInACustomTabTest (TestRail 3080101). Green first try.\n\nCarries over the legacy next/prev cycling (1/3 .. 3/3 and back) via FindInPagePage.verifyFindInPageElement,\nthe next/prev/close button assertions, and a FIND_IN_PAGE_BAR check that the bar is gone after closing.\n\nParity gap: the legacy test then reopened find-in-page, searched \"3\" for a 1/1 result and closed with the\ndevice back button. That leg is omitted -- closing the bar returns to the custom tab but leaves\nPageStateTracker on FindInPagePage, and there is no return edge to re-sync it, so navigateToPage() would\nlook for a FindInPagePage -\u003e FindInPagePage path. Logged as the same stateful-nav harness gap as\nBookmarksPage -\u003e BrowserPage, not a locator issue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313955\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/MainMenuTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/FindInPagePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/FindInPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/CustomTabsTest.kt"], "git_node": "1a0fa2031efea39de157bd8b482c3171c033932b", "git_parents": ["ce7b780b459390d6658d32b53dd1a0b7ff2a4274"], "node": "8d94c6f56e4fd53e3f8d12406e6c22c73e5270a2", "parents": ["24357325ee3dbc8aa68586f55d1760c5c06763d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057407 - [efficiency] Logins capability + convert verifyNeverSaveLoginOptionTest r=isabel_rios\n\nFoundational logins capability (reused by the logins/autofill family + login-save-in-custom-tab):\n- BrowserPageSelectors: SUBMIT_LOGIN_BUTTON (web form submit; raw web DOM id via the raw-resourceId\n  strategy, no package prefix) + SAVE_LOGIN_PROMPT (app res-id feature_prompt_login_fragment).\n- BrowserPage: clickSubmitLoginButton / verifySaveLoginPromptIsDisplayed / verifySaveLoginPromptIsNotDisplayed.\n- SettingsSavePasswords: NEVER_SAVE_OPTION + clickNeverSaveOption(); plus a SettingsSavePasswordsPage -\u003e\n  HomePage back-edge (up-button chain) so a test can set a passwords option then load a page (home-\u003ebrowser).\n\nConverts LoginsTest.verifyNeverSaveLoginOptionTest (TestRail 517818) into SettingsPasswordsTest. Green.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313956\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/LoginsTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSavePasswordsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSavePasswordsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsPasswordsTest.kt"], "git_node": "d320dafdd616708549366fee75b4c1c344478c69", "git_parents": ["1a0fa2031efea39de157bd8b482c3171c033932b"], "node": "5f0d037fa9f9ae7438fff23fc0695771c759892f", "parents": ["8d94c6f56e4fd53e3f8d12406e6c22c73e5270a2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057954 - [efficiency] Add res-id-containing-text & web-id-and-text selector strategies and auto-dismiss blocking system overlays r=aaronmt\n\nTwo UIAutomator selector strategies mirroring legacy MatcherHelper matchers that no\nefficiency strategy covered:\n- UIAUTOMATOR_WITH_RES_ID_CONTAINING_TEXT: package-prefixed app res-id + textContains.\n- UIAUTOMATOR_WITH_WEB_ID_AND_TEXT: raw web DOM id + exact text (web/GeckoView content).\n\nAdds OverlayRegistry + BasePage.dismissKnownOverlaysIfPresent(), auto-invoked by\nmozClick/mozVerify on a locate miss (dismiss + retry once) so a system dialog covering\nthe app (e.g. the Android stylus-handwriting prompt) cannot masquerade as\nelement-not-found. Seeded with the stylus prompt.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314453\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/OverlayRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/Selector.kt"], "git_node": "e30cbf77e00d80ff07d49cd0cb2ed831b3f87655", "git_parents": ["d320dafdd616708549366fee75b4c1c344478c69"], "node": "cda30849eb4e301b6b8afaa2ccb7d26afb4a4729", "parents": ["5f0d037fa9f9ae7438fff23fc0695771c759892f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057955 - [efficiency] Emit all layers plus a window/focus summary on ScreenDump failure r=isabel_rios\n\nOn a locate failure ScreenDump now emits Compose + UIAutomator + Espresso layers plus a\n[windows] summary (window titles/types, IME/overlay flags, focused input) instead of\nCompose only. This surfaces system dialogs, legacy Views, and the soft keyboard that sit\non top of the app and cause spurious \"element not found\" failures, letting an author tell\n\"covered / focus stolen\" from \"genuinely absent\" from the report alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314454\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/ScreenDump.kt"], "git_node": "336a5231046ec041ce4072ffc72198a363f4f50f", "git_parents": ["e30cbf77e00d80ff07d49cd0cb2ed831b3f87655"], "node": "3ceb9284e8b0f936dd79c2380d835b4ae0327ed0", "parents": ["cda30849eb4e301b6b8afaa2ccb7d26afb4a4729"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057956 - [efficiency] BaseTest: clear autofill state between retry attempts r=isabel_rios\n\nClears saved autofill addresses at the start of every attempt in the retry rule, inside the same\nDispatchers.IO block as the existing session-storage cleanup (getAllAddresses/deleteAddress are suspend\nstorage calls, so they belong off the runBlocking thread alongside it).\n\nA leftover address from a failed first attempt changes the Autofill settings layout and can push\n\"Add address\" off-screen, so a one-off failure would otherwise turn into a retry that fails for a\ndifferent reason and hides the original cause.\n\nBest-effort (runCatching) so a storage error never fails the attempt on its own, but the failure is\nlogged rather than swallowed: silently failing to clear is indistinguishable from a state leak, which\nis exactly the condition this is meant to prevent.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314455\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt"], "git_node": "3d88a589f14a2b5ab2f6dab5d8ea65c69db2f503", "git_parents": ["336a5231046ec041ce4072ffc72198a363f4f50f"], "node": "52c025028dffa5b3f278d30b27ebade01cac1cc8", "parents": ["3ceb9284e8b0f936dd79c2380d835b4ae0327ed0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057957 - [efficiency] Convert verifyTheExpandedToolbarNewTabButtonTest to ui/efficiency r=isabel_rios\n\nFaithful port of legacy NavigationToolbarExpandedTest.verifyTheExpandedToolbarNewTabButtonTest\nonto ui/efficiency (launches with the expanded toolbar, taps the new-tab button, verifies\nthe search/edit view opens).\n\nCarries over every legacy assertion: page content after load, the search view opening in edit mode, the\n\"Search or enter address\" placeholder, and keyboard visibility.\n\nTwo supporting additions:\n- SearchBarSelectors.SEARCH_BAR_PLACEHOLDER - the placeholder is exposed as the address bar's\n  content-description rather than as text, keyed off R.string.search_hint.\n- BasePage.mozIsKeyboardVisible() / mozVerifyKeyboardVisible() - reads the accessibility window list for\n  an IME window instead of shelling out to `dumpsys input_method` and grepping its output the way the\n  legacy AppAndSystemHelper.verifyKeyboardVisibility does. Shared on BasePage so it is reusable rather\n  than another page-local copy of the same window-type check.\n\nTestRail: https://mozilla.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/3333213\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314456\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/NavigationToolbarExpandedTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SearchBarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/ToolbarTest.kt"], "git_node": "fcd244789bf6ae9330adbcaf77e2ebc8093f0582", "git_parents": ["3d88a589f14a2b5ab2f6dab5d8ea65c69db2f503"], "node": "6acebfe8e2049533d2d7da82ed1ccccd4d49b0d3", "parents": ["52c025028dffa5b3f278d30b27ebade01cac1cc8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057958 - [efficiency] Convert verifyAddressAutofillTest to ui/efficiency r=isabel_rios\n\nFaithful port of legacy AddressAutofillTest.verifyAddressAutofillTest: add and save an\naddress in Settings \u003e Autofill, load the web address form, trigger the autofill prompt,\nselect the saved address, and verify the street field autofills. Adds SettingsAutofill\naddress-form page/selectors and BrowserPage web-autofill helpers.\n\nAddress values live in a new ui/efficiency/data/AddressTestData rather than inline in the test. The same\nstreet/city/zip are typed into the settings form, matched in the suggestion list and asserted in the\nautofilled web field, so those uses have to agree \u2014 and the next autofill test will need the same\nfixture. AddressDetails is an immutable data class; the legacy equivalents\n(AddressAutofillTest.FirstAddressAutofillDetails) are objects of `var`s, where one test mutating a field\nsilently changes what every other test fills in.\n\nSettingsAutofillPage.fillAndSaveAddress now takes an AddressDetails instead of eight positional strings,\nand its waitForKeyboardDismiss reuses BasePage.mozIsKeyboardVisible() (added in bug 2057957) rather than\nrepeating the IME window-type check.\n\nTestRail: https://mozilla.testrail.io/index.php?/cases/view/3205329\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314457\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/AddressAutofillTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/data/AddressTestData.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsAutofillPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsAutofillSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/AddressAutofillTest.kt"], "git_node": "2bdea7ea9a3dc9b57127a92b845b666afbf83814", "git_parents": ["fcd244789bf6ae9330adbcaf77e2ebc8093f0582"], "node": "218fb25397380b04197813e8007c2f8eb454d282", "parents": ["6acebfe8e2049533d2d7da82ed1ccccd4d49b0d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057959 - [efficiency] Add in-tree harness docs and an interactive-inspect devtool r=isabel_rios,aaronmt\n\nAdds in-tree documentation for the ui/efficiency harness (docs/ + docs/guides/) and an\nInteractiveInspectTest devtool for exploring the live UI tree across layers.\n\nBoth devtool methods gate on assumeFalse(isTestLab()): the TAE flank config (arm-tae-tests.yml) scans the\nwhole efficiency.devtools package, and inspect() polls a trigger file for 30 minutes, which would\notherwise occupy a Firebase device slot on every TAE run. They stay runnable by hand from Android Studio\nor the command line, which @Ignore would have prevented.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314458\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/InteractiveInspectTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/README.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/architecture.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/converting-a-test.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/gotchas.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/adding-navigation.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/authoring-selectors.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/creating-a-page-object.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/debugging-tests.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/discovering-selectors.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/extending-basepage.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/guides/writing-a-test.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/docs/tooling.md"], "git_node": "2c4de866daeb3fa3a92a427802d505a122f79ea9", "git_parents": ["2bdea7ea9a3dc9b57127a92b845b666afbf83814"], "node": "74920ebc3ad08409e6b236059933cda8d4b54b5f", "parents": ["218fb25397380b04197813e8007c2f8eb454d282"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jackie Johnson \u003cjajohnson@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058263 - [efficiency] Add effview interactive selector discovery tool r=isabel_rios\n\nVisual tool for finding selectors during test authoring: click any element on a screenshot of the current\nscreen and see every matching selector across the Compose, Espresso and UIAutomator layers, ranked by\nstability (testTag \u003e res-id \u003e content-desc \u003e text) with a copy-pasteable catalog entry.\n\nRenders the artifacts ScreenDump.dumpAll() writes (bug 2057955) into an HTML overlay: elements boxed on\nthe screenshot, colour-coded by layer, with overlap detection so a tap on stacked elements lists all of\nthem rather than only the topmost. effview.sh is the one-command wrapper \u2014 trigger a fresh dump, pull the\nJSON + PNG with run-as, render, open.\n\nPairs with InteractiveInspectTest#inspect (bug 2057959), which keeps the app alive for interactive\nexploration so a dump can be taken per screen without a rebuild.\n\n  cd mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview\n  ./effview.sh              # or ./effview.sh --no-trigger after InteractiveInspectTest#dumpOnce\n\nOutput goes to ./eff-view relative to the working directory; set OUT to write it somewhere outside the\ncheckout.\n\nSee devtools/effview/README.md for complete documentation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314459\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview/README.md", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview/effview.sh", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview/effviewdump-v2.py", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/effview/example_effview.png"], "git_node": "74687ec17a92aa83fdb8356e1fa36c38608b5c4f", "git_parents": ["2c4de866daeb3fa3a92a427802d505a122f79ea9"], "node": "9d2b45556b6bd99bc8969d825947680869aa5e26", "parents": ["74920ebc3ad08409e6b236059933cda8d4b54b5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057509 - Add a way to run a wrench test case with different device pixel scales. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314014\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/aa/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/backface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/blend/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/boxshadow/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/crash/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/mask/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/performance/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/split/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/reftest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "15c8ebdc7193c3b8b2bed13a35493720c1643c41", "git_parents": ["74687ec17a92aa83fdb8356e1fa36c38608b5c4f"], "node": "80eaa0424dc605082ebce9fcbfa73d082d49d134", "parents": ["9d2b45556b6bd99bc8969d825947680869aa5e26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057509 - Allow per-scale wrench reference images. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nWith this change, when wrench loads a reference for a test run a certain scale (say 0.5), it will first look for foo-scale:0.5.png and fall back to foo.png if the former does not exist.\nThis enables declaring reftest at multiple scales and png reference images in a single line for example scale(1, 2, 0.5) == foo.yaml foo.png.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314024\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale0.51.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale1.51.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale2.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/reftest.rs"], "git_node": "351e76d06c6792ca615f731745872d5085779c86", "git_parents": ["15c8ebdc7193c3b8b2bed13a35493720c1643c41"], "node": "a48071e36852adcb660aa75b144b3c815a67bfb9", "parents": ["80eaa0424dc605082ebce9fcbfa73d082d49d134"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 299116 - Require user activation for opening mailto without prompt. r=Gijs,dom-core-reviewers,edgar\n\nOnly web content has to prove user activation to take the silent-launch\nshortcut. Chrome- and extension-triggered loads are exempt, matching the\n\"Add-on principals are always allowed\" carve-out already in\nnsExternalHelperAppService::LoadURI.\n\nnsIExternalProtocolService::loadURI takes aHasValidUserGestureActivation as\nan optional argument, and privileged callers leave it unset, so gating on it\nalone made every chrome-initiated load look gesture-less. That broke\n\"Email Link\" in the File menu, and hung the talos twinopen and damp suites:\nboth register a WebExtension protocol_handlers entry and testing/profiles/perf\nsets network.protocol-handler.external.ext+{damp,twinopen}, so the pageloader's\nchrome navigation to ext+damp:/ext+twinopen: stalled on the permission dialog\nuntil the task hit its max runtime.\n\nThe exemption is applied in both halves so they cannot drift: the prompt\ndecision in nsContentDispatchChooser._hasProtocolHandlerPermission, and the\nactivation consumption in SchemeRequiresUserActivationToLaunch, which now\ntakes the triggering principal.\n\ntest_mailto_without_user_activation_prompts drove the navigation by assigning\ncontent.location from a SpecialPowers sandbox. That sandbox is chrome and has\nno incumbent window, so LocationBase::Navigate attributed the load to the\nsystem principal - it was never testing web content. It now injects page\nscript instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312286\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLFormElement.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "toolkit/mozapps/handling/ContentDispatchChooser.sys.mjs", "uriloader/exthandler/nsExternalHelperAppService.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/nsExternalHelperAppService.h", "uriloader/exthandler/nsIContentDispatchChooser.idl", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser.toml", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser_first_prompt_not_blocked_without_user_interaction.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser_mailto_user_activation.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser_protocol_ask_dialog.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/head.js"], "git_node": "8fb766fb5e96bc29bfa9a6a0c8f5c510369761b3", "git_parents": ["351e76d06c6792ca615f731745872d5085779c86"], "node": "b3eddff25d3018f55ddbbfdd929d107006ff36d9", "parents": ["a48071e36852adcb660aa75b144b3c815a67bfb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057509 - Allow per-scale wrench reference images. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\" for causing wrench bustages.\n\nThis reverts commit 351e76d06c6792ca615f731745872d5085779c86.\n\nThis reverts commit 15c8ebdc7193c3b8b2bed13a35493720c1643c41.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/aa/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/backface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/blend/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/boxshadow/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/crash/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale0.51.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale1.51.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale2.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/mask/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/performance/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/split/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/reftest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "0b1b47e63659cb5c1f2b9c8440366c3df81d9aeb", "git_parents": ["8fb766fb5e96bc29bfa9a6a0c8f5c510369761b3"], "node": "4996e618631f02722f5a25110f87c2912dcedb45", "parents": ["b3eddff25d3018f55ddbbfdd929d107006ff36d9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert (Bug 2037102, Bug 2037103, Bug 2041008, Bug 2041372, Bug 2041381) for causing multiple wpt failures\n\nThis reverts commit 8ccf29060abe0da46201895f718e22eef0f64a78.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041381 - pass cookies storage info while creating channel in prefetch parent. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\"\n\nThis reverts commit 008ffa2ba87ae1c6d8673cac70ca725266e63166.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041381 - [speculation-rules] Part 6: Integrate DOM speculation rules parser with PrefetchRecord Actors and SpeculationRules manager. r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit ca0146509e5cb40a83c2ba54199e199e8f435b9f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041381 - [speculation-rules] Part 5.2: Expose deliveryType=\"navigational-prefetch\" on PerformanceNavigationTiming r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,webidl,emilio,canova,saschanaz,kershaw,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit da473bf5d90f3ee0e954980afb5d5369d7a7dbf6.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041381 - [speculation-rules] Part 5.1: Serve navigation from prefetch cache in DocumentLoadListener. r=necko-reviewers,cookie-reviewers,valentin\"\n\nThis reverts commit c67d0357b8d7b02051c2df59a0d1530154912486.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041372 - [speculation-rules] Part 4.2: Implement async PrefetchMatchWaiter for the wait algorithm r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit d67227677ad6401be9483227037777137316ea9d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041372 - [speculation-rules] Part 4.1: Implement navigation matching algorithms r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 873c10649282de0309f61633b7d0fdf43b726946.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 3.2: Implement OnStopRequest completion path and DedupePrefetchRecords r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit ce0009f861369a57fc155b138644c52bcc23d308.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 3.1: Implement RecvCancel, ActorDestroy safety net, and FirePrefetchStatusUpdated stub r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7d01ece758957947ff5a7af6387435e5413a316a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 2.2: Add cross-site redirect partition-key check r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,valentin\"\n\nThis reverts commit e938bb5a14d65ee861b40ddc7d0e47e87ec22c3a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2037103 - [speculation-rules] Part 2.1: Implement PrefetchRecordParent::Init() and streaming interfaces r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit e1eda86cd494ce45705cb43758c69d1cbaa2856c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.5: Wire lifecycle log calls for prefetch actors and SpeculationRulesManager r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit 64fdd69b2a3f35144126516b7e973a79afe57086.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.4: Add SpeculationRules MOZ_LOG module and prefs r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4ea28edd5548351668dae252f0a3e4615b46e7d2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.3: Integrate SpeculationRulesManager with Document r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\"\n\nThis reverts commit 1e50caebc3a9cfc907ceb0f6cee90f82718473a3.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2041008 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.2: Add SpeculationRulesManager skeleton r=dom-core-reviewers,avandolder\"\n\nThis reverts commit cc7b215f7e4005d6b49748d057fa6aa28bad45a8.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2037102 - [speculation-rules] Part 1.1: Add PPrefetchRecord IPDL actor scaffolding r=dom-core-reviewers,necko-reviewers,avandolder,nika,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit b283608ec69b939a04ebfab2470c35c27cacc67e.\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRulesManager.h", "dom/base/moz.build", "dom/base/nsDOMNavigationTiming.cpp", "dom/base/nsDOMNavigationTiming.h", "dom/base/speculationrules/lib.rs", "dom/ipc/PPrefetchRecord.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PWindowGlobal.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PrefetchIPCTypes.ipdlh", "dom/ipc/PrefetchLog.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchMatchWaiter.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchMatchWaiter.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordChild.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/PrefetchRecordParent.h", "dom/ipc/PrefetchTypes.h", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.h", "dom/ipc/moz.build", "dom/performance/PerformanceMainThread.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceResourceTiming.cpp", "dom/performance/PerformanceResourceTiming.h", "dom/webidl/PerformanceResourceTiming.webidl", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/cookie/PrefetchCookieCopier.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/PrefetchCookieCopier.h", "netwerk/cookie/moz.build", "netwer