d1532bbc5fd90d84cafc1e65e04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007174: Add WebTransportDatagramsWritable to interface exposure lists r=webidl,dom-worker-reviewers,emilio,edenchuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314814\n", "files": ["dom/serviceworkers/test/test_serviceworker_interfaces.js", "dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js", "dom/workers/test/test_worker_interfaces.js"], "git_node": "cccf383abbebc2ebe38ef3ddc51af6caf04be831", "git_parents": ["6fe877216144603cabdd029c4c8c1cf0d0b88204"], "node": "1e9b817b8ffc9261ed77e2d2fca16c7e3edd8ac6", "parents": ["f2442344eef62ec1f24bd5cdfc26c22d80f3c24c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007174: Add createWritable() to WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream r=saschanaz,webidl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D277252\n", "files": ["dom/webidl/WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.webidl", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransport.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.cpp", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportDatagramDuplexStream.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportDatagramsWritable.cpp", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportDatagramsWritable.h", "dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportSendGroup.h"], "git_node": "6d58b4f42a867e52f0f3aeb3fcf38eb75695d526", "git_parents": ["cccf383abbebc2ebe38ef3ddc51af6caf04be831"], "node": "95d8c0a729c85462e5b3f0dc48519d577bab1dd9", "parents": ["1e9b817b8ffc9261ed77e2d2fca16c7e3edd8ac6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Randell Jesup \u003crjesup@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2007174: Add WPTs for createWritable r=jib\n\nThe 'ready to use before session is established' subtest hits the\npre-existing single-slot mWaitConnect queue (Bug 1822138): createWritable()\n(landed just before this point) lets write_N_datagrams() issue several\nconcurrent early writes, and all but the last are silently dropped, hanging\nthe promise until the harness times out. That aborts the remaining\noutgoingMaxBufferedDatagrams/incomingMaxBufferedDatagrams/MaxBufferedDatagrams\nsubtests in the same global (NOTRUN) and can push the whole-file status to\nTIMEOUT.\n\nThis is fixed for real by the later 'Allow more than one datagram to be\nqueued waiting for connection to open' patch. Until the stack reaches that\npoint, mark TIMEOUT/NOTRUN as expected here so ./mach wpt reports no\nunexpected results.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D280254\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/datagram-bad-chunk.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/datagrams.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/idlharness.https.sub.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webtransport/sendgroup.https.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/datagrams-writable.https.any.js"], "git_node": "0c97c67ac0a117ec92d713df4174539709617759", "git_parents": ["6d58b4f42a867e52f0f3aeb3fcf38eb75695d526"], "node": "13e954c140f22a47f125a7ee5f898b1d0599ab88", "parents": ["95d8c0a729c85462e5b3f0dc48519d577bab1dd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058891 - Make #hash based content selection work on about:policies. r=mkaply\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314909\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/content/aboutPolicies.js"], "git_node": "071049fcca0f1dae26706922b3a848aed49206b1", "git_parents": ["0c97c67ac0a117ec92d713df4174539709617759"], "node": "406295b89f794c7d6822451c3e49733f30d85cb7", "parents": ["13e954c140f22a47f125a7ee5f898b1d0599ab88"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057530 - Skip the PopupNotification window-move security delay test on Wayland. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs\n\nbrowser_popupNotification_security_delay.js was skipped on linux 22.04 opt with\nthe Nova design enabled, but Nova is incidental: `mach manifest skip-fails`\nderives its condition from the failing job's mozinfo, and every linux2204\nbrowser-chrome platform is Wayland with Nova on by default. A control run with\nbrowser.nova.enabled=false fails identically.\n\ntest_notificationWindowMove calls window.moveTo() and then waits for the panel's\n\"popuppositioned\" event. On Wayland a client can't position its own toplevel, so\nthe gtk_window_move() in nsWindow::NativeMoveResize does nothing, the panel's\nscreen rect never changes, nsMenuPopupFrame never dispatches the event, and the\ntest times out.\n\nSkip that task on Wayland, as browser_popup_linux_move.js already does for window\nmoves, and drop the manifest skip so the other three tasks run there again.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314912\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/popupNotifications/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/popupNotifications/browser_popupNotification_security_delay.js"], "git_node": "fccde1fb92745ea6dd030bf1ce6d5c03122a1603", "git_parents": ["071049fcca0f1dae26706922b3a848aed49206b1"], "node": "ce7e996843a6ac52c321f0f74f3b9a574970ff9c", "parents": ["406295b89f794c7d6822451c3e49733f30d85cb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Apply cargo fmt; r=emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nApply cargo fmt to existing code to reduce unrelated formatting changes in\nfollow-up patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314834\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/values/computed/image.rs"], "git_node": "abcb2cb48be643fa92567593ac9629c279381f3a", "git_parents": ["fccde1fb92745ea6dd030bf1ce6d5c03122a1603"], "node": "edca742566534624b9d132e8943e7107e154660d", "parents": ["ce7e996843a6ac52c321f0f74f3b9a574970ff9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057509 - Add a way to run a wrench test case with different device pixel scales. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314014\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/aa/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/backface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/blend/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/border/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/boxshadow/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor-surface/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/compositor/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/crash/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/mask/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/performance/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/split/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/tiles/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/reftest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "ded2ffd3c866d418a35a79dbcb82c1a12bee036d", "git_parents": ["abcb2cb48be643fa92567593ac9629c279381f3a"], "node": "8c7fe5bd88e64a7a947b44bf73d537841c5d9bf0", "parents": ["edca742566534624b9d132e8943e7107e154660d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057509 - Allow per-scale wrench reference images. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nWith this change, when wrench loads a reference for a test run a certain scale (say 0.5), it will first look for foo-scale:0.5.png and fall back to foo.png if the former does not exist.\nThis enables declaring reftest at multiple scales and png reference images in a single line for example scale(1, 2, 0.5) == foo.yaml foo.png.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314024\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale0.51.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale1.51.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/linear-aligned-border-radius-scale2.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/reftest.rs"], "git_node": "61eef9cfe4e2b3396646d59e12466d527f92af32", "git_parents": ["ded2ffd3c866d418a35a79dbcb82c1a12bee036d"], "node": "8a4e261866408f102eedcf3f5ef1968ef445bfc9", "parents": ["8c7fe5bd88e64a7a947b44bf73d537841c5d9bf0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051146 - Exit Fullscreen when opening Document PiP. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309778\n", "files": ["dom/documentpip/DocumentPictureInPicture.cpp", "dom/documentpip/tests/browser/browser.toml", "dom/documentpip/tests/browser/browser_pip_exits_fs.js", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp"], "git_node": "3565e65886c5b9ff8df0d211de4942247652245c", "git_parents": ["61eef9cfe4e2b3396646d59e12466d527f92af32"], "node": "c4ec816a1c9734458e87da37e90f3312f7fd470f", "parents": ["8a4e261866408f102eedcf3f5ef1968ef445bfc9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1934364 - Fix intermittent timeout in browser_new_tab_in_privilegedabout_process_pref.js, r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sclements.\n\nThe goBack() call in process_switching_through_navigation_features is a\nsilent no-op unless the about:newtab session history entry is marked as\nhaving had user interaction. That flag is set by the system principal load\nof the http page, but it reaches the parent process as an asynchronous\nWindowContext update that races with the entry for the new load becoming\nthe active one. When it loses the race the flag lands on the http entry\ninstead, canGoBack stays false, and the test waits forever for a location\nchange that never comes. Waiting longer cannot help: by the time the load\nhas completed the flag has already been applied to the wrong entry.\n\nSet browser.navigation.requireUserInteraction to false, matching what\nbrowser_hashChangeProxyState.js and browser_remoteness_switch.js already do\nfor programmatic history navigation, and drop the skip-if annotations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314346\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_new_tab_in_privilegedabout_process_pref.js"], "git_node": "6ae1a3d840fe0f0c12534e6eca075ba10a61c9ca", "git_parents": ["3565e65886c5b9ff8df0d211de4942247652245c"], "node": "b16d81bc763e474d11e1ab2b3e7bcd70271c9757", "parents": ["c4ec816a1c9734458e87da37e90f3312f7fd470f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058742 - Update ML Kit GenAI Prompt API to version 1.0.0-beta4. r=android-reviewers,matt-tighe\n\nThe GenerativeModel interface gained typed content generation and several feature-availability checks, and\ndropped its ListenableFuture-based variants, so update the test fake to match.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314795\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/llm-gemininano/src/test/java/mozilla/components/lib/llm/gemini/nano/fakes/FakeGenerativeModel.kt"], "git_node": "26e63c9e42a99a08ab8d6d77e178f8ee1db7807a", "git_parents": ["6ae1a3d840fe0f0c12534e6eca075ba10a61c9ca"], "node": "501fc4faa4334e3a89cfab0cb254e463033ded7f", "parents": ["b16d81bc763e474d11e1ab2b3e7bcd70271c9757"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047735 - Tab group expanded view now has an add new homepage tab r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313591\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/ExpandedTabGroup.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/TabsTrayTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/TabManagementFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/ExpandedTabGroupTest.kt"], "git_node": "3a67eb27ecb2b06b9c608c7e937651e4fc8428ef", "git_parents": ["26e63c9e42a99a08ab8d6d77e178f8ee1db7807a"], "node": "91dfee421b6fd30377efc9720ba601bdc84deae5", "parents": ["501fc4faa4334e3a89cfab0cb254e463033ded7f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030683 - Show Bookmark Bar on SW New Tab based on user settings and track its usage from new tab r=places-reviewers,flozia,desktop-theme-reviewers,dao,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313903\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-places.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_bookmarks_toolbar.js", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css"], "git_node": "dc1e40f501ff8bb6d1324bc744e89b7e5100aefa", "git_parents": ["3a67eb27ecb2b06b9c608c7e937651e4fc8428ef"], "node": "d1ff697986782243545bbf05e55e20a1a0a01d67", "parents": ["91dfee421b6fd30377efc9720ba601bdc84deae5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nirmaladvani \u003cnirmaladvani@live.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2003177 - Remove unused dom.vr.controller.enumerate.interval pref. r=gregp\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314966\n", "files": ["dom/vr/test/mochitest/runVRTest.js", "dom/vr/test/reftest/reftest.list", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "04410274d88b48d898ee34e9c0d578f1b56e8b4b", "git_parents": ["dc1e40f501ff8bb6d1324bc744e89b7e5100aefa"], "node": "20ce48d7572f449672c77d9cf59a17d4b8680fd2", "parents": ["d1ff697986782243545bbf05e55e20a1a0a01d67"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052731 - Keep a few levels of style sharing cache around. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDo some clean-up while at it, and remove some checks that the caller\nalready does.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314978\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/sharing/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/style_resolver.rs"], "git_node": "e0da100669c053f2136b91424543a9cb0b49d947", "git_parents": ["04410274d88b48d898ee34e9c0d578f1b56e8b4b"], "node": "105e67e7d98675008dd8729e424771db9cf5b72a", "parents": ["20ce48d7572f449672c77d9cf59a17d4b8680fd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shawn Zivontsis \u003cshawnz@shawnz.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2025999: Swap moz_origins index to UNIQUE(host, prefix) r=mak,places-reviewers\n\nThis change has two benefits: for queries that filter on both host\nand prefix, this reduces the number of comparisons necessary since\nthe higher-cardinality column now occurs first. For queries that only\nfilter on host, this makes it possible to use the index in situations\nwhere previously it might not have been usable at all.\n\nSQLite doesn't support reordering index columns in place, so the table\nhas to be rebuilt, but it can't be dropped while moz_places references\nit. We defer the foreign keys, stash the origins in a temporary table,\ndrop and recreate moz_origins with the new constraint, then refill it.\nRefilling under the original name resolves the deferred violations left\nby the drop, so the whole change commits in one transaction without\ntouching moz_places.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313507\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/places/Database.cpp", "toolkit/components/places/Database.h", "toolkit/components/places/nsINavHistoryService.idl", "toolkit/components/places/nsPlacesTables.h", "toolkit/components/places/nsPlacesTriggers.h", "toolkit/components/places/tests/migration/places_v87.sqlite", "toolkit/components/places/tests/migration/test_current_from_v86.js", "toolkit/components/places/tests/migration/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "135df0ad91eadb99640667df1befedd03d474b09", "git_parents": ["e0da100669c053f2136b91424543a9cb0b49d947"], "node": "6c1d2b74f796b5604ceb2b595ae22650dfce7848", "parents": ["105e67e7d98675008dd8729e424771db9cf5b72a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058912 - Add a webrender-wrench try preset. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314956\n", "files": ["tools/tryselect/try_presets.yml"], "git_node": "c3d051ab4d89118528ccdd54848f611f35a939e4", "git_parents": ["135df0ad91eadb99640667df1befedd03d474b09"], "node": "1ef984267457334ec9cecec6efb3ff0fa5a170fa", "parents": ["6c1d2b74f796b5604ceb2b595ae22650dfce7848"], "tags": []}, {"author": "alastor0325 \u003calastor0325@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057991 - Update asynchronous promise handling in MFCDMChild. r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314732\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/MFCDMChild.cpp"], "git_node": "86101509f7626ef7eee7d817b2a13a38f655eaa6", "git_parents": ["c3d051ab4d89118528ccdd54848f611f35a939e4"], "node": "9907749597973bec1d371a9a044fde4bec07cf00", "parents": ["1ef984267457334ec9cecec6efb3ff0fa5a170fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "yazan \u003cyalmacki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056338 - Fix keyboard focus order for secondary top buttons in about:welcome. r=omc-reviewers,jprickett\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314460\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/modules/AboutWelcomeDefaults.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_configurable_ui.js", "browser/components/aboutwelcome/tests/browser/browser_aboutwelcome_multistage_mr.js", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "c13b26af40122551bca0e2de210d9b05252487de", "git_parents": ["86101509f7626ef7eee7d817b2a13a38f655eaa6"], "node": "6fb3613967790a82c4b3fad0635df2ecadd806db", "parents": ["9907749597973bec1d371a9a044fde4bec07cf00"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjcoppeard@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057460 - Don't track memory for queued finalization registry records against the zone r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDoing this creates problems because the GC assumes that a container can't be\nboth grow and be freed in the same GC cycle (because if it is freed then there\nwere no references to it and so nothing could access it to grow it).\n\nUnfortuantely this is baked in to the memory tracking. The simplest thing to do\nhere is to not count this memory against the zone. In most cases it is\ntransient anyway: finalization registry records are added to it during sweeping\nand then removed when they have been passed to the callback.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314855\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/FinalizationRegistryObject.cpp", "js/src/builtin/FinalizationRegistryObject.h", "js/src/jit-test/tests/gc/bug-2057460.js"], "git_node": "ae6cef69e126ab39b84d88fb72eb6b2257715234", "git_parents": ["c13b26af40122551bca0e2de210d9b05252487de"], "node": "db2032dcd47764ac5f6355e4bfa564d77c1b3398", "parents": ["6fb3613967790a82c4b3fad0635df2ecadd806db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochr