erential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314418\n", "files": ["dom/html/EditContext.cpp", "dom/html/EditContext.h", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/test_editcontext_redundant_characterboundsupdate.html"], "git_node": "67a62b40e7910ea337e8c761654841abe1d52032", "git_parents": ["de96e1d8eace76c19a8526abcd800135e1ff5219"], "node": "7b1f7673b9c164bd9f8aa8241c9e271ff2e51a68", "parents": ["666182a353e308344db6916da812d4f81e250f63"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058958 - Fix compile problems for Servo after bug 2028142. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nUnlike in Gecko, LocalName and AtomIdent are different things in Servo,\nso the conversion needs to be handled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314980\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/custom_properties.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/container_rule.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs"], "git_node": "b0368e6ed45f182fd3f286015ba4de403f025bbe", "git_parents": ["67a62b40e7910ea337e8c761654841abe1d52032"], "node": "3b6e4bb45c569e4b8fd2221c8ca6f9b4cd19da97", "parents": ["7b1f7673b9c164bd9f8aa8241c9e271ff2e51a68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Roger Yang \u003croyang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058711 - Refactor IPProtectionLocationsScreen to use existing composables. r=android-reviewers,gmalekpour\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315031\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/compose/MenuItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ipprotection/IPProtectionLocations.kt"], "git_node": "5b1c290a5648acc3821bf2c97032158b3807412a", "git_parents": ["b0368e6ed45f182fd3f286015ba4de403f025bbe"], "node": "d5833e2011354855a5efa934b43db7f0ce0b72ba", "parents": ["3b6e4bb45c569e4b8fd2221c8ca6f9b4cd19da97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2050584. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\" for causing webgl failures @test_2_conformance2__extensions__ovr_multiview2_draw_buffers.html.\n\nThis reverts commit 117172f0e6d07fdac97eea3c645966b13fd93c45.\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.cpp", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochitest-errata.toml"], "git_node": "5804455c67fd58db1a81bcdcdc5528ae9317b772", "git_parents": ["5b1c290a5648acc3821bf2c97032158b3807412a"], "node": "cd80dbcd781c5517734198a51f57a638a1899dc6", "parents": ["d5833e2011354855a5efa934b43db7f0ce0b72ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hannajones \u003chjones@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056349 - ensure theme-picker reflects device appearance pref r=mstriemer,niklas\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313217\n", "files": ["browser/actors/ThemePickerChild.sys.mjs", "browser/actors/ThemePickerParent.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/content/edit-profile-card.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_edit_profile_theme_picker_nova_test.js", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_theme_picker.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/theme-picker/theme-picker-direct-controller.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/theme-picker/theme-picker-remote-controller.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/theme-picker/theme-picker.mjs"], "git_node": "a6c3a921ec4fcd3dc41634316d0ac4feb71e6b08", "git_parents": ["5804455c67fd58db1a81bcdcdc5528ae9317b772"], "node": "197c1c3968ada0bea7ed9601523a4a37d2665285", "parents": ["cd80dbcd781c5517734198a51f57a638a1899dc6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Add frame-build traversal counters to the WebRender profiler r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nCounts primitives visited by visibility and by prepare, the (primitive,\ncommand buffer) pairs prepare emits, and the pictures it entered, under a\nnew Frame build traversal preset. Against the existing Visible primitives\ncounter these show how much of each pass's traversal produces a draw, and\nthe per-primitive fan-out across dirty tiles. Accumulated at cluster and\npicture granularity, so no new per-primitive cost.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314815\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "045709c183b18a6e6a56b1aa26f6fe2b1f4ef5c9", "git_parents": ["a6c3a921ec4fcd3dc41634316d0ac4feb71e6b08"], "node": "2e59f4fecd8b817406c04c2dec3bbf48ec29be43", "parents": ["197c1c3968ada0bea7ed9601523a4a37d2665285"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Stop treating a draw index and a prim instance index as interchangeable r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe draw storage is identity-indexed by primitive instance, so the two\nindices share a numeric value and batch.rs reached the instance by reusing\nthe draw index from the command stream. Add PrimitiveDrawIndex to separate\nthe concepts and draw_index_for_instance as the only place relying on the\nidentity; batch.rs now uses the header's prim_instance_index back-reference,\nand PlaneSplitAnchor and ExternalSurfaceDescriptor carry draw indices.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314816\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/internal_types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "de33a97a3c791d3e0cf5c068bde8a2a84565b76d", "git_parents": ["045709c183b18a6e6a56b1aa26f6fe2b1f4ef5c9"], "node": "ee2f71638378d179e94dac2af4ecf2d21fd2816e", "parents": ["2e59f4fecd8b817406c04c2dec3bbf48ec29be43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Return the picture clip-task index instead of writing it through the draw storage r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nprepare_picture_clips took the whole draw slice for a single write, and\nprepare_picture_primitive wrote the same field while holding pic_scratch, a\nborrow of the frame scratch spanning its whole body. Both now return the\nindex for the caller to record. Moving the write later is equivalent: only\nbatching reads clip_task_index, and it runs after prepare.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314817\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs"], "git_node": "4cb84e86dcd8f2035d0f1c7434788c3e5cfb9944", "git_parents": ["de33a97a3c791d3e0cf5c068bde8a2a84565b76d"], "node": "719658629427a9437c07903726d1b1ff722afc35", "parents": ["ee2f71638378d179e94dac2af4ecf2d21fd2816e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Seal the per-frame draw storage behind accessors r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nPrimitiveFrameScratch::draws was public and indexed from six modules, so\nchanging its layout meant changing every call site with no way to know they\nhad all been found. Make it private behind draw/draw_mut, keyed by\nPrimitiveDrawIndex, with draw_for_instance for the passes that still walk\ninstances and reset_draws for the frame reset.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314818\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "3a87b4b433dcd6c1ec4c5cfa1cdc085d15212a9b", "git_parents": ["4cb84e86dcd8f2035d0f1c7434788c3e5cfb9944"], "node": "74589622268e6c7108e05dacfad19e97d7d0b1d2", "parents": ["719658629427a9437c07903726d1b1ff722afc35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Push draw headers as they are found instead of one per scene primitive r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe storage was sized to the whole scene, so every frame reset a\nhundred-byte header for every primitive of every cluster of every visited\npicture, before the cluster visibility check and regardless of whether it\nwas drawn. Visibility now accumulates the header in a local and pushes it\nonce the primitive is known to be drawn, with an instance_to_draw side\ntable for the passes that still walk instances. This removes the reset loop\nand the failure mode its comment described - a missed reset making a\nprimitive wrongly considered visible - along with prepare's defensive\nreset, and turns reset into mark_culled for the backdrop paths that\ndiscover late that a draw is not drawn.\n\nThe two push points are a pass-through picture and a primitive whose clip\nchain resolved. The latter pushes before the tile cache dependency update,\nbecause that update records a draw index on any compositor surface it\npromotes; a primitive it then culls keeps its draw and is skipped by\nprepare on DrawState, as before.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314819\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/command_buffer.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "a34137091d5f558c9e56fdfd99c5e61e482fea89", "git_parents": ["3a87b4b433dcd6c1ec4c5cfa1cdc085d15212a9b"], "node": "67fd8ec25ecc15df3dfa7c8a07a6eef3d45eb0c7", "parents": ["74589622268e6c7108e05dacfad19e97d7d0b1d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Make the quad emit path draw-keyed r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe quad helpers and the per-kind prepare helpers calling them took a\nprimitive instance index but emit draw-keyed commands, so they had to look\nthe draw index back up - fallibly, on a path where the caller already had\nit. Thread it down instead; none of them used the instance index for\nanything else, so the lookup helper and its three expect sites go away.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314820\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/border_image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/box_shadow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs"], "git_node": "fd228e5ccf9d259b804bd3155580e02f87477b43", "git_parents": ["a34137091d5f558c9e56fdfd99c5e61e482fea89"], "node": "310729f492ace2801107d50d780d7dd9dd0a5b4f", "parents": ["67fd8ec25ecc15df3dfa7c8a07a6eef3d45eb0c7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058750 - Guard the resolved-state invariant of the per-frame draw storage r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nVisibility pushes a draw before its state is known, since the tile cache\ndependency update decides it, so a path that pushed without resolving would\nhand DrawState::Unset to prepare and batching. Add a debug-only check after\nthe visibility pass that every pushed draw got a state.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314821\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs"], "git_node": "455f5e7d4be56f796f9464128350c3a8bf6f45ce", "git_parents": ["fd228e5ccf9d259b804bd3155580e02f87477b43"], "node": "5bf72a83202ec2bfe192a0853570b427120af17f", "parents": ["310729f492ace2801107d50d780d7dd9dd0a5b4f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yury Delendik \u003cydelendik@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053150 - Use readonlyThreadsafeLookup for Debugger frames in traceWasmContFrame. r=jandem\n\nDebugAPI::traceWasmContFrame runs on parallel marking threads (via\nContObject::trace -\u003e ContStack::traceSuspended), so the guarded\nHashMap::lookup() is not appropriate there: two threads tracing different\nContObjects that resolve to the same Debugger read Debugger::frames\nconcurrently and trip lookup()'s single-threaded ReentrancyGuard.\n\nreadonlyThreadsafeLookup returns the same result as lookup() -- lookup() is\njust a ReentrancyGuard around it -- so this is a no-op in release builds and\nonly drops the debug-only guard.\n\nSafety verified: nothing mutates Debugger::frames while marking. Every\nmutator (getFrame, slowPathOnResumeFrame, replaceFrameGuts,\nsuspendGeneratorDebuggerFrames, terminateDebuggerFrame) runs on the\nmutator/main thread, which is paused for the duration of parallel marking;\nthe sole GC-phase mutator, DebugAPI::sweepAll, runs strictly after marking\ncompletes. The concurrent reads therefore have no concurrent writer, so\nreadonlyThreadsafeLookup is the correct primitive.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314713\n", "files": ["js/src/debugger/Debugger.cpp"], "git_node": "c67897e8373123f0dd091c262cbec1b0bd78ce5c", "git_parents": ["455f5e7d4be56f796f9464128350c3a8bf6f45ce"], "node": "3164eae89e9f84ed5e6f1e15f691ab4ced85f3cd", "parents": ["5bf72a83202ec2bfe192a0853570b427120af17f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058479: Add missing subviewbutton-nav class to the ai-window-toggle r=jlewis\n\nAdded the missing class \"subviewbutton-nav\" that adds a chevron-right icon to the `ai-window-toggle` element on the overflow menu.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315068\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AIWindow.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "35eeafb5aaa3e83c3314a3fa815e6e035ab537d3", "git_parents": ["c67897e8373123f0dd091c262cbec1b0bd78ce5c"], "node": "d8c399469f43e2198538a21a35fd72715bae17fc", "parents": ["3164eae89e9f84ed5e6f1e15f691ab4ced85f3cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Nimalan \u003cabhisheknimalan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058526 - Disable alerts from Windows Speedometer 3 Autoland jobs with native profiling. r=perftest-reviewers,sparky\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314711\n", "files": ["testing/raptor/browsertime/support-scripts/speedometer3.py"], "git_node": "ce79dbe410606bd7674641375922f12eaaea9e4d", "git_parents": ["35eeafb5aaa3e83c3314a3fa815e6e035ab537d3"], "node": "9155a9a7ecfc9bc0324762299a3fb00ce4b4426f", "parents": ["d8c399469f43e2198538a21a35fd72715bae17fc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Nimalan \u003cabhisheknimalan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030166 - Add Samply profiling support for macOS Raptor tests. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nmacOS aarch64 and macOS x86_64 only. Support native (OS-wide) profiling\nfor Raptor tests in CI and locally using the Samply Profiler.\n\nThis is implemented by building a Clang compiled, C++ wrapper around the\nFirefox binary that sets environment variables DYLD_INSERT_LIBRARIES and\nSAMPLY_BOOTSTRAP_SERVER_NAME with values taken from a running \"helper\"\nbinary that's being recorded by Samply. This allows the wrapped binary\nto be registered with Samply for profiling and recorded over multiple\nbrowser cycles. The resulting profile is then symbolicated with build\nsymbols and converted into a JSON profile in the Firefox Profiler\nformat.\n\n--samply-profile is introduced as a Raptor option and a Mozharness extra\noption. A CI job with Samply profiling can be created by adding\n--samply-profile (and its respective dependencies Clang++, macOSX SDK\nand Samply) to the job's configuration.\n\nTo run a Raptor test with Samply profiling locally, use the\n--samply-profile flag with ./mach raptor.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306848\n", "files": ["testing/mozharness/mozharness/mozilla/testing/raptor.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/browsertime/base.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/chrome_trace.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/cmdline.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/gecko_profile.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/perftest.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/raptor.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/raptor_profiling.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/results.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/samply_profile.py", "testing/raptor/raptor/utils.py", "testing/raptor/test/test_chrome_trace.py", "testing/raptor/test/test_gecko_profile.py"], "git_node": "e782ba253fa2730b7d7a0baec617566f5f5955b2", "git_parents": ["ce79dbe410606bd7674641375922f12eaaea9e4d"], "node": "2aa8cdc634bf3d9b58b49bde92eccd89e1aee9fe", "parents": ["9155a9a7ecfc9bc0324762299a3fb00ce4b4426f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Nimalan \u003cabhisheknimalan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030166 - Add transform and Autoland tasks for Speedometer 3 native profiling on macOS. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nThese transforms configures Samply profiling and symbolication dependencies\nfor Speedometer 3 macOS CI tasks when --native-profiling is used or\nwhen running on Autoland.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306849\n", "files": ["taskcluster/gecko_taskgraph/transforms/test/raptor.py", "testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/browsertime/support-scripts/speedometer3.py"], "git_node": "dc9a6a0dfc3089104db25b968ff4f955ae1e8c2e", "git_parents": ["e782ba253fa2730b7d7a0baec617566f5f5955b2"], "node": "1ed466a250ff720708d7c6ac170bccb8d6980096", "parents": ["2aa8cdc634bf3d9b58b49bde92eccd89e1aee9fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Abhishek Nimalan \u003cabhisheknimalan@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2030166 - Update perfdocs to include info on native profiling on macOS. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306850\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/browsertime.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/perfdocs/browsertime.md"], "git_node": "e8e0ca4487761b4eae1c6b6213c83b27d93a595d", "git_parents": ["dc9a6a0dfc3089104db25b968ff4f955ae1e8c2e"], "node": "8f259359e7c8a1a63be7d18615688de254a68f40", "parents": ["1ed466a250ff720708d7c6ac170bccb8d6980096"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1714720 - Factor the main-thread keyboard scroll out into PresShell::ScrollByKeyboard. r=botond,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nScrollLine, ScrollCharacter, ScrollPage and CompleteScroll each duplicated the\n\"find the scroll container, then ScrollBy\" logic. Move the per-action ScrollBy\ninto a shared PresShell::ScrollByKeyboard(aAction[, aStartFrame]) that switches\non the KeyboardScrollAction type, so the four nsISelectionController methods\nbecome thin wrappers. GetScrollContainerFrameToScrollOrHandoff now takes the\nalready-resolved start frame, with the focused/selected-content seeding moved\ninto ScrollByKeyboard.\n\nThis is a pure refactor with no behavior change; it prepares for the\ncross-process keyboard scroll handoff, which needs to drive the same scrolling\nseeded from the embedder's frame rather than from the focused content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306679\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.h"], "git_node": "962c7818e70e0271fbf28eadd7454a74d0005d87", "git_parents": ["e8e0ca4487761b4eae1c6b6213c83b27d93a595d"], "node": "b06ecb87abb59f8f3b5f1c2205914c2e02ff67b6", "parents": ["8f259359e7c8a1a63be7d18615688de254a68f40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1714720 - Hand off main-thread keyboard scrolling to the embedder process. r=botond,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306680\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserBridgeChild.h", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.h", "dom/ipc/PBrowser.ipdl", "dom/ipc/PBrowserBridge.ipdl", "layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.h", "layout/base/tests/file_keyboard_scroll_handoff_oopif.html", "layout/base/tests/mochitest.toml", "layout/base/tests/test_keyboard_scroll_handoff_oopif.html", "layout/base/tests/window_keyboard_scroll_handoff_oopif.html"], "git_node": "ef46caafe548f1aa36204c93324e4a1c21269b8a", "git_parents": ["962c7818e70e0271fbf28eadd7454a74d0005d87"], "node": "663882654cd1fe59ffe17d5456e13931d41f0cb5", "parents": ["b06ecb87abb59f8f3b5f1c2205914c2e02ff67b6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Giles \u003ctgiles@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056588 - Move theme-picker strings out of locales-preview r=fluent-reviewers,hjones,bolsson,omc-reviewers,mossop,jprickett\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313304\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.html", "browser/components/profiles/content/edit-profile.html", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/CustomizeMenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/PrefsFeed.sys.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/theme-picker/theme-picker.mjs", "toolkit/locales-preview/theme-picker.ftl", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/theme-picker.ftl", "toolkit/locales/jar.mn"], "git_node": "d547f596558391813c1291fe15ea83acd046d24d", "git_parents": ["ef46caafe548f1aa36204c93324e4a1c21269b8a"], "node": "ac8146f7adbd4226498502696d5cc1ccfc96a22a", "parents": ["663882654cd1fe59ffe17d5456e