003cemcminn@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051691 - Add toolbar entry point for referrals r=nbarrett,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,omc-reviewers,yazan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313258\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/browser-menubar.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-menubar.js", "browser/base/content/test/menubar/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/menubar/browser_menu_referrals_page.js", "browser/base/content/utilityOverlay.js", "browser/components/referrals/Referrals.sys.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/appmenu.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/menubar.ftl", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser_sma_get_referral_code.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/head.js", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuBarX.h", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuBarX.mm", "widget/cocoa/nsMenuGroupOwnerX.h"], "git_node": "10ece13b4d59449c561bedc9c5c28beb85b6bc72", "git_parents": ["44094a07d3f82206aa41761695b7f25a549da096"], "node": "f4540d8f4c55511772f511d4fbebfed261afb4fe", "parents": ["0553e1874eed7b3346424a38815b182e2473f2de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058276 - Update the private browsing newtab subheader to say data is erased when all private windows are closed. r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315033\n", "files": ["browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aboutPrivateBrowsing.ftl"], "git_node": "fd4c03707085058002fb9379fe645e609eaaecb5", "git_parents": ["10ece13b4d59449c561bedc9c5c28beb85b6bc72"], "node": "1504e0d60c6209a75f6efc449906a588190c90be", "parents": ["f4540d8f4c55511772f511d4fbebfed261afb4fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058370 - Time out a headless page read that never loads. r=ai-platform-reviewers,ai-security-reviewers,nordzilla,bjohns,omarg\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314825\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_smartwindow_get_page_content_timeout.js", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/MLTestUtils.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pageextractor/PageExtractorParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/pageextractor/tests/browser/browser_headless_extractor.js"], "git_node": "900a2c58924a65093f2eead579dace01f18bd357", "git_parents": ["fd4c03707085058002fb9379fe645e609eaaecb5"], "node": "0e766e62aa6b59bdfe212a69623b795d5ef39bd8", "parents": ["1504e0d60c6209a75f6efc449906a588190c90be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Group the debugging documentation under its own section r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nThe 16 pages under docs/contributing/debugging/ were pulled straight into the\n\"Working on Firefox\" toctree by a glob, so every one of them showed up in the\nflat list on the documentation home page.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314508\n", "files": ["docs/contributing/debugging/index.md", "docs/contributing/index.md"], "git_node": "0471b087c4efed451b9f0b89063a147d2149dc17", "git_parents": ["900a2c58924a65093f2eead579dace01f18bd357"], "node": "b4eaf20e406a0d9fb54136c875a43601789f3628", "parents": ["0e766e62aa6b59bdfe212a69623b795d5ef39bd8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Group the bug handling documentation under its own sections r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nThe Guides, Policies and Processes headings in docs/bug-mgmt/index.md wrapped\nglobbed toctrees, so their 17 pages were direct children of \"Bug Handling\" and\nshowed up flat on the documentation home page.\n\nGive each subdirectory its own index page and point the parent toctree at them,\nso the home page shows three entries instead of seventeen.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314608\n", "files": ["docs/bug-mgmt/guides/index.md", "docs/bug-mgmt/index.md", "docs/bug-mgmt/policies/index.md", "docs/bug-mgmt/processes/index.md"], "git_node": "31faa66b8d55d13f20e83060473a7637a323a444", "git_parents": ["0471b087c4efed451b9f0b89063a147d2149dc17"], "node": "4fa9a3da4b0fa29fc8bb6103e1ea654ba4f7a8e7", "parents": ["b4eaf20e406a0d9fb54136c875a43601789f3628"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Group the memory documentation under its own section r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\nThe hidden toctree in docs/performance/index.md globbed memory/*, so the 18\nmemory pages were direct children of \"Performance\" in the sidebar.\n\nGive docs/performance/memory/ its own index page, grouped by measuring memory\nusage, leak detection, DMD and the DevTools Memory panel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314609\n", "files": ["docs/performance/index.md", "docs/performance/memory/index.md"], "git_node": "1e7fbc2fcda4bebc8fb322368d366ea0f8b4978b", "git_parents": ["31faa66b8d55d13f20e83060473a7637a323a444"], "node": "c2b602e796130210db50152c8f85aaf5f5133354", "parents": ["4fa9a3da4b0fa29fc8bb6103e1ea654ba4f7a8e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Move the Jujutsu documentation to a Version control section r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal DONTBUILD\n\n\"Introduction to Jujutsu\" sat in the middle of \"Making Changes To Firefox\",\nbetween the data collection pages and Searchfox, which says nothing about what\nit is.\n\nGive it a Version control section, together with Git Tricks. The latter was in\nno toctree at all, so it was built but unreachable from the navigation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314610\n", "files": ["docs/contributing/index.md"], "git_node": "829e55b020fefed7aa68dc2bdb7cbd3f70305ee8", "git_parents": ["1e7fbc2fcda4bebc8fb322368d366ea0f8b4978b"], "node": "732baab65f8397ac3a1deb211c3e97cfda32ea7b", "parents": ["c2b602e796130210db50152c8f85aaf5f5133354"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058892 - Allow Nimbus to control pdfjs.enableSignatureVerification r=calixte\n\nThis is mostly to experiment\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314959\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml", "toolkit/components/pdfjs/PdfJsOverridePrefs.js"], "git_node": "dda713898222daf0b334f1ef0fe1b76b512e5d8d", "git_parents": ["829e55b020fefed7aa68dc2bdb7cbd3f70305ee8"], "node": "cb8fedd1355ba055816de705218c42a36741eb97", "parents": ["732baab65f8397ac3a1deb211c3e97cfda32ea7b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - address a trivial bugprone-suspicious-semicolon warning r=keeler\n\nhttps://clang.llvm.org/extra/clang-tidy/checks/bugprone/suspicious-semicolon.html\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314883\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/nsSecurityHeaderParser.cpp"], "git_node": "bd6312a6bc84f3d503a2bc41799d25c2eb4756ab", "git_parents": ["dda713898222daf0b334f1ef0fe1b76b512e5d8d"], "node": "89c61c2682b525c5f89959e0f993cb361352e19f", "parents": ["cb8fedd1355ba055816de705218c42a36741eb97"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "no bug - docs telemetry: adjust the urls and highlight telemetry alert dashboard r=perftest-reviewers,aglavic DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314839\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/telemetry-alerting.md", "testing/performance/telemetry-alerting/perfdocs/index.md"], "git_node": "ad17855cca358cfddd2bbc77e7ee4580473e2cbc", "git_parents": ["bd6312a6bc84f3d503a2bc41799d25c2eb4756ab"], "node": "519f36806713a244810d1490eda0bb9a4b253298", "parents": ["89c61c2682b525c5f89959e0f993cb361352e19f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058749 - Document WebRender screenshot readback in gfx/wr/AGENTS.md r=ai4dev-reviewers,gfx-reviewers,nical,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314800\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "aac59414eebfc33606bb89c4b19d559a2988df23", "git_parents": ["ad17855cca358cfddd2bbc77e7ee4580473e2cbc"], "node": "6dc73f4f8353f9e2a5cbacc0ce4cc526b96f309b", "parents": ["519f36806713a244810d1490eda0bb9a4b253298"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1643960 - Update Adding Documentation guide to use Markdown r=firefox-source-docs-reviewers,ahal\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D299884\n", "files": ["tools/moztreedocs/docs/adding-documentation.md"], "git_node": "5315fa3ab5f4d130dc09fb34888094b2a05b2afa", "git_parents": ["aac59414eebfc33606bb89c4b19d559a2988df23"], "node": "d9142d026fcaea1e207da45656961a4774bcdf79", "parents": ["6dc73f4f8353f9e2a5cbacc0ce4cc526b96f309b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055481 - Avoid opening the ai chat sidebar during the contextmenu test. r=Mardak\n\n- And un-skip the test.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313480\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tabContextMenu_altStructure.js"], "git_node": "ed1ee75a071074dc6d1810abf2c1e3fcb6577102", "git_parents": ["5315fa3ab5f4d130dc09fb34888094b2a05b2afa"], "node": "c0bd8e3b0143ccb24b75df5ca10886c17843002a", "parents": ["d9142d026fcaea1e207da45656961a4774bcdf79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1821429 - Alias openBookmarkedURL to bookmarkAdded and added extend features. r=omc-reviewers,mimi\n\nPreviously, the `openBookmarkedURL` trigger was used to fire when a user added a bookmark. This was confusing and not descriptive of the trigger's purpose. This patch updates `openBookmarkedURL` to  `visitBookmarkedURL` and `bookmarkAdded` but keeps `openBookmarkedURL` as an alias for `bookmarkAdded` to avoid breaking existing triggers. Additionally, this patch adds the ability to extend the `visitBookmarkedURL` trigger to fire when a user visits a bookmarked URL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312144\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTriggerListeners.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/test2", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/ASRouterTriggerListeners.test.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/TriggerActionSchemas/TriggerActionSchemas.json", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/TriggerActionSchemas/index.md"], "git_node": "2aa1da32dd26a351aacb1a5c20c21bcdabe2dc03", "git_parents": ["ed1ee75a071074dc6d1810abf2c1e3fcb6577102"], "node": "1475e10f2fd733885f2540ebb30324689e5db1ad", "parents": ["c0bd8e3b0143ccb24b75df5ca10886c17843002a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054161 - Make `FontFaceSet` create `Promise` only when `GetReady` is called r=smaug,emilio,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314584\n", "files": ["layout/style/FontFaceSet.cpp"], "git_node": "a4dc471431af1d243063629af2854da0c590eeef", "git_parents": ["2aa1da32dd26a351aacb1a5c20c21bcdabe2dc03"], "node": "eb0c294a60499ba41f067d7d1918df9805fac31e", "parents": ["1475e10f2fd733885f2540ebb30324689e5db1ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051354 - part 1: Update `IsIBusInSyncMode()` for the newer ibus r=m_kato\n\nibus added a new value, `2`, to `IBUS_ENABLE_SYNC_MODE` and only `1`\nis the synchronous mode. So, we need to update the logic here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314535\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp"], "git_node": "8ba2c2e3167041aa6bbf279a1cbbb420f1bc5a03", "git_parents": ["a4dc471431af1d243063629af2854da0c590eeef"], "node": "a6f80307f1271b552482a9d862ec9be1734debfc", "parents": ["eb0c294a60499ba41f067d7d1918df9805fac31e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051354 - part 2: Improve Logging of `IMContextWrapper` r=m_kato\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314536\n", "files": ["widget/IMEData.cpp", "widget/IMEData.h", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.h", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "7540a46436f1947f229f986952bf63577ec3654a", "git_parents": ["8ba2c2e3167041aa6bbf279a1cbbb420f1bc5a03"], "node": "351b2b6586fbf583eac450ad0274a6ce5e978c8d", "parents": ["a6f80307f1271b552482a9d862ec9be1734debfc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051354 - part 3: Make `KeymapWrapper::ComputeDOMKeyNameIndex` return `KEY_NAME_INDEX_USE_STRING` r=m_kato\n\nWe don't map any `keyval` values to `KEY_NAME_INDEX_USE_STRING` because\nthere are too big number of values which introduce text input.\nTherefore, we need to make it return `KEY_NAME_INDEX_USE_STRING` since\nit's unclear whether it won't return `KEY_NAME_INDEX_USE_STRING` and\nactually there are some wrong users. [1][2][3].\n\n1. https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/3b3f727963c10fe58e6e72c15989ad0e35dbf832/widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp#1644-1645\n2. https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/3b3f727963c10fe58e6e72c15989ad0e35dbf832/widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp#1756-1757\n3. https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/rev/3b3f727963c10fe58e6e72c15989ad0e35dbf832/widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp#1908-1909\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314537\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.h"], "git_node": "df2c23b1fc3b476133e58504c55fa6e27fbcc4c4", "git_parents": ["7540a46436f1947f229f986952bf63577ec3654a"], "node": "185cfe37e25dde480367db484aa389f378fb8945", "parents": ["351b2b6586fbf583eac450ad0274a6ce5e978c8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051354 - part 4: Relax to dispatch `eKeyPress` events for typing a grapheme cluster r=m_kato\n\nCurrently, we use `eKeyPress` event for a commit composition without\ncomposing state if:\n* the commit string is a non-BMP character\n* the commit string matches with the source key press event's `keyval`\n\nThe former was for a safe. We synthesized a set of composition events\nas its fallback. However, we stopped doing that in bug 1712269 for the\ncompatibility with Chromium and consistency with Firefox for macOS.\nHowever, on Linux, this case is used more frequently and the fallback\npath causes only `beforeinput` and `input` so that web apps may fail\nto handle that like Microsoft Word. Additionally, we already dispatch\nmultiple `eKeyPress` events after a `eKeyDown`. Therefore, we should\nuse the path for a grapheme cluster for the safe in these days.\n\nThe latter was for the safe. However, IIRC, some keyboard layouts\nimplemented with IME does not modify the keyboard layout but overrides\nwith the commit event without composing state. So, I think we don't need\nthis restriction now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314538\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.h", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.h"], "git_node": "b822beffd1947a6da6fca5fb58634402111fdb3c", "git_parents": ["df2c23b1fc3b476133e58504c55fa6e27fbcc4c4"], "node": "3b0083933b75ced04e578297259636699e7aa86c", "parents": ["185cfe37e25dde480367db484aa389f378fb8945"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051354 - part 5: Support asynchronous IME handling of ibus better r=m_kato\n\nWe changed not to dispatch a set of composition events to commit a\ncharacter in bug 1712269 for the consistency with macOS and Chrome.\nHowever, the new behavior causes only `beforeinput` and `input`\nevents without any user input event except `Process` key value\nkeyboard events. That makes Microsoft Word fail to manage a text\ninput transaction for their undo manager.\n\nAdditionally, on Linux, this behavior is typically used by normal\ntyping of non-ASCII characters by ibus. Therefore, we should use\n`eKeyPress` more on Linux. Now, we do that if we receive a commit signal\nwithout composing state if and only if we're calling\n`gtk_im_context_filter_keypress()`. This is enough for Ubuntu and\nDebian users.\n\nHowever, surprisingly, ibus behaves differently in some environments\nwhen typing a character without composing state.\n\nBasically, it works as on Ubuntu and Debian:\n1. Filter the first `GDK_KEY_PRESS`\n2. Synthesize the same event as the filtered one\n3. While a call of `gtk_im_context_filter_keypress()`, send composition signals\n\nHowever, on Linux Mint:\n1. Filter the first `GDK_KEY_PRESS`\n2. Send composition signals\n\nSo, the copy of the first event is not sent as expected. Therefore, we\nneed to pick the `GDK_KEY_PRESS` event up from the copies of the first\nevents which were filtered by IME.\n\n(Even on Linux Mint, `GDK_KEY_RELEASE` events are handled with\nsynthesizing a copy of the first `GDK_KEY_RELEASE`.)\n\nHowever, in this case, we don't dispatch `eKeyPress` events because\nwe are not calling `gtk_im_context_filter_keypress()`. So, no fallback\n`eKeyPress` event dispatcher is not there.\n\nTo solve this issue, this patch makes `GDKEventKeyQueue` manages the\nfiltered event state with 3 states.\n1. Whether the synthesized event is received\n2. Whether a composition signal is received\n3. Whether the synthesized event is processed completely\n\nThen, `OnKeyEvent` considers whether the received event is unexpected\nsynthesized event which does not have `IBUS_IGNORED_MASK` flag with\nchecking whether it's not handled nor processed.\n\nEach composition signal mark the handling event or the oldest\nnon-processed `GDK_KEY_PRESS` event in the queue as handled.\n\n`OnKeyEvent` removes handled events from the queue if its synthesized\nevent hasn't been received but it's already been handled by a signal\nhandler.\n\nFinally, we should dispatch `eKeyPress` event if we receive a commit\nsignal without composing state even when it's not called during a call\nof `gtk_im_context_filter_keypress()`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314539\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.h", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.h"], "git_node": "8a8edef49eebe25797d0064b482d3d2efab039ab", "git_parents": ["b822beffd1947a6da6fca5fb58634402111fdb3c"], "node": "388857f92acbff6d5375b05bd9531acb0cc9b010", "parents": ["3b0083933b75ced04e578297259636699e7aa86c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054529 - [Monitor Agent][FE] Move hardcded string to locals preview file r=yjamora,fluent-reviewers,bolsson import uuid\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314066\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/agent-monitor-item/agent-monitor-item.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-tasks/ai-tasks.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-tasks/ai-tasks.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/monitors-display/monitors-display.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aiChatContent.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/tasks.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_item.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_monitor_create.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/test_agent_monitor_item_page.html", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "1ce67dcb6ce019322dd68470c0ee960bbc21c766", "git_parents": ["8a8edef49eebe25797d0064b482d3d2efab039ab"], "node": "0faca76bc591445f1de70a0081901faea33c8242", "parents": ["388857f92acbff6d5375b05bd9531acb0cc9b010"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Timothy Nikkel \u003ctnikkel@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058355. Upgrade jxl-rs to 0.5.1. r=saschanaz,supply-chain-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314863\n", "files": [".cargo/config.toml.in", "Cargo.lock", "Cargo.toml", "image/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml", "supply-chain/audits.toml", "supply-chain/config.toml", "supply-chain/imports.lock", "third_party/rust/jxl/.cargo-checksum.json", "third_party/rust/jxl/.cargo_vcs_info.json", "third_party/rust/jxl/Cargo.lock", "third_party/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml", "third_party/rust/jxl/Cargo.toml.orig", "third_party/rust/jxl/README.md", "third_party/rust/jxl/benches/blending.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/color.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/data_types.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/decoder.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/inner/box_parser.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/inner/codestream_parser/frame_info.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/inner/codestream_parser/frame_scan_info.rs", "third_party/rust/jxl/src/api/inner/c