sInSyncMode()` for the newer ibus r=m_kato\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8ba2c2e3167041aa6bbf279a1cbbb420f1bc5a03.\n", "files": ["widget/IMEData.cpp", "widget/IMEData.h", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.cpp", "widget/gtk/IMContextWrapper.h", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsGtkKeyUtils.h"], "git_node": "878b64a4c024f657de81fb66a1e7de1aaad9109c", "git_parents": ["fed3468708c4cae84d63a60612b1b9384bba68ab"], "node": "ff789e9f149e00980fe9a47c69751b78848367fd", "parents": ["3a9b17dbd2a9967fe3e8caf2d7bf7ceb0c0fbb10"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785418058, "git_changesets": ["878b64a4c024f657de81fb66a1e7de1aaad9109c"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "44993": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 70679dc17d13e6a5082805d9823d62ece968cd81 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_153_0_2_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "44675888e529be724ea22e6275a50f522b68f203", "git_parents": ["2d6a09b064082bfca4f19deec41b2870bcb28e0e"], "node": "f6c872a50a003443800f8bb781603eacc51c8d9d", "parents": ["c2bc15c9dd71bbfd1ca4b98807f00aeba01311e6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785431672, "git_changesets": ["44675888e529be724ea22e6275a50f522b68f203"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "44994": {"changesets": [{"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-bqi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-sat/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-bqi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-sat/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ar/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-bg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-de/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-dsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-en-rGB/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-gl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-it/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-iw/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ko/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nn-rNO/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rPT/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sk/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sv-rSE/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-vi/strings.xml"], "git_node": "d3d91edda3fddfd609d7816a78b01ae2686ede6a", "git_parents": ["fed3468708c4cae84d63a60612b1b9384bba68ab"], "node": "d4535889055bb21c30208dbe42b766c6b385f0fa", "parents": ["3a9b17dbd2a9967fe3e8caf2d7bf7ceb0c0fbb10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056322 - Remove selectableProfiles Nimbus feature r=jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314541\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_test_nimbus_feature.js", "toolkit/components/nimbus/FeatureManifest.yaml"], "git_node": "5ef05eb9716268dbe97cef9b92164a13851edd23", "git_parents": ["d3d91edda3fddfd609d7816a78b01ae2686ede6a"], "node": "395ed0d3ea20751814f50faceff3c7771c82dcd7", "parents": ["d4535889055bb21c30208dbe42b766c6b385f0fa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057365 - Don't hold a suspend inhibitor for a backgrounded video-playing wake lock on GTK r=emilio\n\nA muted autoplay video still holds the \"video-playing\" wake lock: that lock is\ntaken whenever a playing video has an audio track, and muting only silences the\ntrack without removing it. On GTK, once such a video's tab or subframe is\nbackgrounded, that lock becomes a GNOME SUSPEND inhibitor and blocks the system\nfrom sleeping. Because the video is silent, the tab shows no sound indicator, so\nnothing tells the user what is keeping the machine awake.\n\nGTK was the only backend doing this: macOS, Windows and Android all release\nthe video lock once it is backgrounded. Genuinely audible background playback\nis covered by the separate \"audio-playing\" topic, so a backgrounded\nvideo-playing lock should hold no inhibitor at all.\n\nRelease both the foreground (IDLE) and background (SUSPEND) inhibitors when a\nvideo-playing lock goes to locked-background. Foreground video still holds an\nIDLE inhibitor to keep the display awake.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314022\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/WakeLockListener.cpp"], "git_node": "c2b3867edf5aba188ae040d4db990b17cc8a633c", "git_parents": ["5ef05eb9716268dbe97cef9b92164a13851edd23"], "node": "885b53420b218c49c69aee6d183e684dc4b579e0", "parents": ["395ed0d3ea20751814f50faceff3c7771c82dcd7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058771 - Only keep animation elements alive when a compositor refers to them.\n\nBug 1347168 added an array holding a strong reference to every registered\nanimation element for the duration of SMILAnimationController::DoSample,\nbecause SMILCompositor stores raw SMILAnimationFunction pointers owned by\nthose elements and composing can run script.\n\nThat reference is only load-bearing for elements that actually contributed\nan entry to the compositor table. Animation elements with no resolvable\ntarget attribute never reach a compositor, so holding them costs an addref\nand a release per element per tick for nothing.\n\nHave AddAnimationToCompositorTable report whether it added an entry and only\nhold elements that did. Also drop the now-pointless capacity reservation,\nwhich allocated an array sized for every animation element in the document\non every sample.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314289\n", "files": ["dom/smil/SMILAnimationController.cpp", "dom/smil/SMILAnimationController.h"], "git_node": "2552ace197aff3914c4111e4f7d8ec6186194bf5", "git_parents": ["c2b3867edf5aba188ae040d4db990b17cc8a633c"], "node": "761d9c8cbaa61a8c74a6c076ade98e382d9677f6", "parents": ["885b53420b218c49c69aee6d183e684dc4b579e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050189 - migrate ssl.npn_type custom distribution to tls.npn_type labeled counter r=djackson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312183\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "3c6f207a3eb4ca6344c0d7021f7c0223f693d1f3", "git_parents": ["2552ace197aff3914c4111e4f7d8ec6186194bf5"], "node": "cfdf233361a2769772b00fd5d0503be4a4de6233", "parents": ["761d9c8cbaa61a8c74a6c076ade98e382d9677f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050189 - migrate ssl.key_exchange_algorithm_{full,resumed} to tls.key_exchange_algorithm dual labeled counter r=djackson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312184\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "6b7db7847364da0f72651d5e7a277ba4f7d3ad9c", "git_parents": ["3c6f207a3eb4ca6344c0d7021f7c0223f693d1f3"], "node": "1f5206c29f18b8664732156125c1087c76f508e8", "parents": ["cfdf233361a2769772b00fd5d0503be4a4de6233"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050189 - migrate ssl.reasons_for_not_false_starting custom distribution to tls.reasons_for_not_false_starting labeled counter r=djackson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312185\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "5cca6c09422425a1c2b794c5d58c9247aa5d5e43", "git_parents": ["6b7db7847364da0f72651d5e7a277ba4f7d3ad9c"], "node": "633dc69ff713bd4c8f61962a1a786b0ec8cc34aa", "parents": ["1f5206c29f18b8664732156125c1087c76f508e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050189 - remove unnecessary ssl.{kea_rsa,kea_dhe,auth_rsa}_key_size_full telemetry metrics r=djackson\n\nThese were useful when we were deprecating keys less than 2048 bits. We have\nsince done that, and there are no plans to deprecate keys less than some larger\nsize, so this telemetry is unnecessary at this point.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312549\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "ded41a4aee35bcd87dab9886aa8570e811fc190c", "git_parents": ["5cca6c09422425a1c2b794c5d58c9247aa5d5e43"], "node": "37cf51bb7ec6400177edc17be4a7c57021b49eb0", "parents": ["633dc69ff713bd4c8f61962a1a786b0ec8cc34aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050189 - migrate TLS handshake auth and key exchange curve custom distribution telemetry to labeled counters r=djackson\n\nssl.auth_ecdsa_curve_full -\u003e tls.auth_ecdsa_curve\nssl.kea_ecdhe_curve_full -\u003e tls.kea_ecdhe_curve\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312186\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "0917d7982e7cecf0c9a532f561e3a68b5a7d4b94", "git_parents": ["ded41a4aee35bcd87dab9886aa8570e811fc190c"], "node": "539684f29154323b805cde99c33b907a375c5d36", "parents": ["37cf51bb7ec6400177edc17be4a7c57021b49eb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dana Keeler \u003cdkeeler@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050189 - migrate ssl.auth_algorithm_full custom distribution to tls.auth_algorithm labeled counter r=djackson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312187\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/metrics.yaml", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCallbacks.cpp"], "git_node": "852438554377a308a76628f54406684f5d183edb", "git_parents": ["0917d7982e7cecf0c9a532f561e3a68b5a7d4b94"], "node": "a48995743f1ccd1ed50a6f59dc6045a6fd8eecf4", "parents": ["539684f29154323b805cde99c33b907a375c5d36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Add generated Android sources r=nalexander\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292619\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/ads-client/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/adsclient/ads_client.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/autofill/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/autofill/autofill.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/crashtest/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/crashtest/crashtest.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/errorsupport/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/errorsupport/errorsupport.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/fxaclient/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/fxaclient/fxa_client.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/init_rust_components/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/init_rust_components/init_rust_components.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/logins/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/logins/logins.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/merino/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/merino/merino.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/nimbus/android/src/main/java/org/mozilla/experiments/nimbus/internal/nimbus.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/places/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/places/uniffi/places.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/push/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/push/push.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/relay/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/relay/relay.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/remotesettings/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/remotesettings/remote_settings.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/rust-log-forwarder/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/rust_log_forwarder/rust_log_forwarder.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/search/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/search/search.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/suggest/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/suggest/suggest.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/sync15/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/sync15/sync15.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/syncmanager/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/syncmanager/syncmanager.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/tabs/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/remotetabs/tabs.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/tracing/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/tracing/tracing.kt", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/android/components/viaduct/android/src/main/java/mozilla/appservices/viaduct/viaduct.kt", "tools/rewriting/Generated.txt"], "git_node": "2f694b6f3418e2112a4059534f96913f3fd503ec", "git_parents": ["852438554377a308a76628f54406684f5d183edb"], "node": "12576c89b83b701a13bc95eca8cfae983a9aced5", "parents": ["a48995743f1ccd1ed50a6f59dc6045a6fd8eecf4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055211 - Part 1: Implement HTML PR #10327. r=jonco\n\nDon't cache modules with HTTP errors, this allows devs to retry the imports if\nit was failed due to network failure.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313493\n", "files": ["js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp"], "git_node": "e43b0f7cf3e5b081ef6c94c3b33134582ae5e057", "git_parents": ["2f694b6f3418e2112a4059534f96913f3fd503ec"], "node": "a15c4b8a74c1c4506ddcac50824745586be4aa35", "parents": ["12576c89b83b701a13bc95eca8cfae983a9aced5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055211 - Part 2: Update wpt ini files. r=jonco\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313494\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/css-module/repeated-import.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/json-module/repeated-imports.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/concurrent-failed-imports.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/concurrent-failed-imports.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/repeated-imports.any.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/dynamic-import/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/module/shared-dependency-repeated-import.html.ini"], "git_node": "3c2347fd2d361d9642bac30fecd4733d942e4297", "git_parents": ["e43b0f7cf3e5b081ef6c94c3b33134582ae5e057"], "node": "7aa823c607f07bf0a9defaf0bb55f7effcceea9e", "parents": ["a15c4b8a74c1c4506ddcac50824745586be4aa35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055211 - Part 3: Update repeated-imports.any.js in text module. r=eemeli\n\nRe-import a network errored module should succeed now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313495\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/text-module/repeated-imports.any.js"], "git_node": "a31abd45a0ae7d12890cebc14eff0edba4f1471f", "git_parents": ["3c2347fd2d361d9642bac30fecd4733d942e4297"], "node": "f90f44ab849f01ffa55242131a75b6092ea8377d", "parents": ["7aa823c607f07bf0a9defaf0bb55f7effcceea9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055211 - Part 4: Update /preload/modulepreload-sri-(importmap).html. r=jonco\n\nMake sure the \u003cscript\u003e is inserted after \u003clink rel=\"modulepreload\"\u003e is done,\nso the result would be consistent.\n\nOtherwise the \u003cscript\u003e might also be preloaded by the speculative parser and\nwill join a single in-flight fetch with the \u003clink\u003e.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313496\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/preload/modulepreload-sri-importmap.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/preload/modulepreload-sri.html"], "git_node": "219073d4f5e130c6a4ae173e2bc8b0779c5c6aa9", "git_parents": ["a31abd45a0ae7d12890cebc14eff0edba4f1471f"], "node": "b9da6e4f2dc2926cae0eb615ce34d7ae085601d5", "parents": ["f90f44ab849f01ffa55242131a75b6092ea8377d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Hammond \u003cmhammond@skippinet.com.au\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057976 - refactor OAuth access-token retrieval into FxAccountsOAuth. r=skhamis\n\nMove the session-token access-token fetch out of FxAccountsInternal into a\nnew FxAccountsOAuth.getAccessToken(), and have getOAuthToken() use it via\nwithVerifiedAccountState(). This is a pure refactor with no behavior change,\nsetting the framework for moving all of this to using the refresh token\nin bug 2053654.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314298\n", "files": ["services/fxaccounts/FxAccounts.sys.mjs", "services/fxaccounts/FxAccountsOAuth.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "5b3473e600c4592bf3974a4eff4d34ca76df2129", "git_parents": ["219073d4f5e130c6a4ae173e2bc8b0779c5c6aa9"], "node": "1d8be2d91e49f7f4dffb9c48ea3c405335647492", "parents": ["b9da6e4f2dc2926cae0eb615ce34d7ae085601d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Hearsum \u003cben@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058759: remove firefox.exe hardcoding in make_incremental_updates.sh r=releng-reviewers,ahal\n\nThis was added in https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=2058197 as a short term fix to some start-up crashes we were seeing in 153.0 updates. This patch gets rid of that hardcoding, allowing Thunderbird to benefit from the optimized instruction order as well, and clean up the code more generally.\n\nAFAIK the only caller to `make_incremental_update.sh` is `funsize.py`, which is also being updated here so there should be no risk to changing the required arguments.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315041\n", "files": ["taskcluster/docker/funsize-update-generator/scripts/funsize.py", "tools/update-packaging/make_incremental_update.sh", "tools/update-packaging/test/buildrefmars.sh"], "git_node": "9567793acfc9177efc2540e1c4ce712bc8a144ee", "git_parents": ["5b3473e600c4592bf3974a4eff4d34ca76df2129"], "node": "edc056019f09c889303f91b709772a8aec06c977", "parents": ["1d8be2d91e49f7f4dffb9c48ea3c405335647492"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050584. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313883\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLFramebuffer.cpp", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/generated/generated-mochitest-webgl2-core-conformance2.toml", "dom/canvas/test/webgl-conf/mochitest-errata.toml"], "git_node": "46d165bccd8e120d60bdbc76ea4868d9454a8b6e", "git_parents": ["9567793acfc9177efc2540e1c4ce712bc8a144ee"], "node": "6bfb9f58b2ba8831a4181eaad0e49728de3a8f3a", "parents": ["edc056019f09c889303f91b709772a8aec06c977"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kui-Feng Lee \u003cthinker.li@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2039706 - capture wl_display.error message in wayland-proxy r=stransky\n\nWhen the compositor sends a wl_display.error referencing an already-destroyed\nserver-allocated object (e.g. a wl_data_offer torn down during drag-and-drop),\nlibwayland's wl_closure_lookup_objects fails the object lookup and logs only\n\"unknown object (N), message error(ous)\" -- the real error code and message\nare discarded before display_handle_error runs, so WlLogHandler crashes\nwithout the actual reason.\n\nAdd an opt-in capture in wayland-proxy: parse the compositor-\u003eapplication byte\nstream (keeping message-boundary alignment across arbitrarily-split reads) and\nstash the message string of the latest wl_display.error.\nWlLogHandler_UnknownObject() then appends it to the crash reason. That is the\nonly pattern where libwayland has thrown the compositor's text away, so the\nother handlers are left alone.\n\nSetCaptureProtocolErrors() has to run before WaylandProxy::Create(): the\nscanner tracks message boundaries from the first byte the proxy forwards, and\nWayland has no marker to resync on, so switching capture on later would start\nthe parser in the middle of a message. That is too early in startup for a\npreference, so the switch is a Nightly build default that the environment\nvariable MOZ_WAYLAND_PROTOCOL_ERROR_DETAILS overrides.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D308696\n", "files": ["third_party/wayland-proxy/wayland-proxy.cpp", "third_party/wayland-proxy/wayland-proxy.h", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWaylandDisplay.cpp"], "git_node": "5e2c84add892e9914852686fb9c6ae8126308695", "git_parents": ["46d165bccd8e120d60bdbc76ea4868d9454a8b6e"], "node": "1b3c06c8d792e827770c51112ca72c0f50fcf129", "parents": ["6bfb9f58b2ba8831a4181eaad0e49728de3a8f3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055710 - Enable the Audio Session API on Nightly. r=webidl,media-playback-reviewers,smaug,chunmin\n\nTurn on the navigator.audioSession surface, its state changes, and the block on\na page starting its own audio while the platform has that audio interrupted, so\nthe feature gets real-world exposure on Nightly while staying off on Beta and\nRelease.\n\nAlso let GeckoView shape its platform audio-focus request after the session\ntype. Without it the type a page picks would reach no platform at all, because\nGeckoView is its only consumer and desktop has none, leaving the type observable\nonly through telemetry.\n\nExposing the API also puts an AudioSession global on Nightly, which the\ninterface exposure test tracks.\n\nhttps://w3c.github.io/audio-session/\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315078\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "f4f728a6fab40549f63558c2ca86655768de1a16", "git_parents": ["5e2c84add892e9914852686fb9c6ae8126308695"], "node": "b97dd51df19c05340bbf21147d1c5110993c44bc", "parents": ["1b3c06c8d792e827770c51112ca72c0f50fcf129"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057116 - Only initialize the remote media engine once. r=media-playback-reviewers,chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314069\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/MFMediaEngineParent.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/MFMediaEngineParent.h"], "git_node": "2f622e23ce55cf5d503732a1f1073ed17fe9f3f8", "git_parents": ["f4f728a6fab40549f63558c2ca86655768de1a16"], "node": "e73ca8fedd6dbf9c5439c7c229ed7110ef146041", "parents": ["b97dd51df19c05340bbf21147d1c5110993c44bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035575 - Point the Android `glean-build` at the `glean_parser` venv r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers,geckoview-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313320\n", "files": ["config/makefiles/rust.mk"], "git_node": "87a9fad7336c88f0f18d78547c55bf22713633fb", "git_parents": ["2f622e23ce55cf5d503732a1f1073ed17fe9f3f8"], "node": "cc90095f1c0e99b0de2ed8c41986b16d0ced601f", "parents": ["e73ca8fedd6dbf9c5439c7c229ed7110ef146041"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Wire `mozbuild-rustlib` through application-services NSS link chain r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe `mozbuild` crate now exposes `link_nss` and `link_nss_rustlib` so that\n`application-services` build scripts can link NSS from the objdir. `link_nss`\nemits cargo directives for the NSS shared libraries in `dist/bin`, and\n`link_nss_rustlib` adds static `mozpkix` and `pure_virtual` on top.\n\nFor those directives to resolve, the libraries they name have to be in\n`dist/lib`, and some of them were not installed there before. `mozpkix` is a\ngyp `static_library`, so a new `install_static_libs` option on `GYP_DIRS`\nmarks it for installation to `dist/lib` without forcing `DIST_INSTALL` on\nevery target in the gyp directory. `pure_virtual` gets `DIST_INSTALL`\ndirectly. On Windows the shared library import libs are installed to\n`dist/lib` too, so the dylib directives can find them at link time.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306609\n", "files": ["build/pure_virtual/moz.build", "build/rust/mozbuild/generate_buildconfig.py", "build/rust/mozbuild/lib.rs", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/context.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/gyp_reader.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/nss_libs.py", "security/moz.build"], "git_node": "d1f9d2e19f5e549c678c513e1990dd90dc56b862", "git_parents": ["87a9fad7336c88f0f18d78547c55bf22713633fb"], "node": "7891ad66e2f9f656207d2be1e6fa29c5c85b4a1b", "parents": ["cc90095f1c0e99b0de2ed8c41986b16d0ced601f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Add `uniffi-target` encapsulating build steps for `./mach uniffi generate` r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers\n\n`./mach uniffi generate` needs three artifacts that don't belong in the\ndefault build: the host bindgen tool, gkrust-uniffi-components, and the\nbindings test fixtures. This groups them under a new `uniffi-target`\noutput category so they only build when uniffi generation runs. Libxul\nstill pulls gkrust-uniffi-components via its Cargo path dep, activating\njust the `mozbuild` feature so the in-tree NSS link works.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292598\n", "files": ["Cargo.lock", "build/workspace-hack/Cargo.toml", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/frontend/test_emitter.py", "toolkit/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/moz.build", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/moz.build", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/test-fixtures/Cargo.toml", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/test-fixtures/moz.build", "toolkit/library/rust/shared/Cargo.toml"], "git_node": "67c91dd6639b0384cafd8a7683b1c488b2e77513", "git_parents": ["d1f9d2e19f5e549c678c513e1990dd90dc56b862"], "node": "bb593e5ab7fd061ae27c2088a5892efe6dbec883", "parents": ["7891ad66e2f9f656207d2be1e6fa29c5c85b4a1b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Make `uniffi-target` build `embedded-uniffi-bindgen` and the megazord r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nThe `embedded-uniffi-bindgen` dependency is obvious.  What's less\nobvious is that the `USE_LIBS` stanza arranges the full `megazord-so`\ndylib to be built by `uniffi-target`.\n\nTwo small supporting build-system changes make that work: the emitter\naccepts Rust libraries with shared `USE_LIBS` (cargo handles actual\nlinking), and category tiers now depend on their members' shared\n`USE_LIBS` so recursing the tier triggers those shared libs' builds.\n\nThis is all in support of `./mach uniffi generate`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292616\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/backend/recursivemake.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/emitter.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/common.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/shared-library-output-category/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/shared-library-output-category/with-output-category/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/data/shared-library-output-category/without-output-category/moz.build", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/test/backend/test_recursivemake.py", "services/app-services-tools/embedded-uniffi-bindgen/moz.build", "services/moz.build", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/components/moz.build"], "git_node": "6cf3aebd6e7a87f38ae6ab3dcfb64b5bb677d11a", "git_parents": ["67c91dd6639b0384cafd8a7683b1c488b2e77513"], "node": "bfc9b9a71c963ae7eee3a173454f290ea7708874", "parents": ["bb593e5ab7fd061ae27c2088a5892efe6dbec883"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Make `./mach uniffi generate` use `uniffi-target` to build binaries and libraries r=nalexander,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`./mach uniffi generate` now drives a dedicated `obj-uniffi-generate`\nbuild through `recurse_uniffi-target` instead of invoking Cargo directly.\nThis routes through mozbuild for proper dependency ordering (NSS, mozglue,\netc.) and keeps the user's main objdir untouched.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292617\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/clobber.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/frontend/data.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/generated_sources.py", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/util.py", "toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "6ede1c85793f678b41a393aefe6a5cda6bd33ac7", "git_parents": ["6cf3aebd6e7a87f38ae6ab3dcfb64b5bb677d11a"], "node": "38dac305f9d0b931a1b4a7f20af8509df757c9d2", "parents": ["bfc9b9a71c963ae7eee3a173454f290ea7708874"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Gate megazord behind `uniffi-target` on non-Android r=nalexander\n\nOn Android, the megazord cdylib ships in the AAR and must always be\nbuilt. On non-Android, it's only needed by `./mach uniffi generate`\n(and indirectly by desktop libsForTests), so move both\n`RustLibrary(\"megazord\")` and `SharedLibrary(\"megazord-so\")` under the\n`uniffi-target` output category there.\n\niOS needs CoreFoundation linked just like macOS does, so the megazord\ndylib keys the framework on `OS_TARGET == \"Darwin\"` to cover both.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298757\n", "files": ["third_party/application-services/megazords/fenix-dylib/moz.build", "third_party/application-services/megazords/full/moz.build"], "git_node": "cfd563e17a59b299ed5d5a836f0eae401101e599", "git_parents": ["6ede1c85793f678b41a393aefe6a5cda6bd33ac7"], "node": "df1594680c740dffdd0ad4b786f2d9d04ec3afb9", "parents": ["38dac305f9d0b931a1b4a7f20af8509df757c9d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033123 - Make `./mach uniffi generate` generate Android Kotlin sources r=nalexander\n\n`./mach uniffi generate` now also produces the Kotlin bindings for\nAndroid, which get committed to the source tree for gradle to consume.\nOn Windows, the cdylib doesn't preserve Rust `pub static` items through\nthe MSVC link, so `embedded-uniffi-bindgen` reads the megazord staticlib\ndirectly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D292618\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/uniffi-bindgen-gecko-js/mach_commands.py"], "git_node": "d6f35f2932b0d4b1976a86cb8945ea971a6c672c", "git_parents": ["cfd563e17a59b299ed5d5a836f0eae401101e599"], "node": "8fe5e85afcfee196509d63a14da2ddf0dca8f53a", "parents": ["df1594680c740dffdd0ad4b786f2d9d04ec3afb9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057115 - Synchronize access to the CDM proxy state. r=media-playback-reviewers,chunmin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314070\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFCDMProxy.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/wmf/MFCDMProxy.h"], "git_node": "b43d2fb1b75472ecd2e38b9a1c7a51775b078a9d", "git_parents": ["d6f35f2932b0d4b1976a86cb8945ea971a6c672c"], "node": "c9307f7e747fbfdb67c3c1072feec871a72fe3f0", "parents": ["8fe5e85afcfee196509d63a14da2ddf0dca8f53a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054626 - Check for end of charstring. r=jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312931\n", "files": ["gfx/cairo/cairo/src/cairo-cff-subset.c", "gfx/cairo/patches/0047-Bug-2054626-type2-decode-integer.patch"], "git_node": "3e4cf6ba038e6f6b82f6f445204c02dc7a28fc81", "git_parents": ["b43d2fb1b75472ecd2e38b9a1c7a51775b078a9d"], "node": "6a583f98a8c936e37bb1e6fb4ad483af926a197e", "parents": ["c9307f7e747fbfdb67c3c1072feec871a72fe3f0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055710 - Enable the Audio Session API on Nightly. r=webidl,media-playback-reviewers,smaug,chunmin\" for causing devtools and mochitest chrome failures\n\nThis reverts commit f4f728a6fab40549f63558c2ca86655768de1a16.\n", "files": ["dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "b868a26fc3b46b3e9e4a131e42148be7f7768b69", "git_parents": ["3e4cf6ba038e6f6b82f6f445204c02dc7a28fc81"], "node": "43da4148bb64161862dc536f423fa6fa7cbf1545", "parents": ["6a583f98a8c936e37bb1e6fb4ad483af926a197e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054842. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312213\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp"], "git_node": "55cf76d00b5a71083246f386087c69fd152db4f1", "git_parents": ["b868a26fc3b46b3e9e4a131e42148be7f7768b69"], "node": "e8d0360ff3f4bce53c1740da966160499caaee5d", "parents": ["43da4148bb64161862dc536f423fa6fa7cbf1545"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058884 - Fix verifyTheTranslatePageSubMenuOptionTest efficiency UI test r=aaronmt\n\nThe UI test was flaky because the translation sheet failed to dismiss after clicking the \u2018Translate\u2019 button.\nThis occurred because the test attempted to interact with the sheet before it was fully expanded.\nTo fix this, I added a verification step to ensure the translation sheet elements are fully loaded and ready before clicking the button.\n\nThe UI test successfully passed 50x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314933\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/BrowserPageSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/MainMenuTest.kt"], "git_node": "2f8e67ed99fbd19b2295f183263ea951bd697c03", "git_parents": ["55cf76d00b5a71083246f386087c69fd152db4f1"], "node": "3ee30075989d96eac9415694d0f8c63c54f3ed30", "parents": ["e8d0360ff3f4bce53c1740da966160499caaee5d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2054842. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\" for causing build bustages at gfxDWriteFontList.cpp\n\nThis reverts commit 55cf76d00b5a71083246f386087c69fd152db4f1.\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/CoreTextFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxDWriteFontList.cpp", "gfx/thebes/gfxFT2FontList.cpp"], "git_node": "92121942e8844ddf7dcb17617f51414cd2ff7658", "git_parents": ["2f8e67ed99fbd19b2295f183263ea951bd697c03"], "node": "04970c743ef301ca8c4d97bd3afc38944044d98e", "parents": ["3ee30075989d96eac9415694d0f8c63c54f3ed30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053970 - Move the pointer off the rows before testing result explanations r=urlbar-reviewers,adw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314844\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_result_explanations.js"], "git_node": "65fd6cd3dc7133f21aa8b8ca63258a236d3a7f9e", "git_parents": ["92121942e8844ddf7dcb17617f51414cd2ff7658"], "node": "161760a0e09b070469d46604adc28d3be8a2c2f5", "parents": ["04970c743ef301ca8c4d97bd3afc38944044d98e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003cs@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058179 - Add a .watchmanconfig to exclude in-tree objdirs from watchman r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nWithout a .watchmanconfig, watchman watches the whole source tree including the\nin-tree objdir. Watchman's default ignore_vcs covers .git, but build output is\nnot covered. On a Linux checkout this accounted for ~9600 extra inotify watches,\nand a build's event burst can overflow fs.inotify.max_queued_events (16384 by\ndefault), which forces a watchman recrawl.\n\nA recrawl makes git's core.fsmonitor hook report a fresh instance, which\ninvalidates git's untracked cache. The next `git status` then calls opendir() on\n41713 directories instead of 0, costing roughly 1.2s extra on a 472k-file\ncheckout.\n\nBoth obj*/ and artifacts/ are already gitignored, so suppressing watchman events\nfor them cannot cause git to miss a change.\n\nignore_dirs does not support globs, so the entries have to be exact paths: the\ndefault obj-@CONFIG_GUESS@ names produced by mach plus a few common mozconfig\nconventions. Developers using another objdir name can add their own, and an\nobjdir outside the source tree needs no entry at all. The file has to stay\nstrict JSON, because watchman silently discards the entire config if it contains\ncomments.\n\nDONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314383\n", "files": [".watchmanconfig", "moz.build"], "git_node": "aefee1489afe9931754c826bbee2556c45c914b4", "git_parents": ["65fd6cd3dc7133f21aa8b8ca63258a236d3a7f9e"], "node": "7860e912b538a488ec984e4120608d5bdf4e8502", "parents": ["161760a0e09b070469d46604adc28d3be8a2c2f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\naf -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nan -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nar -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nast -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\naz -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbe -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbg -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbn -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbo -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbqi -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbr -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbrx -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nbs -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nca -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nca-valencia -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\ncak -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nckb -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\ncs -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\ncy -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nda -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nde -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\ndsb -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nel -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nen-CA -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nen-GB -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\neo -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nes-AR -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nes-CL -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nes-ES -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7f9\nes-MX -\u003e 15168854110d36b2249f60a954876fb72dd6a7