rovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035439 - [wdspec] Make \"get_document_focus\" a fixture. r=jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314622\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/__init__.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/activate/activate.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/create/background.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/browsing_context/create/type.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/support/bidi/fixtures.py"], "git_node": "2a20464df091c67d82e8c046137be771ce5ea7ef", "git_parents": ["d158559ee71cc1a1f3080b149805b61d7882b20a"], "node": "1b5d8b7663287a31023e20a348525497c9cabb98", "parents": ["0a81792cc5532017e5c6972e8c5aa74a991e564b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035439 - Add tests for focus positioning when starting a download. r=jdescottes\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314623\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/bidi/browser/set_download_behavior/download_behavior_allowed.py", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/webdriver/classic/element_click/download_focus.py"], "git_node": "79ef81e002f3e266c47fa5e9db52d1955fe28d6d", "git_parents": ["2a20464df091c67d82e8c046137be771ce5ea7ef"], "node": "4ca09fa6b1e8e5130bed91722ceee93f81230d7d", "parents": ["1b5d8b7663287a31023e20a348525497c9cabb98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Adam Vandolder \u003cavandolder@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058157 - Add DOM use counters for Speculation Rules. r=dom-core-reviewers,jjaschke\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314362\n", "files": ["dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.cpp", "dom/base/SpeculationRuleSet.h", "dom/base/SpeculationRules.cpp", "dom/base/UseCounters.conf", "dom/base/speculationrules/cbindgen.toml", "dom/base/speculationrules/lib.rs", "dom/base/speculationrules/parser.rs", "dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_use_counters.js", "dom/base/test/file_use_counter_speculationrules.html", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "329010ac2c86e8ac274bb567478a0f47f48dab51", "git_parents": ["79ef81e002f3e266c47fa5e9db52d1955fe28d6d"], "node": "2cfd89575c63ca4be8848a4938da2f4d891b0168", "parents": ["4ca09fa6b1e8e5130bed91722ceee93f81230d7d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Michael Kaply \u003cmozilla@kaply.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2035221 - Allow wallpaper upload when remote settings unavailable r=nina-py\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D299877\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_WallpaperFeed.js"], "git_node": "eb539ac3cb4825b84faaec91ba2192cb55b8c4eb", "git_parents": ["329010ac2c86e8ac274bb567478a0f47f48dab51"], "node": "11ea6ee3b597639edf5ccfbf207f0bd07f6d55c9", "parents": ["2cfd89575c63ca4be8848a4938da2f4d891b0168"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059287 - [loong64] Add div/rem Ion codegen tests. r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315145\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/lib/codegen-loong64-test.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binop-divrem-with-constant-loong64-ion-codegen.js"], "git_node": "96b549af9f193191f61fc7881ba3367b1d469759", "git_parents": ["eb539ac3cb4825b84faaec91ba2192cb55b8c4eb"], "node": "8509c783d702cf06e0285df16a5805e5eb03e647", "parents": ["11ea6ee3b597639edf5ccfbf207f0bd07f6d55c9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rong Bao \u003cwebmaster@csmantle.top\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059293 - [loong64] Relax register allocation for L{Div,Mod}PowTwoI. r=jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315154\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binop-divrem-with-constant-loong64-ion-codegen.js", "js/src/jit/loong64/Lowering-loong64.cpp"], "git_node": "3a041f9d307dd9d47b0a5759d72a71f73e7b33b8", "git_parents": ["96b549af9f193191f61fc7881ba3367b1d469759"], "node": "7ed2ccc1c10262f5e05e7e761bacfa55dd4b9e4a", "parents": ["8509c783d702cf06e0285df16a5805e5eb03e647"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059572 - Only retain as much memory as a captured stack needs, r=profiler-reviewers,canova.\n\nStacks are captured into a buffer that can hold the deepest possible stack,\n128KB, and callers that keep a captured backtrace alive retained all of it.\nTimeout keeps one per pending setTimeout(), so a page scheduling timers faster\nthan they fire could retain tens of GB of mostly unused buffers.\n\nCopy the captured stack into a buffer sized to what it actually used before\nhanding it to the caller.\n\nCopyToRightSizedBuffer lives in baseprofiler's platform.cpp rather than in\nBaseAndGeckoProfilerDetail.cpp, because the latter is also built for\nJS_STANDALONE, where allocating with the vanilla operator new is not allowed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315453\n", "files": ["mozglue/baseprofiler/core/platform.cpp", "mozglue/baseprofiler/public/BaseAndGeckoProfilerDetail.h", "tools/profiler/core/platform.cpp", "tools/profiler/tests/gtest/GeckoProfiler.cpp"], "git_node": "f27d5fe0623a05639d75b6667f9f283968079503", "git_parents": ["3a041f9d307dd9d47b0a5759d72a71f73e7b33b8"], "node": "9dbc889d846b427d040d144eeea18f22e9e6989c", "parents": ["7ed2ccc1c10262f5e05e7e761bacfa55dd4b9e4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan Varga \u003cjvarga@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057579 - Fix invalid coordinate setter tests for CSS transform components; r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nFix the `CSSRotate`, `CSSScale`, and `CSSTranslate` setter tests to use the\n`coord` property from `gInvalidCoordTestCases`.\n\nThe tests previously destructured and assigned a non-existent `value` property,\ncausing `undefined` to be passed to the setters instead of the intended invalid\n`CSSNumericValue`. As a result, the tests did not exercise the numeric type\nvalidation they were intended to cover.\n\nUpdate the expected-failure metadata for the newly exposed failures. The\ncorresponding setter validation is implemented in follow-up patches.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314858\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssRotate.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssScale.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTranslate.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssRotate.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssScale.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-typed-om/stylevalue-subclasses/cssTranslate.tentative.html"], "git_node": "5f2b3468d73e04ce4cd411c36e135a262ac88e17", "git_parents": ["f27d5fe0623a05639d75b6667f9f283968079503"], "node": "f2dd28c62c540d23a98e8d74232ec141cfb0cee9", "parents": ["9dbc889d846b427d040d144eeea18f22e9e6989c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054270 - Scope the tab strip status bar gradient composition to the activity lifecycle r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\n- Scope the gradient overlay Recomposer to the Activity lifecycle so that it will recompose across Activity#recreate, which is how toggling browser mode works.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315532\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/HomeActivity.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/theme/TabStripStatusBarView.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/theme/TabStripStatusBarViewTest.kt"], "git_node": "ba909823d7848eeb5ee1e54696fab0577a52a2d0", "git_parents": ["5f2b3468d73e04ce4cd411c36e135a262ac88e17"], "node": "ff92d770593e6c03fb144bbe93aa3579dbfbf003", "parents": ["f2dd28c62c540d23a98e8d74232ec141cfb0cee9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057117 - Improve shutdown handling for the media engine child actor. r=media-playback-reviewers,azebrowski\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314068\n", "files": ["dom/media/ipc/MFMediaEngineChild.cpp", "dom/media/ipc/MFMediaEngineChild.h"], "git_node": "e24e620ae68ef284b3df0e24fd1e9012b2be36f6", "git_parents": ["ba909823d7848eeb5ee1e54696fab0577a52a2d0"], "node": "9644c3642cabbdd67aa3b677365fbfcd78102ad8", "parents": ["ff92d770593e6c03fb144bbe93aa3579dbfbf003"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Beth Rennie \u003cbeth@brennie.ca\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052677 - Only process legacyHeartbeat in Normandy r=nimbus-reviewers,chumphreys\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315642\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/normandy/lib/RecipeRunner.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/normandy/test/browser/browser_RecipeRunner.js"], "git_node": "c3109aac969dcce6931f70be5f2d4710731cfe8e", "git_parents": ["e24e620ae68ef284b3df0e24fd1e9012b2be36f6"], "node": "e3126868257dbe1e3b21cea4cf03931f8345bf98", "parents": ["9644c3642cabbdd67aa3b677365fbfcd78102ad8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alastor Wu \u003calwu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058165 - Persist a tab's deliberate mute state rather than its live audio mute. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nSession restore now collects tab.muted instead of browser.audioMuted when it\nrecords a tab's mute state. The two are easy to confuse, but they differ in\nmeaning and in lifetime:\n\n- tab.muted is the tab's muted attribute. Only muting through the tab sets it,\n  it is what draws the mute indicator, and it outlives the tab's browsing\n  context.\n- browser.audioMuted is a live read of the media controller's mute state. Any\n  caller that silences the tab sets it, it is invisible on its own, and it is\n  cleared whenever the tab gets a new browsing context.\n\nEvery deliberate mute sets both, but some internal mutes set only the second,\nand those must not be persisted. Closing an audible tab is one of them: Firefox\nsilences it as the close begins so the sound stops at once instead of trailing\nthrough the close animation. Collecting the live state captured that internal\nmute and recorded it as though the user had asked for it, so reopening the tab\ncame back muted.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314724\n", "files": ["browser/components/sessionstore/SessionStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/sessionstore/TabState.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabMediaIndicator/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabMediaIndicator/browser_mute_restore_closed_audible_tab.js"], "git_node": "51f12ad36625f3aeafe7441dbdc6516f276c69f6", "git_parents": ["c3109aac969dcce6931f70be5f2d4710731cfe8e"], "node": "1ebb5e65f66420c38fc7c146c9444c9be4251ae9", "parents": ["e3126868257dbe1e3b21cea4cf03931f8345bf98"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059789 - Update jsoup to version 1.23.1. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315646\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node": "d8cde1f01b167775cbfaaf7fd686a5909db2cb48", "git_parents": ["51f12ad36625f3aeafe7441dbdc6516f276c69f6"], "node": "51a67c83e98a93661e0bb36ed8166732ace9bd42", "parents": ["1ebb5e65f66420c38fc7c146c9444c9be4251ae9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059053 - Part 2: Disallow retrieving push subscription in partitioned worker r=asuth\" for causing wpt failures @ push-api/worker-subscribe.https.window.html\n\nThis reverts commit 36ebdc894327fa71778d42f41efc794d1560b4bf.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059053 - Part 1: Add tests for push subscribes r=asuth\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2db1faa852243a2f25263f39ad8fc4f9259bf505.\n", "files": ["dom/push/PushManager.cpp", "dom/push/test/mochitest.toml", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/cross-origin-nested.tentative.https.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/cross-origin-same-site-request.tentative.https.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/cross-origin-serviceworker.tentative.https.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/resources/cross-origin-nested-child.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/resources/cross-origin-nested-parent.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/resources/cross-origin-serviceworker-iframe.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/resources/permission-helper.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/resources/permission-sw.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/resources/permission-worker.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/push-api/worker-subscribe.https.window.js"], "git_node": "cbc584367e1167d95d41ad2568ac45b5b8be37f1", "git_parents": ["d8cde1f01b167775cbfaaf7fd686a5909db2cb48"], "node": "cc6171c229a72c52cc2972f23dec6f44fd8b3d48", "parents": ["51a67c83e98a93661e0bb36ed8166732ace9bd42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sajid Anwar \u003csajidanwar94@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059737 - Fix WPTs for CSS alpha() resolved value serialization. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315606\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-color/parsing/alpha-color-computed.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-color/parsing/alpha-color-computed.html"], "git_node": "04dd130606c0493f2d6744153b39746e534d3a2e", "git_parents": ["cbc584367e1167d95d41ad2568ac45b5b8be37f1"], "node": "bd6d8ad1e75952778859a960d7e3c5a93fa35adc", "parents": ["cc6171c229a72c52cc2972f23dec6f44fd8b3d48"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Katherine Ye \u003ckye@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043000 - Support block-ellipsis values for line-clamp markers. r=dshin,layout-reviewers\n\nAdded wpt for  non-empty custom ellipsis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314664\n", "files": ["layout/generic/TextOverflow.cpp", "layout/generic/TextOverflow.h", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-023.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-024.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/line-clamp-034.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-038.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/block-ellipsis-038-ref.html"], "git_node": "5242e6d6546adeebcd9b3ae46498ba0c94656bb0", "git_parents": ["04dd130606c0493f2d6744153b39746e534d3a2e"], "node": "9c5df4cb2fbd60ac9e66ca19c2a42a7957284408", "parents": ["bd6d8ad1e75952778859a960d7e3c5a93fa35adc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054135: Clean house in our wpt ini files. r=ng\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312114\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc-encoded-transform/RTCEncodedFrame-copy-construction.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc-encoded-transform/RTCRtpScriptTransform-bad-chunk.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc-encoded-transform/RTCRtpScriptTransform-encoded-transform.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc-encoded-transform/RTCRtpSc