097517e40dd8557a9\nms -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nmy -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nnb-NO -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nne-NP -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nnl -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nnn-NO -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\noc -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\npa-IN -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\npl -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\npt-BR -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\npt-PT -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nrm -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nro -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nru -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nsk -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nsl -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nson -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nsq -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nsr -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nsv-SE -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nta -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nte -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nth -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\ntl -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\ntr -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\ntrs -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nuk -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nur -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nuz -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nvi -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nwo -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nxh -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nzam -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nzh-CN -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\nzh-TW -\u003e 2f276e114787d954964bb50097517e40dd8557a9\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "d8c812646e0338fd701bd21649aa6df7bcb9c87b", "git_parents": ["0e22b3b7605f2edd7845e170954880f8bf225a2b"], "node": "dd7f97fe69593b303454920f873996e883af8226", "parents": ["4b4be67952981f5f39e7844b2a1f3050a23da665"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 1 - Report per-scene-build interner insertions and removals to the profiler r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe per-interner counters only expose live entry counts, so intern churn is\ninvisible: a key inserted and garbage-collected every scene build leaves the\ntotals flat. Sum the update-list lengths across every interner instead, and only\nset the counters when a scene build is applied, so an absent value means \"no\nscene built\" rather than \"scene built, nothing new interned\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315448\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs"], "git_node": "333cdf2c672ba3f235a973502faa683cd7f977e2", "git_parents": ["d8c812646e0338fd701bd21649aa6df7bcb9c87b"], "node": "8dea7e616c3d8379bf2dfedbcafb5b1c3df49e35", "parents": ["dd7f97fe69593b303454920f873996e883af8226"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 2 - Add invalidation tests for external-scroll-offset and sticky repaints r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nInterned primitive uids have to stay stable across a content-side scroll: the\ndisplay list builder normalizes each item by the accumulated external scroll\noffset, and subtracts a sticky frame's previously-applied offset. Nothing covered\nthat - test_scroll_subpic only varies the async scroll delta, which never re-runs\nscene building.\n\nEach pair describes the same visual state twice, differing only in how the offset\nis split between baked-into-coordinates and declared-to-WebRender, so the tile\nmust stay valid. Both pairs were confirmed to fail with normalization disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315449\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/eso_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/eso_repaint_2.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/sticky_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/sticky_repaint_2.yaml"], "git_node": "8d41449d5228022ba0a07bdbcdf22c58db716215", "git_parents": ["333cdf2c672ba3f235a973502faa683cd7f977e2"], "node": "b8308585d6cedb14ebd17268a14282b7dda0027f", "parents": ["8dea7e616c3d8379bf2dfedbcafb5b1c3df49e35"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 3 - Normalize external scroll offsets in whole app units r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nNormalizing an item by its accumulated external scroll offset has to be exact, or\nthe coordinates WebRender interns drift with the scroll position even though\nnothing moved on screen. Doing it as p + S in f32 is not exact: Gecko's coordinate\nis p_au / appUnitsPerDevPixel, generally not a binary fraction, so both the\nconversion and the addition round. Quantizing to a finer grid does not help, since\nquantization is not additive. The addition has to happen in the domain the\nsubtraction happened in: Gecko computed p_au = x_au - S_au in integer app units,\nso re-adding S_au as an integer recovers x_au exactly.\n\nCarry accumulated offsets as whole app units, and add them to app-unit\ncoordinates on the grid the producer declares to begin(). Coordinates that are not\nwhole app units on that grid cannot be normalized exactly; they are counted and\nreported as the Off-grid coords profiler counter rather than asserted, since that\nis a producer bug. It reads zero on Gecko today, including with content zoomed\nwhile chrome is not, where the two pipelines' grids differ within one document.\nDisplay lists are built in the content process, so the grid needs no IPC.\n\nThe drift is eliminated: on a static sticky page, sub-pixel movers go from 30 to 0\nat dpr 1.0 and 424 to 0 at 1.3333; on Wikipedia, every scroll pass after the first\nand every idle frame report zero.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315450\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/AsyncImagePipelineManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderLayerManager.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/common/boilerplate.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/document.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/iframe.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/multiwindow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtests/snapping.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "57fa75d9c21fe426d73b28a9c34aaad1810d0a86", "git_parents": ["8d41449d5228022ba0a07bdbcdf22c58db716215"], "node": "ea64058d642b92f016860ec1a90ee7b2bce16430", "parents": ["b8308585d6cedb14ebd17268a14282b7dda0027f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 4 - Remove apz.rounded_external_scroll_offset r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nRounding the external scroll offset to whole device pixels desynchronises it from\nthe position the display items were painted at: it does not cancel the offset\nGecko baked into the coordinates, it replaces one scroll-dependent residue with a\nlarger one. Measured on Wikipedia at dpr 1.3333 with the pref enabled, primitives\nwhose position changed per scene build went from 5297 to 22904, and picture tiles\nrasterized rose 27%. At dpr 1.0 it is a no-op.\n\nPt 3 makes the normalization exact by accumulating in whole app units, which is\nwhat this pref was reaching for, so it has no remaining purpose. Nothing sets it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315451\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/ClipManager.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "0321731e3bf54b2eb20f440d81eedef946f4cf29", "git_parents": ["57fa75d9c21fe426d73b28a9c34aaad1810d0a86"], "node": "dac4877e9935a024f893bf75bd08dd4d112ab4c8", "parents": ["ea64058d642b92f016860ec1a90ee7b2bce16430"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iulian moraru \u003cimoraru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059570 - Pt 4 - Remove apz.rounded_external_scroll_offset r=gfx-reviewers,nical\" for causing webrender build bustages.\n\nThis reverts commit 0321731e3bf54b2eb20f440d81eedef946f4cf29.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059570 - Pt 3 - Normalize external scroll offsets in whole app units r=gfx-reviewers,nical\"\n\nThis reverts commit 57fa75d9c21fe426d73b28a9c34aaad1810d0a86.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059570 - Pt 2 - Add invalidation tests for external-scroll-offset and sticky repaints r=gfx-reviewers,nical\"\n\nThis reverts commit 8d41449d5228022ba0a07bdbcdf22c58db716215.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2059570 - Pt 1 - Report per-scene-build interner insertions and removals to the profiler r=gfx-reviewers,nical\"\n\nThis reverts commit 333cdf2c672ba3f235a973502faa683cd7f977e2.\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/AsyncImagePipelineManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/ClipManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderLayerManager.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/common/boilerplate.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/document.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/iframe.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/multiwindow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/eso_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/eso_repaint_2.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/sticky_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/sticky_repaint_2.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtests/snapping.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "e9c1e4587fbb7efb97b9c756c99c6bb2ba2ab354", "git_parents": ["0321731e3bf54b2eb20f440d81eedef946f4cf29"], "node": "8579ae2f3f74868e2368730487021372bfd1cbeb", "parents": ["dac4877e9935a024f893bf75bd08dd4d112ab4c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings mobile-experiments ct-logs - r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315891\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_experiments.json", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json"], "git_node": "a73226f9736fa89150fd46953ff26d69e509c48a", "git_parents": ["e9c1e4587fbb7efb97b9c756c99c6bb2ba2ab354"], "node": "df85ba43e9966aa9ec8ac053168a058f851dbb13", "parents": ["8579ae2f3f74868e2368730487021372bfd1cbeb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 1 - Report per-scene-build interner insertions and removals to the profiler r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThe per-interner counters only expose live entry counts, so intern churn is\ninvisible: a key inserted and garbage-collected every scene build leaves the\ntotals flat. Sum the update-list lengths across every interner instead, and only\nset the counters when a scene build is applied, so an absent value means \"no\nscene built\" rather than \"scene built, nothing new interned\".\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315448\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/intern.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs"], "git_node": "caeda75826a4ce0635d347bdea1d8b57848207a5", "git_parents": ["a73226f9736fa89150fd46953ff26d69e509c48a"], "node": "1821a70c910c6fe48b96b1b64c22e06662d6864d", "parents": ["df85ba43e9966aa9ec8ac053168a058f851dbb13"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 2 - Add invalidation tests for external-scroll-offset and sticky repaints r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nInterned primitive uids have to stay stable across a content-side scroll: the\ndisplay list builder normalizes each item by the accumulated external scroll\noffset, and subtracts a sticky frame's previously-applied offset. Nothing covered\nthat - test_scroll_subpic only varies the async scroll delta, which never re-runs\nscene building.\n\nEach pair describes the same visual state twice, differing only in how the offset\nis split between baked-into-coordinates and declared-to-WebRender, so the tile\nmust stay valid. Both pairs were confirmed to fail with normalization disabled.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315449\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/eso_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/eso_repaint_2.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/invalidation.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/sticky_repaint_1.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/invalidation/sticky_repaint_2.yaml"], "git_node": "f72ca9c2a4e1426c01f1d044e45e97fa623345a2", "git_parents": ["caeda75826a4ce0635d347bdea1d8b57848207a5"], "node": "82fd51ab52de76fa9a2fd7db5dcd273c6de2063e", "parents": ["1821a70c910c6fe48b96b1b64c22e06662d6864d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 3 - Normalize external scroll offsets in whole app units r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nNormalizing an item by its accumulated external scroll offset has to be exact, or\nthe coordinates WebRender interns drift with the scroll position even though\nnothing moved on screen. Doing it as p + S in f32 is not exact: Gecko's coordinate\nis p_au / appUnitsPerDevPixel, generally not a binary fraction, so both the\nconversion and the addition round. Quantizing to a finer grid does not help, since\nquantization is not additive. The addition has to happen in the domain the\nsubtraction happened in: Gecko computed p_au = x_au - S_au in integer app units,\nso re-adding S_au as an integer recovers x_au exactly.\n\nCarry accumulated offsets as whole app units, and add them to app-unit\ncoordinates on the grid the producer declares to begin(). Coordinates that are not\nwhole app units on that grid cannot be normalized exactly; they are counted and\nreported as the Off-grid coords profiler counter rather than asserted, since that\nis a producer bug. It reads zero on Gecko today, including with content zoomed\nwhile chrome is not, where the two pipelines' grids differ within one document.\nDisplay lists are built in the content process, so the grid needs no IPC.\n\nThe drift is eliminated: on a static sticky page, sub-pixel movers go from 30 to 0\nat dpr 1.0 and 424 to 0 at 1.3333; on Wikipedia, every scroll pass after the first\nand every idle frame report zero.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315450\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/AsyncImagePipelineManager.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderLayerManager.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/common/boilerplate.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/document.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/iframe.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/multiwindow.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/profiler.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_builder_thread.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/shutdown_test.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtests/snapping.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "226cd706cbd59617d36f4cdac11f580189aa8368", "git_parents": ["f72ca9c2a4e1426c01f1d044e45e97fa623345a2"], "node": "cfcc654c5ce376e417a03997f2e9c5e1bb19c9ed", "parents": ["82fd51ab52de76fa9a2fd7db5dcd273c6de2063e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059570 - Pt 4 - Remove apz.rounded_external_scroll_offset r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nRounding the external scroll offset to whole device pixels desynchronises it from\nthe position the display items were painted at: it does not cancel the offset\nGecko baked into the coordinates, it replaces one scroll-dependent residue with a\nlarger one. Measured on Wikipedia at dpr 1.3333 with the pref enabled, primitives\nwhose position changed per scene build went from 5297 to 22904, and picture tiles\nrasterized rose 27%. At dpr 1.0 it is a no-op.\n\nPt 3 makes the normalization exact by accumulating in whole app units, which is\nwhat this pref was reaching for, so it has no remaining purpose. Nothing sets it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315451\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/ClipManager.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "327fb3db124b22062f7e1694da505a7199853774", "git_parents": ["226cd706cbd59617d36f4cdac11f580189aa8368"], "node": "baed5659f21a3cbc4e158e43b8cdd25f31bbe949", "parents": ["cfcc654c5ce376e417a03997f2e9c5e1bb19c9ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060090 - Add a VPN incompatibility warning for www.bbc.co.uk/iplayer r=lesleynorton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315901\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/ipp-activator/extension/breakages/tab.json"], "git_node": "d279259c9db046e312f8007b81f66fa877e3dcc6", "git_parents": ["327fb3db124b22062f7e1694da505a7199853774"], "node": "8740ec25f955fb844779edad6af36827e9809576", "parents": ["baed5659f21a3cbc4e158e43b8cdd25f31bbe949"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-be/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/app-links/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/password-importer/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/protection-dashboard/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/sitepermissions/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-be/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/tabcounter/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/longfox/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-be/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-el/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ja/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml"], "git_node": "df5fe57f52620d7697943af831a7cb31dad91f1d", "git_parents": ["d279259c9db046e312f8007b81f66fa877e3dcc6"], "node": "ba4c486e3ed458368bfab32a577026a3793dc127", "parents": ["8740ec25f955fb844779edad6af36827e9809576"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058008 - Make `TSFTextStoreBase` retrieve TSF attr \u003c-\u003e index with checking its type r=m_kato\n\n`TSFTextStoreBase` should consider the number of supported TSF\nattributes from `IsEditable()` result which indicates whether the\ninstance is `TSFEmptyTextStore` or `TSFTextStore`.\n\nThen, we can simplify the implementation of\n`TSFTextStoreBase::HandleRequestAttrs` and\n`TSFTextStoreBase::RetrieveRequestedAttrsInternal`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314564\n", "files": ["widget/windows/TSFEmptyTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStoreBase.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStoreBase.h", "widget/windows/TSFUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFUtils.h"], "git_node": "0af14c4a6bcb924ae1ae3028374d0038a9521d87", "git_parents": ["df5fe57f52620d7697943af831a7cb31dad91f1d"], "node": "8b2276905422c84386b3b1bcaf6e79874bc95286", "parents": ["ba4c486e3ed458368bfab32a577026a3793dc127"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1906769 - Don't rasterize blobs when the raster scale is degenerate r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nChooseScale substitutes a scale of 1.0 when the real scale is below 1e-8,\non the grounds that the content is scaled out of sight. The blob paths size\ntheir buffers from untransformed bounds, which can reach nscoord saturation,\nso taking that placeholder at face value asks for a 26843546x26843546 blob\nand OOMs while enumerating tiles.\n\nReport the substitution out of ChooseScale and skip the group, fallback and\nmask blobs instead of rasterizing them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315899\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/wr/StackingContextHelper.cpp", "gfx/layers/wr/StackingContextHelper.h", "gfx/layers/wr/WebRenderCommandBuilder.cpp", "layout/svg/crashtests/1906769-1.html", "layout/svg/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": "d217f3afb9e46cd8b421b67f0aa371c8e12e828c", "git_parents": ["0af14c4a6bcb924ae1ae3028374d0038a9521d87"], "node": "45352475ffa4f03f8f4ab1d2ea4adb1d9a76a3cf", "parents": ["8b2276905422c84386b3b1bcaf6e79874bc95286"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059620 - Move the unsnapped prim rect back into the interning key and template r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nThis was initially moved as part of the fractional snapping work, but turned\nout to not be needed. Moving this back to the key/template gets us one\nstep closer to being able to completely remove PrimitiveInstance (and instead\nhave only primitive template and draw instance(s)).\n\nSafe because the display-list builder normalizes the external scroll offset away in\nwhole app units: a uid compare during invalidation is bit-exact, unlike the\nquarter-device-pixel raster corners beside it, so sub-pixel drift in the scroll\nround-trip would invalidate tiles at every offset.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315510\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/cached_surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/line_dec.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/rectangle.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/key_types.rs"], "git_node": "6bfdf0b9d1c8449a900ca3df4378e858966270c4", "git_parents": ["d217f3afb9e46cd8b421b67f0aa371c8e12e828c"], "node": "f5d73ead5679589b60e120bc40d44ac9c430db08", "parents": ["45352475ffa4f03f8f4ab1d2ea4adb1d9a76a3cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yuxiao Zhu \u003cyuxiao.zhu.cn@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1861034 - Apply text range offsets before CSS transforms in query content events. r=masayuki\n\nOnQueryCharacterAtPoint selected the target frame using transform-aware hit\ntesting, but converted the query point to target-frame coordinates using only\nframe offsets and app-unit scaling. This could resolve to a neighboring\ncharacter when the text frame was scaled.\n\nOnQueryTextRect also mixed transformed frame rectangles with untransformed\ncharacter offsets, producing incorrectly positioned or sized text ranges.\n\nTransform query points through the complete frame transform chain, and clip\ntext ranges in frame-local coordinates before converting them to root-relative\ncoordinates. Add regression coverage for horizontally scaled text.\n\nBefore\n{F75908499}\n\nAfter\n{F75908505}\n\nThis also affects Zotero\u2019s PDF reader, which currently ships Gecko 140.12.0esr.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313653\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/test_sendQueryContentAndSelectionSetEvent.html", "dom/events/ContentEventHandler.cpp"], "git_node": "32731ace5f168d6cd64882afa49a36cd62937011", "git_parents": ["6bfdf0b9d1c8449a900ca3df4378e858966270c4"], "node": "b45c40f078fd7b6b2aeb2950d61dc296edae3fd6", "parents": ["f5d73ead5679589b60e120bc40d44ac9c430db08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059620 - Move the unsnapped prim rect back into the interning key and template r=gfx-reviewers,nical\" for causing wrench failures\n\nThis reverts commit 6bfdf0b9d1c8449a900ca3df4378e858966270c4.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/example-compositor/compositor/src/main.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/cached_surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prepare.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/borders.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/gradient/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/line_dec.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/rectangle.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_backend.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/key_types.rs"], "git_node": "b8dc59e56ddd0e22f8350d8253bdd9be3c6f6b9c", "git_parents": ["32731ace5f168d6cd64882afa49a36cd62937011"], "node": "749cb480df3d3514e384b51968677b65eb061136", "parents": ["b45c40f078fd7b6b2aeb2950d61dc296edae3fd6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056856 - Round a bitmap-strike glyph's pen to nearest r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nA glyph that rasterizes from an embedded bitmap strike ignores the sub-pixel\noffset its key asks for and lands on the device grid, so flooring its pen with\nthe sub-pixel bias put it up to 0.875px left of where layout placed it, outside\nits own element. A snapped clip or mask edge then shaved its leading column,\nwhich is what cut the first letter off MS UI Gothic tab titles. Rounding to\nnearest keeps the pen within 0.5px and on the same grid line as a nearest-snapped\nmask edge, so nothing downstream has to compensate.\n\nGlyphFormat::Bitmap and ColorBitmap identify these glyphs exactly: on every\nbackend, the branch that produces them is the branch that discards the sub-pixel\noffset. That is only known after rasterization, so the pen is stored unsnapped\nand snapped in the shader, with the bias chosen by a flag packed into the\ninstance flags at batch time. Snapping a value the shader receives verbatim\nkeeps it bit-exact; re-deriving the pen GPU-side would risk crossing a floor\nboundary at the fractions layout produces.\n\nThe reftest draws Proggy's ppem-11 strike at a range of fractional x positions\nand references each at round(x), with rows either side of the interesting range\nguarding against the pen moving when it should not. Pinned to scale(1.0) because\nthe pen rounds in device space, so the reference position only holds at one\nscale.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315917\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/res/ps_text_run.glsl", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/gpu_types.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2056856-bitmap-pen-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/2056856-bitmap-pen.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "e665c1a3c74852f634e44df92352f305c883af14", "git_parents": ["b8dc59e56ddd0e22f8350d8253bdd9be3c6f6b9c"], "node": "62f45fdc2f797480ea0a1089a1525a4944d42cbe", "parents": ["749cb480df3d3514e384b51968677b65eb061136"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058623 - Make `HTMLWithContextInserter::Run` ensure the new caret is in the found link before trying to split it r=m_kato\n\nAnd also `HTMLWithContextInserter::MoveCaretOutsideOfLink` should not\nrefer the result if it's error.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315135\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDataTransfer.cpp"], "git_node": "1fab04c3f9fe8d72b22d697bcdb501fd2ccebba9", "git_parents": ["e665c1a3c74852f634e44df92352f305c883af14"], "node": "38fabd2e22ca6f3332f7260d5f50ed7cb8ecf9fe", "parents": ["62f45fdc2f797480ea0a1089a1525a4944d42cbe"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785747229, "git_changesets": ["520004520079c851dcac9879440bddeb34afd912", "0e22b3b7605f2edd7845e170954880f8bf225a2b", "d8c812646e0338fd701bd21649aa6df7bcb9c87b", "333cdf2c672ba3f235a973502faa683cd7f977e2", "8d41449d5228022ba0a07bdbcdf22c58db716215", "57fa75d9c21fe426d73b28a9c34aaad1810d0a86", "0321731e3bf54b2eb20f440d81eedef946f4cf29", "e9c1e4587fbb7efb97b9c756c99c6bb2ba2ab354", "a73226f9736fa89150fd46953ff26d69e509c48a", "caeda75826a4ce0635d347bdea1d8b57848207a5", "f72ca9c2a4e1426c01f1d044e45e97fa623345a2", "226cd706cbd59617d36f4cdac11f580189aa8368", "327fb3db124b22062f7e1694da505a7199853774", "d279259c9db046e312f8007b81f66fa877e3dcc6", "df5fe57f52620d7697943af831a7cb31dad91f1d", "0af14c4a6bcb924ae1ae3028374d0038a9521d87", "d217f3afb9e46cd8b421b67f0aa371c8e12e828c", "6bfdf0b9d1c8449a900ca3df4378e858966270c4", "32731ace5f168d6cd64882afa49a36cd62937011", "b8dc59e56ddd0e22f8350d8253bdd9be3c6f6b9c", "e665c1a3c74852f634e44df92352f305c883af14", "1fab04c3f9fe8d72b22d697bcdb501fd2ccebba9"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45010": {"changesets": [{"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060020 - update metadata for mousemove-action-interpolation.html on macos debug\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/uievents/mouse/mousemove-action-interpolation.html.ini"], "git_node": "45135a4adb3c83c65c090e9c613775a5e193aba5", "git_parents": ["1fab04c3f9fe8d72b22d697bcdb501fd2ccebba9"], "node": "fc3948f401b3ed789049f4162edf2e820e80771b", "parents": ["38fabd2e22ca6f3332f7260d5f50ed7cb8ecf9fe"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785747360, "git_changesets": ["45135a4adb3c83c65c090e9c613775a5e193aba5"], "user": "asilaghi@mozilla.com"}, "45011": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 48b2e859736ff45d398343c08118715ef72ff460 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_154_0b6_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "a6d6de850513d750152e72b2cbc54847473bf167", "git_parents": ["db564c9f7ac673cfd5d3fe