"parents": ["1c8cc6a9f2a973bd6a42e362d30b85761aa00cae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060381 - Remove CHROME_PRIVATE_LIFETIME. r=smaug\n\nNoticed while working on bug 2059942. I thought we had no bits. Turns\nout we do, but also this is unused.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315895\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "toolkit/components/browser/nsIWebBrowserChrome.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp"], "git_node": "ce4834e39d686d907b818b57d8fbe6fd8f7afd13", "git_parents": ["09fc731d5343b8a915288770b3c5855efbf415ad"], "node": "3aa0970c1c31d461842d1a66d42fefe786c6d40d", "parents": ["bc2f2ffc8aa5a3e2911d37e28cfd0cbae991e678"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060383 - Remove unused aModifiers argument to content chrome flags computation. r=smaug\n\nNoticed while working on bug 2059942.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316037\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsPIWindowWatcher.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.h"], "git_node": "be778d59e348052882cf0adc58bfe4664e0d8e24", "git_parents": ["ce4834e39d686d907b818b57d8fbe6fd8f7afd13"], "node": "764fd041057d506448afd3d1120e929162bd282e", "parents": ["3aa0970c1c31d461842d1a66d42fefe786c6d40d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060381 - Remove CHROME_WINDOW_BORDERS. r=smaug\n\nNo flag sets it and all the consumers pass it one way or another so we\ncan just remove it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315896\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/browser/nsIWebBrowserChrome.idl", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/nsWindowWatcher.cpp", "toolkit/components/windowwatcher/test/head.js", "xpfe/appshell/nsAppShellService.cpp"], "git_node": "00c837bd6da4d7a34db448c3701f6e19a423dc0d", "git_parents": ["be778d59e348052882cf0adc58bfe4664e0d8e24"], "node": "f1d8b2ceba4186da4ff227096397a9769b66f2ff", "parents": ["764fd041057d506448afd3d1120e929162bd282e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058616 - Don't crash on simplified-out anchor-pos functions. r=TYLin\n\nVarious calc() simplification steps could throw away the anchor-size()\nfunction. Since it's only an optimization to keep track whether there's\nany anchor-size(), just deal with the simplification having thrown it\naway.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316034\n", "files": ["layout/style/nsStyleStruct.cpp", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-size-simplified-crash.html"], "git_node": "2370867dfac51e5ea0848bc01f43ae294af1212e", "git_parents": ["00c837bd6da4d7a34db448c3701f6e19a423dc0d"], "node": "b506ae21b07a6d64c75c653b768379085790a604", "parents": ["f1d8b2ceba4186da4ff227096397a9769b66f2ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmhommey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059623 - Move Windows SDK detection to windows-toolchain.configure. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nwindows.configure is included after the compiler checks, but the Windows\nSDK directory doesn't depend on the compiler in any way. Moving its\ndetection next to the other toolchain path lookups makes it available to\nthings that need to run before the first compiler invocation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315514\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/windows-toolchain.configure", "build/moz.configure/windows.configure"], "git_node": "85f1dec3295146187702c69eb4e3c434e27c290d", "git_parents": ["2370867dfac51e5ea0848bc01f43ae294af1212e"], "node": "f6cde698868ba6c99dd1228793a10ed580c162f7", "parents": ["b506ae21b07a6d64c75c653b768379085790a604"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmhommey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059623 - Set SCCACHE_BASEDIRS in the environment before invoking sccache. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nsccache only reads SCCACHE_BASEDIRS when its server starts, and the\nserver is started by the first sccache invocation, which, during\nconfigure, is one of the compiler checks. Because the variable was only\nexported from config.mk at build time, the daemon left running after\nconfigure had no base directories at all.\n\nCompute the value before the compiler checks and set it in the\nenvironment there, so that the daemon configure starts is configured\ncorrectly, and so that configure's own compilations get the same cache\nkeys as the build's.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315515\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure"], "git_node": "6dc4b2df63f0bec300bb9a260539d41e4e1a3a71", "git_parents": ["85f1dec3295146187702c69eb4e3c434e27c290d"], "node": "6a5437427b8b9d8bdb8d0aa341998e8e2b83153c", "parents": ["f6cde698868ba6c99dd1228793a10ed580c162f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmhommey@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059623 - Pass SCCACHE_BASEDIRS to the sccache daemon managed by client.mk. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\n\nIn automation, the daemon is started from client.mk so that it inherits\nmake's jobserver, but SCCACHE_BASEDIRS is a configure output and client.mk\nonly knows about mozconfig options, so the daemon was started without it.\nAdd it to the environment mach runs client.mk with.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315516\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py"], "git_node": "5aef16c9b58b3e5791f849bdabbf9affb4a96844", "git_parents": ["6dc4b2df63f0bec300bb9a260539d41e4e1a3a71"], "node": "883a33ae6c6a3ac8081cd948e1f9f7b440d29b36", "parents": ["6a5437427b8b9d8bdb8d0aa341998e8e2b83153c"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785817964, "git_changesets": ["eee015fac251a3ec4fa1dbf4e58649b0eb000677", "a4f93c6568619a47cecfe7e5c006845d67df1399", "d79cafd56f18498863b8fedb8e9e2be2467be7bc", "b223385e4a4d25d1c38fb4b9e2e733d3258c29a9", "557dbb9c862a84632970f90d09ed0c1c13b1eb96", "90968236e0b4624ef3ac76a337bce99309c3b788", "c2bb31ec9ee389901cdc81f83723384bff3688ba", "cce7703e1d2f858fe4a229ebd0b330fea143d97c", "9d3074b0f3cd091988a33647298c5d230177d059", "ef9a66d5c28e67a77fa7e80a83dfb2b8a78f60ec", "9440287931e8d3aeab1d1fc0266d150c65d70991", "e71351b6c949a93bcdca01c42b8a8c2be5395013", "cab18aff60c8d352eb0c6d3edb4c9fccc6725d44", "63b39a300e3c7e24ddc86be2d6c58a22d6046fb0", "09fc731d5343b8a915288770b3c5855efbf415ad", "ce4834e39d686d907b818b57d8fbe6fd8f7afd13", "be778d59e348052882cf0adc58bfe4664e0d8e24", "00c837bd6da4d7a34db448c3701f6e19a423dc0d", "2370867dfac51e5ea0848bc01f43ae294af1212e", "85f1dec3295146187702c69eb4e3c434e27c290d", "6dc4b2df63f0bec300bb9a260539d41e4e1a3a71", "5aef16c9b58b3e5791f849bdabbf9affb4a96844"], "user": "agoloman@mozilla.com"}, "45022": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 5ea6f25c57d411c3dea06f0405775b4066302e09 with FIREFOX-ANDROID_153_0_3_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "ad48002cd43493881c3d8f12d1c7fbcf2f374c95", "git_parents": ["38b512743f5593b5958912ae7413757ef6992c00"], "node": "fc72221cd30ea6e4c0c5bd0f58a55242b6df0646", "parents": ["66feaee2b275e7f3d9349ca41bacd439473c023d"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785847030, "git_changesets": ["ad48002cd43493881c3d8f12d1c7fbcf2f374c95"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45023": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging 5ea6f25c57d411c3dea06f0405775b4066302e09 with FIREFOX_153_0_3_RELEASE a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "61911f45393adaa806b8bdfc0c66fd4993c4e2cb", "git_parents": ["ad48002cd43493881c3d8f12d1c7fbcf2f374c95"], "node": "7a2c39e77a1e0d26666f8fa8e8311d7bc5434bcb", "parents": ["fc72221cd30ea6e4c0c5bd0f58a55242b6df0646"], "tags": []}], "date": 1785847156, "git_changesets": ["61911f45393adaa806b8bdfc0c66fd4993c4e2cb"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45024": {"changesets": [{"author": "Yoshi Cheng-Hao Huang \u003callstars.chh@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060238 - Bail out in ProcessDynamicImport when loading the imports failed. r=jonco\n\nA dynamic import has two error cases:\n1. Failing to fetch/compile the dynamically imported module script itself,\n   which is handled in OnFetchFailed.\n2. Failing to load the module script's dependencies, which is handled in\n   OnLoadRequestedModulesRejected.\n\nBoth reject the promise of the dynamic import, but only the first one is\ncovered by ModuleLoadRequest::IsErrored(), so for the second case\nProcessDynamicImport went on to call FinishLoadingImportedModule() for an\nimport that was already rejected.\n\nAlso clear the import in OnLoadRequestedModulesRejected, so that the payload is\nnot kept alive until the request dies.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316024\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_evaluated.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_indirect.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_indirect_1.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_sibling.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/test_dynamicImport_dependency_load_failure.html", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.h", "js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp"], "git_node": "405261caa0a8e2856f6c8749ce639f98faf3c83c", "git_parents": ["5aef16c9b58b3e5791f849bdabbf9affb4a96844"], "node": "f953e533d96b13b5805f9d1a1fc5a396ae6ac43a", "parents": ["883a33ae6c6a3ac8081cd948e1f9f7b440d29b36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "smayya \u003csmayya@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053608 - Additional validation of URL segments in nsStandardURL. r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312991\n", "files": ["netwerk/base/nsStandardURL.cpp"], "git_node": "59ae57efffd310e77d481454bdfe49f170f08195", "git_parents": ["405261caa0a8e2856f6c8749ce639f98faf3c83c"], "node": "26cb7fc95499ffe5abdb6f6ed348b9775b452d59", "parents": ["f953e533d96b13b5805f9d1a1fc5a396ae6ac43a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-bg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cak/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-de/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-el/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-en-rGB/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rMX/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-gl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-hsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ia/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-it/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-iw/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ko/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-nn-rNO/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pa-rIN/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rPT/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-ru/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sv-rSE/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-tg/strings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/values-nn-rNO/strings.xml"], "git_node": "a2ca0751852f16665cad0bb5bd662971f9c38a0c", "git_parents": ["59ae57efffd310e77d481454bdfe49f170f08195"], "node": "ec13df9717c41d3c2135075aa9adc54307f65bae", "parents": ["26cb7fc95499ffe5abdb6f6ed348b9775b452d59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055751 - Make HTMLCanvasElement::CaptureStream() to use async readback IPC with WebGLs r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nUsing MozPromise to asynchronize taking snapshot. The async taking screenshot is used only for capture stream. With it, main thread is not blocked for waiting sync IPC.\n\nBorrowed from the following implementations.\n- HTMLCanvasElement::GetSurfaceSnapshot()\n- ClientWebGLContext::BackBufferSnapshot()\n- ClientWebGLContext::DoReadPixels()\n- WebGLParent::RecvReadPixels()\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312647\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.cpp", "dom/canvas/ClientWebGLContext.h", "dom/canvas/PWebGL.ipdl", "dom/canvas/WebGLParent.cpp", "dom/canvas/WebGLParent.h", "dom/canvas/nsICanvasRenderingContextInternal.h", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.cpp", "dom/html/HTMLCanvasElement.h"], "git_node": "fe6d7e59fbe9cdaa7a3c35251d8041cf076f8c7f", "git_parents": ["a2ca0751852f16665cad0bb5bd662971f9c38a0c"], "node": "d3fc53fbd3ae3f7755f22bda1851634a57dd9ad3", "parents": ["ec13df9717c41d3c2135075aa9adc54307f65bae"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051264 - [devtools] Fix selection for duplicate stylesheets in the debugger r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nAlso reworking the browser_dbg-pretty-print-stylesheet.js test to make\nit more generic for subsequent stylesheet assertions.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314234\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/client/firefox/create.js", "devtools/client/debugger/src/reducers/sources-tree.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-pretty-print-stylesheet.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-sources-tree.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-stylesheets.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_gp.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_qz.toml", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/head.js"], "git_node": "e2fc3bf45ff2353fa2fcfb34bed98caae5e73247", "git_parents": ["fe6d7e59fbe9cdaa7a3c35251d8041cf076f8c7f"], "node": "25b01533ba9af5eb50e7e4e6501281656484f0c4", "parents": ["d3fc53fbd3ae3f7755f22bda1851634a57dd9ad3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hubert B Manilla \u003chmanilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2051029 - [devtools] Reselect selected stylesheet after reload r=devtools-reviewers,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314284\n", "files": ["devtools/client/debugger/src/actions/sources/newSources.js", "devtools/client/debugger/test/mochitest/browser_dbg-stylesheets.js"], "git_node": "700c01dff29829a9e46552be8dabc2355c1c3ef2", "git_parents": ["e2fc3bf45ff2353fa2fcfb34bed98caae5e73247"], "node": "9606e3dfb0dc1688cee09f65e575d198b4b038a5", "parents": ["25b01533ba9af5eb50e7e4e6501281656484f0c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "agoloman \u003cagoloman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060238 - Bail out in ProcessDynamicImport when loading the imports failed. r=jonco\" for causing wpt failures @ModuleLoaderBase.cpp.\n\nThis reverts commit 405261caa0a8e2856f6c8749ce639f98faf3c83c.\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_evaluated.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_indirect.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_indirect_1.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/import_404_sibling.mjs", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/mochitest.toml", "dom/base/test/jsmodules/test_dynamicImport_dependency_load_failure.html", "js/loader/ModuleLoadRequest.h", "js/loader/ModuleLoaderBase.cpp"], "git_node": "5f6e4ea23c910f9a9608f42f98a1decd03f940a6", "git_parents": ["700c01dff29829a9e46552be8dabc2355c1c3ef2"], "node": "3e7005ea74f3af431dbb4a05237fbcad728a171a", "parents": ["9606e3dfb0dc1688cee09f65e575d198b4b038a5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060000. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315942\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContextGL.cpp"], "git_node": "373c8e078e64ccc0ad9df7d4e4737fc71b916c55", "git_parents": ["5f6e4ea23c910f9a9608f42f98a1decd03f940a6"], "node": "9b7c193be76d0c4306ce22207c17801a05395b22", "parents": ["3e7005ea74f3af431dbb4a05237fbcad728a171a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060342 - Keep 3D-transformed text off the device glyph path r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe device glyph path has the shader map each glyph's device rect back to local\nspace with the full 4x4 inverse, z forced to 0. That only inverts how the\ntransform maps the glyphs' z=0 plane while the third row or the third column is\nentirely zero; when both carry terms the round trip displaces the quad and\noffsets its UV fraction, shaving a slice off every glyph. A perspective paired\nwith a translateZ hits this (bug 2052019 let it onto the path), and so does any\n3D rotation, which has been broken since bug 2044211.\n\nGate on is_2d_on_z_plane() instead of has_2d_plane_perspective(): the transform\nmust map that plane, and invert it, exactly as its 2D terms would. Requiring\nm44 == 1 as well keeps the fix CPU-side, with no shader change. A flat\nperspective and a bare translateZ each stay on the sharp device path; pairing\nthem, a 3D rotation, or a matrix3d with a constant w != 1 now rasterize in local\nspace.\n\nperspective-clip.png goes back to its pre-bug-2052019 rendering, since that\ntest's matrix pairs a perspective with a translateZ.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316117\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/text_run.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/util.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/3d-device-text.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/3d-device-text.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/perspective-clip.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "38f6abc7ac1b06f2ca7b59fdd066befd3330e84e", "git_parents": ["373c8e078e64ccc0ad9df7d4e4737fc71b916c55"], "node": "6d9efa091c9d046fe698231eacd25d758c9ce5c2", "parents": ["9b7c193be76d0c4306ce22207c17801a05395b22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Khamis \u003cskhamis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049002: Add dismissable button to promo button r=sync-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,akulyk,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314167\n", "files": ["browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_about_default_promo.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_about_nimbus_dismiss.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/browser_privatebrowsing_about_nova_promo.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/test/browser/head.js", "browser/themes/shared/privatebrowsing/aboutPrivateBrowsing.css", "toolkit/content/tests/widgets/test_moz_promo.html", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-promo/moz-promo.css", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-promo/moz-promo.mjs", "toolkit/content/widgets/moz-promo/moz-promo.stories.mjs", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/mozPromo.ftl"], "git_node": "17af8f4309a4e17f57020052de2ce80a55cb6d62", "git_parents": ["38f6abc7ac1b06f2ca7b59fdd066befd3330e84e"], "node": "f602e857520fa8cea9cfc7429a358c6dca74dfda", "parents": ["6d9efa091c9d046fe698231eacd25d758c9ce5c2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Khamis \u003cskhamis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057674: Add dismissable sync promo to app menu history panel r=sync-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,tgiles\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314168\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-menubar.js", "browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/customizableui/content/jar.mn", "browser/components/customizableui/content/sync-promo.css", "browser/components/customizableui/content/sync-promo.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_history_sync_promo.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/appmenu.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/fxa/sync-promo-connectdevice.svg", "browser/themes/shared/fxa/sync-promo-signin.svg", "browser/themes/shared/fxa/sync-promo-turnonsync.svg", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn"], "git_node": "052a1686adc82ba4b8b7395d2cc7d287e2729cd4", "git_parents": ["17af8f4309a4e17f57020052de2ce80a55cb6d62"], "node": "5d2bdf1a40430498f8755e426e8efc8964ece6bc", "parents": ["f602e857520fa8cea9cfc7429a358c6dca74dfda"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sammy Khamis \u003cskhamis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059270: Add dismissable sync promo to app menu bookmarks panel r=sync-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,places-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,Standard8,tgiles,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315146\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-places.js", "browser/components/customizableui/content/sync-promo.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_bookmarks_sync_promo.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/appmenu.ftl", "browser/themes/shared/fxa/sync-promo-bookmarks.svg", "browser/themes/shared/jar.inc.mn"], "git_node": "0c4dc7a699697fb491e7e855b3273246a9716a6b", "git_parents": ["052a1686adc82ba4b8b7395d2cc7d287e2729cd4"], "node": "ae2cc46e0f5d4585c2cefa2e548e0b03557c582b", "parents": ["5d2bdf1a40430498f8755e426e8efc8964ece6bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060361 - Use exact scale factors for perspective surfaces that map coplanar content affinely r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nA picture surface's contents are coplanar (z=0) in its own space, so the\nperspective divide over them is w = x*m14 + y*m24 + m44. When m14 and m24\nare both zero -- which is the case for a plain perspective or perspective()\napplied to flat content -- w is constant and the surface is mapped by a 2D\naffine transform, for which exact scale factors exist. Only a true keystone\nhas no single reasonable scale, so restrict the (1,1) fallback to that case.\n\nPreviously any matrix with a perspective component was rasterized at the\nparent's scale, so an image scaled up inside a perspective + preserve-3d\nwrapper was rasterized at device scale and then bilinear-upscaled, losing\nimage-rendering: pixelated.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316131\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_tree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/util.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/preserve-3d.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/split/same-plane.png", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "174534f884b455ab756906061f46c07c62f234cf", "git_parents": ["0c4dc7a699697fb491e7e855b3273246a9716a6b"], "node": "a6c87042e92ff10a4382d58ee3b00bf1d6f1c8ba", "parents": ["ae2cc46e0f5d4585c2cefa2e548e0b03557c582b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057847 - Fix and re-enable test browser_bookmark_popup.js. r=places-reviewers,daisuke\n\nThe test hangs while waiting for the mouseover event. It's not related to Nova\nat all and can be reproduced with Proton. The problem seems to be entirely with\nsynthesizing the event properly and not a defect in Firefox.\n\nI tried a number of things to fix it and ended up with this. At first I fixed\nthe Linux hang but either caused or revealed a hang on Windows in verify mode.\n\nThe changes related to checking if the panel is visible are due to the task that\ndouble-clicks the star button. Double-clicking the button closes the panel, so\nthere was a race between that and waiting for the mouseout event to close it.\n\nGreen try push:\n\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=5cc65c9b4e614b336ec57c86b949c62894e6a7d1\n\nPrevious try pushes with older versions of this patch that still had Windows\nfailures:\n\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=b041bfdd9720f24a1a83f1a2bffbe3f383854ac9&selectedTaskRun=LyhcCPxYQKaLyifu9JG3iQ.0\n\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=94253648d8212c9852c827b2e40efa7fde120307&selectedTaskRun=O02oxeC8QyeTdOnwdBgNxA.0\n\nhttps://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=67dae93dd4b3e65587633acb10aa6cd17e51c9a6\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316139\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/places/tests/browser/browser_bookmark_popup.js"], "git_node": "c6e747398811f7f821063d2af472eaabe4808ed2", "git_parents": ["174534f884b455ab756906061f46c07c62f234cf"], "node": "7ce52ca27a9339b1e5fc5cefc120f6037f4a020c", "parents": ["a6c87042e92ff10a4382d58ee3b00bf1d6f1c8ba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059270, Bug 2057674, Bug 2049002: Add dismissable sync promo to app menu bookmarks panel r=sync-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,places-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,Standard8,tgiles,bolsson\" for causing bc failures at browser_history_recently_closed.js\n\nThis reverts commit 0c4dc7a699697fb491e7e855b3273246a9716a6b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057674: Add dismissable sync promo to app menu history panel r=sync-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,tgiles\"\n\nThis reverts commit 052a1686adc82ba4b8b7395d2cc7d287e2729cd4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2049002: Add dismissable button to promo button r=sync-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,bolsson,akulyk,dao\"\n\nThis reverts commit 17af8f4309a4e17f57020052de2ce80a55cb6d62.\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-menubar.js", "browser/base/content/browser-places.js", "browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/browser.js", "browser/components/customizableui/content/jar.mn", "browser/components/customizableui/content/sync-promo.css", "browser/components/customizableui/content/sync-promo.mjs", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser.toml", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_bookmarks_sync_promo.js", "browser/components/customizableui/test/browser_history_sync_promo.js", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.html", "browser/components/privatebrowsing/content/aboutPrivateBrowsing.js", "browser/components/private