", "desc": "Bug 2060215 - Fix all disabled checkbox color tints r=android-reviewers,skhan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316559\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/color/compound_button_tint.xml"], "git_node": "ca8eac19dce6c3a26a49ab499751704c664a95e2", "git_parents": ["a8e9f7eb74361a8873826ffd2fcef1225e5630fa"], "node": "7705e72c31f7d218bfdd470302cc120519b900ac", "parents": ["de202723eb0781b77b617de569bc55a82c4db2ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Franchuk \u003cafranchuk@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056369 - Show tracebacks when an ipdl compile subprocess fails r=ipc-reviewers,nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314111\n", "files": ["ipc/ipdl/ipdl.py"], "git_node": "61816ed76b26789aa2e73eac42bca3cac74c3c93", "git_parents": ["ca8eac19dce6c3a26a49ab499751704c664a95e2"], "node": "63abdb5a8193817d6f81eb0e1cceb1c39ee1bd0d", "parents": ["7705e72c31f7d218bfdd470302cc120519b900ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chukwuka Rosemary Uche \u003cchukwukarosemary2020@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049517 - Fix missing hyphen in splitview onboarding subtitle r=sfoster,fluent-reviewers,omc-reviewers,aminomancer,bolsson\n\nChanged \"Right click\" to \"Right-click\" in the splitview-onboarding-callout-subtitle-1 string in featureCallout.ftl to match Firefox's hyphenation convention.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314266\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/featureCallout.ftl"], "git_node": "901f80b24a456cdabfcdfe3abf93c60cedd25371", "git_parents": ["61816ed76b26789aa2e73eac42bca3cac74c3c93"], "node": "4230e534472186c38c11e8cb8c53846b5beea789", "parents": ["63abdb5a8193817d6f81eb0e1cceb1c39ee1bd0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Poon \u003cnpoon@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057330 - Fix right padding of send to devices bottom sheet in landscape mode r=android-reviewers,gl\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315445\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/share/SendToDevicesDialogFragment.kt"], "git_node": "8fe5692e1f504f87b9ae9a251b1912db26ac405b", "git_parents": ["901f80b24a456cdabfcdfe3abf93c60cedd25371"], "node": "0c2101546ffa8e6bb940768e165431cfe043625b", "parents": ["4230e534472186c38c11e8cb8c53846b5beea789"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060798 - Remove use of EARLY_BETA_OR_EARLIER from the buffer allocator r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nThe buffer allocator limits poisoning to the first 256 bytes in release builds\n(the same as jemalloc).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316498\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/BufferAllocator.cpp"], "git_node": "3f3503218dbb698123a065b7b752ca6a49749862", "git_parents": ["8fe5692e1f504f87b9ae9a251b1912db26ac405b"], "node": "d953cbc52bdd4d53a1810d823b76ecb673805fcf", "parents": ["0c2101546ffa8e6bb940768e165431cfe043625b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058485 - Fix incorrect and missing @nova-cleanup comments r=thecount,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nNote that this commit only comment updates/additions only.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314647\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/tests/home/browser_homepage_firefox_home.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/_Base.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/CardGrid/CardGrid.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/DSCard/DSCard.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/DSContextFooter/DSContextFooter.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Weather/LocationSearch.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/FocusTimer/FocusTimer.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Lists/Lists.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/activity-stream.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_CardSections.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_DSCard.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_TopSites.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Wallpapers/WallpaperFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/browser/browser_newtab_sticky_search.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl"], "git_node": "71c08dd35b2c450b6121ae23b3cf6d5fe3762504", "git_parents": ["3f3503218dbb698123a065b7b752ca6a49749862"], "node": "1681833d54379659bde3889aa3ad9a98cca70782", "parents": ["d953cbc52bdd4d53a1810d823b76ecb673805fcf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055660 - Add tab-open reconciliation helpers to TabManagementService r=pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315050\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/TabManagementService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_TabManagementService.js"], "git_node": "9a018212208facb6c2068bf7fce6b7147db029a7", "git_parents": ["71c08dd35b2c450b6121ae23b3cf6d5fe3762504"], "node": "6c132b60121755f733f92d4d325e9f9be2cd6a87", "parents": ["1681833d54379659bde3889aa3ad9a98cca70782"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Elissa Cha \u003cecha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055660 - Support opening and grouping tabs from the tab-selection confirmation card r=pdahiya,fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\n- Adds a new open_tabs action alongside the existing close_tabs/group_tabs flows, reusing the existing tab-selection confirmation card UI\n- Reconciles selected tabs against already-open tabs, only opening new tabs when needed before grouping them\n- Special-cases single-tab selections: switches to an already-open tab, or opens a closed tab without creating a group\n- Intentionally omits undo for open_tabs, since the resulting actions are already reversible through normal browsing\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313549\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ToolUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ToolUI.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/aiWindowContent.ftl"], "git_node": "3046527fc1f8594d63c9e4db36f7bb5790adfe2a", "git_parents": ["9a018212208facb6c2068bf7fce6b7147db029a7"], "node": "74eae8404af13d7bdc98eab169610ae0985043be", "parents": ["6c132b60121755f733f92d4d325e9f9be2cd6a87"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hanna.alemu \u003chalemu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060651 - Make information about active versus lapsed users available to WNP r=omc-reviewers,aminomancer\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316361\n", "files": ["browser/components/uitour/UITour.sys.mjs", "browser/components/uitour/test/browser_UITour.js"], "git_node": "e343d5b0b817ded0b7c3eab70a1b58760e79c289", "git_parents": ["3046527fc1f8594d63c9e4db36f7bb5790adfe2a"], "node": "14338da74b3fb471e0ada284dc08641deeee64ed", "parents": ["74eae8404af13d7bdc98eab169610ae0985043be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060361 - Use exact scale factors for perspective surfaces that map coplanar content affinely r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nA picture surface's contents are coplanar (z=0) in its own space, so the\nperspective divide over them is w = x*m14 + y*m24 + m44. When m14 and m24\nare both zero -- which is the case for a plain perspective or perspective()\napplied to flat content -- w is constant and the surface is mapped by a 2D\naffine transform, for which exact scale factors exist. Only a true keystone\nhas no single reasonable scale, so restrict the (1,1) fallback to that case.\n\nPreviously any matrix with a perspective component was rasterized at the\nparent's scale, so an image scaled up inside a perspective + preserve-3d\nwrapper was rasterized at device scale and then bilinear-upscaled, losing\nimage-rendering: pixelated.\n\nOnly ever scale up. The foreshortening at the perspective origin makes the\nexact scale marginally less than one for content that is essentially flat,\nso taking it unclamped rasterized such a surface about a percent smaller and\nresampled it for no gain. That shifted edge antialiasing enough to push\nlayout/reftests/transform-3d/preserve3d-6a.html three pixels past its fuzz\nallowance on macOS, which backed out the first version of this patch.\nClamping also leaves every existing reference image unchanged.\n\nRegression test: perspective-pixelated.yaml scales an 8x8 checkerboard up by\n40 inside a perspective + preserve-3d wrapper and compares it against the\nsame image scaled without the perspective surface. It runs at integer scales\nonly, because at a fractional scale the surface raster grid and the directly\ndrawn reference sit on different sub-pixel phases.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316131\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/spatial_tree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/util.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/perspective-pixelated-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/perspective-pixelated.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/transforms/reftest.list"], "git_node": "1d043b4d775e4658addef8b121d79a727deb302e", "git_parents": ["e343d5b0b817ded0b7c3eab70a1b58760e79c289"], "node": "17787c47f802a4b7e221d7fbeca8a5eb53b0567d", "parents": ["14338da74b3fb471e0ada284dc08641deeee64ed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego Escalante \u003cdescalante@mozilla.com\u003e", "branc