ckMaker", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-weather/src/test/resources/robolectric.properties", "taskcluster/config.yml"], "git_node": "f03053b8cb47b4cab3b2d825f32b06cf49a10550", "git_parents": ["5b3ae8a49df2709648271c17ceb8b54f9ed9d90a"], "node": "eb9a70cd52844abea8604f2676fbea611a07615e", "parents": ["176605ed3220f0a13205a997ef65c641e9d296b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056721 - Part 2: Add the weather forecast model, JSON parsing, and MerinoWeatherProvider r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316185\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/.buildconfig.yml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-weather/build.gradle", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-weather/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/weather/MerinoWeatherForecast.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-weather/src/main/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/weather/MerinoWeatherProvider.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-weather/src/test/java/mozilla/components/service/merino/weather/MerinoWeatherProviderTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/service/merino-weather/src/test/resources/forecast.json"], "git_node": "658edaad86299d0f7315e04a385db4543dc1e3cb", "git_parents": ["f03053b8cb47b4cab3b2d825f32b06cf49a10550"], "node": "c2c12f8adf6a0815043f4a9e2fe4c600ee7a7a59", "parents": ["eb9a70cd52844abea8604f2676fbea611a07615e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060686 - Apply search mode before starting the query it restricts. r=mbeier\n\nEntering search mode from a result assigns through the searchMode setter, which\ndelegates to the async setSearchMode without awaiting it, and starts the\nrestricted query on the next line. setSearchMode awaits the engine store when it\nisn't populated, so the assignment can return before the mode has been applied,\nand the query then runs unrestricted.\n\nThe engine store initializes after paint, so this is reachable on both\ntransports. With the message path off, init() is already resolved by the time a\nresult arrives and the await costs a single microtask -- enough, because\nstartQuery runs synchronously on the next line. The message path widens that to\na real round-trip to the parent, which is why the Windows urlbar-ipc variant is\nwhere CI catches it, as browser_no_results.js.\n\nThe setter now keeps the promise setSearchMode returns and the query waits on it.\nTwo things worth checking, both consequences of the query no longer running\nsynchronously:\n\n- The mode is entered confirmed instead of previewed when a query follows,\n  because closing the view discards a previewed mode and every pick path here\n  closes it on the same stack.\n- That makes the subsequent confirmSearchMode a no-op, which drops the second\n  pass through setSearchMode that had been re-capturing userTypedValue after the\n  input value was replaced by the query string. That capture is now explicit.\n  Setting the value before entering the mode would get it for free, but search\n  mode has to be active across setValue.\n\nSmartbarInput carries its own copy of all of this and gets the same change. Its\nsetter drops the assignment entirely in smartbar mode, so nothing waits there.\n\nspaceToEnterSearchMode moves out of browser_no_results.js into its own file. It\ndoesn't depend on the scotchBonnet.enableOverride override that file applies to\nevery task, and nothing on this path does. Its one-off visibility check went\naway with the move: it asserted against the wrong window, and one-offs aren't\nwhat the subtest exercises.\n\nThe new file pins the engine store's state instead of leaving it to a race, and\nruns the alias both ways. Only the uninitialized case fails without this patch,\nand it does so on both transports.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316495\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_no_results.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-searchMode/browser_spaceToEnterSearchMode.js"], "git_node": "07920a5447720a9cfa097ceb9aa8380d09d07e78", "git_parents": ["658edaad86299d0f7315e04a385db4543dc1e3cb"], "node": "6dd65133b21a3b9bd17a46cff8a4974d40897dd9", "parents": ["c2c12f8adf6a0815043f4a9e2fe4c600ee7a7a59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061219 - Compare the switcher's engine icon by image in browser_testUrlbarIcons.js. r=mbeier\n\nBug 2060639 made engine icons cross the actor as data URLs, since a blob URL\nonly resolves in the process that created it, and gave UrlbarTestUtils an\nicon comparison that reads the image behind the URL for the tests it knew\nwere affected. This test compares iconsrc as a string, so its three\nengine-icon assertions can't hold over the wire: same image, different URL.\nIt went unnoticed because our try pushes scoped the paths to\ntests/browser, which since bug 2048207 no longer covers the sibling\nbrowser-*/ directories, so this file was never run on the message path.\n\nThe glass and globe assertions keep comparing strings \u2014 those are chrome://\nURLs that don't change shape across transports \u2014 and they also exercise the\nCSS-override branch of the local helper, which UrlbarTestUtils doesn't read.\n\nBoth transports now report 18 assertions where the message path previously\nmanaged 6 before timing out.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316812\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-results/browser_testUrlbarIcons.js"], "git_node": "9eae192287a633cf493c13c79fa2f11fbe306b1d", "git_parents": ["07920a5447720a9cfa097ceb9aa8380d09d07e78"], "node": "137da4e271e87fb128457ab2569fcdbe568bfd36", "parents": ["6dd65133b21a3b9bd17a46cff8a4974d40897dd9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "yazan \u003cyalmacki@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056382 - Add a shortcut to per user start menu folder so taskbar icon can be modified. r=mconley,hsohaney,fluent-reviewers,bolsson,mossop\n\nThe taskbar falls back to using the icon of the shortcut (with a matching AUMID) located at the system-wide start menu path, when a matching shortcut doesn\u2019t exist at the user-level start menu. We cannot modify the icon at the system-wide shortcut so it stays the same.\n\nWhen pinned, a shortcut gets created at the user-level, which we can edit, and hence the problem doesn\u2019t exist there. The fix is to add a shortcut to the per user start menu directory. The shell prioritizes that shortcut\u2019s icon over the system-wide one when both are present, and we have the ability to modify it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313551\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/browser-icon.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfileService.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/CustomIconManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/test/unit/test_customIconManager.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/browser.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2056382_browser_shortcut_description.py", "widget/nsIWinTaskbar.idl", "widget/windows/WinTaskbar.cpp"], "git_node": "cba4ffe327de81f847b58b39074d909602aaed1f", "git_parents": ["9eae192287a633cf493c13c79fa2f11fbe306b1d"], "node": "5a12167c19e6ac930be01df504b98a7da764ee60", "parents": ["137da4e271e87fb128457ab2569fcdbe568bfd36"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060310 - Derive the BTP extended navigation's initial host from the site being navigated away from r=timhuang\n\nThe bounce tracking record's initial host came from the navigation's triggering\nprincipal, which for a navigation started by a nested navigable is the frame's own\nprincipal. RecordStatefulBounces exempts the initial host, so a cross-site iframe\ncould navigate the top level through its own origin and back to the embedder without\never being classified, gaining a first party context to write unpartitioned cookies\nfrom. The spec derives it from the navigation's source document, which is where the\ngap comes from; a spec issue will be filed separately.\n\nUse the site the context is leaving instead: the most recent non-initial document\ncommitted in it, via BrowsingContext::GetHasLoadedNonInitialDocument and the current\nwindow context, both updated at commit. A context with no committed document of its\nown was opened by this navigation, so its opener is used.\n\nThe derivation no longer needs the navigation to have an initiator, so one started by\nthe browser also exempts the site it is leaving. That fixes bug 2060555.\n\nThis matches how user activation is already attributed:\nWindowGlobalParent::RecvRecordUserActivationForBTP keys on the top window context, so\na click in a frame is credited to the embedding site. The record's user activation set\ndeliberately still keeps the triggering principal's site, because it feeds the dynamic\nFPI storage access heuristic, which wants the site that was interacted with.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316548\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingRecord.h", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/nsIBounceTrackingRecord.idl", "toolkit/components/antitracking/docs/bounce-tracking-protection/index.md"], "git_node": "1b7232980c3dfbc0aa7c0ce13deecede4d058123", "git_parents": ["cba4ffe327de81f847b58b39074d909602aaed1f"], "node": "1d8bf3c7775e76206856115b823faa55ea335c59", "parents": ["5a12167c19e6ac930be01df504b98a7da764ee60"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060310 - Test initial host derivation for frame and cross context initiated navigations r=timhuang\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316549\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_iframe_initiated_load.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_iframe_popup.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_userActivation.js", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "514fc74dd92ed57b57b8a0e222169afe9200d51c", "git_parents": ["1b7232980c3dfbc0aa7c0ce13deecede4d058123"], "node": "7bdd7fc3d9250edfcb68e83ecebd93c98f498623", "parents": ["1d8bf3c7775e76206856115b823faa55ea335c59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2058621 - Part 3: Revert adding mIsFirstCharFallbackRect from bug 2057662, since it's no longer needed. r=masayuki\" for causing devtools failures crashes @mozilla::Maybe\u003cmozilla::ContentCache::TextRectArray\u003e::operator-\u003e.\n\nThis reverts commit 54fd9fc147df850a4b0091c3041e7c8909bba427.\n\nThis reverts commit b916ea614b6c99cb221c5b1ca68e03965f3c1f7a.\n\nThis reverts commit 8f0c4724a2eedb4fcce773d1cbedf1ad8e995d48.\n", "files": ["dom/events/ContentEventHandler.cpp", "dom/html/EditContext.cpp", "dom/html/EditContext.h", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/test_editcontext_characterboundsupdate_focus.html", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/test_editcontext_query_characters.html", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/test_editcontext_redundant_characterboundsupdate.html", "modules/libpref/init/all.js", "widget/ContentCache.cpp", "widget/ContentCache.h", "widget/TextEvents.h"], "git_node": "b7fc43c025f899fcacc004edb6a210ae7f373b6d", "git_parents": ["514fc74dd92ed57b57b8a0e222169afe9200d51c"], "node": "95d4926506a26de5758503513587d1c3191ab836", "parents": ["7bdd7fc3d9250edfcb68e83ecebd93c98f498623"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057270 - Update test_xrayToJS for Promise.allKeyed and allSettledKeyed; r=nika\" for causing reftest failures @ allKeyed.js\n\nThis reverts commit 5b3ae8a49df2709648271c17ceb8b54f9ed9d90a.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057270 - Ship Promise.allKeyed and Promise.allSettledKeyed. r=arai,dminor\"\n\nThis reverts commit e51bf69476aa3f862bf7aede7ccb4557cc664b16.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057270 - Update test262 snapshot r=dminor\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3c3726ef6f7d9f9d93c3b10ca8078f24e9fb1bc4.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2057270 - Clarify working directory for test262-update.py in js/src/tests/README.txt r=dminor\"\n\nThis reverts commit edd301e281f6dd35ca41d2265cba14a67101b749.\n", "files": ["js/src/builtin/Promise.cpp", "js/src/tests/README.txt", "js/src/tests/jstests.list", "js/src/tests/test262/GIT-INFO", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/Array/fromAsync/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncDisposableStack/prototype/adopt/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncDisposableStack/prototype/defer/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncDisposableStack/prototype/disposeAsync/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncDisposableStack/prototype/move/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncDisposableStack/prototype/use/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncFromSyncIteratorPrototype/next/shell.js", "js/src/tests/test262/built-ins/AsyncFromSyncIteratorProt