39a9a0d5ac53"], "node": "e2bf6281df9bea8004e541a9d0e9542cd69b88d8", "parents": ["8ccc22997d2d8f345620eaa93e78aefb7f397b68"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2061026 - Fix for overflowing summary headers for cards in the History sidebar panel r=sclements\" for causing mochitests failures in browser_parsable_css.js.\n\nThis reverts commit a9e2daf46efcf854eb1a6ce254cb9b6282463067.\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar.css"], "git_node": "1ba721839a1b5cfcc943dbfefdd305fc82d87d75", "git_parents": ["7437dd9bfb5b3e961fd8f575c83431cbe2207646"], "node": "dd7848e8c585677f56a5f7a0344c90c0a15d0892", "parents": ["e2bf6281df9bea8004e541a9d0e9542cd69b88d8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060976 - Build the apilint plugin with the kotlin-dsl plugin. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\n`kotlin-dsl` subsumes both `java-gradle-plugin` and the explicit `kotlin(\"jvm\")` application, and\nbuilds against Gradle's embedded Kotlin by construction rather than by convention. It also supplies\nthe Gradle API through `gradleKotlinDsl()`, making the explicit `gradleApi()` dependency redundant.\n\n`kotlin-dsl` applies the sam-with-receiver compiler plugin, which gives every Gradle `Action\u003cT\u003e`\nlambda an implicit receiver, so the task configuration blocks that took an explicit parameter no\nlonger compile. Rewrite them in the equivalent implicit-receiver style. Note that a nested `doFirst`\nblock receives `Task`, which has no `args`, so the `args()` calls inside one resolve against the\nenclosing `PythonExec` receiver rather than the innermost one.\n\nWhile here, merge the two `dependencies` blocks, drop an import that the Kotlin DSL provides by\ndefault, and fix a comment that described the doclet jar task as a `Copy` when it is a `Sync`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316676\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiLintPlugin.kt"], "git_node": "ea87c581d815a7d3df55857a55821ddae0c6fb73", "git_parents": ["1ba721839a1b5cfcc943dbfefdd305fc82d87d75"], "node": "b0ba7127062b9b450e2055120cac3132b86e0151", "parents": ["dd7848e8c585677f56a5f7a0344c90c0a15d0892"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060976 - Convert the remaining Groovy build scripts to the Kotlin DSL. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nThe apidoc-plugin script and the root script were the last two Groovy build scripts under the apilint\nplugin build; everything around them is Kotlin DSL already.\n\nThe apidoc-plugin conversion also drops the `jar.outputs.files.singleFile` and `tasks.findByName`\nlookups, which realize the `jar` task while the script is still being evaluated, in favour of\n`tasks.named` references that realize it only when something asks for it. The archive path itself is\nstill resolved while `testApiDoclet` is being configured, which the configuration cache stores and\nreuses without complaint, so there is no need to defer it through `argumentProviders`.\n\nThe `findByName` lookup is worth calling out separately: it returns null for a task that has not\nbeen created yet, so that line was order-dependent on when Spotless registers `spotlessCheck`.\nDepending on the task by name cannot resolve to nothing.\n\nFinally, replace the deprecated `buildDir` property with `layout.buildDirectory`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316677\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apidoc-plugin/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apidoc-plugin/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/build.gradle.kts"], "git_node": "1890b529457842db1acc719107f2d561c796bd01", "git_parents": ["ea87c581d815a7d3df55857a55821ddae0c6fb73"], "node": "8f3da1379aea7fa23bc53a8dda8418288c8ff4dc", "parents": ["b0ba7127062b9b450e2055120cac3132b86e0151"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060976 - Format the apilint plugin's Kotlin sources with Spotless. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nThe plugin's Kotlin had no formatting enforcement: the build applied Spotless to the doclet's Java\nonly, and mozlint's `android-format` runs Spotless over the GeckoView projects, which do not include\nthis directory. Add a `kotlin` format using the same ktlint version and GeckoView's `.editorconfig`\nas the rest of the Android Kotlin in the tree, and hang it off `test` the way the Java format already\nis, so the `android(apilint)` task enforces it.\n\nSpotless has to be requested from the root build script without being applied, because applying it\nindependently in sibling projects gives each of them a separate copy of its shared build service and\nGradle refuses to create the tasks.\n\nThe reformatting this brings in is confined to the `string-template` rule, which drops the braces\nfrom interpolations of a bare name.\n\nThe format covers the plugin's source sets. Gradle build scripts would need a separate\n`kotlinGradle` format, which is left for now because bug 2050591 is replacing ktlint with ktfmt.\n\nOne of the reformatted strings is the extension's default `helpCommand`, which interpolates the\nvariant name next to an escaped `$` and reaches developers verbatim, so cover it with a test.\n\nWhile in the tree's Spotless setup, fix the comment that says to keep the GeckoView project list in\nsync with `spotless_projects`: it pointed at `mobile/android/geckoview/gradle.configure`, which does\nnot exist, rather than `mobile/android/gradle.configure`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316678\n", "files": ["build.gradle", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiLintPlugin.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiLintPluginExtension.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/test/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiLintPluginExtensionTest.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/build.gradle.kts"], "git_node": "74cbfc0ff35ae1bf3f62fdd38590f870e915b61b", "git_parents": ["1890b529457842db1acc719107f2d561c796bd01"], "node": "c450854ac3b5f5e6e5daddf85beb526f58430e9e", "parents": ["8f3da1379aea7fa23bc53a8dda8418288c8ff4dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Duncan McIntosh \u003cdmcintosh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053455 - Add support for multiple arguments in jump list items. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314118\n", "files": ["browser/modules/WindowsJumpLists.sys.mjs", "dom/chrome-webidl/WindowsJumpListShortcutDescription.webidl", "widget/windows/JumpListBuilder.cpp", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestJumpListBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "b3ccdee1272d64bd377acde604901300a3b20c3e", "git_parents": ["74cbfc0ff35ae1bf3f62fdd38590f870e915b61b"], "node": "955d237915be0ddaff5d0e2ce08c89fcab650c37", "parents": ["c450854ac3b5f5e6e5daddf85beb526f58430e9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060706 - Fit browser_scroll_size_determination.js into the test-verify budget. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,kcochrane\n\nNot a regression: the chaos-mode runtime is the same before and after bug\n2059794, which only caused test-verify to run this file at all because it\ntouched it. The test simply doesn't fit the 180s budget once chaos mode\nmultiplies six window-and-overflow cycles by roughly thirty.\n\nOverflowing by the default factor still leaves room to scroll and cuts the\nruntime by about 40%; the longer timeout covers the remaining margin.\n\nWorth checking: the wheel events now take the APZ path. Without asyncEnabled\nthey went through widget-\u003eDispatchEvent, so vertical mode was exercising the\nmain-thread fallback rather than the native scrolling bug 2059794 handed to\nthe platform.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316799\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_scroll_size_determination.js"], "git_node": "8d2308ad493bdb83a4b584bb09d2881b70b34b7e", "git_parents": ["b3ccdee1272d64bd377acde604901300a3b20c3e"], "node": "a59288ba4815588e8859f93be8f9cc8659398fba", "parents": ["955d237915be0ddaff5d0e2ce08c89fcab650c37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057553 - Remove Nova from skip-if on browser_smartwindow_telemetry r=gcardieri\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316666\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "ce71ea2cf8d1f1f2e76c760c33920c57d4c29fc6", "git_parents": ["8d2308ad493bdb83a4b584bb09d2881b70b34b7e"], "node": "d4a55cab3bf465677c47fd1a112face5af5a26b3", "parents": ["a59288ba4815588e8859f93be8f9cc8659398fba"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rob Wu \u003crob@robwu.nl\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060892 - Drop alert override from background pages r=rpl,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\n... and move ignoredSuspendListener logic to the parent because it was\nthe only remaining part of initializeBackgroundPage, and does not need\nto be in the child.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316695\n", "files": ["devtools/client/framework/devtools.js", "devtools/client/framework/toolbox.js", "devtools/startup/DevToolsShim.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/Extension.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionPageChild.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/ExtensionParent.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-backgroundPage.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-runtime.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/mochitest/test_ext_background_page.html"], "git_node": "61baf1ee061e57a835f3346009c5a5f804e752f1", "git_parents": ["ce71ea2cf8d1f1f2e76c760c33920c57d4c29fc6"], "node": "07522e63111e236fbd8985c96fe3d9688750e4cd", "parents": ["d4a55cab3bf465677c47fd1a112face5af5a26b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2031748 - Harden Linux and Android builds of libonnxruntime r=glandium\n\nPassing down most of the flags we already use to build firefox,\nincluding -Wl,-z,noexecstack.\n\nThe Linux shared libraries built by taskcluster have been passed through\nreadelf -l and the GNU_STACK is confirmed not to be executable anymore.\nThe Android one was unaffected.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D298746\n", "files": ["taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-onnxruntime.sh"], "git_node": "2d89d06f33ea26b509a4869c96386e7570cc495d", "git_parents": ["61baf1ee061e57a835f3346009c5a5f804e752f1"], "node": "28e6f996690176fd9280d3fae1b1ae902e50cea3", "parents": ["07522e63111e236fbd8985c96fe3d9688750e4cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sameem-baba \u003cssssameembaba@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1943359 - Clean up subscriptions from session subscription map when a context is destroyed. r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316264\n", "files": ["remote/webdriver-bidi/modules/root/session.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "aa9d7a5bc2acf0a5ab677d12c06a5b77fb340095", "git_parents": ["2d89d06f33ea26b509a4869c96386e7570cc495d"], "node": "429f3556d399392013c5e4f1e430908edbb9a204", "parents": ["28e6f996690176fd9280d3fae1b1ae902e50cea3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nirmaladvani \u003cnirmaladvani@live.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058556 - Synthesize dblclick events for Ctrl-click on non-Mac platforms r=Sasha\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316370\n", "files": ["remote/shared/webdriver/Actions.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/bidi/input/perform_actions/pointer_mouse_modifier.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/perform_actions/pointer_modifier_click.py"], "git_node": "3bd4b704767bd182270473c8f93edcd4c65261c5", "git_parents": ["aa9d7a5bc2acf0a5ab677d12c06a5b77fb340095"], "node": "a511fb644cf5a9ce2f9749ca58cf9bf027f0681e", "parents": ["429f3556d399392013c5e4f1e430908edbb9a204"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Hirsch \u003cohai@6a68.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055255 - Submit referral code via separate ping on first run, and exclude from attribution r=nbarrett,TravisLong,data-stewards,nrishel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315474\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/attribution/AttributionCode.sys.mjs", "browser/components/attribution/test/xpcshell/test_referralAttribution.js", "browser/components/attribution/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/referrals/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/referrals/pings.yaml", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py"], "git_node": "037c5e5f7accb1a9d6f3ec8e977108120909c94f", "git_parents": ["3bd4b704767bd182270473c8f93edcd4c65261c5"], "node": "48eda968a162ab66637486a4a95a4854e77d5af5", "parents": ["a511fb644cf5a9ce2f9749ca58cf9bf027f0681e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joel \u003cjoelkelly@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060323 - Add topsites.change_display event to newtab ping r=thecount\n\nRecords the number of topsite rows the user selects in the newtab\ncustomize menu. The existing topsites.rows metric reports the configured\nvalue at session start, but nothing captures the change itself, and\ntopsites.pref_changed cannot carry it because its new_value extra is a\nboolean.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316186\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "0a056a0948b2e7b52117dee677c44db9f9cb5c2f", "git_parents": ["037c5e5f7accb1a9d6f3ec8e977108120909c94f"], "node": "7490dfdabb554552817d50c6ccdfb08f1cad9619", "parents": ["48eda968a162ab66637486a4a95a4854e77d5af5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Duncan McIntosh \u003cdmcintosh@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045944 - Return the shortcut path from EnsurePinnableShortcutExists when it creates the shortcut itself. r=nrishel\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316349\n", "files": ["browser/components/shell/nsWindowsShellService.cpp"], "git_node": "d10db8a059be9d09b97d736c5b3b8d9f9b39c51e", "git_parents": ["0a056a0948b2e7b52117dee677c44db9f9cb5c2f"], "node": "486d3cbe69bf4f634112e32ae2675892ed269013", "parents": ["7490dfdabb554552817d50c6ccdfb08f1cad9619"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brian Smith \u003cbrian@smith.berlin\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059713 - Add compat info, tests, for ent policies. r=jneuberger,mkaply\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315620\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/schemas/policies-schema.meta.json", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/xpcshell/test_policies_schema.js"], "git_node": "9c5d51ecfd6279861b2215600e61f27386563b55", "git_parents": ["d10db8a059be9d09b97d736c5b3b8d9f9b39c51e"], "node": "a5c3959d9b89835440acc5c6f100c5433047476a", "parents": ["486d3cbe69bf4f634112e32ae2675892ed269013"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059996 - Fix width/height inversion in QuadTileClassifier. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316731\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/quad.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/tiled-thin-quads-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/clip/tiled-thin-quads.yaml"], "git_node": "ea44d3f7a761d1f32eae76c02b72d47ea3bde4aa", "git_parents": ["9c5d51ecfd6279861b2215600e61f27386563b55"], "node": "c5d8e772e34d1cc98e0767dda88af493cb54e530", "parents": ["a5c3959d9b89835440acc5c6f100c5433047476a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053421 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on OSX r=media-playback-reviewers,profiler-reviewers,migration-reviewers,mconley,canova,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311090\n", "files": ["accessible/mac/AccessibleWrap.mm", "accessible/mac/DocAccessibleWrap.mm", "accessible/mac/GeckoTextMarker.h", "accessible/mac/GeckoTextMarker.mm", "accessible/xpcom/xpcAccessibleMacInterface.h", "browser/components/migration/nsKeychainMigrationUtils.h", "browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.h", "dom/gamepad/cocoa/CocoaGamepad.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/synth/cocoa/OSXSpeechSynthesizerService.mm", "dom/system/mac/nsOSPermissionRequest.h", "dom/webgpu/SharedTextureMacIOSurface.cpp", "hal/cocoa/CocoaBattery.cpp", "hal/cocoa/CocoaSensor.mm", "image/decoders/icon/mac/nsIconChannelCocoa.mm", "toolkit/components/parentalcontrols/nsParentalControlsServiceCocoa.mm", "tools/profiler/core/PowerCounters-mac-amd64.cpp", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherMac.cpp", "xpcom/build/PoisonIOInterposerMac.cpp"], "git_node": "27e546ec34b81256b18dd14958372f182352d2a7", "git_parents": ["ea44d3f7a761d1f32eae76c02b72d47ea3bde4aa"], "node": "24490b3e7b48c3badda30680d25d49e9bd77e346", "parents": ["c5d8e772e34d1cc98e0767dda88af493cb54e530"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Lin \u003cjolin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047221 - test crypto subsample size validation. r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306898\n", "files": ["dom/media/gtest/TestMediaFormatReader.cpp"], "git_node": "d925d6e72f650c4f54a25cd98a004e764b16e98b", "git_parents": ["27e546ec34b81256b18dd14958372f182352d2a7"], "node": "f4de3633adb151f57b71d34614eda3e531c7b4f6", "parents": ["24490b3e7b48c3badda30680d25d49e9bd77e346"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jens Manuel Stutte \u003cjstutte@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055964 - Don't warn when NS_DispatchToMainThread fails to get the main thread during shutdown. r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8\n\nNS_DispatchToMainThread wraps the NS_GetMainThread failure check in NS_WARN_IF. NS_GetMainThread only fails (with NS_ERROR_NOT_INITIALIZED) when there is no main thread, which is an expected condition during shutdown. As a result this warning was the single most frequent warning in macOS debug test logs (~48,400 instances, top source \"Shutdown\"), providing no diagnostic value.\n\nDrop the NS_WARN_IF wrapper (keeping the NS_FAILED check and early return). The genuine-misuse case -- a non-fallible dispatch failing and thus leaking the runnable -- is still caught by the NS_ASSERTION immediately below.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315246\n", "files": ["xpcom/threads/nsThreadUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "fb60b34c851b92f3c4a10833e7d45ee76a3a17c7", "git_parents": ["d925d6e72f650c4f54a25cd98a004e764b16e98b"], "node": "477fcdf4fd84103381708e57eb75faf781f42bdb", "parents": ["f4de3633adb151f57b71d34614eda3e531c7b4f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060521 - [efficiency] Convert DownloadFileTypesTest.allFilesAppearInDownloadsMenuTest to ui/efficiency r=jajohnson,aaronmt\" for causing ui-test failures @ CustomTabsTest\n\nThis reverts commit 72e01d1948f58e60e8e367b1c29f24ce4932a30d.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/pages/audioMediaPage.html", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/pages/downloads.html", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/audioSample.mp3", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/csv_file.csv", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/docx_document.docx", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/mp3_audio.mp3", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/png_image.png", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/smallZip.zip", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/svg_image.svg", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/textfile.txt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/txt_file.txt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/web_icon.png", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/webm_video.webm", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/xml_file.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/assets/resources/zip_small.zip", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/DownloadFileTypesTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/DownloadTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/EffScreenDumpRunner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BasePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/Selector.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/BrowserPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/DownloadsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/DownloadsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/DownloadFileTypesTest.kt"], "git_node": "3a2f808d5416532793afde08de14a54606c26f4e", "git_parents": ["fb60b34c851b92f3c4a10833e7d45ee76a3a17c7"], "node": "400cf94b41746c312abca54852730f773f013149", "parents": ["477fcdf4fd84103381708e57eb75faf781f42bdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060940 - Update Sentry to version 8.52.0. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316598\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml"], "git_node": "7b5702cedadea5321e7285072ee6dd18a647dd6d", "git_parents": ["3a2f808d5416532793afde08de14a54606c26f4e"], "node": "e320b957044778d0948e460875772fcf65f49c59", "parents": ["400cf94b41746c312abca54852730f773f013149"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2032628: Use 'visibility:collapse' instead of 'display:none' to show/hide tab-close-button on hovered/unhovered tabs. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,desktop-theme-reviewers,sthompson,kcochrane\n\nAlso, this patch gives .tab-content 'contain: size layout' so that it can be a\ndynamic reflow root, so that hovered tabs can reflow in a more granular way.\n\nAnd then, to ensure that .tab-content still sizes to fit its anticipated\ncontent-height (despite now having 'contain:size'), this patch adds\n'contain-intrinsic-block-size' and 'line-height' declarations to match the\ntab-label's height (assuming it uses the same 'font' as .tab-content).\n\nI don't think this results in any user-facing behavior difference, but it\nshould be a performance win for tab-heavy situations, particularly in \"always\nshow scrollbars\" configurations.\n\nChanges to 'visibility:collapse' just trigger a reflow (not frame\nreconstruction), and with 'contain: size layout' on the .tab-content, that\nreflow can be done in a very targeted way.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D294825\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css"], "git_node": "5959fc3a8e181038fa8997cb920b4029007755c6", "git_parents": ["7b5702cedadea5321e7285072ee6dd18a647dd6d"], "node": "762c7c36846db1a1cf050559cf69bc7a854a11ea", "parents": ["e320b957044778d0948e460875772fcf65f49c59"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060603 - Declare the adaptive launcher icon layers at their spec size. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThese layers are authored at four times the 108dp adaptive icon size that Fenix's primary\nic_launcher_foreground already uses. AdaptiveIconDrawable renders each layer into a 108dp box and the\npath data is expressed in viewport coordinates, so only the declared intrinsic size changes here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316327\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/samples/acorn-components/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/debug/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_background_cool.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_background_cuddling.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_cool.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_cuddling.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_flaming.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_minimal.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_momo.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_pixelated.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_pride.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_launcher_foreground_retro_2004.xml"], "git_node": "7093d93415769f4866a034ee067cc7c590483094", "git_parents": ["5959fc3a8e181038fa8997cb920b4029007755c6"], "node": "ab56f838b21e047b2cd1ac17e30e3114b5010871", "parents": ["762c7c36846db1a1cf050559cf69bc7a854a11ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060603 - Declare the alternative app icon foregrounds at a quarter of their authored size. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThese are the icon picker's preview foregrounds, authored at four times the 108dp adaptive icon size like\nthe launcher layers they mirror. Both consumers ask for an explicit size, the picker through Modifier.size\nand the search widget through a fixed ImageView with centerInside, so dividing the declared size by four\nkeeps each aspect ratio exactly and leaves the drawn result unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316328\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_cool.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_cuddling.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_flaming.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_minimal.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_momo.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_pixelated.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_pride.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_retro_2004.xml"], "git_node": "691db85ea6b9713a0f1c6b905378fafff618acc8", "git_parents": ["7093d93415769f4866a034ee067cc7c590483094"], "node": "c94f130a829cbc52a4e10e72beab4229d5b09f6e", "parents": ["ab56f838b21e047b2cd1ac17e30e3114b5010871"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060603 - Scale down the debug build's Firefox logo drawable. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThe debug variant declares this at 811x760dp while the copy in main is around 108dp wide. It is the\ndefault foreground in AppIcon, so debug builds hand the oversized copy to the search widget. Every\nconsumer asks for an explicit size, so scaling the declared size to match main leaves the drawn result\nunchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316329\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/debug/res/drawable/ic_firefox.xml"], "git_node": "0ea9b0895ead24bf445a726259889f453867e371", "git_parents": ["691db85ea6b9713a0f1c6b905378fafff618acc8"], "node": "66f30894817c9cc1b0d24d267c81c5c3ecbca3dc", "parents": ["c94f130a829cbc52a4e10e72beab4229d5b09f6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060603 - Suppress VectorRaster where the drawable's size is inherent. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThe 200x200 guidance the check points at is about icons. These are full screen backgrounds, a wordmark and\nonboarding illustrations, so their size follows from what they are rather than from how they were exported.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316330\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_high_five.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_notification_permission.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_onboarding_customize_toolbar.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_onboarding_key_features.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_onboarding_key_features_icons_only.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_onboarding_search_widget.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_onboarding_sync.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_onboarding_welcome.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/nova_onboarding_notifications.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/nova_onboarding_tou.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/nova_onboarding_tou_2.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/drawable/nova_onboarding_widget.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-land-night/home_background.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-land/home_background.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable-night/home_background.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable/home_background.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable/ic_error_session_crashed.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/drawable/wordmark2.xml"], "git_node": "049f59270d266f944b3a87013e196bec7a02e257", "git_parents": ["0ea9b0895ead24bf445a726259889f453867e371"], "node": "40e5e67acac2acc0c14db9d2e61502485672cd30", "parents": ["66f30894817c9cc1b0d24d267c81c5c3ecbca3dc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060603 - Drop the VectorRaster lint baseline entries. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316331\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/samples/acorn-components/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/lint-baseline.xml"], "git_node": "110a5812ac80e550b204293e437fc1f6bc86578a", "git_parents": ["049f59270d266f944b3a87013e196bec7a02e257"], "node": "75cc55dd2ea02c94d42361a6770b7b72124a4938", "parents": ["40e5e67acac2acc0c14db9d2e61502485672cd30"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060619 - Stop painting the Focus settings background over itself. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThe window already paints this colour. AppTheme's windowBackground resolves to modal_background, which is\nthe same photonLightGrey05 in light mode and photonInk05 in dark mode as settings_background, and the night\nstyles do not override it. The activity root, the toolbar it inflates and the fragments it hosts were each\nfilling that colour again. The ViewStub that inflates the toolbar also set it, which never had any effect\nsince a ViewStub hands only its layout params to the view replacing it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316332\n", "files": ["mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/activity_main.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_autocomplete_add_domain.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_autocomplete_customdomains.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_exceptions_domains.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_settings.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/toolbar.xml"], "git_node": "5712ab4c557dc89650b662374e95082c5f37bcfe", "git_parents": ["110a5812ac80e550b204293e437fc1f6bc86578a"], "node": "cd58ac2b34f1c1bf1f4015b6c43237c21333492a", "parents": ["75cc55dd2ea02c94d42361a6770b7b72124a4938"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060619 - Suppress Overdraw where the root background is not drawn over the window. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nThe check assumes each layout's root element covers the window. These roots do not. The create shortcut,\ncreate collection and PWA onboarding dialogs draw their scrim into a dialog window whose own background is\ntransparent, the select bars, find in page bar, info banner, navigation toolbar and sign out sheet sit over\npage content rather than over the window, and the preference and list rows paint a ripple rather than a\nfill. The two remaining roots paint a colour the window does not.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316333\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/account_auth_error_preference.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/address_select_bar.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/checkbox_left_preference.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/checkbox_left_preference_etp.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/checkbox_left_sub_preference.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/component_find_in_page_bar.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/creditcard_select_bar.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_create_collection.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_create_shortcut.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_create_xiaomi_shortcut.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_pwa_onboarding.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_sign_out.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/info_banner.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/layout_add_credit_card.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/login_select_bar.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/navigation_toolbar.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/preference_search_add_engine.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/fragment_crash_reporter.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/item_add_custom_domain.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/search_engine_checkbox_button.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/res/layout/search_engine_radio_button.xml"], "git_node": "d32a543904852c868bf577e39c2a736e345f58dc", "git_parents": ["5712ab4c557dc89650b662374e95082c5f37bcfe"], "node": "e4a50ca8db29cb75ed5ec2f468a8fbb527eb7590", "parents": ["cd58ac2b34f1c1bf1f4015b6c43237c21333492a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060619 - Drop the Overdraw lint baseline entries. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316334\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/lint-baseline.xml"], "git_node": "1568f18743533c9e37b0dc64130c5de50c1cd264", "git_parents": ["d32a543904852c868bf577e39c2a736e345f58dc"], "node": "9cdf8c34dec39ce49517fe4a6b3a88235055a94a", "parents": ["e4a50ca8db29cb75ed5ec2f468a8fbb527eb7590"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060711 - Say that subclasses may use these members, not just tests. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nA bare @VisibleForTesting says the member would be private if tests did not need it, so lint objects when a\nsubclass touches it. The exceptions and info banner views hand their view binding to their subclasses, and\nBrowserFragment asks BaseBrowserFragment which tab is current, all of which is ordinary production use.\nWiden each annotation to say so, as the surrounding code already does in several places.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316434\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/infobanner/InfoBanner.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/exceptions/ExceptionsView.kt"], "git_node": "b218852b60c5828fff72509897eac5e7cbe87bb3", "git_parents": ["1568f18743533c9e37b0dc64130c5de50c1cd264"], "node": "c66403411e7bb397831106f6d4ab4dd6a1b230a7", "parents": ["9cdf8c34dec39ce49517fe4a6b3a88235055a94a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060711 - Drop two @VisibleForTesting annotations that no test relies on. r=android-reviewers,mcarare\n\nNothing in the test sources reaches for either member. filterOutTab is called only by AppStoreReducer, and\nsearchGroupMinimumSites is a production threshold that two tests lower rather than read, so in both cases\nthe annotation claims a test-only member where there is none. Being internal already keeps them inside the\nmodule.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316435\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/lint-baseline.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/RecentTabs.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt"], "git_node": "7cc5db845b6938c3c6a10e56c055a631fff23e5b", "git_parents": ["b218852b60c5828fff72509897eac5e7cbe87bb3"], "node": "fda47d157c7c281844988ae6ca4e6d3ee586f7e1", "parents": ["c66403411e7bb397831106f6d4ab4dd6a1b230a7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059680 - Fix wrench scroll offsets and fixed position content at emulated device pixel scales. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nThis one turned out to be an issue with the test harness rather than WebRender.\n\nWrench emulates a device pixel ratio by wrapping the root pipeline's content in a\nscale reference frame, but that reference frame is a child of the pipeline's root\nscroll node, so the implicit root reference frame and root scroll node are above\nthe scale. So two kinds of content escaped it:\n\n - The root scroll node's scroll offset (the root `scroll-offset` yaml key, sent\n   as ExternalScrollId(0)). Scroll offsets accumulate in the scrolled node's own\n   coordinate space, which is unscaled for the root scroll node, so content was\n   displaced by exactly offset * (scale - 1) device pixels: 100 device pixels at\n   scale 2 for scrolling/root-scroll.yaml, 51 at 1.51, -49 at 0.51.\n\n - Items attached to `spatial-id: root-reference-frame` or `root-scroll-node`,\n   which is how wrench expresses fixed position content. Those resolved to the\n   real root nodes and so were rendered at scale 1 while their surroundings were\n   scaled.\n\nPush a second scale reference frame under the root reference frame and redirect\nthe two special yaml spatial ids to the scaled equivalents (the sibling for\nroot-reference-frame so fixed content is scaled without scrolling, the existing\none for root-scroll-node), and scale the root pipeline's scroll offset by the\ndevice pixel scale, which matches Gecko where APZ offsets are in device pixels.\nNothing changes at scale 1.0.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315583\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/scrolling/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs"], "git_node": "784d3b1b2fbede60b6561634e3da186af5c83a09", "git_parents": ["7cc5db845b6938c3c6a10e56c055a631fff23e5b"], "node": "1dec57807abf686266ca03706d385e73b58c798f", "parents": ["fda47d157c7c281844988ae6ca4e6d3ee586f7e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059680 - Restrict the blur clamping reftests to device pixel scales of 1 and above. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315586\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/filters/reftest.list"], "git_node": "5f597174d0ea53a2ce285c244e3e12a370712921", "git_parents": ["784d3b1b2fbede60b6561634e3da186af5c83a09"], "node": "449d5949116a1d2eb1f868facc3cf751e4d651f9", "parents": ["1dec57807abf686266ca03706d385e73b58c798f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059680 - Restrict the wrench thickness snapping reftests to the scales where they compare something. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nborder-thickness, border-even-thickness and line-decoration-thickness assert a\nthickness expressed in device pixels (a sub-device-pixel edge snapped up to one\nwhole device pixel), while their references can only express it in layout units,\nwhich the emulated device pixel scale multiplies. Measured outline ink shows the\ntest edge is round(edge_layout * scale) device pixels and the reference edge\nround(1 layout unit * scale): 1 against 2 device pixels for border-thickness at\nscale 2, 3 against 4 for border-even-thickness. At scale 2 the 0.5 unit edge of\nborder-thickness is exactly one device pixel and does not exercise the snap the\ntest was written for at all. Nothing in the renderer is wrong at those scales, so\nthe tests are restricted rather than the code changed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315587\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list"], "git_node": "754a1b16fb2774b5dc6710bbc4e9d56599bbd637", "git_parents": ["5f597174d0ea53a2ce285c244e3e12a370712921"], "node": "6563390cb4588aba5ce2d1f5f5717c48ac6f14ff", "parents": ["449d5949116a1d2eb1f868facc3cf751e4d651f9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059680 - Don't scale wrench snapping reftests whose reference bakes a scale-1 snapped position. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315588\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/snap/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "32da0b565b54243139c4529661db74e69a4cc7a2", "git_parents": ["754a1b16fb2774b5dc6710bbc4e9d56599bbd637"], "node": "21afd88e4df792c6ad6e6f402bd0fb2ab3a53329", "parents": ["6563390cb4588aba5ce2d1f5f5717c48ac6f14ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059680 - Restrict text/decorations.yaml to integral scales. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nAt factional scales, the lines and rects snap differently.\n\nA decoration line snaps its thickness to a phase-independent whole device pixel\n(SnapRounding::Line: round the near edge, add max(round(thickness), 1)), so a\nsub-pixel line can neither vanish nor double with the sub-pixel position it\nlands at (bug 1783779). A rect rounds both of its edges independently\n(SnapRounding::Nearest), which is what makes adjacent rects share an edge and\ntile without seams, and is phase dependent by construction.\n\nThe two rules agree exactly when round(min) + round(t) == round(min + t), which\nalways holds when every edge is integral in device space.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315589\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/text/reftest.list"], "git_node": "8886d46a24fb6ffbb1f28ad144df87cfcb9c5592", "git_parents": ["32da0b565b54243139c4529661db74e69a4cc7a2"], "node": "9be6e7489c8c6a40536227fce9342499746c2a37", "parents": ["21afd88e4df792c6ad6e6f402bd0fb2ab3a53329"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnical@fastmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059680 - Avoid a NaN at the exact centre of a radial gradient in swgl. r=lsalzman\n\n`commitRadialGradientFromStops` computed the gradient offset for each chunk\nof pixels with `fastSqrt\u003cfalse\u003e(dotPos)`, which on SSE2/NEON evaluates\n`v * inversesqrt(v)`. The reciprocal square root of zero is infinity, so for\nthe pixel whose position is exactly the gradient's centre the product is NaN,\n`round_pixel` turns that into zero and the pixel is written as transparent\nblack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315590\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/swgl/src/swgl_ext.h", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/gradient/reftest.list"], "git_node": "6e7b1585d8814e407b1f35d8782d0617925f0e09", "git_parents": ["8886d46a24fb6ffbb1f28ad144df87cfcb9c5592"], "node": "5e8dacd9d3786bcdd77dc074864c7351415c817b", "parents": ["9be6e7489c8c6a40536227fce9342499746c2a37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060904 - Part 1: Update mark bits atomically in rope flattening pre-barrier r=sfink\n\nThe main problem is that rope flattening can overwrite mark bits written by\nconcurrent marking because the pre-barrier doesn't update them with an atomic\noperations but with separate non-atomic load and store operations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316750\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Marking.cpp"], "git_node": "7ac9ccfd49300c92cfabfdd79437940588364dbc", "git_parents": ["6e7b1585d8814e407b1f35d8782d0617925f0e09"], "node": "fb8dc84464d9758800cb3b73a2b80f112304834b", "parents": ["5e8dacd9d3786bcdd77dc074864c7351415c817b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jon Coppeard \u003cjonco@pobox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060904 - Part 2: Also fix potential issues with detecting updates to rope marking flags r=sfink\n\nPreviously the trace method was updated to also detect changes to rope flags\nmade during flatting (not just at the end). But these updates don't follow the\nprotocol outlined where we update the flags, perform a fence and then write\ndependent fields. The patch fixes this.\n\nAlso the flag updates don't use a single atomic update operation. This is not\nwrong because nothing else is updating the flags but it's surprising as writes\nto the flags use an atomic store by default.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316751\n", "files": ["js/src/gc/Cell.h", "js/src/vm/StringType.cpp"], "git_node": "d7a7ff51f0a982d6a487512af495185307f0c38e", "git_parents": ["7ac9ccfd49300c92cfabfdd79437940588364dbc"], "node": "628036064d54cab5874f3aae9e64cecc903cd6e7", "parents": ["fb8dc84464d9758800cb3b73a2b80f112304834b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vasish Baungally \u003cvbaungally@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060260 - Add agglomerative clustering algorithm for Auto Tab Grouping. r=rrando,jlewis,tabbrowser-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,dao,valentinp\n\nThis patch  switches the KMeans clustering algorithm used for Auto Tab Grouping to\nAgglomerative clustering. The latter is more performant and has better metrics on our\ngolden dataset. It is also deterministic.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316350\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/SmartTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/smarttabgrouping/browser_tab_grouping.js", "toolkit/components/ml/content/ClusterAlgos.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_smart_tab_clustering_perf.js"], "git_node": "7d249b9965ab4aaaf21860eb8b1127f1c98ff2cb", "git_parents": ["d7a7ff51f0a982d6a487512af495185307f0c38e"], "node": "35ce7d7113472c49d3a8399340233b719cf48316", "parents": ["628036064d54cab5874f3aae9e64cecc903cd6e7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048379 - Move homepage and customHomepage setting groups to the preferences component r=fluent-reviewers,reemhamz,mconley,bolsson,flod\n\nInitialises the homepage and custom homepage settings in the preferences component instead of the New Tab extension. This makes them available to downstream browsers like Tor that don't bundle New Tab but still need to expose homepage configuration. The Firefox Home content settings stay in New Tab since they only matter when New Tab is the active surface.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D307703\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/config/home-startup.mjs", "browser/components/preferences/main.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/karma.mc.config.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AboutPreferences.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/mach_commands.py", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/lib/AboutPreferences.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/stubs/AppConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/preferences/preferences.ftl", "python/l10n/fluent_migrations/bug_2048379_homepage_settings_platform_move.py"], "git_node": "1b22ae82087379a4cfbc79a700eb44a158858973", "git_parents": ["7d249b9965ab4aaaf21860eb8b1127f1c98ff2cb"], "node": "17f8b43458abdcf2590f41b35bf8b52506483dee", "parents": ["35ce7d7113472c49d3a8399340233b719cf48316"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059104 - Generate New Tab train-hop locales at build time and package them into the XPI. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315410\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/moz.configure", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales.configure", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/gen_locales.py", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/supported-locales.json", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/moz.build", "taskcluster/kinds/build-extensions/kind.yml"], "git_node": "6231d962b498ba8f89be42cc464961519f8bc2b9", "git_parents": ["1b22ae82087379a4cfbc79a700eb44a158858973"], "node": "78c7ea4190d23d0142f2e2157eeca3f442089048", "parents": ["17f8b43458abdcf2590f41b35bf8b52506483dee"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059104 - Document build-time New Tab locales generation in train_hopping.md. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315437\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/docs/v2-system-addon/train_hopping.md"], "git_node": "840603f5fd08a6544577219e649001d21321cc09", "git_parents": ["6231d962b498ba8f89be42cc464961519f8bc2b9"], "node": "b1435a6cd151284ffcbbdca780b5df8c77a08053", "parents": ["78c7ea4190d23d0142f2e2157eeca3f442089048"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059104 - Remove the in-tree New Tab locale snapshots. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315438\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ace/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ach/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/af/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/an/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ar/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/as/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ast/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/az/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/be/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bg/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bn-BD/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bn-IN/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bn/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bo/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bqi/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/br/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/brx/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/bs/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ca-valencia/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ca/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/cak/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/ckb/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/crh/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/cs/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/cy/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/da/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/de/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/dsb/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/el/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/en-CA/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/en-GB/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/en-US/browser/newtab/newtab.ftl", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/locales/eo/bro