@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055152 - Added update pathway for address capture prompt r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,sfamisa,parker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314901\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/address/AddressSaveDialogContent.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/address/AddressSaveDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/address/AddressSaveDialogFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "d732cf0e29554bc45bfd7e23edb7de32857e5891", "git_parents": ["b1be8e55fb401e878b653ed47cfb4fbfc9863014"], "node": "387658a075edc7597347d4d947c5c562bcabb317", "parents": ["49269f4d4b18f3622313a7b9a0fd61c30866b465"], "tags": []}, {"author": "fmasalha \u003cfmasalha@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055153 - Fixed floating address capture prompt r=android-reviewers,sfamisa\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314906\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/prompts/address/AddressSaveDialogFragment.kt"], "git_node": "f87c4e30e6c7288d022a71834a0212e118914297", "git_parents": ["d732cf0e29554bc45bfd7e23edb7de32857e5891"], "node": "9e5a999aadfb5ce6e59cbe4ded0ed15df0f87f7f", "parents": ["387658a075edc7597347d4d947c5c562bcabb317"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052034 - Move new strings added as part of about:addons Nova restyling out of locales preview. r=willdurand,fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316035\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/appExtensionFields.ftl", "toolkit/locales-preview/nova-aboutAddons.ftl", "toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/about/aboutAddons.ftl", "toolkit/locales/jar.mn", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/aboutaddons.html", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/content/components/aboutaddons-themes-picker.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/internal/ThemesBundledLocalization.sys.mjs", "toolkit/mozapps/extensions/test/browser/browser_verify_l10n_strings.js"], "git_node": "1a8c36e8a8506d9f237ea2d469948d4e7812a7c7", "git_parents": ["f87c4e30e6c7288d022a71834a0212e118914297"], "node": "e4b10c81e5af32766a6395a653e6419211039ccf", "parents": ["9e5a999aadfb5ce6e59cbe4ded0ed15df0f87f7f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052034 - Add inline comment note to the theme-picker-mode-device fluent id part of theme-picker.ftl. r=fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nThis patch adds to theme-picker.ftl theme-picker-mode-device the same note for localizers added\nto aboutAddons.ftl themes-mode-device.\n\nDepends on D316035\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316607\n", "files": ["toolkit/locales/en-US/toolkit/global/theme-picker.ftl"], "git_node": "2d8bdc34d047719327fd759bf0567644065ef703", "git_parents": ["1a8c36e8a8506d9f237ea2d469948d4e7812a7c7"], "node": "85c5203b5de55e811c741dad77f6414550a3b796", "parents": ["e4b10c81e5af32766a6395a653e6419211039ccf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060814 - Set `CC_KNOWN_WRAPPER_CUSTOM` from the configured compiler wrapper. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`cc-rs` knows a fixed set of wrapper names and otherwise takes the first entry of\n`CC`/`CXX` for the compiler, so an unrecognized wrapper leaves the `swgl` build\nscript selecting `/u` over `/clang:-undef` and its generated shaders fail to\npreprocess. `COMPILER_WRAPPER` starts with a resolved path, so configure derives\n`CC_KNOWN_WRAPPER_CUSTOM` from it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316638\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "config/makefiles/rust.mk"], "git_node": "52d76fba547356565adfdc4ab487147a6731d14a", "git_parents": ["2d8bdc34d047719327fd759bf0567644065ef703"], "node": "74c66713415034e4bac075551ce594fcfd191336", "parents": ["85c5203b5de55e811c741dad77f6414550a3b796"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059986 - Suppress unnecessary Microsoft assembler output on Windows builds r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\n`ml` and `ml64` print a banner and the name of each file they assemble.\nPass `-nologo` and `-quiet` to suppress this informational output.\n\n`armasm64` supports `-nologo` but rejects `-quiet`. Give it a distinct\nassembler type so flags depend on the assembler rather than the target CPU.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316464\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/compile-checks.configure", "build/moz.configure/flags.configure", "build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure"], "git_node": "d716d1a64f5a48d8082b1bfe97d119cbc51c127d", "git_parents": ["52d76fba547356565adfdc4ab487147a6731d14a"], "node": "c107205f073f14a81be90aed8596bba8f3365896", "parents": ["74c66713415034e4bac075551ce594fcfd191336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luca Greco \u003clgreco@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055606 - Stop mirroring addons-search-detection Glean events to Legacy Telemetry. r=chutten,zombie\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315591\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/search-detection/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/search-detection/tests/browser/browser_client_side_redirection.js", "browser/extensions/search-detection/tests/browser/browser_server_side_redirection.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Events.yaml"], "git_node": "e4adcd45a4d413b855f29bb7af89d659f44d9c39", "git_parents": ["d716d1a64f5a48d8082b1bfe97d119cbc51c127d"], "node": "3a72b1cef66240298981e7312e36e8973d157a83", "parents": ["c107205f073f14a81be90aed8596bba8f3365896"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Drew Willcoxon \u003cadw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059583 - Show the visited and bookmarked urlbar result explanations in the correct order in RTL. r=dao,desktop-theme-reviewers,urlbar-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315475\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css"], "git_node": "84a0df041175a3725c116fee2c48969f7d1d68de", "git_parents": ["e4adcd45a4d413b855f29bb7af89d659f44d9c39"], "node": "51d4e18a0e342269235e7748bc01e56e511852b7", "parents": ["3a72b1cef66240298981e7312e36e8973d157a83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057183 - Replace __VERSION__ earlier during translation. r=gfx-reviewers,gw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316893\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/glsl-to-cxx/src/lib.rs", "gfx/wr/swgl/build.rs"], "git_node": "2aea535b1921082c1227bea3ff4dc2ca03c720d1", "git_parents": ["84a0df041175a3725c116fee2c48969f7d1d68de"], "node": "3fcfe2ee9f22115e32db11f844b84c21727e34a1", "parents": ["51d4e18a0e342269235e7748bc01e56e511852b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060787 - Use the shared useWidgetTelemetry hook for the Stocks widget r=reemhamz\n\nMove the Stocks widget off its inline WIDGETS_IMPRESSION, WIDGETS_USER_EVENT,\nand WIDGETS_ERROR dispatches onto the shared useWidgetTelemetry hook already\nused by Picture of the Day, Lists, and Clocks. Stocks.jsx calls the hook once\nfor the impression observer, the context-menu user events, and the load error\n(passed down to StocksError); the now-unused USER_ACTION_TYPES constant is\nremoved. The events, message routing, impression threshold, and payloads are\nunchanged, so there is no user-facing or telemetry change.\n\nAlso wire the Stocks feed into the ASRouter devtools \"Expire Cache\" button so\nthe load-error state can be exercised without waiting out the cache TTL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316483\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/Stocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/StocksError.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/StocksFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/StocksError.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_StocksFeed.js"], "git_node": "db71183867484b1ad3c221943cb47c9f8841ebdc", "git_parents": ["2aea535b1921082c1227bea3ff4dc2ca03c720d1"], "node": "af5322aa25f7208b79c8338d920739c17c2f7ed4", "parents": ["3fcfe2ee9f22115e32db11f844b84c21727e34a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Pypchenko \u003cnpypchenko@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061063 - Stocks widget: show a \"New\" badge until first interaction r=reemhamz\n\nAdd a \"New\" badge to the Stocks widget title, matching the Crossword and Picture\nof the Day widgets. The badge shows once tickers are displayed and hides\npermanently after the first interaction. It reuses the existing\nwidgets.stocks.interaction pref and the shared newtab-widget-lists-label-new\nstring, so there is no new pref, string, or telemetry.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316700\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/Stocks.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks/_Stocks.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/css/activity-stream.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Stocks.test.jsx"], "git_node": "5d34b8f190d0e3abf7b67bbc74983b0e4d47d994", "git_parents": ["db71183867484b1ad3c221943cb47c9f8841ebdc"], "node": "8b8d7ead27f90a938d74bbb04d2ac4fbd050ca9b", "parents": ["af5322aa25f7208b79c8338d920739c17c2f7ed4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061346 - Make the tab strip's scrolled-to-start check actually run. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nThe assertion compared indexes from the test runner's window against elements\nfrom the window under test, so both sides were -1 and it passed no matter what\nthe tab strip did.\n\nWorth checking: measuring from the scrollbox is what makes the revived check\npass in horizontal mode. The arrowscrollbox also spans the scroll buttons, so\nthe old sample point landed on a button and _elementFromPoint returned null.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316859\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_scroll_size_determination.js"], "git_node": "47b20c76fb211d588a734d66be3568fd1a6f779e", "git_parents": ["5d34b8f190d0e3abf7b67bbc74983b0e4d47d994"], "node": "545e59d6773f72db87d8b302b50a5fedf4b2f997", "parents": ["8b8d7ead27f90a938d74bbb04d2ac4fbd050ca9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Holbert \u003cdholbert@cs.stanford.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056804: Maintain a count of content-visibility:hidden frames, to optimize away provably-unnecessary searches for such frames. r=layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe ultimate goal of this patch is to optimize away the tree-traversal in\nGetClosestContentVisibilityAncestor() (which is typically called via its\nwrapper IsHiddenByContentVisibilityOnAnyAncestor()).  This function walks up\nthe frame tree to find the nearest ancestor that has\n`content-visibility:hidden` or `auto`.\n\nIn the common case, the frame tree doesn't have *any* frames at all with these\n`content-visibility` values, and walking up the frame tree is pointless.  If we\ncan prove that we're in that situation and have zero such frames, then we can\nskip the frame tree walk entirely.\n\nWe already have bookkeeping to keep track of how many `content-visibility:auto`\nframes exist at any given time (and their identities). This patch just mirrors\nthat existing bookkeeping, to also keep track of how many\n`content-visibility:hidden` frames we have (incrementing/decrementing as needed\nwhen the frame is initialized/adjusted in HandlePrimaryFrameStyleChange, and\ndecrementing when the frame is destroyed).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316658\n", "files": ["layout/base/PresShell.cpp", "layout/base/PresShell.h", "layout/generic/nsIFrame.cpp"], "git_node": "0f2de4e4e80f31a9ccc1298457c7f929c773f4f7", "git_parents": ["47b20c76fb211d588a734d66be3568fd1a6f779e"], "node": "21725c8a00974232a28e6ca046fca8608d81c275", "parents": ["545e59d6773f72db87d8b302b50a5fedf4b2f997"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jim Blandy \u003cjimb@red-bean.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058784: Move Pixman from Cairo's directory into its own. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth,sylvestre\n\nMove Mozilla Central's vendored copy of Pixman from `gfx/cairo/libpixman` into\n`gfx/pixman`. This commit makes no changes to Pixman source code, and changes\n`moz.build` files only as required.\n\nDetails:\n\n- Drop the `lib` from `libpixman`. The project's website is `www.pixman.org`,\n  the upstream repository is just called `pixman`, and the source directory\n  within that repository is `pixman`. And everything we're vendoring into\n  Mozilla Central is a library anyway, so the `lib` prefix doesn't seem\n  informative.\n\n- As with Cairo, we introduce a parent directory, `gfx/pixman`, to hold Mozilla\n  metadata like vendoring notes, local patches, and eventually a `moz.yaml`\n  file. So `gfx/cairo/libpixman` becomes `gfx/pixman/pixman/`.\n\n- `gfx/cairo/libpixman/src` becomes `gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman`. This is pretty\n  redundant, but the Pixman repo itself puts the main sources in a subdirectory\n  named `pixman`. It seems simplest to keep our directory structure parallel\n  with the upstream sources.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314827\n", "files": ["gfx/cairo/README", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/COPYING", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/INSTALL", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/README", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/dither/blue-noise-64x64.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/dither/make-blue-noise.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/loongson-mmintrin.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/meson.build", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/moz.build", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-access-accessors.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-access.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-accessor.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-asm.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-common.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-neon-asm-bilinear.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-neon-asm.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-neon-asm.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-neon.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-simd-asm-scaled.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-simd-asm.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-simd-asm.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm-simd.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arm.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arma64-neon-asm-bilinear.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arma64-neon-asm.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-arma64-neon-asm.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-bits-image.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-combine-float.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-combine-float.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-combine32.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-combine32.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-compiler.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-conical-gradient.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-edge-accessors.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-edge-imp.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-edge.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-fast-path.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-filter.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-general.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-glyph.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-gradient-walker.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-image.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-implementation.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-inlines.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-linear-gradient.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-matrix.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mips-dspr2-asm.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mips-dspr2-asm.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mips-dspr2.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mips-dspr2.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mips-memcpy-asm.S", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mips.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-mmx.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-noop.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-ppc.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-private.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-radial-gradient.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-region.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-region16.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-region32.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-region64f.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-riscv.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-rvv.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-solid-fill.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-sse2.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-ssse3.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-timer.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-trap.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-utils.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-version.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-version.h.in", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-vmx.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman-x86.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman.c", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/pixman.h", "gfx/cairo/libpixman/src/solaris-hwcap.mapfile", "gfx/cairo/moz.build", "gfx/cairo/pixman-armasm.patch", "gfx/cairo/pixman-edge-saturate.patch", "gfx/cairo/pixman-export.patch", "gfx/cairo/pixman-interp.patch", "gfx/cairo/pixman-rename.patch", "gfx/cairo/pixman-translation-round-in-wide.patch", "gfx/moz.build", "gfx/pixman/README", "gfx/pixman/moz.build", "gfx/pixman/pixman-armasm.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-edge-saturate.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-export.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-interp.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-rename.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-translation-round-in-wide.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman/COPYING", "gfx/pixman/pixman/INSTALL", "gfx/pixman/pixman/README", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/dither/blue-noise-64x64.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/dither/make-blue-noise.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/loongson-mmintrin.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/meson.build", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/moz.build", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-access-accessors.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-access.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-accessor.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-asm.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-common.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-neon-asm-bilinear.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-neon-asm.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-neon-asm.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-neon.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-simd-asm-scaled.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-simd-asm.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-simd-asm.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm-simd.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arm.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arma64-neon-asm-bilinear.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arma64-neon-asm.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-arma64-neon-asm.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-bits-image.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-combine-float.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-combine-float.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-combine32.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-combine32.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-compiler.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-conical-gradient.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-edge-accessors.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-edge-imp.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-edge.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-fast-path.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-filter.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-general.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-glyph.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-gradient-walker.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-image.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-implementation.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-inlines.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-linear-gradient.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-matrix.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mips-dspr2-asm.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mips-dspr2-asm.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mips-dspr2.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mips-dspr2.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mips-memcpy-asm.S", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mips.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-mmx.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-noop.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-ppc.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-private.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-radial-gradient.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-region.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-region16.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-region32.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-region64f.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-riscv.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-rvv.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-solid-fill.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-sse2.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-ssse3.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-timer.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-trap.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-utils.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-version.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-version.h.in", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-vmx.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman-x86.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman.c", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/pixman.h", "gfx/pixman/pixman/pixman/solaris-hwcap.mapfile", "toolkit/content/license.html", "tools/rewriting/ThirdPartyPaths.txt"], "git_node": "f44af92fb6ae3b44b893a4d4fdc9295463fe9247", "git_parents": ["0f2de4e4e80f31a9ccc1298457c7f929c773f4f7"], "node": "d034f45a42f7b5cace1e32f0b278c8422ead3927", "parents": ["21725c8a00974232a28e6ca046fca8608d81c275"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jim Blandy \u003cjimb@red-bean.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058784: Place Pixman under `mach vendor` control. r=gfx-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nAdd a `gfx/pixman/moz.yaml` metadata file to allow `mach vendor` and\nUpdateBot to manage Mozilla Central's vendored copy of Pixman.\n\nMove our local patches into a `patches` subdirectory and adjust their metadata.\n\nThis commit should have no effect on Mozilla Central code: running `mach vendor\ngfx/pixman/moz.yaml ...` as recommended in `gfx/pixman/README` introduces no\nchanges to the source tree.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314828\n", "files": ["gfx/pixman/README", "gfx/pixman/moz.yaml", "gfx/pixman/patches/0000-armasm.patch", "gfx/pixman/patches/0001-export.patch", "gfx/pixman/patches/0002-interp.patch", "gfx/pixman/patches/0003-rename.patch", "gfx/pixman/patches/0004-translation-round-in-wide.patch", "gfx/pixman/patches/0005-edge-saturate.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-armasm.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-edge-saturate.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-export.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-interp.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-rename.patch", "gfx/pixman/pixman-translation-round-in-wide.patch"], "git_node": "26eaae98877226b6fe3d3b856f480260de4c9011", "git_parents": ["f44af92fb6ae3b44b893a4d4fdc9295463fe9247"], "node": "30fcd22ea1454643100182e7305b0e0e4fc4f862", "parents": ["d034f45a42f7b5cace1e32f0b278c8422ead3927"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Import translations from https://github.com/mozilla-l10n/android-l10n CLOSED TREE\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/errorpages/src/main/res/values-sl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/src/main/res/values-dsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/addons/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/downloads/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/importer/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/password-importer/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/prompts/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/sitepermissions/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-in/strings.xml", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/summarize/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-cy/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-dsb/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rAR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-es-rCL/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-eu/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-fr/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-gn/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-iw/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pl/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-pt-rBR/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-sat/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values-zh-rTW/strings.xml"], "git_node": "599d6217169b4ea4401682e7d37a5943d3fed355", "git_parents": ["26eaae98877226b6fe3d3b856f480260de4c9011"], "node": "86f9246621b3829d53ca7f59f44d53ec93d57387", "parents": ["30fcd22ea1454643100182e7305b0e0e4fc4f862"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Glenn Watson \u003cgit@chillybin.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1452337 - Revert \"Restrict WebRender image sampling to the visible sprite sheet cell\"\n\nReverts 2a5a0815893f.\n\nBug 2060286 has since renamed QuadDescriptor's rects and made `bounds` the sole\ncoverage term, so the image quad cannot go back to the literal pre-patch line.\nIt is restored as `pattern_rect: prim_rect` with `bounds` intersected against\nthat same rect, which reproduces the old coverage under the new semantics.\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/WebRenderAPI.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/src/bindings.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/blob.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/image_resize.rs", "gfx/wr/examples/texture_cache_stress.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/prim_store/image.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/scene_building.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_item.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/display_list.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender_api/src/interned_prims.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/reftest.list", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-clamp-ref.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/reftests/image/sub-rect-clamp.yaml", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/rawtest.rs", "gfx/wr/wrench/src/yaml_frame_reader.rs", "layout/painting/nsImageRenderer.cpp", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/reftest.list", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-1-ref.html", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-1.html", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp-ref.png", "layout/reftests/backgrounds/sprite-sampling-clamp.png", "layout/reftests/bugs/reftest.list"], "git_node": "6ff86a1d64c0c8c5942f58aa0c9e3985efe4a8bc", "git_parents": ["599d6217169b4ea4401682e7d37a5943d3fed355"], "node": "83e7b66d32aaeaf6703de3f9779e4bb402f06607", "parents": ["86f9246621b3829d53ca7f59f44d53ec93d57387"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ahanot \u003cahanot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058567 - Enable Glean telemetry for AdsClient by implementing MozAdsTelemetry against FOG r=mconley\n\nReplace the LoggerTelemetry console stub with a Glean-backed MozAdsTelemetry\nimplementation so the vendored ads-client component's telemetry callbacks\nrecord through FOG.\n\nThe ads-client crate ships its own metrics.yaml (category ads_client), but that\nfile is only consumed by the mobile Glean gradle plugin, so the ads_client\ncategory is redeclared in browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml to register it\nwith FOG on Desktop. Bug 2012752 will let the component record its own metrics,\nat which point both the duplicated definitions and the JS callback\nimplementation can go away.\n\nThe telemetry object is built in buildTelemetry() and resolves the\nGlean.adsClient category per recording, so metrics backfilled by the trainhop\nruntime registration are still picked up, and recordings are dropped rather than\nthrowing across the FFI boundary when the category is absent on older libxul.\n\nMetrics: client_operation_total, client_error, http_cache_outcome,\nbuild_cache_error, deserialization_error.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315434\n", "files": ["browser/components/newtab/metrics.yaml", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsClient.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsClient.js"], "git_node": "1865029800dbed080ef7a0f61b0ab98e79cfda2f", "git_parents": ["6ff86a1d64c0c8c5942f58aa0c9e3985efe4a8bc"], "node": "3f3203aa2d5c453653510f798a539e5ff677b775", "parents": ["83e7b66d32aaeaf6703de3f9779e4bb402f06607"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kelly Cochrane \u003ckcochrane@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061026 - Fix for overflowing summary headers for cards in the History sidebar panel r=sclements\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316803\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar.css"], "git_node": "ed7fb05130cc065200f49dc63e25840b57ba2633", "git_parents": ["1865029800dbed080ef7a0f61b0ab98e79cfda2f"], "node": "143065a14eb51dd9c5724305d6c6b63108f532fb", "parents": ["3f3203aa2d5c453653510f798a539e5ff677b775"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057114 - Simplify GMP library unload by letting process exit handle it r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316120\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "eb95c87b3e293fd86947e45a92a20ca04bff4b87", "git_parents": ["ed7fb05130cc065200f49dc63e25840b57ba2633"], "node": "79b212152055cdb0d21cfbebd5e89ff289c76685", "parents": ["143065a14eb51dd9c5724305d6c6b63108f532fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update remote-settings mobile-experiments ct-logs - r=release-managers,diannaS\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316916\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/raw/initial_experiments.json", "security/ct/CTKnownLogs.h", "security/manager/tools/log_list.json", "services/settings/dumps/blocklists/addons-bloomfilters.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/ai-window-prompts.json", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": "8fc60758990a15cb341b2a68ed3cf3df195f139d", "git_parents": ["eb95c87b3e293fd86947e45a92a20ca04bff4b87"], "node": "86dbb784b8b96863c67b2be77e2f5ab29064bd54", "parents": ["79b212152055cdb0d21cfbebd5e89ff289c76685"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056065 - Hold a strong ref to platform font entry. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316012\n", "files": ["gfx/thebes/gfxTextRun.cpp"], "git_node": "4061800c286ff9adf332900aff0762e07cd39241", "git_parents": ["8fc60758990a15cb341b2a68ed3cf3df195f139d"], "node": "fc31636d3aa4111fe417bbc90ec24774b2a6b918", "parents": ["86dbb784b8b96863c67b2be77e2f5ab29064bd54"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Almeida \u003cjonalmeida942@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061031 - Add the error from IPProtectionController to vpn.error_encountered r=geckoview-reviewers,android-reviewers,kaya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316675\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/IPProtectionFeature.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/Actions.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/ipprotection/src/test/java/mozilla/components/feature/ipprotection/store/IPProtectionReducerTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionTelemetryMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionSnackbarMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/ipprotection/IPProtectionTelemetryMiddlewareTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/api.txt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/test/IPProtectionControllerTest.kt", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/IPProtectionController.java", "mobile/android/geckoview/src/main/java/org/mozilla/geckoview/doc-files/CHANGELOG.md"], "git_node": "d92cc9c302c9432fe86d62f7d7759f5ff6841c37", "git_parents": ["4061800c286ff9adf332900aff0762e07cd39241"], "node": "3fc6ebbc3f9a6f2cf3115bd4ac418b1064d4592d", "parents": ["fc31636d3aa4111fe417bbc90ec24774b2a6b918"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061202 - Remove the global device pixel scale. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nIt was always equal to 1.0 so it added plumbing and complexity for no value.\nThis cascaded into a lot of changes due to how the scale factor was used as a type-safe mapping from world space (the root picture local space) to device space.\nSince the scale between the root picture space and device was always one, it effectively collapsed a lot of world space usage into device space.\nThat's actually rather good news, since we want to gradually get rid of world space.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316810\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/cached_surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/quadtree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "6ad307a659bf82123049a43fe2fe71859ffa8550", "git_parents": ["d92cc9c302c9432fe86d62f7d7759f5ff6841c37"], "node": "d7a0ed0a0ee3d9a9120439d350a91c8a7a4f10a1", "parents": ["3fc6ebbc3f9a6f2cf3115bd4ac418b1064d4592d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061202 - Cleanup remaining references to world space in tile_cache/mod.rs. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nFix a few stragglers that weren't caught by the compiler.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316811\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs"], "git_node": "23016a076480e35e2d49f1e465429597fbbb113c", "git_parents": ["6ad307a659bf82123049a43fe2fe71859ffa8550"], "node": "75467d5dca04f262520dc9b3ac6381fd03b858d5", "parents": ["d7a0ed0a0ee3d9a9120439d350a91c8a7a4f10a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Federico Cucinotta \u003cgithub@fedec.online\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046774 - Resolve the tab group from descendant trigger nodes in tab group context menus r=tabbrowser-reviewers,sthompson\n\nThe tab group context menus in the tab groups list are opened with\nopenPopupAtScreen(..., event), so the popup's triggerNode is the\noriginal event target. When the right-click lands on a row's label or\nicon, the triggerNode is that descendant element rather than the row\nbutton carrying data-tab-group-id, making every menu action fail with\n'tabGroup is null'. Resolve the tab group id via\ntriggerNode.closest(\"[data-tab-group-id]\") instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306142\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/main-popupset.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups_list.js"], "git_node": "3e19d93d31b531702b06c2768f88a71ce4677c97", "git_parents": ["23016a076480e35e2d49f1e465429597fbbb113c"], "node": "c9968e1b7ac48e6bdc09204f198dc158450015ad", "parents": ["75467d5dca04f262520dc9b3ac6381fd03b858d5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Federico Cucinotta \u003cgithub@fedec.online\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2040498 - Dismiss the tab groups list panel when a group is deleted from the context menu r=tabbrowser-reviewers,jswinarton,sthompson\n\nDeleting a group from the tab groups list left the panel open, still\nshowing the deleted group, unlike the other context menu actions\nwhich all end with the panel dismissed. Hide the panel containing the\ntrigger node before deleting the group.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306143\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/main-popupset.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_tab_groups_list.js"], "git_node": "1acd09a997b3db450697c253e03198a308e80045", "git_parents": ["3e19d93d31b531702b06c2768f88a71ce4677c97"], "node": "d888cbc3972da43083f20d6c0ecf341aef4ce8cd", "parents": ["c9968e1b7ac48e6bdc09204f198dc158450015ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "0xanshu \u003cpriyanshu.jsx@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1977947 - Set site localization arguments before sizing the forget-site dialog. r=places-reviewers,sfoster,Standard8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316643\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/clearDataForSite.js", "browser/components/places/content/clearDataForSite.xhtml", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_history_sidebar.js"], "git_node": "49ede445def5edcf1f33b9220dc607a324b1e5ae", "git_parents": ["1acd09a997b3db450697c253e03198a308e80045"], "node": "83aedfa5d4b25cc0d04a757a95a79a4b8f0015bd", "parents": ["d888cbc3972da43083f20d6c0ecf341aef4ce8cd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1322643 - Check for infinity in SVGGeometryFrame::GetBBoxContribution r=firefox-svg-reviewers,dholbert\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316896\n", "files": ["layout/svg/SVGGeometryFrame.cpp", "layout/svg/crashtests/1322643.svg", "layout/svg/crashtests/1932954.html", "layout/svg/crashtests/crashtests.list"], "git_node": "c3b058e910a6932cc0c03cdcd5dd6e4ab6040d85", "git_parents": ["49ede445def5edcf1f33b9220dc607a324b1e5ae"], "node": "c28e02c9812c59b56452a543ebff17b032132263", "parents": ["83aedfa5d4b25cc0d04a757a95a79a4b8f0015bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060948 - SW Organize Tabs: Ensure \"Just created\" only persists for current menu instance r=echa\n\nAuto Tab Grouping / 'Organize Tabs'\n\nSpec: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eEDfKdPECzFYQm5_gkIz8lG_t32VPrCQwO-ZMvJpUpM/edit?gid=0#gid=0\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316608\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-group-tabs/smartwindow-group-tabs.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js"], "git_node": "d4fa5af3e53e76e57a100ab47bd205868d444850", "git_parents": ["c3b058e910a6932cc0c03cdcd5dd6e4ab6040d85"], "node": "59c35c7cb010a0e0d9757ac533e1874bafbd51c5", "parents": ["c28e02c9812c59b56452a543ebff17b032132263"], "tags": []}, {"author": "longsonr \u003clongsonr@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061315 - check we're in the composed doc before calling ScheduleForPresAttrEvaluation r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316883\n", "files": ["dom/svg/SVGSVGElement.cpp"], "git_node": "36433a9ba25b5fb9ba87c7ef6acb2172d78bd9f3", "git_parents": ["d4fa5af3e53e76e57a100ab47bd205868d444850"], "node": "2e3ca41e94bec502e657275033acd558b7ad91b0", "parents": ["59c35c7cb010a0e0d9757ac533e1874bafbd51c5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003cevilpies@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060943 - Improve stringification for uncaught errors further. r=spidermonkey-reviewers,iain\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316591\n", "files": ["js/src/jsapi-tests/testPrintError.cpp", "js/src/vm/ErrorObject.cpp"], "git_node": "3dc5b0f15b740639e4ce0331ce4c4739237c2042", "git_parents": ["36433a9ba25b5fb9ba87c7ef6acb2172d78bd9f3"], "node": "25d22d076b49fd30978bddb12466d486f3bd9860", "parents": ["2e3ca41e94bec502e657275033acd558b7ad91b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "kpatenio \u003ckpatenio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058050 \u2014 remove EARLY_BETA_OR_EARLIER in default-bookmarks.html r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316892\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/default-bookmarks.html"], "git_node": "dd53321bab7cf92a0bd0ed5c65a85b715b164c3f", "git_parents": ["3dc5b0f15b740639e4ce0331ce4c4739237c2042"], "node": "9f58fedd8ce60f5663ad1dc8ca4cfa24fb5da186", "parents": ["25d22d076b49fd30978bddb12466d486f3bd9860"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mike Hommey \u003cmh+mozilla@glandium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061012 - Fix building the mozsearch plugin with clang 22. r=nicolas.guichard\n\nclang 22 changed several AST APIs the plugin uses: NestedNameSpecifier became\na value type, and the prefix of a qualifier naming a type is now stored in the\ntype itself (llvm-project commit 91cdd35008e9), DependentTemplateSpecializationType\nwas removed (ba9d1c41c41d), and TypedefTypeLoc::getTypedefNameDecl is gone.\nThe latter was only a shorthand for getTypePtr()-\u003egetDecl(), so just use that\nunconditionally.\n\nFor the NestedNameSpecifier walk in VisitDependentScopeDeclRefExpr, use the\nname and qualifier locations of the DependentNameTypeLoc rather than\ngetLocalBeginLoc, which now spans the prefix of the type too, and would thus\nneither point at each dependent identifier nor let us reach the inner ones.\n\nMozsearchIndexer.cpp only uses our copy of clangd's HeuristicResolver when\nbuilding against clang older than 20, since clang provides its own in\nclang/Sema/HeuristicResolver.h as of that version, but the copy was built\nunconditionally. Only build it when it is actually used, and remove the clang\n21 compatibility added to it in bug 2042682, which is now irrelevant.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316715\n", "files": ["build/clang-plugin/moz.build", "build/clang-plugin/mozsearch-plugin/MozsearchIndexer.cpp", "build/clang-plugin/mozsearch-plugin/from-clangd/HeuristicResolver.cpp", "build/clang-plugin/mozsearch-plugin/from-clangd/README.md"], "git_node": "05fe84b96b4b90ec8eced12af2278cc82644bd9d", "git_parents": ["dd53321bab7cf92a0bd0ed5c65a85b715b164c3f"], "node": "b2fd71c122c23cfc6ca52e50101b40a5234b268f", "parents": ["9f58fedd8ce60f5663ad1dc8ca4cfa24fb5da186"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2061202 - Cleanup remaining references to world space in tile_cache/mod.rs. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\" for causing webrender build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 23016a076480e35e2d49f1e465429597fbbb113c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2061202 - Remove the global device pixel scale. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\"\n\nThis reverts commit 6ad307a659bf82123049a43fe2fe71859ffa8550.\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/cached_surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/quadtree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "163c55d7f47dd3e29d0dc29978dc855eead9b3a2", "git_parents": ["05fe84b96b4b90ec8eced12af2278cc82644bd9d"], "node": "5e125b3454938d738c74565d4ef82123a0a4b4dd", "parents": ["b2fd71c122c23cfc6ca52e50101b40a5234b268f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061404 - Add a Weather preference in the Homepage Settings r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316879\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/home_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "5bf8da2c926614648477e67977d234e3bf0bb52c", "git_parents": ["163c55d7f47dd3e29d0dc29978dc855eead9b3a2"], "node": "cd4d77166dd1652ed4d8760b5ebe8a0f2cfe3686", "parents": ["5e125b3454938d738c74565d4ef82123a0a4b4dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maile Lucks \u003cmaile.lucks@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061542 - Clear dummy content - r=pdahiya\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316953\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/OnboardingMessageProvider.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "ca2a8e42a61a004391f63fb8fdb3efbe05743692", "git_parents": ["5bf8da2c926614648477e67977d234e3bf0bb52c"], "node": "70034d600d15cd8bb4609322c8135d38ec571027", "parents": ["cd4d77166dd1652ed4d8760b5ebe8a0f2cfe3686"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056630 - Fix broken sidebar borders and color mismatch for lightweight themes when using expand on hover in Nova. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,kcochrane\n\nPre-existing rules ensured that, when using expand on hover in a lightweight theme, the sidebar background is a solid color (--toolbox-background-color), thus making it so content area won't bleed in and obscure the contents of the sidebar. These rules were kept.\n\nThe unsetting of border-radius and border-inline seems unnecessary - disabled these for Nova.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316856\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/sidebar.css"], "git_node": "a477e2e22efb87ce81c9980442d97e0aa44f2dc4", "git_parents": ["ca2a8e42a61a004391f63fb8fdb3efbe05743692"], "node": "cb172dd963ad90c4b36144c5afc5e92427ea5b5b", "parents": ["70034d600d15cd8bb4609322c8135d38ec571027"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gijs Kruitbosch \u003cgijskruitbosch@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057898 - fix browser_save_filenames.js to be more reliable, r=mossop\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316308\n", "files": ["uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser.toml", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/browser_save_filenames.js", "uriloader/exthandler/tests/mochitest/head.js"], "git_node": "6db260a14b6ea7dab0251b484520d90f8f6e3c46", "git_parents": ["a477e2e22efb87ce81c9980442d97e0aa44f2dc4"], "node": "2ee25b8a0abeb84ee87f48e931ebab9568ad5dc0", "parents": ["cb172dd963ad90c4b36144c5afc5e92427ea5b5b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nirmaladvani \u003cnirmaladvani@live.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053977 - Remove unused AssertNotMallocAllocated. r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316882\n", "files": ["xpcom/components/nsComponentManager.cpp"], "git_node": "6972268512c52557650ac35ab20c0e0cfbbdca23", "git_parents": ["6db260a14b6ea7dab0251b484520d90f8f6e3c46"], "node": "7c118f624991b1e521a32b79b4fbb44ac7ff7f43", "parents": ["2ee25b8a0abeb84ee87f48e931ebab9568ad5dc0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jack Brown \u003cjbrown@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055378 - Add browser.netError.searchCTA.enabled pref and expose it to about:neterror r=rking\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313112\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "toolkit/modules/RemotePageAccessManager.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "7bd37455013c2093fe7c533318e4df88958311eb", "git_parents": ["6972268512c52557650ac35ab20c0e0cfbbdca23"], "node": "d4f83b4bf864f85484b3dea2c4ee6b8d77284971", "parents": ["7c118f624991b1e521a32b79b4fbb44ac7ff7f43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2005783 - Remove the SearchModeSwitcher observers when the input is disconnected. r=daleharvey\n\nThe switcher registered its pref, engine and DOM observers in its constructor\nand never removed them, so an input that is disconnected but still alive, such\nas a searchbar in the palette, kept reacting to engine and pref changes.\nPairing the registrations with the input's connect and disconnect callbacks\nalso obsoletes the isConnected check in the engine observer.\n\nThis isn't a leak fix: apart from the pref observer, which is held weakly,\neverything the switcher observes is owned by the input's own controller and\nsubtree.\n\nThe enable check was missing its call parens and therefore always passed.\nFixing it means an input other than the searchbar now stops observing while\nscotchBonnet.enableOverride is off, which is the only behavior change here\nbeyond the teardown itself.\n\nWorth checking while reviewing: connect and disconnect need to stay balanced,\nbecause UrlbarPrefs doesn't dedupe observers.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314853\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_new_searchbar_init.js"], "git_node": "45162efbc4074c8e18d73b2a1b129d4f1a8fc8fa", "git_parents": ["7bd37455013c2093fe7c533318e4df88958311eb"], "node": "dab1fa75bc9b136e73d388e220c1c0b778120be8", "parents": ["d4f83b4bf864f85484b3dea2c4ee6b8d77284971"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061016: Avoid reallocating when compressing small scripts r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nIn my quick testing, roughly 1/3 of compressed scripts in JS3/SP3 have to reallocate, but none of those scripts is larger than ~2500 bytes. Saving a couple KB isn't worth the cost of reallocating if we're wrong.\n\nIf I let the browser sit on cnn.com long enough, we eventually compress a 3428461-byte source file that reallocates, so this patch doesn't completely eliminate reallocation, but it does significantly reduce the frequency.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316669\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/JSScript.cpp"], "git_node": "080d1f8249bd9d71e7ef10982a8887615e81f7f9", "git_parents": ["45162efbc4074c8e18d73b2a1b129d4f1a8fc8fa"], "node": "926cd28a2778a1a2e9d657b354288db99bd7926c", "parents": ["dab1fa75bc9b136e73d388e220c1c0b778120be8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Micah Killoran \u003cmtigley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059343 - Toggle reveal password on the composed context menu target so it works for inputs in a shadow root. r=credential-management-reviewers,NeilDeakin\n\nThe textbox context menu decides whether to show \"Reveal Password\" from\ne.composedTarget, but the command handler toggled revealPassword on\npopup.triggerNode. triggerNode comes from the event's retargeted target,\nso once bug 2034256 moved the password doorhanger's field into\nmoz-input-password it is the host element, not the input. The menu item\nshowed with the right checked state and did nothing.\n\nAssign the reveal handler on every contextmenu so it closes over the\ncurrent target. It can't be registered once alongside the popup: the\npopup is built once per window and reused, so a single registration\nwould capture whichever field was right clicked first.\n\nfile_edit_contextmenu.xhtml grows a password variant of shadow-input,\nwhich the existing test then covers. Its type is set in\nconnectedCallback because attributes are not set yet when the\nconstructor runs for parser-created custom elements. testConsecutiveReveals\ncovers reusing the menu across two different fields, which the existing\nper-element loop cannot because it removes the popup each iteration.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316412\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/editMenuOverlay.js", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/file_edit_contextmenu.xhtml", "toolkit/content/tests/chrome/test_edit_contextmenu.html"], "git_node": "013eb4236fa2bc3d428ff1e66754e7b11fc12a30", "git_parents": ["080d1f8249bd9d71e7ef10982a8887615e81f7f9"], "node": "77d29afdef0b5404a952d9172d08622cdb850fb6", "parents": ["926cd28a2778a1a2e9d657b354288db99bd7926c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chun-Min Chang \u003cchun.m.chang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059164 - Reject invalid AudioSegment resample sizes r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315520\n", "files": ["dom/media/AudioSegment.cpp", "dom/media/AudioSegment.h", "dom/media/MediaTrackGraph.cpp", "dom/media/mediasink/AudioDecoderInputTrack.cpp"], "git_node": "73aeb6c2eb448ce65516ab0b8da884ff57f23ca9", "git_parents": ["013eb4236fa2bc3d428ff1e66754e7b11fc12a30"], "node": "1cc4a9beadf70272b6dce5a05924da95b1a81425", "parents": ["77d29afdef0b5404a952d9172d08622cdb850fb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sotaro Ikeda \u003csotaro.ikeda.g@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059636 - Move GetBufferSize() calling place in RendererOGL::UpdateAndRender() r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nBy changing the place, the GetBufferSize() is not called when mCompositor-\u003eBeginFrame() fails.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316752\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RendererOGL.cpp"], "git_node": "641e79a14ac1dcc010924284cab7f9d0039e4c97", "git_parents": ["73aeb6c2eb448ce65516ab0b8da884ff57f23ca9"], "node": "47193664c2b250e6f1643f7f446f42353cb19516", "parents": ["1cc4a9beadf70272b6dce5a05924da95b1a81425"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061153 - Scan the listener array by raw element in AddEventListenerInternal. r=smaug\n\nnsTArray::ElementAt() bounds-checks in every build, so iterating the range\nreloads the array header once per listener. nsTObserverArray's own iterator\nindexes Elements() directly for the same reason.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315915\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp"], "git_node": "98862f7796315f109e19ce2b22f7a6c25c253da9", "git_parents": ["641e79a14ac1dcc010924284cab7f9d0039e4c97"], "node": "96c9e072203966be56d47b24e5096dac5010475e", "parents": ["47193664c2b250e6f1643f7f446f42353cb19516"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061082 - Avoid strong references when walking an unfiltered TreeWalker. r=smaug\n\nTreeWalker::NextNode() holds every node it visits in an nsCOMPtr because\nTestNode() can invoke a NodeFilter, and that script can remove nodes from the\ntree. nsINode uses a cycle collected refcount, so each step costs several\nAddRef/Release pairs; on the bug 2061082 testcase these are around two thirds\nof NextNode()'s time.\n\nWhen mFilter is null TestNode() only reads mInAcceptNode, the node type and\nmWhatToShow, so it cannot run script, and the loop performs no reference count\ndecrements until its final assignment to mCurrentNode. Nothing can therefore\nmutate the tree or destroy a node mid-walk, and raw pointers are sufficient.\n\nTemplatize the body on the pointer type so both variants share one copy of the\ntraversal logic, and dispatch on mFilter. This removes one AddRef and one\nRelease of the five refcount operations performed per unfiltered step.\n\nThe same reasoning applies to the other traversal methods, but only NextNode()\nwas measured, so they are left alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314243\n", "files": ["dom/base/TreeWalker.cpp", "dom/base/TreeWalker.h"], "git_node": "2c390be335d6f388c3073ee0c8573267c20c7a1f", "git_parents": ["98862f7796315f109e19ce2b22f7a6c25c253da9"], "node": "0eb40a50e1a5ba3d26367d17b922b5bcb7b281e3", "parents": ["96c9e072203966be56d47b24e5096dac5010475e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061512 - Update Gradle to version 9.7.0. r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316956\n", "files": ["gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar", "gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties", "mobile/android/android-components/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar", "mobile/android/android-components/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties", "mobile/android/fenix/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar", "mobile/android/fenix/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties", "mobile/android/focus-android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.jar", "mobile/android/focus-android/gradle/wrapper/gradle-wrapper.properties"], "git_node": "a228ddb9ec82e6b2a553ea5d5fa56a4fde50e837", "git_parents": ["2c390be335d6f388c3073ee0c8573267c20c7a1f"], "node": "5dadb4b6ca9e7350bc892a45cd382da6a0bae936", "parents": ["0eb40a50e1a5ba3d26367d17b922b5bcb7b281e3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061512 - Enable parallel builds for Fenix & Focus. r=android-reviewers,jonalmeida\n\nWhatever issues we had with it in CI once upon a time seem to be gone now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316957\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/gradle.properties", "mobile/android/focus-android/gradle.properties"], "git_node": "6c13b686974353a2d930bf9d2549b26d55f96336", "git_parents": ["a228ddb9ec82e6b2a553ea5d5fa56a4fde50e837"], "node": "4b2d172f428bd248d5227c25a5b90887a37bce2d", "parents": ["5dadb4b6ca9e7350bc892a45cd382da6a0bae936"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2061404 - Add a Weather preference in the Homepage Settings r=android-reviewers,npoon\" for causing linting opt failures.\n\nThis reverts commit 5bf8da2c926614648477e67977d234e3bf0bb52c.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/home_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "8956c28a440cdc8347d24f613dd6b41427c82978", "git_parents": ["6c13b686974353a2d930bf9d2549b26d55f96336"], "node": "3fdf0c1ee4322b5b51644d110319074dc96cf38d", "parents": ["4b2d172f428bd248d5227c25a5b90887a37bce2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "hanna.alemu \u003chalemu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060337 - Land strings for Taskbar Tabs Discovery rollout r=omc-reviewers,fluent-reviewers,andhuang,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316103\n", "files": ["browser/locales/en-US/browser/featureCallout.ftl"], "git_node": "3be1cb88ea5c76ea62203465aa65e59831a719ed", "git_parents": ["8956c28a440cdc8347d24f613dd6b41427c82978"], "node": "f3f65d4ec0e1704fea6bbc7939836cddd1a1220f", "parents": ["3fdf0c1ee4322b5b51644d110319074dc96cf38d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yannis Juglaret \u003cyjuglaret@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061342 - Treat whitelistedPaths as folder prefixes rather than arbitrary prefixes. r=win-reviewers,gstoll\n\nThis avoids capturing paths that start with C:\\Windows.old\\ when %SystemRoot% resolves to C:\\Windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316866\n", "files": ["widget/windows/WinUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/WinUtils.h", "widget/windows/tests/gtest/TestWinUtils.cpp"], "git_node": "babf9c5b01220a6295423afc8de9bbb3867067dd", "git_parents": ["3be1cb88ea5c76ea62203465aa65e59831a719ed"], "node": "d16a74e6c6f463f9c9b3592aca4d1a2c35056699", "parents": ["f3f65d4ec0e1704fea6bbc7939836cddd1a1220f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Swarup Ukil \u003csukil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057005 - Add preference for display animations. r=boris\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316338\n", "files": ["modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "f6a2e162905cddbc834821a7c93d13ac00feef0f", "git_parents": ["babf9c5b01220a6295423afc8de9bbb3867067dd"], "node": "70a4883aadc281352c95e414aefa38c56b6dadfb", "parents": ["d16a74e6c6f463f9c9b3592aca4d1a2c35056699"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Swarup Ukil \u003csukil@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057005 - Implement interpolation for display property. r=boris,firefox-style-system-reviewers\n\nThanks to connor.pearson for their draft as a base. We keep display\nnon-animatable for CSS animations while the pref is off.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316339\n", "files": ["dom/animation/KeyframeUtils.cpp", "layout/style/nsAnimationManager.cpp", "layout/style/nsTransitionManager.cpp", "servo/components/style/gecko/wrapper.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/helpers/animated_properties.mako.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "servo/components/style/properties/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/keyframes_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/values/animated/mod.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/box.rs", "servo/ports/geckolib/glue.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/display-interpolation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-display/animations/display-interpolation-none.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-display/animations/display-interpolation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-transitions/CSSTransition-not-canceling.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "e704fe3c9658e16222f6de8ebc93f0bab0d076c3", "git_parents": ["f6a2e162905cddbc834821a7c93d13ac00feef0f"], "node": "a3bcb737300b197112b85f6fe793c56877d2371d", "parents": ["70a4883aadc281352c95e414aefa38c56b6dadfb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "mayankleoboy1 \u003cmayankleoboy1@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061153 - Check the flags before the listener in RemoveEventListenerInternal. r=smaug\n\nBug 1834370 bucketed listeners per event type and dropped the EVENT_TYPE_EQUALS\nguard that used to sit in front of this test, leaving the slow comparison first.\nThe add path already orders these the other way.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315916\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventListenerManager.cpp"], "git_node": "d74baaa11e81e21bb8d0ad31f4cb9647ec850ca4", "git_parents": ["e704fe3c9658e16222f6de8ebc93f0bab0d076c3"], "node": "b2ba8580acbdb320ae5ac17c60e5b4815bebfeed", "parents": ["a3bcb737300b197112b85f6fe793c56877d2371d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Micah Killoran \u003cmtigley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059294 - Remove the password card border and match moz-card's border radius. r=credential-management-reviewers,dimi\n\nThe password card drew its own 1px border, and the moz-message-bar nested at the\nbottom of the card drew a second one, so three sides rendered as a double border.\nRemove the card's border and keep only the message bar's block-start border,\nwhich separates it from the login lines above.\n\nThe card's radius now uses --card-border-radius, the same token moz-card reads,\nrather than --border-radius-medium.\n\nAdjust the hardcoded heights the virtual list uses to pre-compute item\npositions: dropping the card's block borders removes 2px from both, and dropping\nthe message bar's block-end border removes another 1px from the alert variant.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315521\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/components/password-card/password-card.css", "toolkit/components/satchel/megalist/content/components/password-card/password-card.mjs"], "git_node": "11a25f3178a51c223c9fce31f6bae8f2d837cab8", "git_parents": ["d74baaa11e81e21bb8d0ad31f4cb9647ec850ca4"], "node": "dbf4ebc57fa1255b706f5f46d00a9ae1da76913a", "parents": ["b2ba8580acbdb320ae5ac17c60e5b4815bebfeed"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2057114 - Simplify GMP library unload by letting process exit handle it r=aosmond,media-playback-reviewers\" for causing gtests failures at GeckoMediaPlugins\n\nThis reverts commit eb95c87b3e293fd86947e45a92a20ca04bff4b87.\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPLoader.cpp"], "git_node": "972d34f47da2ef9cc7ec9b519b79a1308a2e52f4", "git_parents": ["11a25f3178a51c223c9fce31f6bae8f2d837cab8"], "node": "a96419b2c2b7729989835806220d9622a701400c", "parents": ["dbf4ebc57fa1255b706f5f46d00a9ae1da76913a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2056134: apply code formatting via Lando\" at Arai dev request.\n\nThis reverts commit 1abc6298e106c4ef94528857a4d7120d162a786f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2056134 - Part 5: Add tests. r=bthrall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 7bb924079862d7bab5c3be822354f2ab3ae63687.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2056134 - Part 4: Use pre-calculated fallback encoding for the classic script disk cache MIME-Type. r=bthrall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 07b098aa0decb8ba9e07e96195cf47cd768a9644.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2056134 - Part 3: Use pre-calculated fallback encoding for the in-memory cache key. r=bthrall\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3173e731bf5aba65d25af591398996042ee7e643.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2056134 - Part 2: Pre-calculate the fallback encoding for the classic script source. r=bthrall,dom-worker-reviewers,edenchuang\"\n\nThis reverts commit fd0eb6927252ff3dbf261dd927e14b8826eac206.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2056134 - Part 1: Include the hint charset into the cache key string for the ChromeUtils.getCachedJavaScriptSource. r=bthrall,devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\"\n\nThis reverts commit c0bc4e330d9dd12226c9784fa83979e9217abf71.\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/network-monitor/network-event-actor.js", "devtools/server/actors/resources/network-events-content.js", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.cpp", "dom/base/ChromeUtils.h", "dom/base/test/browser.toml", "dom/base/test/browser_script_loader_js_cache_charset.js", "dom/base/test/file_js_cache_charset.sjs", "dom/base/test/head.js", "dom/chrome-webidl/ChromeUtils.webidl", "dom/script/ScriptLoadHandler.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.cpp", "dom/script/ScriptLoader.h", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.cpp", "dom/script/SharedScriptCache.h", "dom/workers/ScriptLoader.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.cpp", "js/loader/LoadedScript.h", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.cpp", "js/loader/ScriptLoadRequest.h", "remote/shared/NetworkResponse.sys.mjs", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/scripting-1/the-script-element/script-charset-03.html.ini"], "git_node": "4d25de2435cc614267dae2909e2d70b7b798bae5", "git_parents": ["972d34f47da2ef9cc7ec9b519b79a1308a2e52f4"], "node": "12aa864a16ec0c177233fede6574713056990c3a", "parents": ["a96419b2c2b7729989835806220d9622a701400c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Silaghi \u003casilaghi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2053447: Part 5 - Update for enterprise policies.r=mkaply\" for causing bc failures at /browser_suppressTips.js\n\nThis reverts commit 4e82ceeeb78fa5b9a944becb02290f4a48ff84c8.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053447: Part 4 - Update rest of LaunchOnLogin code to use new API.r=omc-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,aminomancer\"\n\nThis reverts commit 07e458f549406c060e81aa0dc14cf7fbd874aa4e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053447: Part 3 - Update Launch on Login pref to use new API.r=tgiles\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9f8a694edd7d84aac01ff7f1a6f9cd4436e53fa2.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053447: Part 2 - Port the existing LaunchOnLogin code.r=hsohaney\"\n\nThis reverts commit 4a2e7ad160211f692de033e21556290bf78d675f.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2053447 - Part 1: Create a LaunchOnLogin interface for macOS. r=hsohaney\"\n\nThis reverts commit 2f90071a94c7481516a555bc2bc2de05b1c36e95.\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/base/content/test/performance/browser_startup.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/StartupTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTargeting.sys.mjs", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/DefaultLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/moz.build", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/tests/test_DefaultLaunchOnLogin.js", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/tests/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/DefaultWindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/moz.build", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/tests/test_DefaultWindowsLaunchOnLogin.js", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/tests/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_disable_launch_on_login.js", "browser/components/moz.build", "browser/components/preferences/main.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_windows_launch_on_login.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_windows_launch_on_login_msix.js", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/nsIMacShellService.idl", "browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.mm", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_startupTelemetry_launchOnLoginState.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser_sma_launch_on_login.js", "toolkit/modules/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/LaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/MacOSLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/UnsupportedLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.darwin.d.ts"], "git_node": "17c317251513c6178e7d15d95a2ccab3d0f74476", "git_parents": ["4d25de2435cc614267dae2909e2d70b7b798bae5"], "node": "bca44a4f0943767ac0daa9f6a4b8e2f8b6300426", "parents": ["12aa864a16ec0c177233fede6574713056990c3a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2014830 - Saturate TimeDurationValueCalculator::Multiply\u003cdouble\u003e on overflow r=boris\n\nMultiplying a TimeDuration by a double promotes the tick count to double and\nconverts the product back to int64_t. When the product falls outside the range\nof int64_t that conversion is undefined behavior, so saturate to\nINT64_MAX/INT64_MIN beforehand. FromTicks(double) already performed the same\nsaturation, so it is factored out into SaturatingTicksFromDouble and shared.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312410\n", "files": ["mozglue/misc/TimeStamp.h"], "git_node": "a19fafbf9d0951a49aa6db71ac04d45b34d9787d", "git_parents": ["17c317251513c6178e7d15d95a2ccab3d0f74476"], "node": "67a2c65af5aed2e57f97c0ae64946c2b9de1d21e", "parents": ["bca44a4f0943767ac0daa9f6a4b8e2f8b6300426"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2014830 - Zero start/end delays when the normalized iteration duration overflows to Forever r=boris\n\nWhen the normalized iteration duration saturates to Forever, the start and end\ndelays are strictly finite and normalize to zero in that limit. Zero them, as\nthe existing mEndTime == Forever() branch already does, so that the active time\nremains well defined.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312411\n", "files": ["dom/animation/TimingParams.cpp"], "git_node": "6a3f8140a11766dbbf92c26a21eb13f8fea0733b", "git_parents": ["a19fafbf9d0951a49aa6db71ac04d45b34d9787d"], "node": "8956ba0ec24d2a7d2dbfb4a94d9895aa179fa76d", "parents": ["67a2c65af5aed2e57f97c0ae64946c2b9de1d21e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hiroyuki Ikezoe \u003chikezoe.birchill@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2014830 - Saturate StickyTimeDurationValueCalculator::Multiply on overflow r=boris\n\nThe integer specialization can overflow int64_t, and the double specialization\nperforms an out-of-range double-to-int64_t conversion, which is undefined\nbehavior. Detect overflow with CheckedInt for the integer case and check the\nproduct against the int64_t range before converting for the double case,\nfolding both into the existing Forever/-Forever handling.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312412\n", "files": ["xpcom/ds/StickyTimeDuration.h"], "git_node": "a38dff894410be4c579aeb132a8f1218b3196c1a", "git_parents": ["6a3f8140a11766dbbf92c26a21eb13f8fea0733b"], "node": "9ea47860f84d4f5a9b9db366b9db369