atic-analysis on OSX r=media-playback-reviewers,profiler-reviewers,migration-reviewers,mconley,canova,alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311090\n", "files": ["accessible/mac/AccessibleWrap.mm", "accessible/mac/DocAccessibleWrap.mm", "accessible/mac/GeckoTextMarker.h", "accessible/mac/GeckoTextMarker.mm", "accessible/xpcom/xpcAccessibleMacInterface.h", "browser/components/migration/nsKeychainMigrationUtils.h", "browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.h", "dom/gamepad/cocoa/CocoaGamepad.cpp", "dom/media/webspeech/synth/cocoa/OSXSpeechSynthesizerService.mm", "dom/system/mac/nsOSPermissionRequest.h", "dom/webgpu/SharedTextureMacIOSurface.cpp", "hal/cocoa/CocoaBattery.cpp", "hal/cocoa/CocoaSensor.mm", "image/decoders/icon/mac/nsIconChannelCocoa.mm", "toolkit/components/parentalcontrols/nsParentalControlsServiceCocoa.mm", "tools/profiler/core/PowerCounters-mac-amd64.cpp", "xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryWatcherMac.cpp", "xpcom/build/PoisonIOInterposerMac.cpp"], "git_node": "796378be9ef3b6c6ec64e833c0db93a7a89695ad", "git_parents": ["c52eaa9c6798bd845cc796b3fd793b9c69480d96"], "node": "efac021ce3702ca72b340526ba8f20bf27c18280", "parents": ["e9f9f689b327cb9c02c98f38d2692a06e4b8b664"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tymur Boiko \u003ctboiko@nvidia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058347 - DOM Media - Use vkGetDeviceQueue2 with FFmpeg queue_flags for Vulkan copy queues. r=stransky\n\nFFmpeg may create device queues with non-zero VkDeviceQueueCreateFlags\n(e.g. INTERNALLY_SYNCHRONIZED). vkGetDeviceQueue is illegal for those\nqueues; fetch them with vkGetDeviceQueue2 using AVVulkanDeviceContext.queue_flags\n(lavu 60.32.100+). Fixes RDD AbnormalShutdown on the Vulkan copy-export path.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316672\n", "files": ["dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/platforms/ffmpeg/FFmpegVulkanVideoDecoder.h"], "git_node": "265f4b8feb80279136bee4245e8730e9efc49ffa", "git_parents": ["796378be9ef3b6c6ec64e833c0db93a7a89695ad"], "node": "d635771d607d1aeee4856cb69526a3600214b32b", "parents": ["efac021ce3702ca72b340526ba8f20bf27c18280"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Luk\u00e1\u0161 Lipinsk\u00fd \u003c6032558+Mr-Tao@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1707415 - Restore GTK X11 windows to workspace zero. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nTreat workspace zero as a valid EWMH desktop. Defer workspace requests for unmapped GTK windows until gtk_widget_show() has queued the MapRequest, because GTK3 rewrites its initial hints and window managers ignore requests for unmanaged windows.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315322\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowX11.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWindowX11.h"], "git_node": "3c7521444e302dc0c08700a9cb315f9e123519fb", "git_parents": ["265f4b8feb80279136bee4245e8730e9efc49ffa"], "node": "d331a39e95992e9acafafd48ca60b72e0b9edd52", "parents": ["d635771d607d1aeee4856cb69526a3600214b32b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tiaan Louw \u003ctlouw@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056189 - Add tests for applying margin-trim styles dynamically r=layout-reviewers,jfkthame\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312980\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-style-change-triggers-layout-block-end.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-style-change-triggers-layout-block-start.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-style-change-triggers-layout-block.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-style-change-triggers-layout-block-end.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-style-change-triggers-layout-block-start.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-box/margin-trim/block-container-style-change-triggers-layout-block.html"], "git_node": "737abad80cbc2631f937dcb3a8ed64964b5734da", "git_parents": ["3c7521444e302dc0c08700a9cb315f9e123519fb"], "node": "1d89804c965084bb0f765d914929315dfd2fdec3", "parents": ["d331a39e95992e9acafafd48ca60b72e0b9edd52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061202 - Remove the global device pixel scale. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nIt was always equal to 1.0 so it added plumbing and complexity for no value.\nThis cascaded into a lot of changes due to how the scale factor was used as a type-safe mapping from world space (the root picture local space) to device space.\nSince the scale between the root picture space and device was always one, it effectively collapsed a lot of world space usage into device space.\nThat's actually rather good news, since we want to gradually get rid of world space.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316810\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/batch.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/composite.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/frame_builder.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/cached_surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/invalidation/quadtree.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/picture.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/render_target.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/space.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/surface.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs", "gfx/wr/webrender/src/visibility.rs"], "git_node": "f5f15bdce5583cede8fb25fd1cda3df109a58ec8", "git_parents": ["737abad80cbc2631f937dcb3a8ed64964b5734da"], "node": "5f6217028f8473b359566e49a6151e99bcc74af9", "parents": ["1d89804c965084bb0f765d914929315dfd2fdec3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Silva \u003cnsilva@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061202 - Cleanup remaining references to world space in tile_cache/mod.rs. r=gfx-reviewers,wsmind\n\nFix a few stragglers that weren't caught by the compiler.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316811\n", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/tile_cache/mod.rs"], "git_node": "19b69c4b321ae145ec81c6b4afe5231e4333bf2b", "git_parents": ["f5f15bdce5583cede8fb25fd1cda3df109a58ec8"], "node": "033eb6d4e3ad46fb5262b486d561c4901cfc2ffb", "parents": ["5f6217028f8473b359566e49a6151e99bcc74af9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Ledbetter \u003ctim.ledbetter@ladybird.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060080 [wpt PR 61680] - [css-view-transitions] Remove references to non-existent scripts, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-view-transitions] Remove references to non-existent scripts (#61680)\n\n`support/utils.js` didn't exist at the point `document-active-view-transition.html` was added in 7f9e7d2d3b.\n\nSimilarly, `transitionevent-interface.js` didn't exist at the point `transitionevent-interface.html` was added in b040cb2a07.\n--\n\nwpt-commits: b318e17a2f726eeb33bf9d88275341675da28fc5\nwpt-pr: 61680\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-transitions/transitionevent-interface.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/document-active-view-transition.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-view-transitions/scoped/element-active-view-transition.html"], "git_node": "c5274d408f5844108c5d3676eb8b49c6abeb5273", "git_parents": ["19b69c4b321ae145ec81c6b4afe5231e4333bf2b"], "node": "6f4eff62eb962f37a256daae9031689be62392b7", "parents": ["033eb6d4e3ad46fb5262b486d561c4901cfc2ffb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059689 [wpt PR 61656] - script: More carefully handle dirty root and descendant damage marking, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nscript: More carefully handle dirty root and descendant damage marking\n\nScript passes a dirty root to layout along with setting the\nHAS_DIRTY_DESCENDANTS flag on elements at or below that root indicating\nthat children need to be traversed. There was an undocumented invariant\nthat no nodes above that dirty root were marked with\nHAS_DIRTY_DESCENDANTS, as the flag itself was used to determine\nwhen the dirty root is raised to some common ancestor of the old dirty\nroot and a damaged node.\n\nThere were some problems with the old implementation and this change\nfixes them by hewing closer to Gecko (from which we took this design).\nNotably:\n\n- In the complex situation where we cannot trivially calculate the dirty\n  root, we now calculate it by walking up from the old dirty root and\n  finding the first element which already has the flag set.\n- When removing nodes from the flat tree, if they were the previous\n  dirty root, the dirty root is cleared.\n- Ensure that all marking traversals for HAS_DIRTY_DESCENDANTS flag\n  marking happen in the flat tree.\n- When slotting nodes into `\u003cslot\u003e` elements, the style and layout data\n  of fallback content is cleared, and the dirty root is potentially reset.\n- Comments are added everywhere in this tricky algorithm explaining what\n  the heck is going on.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 109157591bbac64650ebb8c4e4875d4fdbff2669\nwpt-pr: 61656\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/shadow-dom/crashtests/modify-sibling-of-shadowroot-after-attach.html"], "git_node": "964c21252ea9188707445546be3511a63be76c18", "git_parents": ["c5274d408f5844108c5d3676eb8b49c6abeb5273"], "node": "0e05babc9a1560e07afef50cd2f9bc6468f87ab0", "parents": ["6f4eff62eb962f37a256daae9031689be62392b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joanne Pan \u003c71951015+J0pan@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060566 [wpt PR 61722] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319929, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=319929 (#61722)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 18234c81f0fa4201252df42038ffb8cde832a7b2\nwpt-pr: 61722\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-values/random-item-in-container-query.tentative.html"], "git_node": "1afd4074fddfaafb4db9c4943dce74ab46171ed3", "git_parents": ["964c21252ea9188707445546be3511a63be76c18"], "node": "4a532ec5013e60d0c0203505a14537b187660c08", "parents": ["0e05babc9a1560e07afef50cd2f9bc6468f87ab0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ravjit Uppal \u003cravjit@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060507 [wpt PR 61718] - [CE] Replace stream attribute in \u003ccamera\u003e and \u003cmicrophone\u003e with track, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CE] Replace stream attribute in \u003ccamera\u003e and \u003cmicrophone\u003e with track\n\nThis CL refactors HTMLCameraElement and HTMLMicrophoneElement to inherit\nfrom a new base class, HTMLMediaTrackElementBase (which inherits from\nHTMLMediaCaptureElementBase). This new base class replaces the 'stream'\nattribute and 'onstream' event handler with a 'track' attribute\n(returning a MediaStreamTrack) and an 'ontrack' event handler, which are\nmore appropriate for single-track media elements.\n\nThe 'stream' attribute and 'onstream' event handler are moved to\nHTMLUserMediaElement. UserMediaRequestProviderImpl is updated to extract\nand set the correct audio or video track for microphone and camera\nelements respectively. Web platform tests and unit tests are added to\nverify the new IDL and behavior.\n\nBug: 538119454\nChange-Id: Ia3ce2211768a66ee2e2f45d8c08140dc18eac58c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8139699\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Bo Liu \u003cboliu@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ravjit Uppal \u003cravjit@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673287}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 123fbf3003bb1277efbc0612ff55e689ba755db9\nwpt-pr: 61718\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/camera-track-attribute.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/idlharness.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/idlharness.tentative.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/microphone-track-attribute.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/camera-element.tentative.idl", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/microphone-element.tentative.idl"], "git_node": "6a5ba108d49ca07f5f4b6c6852dead572edd36e1", "git_parents": ["1afd4074fddfaafb4db9c4943dce74ab46171ed3"], "node": "2784419b56f0511ad4255b8a396a72b41d41a3b8", "parents": ["4a532ec5013e60d0c0203505a14537b187660c08"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060507 [wpt PR 61718] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61718\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/camera-track-attribute.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/idlharness.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/idlharness.tentative.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/microphone-track-attribute.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "8a1f46e05fa1fb0169f38e30ba609940ea84dd80", "git_parents": ["6a5ba108d49ca07f5f4b6c6852dead572edd36e1"], "node": "9e072f919882d5c587602c08e9878fb832375b29", "parents": ["2784419b56f0511ad4255b8a396a72b41d41a3b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050062 [wpt PR 60843] - [iframe] Disregard initial 0 from ResizeObserver, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iframe] Disregard initial 0 from ResizeObserver (#60843)\n\nThis change deflakes the tests.\n\nFixed: 525685238, 526855496\nChange-Id: I6d286e8cca28c53227bbc96c665c4bdadc118c5b\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/7989292\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1651384}\n\nCo-authored-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e0323e5fe8dec1028cd6891783f9ae91ba8419bc\nwpt-pr: 60843\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-navigation.html"], "git_node": "c5ea762ba11a45f06a03c2bf9b82992a2f56d133", "git_parents": ["8a1f46e05fa1fb0169f38e30ba609940ea84dd80"], "node": "c0b0f797fdb8e9f25c7b6a59571db438cf7dacf7", "parents": ["9e072f919882d5c587602c08e9878fb832375b29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050614 [wpt PR 60905] - [iframe] Re-Fix yet another flaky case, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iframe] Re-Fix yet another flaky case (#60905)\n\nIt turned out that the last effort to fix \"yet another flaky\ncase\" in crrev.com/c/8001110 incorrectly used `assert_equals`\nwhen comparing arrays. That made the flakiness worse. This\npatch fixes it to use `assert_array_equals` instead.\n\nRan the test 100 times locally and observed no flakes.\n\nBug: 525685238, 418397278\nChange-Id: Id0c0747b436a22956bb2c48fb020a1730f193fc4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8001131\nCommit-Queue: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1652488}\n\nCo-authored-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 1200f01b287fa2bea1a52ec40c7f7194a555d6cd\nwpt-pr: 60905\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-navigation.html"], "git_node": "456a9d995b9a79dd6c730aa1485305e2180e8c94", "git_parents": ["c5ea762ba11a45f06a03c2bf9b82992a2f56d133"], "node": "2c4ca720faa76cd562b4ce58cf64412bfbc11646", "parents": ["c0b0f797fdb8e9f25c7b6a59571db438cf7dacf7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055715 [wpt PR 61344] - [iframe] Support `allowed-origins` attribute, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iframe] Support `allowed-origins` attribute (#61344)\n\nThis patch support the `allowed-origins` attribute of the\n`\u003cmeta\u003e` element for responsively-sized iframes. The addition\nof this attribute is discussed with the security team, and is\ncurrently being discussed at WHATWG[1].\n\nThis attribute has the same syntax as CSP `frame-ancestors`,\nand that it reuses the underlying logic. It restricts the\neffect of `responsive-embedded-sizing` meta tag by the origin\nof the container.\n\nAll the changes are under an experimental runtime flag.\n\n[1]: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12444#issuecomment-4954800369\n\nBug: 418397278\nChange-Id: I2af4c4d4e80e1a3efb8b52ad512f1493157d01b8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8084061\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1663715}\n\nCo-authored-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f1401e8ac6cac0cbe6f3008fbbc0edafd73b9d34\nwpt-pr: 61344\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-400x200root.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-allowed-origins-missing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-allowed-origins.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-dom-content-loaded.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-icb.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-after-head.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-append-after-body.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-append-to-doc.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-append.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-name-change-after-body.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-name-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-remove.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-write.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-in-body.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-navigation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-request-resize.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-slow.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-allowed-origins.html"], "git_node": "0df1f26d1bf3ab73435a286396643e1dcb474516", "git_parents": ["456a9d995b9a79dd6c730aa1485305e2180e8c94"], "node": "3e75bf2feb9ea5940b63782b049de9c5e0ae5941", "parents": ["2c4ca720faa76cd562b4ce58cf64412bfbc11646"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055715 [wpt PR 61344] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61344\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-allowed-origins.html.ini"], "git_node": "178f0bec9959d9455f6ccf97339e5afe97bcab21", "git_parents": ["0df1f26d1bf3ab73435a286396643e1dcb474516"], "node": "2b49f2a5d1de75af0c23333bd8b729d29a99750d", "parents": ["3e75bf2feb9ea5940b63782b049de9c5e0ae5941"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056746 [wpt PR 61465] - Make fragmented-inline-block-002-print.html pass in Blink., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake fragmented-inline-block-002-print.html pass in Blink. (#61465)\n\nSet body margin to 0, to prevent a last-resort break before the tall\ninline-block.\n\nSee also crbug.com/40277379 regarding last-resort breaks. Blink is the\nonly engine that allows breaks like this. It's not a spec violation, but\nit may be a compat issue. This detail doesn't seem to be relevant for\nthis test though, so just avoid the problem by setting the margin to 0.\n\nBug: 40133842\nChange-Id: Ic487493d1defd691114faaa2289e6337dc723c9e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8131600\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1666939}\n\nCo-authored-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f7fd85429ab4276e076c4157d18d823393bb67f0\nwpt-pr: 61465\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/printing/fragmented-inline-block-002-print-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/printing/fragmented-inline-block-002-print.html"], "git_node": "466ca8d520c6c97b8f236ab7869bc03cb1f85925", "git_parents": ["178f0bec9959d9455f6ccf97339e5afe97bcab21"], "node": "e092ffdbfcc693885d821f84af1ba3d20a18de19", "parents": ["2b49f2a5d1de75af0c23333bd8b729d29a99750d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "dependabot[bot] \u003c49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056422 [wpt PR 61431] - Bump actions/setup-node from 4 to 7, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBump actions/setup-node from 4 to 7\n\nBumps [actions/setup-node](https://github.com/actions/setup-node) from 4 to 7.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/setup-node/compare/v4...v7)\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/documentation.yml"], "git_node": "7e35810864e9a6835ed49321946faf65d97c1a1e", "git_parents": ["466ca8d520c6c97b8f236ab7869bc03cb1f85925"], "node": "c48d8d9a26bd37f7d2a2eec7f9c871f9ff33becf", "parents": ["e092ffdbfcc693885d821f84af1ba3d20a18de19"], "tags": []}, {"author": "dependabot[bot] \u003c49699333+dependabot[bot]@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056423 [wpt PR 61432] - Bump actions/setup-python from 5 to 7, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBump actions/setup-python from 5 to 7\n\nBumps [actions/setup-python](https://github.com/actions/setup-python) from 5 to 7.\n- [Release notes](https://github.com/actions/setup-python/releases)\n- [Commits](https://github.com/actions/setup-python/compare/v5...v7)\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/documentation.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/manifest.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/regen_certs.yml", "testing/web-platform/tests/.github/workflows/update_codeowners.yml"], "git_node": "0584441b1b15e224af2e58e1c2a5bb2e6992f239", "git_parents": ["7e35810864e9a6835ed49321946faf65d97c1a1e"], "node": "1bde2f5980c9b5dc792b28955b63efd9ca5f8e0a", "parents": ["c48d8d9a26bd37f7d2a2eec7f9c871f9ff33becf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Viktoriya Bryhider \u003cvbryhider@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060466 [wpt PR 61713] - WebTransport: draining promise implementation, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebTransport: draining promise implementation\n\nPlumbs a server-originated \"draining\" signal (DRAIN_WEBTRANSPORT_SESSION\ncapsule / HTTP/3 GOAWAY) up to the WebTransport.draining promise.\n\nSpec: https://w3c.github.io/webtransport/#dom-webtransport-draining\nIETF: https://www.ietf.org/archive/id/draft-ietf-webtrans-http3-13.html#name-interaction-with-the-http-3\nChange-Id: Ia7212e6403a7a3fe4bcebbab0940db5cbb5ef39c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8139201\nReviewed-by: Dave Risney \u003cdavid.risney@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Camille Lamy \u003cclamy@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Viktoriya Bryhider \u003cvbryhider@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673494}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ac360c95fad7fb32f9c777238ac29681369e8dd5\nwpt-pr: 61713\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webtransport/draining.https.any.js"], "git_node": "19a6bc978c7d6ded98b6506bb1b04b3ca920a6ce", "git_parents": ["0584441b1b15e224af2e58e1c2a5bb2e6992f239"], "node": "a1fe6de4d287dc114d20786d9f85a38ceb25ea18", "parents": ["1bde2f5980c9b5dc792b28955b63efd9ca5f8e0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060485 [wpt PR 61715] - paint: Lock touch panning to its initial dominant axis, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd test for \"axis lock with direction change\"\n\nSigned-off-by: Euclid Ye \u003cyezhizhenjiakang@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 73dff7c1179ee471bee7e005cdc8fc854ed76885\nwpt-pr: 61715\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/pointerevents/touch-scroll-axis-lock-with-scroll-chain.html"], "git_node": "4d9ce1998c5eb26e8997b146dd5ddec0a619a935", "git_parents": ["19a6bc978c7d6ded98b6506bb1b04b3ca920a6ce"], "node": "2b8c2b9f85d8f5cbd1edfb61d83b69b319826b63", "parents": ["a1fe6de4d287dc114d20786d9f85a38ceb25ea18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060485 [wpt PR 61715] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61715\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/pointerevents/touch-scroll-axis-lock-with-scroll-chain.html.ini"], "git_node": "75577323891e8fda1bcccd7bdc4bb48757e5ba23", "git_parents": ["4d9ce1998c5eb26e8997b146dd5ddec0a619a935"], "node": "93004401323b537d2aad8666022ec95f85129816", "parents": ["2b8c2b9f85d8f5cbd1edfb61d83b69b319826b63"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nina Satragno \u003cnsatragno@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059909 [wpt PR 61670] - [webauthn] Fix webdriver WPTs missing user_handle, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[webauthn] Fix webdriver WPTs missing user_handle\n\n`user_handle` is required when adding resident credentials through\nWebDriver. Update WPT tests that create resident credentials to\nexplicitly provide it, and add a test that validates that webdriver\nrejects when it is not provided for resident credentials.\n\nIt should also be required for large blobs, although this isn't\ncurrently spec'd (https://github.com/w3c/webauthn/issues/2452). For now,\nupdate the large blob test so it runs on Chrome.\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=1778f6b3-0c94-4274-9357-79eaa4657b86\n\nFixes https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/issues/61546\n\nInclude-Ci-Only-Tests: chromium.linux:Linux Tests|webdriver_wpt_tests\nChange-Id: Iba8f130b8a1859a6239cbe4fc3611d5f646da890\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8179309\nReviewed-by: Ken Buchanan \u003ckenrb@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Nina Satragno \u003cnsatragno@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673501}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 93325425d87361745041aa3d94f9df7d9edd805f\nwpt-pr: 61670\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/add.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/invalid.py", "testing/web-platform/tests/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/get_credentials/get.py"], "git_node": "2e59ef55d5e415a65e10efa0e23b151acdcf041c", "git_parents": ["75577323891e8fda1bcccd7bdc4bb48757e5ba23"], "node": "62f40cfe7912a7c605024736514d9556cbe84e29", "parents": ["93004401323b537d2aad8666022ec95f85129816"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059909 [wpt PR 61670] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61670\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webdriver/tests/classic/external/webauthn/add_credential/invalid.py.ini"], "git_node": "0018be2e1d73fda63c66280a639d2aef3217cb4b", "git_parents": ["2e59ef55d5e415a65e10efa0e23b151acdcf041c"], "node": "518bfb594f2726da18ae8cad6176eef7e37094cb", "parents": ["62f40cfe7912a7c605024736514d9556cbe84e29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Russ Hamilton \u003cbehamilton@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060593 [wpt PR 61723] - Add a fieldtrial testing entry for ProtectedAudienceDeprecation., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd a fieldtrial testing entry for ProtectedAudienceDeprecation.\n\nThis CL was created on behalf of behamilton.\nPlease review the CL and approve it if it looks good.\nContact the listed reviewers if you have any questions.\n\nBUG=460501344\n\nChange-Id: I2643883dfa2fff9b5e9c6a32da4a6527051389bb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8180889\nReviewed-by: Russ Hamilton \u003cbehamilton@google.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Chrome Metrics Config Manager \u003cchrome-metrics-config-manager-server@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mike West \u003cmkwst@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Russ Hamilton \u003cbehamilton@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Luc Nguyen \u003clucnguyen@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673517}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8bba523e927787d19068e9ae287671c18612b834\nwpt-pr: 61723\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/csp-fenced-frame-src-blocked.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/csp-frame-src-blocked.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/insecure-context.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/fenced-frame/sandbox-mandatory-flags.https.html"], "git_node": "e0279a0e2c52258d0f3aba2416ef9aac26fad66c", "git_parents": ["0018be2e1d73fda63c66280a639d2aef3217cb4b"], "node": "176ee8de6848ebe6b67ec1b4ca50167d418bcd61", "parents": ["518bfb594f2726da18ae8cad6176eef7e37094cb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ananya Anand \u003ct-anaanand@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060627 [wpt PR 61724] - [symbols] Support symbols() in list-style-type, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[symbols] Support symbols() in list-style-type\n\nWire `symbols()` into the `list-style-type` longhand (and `list-style`\nby delegation). The value is stored as a nameless `kCounterStyle`\ndistinguished by `IsSymbolsFunction()`, so layout/paint/a11y treat it\nlike any other counter style; the anonymous `CounterStyle` is built\neagerly. The inspector reports no at-rule for it.\n\nBecause `list-style-type` now parses `symbols()`, its previously failing\n`symbols()` subtests pass: the valid/computed `-expected.txt` baselines\nbecome all-pass and are deleted, and the typed-om `symbols()`\nunsupported-value subtest flips FAIL to PASS. Also add `symbols()`\ncoverage to the `list-style` shorthand parsing tests and an inspector\nunit test asserting an anonymous `symbols()` style reports no\n`@counter-style` at-rule.\n\nBug: 40747844\nChange-Id: I6f7e33f290b59d9cbff79bc6b633dd78b5084a97\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8066847\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ananya Anand \u003ct-anaanand@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673607}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 45745065b834342c9ca494d0f484f19e50f7d774\nwpt-pr: 61724\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/parsing/list-style-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/parsing/list-style-type-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-lists/parsing/list-style-valid.html"], "git_node": "3ea9a929bcd6657f79d2024145dfee598eb7e31b", "git_parents": ["e0279a0e2c52258d0f3aba2416ef9aac26fad66c"], "node": "5741800b7293e1e5361f8e0cce27e4f310c6375f", "parents": ["176ee8de6848ebe6b67ec1b4ca50167d418bcd61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060676 [wpt PR 61728] - [Masonry] Implement flow-tolerance in dense-packing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Implement flow-tolerance in dense-packing\n\nThis change implements flow-tolerance in dense-packing, and fixes a bug\nfound where with dense-packing enabled, flow-tolerance was not being\ncorrectly honored. This also adds new tests, to ensure that within\nmultiple track openings, we will choose the first track opening that is\nwithin flow-tolerance of the minimum.\n\nOur implementation of the dense-packing algorithm now requires 2 passes\n-- the first to find the absolute minimum running position among the\neligible track openings, and a second to select the first eligible track\nopening which is within flow-tolerance of the minimum. Previously,\nbecause we didn't need to account for flow-tolerance, we could just keep\nwhatever was the absolute minimum running position as our placement\nlocation, but now we have to make sure we're picking the first track we\nsee in the flow which is within flow-tolerance of the minimum running\nposition.\n\nApplying flow-tolerance to dense-packing uncovers a new bug, where the\nsecond part of a split track opening was not correctly calculated;\n`column-dense-packing-multi-span-009.html` and\n`column-dense-packing-001.html` are split-track-opening-focused tests\nwhich catch this problem.\n\nTests references for\n`[row|column]-fill-reverse-dense-packing-[definite|indefinite]-size-001.html`\nwere updated, as item 4 should affect the auto-placement cursor, and\neven though item 5 does not, that makes track 4 the logical\nauto-placement position for item 6, given that it doesn't get densely\npacked.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/css-grid-3/#grid-lanes-layout-algorithm\n\nBug: 343257585, 517847439\nChange-Id: If2fb596867778854c4d9168dfefa3ec217b7ac4e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8111177\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673693}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 76a28a20b782121a7c36f5ddf6322de94a5e2b04\nwpt-pr: 61728\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-fill-reverse-dense-packing-definite-size-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-fill-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-fill-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-fill-reverse-dense-packing-indefinite-size-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-fill-reverse-dense-packing-definite-size-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-fill-reverse-dense-packing-indefinite-size-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002.html"], "git_node": "9a86adb8aa5dc159916f8307ee579065dc956e51", "git_parents": ["3ea9a929bcd6657f79d2024145dfee598eb7e31b"], "node": "1801f31fb8f1f4de5c7de3632aed2349e66eba45", "parents": ["5741800b7293e1e5361f8e0cce27e4f310c6375f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060676 [wpt PR 61728] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61728\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-003.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-fill-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/column-track-reverse-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/item-placement/dense-packing/row-dense-packing-flow-tolerance-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lan