entative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/soft-navigation-heuristics/replace.tentative.html"], "git_node": "e9b928ba26e78064cd2cbefcebb9d5eca7bbdfc9", "git_parents": ["eb7cefdc0649ac9e482f8c0e97e5f6233e11b58e"], "node": "253452bbb5944233da40635c878de17539816bb0", "parents": ["1d8a6b49cd7103af22e3277478d0dd9671642284"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060704 [wpt PR 61734] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320980, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320980 (#61734)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 01eee1c621c99c1282002d23c2e568e6866526d8\nwpt-pr: 61734\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/preload/link-preload-as-case-insensitive.html"], "git_node": "b683d922ef5455e1a7bc689f0ec71f6507480eea", "git_parents": ["e9b928ba26e78064cd2cbefcebb9d5eca7bbdfc9"], "node": "5c91daf3bf87351317ba4ffb5eb5ee3564665779", "parents": ["253452bbb5944233da40635c878de17539816bb0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060704 [wpt PR 61734] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61734\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/preload/preload-in-data-doc.html.ini"], "git_node": "f4485f12a598d08d01e0ea945f80b10f838e294d", "git_parents": ["b683d922ef5455e1a7bc689f0ec71f6507480eea"], "node": "fed4dccae8de7684adfd778e617f9f7a00afa72a", "parents": ["5c91daf3bf87351317ba4ffb5eb5ee3564665779"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060693 [wpt PR 61732] - Create IAMF playback test, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCreate IAMF playback test\n\nThis CL introduces a basic test to ensure that iamf audio files can be\nplayed. We confirm 'played' status by checking `timeupdate`.\n\nBug: 540492014\nChange-Id: Iaaa8e8b414a253d17b34245e914c0a7fc45baa48\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8168460\nCommit-Queue: Syed AbuTalib \u003clowkey@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673809}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9ef14f2a2923158e5d1ff065b9d41066ec174e73\nwpt-pr: 61732\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/mediasource-iamf-playback.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/media/iamf_alternating_sine_waves_stereo.mp4"], "git_node": "6b627d25865a71f8d99dd2075ffbce7a1896839b", "git_parents": ["f4485f12a598d08d01e0ea945f80b10f838e294d"], "node": "702e8c8ca5b2448a17ce6f47c59fad3bd7ed8cb1", "parents": ["fed4dccae8de7684adfd778e617f9f7a00afa72a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060693 [wpt PR 61732] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61732\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/media-source/mediasource-iamf-playback.html.ini"], "git_node": "cd2168d30dc85bad1a3e9cd4fa67fd0e6ec2c7c9", "git_parents": ["6b627d25865a71f8d99dd2075ffbce7a1896839b"], "node": "d79f9f786ddddf1ffcbc5b311bca3075b18fc3f1", "parents": ["702e8c8ca5b2448a17ce6f47c59fad3bd7ed8cb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lu \u003cluhua@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060698 [wpt PR 61733] - Route web app origin association handlers, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRoute web app origin association handlers (#61733)\n\nAllow tests to provide dynamic responses from the extensionless\n/.well-known/web-app-origin-association endpoint. This supports scope\nextension tests whose association response depends on the runtime app ID and\nvirtual host.\n\nCo-authored-by: Copilot \u003c223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e8ec9b3f2b87b81fad010dc50bb3bc05c022999b\nwpt-pr: 61733\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/serve/serve.py"], "git_node": "c624dfdc4636a41a796fe8491ebc9e4b02ea8ff4", "git_parents": ["cd2168d30dc85bad1a3e9cd4fa67fd0e6ec2c7c9"], "node": "edf44fff40232b63eeb912067022071751f62a1f", "parents": ["d79f9f786ddddf1ffcbc5b311bca3075b18fc3f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Verde \u003cthesalsa@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060446 [wpt PR 61710] - [CORS] Tighten safelisted Range header value parsing, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CORS] Tighten safelisted Range header value parsing\n\nIsCorsSafelistedHeader() delegated the Range value check to the\npermissive RFC-7233 parser net::HttpUtil::ParseRangeHeader, which\naccepts values that the Fetch \"simple range header value\" algorithm\nrejects: a leading sign on byte positions, \"-1\" as last-byte-pos,\nand a case-insensitive \"bytes=\" prefix.\n\nReplace the delegation with net::HttpUtil::ParseFetchSingleRange,\nwhich strictly implements the Fetch \"simple range header value\"\nalgorithm (allow_whitespace=false). Additionally, reject values\nthat overflow int64_t by checking for std::numeric_limits\u003cint64_t\u003e::max().\n\nTAG=agy\nCONV=6c0675d2-d765-4cce-9da4-2bd9456132ec\n\nBug: 513438970\nChange-Id: Ie81a1b3b639cf9c5ae119be81c8956066e04fe69\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8189598\nReviewed-by: James Scott \u003cjamescscott@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Martin Pan-Verde \u003cthesalsa@google.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kenichi Ishibashi \u003cbashi@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673857}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0e4473863a78276e64f55d3ff1b895a6e9a660e1\nwpt-pr: 61710\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/cors/cors-safelisted-request-header.any.js"], "git_node": "17300c627a5eb4e963e055e101796ca7d6c934e3", "git_parents": ["c624dfdc4636a41a796fe8491ebc9e4b02ea8ff4"], "node": "4b95c345a500486bdb1d8aaa85cad137d3c0ec28", "parents": ["edf44fff40232b63eeb912067022071751f62a1f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "jack \u003c75576058+jackholden@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060552 [wpt PR 61720] - [css-anchor-position] Add tests for referencing anchor-name across shadow trees, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-anchor-position] Add tests for referencing anchor-name across shadow trees (#61720)\n\n* [css-anchor-position] add tentative WPT's for referencing anchor-name from across trees\n\n* [css-anchor-position] remove tentative labelling as behaviour is specified\n\n* [css-anchor-position] lint: remove whitespace in anchor-name-shadow-lower-tree.html\n\n* [css-anchor-position] add assertion verifying positioned element is not aligned to lower-tree anchor\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3a0d734bffeb03c9cfccea0e5324dd2ffdfc2efe\nwpt-pr: 61720\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-name-shadow-higher-tree.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-name-shadow-lower-tree.html"], "git_node": "ad70f8a8c27c06a6a9a1fecd7e86f03f5ddf548e", "git_parents": ["17300c627a5eb4e963e055e101796ca7d6c934e3"], "node": "d11976db16c60ca55681fd3167568219957b8099", "parents": ["4b95c345a500486bdb1d8aaa85cad137d3c0ec28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060552 [wpt PR 61720] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61720\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-name-shadow-higher-tree.html.ini"], "git_node": "b07bbdd7025c9f64fa004d3445795432dc674016", "git_parents": ["ad70f8a8c27c06a6a9a1fecd7e86f03f5ddf548e"], "node": "f37752b932e598e2b61de6b4ad2f7aae7135026f", "parents": ["d11976db16c60ca55681fd3167568219957b8099"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060792 [wpt PR 61747] - Fix typo in interim-response-times.h2.html test., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix typo in interim-response-times.h2.html test.\n\nIt uses header-delay.h2.py which is supposed to reply with a status of\n100 or 103 depending on whether the GET parameter with100 or with103 is\nspecified, but it currently always return 103.\n\nBug: 40251053\nChange-Id: I311b0fbbbdeabc0aab419ff0881867db51639bf6\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8200345\nReviewed-by: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673971}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 33c1f977ed57205c99526805a73fa0c3e2f855d2\nwpt-pr: 61747\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/resource-timing/resources/header-delay.h2.py"], "git_node": "11cb828127685ac3fd0913e1e69db24fca13aa54", "git_parents": ["b07bbdd7025c9f64fa004d3445795432dc674016"], "node": "4ceefa5cc0ba1e9d195535791f017e9732895bbc", "parents": ["f37752b932e598e2b61de6b4ad2f7aae7135026f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060807 [wpt PR 61749] - Make sure we don't try lookup empty ids in SelectorQuery fast path, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake sure we don't try lookup empty ids in SelectorQuery fast path\n\nBug: 542447316\nChange-Id: I9b5de2f48e06c51857238e175465edc19b7bf49d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8194906\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673995}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 00101466e2406273c845d7f528d5e81ebd2a467d\nwpt-pr: 61749\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/querySelector-empty-id.html"], "git_node": "4d3c8ac3753f54c1e92bdf91e415a3ebdc373f51", "git_parents": ["11cb828127685ac3fd0913e1e69db24fca13aa54"], "node": "fc93414443cc95d40dc3be65c11ac9841db24af2", "parents": ["4ceefa5cc0ba1e9d195535791f017e9732895bbc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060807 [wpt PR 61749] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61749\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/dom/nodes/moveBefore/moveBefore-range-iframe-crash.html.ini"], "git_node": "440be11162dde656e90b480a9eb7666f6e238551", "git_parents": ["4d3c8ac3753f54c1e92bdf91e415a3ebdc373f51"], "node": "7be987cdf4b9a6d308984f67c36fbd660a5f275e", "parents": ["fc93414443cc95d40dc3be65c11ac9841db24af2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060487 [wpt PR 61716] - Inverted unknown sibling index condition in SelectorQuery fast path, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nInverted unknown sibling index condition in SelectorQuery fast path\n\nAdd DCHECKs to detect other fast path discrepancies in the future.\n\nBug: 542266637\nChange-Id: Id3cbf10817e0e7f907a43c86faffbb7e86a8c17c\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8194984\nCommit-Queue: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673996}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0ce90816c524defe954e2d1f72d80eb66a83cba4\nwpt-pr: 61716\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/dom/nodes/querySelector-id-nth-child.html"], "git_node": "29c50a96fd9a1d206186520a2bc66d86a7d01d83", "git_parents": ["440be11162dde656e90b480a9eb7666f6e238551"], "node": "b6c0930a88a7de547ae14520df0374deeca07ff3", "parents": ["7be987cdf4b9a6d308984f67c36fbd660a5f275e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060456 [wpt PR 61711] - [compression-dictionary] Add dummy end points when ReportingObserver is used, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[compression-dictionary] Add dummy end points when ReportingObserver is used.\n\nPer the CSP specification, 'csp-violation' reports are only generated when there\nis a 'report-to' directive. See https://github.com/w3c/webappsec-csp/issues/819\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: cadff610b0891de565870cb6759051388cfd090e\nwpt-pr: 61711\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src-nonce.tentative.https.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/dictionary-fetch-with-link-connect-src.tentative.https.html.headers"], "git_node": "0faf7c9834c0cc37aa064aacc522da9371e7efbe", "git_parents": ["29c50a96fd9a1d206186520a2bc66d86a7d01d83"], "node": "f31464ec69cb1ccfc78eb4257017d3d303f4ade0", "parents": ["b6c0930a88a7de547ae14520df0374deeca07ff3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "James Graham \u003cjames@hoppipolla.co.uk\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060477 [wpt PR 61714] - Remove extra debugger pathway for android commands, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove extra debugger pathway for android commands\n\nPassing --debug will have the same effect\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: c9e37547a2dbab0f0fa310b2d7a1e20f623a8e3c\nwpt-pr: 61714\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/tools/wpt/android.py"], "git_node": "f9ba211f8410bd993b3425936fb3f25b3d38d98a", "git_parents": ["0faf7c9834c0cc37aa064aacc522da9371e7efbe"], "node": "0c398d255fdf807883218de4799e1e42945540d6", "parents": ["f31464ec69cb1ccfc78eb4257017d3d303f4ade0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060850 [wpt PR 61750] - Support sanitization using \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" sanitize\u003e, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nSupport sanitization using \u003ctemplate for=\"...\" sanitize\u003e\n\nThe sanitize boolean attribute makes all the descendants go through\nbaseline sanitization (removing scripts and unknown attributes).\n\nThe Sanitizer instance created for those intermediate templates are a\n\"safe clone\" of the main parser sanitizer, or a \"safe baseline\"\nsanitizer if that isn't present.\n\nThis is guarded by the DeclarativeFragment flag, and is meant for\nexperimenting and developer feedback at this point.\n\nBug: 535664974\nChange-Id: I2e9b4f5753e4043cff348ff2b975d1f1f3f73e0e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8125134\nReviewed-by: Daniel Vogelheim \u003cvogelheim@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Noam Rosenthal \u003cnrosenthal@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674017}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 904a89586ce51c18f133f307304e418a3f42bfa7\nwpt-pr: 61750\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-boolean.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-default.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-nested.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-regular.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-template-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-unsafe.html"], "git_node": "ff532d3fecaf8834bc1dbb6bc57c02841df1ef15", "git_parents": ["f9ba211f8410bd993b3425936fb3f25b3d38d98a"], "node": "c3339e02f92629eb97bc1fff02e3fd4c302f31eb", "parents": ["0c398d255fdf807883218de4799e1e42945540d6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060850 [wpt PR 61750] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61750\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-boolean.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-default.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-nested.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-template-element.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/dom/partial-updates/tentative/fragment/sanitize-unsafe.html.ini"], "git_node": "1b996d7516081c349a41b5c8f6a06a1f7cbe4509", "git_parents": ["ff532d3fecaf8834bc1dbb6bc57c02841df1ef15"], "node": "ea5d484c18fc6363d930730bfa6ad5b3736f8dc7", "parents": ["c3339e02f92629eb97bc1fff02e3fd4c302f31eb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniil Sakhapov \u003csakhapov@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060681 [wpt PR 61729] - [border-shape] Limit high miter limit to polygon shapes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[border-shape] Limit high miter limit to polygon shapes\n\nRestrict the large stroke miter limit exclusively to polygon shapes.\nApplying a very high miter limit globally causes curves and arcs\ncontaining cusps (e.g., shape() with arc segments) to draw massive,\nunwanted miter spikes. Polygons still retain the large miter limit to\nensure sharp corners remain mitered.\n\nFixed: 539636521\nChange-Id: I92b8cedd5d30928d49857fffe5de22f4660fed7d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8163886\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Daniil Sakhapov \u003csakhapov@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674105}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9930eb76d90b4569e8563788e9e8d0e8f8102102\nwpt-pr: 61729\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/border-shape/border-shape-polygon-miter-limit-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/border-shape/border-shape-polygon-miter-limit.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/border-shape/border-shape-shape-arc-miter-limit-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-borders/border-shape/border-shape-shape-arc-miter-limit.html"], "git_node": "880fa3fd99363ec3a9c1d7a1efb79297a6a0df91", "git_parents": ["1b996d7516081c349a41b5c8f6a06a1f7cbe4509"], "node": "7324f12a69de6e8e7484c15f2784ac7a2c325ddc", "parents": ["ea5d484c18fc6363d930730bfa6ad5b3736f8dc7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060681 [wpt PR 61729] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61729\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-borders/border-shape/border-shape-shape-arc-miter-limit.html.ini"], "git_node": "5a5040e68eb395524eeeb4383fb7613aab5342c5", "git_parents": ["880fa3fd99363ec3a9c1d7a1efb79297a6a0df91"], "node": "a0c83465e8f49351de40c050b131a746767b4f22", "parents": ["7324f12a69de6e8e7484c15f2784ac7a2c325ddc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jake Archibald \u003cjaffathecake@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059701 [wpt PR 61660] - Add click test for auto popover nested inside hint, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd click test for auto popover nested inside hint (#61660)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: f9a50c1cea3305dbea06dcf55cce4fbb01839fe2\nwpt-pr: 61660\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/popovers/popover-light-dismiss-hint.html"], "git_node": "b4f8f5a6132183fef33ce363f8b7f6e4b14a1116", "git_parents": ["5a5040e68eb395524eeeb4383fb7613aab5342c5"], "node": "4cbff6cc75a2f3fbf41787c8ddcd8ec08622a2ae", "parents": ["a0c83465e8f49351de40c050b131a746767b4f22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yanling Wang \u003cyanlingwang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060981 [wpt PR 61755] - [Masonry] Add baseline tests for grid subgridded to grid-lanes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[Masonry] Add baseline tests for grid subgridded to grid-lanes\n\nThis CL adds item-level and container-level baseline alignment tests for\na grid container subgridded into a grid-lanes container, across the row\nand column subgridded axes.\n\nBaseline alignment that does not depend on the subgrid's own margin,\nborder, or padding already passes with the current code. Tests that\nexercise the subgrid's MBP contribution to the shared baseline are\nexpected to fail and are marked in TestExpectations; they will be fixed\nin the follow-up subgrid baseline implementation CLs.\n\nBug: 343257585\nChange-Id: Ide383fe1edd4cea295f8c163917e3440810df20e\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8159959\nReviewed-by: Celeste Pan \u003ccelestepan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yanling Wang \u003cyanlingwang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674126}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: e54ce28233c78351429e5e7a61d787892c244e7f\nwpt-pr: 61755\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-container-baseline-subgrid-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-container-baseline-subgrid-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-003.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-004-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-004.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-005-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-005.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-006-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/column-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-006.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-container-baseline-subgrid-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-container-baseline-subgrid-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-001-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-001.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-002-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/row-grid-lanes-item-baseline-subgrid-003-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/basel