{"author": "John M. Schanck \u003cjschanck@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055978 - upgrade NSS to dc51b81292977ace436f287cd531967332e977fe. r=nss-reviewers,nkulatova UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316987\n", "files": ["security/nss/cmd/pk12util/pk12util.c", "security/nss/cmd/tests/nonspr10.c", "security/nss/gtests/der_gtest/p12_import_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/dh_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/freebl_gtest.gyp", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/manifest.mn", "security/nss/lib/freebl/blapi.h", "security/nss/lib/freebl/dh.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/ldvector.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/loader.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/loader.h", "security/nss/lib/mozpkix/mozpkix.gyp", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/manifest.mn", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12creat.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12d.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12dec.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12exp.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12local.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12local.h", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/pkcs12.gyp", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/pkcs12.h", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/pkcs12t.h", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmsdecode.c", "security/nss/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "4c985e6fb07bdba0f02605796bc33cf09efce1d6", "git_parents": ["36bb0f76c9fbae695173f4b0c608461cf3f1500f"], "node": "06e87943f13b1f158507775e28c54c74e2ba9fe5", "parents": ["c0e3bad064ced109b726fea7d8cc342706395054"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Lin \u003cjolin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053681 - Treat live-stream media resources as controllable regardless of reported duration r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nHTMLMediaElement::IsControllableMediaSource() gated eligibility for the\nOS media-control interface purely on Duration() vs a fixed threshold,\nto filter out short local sound effects. This is unreliable for a live\nstream (e.g. internet radio): some demuxers (like MP3) estimate a\nduration that grows from bytes received so far instead of reporting\nInfinity, so a live stream's element can stay under the threshold\nindefinitely and never become controllable even though it's playing\nindefinitely.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316305\n", "files": ["dom/media/ChannelMediaResource.cpp", "dom/media/MediaDecoder.cpp", "dom/media/MediaDecoder.h", "dom/media/mediaelement/HTMLMediaElement.cpp"], "git_node": "957c35be0085cee6f75a338025d721b21ce979a0", "git_parents": ["4c985e6fb07bdba0f02605796bc33cf09efce1d6"], "node": "61feebe87c4bdf0a538468eb03ef95b51ab940db", "parents": ["06e87943f13b1f158507775e28c54c74e2ba9fe5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "John Lin \u003cjolin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053681 - Add a browser-mochitest for live-stream media control eligibility r=media-playback-reviewers,alwu\n\nVerifies that IsControllableMediaSource() treats a live-stream media element\nas controllable regardless of its reported duration: both while the duration\nis under the eligible-duration threshold, and after it grows past it.\n\nUses the single-xing-header-no-content-length.mp3 fixture, which carries a\nshort declared-duration prelude followed by a header-less stream whose\nduration is only known once played, so the reported duration grows over\ntime like a real live broadcast instead of jumping straight to a final\nvalue.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316306\n", "files": ["dom/media/mediacontrol/tests/browser/browser.toml", "dom/media/mediacontrol/tests/browser/browser_media_control_live_stream.js", "dom/media/mediacontrol/tests/browser/file_live_stream.html", "dom/media/mediacontrol/tests/browser/live_stream.sjs"], "git_node": "93e7ec7298b7dce82019c7da80fec4366c526073", "git_parents": ["957c35be0085cee6f75a338025d721b21ce979a0"], "node": "660c210e8b43e3bd848ac6e3ddf745cd697ebc28", "parents": ["61feebe87c4bdf0a538468eb03ef95b51ab940db"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nickgrato \u003cngrato@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060582 - [Monitor Agent][FE] message for pages we cant monitor for example about pages. r=yjamora,tetchart,fluent-reviewers,flod\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316860\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/agents/Monitor.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/content/aiChatContent.html", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AgentUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agentui_command.js", "browser/locales-preview/aiWindow.ftl"], "git_node": "9eb65120d9768339eb749f9e89d4f951fcc5f663", "git_parents": ["93e7ec7298b7dce82019c7da80fec4366c526073"], "node": "6ca1e92d477ad8e38156a8ea351a0ee7ab8195e8", "parents": ["660c210e8b43e3bd848ac6e3ddf745cd697ebc28"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054093 - Add /monitor command palette in smartbar r=flozia,urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312316\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/agent-watch.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AgentUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agentui_command.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_command_palette.js", "browser/components/multilineeditor/jar.mn", "browser/components/multilineeditor/plugins/CommandsPlugin.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInputUtils.mjs", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "925d1559db864f88c8f1f41cace825d406854a0c", "git_parents": ["9eb65120d9768339eb749f9e89d4f951fcc5f663"], "node": "aaff4913c4c3c5085159925ee36524543b2c038d", "parents": ["6ca1e92d477ad8e38156a8ea351a0ee7ab8195e8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059538 - Polish command palette ui r=flozia,mlucks\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315415\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.stories.mjs"], "git_node": "ac9309c6170bb17c89aa6f5e25d5d004367a9714", "git_parents": ["925d1559db864f88c8f1f41cace825d406854a0c"], "node": "1da3ba8b3ea51d539bbeaa313edf1023634ddf70", "parents": ["aaff4913c4c3c5085159925ee36524543b2c038d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061404 - Add a Weather preference in the Homepage Settings r=android-reviewers,npoon\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316879\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/static_strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/home_preferences.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/HomeSettingsFragmentTest.kt"], "git_node": "0e7d413e708d7eb994dc0d9d0c81fd051588fee2", "git_parents": ["ac9309c6170bb17c89aa6f5e25d5d004367a9714"], "node": "c5109328ec3604bf7df1efb43a1ea27e4d18c4a1", "parents": ["1da3ba8b3ea51d539bbeaa313edf1023634ddf70"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060980 - Clear the search bar's query context cache between tests. r=Standard8\n\nThe search bar and its view live as long as the browser window, so the view's\nquery context cache outlives an individual test file. browser_searchbar_\nqueryContextCache.js asserts that no context is cached for a page it then goes\non to query on, so from the second run onwards in the same session it trips\nover its own leftovers -- deterministically so under test-verify.\n\nClearing the cache in the shared cleanup also keeps any other search bar test\nfrom inheriting a stale context, which would make the view open synchronously\nwith results fetched by an earlier test.\n\n`mach mochitest --verify` on the test now passes all four steps.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316776\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/head.js"], "git_node": "74b0fac7d8b6f6321afdb1e31e54980a82f39c37", "git_parents": ["0e7d413e708d7eb994dc0d9d0c81fd051588fee2"], "node": "4b6701b26a1cedf3f3d11af409c987b49f35b5af", "parents": ["c5109328ec3604bf7df1efb43a1ea27e4d18c4a1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Kennedy \u003cmkennedy@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054029 - Use moz-button ghost for the preferences dialog close button r=akulyk,kcochrane\n\nThis changes the preferences sub-dialog close button to use the standard ghost button, so its hover state matches the rest of the design system.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314687\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/preferences.xhtml", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_advanced_update.js", "browser/themes/shared/preferences/preferences.css", "toolkit/modules/SubDialog.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "58bd4c92ab1fd70eab48cb3f405cac5d3959d9d9", "git_parents": ["74b0fac7d8b6f6321afdb1e31e54980a82f39c37"], "node": "93f022f82ace16b6bc8210473b7920382a1b5db4", "parents": ["4b6701b26a1cedf3f3d11af409c987b49f35b5af"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rana Al-Khulaidi \u003cralkhulaidi@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060546 - Update broken links in Implementing a Nimbus Experiment Fenix doc. r=nimbus-reviewers,android-reviewers,chumphreys,ohall\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316571\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/docs/Implementing-a-Nimbus-Experiment.md"], "git_node": "c8c19ef4437a9daad4cfa2127e37b19c38f21726", "git_parents": ["58bd4c92ab1fd70eab48cb3f405cac5d3959d9d9"], "node": "d427a8a9d00e87d471da215f0c7670a5a6349d07", "parents": ["93f022f82ace16b6bc8210473b7920382a1b5db4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061631 - Remove unused environ_size counter in setproctitle_init r=ipc-reviewers,nika\n\nGCC 16 fails the build with -Werror=unused-but-set-variable: environ_size is\nincremented in the loop's increment clause but never read. The loop only\nvalidates that the environment strings follow argv contiguously, so the\ncounter can go.\n\nThe environ_size in setproctitle() is unrelated and left alone.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317000\n", "files": ["ipc/chromium/src/base/set_process_title_linux.cc"], "git_node": "2e8442b4d133eca4effbafa2338b4bd79fe5e478", "git_parents": ["c8c19ef4437a9daad4cfa2127e37b19c38f21726"], "node": "32454dc20b7d326a9cd9de6987370d5a680b5fd4", "parents": ["d427a8a9d00e87d471da215f0c7670a5a6349d07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "AndiAJ \u003candiaj@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061643 - Migrate verifyTheExtensionsMenuListAfterRemovingAnExtensionTest and verifyTheManageExtensionsItemTest UI tests to the efficiency framework r=jajohnson\n\nBoth UI tests successfully passed 25x on Firebase \u2705\nAll UI tests successfully passed 1x on Firebase \u2705\n\nDifferential