63957abbc824d338d28c498\nth -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\ntl -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\ntr -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\ntrs -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nuk -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nur -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nuz -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nvi -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nwo -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nxh -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nzam -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nzh-CN -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\nzh-TW -\u003e d1d2694179f2dd76063957abbc824d338d28c498\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "513a7bc066e3b5d8a68a8f7f33919d97c78902ba", "git_parents": ["540de38b334b9a7985e2db48eb12a0d3de58d04e"], "node": "e0e394deb108a2d88f6f2f380e877680f1882404", "parents": ["a0e45b4dce6c924934455b6206514407766a36f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2055978 - upgrade NSS to dc51b81292977ace436f287cd531967332e977fe. r=nss-reviewers,nkulatova UPGRADE_NSS_RELEASE\" for causing linux build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 4c985e6fb07bdba0f02605796bc33cf09efce1d6.\n", "files": ["security/nss/cmd/pk12util/pk12util.c", "security/nss/cmd/tests/nonspr10.c", "security/nss/gtests/der_gtest/p12_import_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/dh_unittest.cc", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/freebl_gtest.gyp", "security/nss/gtests/freebl_gtest/manifest.mn", "security/nss/lib/freebl/blapi.h", "security/nss/lib/freebl/dh.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/ldvector.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/loader.c", "security/nss/lib/freebl/loader.h", "security/nss/lib/mozpkix/mozpkix.gyp", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/manifest.mn", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12creat.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12d.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12dec.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12exp.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12local.c", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/p12local.h", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/pkcs12.gyp", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/pkcs12.h", "security/nss/lib/pkcs12/pkcs12t.h", "security/nss/lib/smime/cmsdecode.c", "security/nss/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "c5640951b4be0722c39daf2cd6c37f25b59e40cc", "git_parents": ["513a7bc066e3b5d8a68a8f7f33919d97c78902ba"], "node": "6f0f7f3b4e3bb2e22d8fe20910a8aaea681c1f62", "parents": ["e0e394deb108a2d88f6f2f380e877680f1882404"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060905 - Migrate installPWAFromTheMainMenuTest UI test to the efficiency framework r=jajohnson\n\nConverted the installPWAFromTheMainMenuTest UI test to the efficiency framework.\n\n Moved the \"Add to Home screen\" prompt handling from a per-test flag into the harness:\n  - OverlayRegistry.kt \u2014 added ADD_TO_HOME_SCREEN_PROMPT (presence + dismiss both cancel_button, side-effect-free.\n\nRetested LoginsTest#verifyMultipleLoginsSelectionsTest and LoginsTest#verifyUpdatedLoginIsSavedTest.\n\nAll 3 UI tests successfully passed 50x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=76274  | try ]]\n\nAll efficiency UI test successfully passed 1x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=76273  | try ]]\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316743\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/PwaTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/OverlayRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/LaunchConfig.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/MainMenuSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/PWASelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/PWATest.kt"], "git_node": "51b1d413c5f07847c243a51cb10ae93362adfb8c", "git_parents": ["c5640951b4be0722c39daf2cd6c37f25b59e40cc"], "node": "4b48d5cf048fa099a0be97f0210761262a173b9f", "parents": ["6f0f7f3b4e3bb2e22d8fe20910a8aaea681c1f62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joel \u003cjoelkelly@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060320 - Scope the newtab event buffer to its owning session r=thecount\n\nEvery concurrent newtab session shares one event buffer, and its entries\ncarry no session identity. Whichever session ends first drains and reports\nthe events queued by all the others, in a ping that describes the wrong\nsession.\n\nTag each queued event with the session that recorded it, and drain only that\nsession's events. The tag routes events and is never reported, so the data is\nunchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316923\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "70a58efaab32c5d3c494313a66a9cf79dc6e8534", "git_parents": ["51b1d413c5f07847c243a51cb10ae93362adfb8c"], "node": "ca1e964ff66052e9e2991846d16bf3440d539d04", "parents": ["4b48d5cf048fa099a0be97f0210761262a173b9f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joel \u003cjoelkelly@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060320 - Flush buffered newtab events at TelemetryFeed shutdown r=thecount\n\nSessions still open when the feed goes away never receive a NEW_TAB_UNLOAD,\nso they never call endSession, and uninit() discarded their queued events\nwithout sending them.\n\nFlush the buffer into the newtab ping before NewTabContentPing.uninit()\nthrows its own away. That covers the \"Send any unfinished sessions\" TODO far\nenough to stop losing events; reporting those sessions as ended is still\nopen.\n\nThe flush reuses the newtab_session_end reason. A new reason means a\npings.yaml change, which is neither trainhoppable nor free of data review, so\ndistinguishing shutdown flushes in the data belongs in its own change.\n\nNewTabContentPing's buffer is left alone. Its submission delay is randomised\nfor privacy, and forcing a submit at shutdown would collapse that to a\npredictable moment.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316405\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "900102cd3173afc593983ce7efc532acec1da75e", "git_parents": ["70a58efaab32c5d3c494313a66a9cf79dc6e8534"], "node": "f26fbdcd3f60dda86060058b5b15b806e93acaf9", "parents": ["ca1e964ff66052e9e2991846d16bf3440d539d04"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joel \u003cjoelkelly@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060320 - Don't report newtab sessions the user never saw r=thecount\n\nendSession() recorded newtab.closed and submitted the newtab ping before\nchecking whether the session had ever been visible, so the never-shown guard\nonly suppressed the session_duration bookkeeping. A hidden preloaded newtab\nstill produced a full newtab_session_end ping for a visit the user never saw.\n\nThat is what the reported cases have in common. Opening a link in a new\nwindow or tab from the topsite menu, the content menu, or the weather\nright-click each consume the preloaded newtab, which then unloads and ends a\nsession that was never displayed.\n\nHoist the guard above the recording so such a session is dropped without\nemitting anything, and discard its queued events with it.\n\nThe guard keys on visibility_event_rcvd_ts rather than perf.is_preloaded.\nis_preloaded is sampled once at NEW_TAB_INIT, which for a preloaded browser\nfires while it is still hidden, and getPreloadedBrowser() removes the\nattribute without the page reloading. A newtab the user does see therefore\nalso carries is_preloaded: true, so gating on it would suppress most real\nsessions.\n\ntest_endSession_no_ping_on_no_visibility_event described this behaviour\nalready but only asserted over legacy telemetry events, so it passed\nthroughout. It now covers the newtab ping too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316406\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/TelemetryFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_TelemetryFeed.js"], "git_node": "dbd4434676e0463851d3a8dd53f73189dc175cb6", "git_parents": ["900102cd3173afc593983ce7efc532acec1da75e"], "node": "01a761b400cfddd18e9f8209bf667d1ab7da05b9", "parents": ["f26fbdcd3f60dda86060058b5b15b806e93acaf9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morgan Rae Reschenberg \u003cmreschenberg@berkeley.edu\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061113: Announce description changes on macOS with AXAnnouncementRequested r=Jamie\n\nThere isn't a specific mac notification for description changes, like\nthere is for name (title) changes. To get around this, we use\nAXAnnouncementRequested with the description string. If Apple introduces\na specific event, we should update this code to use that instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316905\n", "files": ["accessible/mac/Platform.mm", "accessible/mac/mozAccessible.mm", "accessible/tests/browser/mac/browser_description.js"], "git_node": "d4366520117268f43b8cc23353b460bf899b956c", "git_parents": ["dbd4434676e0463851d3a8dd53f73189dc175cb6"], "node": "687c1c2cd3c8341216d8798a34e2935851463e0a", "parents": ["01a761b400cfddd18e9f8209bf667d1ab7da05b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059160 - [nova] Use more native colors in the native theme. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,mstriemer,dao\n\nRemove the toolbox gradient (so that the native titlebar colors appear),\nand the tab border gradient as per slack discussion.\n\nThe color: var(--toolbar-text-color) fix is drive-by but we shouldn't be\noverriding backgrounds without also overriding colors.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315278\n", "files": ["browser/themes/linux/browser.css", "browser/themes/shared/browser-shared.css", "browser/themes/shared/tabbrowser/tabs.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/semantic-categories.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-table.mjs", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbar.nova.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbar.tokens.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbox.tokens.json"], "git_node": "ceb48f2831af1dda7cdb55e6b102cd8939655422", "git_parents": ["d4366520117268f43b8cc23353b460bf899b956c"], "node": "71d1e12c7f251794ddac2fad18a41ec4c7d9badd", "parents": ["687c1c2cd3c8341216d8798a34e2935851463e0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060864 - Remove unnecessary re-exports from profiler rust API. r=canova,profiler-reviewers\n\nRust nightly warns about the glob re-export because it's unused. The\nmarkers module already exports these.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316535\n", "files": ["tools/profiler/rust-api/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "181659b8e075bada911dfd831f77624b44d0ec43", "git_parents": ["ceb48f2831af1dda7cdb55e6b102cd8939655422"], "node": "fdd25687cde281d1361b0b75a7aca097618b19c0", "parents": ["71d1e12c7f251794ddac2fad18a41ec4c7d9badd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055554 - Part 1: Add stripping OriginAttributes comparators, r=vhilla\n\nAdd some extra comparators to OriginAttributes. These will be used in\nlater parts.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312532\n", "files": ["caps/OriginAttributes.h", "caps/tests/gtest/TestOriginAttributes.cpp", "dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp"], "git_node": "6b387a34455d871b869e29f84a5c5b03a3bc1c62", "git_parents": ["181659b8e075bada911dfd831f77624b44d0ec43"], "node": "d84c10cf9c92d2e3653a97469358ad7f13a32a79", "parents": ["fdd25687cde281d1361b0b75a7aca097618b19c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055554 - Part 2: Track loaded origins in content processes, r=necko-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,ai-platform-reviewers,vhilla,asuth,permissions-reviewers,valentin,timhuang\n\nAdd a number of changes to track which origins are loaded in each\ncontent process. This adds a new API to nsIDOMProcessParent\n(AboutToLoadOrigin), which will start tracking this information.\n\nIn order to allow this to be shared with BlobURL broadcast checking, a\nmulti-tier map is used, tracking OAs-\u003eoriginNoSuffix-\u003eloadedAsOrigin,\nwhich allows tracking both sites and origins in a single data structure.\n\nTo align with the way we've previously handled BlobURL broadcasting,\nthis does actually track null principals, though that's unlikely to be\nusable yet. Unfortunately this could lead to a number of \"useless\"\nentries in the table. Future improvements could help things here\nfurther.\n\nNotably, this also tracks whether or not the system principal has been\nloaded in the process, which is intended to allow us to further tighten\nsystem principal checks in content.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312533\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContext.cpp", "dom/interfaces/base/nsIRemoteTab.idl", "dom/ipc/BrowserHost.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentChild.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentChild.h", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/InProcessImpl.cpp", "dom/ipc/LoadedOriginSet.cpp", "dom/ipc/LoadedOriginSet.h", "dom/ipc/PContent.ipdl", "dom/ipc/WindowGlobalParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/moz.build", "dom/ipc/nsIDOMProcessParent.idl", "dom/serviceworkers/ServiceWorkerManager.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerChild.cpp", "dom/workers/remoteworkers/RemoteWorkerManager.cpp", "extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.cpp", "extensions/permissions/PermissionManager.h", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "toolkit/components/ml/content/EngineProcess.sys.mjs", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.xpcom.d.ts"], "git_node": "ef4f6e06d6308266dff63d707808e13eb769b621", "git_parents": ["6b387a34455d871b869e29f84a5c5b03a3bc1c62"], "node": "109be24e269341dbb956452e3d897cacc01e2791", "parents": ["d84c10cf9c92d2e3653a97469358ad7f13a32a79"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055554 - Part 3: Check loaded sites in ValidatePrincipal, r=necko-reviewers,dom-storage-reviewers,dom-worker-reviewers,vhilla,jesup,asuth\n\nUse the loaded origin tracking from the pervious part in\nValidatePrincipal, and update call-sites to specify flags which modify\nthe behaviour here.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312534\n", "files": ["docshell/base/BrowsingContextGroup.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShell.cpp", "docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp", "dom/cache/PrincipalVerifier.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientHandleParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientManagerOpParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientSource.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientSourceParent.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.cpp", "dom/clients/manager/ClientValidation.h", "dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreParent.cpp", "dom/fetch/FetchParent.cpp", "dom/fs/child/FileSystemBackgroundRequestHandler.cpp", "dom/indexedDB/IndexedDBCommon.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserHost.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ContentParent.h", "dom/ipc/LoadedOrigi