ifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315704\n", "files": ["ipc/glue/Endpoint.cpp"], "git_node": "11f32453bad1e9d166b4d388509522fc12e36998", "git_parents": ["e4b02b1ea8da52120c51fc5dc993bf9aa9068040"], "node": "5b113e029a05cdbacbad535ea4081459743f9e25", "parents": ["18b7a0374c3da3ada243bc87281bab09f780bc6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061321: Handle argument underflow in PBL stack check r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nI'm not including a testcase because this only fails in an ASAN build of PBL, and we don't run those anywhere.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316960\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/PortableBaselineInterpret.cpp"], "git_node": "e83443ea1399eae74401dbfe8d427e439eb77df3", "git_parents": ["11f32453bad1e9d166b4d388509522fc12e36998"], "node": "63b9ed9930269faea7f5f93939afca8b093aaa0d", "parents": ["5b113e029a05cdbacbad535ea4081459743f9e25"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050954 - (Part 1) Add message scheduling logic to the Privacy New Tab widget r=Dre\n\nReplaces the Privacy widget's hardwired tip with logic that picks which secondary message (or a blank) to show on each new tab, and reworks the count readout so it shows the real number.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309610\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/Actions.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/Reducers.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/Privacy.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy/_Privacy.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/css/activity-stream.css", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyMessages.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/Privacy.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsRegistry.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/Widgets/PrivacyMessages.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_PrivacyFeed.js"], "git_node": "64ae29810ebee5eecbb7a5910f008e0b62f579af", "git_parents": ["e83443ea1399eae74401dbfe8d427e439eb77df3"], "node": "7f48351f9533a00f5d7fcc1cc407cf1736c0a71b", "parents": ["63b9ed9930269faea7f5f93939afca8b093aaa0d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050954 - (Part 2) Gate Privacy widget VPN promo messages behind a pref + trainhopConfig r=Dre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311203\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyMessages.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/Widgets/PrivacyMessages.test.js"], "git_node": "e842b22bb664a9efd5e0b9a534b7dfc61a48cd4a", "git_parents": ["64ae29810ebee5eecbb7a5910f008e0b62f579af"], "node": "8a6faed89569f11db9841c6a96ee5f9e786c9e22", "parents": ["7f48351f9533a00f5d7fcc1cc407cf1736c0a71b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050954 - (Part 3) Add forceMessageId debug pref for the Privacy widget r=reemhamz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313241\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/common/WidgetsRegistry.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/data/content/activity-stream.bundle.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/Widgets/PrivacyMessages.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/lib/Widgets/PrivacyMessages.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_PrivacyFeed.js"], "git_node": "5147a02cd60c65e74faa6c3691a44a95c30860a2", "git_parents": ["e842b22bb664a9efd5e0b9a534b7dfc61a48cd4a"], "node": "7ef001eee9acc6eb99468e62daeff1a5fc80e531", "parents": ["8a6faed89569f11db9841c6a96ee5f9e786c9e22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sam Foster \u003csfoster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050160 - Re-enable browser_backOrSidebarButtonFitts.js under nova. r=jsudiaman\n\n- bug 2054183 snugs up the button in maximized windows with nova.\n- but also, maximize is not always sync. Wait for the sizemode to change\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316975\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/general/browser.toml", "browser/base/content/test/general/browser_backOrSidebarButtonFitts.js"], "git_node": "5dd170a61c5de2be5f1b48b9873622d7cac7631d", "git_parents": ["5147a02cd60c65e74faa6c3691a44a95c30860a2"], "node": "782f638a72f4b236c74b16c81540552c8898a6a6", "parents": ["7ef001eee9acc6eb99468e62daeff1a5fc80e531"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061325. r=gfx-reviewers,nical\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316984\n", "files": ["gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHost.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostSWGL.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostSWGL.h", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.cpp", "gfx/webrender_bindings/RenderTextureHostWrapper.h"], "git_node": "cf0ce8b72df211808e73398bcdce036845a35bbb", "git_parents": ["5dd170a61c5de2be5f1b48b9873622d7cac7631d"], "node": "3a078f20d8e37f9dbb7553447d2dbd2462f35a37", "parents": ["782f638a72f4b236c74b16c81540552c8898a6a6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bryan Johns \u003cbjohns@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047564 - moved sanitizeUntrustedData from SearchBrowsingHistory to Tools r=ai-security-reviewers,omarg,tetchart\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316950\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/SearchBrowsingHistory.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/Tools.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_SearchBrowsingHistory.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_security_search_browsing_history.js"], "git_node": "6c7d9160bc9e16f196ca9772f903254d9e62b846", "git_parents": ["cf0ce8b72df211808e73398bcdce036845a35bbb"], "node": "a194da796dd119e4ce5bc5a1590850f823625408", "parents": ["3a078f20d8e37f9dbb7553447d2dbd2462f35a37"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1961577 - Keep tabs in place when collapsing a dragged tab group. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nCollapsing a dragged tab group shrinks the tab strip's scrolled content. While\nthe strip is scrolled away from its start, that clamps the scroll position, and\nif the collapse frees up enough space the strip also stops overflowing and drops\nits scroll buttons, so the tabs that are meant to stay put slide along the strip\ninstead. Locking the tab sizes for the drag doesn't help, since none of this is\nabout how wide the tabs are.\n\nThe space of the dragged item, which the drag takes out of the layout, was\nalready being reserved at the end of the strip. This extends that reservation to\nthe tabs of a collapsing group and keeps it until they have animated back to\ntheir full size after the drop. Reserving the dragged item's margin box instead\nof its border box takes care of the same problem in the small, which is visible\nwhen dragging an already collapsed group label.\n\nWorth checking that the reservation is released on every way out of a drag,\nincluding a drop in another window: _resetTabsAfterDrop leaves it alone when a\ngroup is about to expand again, and _expandGroupOnDrop takes over from there.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315576\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/drag-and-drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser.toml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_tab_group_overflow.js"], "git_node": "0241ffc863f0802913b245ab37efc47b1001742b", "git_parents": ["6c7d9160bc9e16f196ca9772f903254d9e62b846"], "node": "6b13458c046aa3f1f000d3406a78a3657ee9850e", "parents": ["a194da796dd119e4ce5bc5a1590850f823625408"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059312 - Part 2: Add MathMLAnchorElement class and WebIDL bindings r=emilio,webidl,firefox-svg-reviewers\" for causing build bustages @ nsINode.h\n\nThis reverts commit 196a701b28e5ea4c2cfbf6f3f1e688f3464c5f98.\n", "files": ["dom/base/Link.cpp", "dom/base/Link.h", "dom/bindings/Bindings.conf", "dom/html/HTMLAnchorElement.cpp", "dom/mathml/MathMLAnchorElement.cpp", "dom/mathml/MathMLAnchorElement.h", "dom/mathml/MathMLElement.cpp", "dom/mathml/MathMLElement.h", "dom/mathml/MathMLElementFactory.cpp", "dom/mathml/moz.build", "dom/svg/SVGAElement.cpp", "dom/tests/mochitest/general/test_interfaces.js", "dom/webidl/MathMLAnchorElement.webidl", "dom/webidl/moz.build", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-hreflang-getter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-hreflang-setter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-type-getter-001.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-type-getter-002.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/a-type-setter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/anchor-hyperlinkutils-getter-setter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/anchor-hyperlinkutils-getter.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/mathml/relations/html5-tree/href-navigation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/mathml/relations/html5-tree/href-target-base.html"], "git_node": "ff286ea0608c030dfb9eb1a274f9f0c3576c7e06", "git_parents": ["0241ffc863f0802913b245ab37efc47b1001742b"], "node": "94012f6dc60a297b902e9ef4bd8e2b1d7ae0d36d", "parents": ["6b13458c046aa3f1f000d3406a78a3657ee9850e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2060905 - Migrate installPWAFromTheMainMenuTest UI test to the efficiency framework r=jajohnson\" for causing fenix debug failures\n\nThis reverts commit 51b1d413c5f07847c243a51cb10ae93362adfb8c.\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/PwaTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/BaseTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/OverlayRegistry.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/navigation/LaunchConfig.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/MainMenuSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/PWASelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/PWATest.kt"], "git_node": "9704fd76330a579997a3cae4dabc2016f7b753c9", "git_parents": ["ff286ea0608c030dfb9eb1a274f9f0c3576c7e06"], "node": "352e68f5a8284dc0fea8ee43facd035bf8c2af62", "parents": ["94012f6dc60a297b902e9ef4bd8e2b1d7ae0d36d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "az \u003cazebrowski@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058048 - r=padenot\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314974\n", "files": ["media/ffvpx/README_MOZILLA", "media/ffvpx/cbs_decoder_sync.patch", "media/ffvpx/libavcodec/cbs_av1_syntax_template.c"], "git_node": "9c1d76e866e17b6cd6989eb8ec36f85eed925182", "git_parents": ["9704fd76330a579997a3cae4dabc2016f7b753c9"], "node": "d90d09622889f2771b1536ce1c68d182198e2139", "parents": ["352e68f5a8284dc0fea8ee43facd035bf8c2af62"], "tags": []}, {"author": "unifolia \u003cjlewis@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060959 - SW ATG: Suggested group's hover state lingers when moving to another Organize Tabs menu item r=flozia\n\nAuto Tab Grouping / 'Organize Tabs'\n\nSpec: https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1eEDfKdPECzFYQm5_gkIz8lG_t32VPrCQwO-ZMvJpUpM/edit?gid=0#gid=0\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316614\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-group-tabs/smartwindow-group-tabs.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AutoTabGrouping.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_group_tabs_button.js"], "git_node": "dd973208f1c5c40f277f68afd05010d623c884ae", "git_parents": ["9c1d76e866e17b6cd6989eb8ec36f85eed925182"], "node": "c40831b012ccbebb1e52807af782cbf581d35dd2", "parents": ["d90d09622889f2771b1536ce1c68d182198e2139"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Seva Alipov \u003csalipov@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1998331: Making button element selectable by default r=dholbert,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,devtools-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin,nchevobbe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D300613\n", "files": ["accessible/tests/browser/mac/browser_text_selection.js", "devtools/client/themes/webconsole.css", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_accessibility_node.js", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_accessibility_node_events.js", "layout/base/tests/test_caret_browsing_around_form_controls.html", "layout/style/res/forms.css", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-ui/tentative/button-user-select.html"], "git_node": "9f7519efb8a796c876842b64f622387f9a229d8a", "git_parents": ["dd973208f1c5c40f277f68afd05010d623c884ae"], "node": "c8c5e51b944ff81e4d0fc86d1a381be2dd61ad69", "parents": ["c40831b012ccbebb1e52807af782cbf581d35dd2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nika Layzell \u003cnika@thelayzells.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056360 - Part 3: Add test for new P-prefix error, r=ipc-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317149\n", "files": ["ipc/ipdl/test/ipdl/error/NoPPrefix.ipdl"], "git_node": "97bcad98810897fc61762e065590854044eb9537", "git_parents": ["9f7519efb8a796c876842b64f622387f9a229d8a"], "node": "baa35e54388cc6bdd0b794d40d87abe385394b14", "parents": ["c8c5e51b944ff81e4d0fc86d1a381be2dd61ad69"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Katherine Ye \u003ckye@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2043000 - Support block-ellipsis values for line-clamp markers. r=dshin,layout-reviewers\n\nAdded wpt for  non-empty custom ellipsis.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314664\n", "files": ["layout/generic/TextOverflow.cpp", "layout/generic/TextOverflow.h", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.cpp", "layout/generic/nsBlockFrame.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-023.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-024.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-034.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/block-ellipsis-038.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-overflow/line-clamp/reference/block-ellipsis-038-ref.html"], "git_node": "ddfdc8ab4d56b6cf449908e6748536c11c86cda3", "git_parents": ["97bcad98810897fc61762e065590854044eb9537"], "node": "60d6dd5b849bc3fff1bb20db59bfca4eb3db47a9", "parents": ["baa35e54388cc6bdd0b794d40d87abe385394b14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hansheng Zhao \u003chzhao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057317 - Provide the New Tab context id to the Mozilla Ads Client r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315026\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsClient.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsClient.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsFeed.js"], "git_node": "d5f7230f41243e128bf5284e6ecfcc1bbcf59382", "git_parents": ["ddfdc8ab4d56b6cf449908e6748536c11c86cda3"], "node": "07836de09a14856ffe0171b13688dcc6af40e51f", "parents": ["60d6dd5b849bc3fff1bb20db59bfca4eb3db47a9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-central repo-update HSTS HPKP - r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317163\n", "files": ["security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc"], "git_node": "16f9d83b2ed609899cff6384a6b73c16f1ab8583", "git_parents": ["d5f7230f41243e128bf5284e6ecfcc1bbcf59382"], "node": "d8c7cdeb0a996531201505f165f6b6b2e2c6cbaf", "parents": ["07836de09a14856ffe0171b13688dcc6af40e51f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ruhollah Majdoddin \u003cr.majdodin@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1856645 - Filter cookie change notifications by the host's originAttributes in the storage actor. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nThe cookies storage actor is a parent-process resource: one instance\nper toolbox, and every instance observes both \"cookie-changed\" and\n\"private-cookie-changed\". getMatchingHosts() decided whether a changed\ncookie belongs to this toolbox by host string alone, so every cookie\nchange was forwarded to every same-host panel regardless of cookie\njar: a cookie set in a normal window shows up in a private window's\nStorage panel and vice versa, and the same happens across containers\n(comment 2). The panel then lists rows its own jar does not contain;\nthe enumeration path is already scoped by the host's originAttributes,\nwhich is why such rows vanish on reopen and cannot be deleted.\n\nFactor the per-host originAttributes collection out of\ngetCookiesFromHost() into getOriginAttributesListFromHost(), and only\nforward a cookie change to a host if the cookie's originAttributes\nmatch one entry of that list - the jars the host's cookie listing\nqueries - comparing complete originAttributes with\nChromeUtils.originAttributesToSuffix. Matching against the whole list\nrather than a single window's originAttributes keeps hosts that are\nbacked by several jars at once correct, eg in the Browser Toolbox,\nwhere one host entry can aggregate normal, private and container\ncontexts. Comparing complete originAttributes also covers\npartitionKey: a partitioned cookie only matches a host whose listing\nqueries its partition's jar (derived from cookieJarSettings), fixing\nbug 2060029 on the same path. undefined entries, returned for\nprivileged hosts that relate to no window, are filtered out - their\nsuffix would be the default jar's. While here, use\noriginAttributesToSuffix instead of JSON.stringify for the uniqueness\nkey in getOriginAttributesListFromHost().\n\nTwo new tests. browser_storage_cookies_jar_isolation.js opens Storage\npanels on the same host in a normal window, a private window and a\ncontainer tab, and asserts that cookie adds and changes appear only in\nthe panel whose jar they belong to, in both directions, while same-jar\nupdates keep working. browser_storage_cookies_all_jars.js drives an\neverything-scope session, where all three contexts back one host row,\nand asserts that changes in every jar backing the host reach the\nsession, while a change in a jar no live context uses is not\nforwarded.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315860\n", "files": ["devtools/client/storage/test/browser.toml", "devtools/client/storage/test/browser_storage_cookies_jar_isolation.js", "devtools/server/actors/resources/storage/cookies.js", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser.toml", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_storage_cookies_all_jars.js"], "git_node": "64d89494022903f97ae8db8dad423e4c5aac4dd3", "git_parents": ["16f9d83b2ed609899cff6384a6b73c16f1ab8583"], "node": "b3c15bc9a2a8ee0a9079a4f1f020de8d076b88b8", "parents": ["d8c7cdeb0a996531201505f165f6b6b2e2c6cbaf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ruhollah Majdoddin \u003cr.majdodin@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060029 - Test that cookie change notifications are filtered by partition key in the storage actor. r=devtools-reviewers,jdescottes\n\nThe fix is in the previous patch (bug 1856645): getMatchingHosts()\ncompares the changed cookie's complete originAttributes, partitionKey\nincluded, against every jar the host's cookie listing queries, so a\ncookie partitioned under one site no longer reaches the panel of\nanother site embedding the same third party.\n\nThe test opens Storage panels on two sites embedding the same\nthird-party iframe and asserts that a partitioned cookie set from one\nsite's iframe appears only in that site's panel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315861\n", "files": ["devtools/client/storage/test/browser_storage_cookies_jar_isolation.js"], "git_node": "5554bf9c6fb0a579914d40869926f42989727e2c", "git_parents": ["64d89494022903f97ae8db8dad423e4c5aac4dd3"], "node": "9e6b55f6a8df39268471f1c8b4cd2d676825da84", "parents": ["b3c15bc9a2a8ee0a9079a4f1f020de8d076b88b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ruhollah Majdoddin \u003cr.majdodin@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061166 - Key cookie rows by the cookie's complete originAttributes in the storage actor. r=jdescottes,devtools-reviewers\n\nThe cookies storage actor keys a cookie row by name, host, path and\npartitionKey (#getCookieUniqueKey), leaving privateBrowsingId and\nuserContextId out of the key. A toolbox scoped to a single tab never\nmixes those jars in one listing, but in an everything-scope session\n(the Browser Toolbox) one host entry aggregates every jar backing the\nhost, and two same-named cookies at the same host and path in\ndifferent jars collapse into a single row. The listing shows one of\nthe two cookies, and which one is unstable: a cookie change keeps the\nlast-changed cookie while re-listing the host keeps the last jar in\nenumeration order. The edit and delete paths resolve the row back to\nnsICookies with the same jar-blind fields: deleting the row removes\nthe cookie from every jar backing the host, and editing the row\nmodifies the first match, which can be a different jar than the one\nwhose value the row displays.\n\nBuild the key's last slot from\nChromeUtils.originAttributesToSuffix(cookie.originAttributes) instead\nof the bare partitionKey, so the key carries the cookie's complete\njar, and compare the same suffix in editCookie() and _removeCookies()\nwhen resolving a row back to a cookie, so edit and delete act on\nexactly the cookie the row shows. A default-jar cookie's suffix is\nthe empty string, so keys of ordinary cookies are unchanged. The key\nstays opaque to the client: nothing outside the actor parses it, and\nthe Storage panel's Partition Key column reads its own field.\n\nbrowser_storage_cookies_all_jars.js grows a same-name scenario: a\ncookie with the same name in the normal, private and container jars\nmust surface as three distinct rows, deleting one row must remove\nonly its jar's cookie, and editing one row must modify only its\njar's cookie. The getCookieId test helpers now take the cookie's\noriginAttributes and derive the suffix, and the tests addressing\nrows in non-default jars pass theirs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316768\n", "files": ["devtools/client/storage/test/browser_storage_basic_usercontextid_2.js", "devtools/client/storage/test/browser_storage_cookies_jar_isolation.js", "devtools/client/storage/test/browser_storage_cookies_partitioned.js", "devtools/client/storage/test/browser_storage_delete_usercontextid.js", "devtools/client/storage/test/head.js", "devtools/server/actors/resources/storage/cookies.js", "devtools/server/tests/browser/browser_storage_cookies_all_jars.js", "devtools/server/tests/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "b5810926a91835854e221abb95eb2ff9e1f1696f", "git_parents": ["5554bf9c6fb0a579914d40869926f42989727e2c"], "node": "1e4694bccd68cd2cf2e8d39d164f3582c7163eb7", "parents": ["9e6b55f6a8df39268471f1c8b4cd2d676825da84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ruhollah Majdoddin \u003cr.majdodin@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061348 - Remove the unused removeCookie and removeAllCookies methods from the cookies storage actor. r=jdescottes,devtools-reviewers\n\nSince bug 1267910 these two methods implemented the jar-scoped cookie\nremoval behind the removeItem and removeAll requests: their\noriginAttributes argument selected the jar that _removeCookies\nenumerated. Bug 1907570 rewired removeItem, removeAll and\nremoveAllSessionCookies to call _removeCookies directly and replaced\nthe jar-scoped enumeration with all-jars enumeration filtered by the\nrow's uniqueKey, leaving removeCookie and removeAllCookies without\ncallers. They are not part of the storage protocol spec, so they are\nnot reachable from a client either, and _removeCookies no longer reads\nthe originAttributes they pass: if called, they would remove matching\ncookies from every jar backing the host, contrary to what their\nsignature suggests. Remove them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316858\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/resources/storage/cookies.js"], "git_node": "94d996443b68d1037d2ff549d5b057a82c1d3ae9", "git_parents": ["b5810926a91835854e221abb95eb2ff9e1f1696f"], "node": "f85e54a6a779866d5e1f419742c81f50cb746fcc", "parents": ["1e4694bccd68cd2cf2e8d39d164f3582c7163eb7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2050900 - Migrate common/Reducers.test.js to Jest.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315097\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/karma.mc.config.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/common/Reducers.test.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/common/Reducers.test.js"], "git_node": "00385adb648c5f19af86e286a0b45b24145ec948", "git_parents": ["94d996443b68d1037d2ff549d5b057a82c1d3ae9"], "node": "3c9bc354b6dbf79d43d4a3b491991c55c94b8dc2", "parents": ["f85e54a6a779866d5e1f419742c81f50cb746fcc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018702 - Migrate simple Redux unit tests to Jest/RTL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315081\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/karma.mc.config.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/ActivationWindowMessage.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Card.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/CollapsibleSection.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/ConfirmDialog.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/ContextMenu/ContextMenu.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/LinkMenu.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/MessageWrapper.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Search.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Weather/Weather.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/ActivationWindowMessage.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/Card.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/CollapsibleSection.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/ConfirmDialog.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/ContextMenu.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/LinkMenu.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/MessageWrapper.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/Search.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/Weather.test.jsx"], "git_node": "ac4fbfb7d76447d5134ba1084e8a903356f389bb", "git_parents": ["00385adb648c5f19af86e286a0b45b24145ec948"], "node": "2c8e234be896abcb23064767717493f21fb4e232", "parents": ["3c9bc354b6dbf79d43d4a3b491991c55c94b8dc2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018705 - Migrate Sections unit test to Jest/RTL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315071\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/karma.mc.config.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Sections.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/Sections.test.jsx"], "git_node": "6ad0a49d2425b9cabd1b28eb48ff9a00104aa28c", "git_parents": ["ac4fbfb7d76447d5134ba1084e8a903356f389bb"], "node": "b7dda7c677c235e0289dbad0143ec0d69598ae43", "parents": ["2c8e234be896abcb23064767717493f21fb4e232"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Reem H \u003c42309026+reemhamz@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018709 - Migrate Base unit test to Jest/RTL.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315083\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/unit/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx"], "git_node": "298e5f224cff072c5df7a665f3a6583082a206db", "git_parents": ["6ad0a49d2425b9cabd1b28eb48ff9a00104aa28c"], "node": "6cee3adbd43cb48b920e25f652189acee92e7a63", "parents": ["b7dda7c677c235e0289dbad0143ec0d69598ae43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054093 - Add /monitor command palette in smartbar r=flozia,urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312316\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/assets/agent-watch.svg", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/ai-chat-content/ai-chat-content.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/jar.mn", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/AgentUI.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agent_monitor_chat.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agentui_command.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_smartbar_command_palette.js", "browser/components/multilineeditor/jar.mn", "browser/components/multilineeditor/plugins/CommandsPlugin.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInputUtils.mjs", "tools/@types/generated/tspaths.json"], "git_node": "6c0c1713accafbf11886fe5562f9154ebeee9ab1", "git_parents": ["298e5f224cff072c5df7a665f3a6583082a206db"], "node": "d93ab30f75868c8003488ba115af9beb78475732", "parents": ["6cee3adbd43cb48b920e25f652189acee92e7a63"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yubin Jamora \u003cyjamora@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059538 - Polish command palette ui r=flozia,mlucks\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315415\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.css", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/components/smartwindow-panel-list/smartwindow-panel-list.stories.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/browser_aiwindow_agentui_command.js"], "git_node": "0b7acd088236d73fa17e1df94118f0a568766b02", "git_parents": ["6c0c1713accafbf11886fe5562f9154ebeee9ab1"], "node": "2b70856e1d880462221a8b9472eb2b21ee8a237f", "parents": ["d93ab30f75868c8003488ba115af9beb78475732"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061844 - Let the apilint tasks participate in the build cache. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\n`Javadoc` is cacheable but Gradle does not extend that to subclasses, and `Exec` disables caching\nbecause it cannot know what an arbitrary command touches. Both of the plugin's task types therefore\nreported \"caching has not been enabled for the task\". Their inputs and outputs are declared, the\nscripts they run are covered by the task implementation classpath, and none of the outputs embed\nabsolute paths, so annotate them.\n\nDoing that exposed a missing output declaration. The doclet writes a source map next to the API file\nand the lint tasks read it, but only the API file was declared, so restoring the task from the cache\nproduced a directory without the map and the next task failed with \"input file does not exist\".\nDeclare the map as an output, deriving its path from the API file so that the task and the lint tasks\nthat read it cannot disagree. This also matters without the cache: deleting the map on its own\npreviously left the task up to date and the map ungenerated.\n\nThree of the lint tasks share one result file, with the later two appending to what the first writes.\nA cache hit on an appending task would restore a whole copy of that file rather than appending to the\ncurrent one, so it would replace what the first task had just written; opt those two out with\n`cacheIf { false }`. Up-to-date checking still works for them, since a sibling rewriting the shared\nfile marks them out of date and they re-run.\n\nKeep `rootDir` out of the cache key while here. It only serves to make the paths recorded in the map\nrelative, and the outputs hold no absolute paths, so including it would key entries to a checkout\nlocation and stop them being shared. Set the javadoc destination directly rather than declaring a\nsecond property for it and assigning it from the task action.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317141\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiCompatLintTask.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiLintPlugin.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/PythonExec.kt"], "git_node": "ee0beee6c2d4543a942751471dacf72d7702428f", "git_parents": ["0b7acd088236d73fa17e1df94118f0a568766b02"], "node": "a62df76126c2887c12be7701781654cbeea0f53a", "parents": ["2b70856e1d880462221a8b9472eb2b21ee8a237f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061844 - Run the apilint scripts with the interpreter mach passes. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\n`mach gradle` exports `GRADLE_MACH_PYTHON` pointing at the interpreter it is running under, but the\nplugin invoked a bare `python3` everywhere: in `PythonExec`'s convention, in the build scripts that run\nthe test suites, and in the suites themselves. A bare `python3` is not necessarily on PATH, which is\nwhat the variable exists to solve.\n\nTake it from `providers.environmentVariable` so the value is tracked, falling back to `python3` when\nthe build is not driven by mach, and use `sys.executable` in the Python test drivers rather than\nre-resolving an interpreter for their subprocesses.\n\nSince the value is now an absolute path that differs per checkout, keep it out of the cache key so\nthat entries stay shareable, the same way the API generation task treats the source root.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317142\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apidoc-plugin/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apidoc-plugin/src/test/resources/apidoc_test.py", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/PythonExec.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/test/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/PythonExecTest.kt", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/test/resources/apilint_test.py", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/test/resources/changelog-check_test.py", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/test/resources/diff_test.py"], "git_node": "ed889b3f7a2e2a2e826b0f236d14905c24aa679b", "git_parents": ["ee0beee6c2d4543a942751471dacf72d7702428f"], "node": "a2ea2883f3348a6707bdb3d345ee80a5bcc6253a", "parents": ["a62df76126c2887c12be7701781654cbeea0f53a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061844 - Take the apilint compile classpath from the variant. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nThe classpath was wired in `afterEvaluate` by looking up `compile\u003cVariant\u003eJavaWithJavac`, because AGP\nregisters that task after the `onVariants` callbacks run. That name is an AGP implementation detail\nrather than part of the variant API, so a rename would break configuration silently, and it needed a\nmap to carry task providers out of `onVariants` and a second derivation of the capitalised variant\nname.\n\n`Variant` exposes `compileClasspath` directly, so set it where the variant is already in scope. It\ncovers the dependencies but not the platform, so add the boot classpath from `sdkComponents`\nalongside it, otherwise javadoc cannot resolve `android.*`.\n\nGeckoView's generated `api.txt` and `api.txt.map` are unchanged, both when the task runs and when it\nis restored from the build cache.\n\nTaking the classpath from the variant also drops `apiGenerate`'s dependency on\n`compile\u003cVariant\u003eJavaWithJavac`, so generating the API no longer waits for GeckoView to compile:\njavadoc parses the sources and needs only the dependencies on the classpath. The generated\n`BuildConfig`, AIDL and `R` sources still reach it through `sources.java`. One consequence worth\nnoting is that `android-api-lint` no longer fails on a GeckoView compile error, which the build and\n`android-lint` cover instead.\n\nDrop the narration from the comment about where the API files are written, and import\n`PathSensitivity` rather than spelling it out at each use.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317143\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/src/main/kotlin/org/mozilla/apilint/ApiLintPlugin.kt"], "git_node": "2eb7973c7952217df013957a54dae4e751ec5dcb", "git_parents": ["ed889b3f7a2e2a2e826b0f236d14905c24aa679b"], "node": "5727b5d87074d6a08683883bde49d0392766baa2", "parents": ["a2ea2883f3348a6707bdb3d345ee80a5bcc6253a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061844 - Write the apilint plugin's build output to the object directory. r=geckoview-reviewers,ohall\n\nThe plugin build was the only one of the three in-tree Gradle plugin builds still writing `build/` into\nthe source tree; `plugins/conventions` and `android-components/plugins/dependencies` both redirect to\nthe object directory. Follow them, in each of the three projects, since Gradle configures them\nindependently.\n\nBesides keeping generated files out of the checkout, this stops `./mach lint` on the plugin directory\nreporting a license error for every file under `build/reports`, which is where Gradle's own\nconfiguration-cache and problems reports land.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317161\n", "files": ["mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apidoc-plugin/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/apilint/build.gradle.kts", "mobile/android/gradle/plugins/apilint/build.gradle.kts"], "git_node": "83aaf017f953b3b711fa79c0a5affb33192a060d", "git_parents": ["2eb7973c7952217df013957a54dae4e751ec5dcb"], "node": "d769d60b3c8578eea17dc0439f0624c52a39a383", "parents": ["5727b5d87074d6a08683883bde49d0392766baa2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Botond Ballo \u003cbotond@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060974 - Document common 'anchor points' in APZ code. r=hiro\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316635\n", "files": ["gfx/docs/AsyncPanZoom.md"], "git_node": "859d457dff86106a3c2fee1f6f0a5c115b7b25b6", "git_parents": ["83aaf017f953b3b711fa79c0a5affb33192a060d"], "node": "0273b2bf6771b6bcc59b065e098b437401368be2", "parents": ["d769d60b3c8578eea17dc0439f0624c52a39a383"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Drop the obsolete apilint doc and fix two dead GeckoView doc links. DONTBUILD\n\n`contributor/apilint.md` documented releasing apilint from the archived\n`mozilla-mobile/gradle-apilint` repository: tagging a branch, `publishToMavenLocal`,\n`apilint:publishPlugins`, asking Releng to publish an `apidoc` bundle, and bumping an\n`org.mozilla.apilint:apilint` classpath coordinate in a root `build.gradle` that no longer looks like\nthat. The plugin has been developed in-tree for some time and the publishing setup was removed\nentirely, so none of it applies. Nothing links to the page except the contributor index, whose entry\ndescribed it as GeckoView's API linter, which is not what it contained.\n\nWhat the index entry promised is already documented: `design/breaking-changes.md` covers what apilint\ntracks and how it enforces removal of deprecated APIs, and the contributor quick start covers running\nit and regenerating `api.txt`, the API hash and the changelog.\n\nTwo links in neighbouring pages return 404. One points at\n`.../geckoview/design/breaking-changes.rst`, which is served as `.html`, so use a relative link to the\nsource file the way the same sentence already does for the quick start. The other points at\n`substitute-local-geckoview.gradle` on `hg.mozilla.org`, which is gone regardless of the misspelling in\nthe link text, so point it at searchfox instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317165\n", "files": ["mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/apilint.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/geckoview-quick-start.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/index.md", "mobile/android/docs/geckoview/contributor/translations-toolkit-to-fenix.md"], "git_node": "b945638ea34a13aa31cc4431d4b766c7c088aa8f", "git_parents": ["859d457dff86106a3c2fee1f6f0a5c115b7b25b6"], "node": "2cdc4e7c026f0a0068823454ddf3fc257ba7b21d", "parents": ["0273b2bf6771b6bcc59b065e098b437401368be2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Giulia Cardieri \u003cgcardieri@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056202: allow customizableUI wrapper have a null node r=sfoster\n\n**Issue**: There's an intermittent CustomizableUI error after the smart window switcher button became a customizable widget.\n\n**Cause**: The switcher widget is registered when smartwindow.enabled is true, but it uses showInPrivateBrowsing: false, so its node is never built in a private window (buildWidgetNode returns null). The problem is that CustomizableUI still creates the wrapper around that null node, and the overflowed getter then calls getAttribute on it and throws. In my perspective, we should either allow the wrapper's node to be null, or not create the wrapper at all.\n\n**Solution**: Went with allowing a null node: added a guard to the overflowed getter in WidgetSingleWrapper so it returns false when there's no node, instead of throwing. This mirrors the existing null guard already present in the sibling [[ https://searchfox.org/firefox-main/source/browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs#7428 | XULWidgetSingleWrapper getter ]], keeping both consistent.\n\nI preferred this approach as it seemed simpler and replicates existing code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315744\n", "files": ["browser/components/customizableui/CustomizableUI.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "1628b1074b4428a5f75acc3760c23143d3405b90", "git_parents": ["b945638ea34a13aa31cc4431d4b766c7c088aa8f"], "node": "28d22a8c0bd61d356a6f7312f7e923b0130d93b8", "parents": ["2cdc4e7c026f0a0068823454ddf3fc257ba7b21d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Iain Ireland \u003ciireland@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058668: Fix getModuleEnvironmentValue for unlinked modules r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jonco\n\nI initially used `module-\u003estatus() \u003c ModuleStatus::Linked` based on the check in ModuleObject::environment(), but that didn't work: we have some tests that use getModuleEnvironmentValue on modules with ModuleStatus::New. If there are additional problems with this testing function in the future, we could consider marking it fuzzing-unsafe; it's doing things that are not otherwise possible in the spec.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316925\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/modules/bug2058668.js", "js/src/shell/js.cpp"], "git_node": "ac2c159f0267d5bdf23a4428d6ff1baaa11d064e", "git_parents": ["1628b1074b4428a5f75acc3760c23143d3405b90"], "node": "aa5d2a4ffca3b9d34c65480674d95addb17b7f27", "parents": ["28d22a8c0bd61d356a6f7312f7e923b0130d93b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Rishel \u003cnrishel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058751 - Add documentation for set default browser on Windows. r=hsohaney,aborondo,mviar,dmose\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314803\n", "files": ["browser/components/shell/docs/set-default.md", "browser/components/shell/moz.build", "widget/windows/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "b933a39915c8d0ce76e63081d6f77c0833740809", "git_parents": ["ac2c159f0267d5bdf23a4428d6ff1baaa11d064e"], "node": "cb0989f146c6af548b066edb4c8f044f3d40fdb5", "parents": ["aa5d2a4ffca3b9d34c65480674d95addb17b7f27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicholas Rishel \u003cnrishel@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058752 - Add documentation for pinning to the Taskbar on Windows. r=hsohaney,aborondo,dmose\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314804\n", "files": ["browser/components/shell/docs/pin-to-taskbar.md", "widget/windows/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "2d3fa36d0a94967a1b1cf0f9af2e170e4090d56e", "git_parents": ["b933a39915c8d0ce76e63081d6f77c0833740809"], "node": "2fd3af5ccab2f5252e4d4c4281d848d6501b7d61", "parents": ["cb0989f146c6af548b066edb4c8f044f3d40fdb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "David Shin \u003cdshin@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046602: Make view-timeline-inset part of the view-timeline shorthand. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio,boris\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316759\n", "files": ["layout/style/test/property_database.js", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/shorthands.toml", "servo/components/style/values/generics/animation.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/css/view-timeline-shorthand.html.ini"], "git_node": "fae2051de6557c43c9b58489c293867c21eda3ff", "git_parents": ["2d3fa36d0a94967a1b1cf0f9af2e170e4090d56e"], "node": "dbd1d79481eeab6c25b6f6c9d789c33f27cc8f76", "parents": ["2fd3af5ccab2f5252e4d4c4281d848d6501b7d61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060589 - Implement getPostScriptGlyphNames in SkFontHost_cairo. r=lsalzman\n\nMuch like SkTypeface_FreeType::getPostScriptGlyphNames. I added the\nerror checking to be a good citizen.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317180\n", "files": ["gfx/skia/skia/src/ports/SkFontHost_cairo.cpp"], "git_node": "ba297350f837cd962bb9473f1b58646365669952", "git_parents": ["fae2051de6557c43c9b58489c293867c21eda3ff"], "node": "70dafa51f84940bb43d058fac36b41ef874712bc", "parents": ["dbd1d79481eeab6c25b6f6c9d789c33f27cc8f76"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059632 - Enable sccache client side mode. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\" for causing Bug 2061715 & Bug 2061716\n\nThis reverts commit aed87c3e0841a58bb57f7dbeb38b0dae1c837c9b.\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "config/config.mk"], "git_node": "d312c6dd611b9a199bb3e9ef6f795ef12e76402b", "git_parents": ["ba297350f837cd962bb9473f1b58646365669952"], "node": "6eac5f802b07a15fba7b1fcddaf18d253b3ae180", "parents": ["70dafa51f84940bb43d058fac36b41ef874712bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2059632 - Move SCCACHE_MAX_FRAME_LENGTH out of mozconfig.cache. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,ahochheiden\" for causing bug 2061715 & Bug 2061716\n\nThis reverts commit 8ff29f8d3883f8b13efb95643afe6352d09f3696.\n", "files": ["build/moz.configure/toolchain.configure", "build/mozconfig.cache", "config/config.mk", "python/mozbuild/mozbuild/controller/building.py"], "git_node": "721a41397a124ddad6600bdcb96dcbe2676f9e23", "git_parents": ["d312c6dd611b9a199bb3e9ef6f795ef12e76402b"], "node": "5a6a30e5c678f2ad4ffb3d9bcde616b8e6ed54bd", "parents": ["6eac5f802b07a15fba7b1fcddaf18d253b3ae180"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2058752 - Add documentation for pinning to the Taskbar on Windows. r=hsohaney,aborondo,dmose\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit 2d3fa36d0a94967a1b1cf0f9af2e170e4090d56e.\n", "files": ["browser/components/shell/docs/pin-to-taskbar.md", "widget/windows/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "f776b457e237655ec0df5e3c73897253f5013a2f", "git_parents": ["721a41397a124ddad6600bdcb96dcbe2676f9e23"], "node": "4d5e95cefa51de2bc56a144f1c3302f0954f8b92", "parents": ["5a6a30e5c678f2ad4ffb3d9bcde616b8e6ed54bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2058751 - Add documentation for set default browser on Windows. r=hsohaney,aborondo,mviar,dmose\" for causing build bustages\n\nThis reverts commit b933a39915c8d0ce76e63081d6f77c0833740809.\n", "files": ["browser/components/shell/docs/set-default.md", "browser/components/shell/moz.build", "widget/windows/docs/index.md"], "git_node": "6a7d0c415696d0b8f1eb0fc854ab83e1f3f4539a", "git_parents": ["f776b457e237655ec0df5e3c73897253f5013a2f"], "node": "f944b18cacdbacf8f0ed4c40dd6e7cdb85919e2f", "parents": ["4d5e95cefa51de2bc56a144f1c3302f0954f8b92"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047733 - Add share button to tab groups r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314983\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupCardTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupListTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupsPageTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/TabGroupOnboardingItemTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/ExpandedTabGroup.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupCard.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/TabManagementFeatureHelper.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/TabsTrayTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/TabManagementFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/SharedTabItemUi.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/NormalTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/PrivateTabsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/TabGroupList.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/TabGroupsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/TabLayout.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabstray/TabsTray.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/ExpandedTabGroupTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/TabLayoutTest.kt"], "git_node": "43bce1148951bcd607abb9ad2f397e43299cfa1d", "git_parents": ["6a7d0c415696d0b8f1eb0fc854ab83e1f3f4539a"], "node": "90bc949de1cd44990b2088188954256a46c4486d", "parents": ["f944b18cacdbacf8f0ed4c40dd6e7cdb85919e2f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "calu \u003ccalu@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047731 - Customize tab group share sheet r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,parker,jdelorenzo\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314984\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/main/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/android/content/Context.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/android/content/ContextTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/metrics.yaml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/share/ShareSheetLauncher.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/ShareUseCases.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/share/ShareCloseView.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/share/ShareFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/ExpandedTabGroup.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/TabsTrayTestTag.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/TabManagerController.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/TabManagementFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/layout/share_close.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/navigation/nav_graph.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/ShareUseCasesTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/usecases/fake/FakeShareSheetLauncher.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/ExpandedTabGroupTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/controller/DefaultTabManagerControllerTest.kt"], "git_node": "e9223f20b62ae22ded38238a0190a8e3237d2a83", "git_parents": ["43bce1148951bcd607abb9ad2f397e43299cfa1d"], "node": "a9be6241d6fe859ce0d3a4f3274f0b6bd847d354", "parents": ["90bc949de1cd44990b2088188954256a46c4486d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Taimur Hasan \u003cthasan@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059814 - Point MLPA callers at the h2 endpoint r=ai-platform-reviewers,android-reviewers,mozperftest-reviewers,again,npodgurski,aglavic,matt-tighe\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316124\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/openAIEngine.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/search/SearchProviders.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_engine_build_object_form.js", "mobile/android/android-components/components/lib/llm-mlpa/src/main/java/mozilla/components/lib/llm/mlpa/service/MlpaService.kt", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/system/ml_services.py", "python/mozperftest/mozperftest/tests/test_ml_services.py", "toolkit/components/ml/eval/evals.py"], "git_node": "69ede3944a9f43f6d9c300ce9d5d172343e74a8e", "git_parents": ["e9223f20b62ae22ded38238a0190a8e3237d2a83"], "node": "a224275dbbbe4b954770faf1e16bdd23c776910a", "parents": ["a9be6241d6fe859ce0d3a4f3274f0b6bd847d354"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joe Bowser \u003cjbowser@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2046861 - Reject InferenceSession.create() on a native session-create failure instead of crashing r=ai-platform-reviewers,valentinp\n\nWhen onnxruntime's CreateSessionFromArray fails (an out-of-memory\ncondition, or a malformed/unsupported model), InferenceSession::Init\ncalled MOZ_CRASH, taking down the whole inference content process. That\nturns a recoverable runtime error into a crash and, because the process\ndies first, prevents JS callers from using the fallback they already\nhave (best-onnx retrying on the wasm backend in MLEngineChild).\n\nReject the promise with the onnxruntime error message instead, matching\nhow the missing-library case a few lines up is already handled.\n\nmach try (all green): https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&revision=96f338c920471bae16a3d3c2bff533aac0224cfa\n\nCo-authored-by: Erik Nordin \u003cenordin@mozilla.com\u003e\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313108\n", "files": ["dom/onnx/InferenceSession.cpp", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/browser_ml_inference_session_error.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser/ml_inference_session_error_stub.worker.mjs"], "git_node": "843fdf148845fd85a9a6dcc53aa2718c6a562aff", "git_parents": ["69ede3944a9f43f6d9c300ce9d5d172343e74a8e"], "node": "f260ddf60d55292823b6826416135757391c926c", "parents": ["a224275dbbbe4b954770faf1e16bdd23c776910a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047285 - Reset the start time if calling play() for a finite timeline and requiring the auto-rewind. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nPer the spec issue, [1] and the spec change [2], we tweak the step 7\nin play() [3] to achieve this:\n\nIf has finite timeline and auto-rewind is true:\n * Set the flag auto align start time to true.\n * Set the animation\u2019s hold time to previous current time.\n\nTo make sure we reset the stickiness of start time in the following\nsteps, for the finite timeline.\n\n[1] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/11469\n[2] https://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/pull/14146\n[3] https://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations-2/#playing-an-animation-section\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317151\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/play-animation.html.ini"], "git_node": "557e4e9762165dd599a348afac517ba5b7a62ac7", "git_parents": ["843fdf148845fd85a9a6dcc53aa2718c6a562aff"], "node": "81e837aaf09863b7d1629ba8bd55322dab2ba3d1", "parents": ["f260ddf60d55292823b6826416135757391c926c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Boris Chiou \u003cboris.chiou@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047285 - Apply the pending playback rate when auto-aligning the start time. r=layout-scroll-driven-animation-reviewers,layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nTo make sure the behavior is consistent with setting the start time.\nAlso, this is based on the spec change recently for the step 8 in [1],\nto address this spec issue:\nhttps://github.com/w3c/csswg-drafts/issues/14173.\n\n[1] https://drafts.csswg.org/web-animations-2/#auto-aligning-start-time\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317184\n", "files": ["dom/animation/Animation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/play-animation.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/scroll-animations/scroll-timelines/reverse-animation.html.ini"], "git_node": "4bca5a5c34d5ddd96d75398c9d6af474054a5e3f", "git_parents": ["557e4e9762165dd599a348afac517ba5b7a62ac7"], "node": "cfaf880d18cd5d91b45a912735a031deb886dcbb", "parents": ["81e837aaf09863b7d1629ba8bd55322dab2ba3d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059765 - Install `python3` explicitly when bootstrapping `openSUSE Leap` r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316724\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/bootstrap/kind.yml"], "git_node": "736dbd4d7d3009c79322cea68bf9eba37658b707", "git_parents": ["4bca5a5c34d5ddd96d75398c9d6af474054a5e3f"], "node": "a4f987db41c8a4fd19b5452c9a0959256d2a80a8", "parents": ["cfaf880d18cd5d91b45a912735a031deb886dcbb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jason Prickett \u003cjprickett@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058288 - Increase theme picker max width to prevent row breaks r=omc-reviewers,yazan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316094\n", "files": ["browser/components/aboutwelcome/content/aboutwelcome.css", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/styles/_multistage.scss", "browser/components/asrouter/content/components/asrouter-newtab-multistage/asrouter-newtab-multistage.css"], "git_node": "5a8a03a15fe410e2fda61d22cbf9c60b5a6c00b4", "git_parents": ["736dbd4d7d3009c79322cea68bf9eba37658b707"], "node": "4b8c63c9fad1188ae770572ca6970c67a4a2dbce", "parents": ["a4f987db41c8a4fd19b5452c9a0959256d2a80a8"], "tags": []}, {"