e11\npt-PT -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nrm -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nro -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nru -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nsk -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nsl -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nson -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nsq -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nsr -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nsv-SE -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nta -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nte -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nth -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\ntl -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\ntr -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\ntrs -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nuk -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nur -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nuz -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nvi -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nwo -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nxh -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nzam -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nzh-CN -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\nzh-TW -\u003e 0d74316f928b6476c854159d78bc3fb628b1ee11\n", "files": ["mobile/locales/l10n-changesets.json"], "git_node": "b1a2561e70d84db7b487ee8b2bd528969f093793", "git_parents": ["5024553fe311f454cd2561df13ff9114ce8dbd75"], "node": "02a9b5c64ed6812a5d77ddda9e9919cdb4f7d709", "parents": ["7f98be726af819ad2d0f9f15a8f45e604ea844aa"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060930 part 1 - Make MSetInitializedLength and MSetArrayLength take a length. r=iain\n\nBoth ops took an index (`length - 1`) instead of the new length. This was confusing and\nthey now take the new length instead.\n\nThe length was always a constant so the register case in `SetLengthFromIndex` was dead\ncode. The length is now stored in the MIR instruction instead of requiring a separate\n`MConstant`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316745\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "e57fa26408688a6f8b684d984e88ae91e3a3adbd", "git_parents": ["b1a2561e70d84db7b487ee8b2bd528969f093793"], "node": "e3baa8e730470c5987f3850cbf0b1588f8cc54bd", "parents": ["02a9b5c64ed6812a5d77ddda9e9919cdb4f7d709"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060930 part 2 - Add a needsPreBarrier flag to MSetInitializedLength. r=iain\n\nCurrent users only grow the length, so they all pass `false` for `needsPreBarrier`\nand the barrier loop is dead code for now. In DEBUG builds we assert this now.\n\nFor Ion-generators we want to set the initialized length of the stack-storage array\nto 0 after a resume, so there we'll need this barrier later.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316746\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp", "js/src/jit/Lowering.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIROps.yaml", "js/src/jit/MacroAssembler.h", "js/src/jit/ScalarReplacement.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "34a33e375932e816a4aa9c45753d30be827deee7", "git_parents": ["e57fa26408688a6f8b684d984e88ae91e3a3adbd"], "node": "822874a285f62454da1a8e8307a8b85c21db01d2", "parents": ["e3baa8e730470c5987f3850cbf0b1588f8cc54bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060930 part 3 - Trace a resuming generator's ResumeFrameArgs in TraceThisAndArguments. r=iain\n\nThis isn't strictly needed yet but will become more important when Ion can resume\ngenerator/async functions directly.\n\nAlso renames `ModuleResumeSlots` to `ModuleResumeArgs` for consistency with other code.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316747\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/BaselineCodeGen.cpp", "js/src/jit/BaselineFrame.h", "js/src/jit/InterpreterEntryTrampoline.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.h", "js/src/jit/VMFunctions.cpp", "js/src/vm/FrameIter.cpp"], "git_node": "3fbe662d8473d78c59353816ae7eb4faa83452d7", "git_parents": ["34a33e375932e816a4aa9c45753d30be827deee7"], "node": "2cde3157352e66a6c71ceecb8dfec495c12e08ca", "parents": ["822874a285f62454da1a8e8307a8b85c21db01d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060930 part 4 - Add a helper function to get the suspend pc preceding a JSOp::AfterYield. r=iain\n\nThis adds a helper function for the code used in `AbstractGeneratorObject::isAfterYieldOrAwait`\nso that we can also use it in WarpBuilder later.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316748\n", "files": ["js/src/vm/BytecodeLocation.h", "js/src/vm/BytecodeUtil.h", "js/src/vm/GeneratorObject.cpp"], "git_node": "fb522d88e220f717def669b04fc24a4facce2c41", "git_parents": ["3fbe662d8473d78c59353816ae7eb4faa83452d7"], "node": "d4cfdae617415d9876bc811db9006a9b7ce2566f", "parents": ["2cde3157352e66a6c71ceecb8dfec495c12e08ca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060930 part 5 - Only check for the hole value in the LoadElementV needsHoleCheck assertion. r=iain\n\nFor Ion-generators we will restore a generator's locals and expression stack\nwith `MLoadElement` ops that don't need a hole check, but those slots can\ncontain `JS_UNINITIALIZED_LEXICAL` magic values.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317121\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "7b13585e85e456d4ebd21dcfe6247bdd82571f49", "git_parents": ["fb522d88e220f717def669b04fc24a4facce2c41"], "node": "8f7de8327cfe672031bbec26cefad366c2092c43", "parents": ["d4cfdae617415d9876bc811db9006a9b7ce2566f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jan de Mooij \u003cjdemooij@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060930 part 6 - Ensure generators and async functions are not inlined. r=iain\n\nGenerators and async functions don't return directly, they jump to the epilogue\nthat ends with `JSOp::FinalYieldRval`. This means the `normallyReachableReturn`\ncheck in `BytecodeAnalysis` already prevented inlining. This just adds an explicit\ncheck instead of relying on the bytecode structure for this.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317127\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/TrialInlining.cpp", "js/src/jit/WarpBuilder.cpp"], "git_node": "1789517bd92a7d528df7b7ca059e4337bb08afb8", "git_parents": ["7b13585e85e456d4ebd21dcfe6247bdd82571f49"], "node": "f6ebb021b0f55996f33acd101721c58ec3dc1807", "parents": ["8f7de8327cfe672031bbec26cefad366c2092c43"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daisuke Akatsuka \u003cdaisuke@birchill.co.jp\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061568 - Remove redundant height declarations for the breakout urlbar r=desktop-theme-reviewers,adw,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316966\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/urlbar-searchbar.css"], "git_node": "91315ffa711316f39e433cd52012c2101ae94c00", "git_parents": ["1789517bd92a7d528df7b7ca059e4337bb08afb8"], "node": "b76e37734072393af33ebd671bd0a4b500cd1f10", "parents": ["f6ebb021b0f55996f33acd101721c58ec3dc1807"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / xpcom part r=xpcom-reviewers,mccr8\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311042\n", "files": ["xpcom/base/AvailableMemoryTracker.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSRuntime.cpp", "xpcom/base/CycleCollectedJSRuntime.h", "xpcom/base/nsISupportsImpl.h", "xpcom/base/nsMemoryReporterManager.cpp", "xpcom/build/PoisonIOInterposerBase.cpp", "xpcom/build/perfprobe.h", "xpcom/components/nsCategoryManager.h", "xpcom/ds/PLDHashTable.h", "xpcom/ds/nsPersistentProperties.cpp", "xpcom/ds/nsPersistentProperties.h", "xpcom/io/nsAnonymousTemporaryFile.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsDirectoryService.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsDirectoryService.h", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileWin.cpp", "xpcom/io/nsLocalFileWin.h", "xpcom/reflect/xptcall/xptcall.h", "xpcom/threads/InputTaskManager.h", "xpcom/threads/TaskController.h"], "git_node": "abe92e3c5b89fb7ec0674743a74ed5899e9bf1fc", "git_parents": ["91315ffa711316f39e433cd52012c2101ae94c00"], "node": "4476e783fa50851d251a10e8a67b1b1930fc9b61", "parents": ["b76e37734072393af33ebd671bd0a4b500cd1f10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / widget part r=win-reviewers,handyman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311043\n", "files": ["widget/nsClipboardProxy.cpp", "widget/nsClipboardProxy.h", "widget/nsIWidget.h", "widget/windows/DirectManipulationOwner.cpp", "widget/windows/IEnumFE.cpp", "widget/windows/IEnumFE.h", "widget/windows/IMMHandler.cpp", "widget/windows/IMMHandler.h", "widget/windows/JumpListBuilder.cpp", "widget/windows/JumpListBuilder.h", "widget/windows/KeyboardLayout.h", "widget/windows/LSPAnnotator.cpp", "widget/windows/RemoteBackbuffer.cpp", "widget/windows/ScreenHelperWin.h", "widget/windows/TSFInputScope.h", "widget/windows/TSFTextStore.cpp", "widget/windows/TSFTextStore.h", "widget/windows/TaskbarPreview.h", "widget/windows/WinCompositorWindowThread.h", "widget/windows/WinMouseScrollHandler.cpp", "widget/windows/WinTaskbar.cpp", "widget/windows/WinTaskbar.h", "widget/windows/WinTextEventDispatcherListener.cpp", "widget/windows/WinTextEventDispatcherListener.h", "widget/windows/WinUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/WinUtils.h", "widget/windows/WindowsTestDebug.cpp", "widget/windows/WindowsTestDebug.h", "widget/windows/WindowsUIUtils.cpp", "widget/windows/WindowsUIUtils.h", "widget/windows/nsBidiKeyboard.cpp", "widget/windows/nsBidiKeyboard.h", "widget/windows/nsClipboard.cpp", "widget/windows/nsClipboard.h", "widget/windows/nsColorPicker.cpp", "widget/windows/nsColorPicker.h", "widget/windows/nsDataObj.cpp", "widget/windows/nsDataObj.h", "widget/windows/nsDataObjCollection.cpp", "widget/windows/nsDataObjCollection.h", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.cpp", "widget/windows/nsPrintDialogWin.h", "widget/windows/nsPrintSettingsServiceWin.h", "widget/windows/nsSound.cpp", "widget/windows/nsSound.h", "widget/windows/nsUserIdleServiceWin.h"], "git_node": "7c5a815c926360e51e8a5160c783789789a4f15c", "git_parents": ["abe92e3c5b89fb7ec0674743a74ed5899e9bf1fc"], "node": "dc757fd371a43816f52467696bf815089932a3dd", "parents": ["4476e783fa50851d251a10e8a67b1b1930fc9b61"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / uriloader part r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311044\n", "files": ["uriloader/exthandler/win/nsLocalHandlerAppWin.h", "uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.cpp", "uriloader/exthandler/win/nsMIMEInfoWin.h"], "git_node": "d6b5a2d381ea5fe54574ec5c4cf0d1d460aabb13", "git_parents": ["7c5a815c926360e51e8a5160c783789789a4f15c"], "node": "923ffe6848c19abb176f74ee3e08e44450f7545d", "parents": ["dc757fd371a43816f52467696bf815089932a3dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / toolkit part r=niklas,emz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311045\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingRecord.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingRecord.h", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/nsUrlClassifierUtils.cpp", "toolkit/components/url-classifier/nsUrlClassifierUtils.h", "toolkit/mozapps/defaultagent/Cache.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/defaultagent/Cache.h", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatecommon.cpp", "toolkit/mozapps/update/common/updatecommon.h", "toolkit/profile/ProfileUnlockerWin.cpp", "toolkit/profile/ProfileUnlockerWin.h", "toolkit/system/windowsDHCPClient/WindowsNetworkFunctionsWrapper.h", "toolkit/system/windowsDHCPClient/nsWindowsDHCPClient.h", "toolkit/system/windowsPackageManager/nsWindowsPackageManager.h", "toolkit/system/windowsproxy/nsWindowsSystemProxySettings.cpp", "toolkit/system/windowsproxy/nsWindowsSystemProxySettings.h", "toolkit/xre/DllPrefetchExperimentRegistryInfo.h", "toolkit/xre/dllservices/UntrustedModulesData.h", "toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp", "toolkit/xre/nsNativeAppSupportWin.cpp"], "git_node": "040aea3c1cd8a17245736b455adb770757e2794c", "git_parents": ["d6b5a2d381ea5fe54574ec5c4cf0d1d460aabb13"], "node": "cf4dfe72b68b6a181ab8f8a9aaac70b606e7e5ac", "parents": ["923ffe6848c19abb176f74ee3e08e44450f7545d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1961577 - Keep the drop's synthesized mouseup from toggling the dragged tab group.\n\nbrowser_drag_tab_group_overflow.js fails with browser.nova.enabled=false, which\nis what the no-nova test variant runs. EventUtils ends a drop by synthesizing a\nmouseup two pixels into the drop target, and since the target here is the tab\ngroup's own label, the tab group takes that for a click and toggles itself. The\ntest then sees the opposite collapsed state from the one it is waiting for.\n\nWhether the mouseup lands on the label or on the container around it depends on\nhow the collapsed label is laid out, which is what differs by theme -- with Nova\nit misses the label and the test passed. Swallow the click instead of relying on\nthat.\n\nAutoland scheduled no-nova only for browser-chrome chunks that don't hold this\ntest, so the landing stuck; the failure shows up on a try push that schedules\nmore of them.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317247\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_drag_tab_group_overflow.js"], "git_node": "05c665ffd18b5b39602a4dd54ae795a81e8a6c8c", "git_parents": ["040aea3c1cd8a17245736b455adb770757e2794c"], "node": "bd2a827b4163d8e5b7b770bf0e0b0d515f74dcdc", "parents": ["cf4dfe72b68b6a181ab8f8a9aaac70b606e7e5ac"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / storage part r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311046\n", "files": ["storage/mozStorageService.cpp", "storage/mozStorageService.h"], "git_node": "fe82c504d90526c452fb23e9ba3245184fc99339", "git_parents": ["05c665ffd18b5b39602a4dd54ae795a81e8a6c8c"], "node": "9eb5fc65aab2cc1fbb9029def7e029200c7572d2", "parents": ["bd2a827b4163d8e5b7b770bf0e0b0d515f74dcdc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / security part r=keeler\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311047\n", "files": ["security/certverifier/OCSPCache.cpp", "security/certverifier/OCSPCache.h", "security/manager/ssl/CredentialManagerSecret.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/CredentialManagerSecret.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsClientAuthRemember.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCertificate.cpp", "security/manager/ssl/nsNSSCertificate.h"], "git_node": "5050d8aef05e40b6e99f33a428da47ef55002796", "git_parents": ["fe82c504d90526c452fb23e9ba3245184fc99339"], "node": "b776685066bc90aadf8d1e553a2dccae5aba36d0", "parents": ["9eb5fc65aab2cc1fbb9029def7e029200c7572d2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / parser part r=hsivonen\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311048\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOpStage.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOpStage.h"], "git_node": "7aac0605d3dbe29d2e0a06310d6028e7f8d363f8", "git_parents": ["5050d8aef05e40b6e99f33a428da47ef55002796"], "node": "675b67558a7411842a770b4a9dda24c245fb147f", "parents": ["b776685066bc90aadf8d1e553a2dccae5aba36d0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053404 - Cleanup default state for static-analysis on Windows / js part r=spidermonkey-reviewers,jandem\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311049\n", "files": ["js/public/ErrorReport.h", "js/src/builtin/TestingFunctions.cpp", "js/src/debugger/Debugger.h", "js/src/ds/LifoAlloc.h", "js/src/gc/AtomMarking.h", "js/src/gc/Scheduling.h", "js/src/irregexp/RegExpShim.h", "js/src/jit/JSJitFrameIter.h", "js/src/jit/JitFrames.cpp", "js/src/jit/Snapshots.cpp", "js/src/jit/Snapshots.h", "js/src/jsapi.cpp", "js/src/vm/Activation.h", "js/src/vm/Compartment.h", "js/src/vm/PropMap.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmGC.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmGenerator.h", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCMaps.cpp", "js/xpconnect/src/XPCMaps.h"], "git_node": "5d78016c3033bd6cfd4d0f155f1b5699d51a3ea3", "git_parents": ["7aac0605d3dbe29d2e0a06310d6028e7f8d363f8"], "node": "daafc1267dd2e110b9a64309e5458dcd18e47318", "parents": ["675b67558a7411842a770b4a9dda24c245fb147f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Updatebot \u003cupdatebot@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061923 - Update android nightly application-services version bump to 5f5a6acb146e782170f384bc0b69cf5e3109e62b r=release-managers,RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317243\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/ApplicationServices.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/plugins/dependencies/src/main/java/moz.yaml"], "git_node": "f5c3e85d800c1984aee61dd254178127042bf584", "git_parents": ["5d78016c3033bd6cfd4d0f155f1b5699d51a3ea3"], "node": "af3fa8b7dc2c81f1b45f5f493f4a48b7ebe49932", "parents": ["daafc1267dd2e110b9a64309e5458dcd18e47318"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Louis-Philippe \u003clpmanette@omnicesoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057813 - Crash during HLG video playback when compositor doesn't support HLG transfer function. r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317117\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/WaylandSurface.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWaylandDisplay.cpp", "widget/gtk/nsWaylandDisplay.h"], "git_node": "cc42ec504b961db89083bd156343d6d7a944b547", "git_parents": ["f5c3e85d800c1984aee61dd254178127042bf584"], "node": "995414e8f050bd14d78d6f8a24cb828d38219e3d", "parents": ["af3fa8b7dc2c81f1b45f5f493f4a48b7ebe49932"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ravjit Uppal \u003cravjit@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061028 [wpt PR 61767] - [CE] Add tentative WPTs for camera and microphone permission elements., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CE] Add tentative WPTs for camera and microphone permission elements.\n\nThis CL introduces tentative Web Platform Tests (WPTs) for the proposed\ncamera and microphone HTML elements. The tests verify successful\npermission requests and track generation upon user click, as well as\nerror handling scenarios such as user-denied permissions and untrusted\nprogrammatic clicks.\n\nBug: 537854348\nChange-Id: I9bd2cc98f9020d4cc0c539f25ec1a4a55dffbad5\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8141012\nReviewed-by: Thomas Nguyen \u003ctungnh@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ravjit Uppal \u003cravjit@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674341}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 6371636b3e1c45c8c5f4d83df0026ea591204638\nwpt-pr: 61767\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/camera-element-use-cases.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/camera-error-scenarios.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/microphone-element-use-cases.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/microphone-error-scenarios.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "60e37b30a0e156d517fb00b000464632c5659ab6", "git_parents": ["cc42ec504b961db89083bd156343d6d7a944b547"], "node": "4df75a1e3b5f24bbea08dbb16d0e1334708a25c8", "parents": ["995414e8f050bd14d78d6f8a24cb828d38219e3d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061028 [wpt PR 61767] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61767\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/camera-element-use-cases.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/camera/camera-error-scenarios.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/microphone-element-use-cases.tentative.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/microphone/microphone-error-scenarios.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "3e7c56f59312815d3775330b6f9f2b16290677d6", "git_parents": ["60e37b30a0e156d517fb00b000464632c5659ab6"], "node": "c250174081673c4d7279e5b1c2c35800f1c73140", "parents": ["4df75a1e3b5f24bbea08dbb16d0e1334708a25c8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061064 [wpt PR 61769] - Make sure spanners don't cause container to lose IsAtBlockEnd()., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMake sure spanners don't cause container to lose IsAtBlockEnd().\n\nFinishFragmentation() returned too early if a spanner had been found, so\nthat any IsAtBlockEnd() state would be lost. Return early a bit later\ninstead. Having IsAtBlockEnd set means that we'll no longer consider\nchild breaks as in-flow (since we're in a parallel flow, since we're\npast the block-end). Therefore, when discovering or propagating a\nspanner, automatically consider this to be an in-flow break.\n\nBug: 542888016\nChange-Id: Ia6af5f727340e3a4f7cb1c61c360d043e0fca175\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8205264\nReviewed-by: Ian Kilpatrick \u003cikilpatrick@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Morten Stenshorne \u003cmstensho@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674557}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: dd49ab208d3e9668e0c34f8a0194c5f8d1637924\nwpt-pr: 61769\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-break/box-decoration-break-clone-037.html"], "git_node": "c6321062fc37e4c977eaf84bee72c11ef37f4571", "git_parents": ["3e7c56f59312815d3775330b6f9f2b16290677d6"], "node": "83c46094e30d961f2a98a6bff993d1e21c5b85fe", "parents": ["c250174081673c4d7279e5b1c2c35800f1c73140"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061064 [wpt PR 61769] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61769\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-break/box-decoration-break-clone-037.html.ini"], "git_node": "e5441e3ddecf2efae0b1ef1f2a5fb0b2f626e7c5", "git_parents": ["c6321062fc37e4c977eaf84bee72c11ef37f4571"], "node": "d328c84610cbe39705426d44afb15e3faf4eab14", "parents": ["83c46094e30d961f2a98a6bff993d1e21c5b85fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061099 [wpt PR 61772] - Fix malformed tags in focus-related WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix malformed tags in focus-related WPTs\n\nRemove unmatched closing tags from object focus and dialog backdrop\ntests, and close the focusgroup table footer with the matching tfoot\ntag.\n\nThese changes correct unintended parser errors while preserving the\ntests' behavior.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: Ie97c6217fcb4e337217e91fb6324af5312472461\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8201866\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674566}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 984ad678143075972c974c1e52e67389c5ee7b4d\nwpt-pr: 61772\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/chrome-object-tab-focus-bug.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusgroup/tentative/grid-navigation/moves-across-table-sections.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/interactive-elements/the-dialog-element/backdrop-in-flow.html"], "git_node": "389172c150734e512be1d0ed852c0f7949fdecbd", "git_parents": ["e5441e3ddecf2efae0b1ef1f2a5fb0b2f626e7c5"], "node": "9e72bf649571e4b8fbf4c3545a9b9c5855bd6633", "parents": ["d328c84610cbe39705426d44afb15e3faf4eab14"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Brent Fulgham \u003c44174109+brentfulgham@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061093 [wpt PR 61771] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=275048, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=275048 (#61771)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7b860c524151c4a5ad6b925ba48719a6e70b2464\nwpt-pr: 61771\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/popovers/popover-hint-dialog-dismisses-unrelated-auto.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/popovers/popover-manual-hide-does-not-close-auto.html"], "git_node": "3e2ca9a0c439231ce16c51eb69d6b6be4f6559cc", "git_parents": ["389172c150734e512be1d0ed852c0f7949fdecbd"], "node": "a31b4f40658d613a5de55aadcf127e37a0d6f770", "parents": ["9e72bf649571e4b8fbf4c3545a9b9c5855bd6633"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061093 [wpt PR 61771] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61771\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/popovers/popover-hint-dialog-dismisses-unrelated-auto.html.ini"], "git_node": "400b78c2dafdf5675bfe64f12acc0c3c4e123bf4", "git_parents": ["3e2ca9a0c439231ce16c51eb69d6b6be4f6559cc"], "node": "dae48514f8cf10b276c946fca95948188d882ed7", "parents": ["a31b4f40658d613a5de55aadcf127e37a0d6f770"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ananya Anand \u003ct-anaanand@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060884 [wpt PR 61752] - [symbols] Support symbols() in counter() and counters(), a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[symbols] Support symbols() in counter() and counters()\n\nComplete CSS Counter Styles L3 `symbols()` by wiring it into `counter()`\nand `counters()`. `CSSCounterContentValue`'s list style generalizes from\na name to a `\u003ccounter-style-name\u003e` or `symbols()`; `CounterContentData`\nbuilds its anonymous counter style eagerly and stores only that, used by\nboth the rendered counter and the accessibility alt-text path;\n`getComputedStyle` round-trips.\n\nAdd WPT coverage for `symbols()` in `counter()`/`counters()`: valid and\ninvalid parsing plus computed value in the css-content\ncontent-{valid,invalid,computed}.html tests, and accessibility unit\ntests for the `counter()` and `counters()` alt-text paths.\n\nThe `content-computed.html` rebaseline only adds a `Found 2 FAIL`\nsummary line: the new passing `symbols()` subtests push the file past\nthe 50-subtest threshold at which the harness emits that summary. The\ntwo failures pre-exist and are an unrelated quote-concatenation issue,\nnot a `symbols()` regression.\n\nClass relationships across the counter() path:\n- CSSCounterContentValue: the parsed CSS value for counter()/counters()\n  in `content`. Holds the counter name, the \u003ccounter-style\u003e argument\n  (a \u003ccounter-style-name\u003e or a symbols() function), and the separator.\n- CounterContentData (a ContentData subclass): the computed-style form.\n  Stores the resolved name, separator, tree scope, and the anonymous\n  CounterStyle built eagerly from symbols(); the symbols() value itself\n  is reconstructed on demand for getComputedStyle.\n- CounterStyle: the runtime object that generates the counter text; for\n  symbols() it is built inline via CreateAnonymousCounterStyle().\n- LayoutCounter: renders the counter, resolving its CounterStyle via\n  CounterContentData::ResolveCounterStyle() (inline symbols() if\n  present, else a named \u003ccounter-style\u003e looked up in scope)\n\nBug: 40747844\nChange-Id: I8fa2cf5c0884a7aada3c9e21ffe32019a50a47f4\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8066695\nReviewed-by: Alison Maher \u003calmaher@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Javier Contreras \u003cjaviercon@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Ananya Anand \u003ct-anaanand@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674627}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bf4714d81e796b9cb98d8e94a31509351a44ac16\nwpt-pr: 61752\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-content/parsing/content-computed.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-content/parsing/content-invalid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-content/parsing/content-valid.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/counter-style-at-rule/symbols-function-dynamic-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-counter-styles/counter-style-at-rule/symbols-function-dynamic.html"], "git_node": "0576e3d17ed780ec0e47201f26df9e854ed02631", "git_parents": ["400b78c2dafdf5675bfe64f12acc0c3c4e123bf4"], "node": "25f7185087d63673ef79c91ad6554611cb3b7d16", "parents": ["dae48514f8cf10b276c946fca95948188d882ed7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061129 [wpt PR 61775] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320114, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320114 (#61775)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 10e2139b375e0462cc996054f9c58cd3b3a79cdb\nwpt-pr: 61775\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/picture-in-picture/request-picture-in-picture-consumes-user-activation.html"], "git_node": "c9c92d207fc8788a0d2c2ef6c88888969846fb94", "git_parents": ["0576e3d17ed780ec0e47201f26df9e854ed02631"], "node": "562db9ff72d8536e39317fa5fc3e10272d1f99d3", "parents": ["25f7185087d63673ef79c91ad6554611cb3b7d16"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Patrick Griffis \u003cpgriffis@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058712 [wpt PR 61587] - compression-dictionary: Relax timing on iframe load, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\ncompression-dictionary: Await the subframe ready message\n\nThe test asserted a flag set by the \"ready\" postMessage handler right\nafter iframe.onload fired, but the message is not guaranteed to be\ndelivered by then. Await a promise for the message instead, which fixes\nconstant failures in WebKit.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ce9441ee673c68c5d175d2363c9ff2e4893b827c\nwpt-pr: 61587\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/fetch/compression-dictionary/compressed-large-resources-002.tentative.https.html"], "git_node": "b0570d3cc2a2dfdecf7510077a3905b07451daf9", "git_parents": ["c9c92d207fc8788a0d2c2ef6c88888969846fb94"], "node": "06e242511bf116dc65818f48c8841a99a2e55fa5", "parents": ["562db9ff72d8536e39317fa5fc3e10272d1f99d3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061134 [wpt PR 61780] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=187454, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=187454 (#61780)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: def40799257dca39d79b213f731629943778a249\nwpt-pr: 61780\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-writing-modes/orthogonal-parent-shrink-to-fit-002.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-border-attributes-computed-style.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-rules-computed-style.html"], "git_node": "bfb5d447beb7cb3468bef0e3108e830cc197fe89", "git_parents": ["b0570d3cc2a2dfdecf7510077a3905b07451daf9"], "node": "9d21ced9b683607fa30ba910bdb2af4e90b535e2", "parents": ["06e242511bf116dc65818f48c8841a99a2e55fa5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061134 [wpt PR 61780] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61780\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/rendering/non-replaced-elements/tables/table-rules-computed-style.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a1034362545e4afe3df01768e4cc0cf745884ae", "git_parents": ["bfb5d447beb7cb3468bef0e3108e830cc197fe89"], "node": "4ba58c631a649041be9ff45e72973cb0335dce29", "parents": ["9d21ced9b683607fa30ba910bdb2af4e90b535e2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061018 [wpt PR 61757] - layout: Map between pre-transformed and post-transformed selection offsets during display list construction, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Map between pre-transformed and post-transformed selection offsets during display list construction\n\nThere are two types of DOM-node-relative text offsets to consider in\nlayout. One is pre-transformed, that is before any white space collapse\nor `text-transform` is applied to the node's text content. This is how\nselections are stored, so that they can be updated without triggering a\nfull layout. The other is post-transformed, that is after white space\ncollapse and `text-transform`. This is how glyph character advances are\nmeasured. This changes moves the mapping from the first to the second to\ndisplay list construction, so that it is done also for form control\nselections. This fixes the behavior of visual selections and\n`text-transform` in form control elements and is also foundational for\nensuring that the reverse transform can happen during hit testing.\n\nSigned-off-by: Martin Robinson \u003cmrobinson@igalia.com\u003e\nCo-authored-by: Simon Sapin \u003csimon@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 65a84f0c44af6db93c1da33643ae1654575c520a\nwpt-pr: 61757\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-transform/reference/text-transform-upperlower-108-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-text/text-transform/text-transform-upperlower-108.html"], "git_node": "76a92dcfcbb4f7d9ec7fe25932bd64c3773d0b80", "git_parents": ["9a1034362545e4afe3df01768e4cc0cf745884ae"], "node": "fe224593bf1d60a71547da794944d00ed40793fb", "parents": ["4ba58c631a649041be9ff45e72973cb0335dce29"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061018 [wpt PR 61757] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61757\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-text/text-transform/text-transform-upperlower-108.html.ini"], "git_node": "9a602e4abe8f0d9d724b8a9e79768ff44f9dff1e", "git_parents": ["76a92dcfcbb4f7d9ec7fe25932bd64c3773d0b80"], "node": "07f5a56cb76e3d247aeb4988bba11bc19cf896df", "parents": ["fe224593bf1d60a71547da794944d00ed40793fb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Yoichi Osato \u003cyoichio@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061150 [wpt PR 61779] - Restrict nested cross-origin subframes in prerendering, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRestrict nested cross-origin subframes in prerendering\n\nWhile current speculation rules permit cross-origin subframe\nprerendering, we've reached the consensus that nested cross-origin\niframes prerendering should be prohibited unless their immediate parent\nexplicitly opts in that via the `Supports-Loading-Mode:\nprerender-cross-origin-frames` header.\n\nThis change updates PrerenderSubframeNavigationThrottle to compare\nsubframe origins against the immediate parent frame rather than the main\nframe. This doesn't change the original behavior: if each children's\norigin is same, it is prerendered. This also updates\nDecidePolicyForCrossOriginSubframeNavigation to enforce deferral of\nnested cross-origin subframe navigations during prerendering when the\nimmediate parent frame lacks the required header.\n\nThis change is guarded by new kPrerender2CrossOriginIframesNesting and\nyou can try this change by\n\"--enable-features=Prerender2CrossOriginIframes:nesting/true\" command\nline flag or selecting \"Enabled (Version 2:nesting/true)\" from\nchrome://flags/#prerender2-cross-origin-iframes.\n\nBug: 440387014\nChange-Id: I0e97b598347f4bc9ac82fb333bbab36b9137d696\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8130521\nReviewed-by: Hiroki Nakagawa \u003cnhiroki@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Yoichi Osato \u003cyoichio@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674756}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 77d52d38104bc4ce5696c01ed4bf402013d00ac0\nwpt-pr: 61779\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/cross-origin-iframe-prerender-nesting.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-nesting-src-no-slm-prerender.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-nesting-src-prerender.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-nesting-src-prerender.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-prerender-nesting.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-prerender-nesting.html.headers", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-prerender.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/speculation-rules/prerender/resources/cross-origin-iframe-src-prerender.html"], "git_node": "da0eee125fc673621ed4a64ffe4fd1ff7a26f4a9", "git_parents": ["9a602e4abe8f0d9d724b8a9e79768ff44f9dff1e"], "node": "b477e068681312d66b44f02a39156a97534d8542", "parents": ["07f5a56cb76e3d247aeb4988bba11bc19cf896df"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061150 [wpt PR 61779] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61779\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/speculation-rules/prerender/cross-origin-iframe-prerender-nesting.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "06c39bc659b0bb6e97390daaf03b4e07db288e3c", "git_parents": ["da0eee125fc673621ed4a64ffe4fd1ff7a26f4a9"], "node": "f4ff5fbd427b30ddc67ea24971e7759d5db1b925", "parents": ["b477e068681312d66b44f02a39156a97534d8542"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060724 [wpt PR 61737] - wpt: Add tests for LCP element removed after paint, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd new tests\n\nSigned-off-by: Shubham Gupta \u003cshubhamg13.work@gmail.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 48c24e54d88e3253b0c738ebc5456ee169f21751\nwpt-pr: 61737\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/image-element-when-fully-active.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/image-removed-after-paint.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/largest-contentful-paint/resources/iframe-stores-image-entry.html"], "git_node": "e948630ee3bb8a58c102f616418f31a11e9a8473", "git_parents": ["06c39bc659b0bb6e97390daaf03b4e07db288e3c"], "node": "86e757bf400eca672f8e812d7c6d8c0e7527397f", "parents": ["f4ff5fbd427b30ddc67ea24971e7759d5db1b925"], "tags": []}, {"author": "jack \u003c75576058+jackholden@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061162 [wpt PR 61783] - [css-anchor-position] add missing contact detail to author meta, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-anchor-position] add missing contact detail to author meta (#61783)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 82ae0730495fd90c7d4f248c6225f23a711c75ab\nwpt-pr: 61783\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-name-shadow-higher-tree.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-anchor-position/anchor-name-shadow-lower-tree.html"], "git_node": "af91e716b785057c3e63b2139c9f28ed84bf9b8f", "git_parents": ["e948630ee3bb8a58c102f616418f31a11e9a8473"], "node": "c072fde04cf0715ca546cedeca493ed54cc02842", "parents": ["86e757bf400eca672f8e812d7c6d8c0e7527397f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060747 [wpt PR 61742] - [approx-geo] Add WPT for approx location, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[approx-geo] Add WPT for approx location\n\nThis CL adds a basic Web Platform Test covering a call to\ngeolocation.getCurrentPosition with accuracyMode set to approximate.\nThis allows us to have minimal coverage for\nhttps://github.com/w3c/geolocation/pull/233.\n\nChange-Id: I78321992cb90a065fee416b2047c05be0892d38f\nForce-WPT-Export: true\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8174483\nReviewed-by: Alvin Ji \u003calvinji@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Antonio Sartori \u003cantoniosartori@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674767}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 070c80e52881e9719ee244563d80b383c76b07bf\nwpt-pr: 61742\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/geolocation/getCurrentPosition-accuracyMode.https.html"], "git_node": "8816144bd027975bda1a8c5d5d6eb43446afd8e0", "git_parents": ["af91e716b785057c3e63b2139c9f28ed84bf9b8f"], "node": "026c3207540faf129c644577003865ec4dc5293a", "parents": ["c072fde04cf0715ca546cedeca493ed54cc02842"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060747 [wpt PR 61742] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61742\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/geolocation/getCurrentPosition-accuracyMode.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "5a9409c943a60598e85e04124ccdd13354bd3d61", "git_parents": ["8816144bd027975bda1a8c5d5d6eb43446afd8e0"], "node": "91bcc971fbdbb7c218c75b52c3c4862317ec81a3", "parents": ["026c3207540faf129c644577003865ec4dc5293a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060946 [wpt PR 61754] - layout: Fix interaction of margin and stretch size on block-level box inside inline box, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nlayout: Fix interaction of margin and stretch size on block-level box inside inline box\n\nSigned-off-by: Oriol Brufau \u003cobrufau@igalia.com\u003e\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: bfb04e06cf7fcf9f4739990b4c0ca252f189840f\nwpt-pr: 61754\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/stretch/block-height-011.html"], "git_node": "eda9b937399b7b944eb170ff713d5d0d563551d5", "git_parents": ["5a9409c943a60598e85e04124ccdd13354bd3d61"], "node": "22dc604491eeaace0ae66bd7254860093cceb261", "parents": ["91bcc971fbdbb7c218c75b52c3c4862317ec81a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060946 [wpt PR 61754] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61754\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/stretch/__dir__.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/stretch/block-height-011.html.ini"], "git_node": "cdb426a25806b5cd78010d23ba4c0240debf504d", "git_parents": ["eda9b937399b7b944eb170ff713d5d0d563551d5"], "node": "5cdcf974ec1c531c754df5e3cc4ca2b3dedc444c", "parents": ["22dc604491eeaace0ae66bd7254860093cceb261"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fran\u00e7ois Beaufort \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061513 [wpt PR 61785] - [WebMCP] Require active frame for declarative tool registration, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebMCP] Require active frame for declarative tool registration\n\nWhen parsing HTML containing a declarative WebMCP form (with `toolname`\nand `tooldescription` attributes) into a document without a browsing\ncontext\u2014such as via `DOMParser.parseFromString(..., 'text/html')` or\n`document.implementation.createHTMLDocument()`\u2014the renderer process is\nterminated with `bad_message::RFHI_WEBMCP_DUPLICATE_BIND` (reason 346).\n\nThis occurs because forms inside inert documents pass the\n`isConnected()` check. Consequently, attempting to register a\ndeclarative WebMCP tool reaches for the parsing frame's interface broker\nand binds the WebMCP interface a second time on an already-bound\n`RenderFrameHostImpl`, triggering a fatal bad IPC message crash.\n\nThis patch fixes the issue by early-returning from\n`ScheduleDeclarativeWebMCPToolRegistration()` if the document has no\nframe (`!GetDocument().GetFrame()`). This prevents scheduling\nunnecessary tool registration tasks or reporting DevTools audit issues\nfor forms in inert or frame-less documents, while ensuring declarative\ntools are only registered for forms connected to an active frame with a\nvalid browsing context.\n\nAdditionally, this ensures we do not attempt registration scheduling or\nunregistration when an element's attribute is modified after its frame\nhas been removed (e.g., when an iframe containing a declarative form\ntool is removed from the DOM).\n\nBug: 540681578\nChange-Id: Id68f6b047f5cd9020d540a57d811f2bafc7ad884\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8194424\nReviewed-by: Dominic Farolino \u003cdom@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fr \u003cbeaufort.francois@gmail.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1674920}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 9a781a6b1e382317d127c4244105f67866506163\nwpt-pr: 61785\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/webmcp/declarative/no-frame-documents.https.html"], "git_node": "7a2e77125070b7dc9fa8558179d1b47bb42bf692", "git_parents": ["cdb426a25806b5cd78010d23ba4c0240debf504d"], "node": "d90bf700be110eb93d07759788efe865e7ccc89c", "parents": ["5cdcf974ec1c531c754df5e3cc4ca2b3dedc444c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061513 [wpt PR 61785] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61785\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/webmcp/declarative/no-frame-documents.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "0837fbc55a8710fe4397336323fa37c2680822e0", "git_parents": ["7a2e77125070b7dc9fa8558179d1b47bb42bf692"], "node": "4c2594c569a2f36b21bf05201c87eb247c6e7c3b", "parents": ["d90bf700be110eb93d07759788efe865e7ccc89c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Filip Skokan \u003cpanva.ip@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061146 [wpt PR 61778] - [WebCryptoAPI] Separate bad algorithm failures, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCryptoAPI] Separate bad algorithm failures (#61778)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 525f1ac17f10f9175183dcda37de51a6460ee2cf\nwpt-pr: 61778\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/generateKey/failures.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/generateKey/failures_bad_algorithm.https.any.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/tools/generate.py"], "git_node": "8907290e9140de5f0856e33ce78c3fcfaaea7270", "git_parents": ["0837fbc55a8710fe4397336323fa37c2680822e0"], "node": "9e0be73b7a98e60f783ce77ad7659026bef02cfd", "parents": ["4c2594c569a2f36b21bf05201c87eb247c6e7c3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jose Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061550 [wpt PR 61787] - ContainerTiming: cover image paint attribution ordering and cost, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nContainerTiming: cover image paint attribution ordering and cost\n\nImage tests race the resource load against the first pre-paint walk, so\nwhether the load is notified before or after attribution depends on\ncache state. No test pins either ordering, so an attribution change that\nonly works one way round has no coverage that would catch it.\n\ncontainertiming-img-already-loaded.html forces the ordering by loading\nthe resource before inserting the \u003cimg\u003e. It passes under both\nimplementations.\n\nThe perf benchmark covers per-image attribution, which nothing measured:\nthe existing ones use CSS background images (no LayoutImage) and repeat\na single element. It asserts that a paint produces an entry, so it\ncannot decay into timing an early return.\n\nBug: 489959278\nChange-Id: If00fd6efde1b249e32065db31071d9f049bc5c0d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8203144\nReviewed-by: Michal Mocny \u003cmmocny@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jos\u00e9 Dapena Paz \u003cjdapena@igalia.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675007}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 10c73efbce86f87250dd64e7488cfcdbeeef2b79\nwpt-pr: 61787\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-already-loaded.html"], "git_node": "288fd882393457c53dfdc4ce2a2fb3df7da8fee4", "git_parents": ["8907290e9140de5f0856e33ce78c3fcfaaea7270"], "node": "4ed123fcf1d12ff092edaede34e9183719e14c83", "parents": ["9e0be73b7a98e60f783ce77ad7659026bef02cfd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061550 [wpt PR 61787] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61787\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/container-timing/tentative/containertiming-img-already-loaded.html.ini"], "git_node": "e962d5c26e7bc478e90b9bd70342dcff4509ac48", "git_parents": ["288fd882393457c53dfdc4ce2a2fb3df7da8fee4"], "node": "13ccc03a3ffd52db9053fd24e58b3ec8281b0a7f", "parents": ["4ed123fcf1d12ff092edaede34e9183719e14c83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061158 [wpt PR 61782] - [css-mixins] Fix @apply contents block brace serialization, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[css-mixins] Fix @apply contents block brace serialization\n\nCSSApplyMixinRule::cssText() appended the closing \" }\" inside the\nper-child loop, so an empty @apply block dropped the brace. Append it\nonce after the loop.\n\nThe crash from the same report was already fixed by CL:8114919 and this\nCL handles the remaining serialization issue.\n\nChange-Id: I1c707229afd84f2af093fc6f15ca073da469dd0e\nFixed: 539569497\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8203047\nCommit-Queue: Stephanie Zhang \u003cstephanie.zhang@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Rune Lillesveen \u003cfuthark@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675008}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 7dc1142c281f6e3314c733d51917d9e373800ebc\nwpt-pr: 61782\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-cssom.tentative.html"], "git_node": "4e7d5f6abc823165485dcc25045d9d3ae8ba80df", "git_parents": ["e962d5c26e7bc478e90b9bd70342dcff4509ac48"], "node": "82c5b572d9d8708edbcc575225418a9a725bf1ef", "parents": ["13ccc03a3ffd52db9053fd24e58b3ec8281b0a7f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061158 [wpt PR 61782] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61782\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-mixins/mixins/mixin-cssom.tentative.html.ini"], "git_node": "f54e9cd60c0d4a683105cda5ed4a0902b658f2d6", "git_parents": ["4e7d5f6abc823165485dcc25045d9d3ae8ba80df"], "node": "c9c8a6b7af338f5759371b4c44e06902b8769a5c", "parents": ["82c5b572d9d8708edbcc575225418a9a725bf1ef"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ravjit Uppal \u003cravjit@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061559 [wpt PR 61791] - [CE] Run \u003cusermedia\u003e WPTs with the correct feature flags., a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[CE] Run \u003cusermedia\u003e WPTs with the correct feature flags.\n\nLegacy mode of usermedia is being deprecated. Currently it can only\nenabled using an OT token. All the WPTs should run in the standard mode,\nas that is the default mode. Also added a few legacy only tests to make\nsure it doesn't regress while it is still available on OT.\n\nChange-Id: Ifa14f9a1e949c5b08440e5d18432b906774cccb3\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8102203\nReviewed-by: Joey Arhar \u003cjarhar@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Ravjit Uppal \u003cravjit@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Thomas Nguyen \u003ctungnh@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Jonathan Lee \u003cjonathanjlee@google.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Jonathan Lee \u003cjonathanjlee@google.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675034}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 775f25e70420865bd2beeae6a1a2072b5c0387f8\nwpt-pr: 61791\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/bounded-sizes-reftest-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/bounded-sizes-reftest.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/display-values.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/granted-selector.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/invalid-type-reftest-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/invalid-type-reftest.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/lang-attribute-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/large-min-size-reftest-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/large-min-size-reftest.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/no-children-rendered.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/no-focus.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/parent-image-mask.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/parent-mask.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/permission-icon/icon-unique-per-type-reftest.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/permission-icon/standard-camera-usermedia-element-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/type-supported-feature-detect.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/unbounded-width-with-border-reftest-ref.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/unbounded-width-with-border-reftest.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/usermedia/lang-attribute-update.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/usermedia/legacy-mode/legacy-mode.tentative.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/permission-element/usermedia/no-focus.tentative.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/interfaces/usermedia-element.tentative.idl"], "git_node": "d2bc428be924af3777442eff0f4f9848a32c79fc", "git_parents": ["f54e9cd60c0d4a683105cda5ed4a0902b658f2d6"], "node": "e3f08a77c2664af7b6c49a83ca9376b38cbdffea", "parents": ["c9c8a6b7af338f5759371b4c44e06902b8769a5c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061559 [wpt PR 61791] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61791\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/granted-selector.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/invalid-css-properties.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/lang-attribute-update.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/no-children-rendered.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/no-focus.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/type-supported-feature-detect.tentative.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/permission-element/usermedia/legacy-mode/legacy-mode.tentative.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "0060eb48fe0e46b56e17156427d7ec320b8d0fc3", "git_parents": ["d2bc428be924af3777442eff0f4f9848a32c79fc"], "node": "41698d28014d088bffacd00ab7da2574d20bed3b", "parents": ["e3f08a77c2664af7b6c49a83ca9376b38cbdffea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061563 [wpt PR 61794] - Fix malformed markup in HTML WPTs, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nFix malformed markup in HTML WPTs\n\nCorrect mismatched closing tags in HTML and soft-navigation WPTs so\ntheir source reflects the intended parsed DOM.\n\nBug: 542686202\nChange-Id: Ifbc29ea490264afa25c2263289edffc48a90de63\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8207981\nReviewed-by: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Fernando Fiori \u003cffiori@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Ana Sollano Kim \u003cansollan@microsoft.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675040}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: d3fcf7674eb52e3fff3db4ed5bbfe62814c6059a\nwpt-pr: 61794\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/fragment-mask-png-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/canvas/element/manual/draw-element-image/privacy/fragment-mask-svg-ignored.tentative.https.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/editing/dnd/remove/022.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/rendering/the-details-element/details-blockification.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/popovers/popover-target-element-disabled.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/soft-navigation-heuristics/detection/tentative/navigation-api-precommit-handler.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/soft-navigation-heuristics/detection/tentative/video-srcObject-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/soft-navigation-heuristics/smoke/tentative/video-src-change.html"], "git_node": "e7e19e85ed2762dd71bf384b076ad22785a7ec8d", "git_parents": ["0060eb48fe0e46b56e17156427d7ec320b8d0fc3"], "node": "c00beb2cd900a654308fb3d024a29626a9dd6d1e", "parents": ["41698d28014d088bffacd00ab7da2574d20bed3b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Blink WPT Bot \u003cblink-w3c-test-autoroller@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060667 [wpt PR 61725] - [iframe] Rename `allowed-origins` to `alloworigins`, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[iframe] Rename `allowed-origins` to `alloworigins` (#61725)\n\nThis patch renames the attribute as per the WHATWG feedback[1].\n\n[1]: https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12444#issuecomment-5168602652\n\nBug: 418397278\nChange-Id: I185e7e7de5411bbfe5d1a6a1c972e05dba49101d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8173946\nAuto-Submit: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Kent Tamura \u003ctkent@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1673080}\n\nCo-authored-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 5e75769b378a7ebf3831c0f3e73042518c7f8209\nwpt-pr: 61725\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-400x200root.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-allowed-origins-missing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-allowed-origins.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-alloworigins-missing.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-alloworigins.sub.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-dom-content-loaded.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-icb.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-after-head.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-append-after-body.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-append-to-doc.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-append.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-name-change-after-body.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-name-change.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-remove.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-dynamic-write.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-meta-in-body.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-navigation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-request-resize.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents-slow.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/resources/iframe-contents.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-allowed-origins.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-alloworigins.html"], "git_node": "6cf385c04a2c8bf77cc0992c881ef4393f2763bf", "git_parents": ["e7e19e85ed2762dd71bf384b076ad22785a7ec8d"], "node": "b416999ab7a929c42b1536fba61c7fef43cda20f", "parents": ["c00beb2cd900a654308fb3d024a29626a9dd6d1e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060667 [wpt PR 61725] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61725\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-sizing/responsive-iframe/responsive-iframe-alloworigins.html.ini"], "git_node": "dc480eaf23d39bb13c9ef20e5473b2a1a335ff07", "git_parents": ["6cf385c04a2c8bf77cc0992c881ef4393f2763bf"], "node": "fab9790a89140e1a05d304cc870a0acfec961a05", "parents": ["b416999ab7a929c42b1536fba61c7fef43cda20f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alan Ding \u003calanding@google.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061561 [wpt PR 61792] - Block LanguageModel.create promise resolution until model initializes, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nBlock LanguageModel.create promise resolution until model initializes\n\nEnsure AILanguageModel::InitializeSafetyChecksComplete issues an Append\ncall to initial_session_ even when initial_prompts is empty. This forces\nthe session creation to wait for the backend on_device_model service to\nfinish loading/initializing the model engine before firing OnResult() to\nresolve the JavaScript create() promise.\n\nAlso update the WPT user-activation test to avoid awaiting the\nlong-running model initialization inside test_driver.bless(), which\ncaused the transient user activation window (~5s) to expire before the\nassertion on navigator.userActivation.isActive could run.\n\nBug: 540980352, 476192657\nChange-Id: I60d6f73f7d958f776b1dcdf055226d0ee44e1d85\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8190677\nReviewed-by: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Mike Wasserman \u003cmsw@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Nathan Memmott \u003cmemmott@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Alan Ding \u003calanding@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675149}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0030ae0c8239c42aeabc71ae5c8f3bf1e5393740\nwpt-pr: 61792\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/ai/language-model/language-model-create-user-activation.tentative.https.window.js"], "git_node": "7a2c5b95bc082098d0fbb8e7b841868e45f57898", "git_parents": ["dc480eaf23d39bb13c9ef20e5473b2a1a335ff07"], "node": "68097ac331e4a36364892fa97210777c003cbf07", "parents": ["fab9790a89140e1a05d304cc870a0acfec961a05"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jochen K\u00fchner \u003cjochen.kuehner@gmx.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060910 [wpt PR 61753] - Implement CSSOM View GeometryUtils, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nImplement CSSOM View GeometryUtils\n\nWeb authors need engine-accurate transformed geometry for editors,\noverlays, and hit testing. JavaScript polyfills have to reconstruct\nBlink layout and frame ancestry, which is incomplete and costly for\ndeep DOM trees.\n\nExpose getBoxQuads() and coordinate conversion on Document, Element,\nText, and CSSPseudoElement behind the existing experimental runtime\nflags. Resolve both endpoints after synchronous layout so lifecycle\nupdates cannot invalidate a captured LayoutObject. Reuse\nLayoutObject::QuadsInAncestor so CSS fragments, inline content, SVG\nlayout boxes, and transforms use Blink's established geometry paths.\n\nFor SVG inline boxes, combine glyph-level fragment items within each\ninline box fragment. This preserves one quad per box fragment and keeps\npositioned \u003ctspan\u003e geometry consistent with Firefox and existing WPTs.\n\nReject conversions when either endpoint has no usable layout reference,\nwhen frame trees are disconnected, or when any document on the frame\npath crosses an origin boundary. For a non-generated source pseudo,\nstart at its originating element as required by the transform algorithm.\nThis matches the non-null IDL while keeping same-origin iframe conversion\navailable.\n\nKeep the connected-callback WPT deterministic with a fixed workload.\nThe feature remains experimental while specification and launch review\ncontinue.\n\nChromeStatus: https://chromestatus.com/feature/6015941766807552\n\nSpec: https://drafts.csswg.org/cssom-view/#the-geometryutils-interface\n\nWPT: https://github.com/web-platform-tests/wpt/pull/61254\n\nBug: 427918516\nChange-Id: I49fab363ea6a14efa97534ded9fd718a741d07dc\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8039580\nCommit-Queue: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675195}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: ff6ddeda853784b0839a832b01050af682ab3009\nwpt-pr: 61753\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-connected-callback.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-convertPointFromNode.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-cross-origin-path.https.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-element-types.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-fragmentation.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-getBoxQuads-options.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-lifecycle.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-same-origin-iframe.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-shadow-dom.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-text.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/resources/geometry-utils-cross-origin-inner.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/css/cssom-view/resources/geometry-utils-cross-origin-middle.html"], "git_node": "c6f52567afeae9d842f59414cec8a28b86b6e4b4", "git_parents": ["7a2c5b95bc082098d0fbb8e7b841868e45f57898"], "node": "bff9c61f388b8ef61b91f6bcf9aa675841071ddd", "parents": ["68097ac331e4a36364892fa97210777c003cbf07"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060910 [wpt PR 61753] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61753\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-convertPointFromNode.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-cross-origin-path.https.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-element-types.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-getBoxQuads-options.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-lifecycle.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-same-origin-iframe.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-shadow-dom.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/cssom-view/cssom-geometryutils-text.html.ini"], "git_node": "2120a9edf6d9a887c6b2dd61a6300c5148d56166", "git_parents": ["c6f52567afeae9d842f59414cec8a28b86b6e4b4"], "node": "43043fd99d76b18ed340e7468f27e855bfaa0d4b", "parents": ["bff9c61f388b8ef61b91f6bcf9aa675841071ddd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061573 [wpt PR 61798] - [focusgroup] Restore focusgroup data after shadow host moves, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[focusgroup] Restore focusgroup data after shadow host moves\n\nRe-parse focusgroup attributes in a shadow tree whenever its host is\nreinserted. Removal clears the cached focusgroup data, so skipping the\nparse when no ancestor is a focusgroup leaves moved components without\ndirectional navigation.\n\nFixed: 540914692\nBug: 40210717\nChange-Id: Id10940c40e49ed5643776770cfc3d9e9438d17bb\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8205924\nCommit-Queue: Jacques Newman \u003cjanewman@microsoft.com\u003e\nReviewed-by: Mason Freed \u003cmasonf@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675252}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4e2249bfdbe39b41b26e39e0d9432d86700ca44f\nwpt-pr: 61798\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/interaction/focus/focusgroup/tentative/shadow/shadow-reattach.html"], "git_node": "25c9ad6f51f17b6435147f6f0debdb4e0a9e9464", "git_parents": ["2120a9edf6d9a887c6b2dd61a6300c5148d56166"], "node": "f9edf94ae9e0e704cd34490edc7215df975164d4", "parents": ["43043fd99d76b18ed340e7468f27e855bfaa0d4b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061573 [wpt PR 61798] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61798\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/html/interaction/focus/focusgroup/tentative/shadow/shadow-reattach.html.ini"], "git_node": "48f092b01a45b348a4f02a5c6c07449b36059448", "git_parents": ["25c9ad6f51f17b6435147f6f0debdb4e0a9e9464"], "node": "a75c385b3b176ad0aeb6b74931c442dba664072c", "parents": ["f9edf94ae9e0e704cd34490edc7215df975164d4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Karl Dubost \u003ckarlcow@apple.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061615 [wpt PR 61806] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320456, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=320456 (#61806)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4a5677a46ea1a8a970669c00b544902c263298e8\nwpt-pr: 61806\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/geometry/svg-geometry-apis-in-non-rendered-elements.html"], "git_node": "7288bb3548db53d1a47a5ac4d03d957eb913ebab", "git_parents": ["48f092b01a45b348a4f02a5c6c07449b36059448"], "node": "8801672e29f2fd41db7934a5b61601b39ca1b48e", "parents": ["a75c385b3b176ad0aeb6b74931c442dba664072c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061615 [wpt PR 61806] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61806\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/geometry/svg-geometry-apis-in-non-rendered-elements.html.ini"], "git_node": "d979ef20705610e0b57043045362355920b99520", "git_parents": ["7288bb3548db53d1a47a5ac4d03d957eb913ebab"], "node": "f9078b514b2f26d879db648df7cc50cdd09b6ba5", "parents": ["8801672e29f2fd41db7934a5b61601b39ca1b48e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061607 [wpt PR 61802] - Remove zoom from SVGImage container scale, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nRemove zoom from SVGImage container scale\n\nThe destination rectangle is in zoomed coordinates, but the source\nrectangle is not. Hence we would get a zoom factor included in it, which\nwould affect the result.\n\nRemove the zoom factor from the container scale.\n\nFixed: 542873380\nChange-Id: I1b4c70723cd6a06059eeb909252715a9da4cb510\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8215099\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nAuto-Submit: Fredrik S\u00f6derquist \u003cfs@opera.com\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675273}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 0efba20b483df0af6d5e06035fffdf3b9480a14b\nwpt-pr: 61802\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/non-scaling-stroke-009.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/svg/painting/reftests/non-scaling-stroke-010.html"], "git_node": "b98d5b2df68a469ebc3b2630e6f3cdc4ec30c8c0", "git_parents": ["d979ef20705610e0b57043045362355920b99520"], "node": "b48b8e461140a515a507e47d38e355d5e6307d58", "parents": ["f9078b514b2f26d879db648df7cc50cdd09b6ba5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061607 [wpt PR 61802] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61802\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/svg/painting/reftests/non-scaling-stroke-009.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/svg/painting/reftests/non-scaling-stroke-010.html.ini"], "git_node": "1e41bf22b064b998796d3d863022ea3a7282ccf1", "git_parents": ["b98d5b2df68a469ebc3b2630e6f3cdc4ec30c8c0"], "node": "d07cca488542431b16d5873c9ae73a3b0b229295", "parents": ["b48b8e461140a515a507e47d38e355d5e6307d58"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stefan Zager \u003cszager@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061611 [wpt PR 61804] - [IntersectionObserver] Fix hit testing for flattened 3D context, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[IntersectionObserver] Fix hit testing for flattened 3D context\n\nWhen hit testing for occlusion in a preserve-3d context inside a\n3d-flattening ancestor, checking for negative z-offset does not\nguarantee the layer being tested is not occluding. The negative\nz-offset will be flattened into the ancestor's plane and normal paint\norder hit testing will apply.\n\nBug: 518039263\nChange-Id: I4fd949f1c72a0a730ec3a05d82fe52e31b9ee9b8\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8202385\nReviewed-by: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675279}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 92d1cd27b2e0fb18abaa4a5e52583fe2e9b54a8c\nwpt-pr: 61804\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/v2/3d-transform-flattened-preserve-3d-occlusion.html"], "git_node": "7283ef99d08d772577c70bdbffe0aea8e8fff3a3", "git_parents": ["1e41bf22b064b998796d3d863022ea3a7282ccf1"], "node": "9181e88120f23246c613ce6643a3d22acabe604b", "parents": ["d07cca488542431b16d5873c9ae73a3b0b229295"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061611 [wpt PR 61804] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61804\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/intersection-observer/v2/3d-transform-flattened-preserve-3d-occlusion.html.ini"], "git_node": "135c4a84cc2442360461f93d78c8197cf3b75f25", "git_parents": ["7283ef99d08d772577c70bdbffe0aea8e8fff3a3"], "node": "4de138890f84047172427d0221734ff15a7ac233", "parents": ["9181e88120f23246c613ce6643a3d22acabe604b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ahmad Saleem \u003c52317531+Ahmad-S792@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061609 [wpt PR 61803] - WebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=281976, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nWebKit export of https://bugs.webkit.org/show_bug.cgi?id=281976 (#61803)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 3c719d233ff52df178ec037a86c959dc04c3a559\nwpt-pr: 61803\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/css/css-cascade/scope-evaluation.html"], "git_node": "c00d9fefddc4797c1b8171e10ea1aa99ec73a3c7", "git_parents": ["135c4a84cc2442360461f93d78c8197cf3b75f25"], "node": "7b27de54e7c4a29bda352ff3b4e9ebcf8506fe6e", "parents": ["4de138890f84047172427d0221734ff15a7ac233"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061613 [wpt PR 61805] - MSE-in-Workers: Fix timeout in mediasource-worker-detach-element.html, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nMSE-in-Workers: Fix timeout in mediasource-worker-detach-element.html\n\nmediasource-worker-detach-element.html defines 15 parallel async tests.\nIn bufferInto(), appending in 100-byte increments caused ~60 sequential\nasynchronous appendBuffer() and updateend IPC round-trips per worker.\nAcross 15 concurrent workers on macOS and Windows platform decoders,\nthis exceeded the default 6-second web test timeout.\n\nThis CL adds \u003cmeta name=\"timeout\" content=\"long\"\u003e to the HTML test and\nincreases the bufferInto() initial append size and increment from 100 to\n1000 bytes. This reduces the number of sequential demuxing steps to ~19\nper worker while preserving test coverage for detachment concurrency.\n\nFixed: 540802562\nChange-Id: Id7f0a5d8310f855175e1c1ce3524358662bf781d\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8211563\nAuto-Submit: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Dale Curtis \u003cdalecurtis@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Thomas Guilbert \u003ctguilbert@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675316}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 320db3b1a6cf19b4de520ad7a2f6a152faa77780\nwpt-pr: 61805\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/dedicated-worker/mediasource-worker-detach-element.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/media-source/dedicated-worker/mediasource-worker-detach-element.js"], "git_node": "c64e32b43ec171bdc2558ebb134d63c3503ca074", "git_parents": ["c00d9fefddc4797c1b8171e10ea1aa99ec73a3c7"], "node": "902abd0027112da489b274144e92cee8625f941e", "parents": ["7b27de54e7c4a29bda352ff3b4e9ebcf8506fe6e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Fr\u00e9d\u00e9ric Wang N\u00e9lar \u003cfwang@igalia.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060502 [wpt PR 61717] - CSP: Extend tests for wildcard host, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nCSP: Extend tests for wildcard host\n\nExtend a bit the test for http://*:{{ports[http][0]}}, checking it matches\nthe default host too and mismatches when port is different.\n\nAdd a similar test with an explicit path\nhttp://*:{{ports[http][0]}}/content-security-policy/support/pass.png\nwhich works the same except that it also mismatches if path is different.\n\nTests for wildcard ports are a bit more tricky because the default port\nis not used by WPT server so they are not added in this simple PR where\nonly image load/error is used as a check.\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 485843dad4014f5d1fc8dd766401f654df177c8e\nwpt-pr: 61717\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/generic/wildcard-host-part-002.sub.window.js", "testing/web-platform/tests/content-security-policy/generic/wildcard-host-part.sub.window.js"], "git_node": "dadd73d859dc8104b255f5cb479bcca89ad147e9", "git_parents": ["c64e32b43ec171bdc2558ebb134d63c3503ca074"], "node": "56d20f7457c8009cd1e7981987d5befb622b5b44", "parents": ["902abd0027112da489b274144e92cee8625f941e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060876 [wpt PR 61751] - Add more cases for shadow root scoped registries , a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nAdd more cases for shadow root scoped registries (#61751)\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8ca1b956490e25c4686b3c80d58969f581fd5397\nwpt-pr: 61751\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/registries/Document-importNode-cross-document.window.js"], "git_node": "f6547637a52a4389d50c83aabf8070c2c602f5b3", "git_parents": ["dadd73d859dc8104b255f5cb479bcca89ad147e9"], "node": "a237b8dc44f095f8fbc91017855eaf1819cf12bf", "parents": ["56d20f7457c8009cd1e7981987d5befb622b5b44"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060876 [wpt PR 61751] - Update wpt metadata, a=testonly\n\nwpt-pr: 61751\nwpt-type: metadata\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/Document-importNode-cross-document.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "5b3f40a4a9cd27ba904fee802d2d7740289bd309", "git_parents": ["f6547637a52a4389d50c83aabf8070c2c602f5b3"], "node": "d2d8f5a341452dfe5844603f88efdcceb84d29e1", "parents": ["a237b8dc44f095f8fbc91017855eaf1819cf12bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061659 [wpt PR 61808] - Deflake callback-cross-realm-report-exception.html tests, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nDeflake callback-cross-realm-report-exception.html tests\n\nThese tests flaked because fixed timeouts were used to check uncaught\nexception reporting, which failed if observer or animation frame\ncallbacks were delayed due to bot load. The tests now dynamically wait\nfor the initial error to fire, followed by a 100ms window to assert\nthat no additional errors were incorrectly reported.\n\nFixed: 536112395\nChange-Id: I9c323920f0534d04d0e2e1bda7f8aef5c4c1fb71\nReviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/8202947\nAuto-Submit: Philip Rogers \u003cpdr@chromium.org\u003e\nCommit-Queue: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nReviewed-by: Koji Ishii \u003ckojii@chromium.org\u003e\nCr-Commit-Position: refs/heads/main@{#1675535}\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: a9ba87f8483737d8b6daabcd264b01e0cdad6c16\nwpt-pr: 61808\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/webappapis/animation-frames/callback-cross-realm-report-exception.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/intersection-observer/callback-cross-realm-report-exception.html", "testing/web-platform/tests/resize-observer/callback-cross-realm-report-exception.html"], "git_node": "d6352af7b2582a9630ddd31203fc9553cab01ac6", "git_parents": ["5b3f40a4a9cd27ba904fee802d2d7740289bd309"], "node": "5890376fc300cf5bed77b3ebdcd86f22927b7af3", "parents": ["d2d8f5a341452dfe5844603f88efdcceb84d29e1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ms2ger \u003cMs2ger@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061522 [wpt PR 61786] - XMLSerializer: test attribute escaping, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\nXMLSerializer: test attribute escaping\n\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 8011b287558c2037c8c4334795d08cd136a2cec3\nwpt-pr: 61786\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/domparsing/XMLSerializer-serializeToString.html"], "git_node": "ef37e17a73f6d030e3308eb64c19bb1e0b983260", "git_parents": ["d6352af7b2582a9630ddd31203fc9553cab01ac6"], "node": "e5b59ed1ffdb72b8828799e6bbcf66c633e5a3fe", "parents": ["5890376fc300cf5bed77b3ebdcd86f22927b7af3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Daniel Huigens \u003cd.huigens@protonmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061574 [wpt PR 61799] - [WebCryptoAPI] ECDH and ECDSA: test that generated key length is consistent, a=testonly\n\nAutomatic update from web-platform-tests\n[WebCryptoAPI] ECDH and ECDSA: test that generated key length is consistent (#61799)\n\nCo-authored-by: Filip Skokan \u003cpanva.ip@gmail.com\u003e\n--\n\nwpt-commits: 4c2fd05ed5d0b90a9e1fcdcb35f6671bd461de0d\nwpt-pr: 61799\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/WebCryptoAPI/generateKey/successes.js"], "git_node": "1f69433126d597c8ea6a8a99ab9f034fdc7b0e06", "git_parents": ["ef37e17a73f6d030e3308eb64c19bb1e0b983260"], "node": "d1a645d3bab4a5e45b4bcafa097688cdec805550", "parents": ["e5b59ed1ffdb72b8828799e6bbcf66c633e5a3fe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "moz-wptsync-bot \u003cwptsync@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061932 - [wpt-sync] Update web-platform-tests to 4c2fd05ed5d0b90a9e1fcdcb35f6671bd461de0d, a=testonly\n\nMANUAL PUSH: wpt sync bot\n\nwpt-head: 4c2fd05ed5d0b90a9e1fcdcb35f6671bd461de0d\nwpt-type: landing\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https.sub.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/margin-padding-clear/margin-right-113.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/selectors/first-letter-punctuation-042.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/selectors/first-letter-punctuation-169.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/CSS2/selectors/first-letter-punctuation-233.xht.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-animations/animation-duration-infinite.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/c