ment per-site association - part 6 - close the tab left behind r=necko-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,nika,jesup,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314887\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp"], "git_node": "16567fa26a999577b33c8b7313552b7c34749c50", "git_parents": ["af74ccc17def85b256bd4e24487e53948260a04e"], "node": "524d4370c947792eed6c063f3a6266a14018c08a", "parents": ["d9d667dba06c49dead7358e2466653327b9c1114"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 7 - tests r=nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313679\n", "files": ["browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_siteContainer.js", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/siteContainer_redirect.sjs", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/siteContainer_sw_intercept.js"], "git_node": "97ce5d1586d8548aad4b2f08c38c2aba0a85a01e", "git_parents": ["16567fa26a999577b33c8b7313552b7c34749c50"], "node": "b5039da504799a7477fc95aa0b119b1f864ff921", "parents": ["524d4370c947792eed6c063f3a6266a14018c08a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060865 - Use UrlbarPrefs instead of Services.prefs in urlbar UI code. r=urlbar-reviewers,mak\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316547\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarPrefs.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SearchModeSwitcher.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs"], "git_node": "14bdbad6bdeb2d39b618649fd8f2c515b59dd2f8", "git_parents": ["97ce5d1586d8548aad4b2f08c38c2aba0a85a01e"], "node": "147191ce1e358f871ea95792752c7a8c9017a72e", "parents": ["b5039da504799a7477fc95aa0b119b1f864ff921"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Moritz Beier \u003cmbeier@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060865 - Use direct import of UrlbarPrefs in SmartbarInput. r=urlbar-reviewers,dao\n\nThis is purely for consistency with UrlbarInput.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317038\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs"], "git_node": "90b2a61d6ea3d67f7fe3cdad98fce8cc1d3834af", "git_parents": ["14bdbad6bdeb2d39b618649fd8f2c515b59dd2f8"], "node": "380a6582addabb5fbb37b96a02af91b10b9d59d7", "parents": ["147191ce1e358f871ea95792752c7a8c9017a72e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 7 - tests r=nika\" for causing build bustages @ BounceTrackingState\n\nThis reverts commit 97ce5d1586d8548aad4b2f08c38c2aba0a85a01e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 6 - close the tab left behind r=necko-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,nika,jesup,dao\"\n\nThis reverts commit 16567fa26a999577b33c8b7313552b7c34749c50.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 5 - Bounce Tracking Protection r=emz\"\n\nThis reverts commit af74ccc17def85b256bd4e24487e53948260a04e.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 4 - plumbing r=necko-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,akulyk,nika,kershaw,sclements,ipc-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit b261e82b2f4b3650e4ef2ce02238466c0ea9274c.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 3 - nsISiteContainerService r=nika\"\n\nThis reverts commit fdd13be7e649ebd2249f7be925f15d271392173b.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 2 - web-ext API r=robwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit eef4cd344e7cbaa6febe8388ae69129d64103a43.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 1 - site association r=robwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit 9337f2922c064d8ddaa83e67a3176542ff9556c1.\n\nRevert \"Bug 2061918 - CookieStore API breaks when used in a service worker running in its own content process, r=valentin,cookie-reviewers\"\n\nThis reverts commit d0394ac3eafd8df0e5ff80b4b13a4d931587550a.\n", "files": ["browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_siteContainer.js", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/siteContainer_redirect.sjs", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/siteContainer_sw_intercept.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreParent.cpp", "dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/test/browser/browser.toml", "netwerk/cookie/test/browser/browser_cookieStore_serviceWorker.js", "netwerk/cookie/test/browser/serviceWorker.js", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.cpp", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/components.conf", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/moz.build", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/nsISiteContainerService.idl", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-contextualIdentities.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/schemas/contextual_identities.json", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_contextual_identities.js"], "git_node": "8f9255f5ece7a493713452c9c0ac070811e76f25", "git_parents": ["90b2a61d6ea3d67f7fe3cdad98fce8cc1d3834af"], "node": "c6f9865b5ff76813156233f96dab111661c1c2c4", "parents": ["380a6582addabb5fbb37b96a02af91b10b9d59d7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062171 - Do not call AdoptBFCacheEntry with a null entry r=smaug\n\nSetActiveSessionHistoryEntry null-checks oldActiveEntry everywhere except the\nAdoptBFCacheEntry call, so on the first active entry of a browsing context the\nNS_ENSURE_STATE in AdoptBFCacheEntry fails, printing a warning and returning an\nerror code the caller discards. Guard the call instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317434\n", "files": ["docshell/base/CanonicalBrowsingContext.cpp"], "git_node": "0a2064c5f0086204cc72445d38949105d50d41e2", "git_parents": ["8f9255f5ece7a493713452c9c0ac070811e76f25"], "node": "4954c955e39c938bee5a84fe8ce7b47fbeb5deea", "parents": ["c6f9865b5ff76813156233f96dab111661c1c2c4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1882163 - Retry removing directory if it fails due to readonly file r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nIt's not clear if this is the cause a small number of users\n(~50 on nightly, ~250K on release) fail to remove the old cache2\nfolders.\n\nThis attempts to retry the removal by after removing the readonly\nattribute from the file.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316623\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheFileIOManager.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-43-purge-residual-folder.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "xpcom/ioutils/IOUtils.h"], "git_node": "fc25bea4e4fcbd4fcba6a96cf964d47d312df80b", "git_parents": ["0a2064c5f0086204cc72445d38949105d50d41e2"], "node": "6a98be34aeb5482c6fa4098ec8c17333e939b78a", "parents": ["4954c955e39c938bee5a84fe8ce7b47fbeb5deea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060419 - Do not trigger essential domain fallbacks for TYPE_DOCUMENT loads r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316490\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_essential_domain_fallback.js"], "git_node": "47445a09895553de619e9fd4ee75921c86e02182", "git_parents": ["fc25bea4e4fcbd4fcba6a96cf964d47d312df80b"], "node": "dcf44b17ab613fa061f078317f54e8532e7640bd", "parents": ["6a98be34aeb5482c6fa4098ec8c17333e939b78a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057073 - Extend networking.residual_cache_folder_* telemetry r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316503\n", "files": ["netwerk/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "cc4326bd268ed530a90e29342e01e289ee33fd78", "git_parents": ["47445a09895553de619e9fd4ee75921c86e02182"], "node": "d9b85fcd33d1d82b4f81513366c16b08e77dc32a", "parents": ["dcf44b17ab613fa061f078317f54e8532e7640bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061918 - CookieStore API breaks when used in a service worker running in its own content process, r=valentin,cookie-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317238\n", "files": ["dom/cookiestore/CookieStoreParent.cpp", "netwerk/cookie/test/browser/browser.toml", "netwerk/cookie/test/browser/browser_cookieStore_serviceWorker.js", "netwerk/cookie/test/browser/serviceWorker.js"], "git_node": "cb3e3eff44fce021b7890da515b03d870a1ba83a", "git_parents": ["cc4326bd268ed530a90e29342e01e289ee33fd78"], "node": "9d18b20db2d55993484abfdd4b3d8945d47e45b3", "parents": ["d9b85fcd33d1d82b4f81513366c16b08e77dc32a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 1 - site association r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310014\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "059da43f0d72e58cc9b5a95c352f379bb4a34e85", "git_parents": ["cb3e3eff44fce021b7890da515b03d870a1ba83a"], "node": "c5008dcb417b533da3b379a3a55c367286f3da9b", "parents": ["9d18b20db2d55993484abfdd4b3d8945d47e45b3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 2 - web-ext API r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310015\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/parent/ext-contextualIdentities.js", "toolkit/components/extensions/schemas/contextual_identities.json", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/test_ext_contextual_identities.js"], "git_node": "03298a1dc3767c31fa6217defa297d2f10c16c96", "git_parents": ["059da43f0d72e58cc9b5a95c352f379bb4a34e85"], "node": "c4e80ff959d0c154658e0f8638ba8e010e5a3334", "parents": ["c5008dcb417b533da3b379a3a55c367286f3da9b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 3 - nsISiteContainerService r=nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310016\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/contextualidentity/ContextualIdentityService.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/components.conf", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/moz.build", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/nsISiteContainerService.idl", "toolkit/components/contextualidentity/tests/unit/test_siteAssociations.js"], "git_node": "4ec84cc280bb2d6f0ce339ca1e010466584bfa22", "git_parents": ["03298a1dc3767c31fa6217defa297d2f10c16c96"], "node": "62af4fb431feadcdcd14cc96680f12552f5e4444", "parents": ["c4e80ff959d0c154658e0f8638ba8e010e5a3334"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 4 - plumbing r=necko-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,akulyk,nika,kershaw,sclements,ipc-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310017\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/ProcessIsolation.cpp", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml", "netwerk/base/nsNetUtil.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp"], "git_node": "907d613967ebf5dc0a5f588652161e7f6ef4e732", "git_parents": ["4ec84cc280bb2d6f0ce339ca1e010466584bfa22"], "node": "390e6fef211a5791f937dd4fbb2185bd84391741", "parents": ["62af4fb431feadcdcd14cc96680f12552f5e4444"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 5 - Bounce Tracking Protection r=emz\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314866\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/BounceTrackingState.cpp"], "git_node": "f85b03f3750d77f58efdafeaaba007dcc1a5ce24", "git_parents": ["907d613967ebf5dc0a5f588652161e7f6ef4e732"], "node": "2e6e7c09878ac1b2d727f4687a36592f28369d15", "parents": ["390e6fef211a5791f937dd4fbb2185bd84391741"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 6 - close the tab left behind r=necko-reviewers,tabbrowser-reviewers,nika,jesup,dao\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314887\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tab.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/content/tabbrowser.js", "netwerk/ipc/DocumentLoadListener.cpp"], "git_node": "0dd0a9628fe8f78056fd83f6d68883d924f0b5bf", "git_parents": ["f85b03f3750d77f58efdafeaaba007dcc1a5ce24"], "node": "69d6b6b80fbd02b8caf377295d193bb806c011f5", "parents": ["2e6e7c09878ac1b2d727f4687a36592f28369d15"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrea Marchesini \u003camarchesini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052136 - Containers: implement per-site association - part 7 - tests r=nika\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313679\n", "files": ["browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/browser_siteContainer.js", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/siteContainer_redirect.sjs", "browser/components/contextualidentity/test/browser/siteContainer_sw_intercept.js"], "git_node": "25df4313d94f4148286391cd92b92d186d24f228", "git_parents": ["0dd0a9628fe8f78056fd83f6d68883d924f0b5bf"], "node": "1a40a111ecfb8ce5f5a64f7a2e55ae724569eb42", "parents": ["69d6b6b80fbd02b8caf377295d193bb806c011f5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062179 - Initialize KeyframeEffect::mKeyframeOffsetsHasRangeOffset and preserve it when copying (Coverity CIDs 1699943, 1699952) r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nThe field had no default member initializer and was set by neither\nconstructor. The copy constructor also cloned aOther.mKeyframes without\ncopying the flag, so a copied effect holding range-based keyframes would\nreport no range offsets and MaybeUpdateKeyframeComputedOffsets() would\nearly-return, never recomputing the offsets against the timeline range.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317426\n", "files": ["dom/animation/KeyframeEffect.cpp", "dom/animation/KeyframeEffect.h"], "git_node": "253ab02db65ebaafa053e59c750b8612e5506a39", "git_parents": ["25df4313d94f4148286391cd92b92d186d24f228"], "node": "163b152b0f167eebf1332a844e1a88bad3a248c0", "parents": ["1a40a111ecfb8ce5f5a64f7a2e55ae724569eb42"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1998984 - Don't set result action labels in the new searchbar. r=mbeier\n\nThe searchbar hid action labels, and the title separator that precedes them,\nfrom a stylesheet it shares with the address bar. Deciding this in the view\nkeeps searchbar-specific rules out of the shared stylesheet and avoids fetching\nstrings that are never shown. The action element itself is still created for\nevery row, so its consumers don't have to handle its absence.\n\nThis should be visually neutral for the searchbar. Worth verifying: with no\naction label a row doesn't get `has-action`, so the pre-existing\n`:not([has-action], [has-url], [restyled-search])` rule is what hides both the\nempty action element and the title separator. That leans on searchbar rows\nnever having a URL, which holds for the providers the searchbar runs.\n\nDynamic rows get their action element, and its text, from the provider's view\ntemplate instead, so `has-action` needs the same gate there; the test covers a\nsearchbar dynamic result whose template declares an action. The address bar and\nthe smartbar keep taking the same path as before, so the change there is a\nno-op.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315046\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_actionLabels.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css"], "git_node": "99576a466e04f1c7b449c699135a182cb42877e2", "git_parents": ["253ab02db65ebaafa053e59c750b8612e5506a39"], "node": "853f6fee963f4098460885be13f48dce04cb150a", "parents": ["163b152b0f167eebf1332a844e1a88bad3a248c0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "nirmaladvani \u003cnirmaladvani@live.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059866 - Fix temporary lock in SharedSection::Reset r=win-reviewers,yjuglaret\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316380\n", "files": ["browser/app/winlauncher/freestanding/SharedSection.cpp"], "git_node": "993dca159dc4c80557eb221d1ce592cd6d1d84eb", "git_parents": ["99576a466e04f1c7b449c699135a182cb42877e2"], "node": "6b1172c6971f1c8f54dc73bfe8cbeb06b241591a", "parents": ["853f6fee963f4098460885be13f48dce04cb150a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1998984 - Don't set result action labels in the new searchbar. r=mbeier\" for causing bc failures at browser_searchbar_actionLabels.js\n\nThis reverts commit 99576a466e04f1c7b449c699135a182cb42877e2.\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_actionLabels.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css"], "git_node": "7b2cdfb9317dd1d230a4894a6a4b5b87478f2526", "git_parents": ["993dca159dc4c80557eb221d1ce592cd6d1d84eb"], "node": "e200fd6c2c8a336c4f61197f2d81ccf3a9ff81d1", "parents": ["6b1172c6971f1c8f54dc73bfe8cbeb06b241591a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "rperta \u003crperta@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1882163 - Retry removing directory if it fails due to readonly file r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\" for causing bc failures at browser_purgeCache_idle_daily.js\n\nThis reverts commit fc25bea4e4fcbd4fcba6a96cf964d47d312df80b.\n", "files": ["netwerk/cache2/CacheFileIOManager.cpp", "netwerk/test/unit/test_cache2-43-purge-residual-folder.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "xpcom/ioutils/IOUtils.h"], "git_node": "2076d07e4e5b5e0873f7b42ac354835879872809", "git_parents": ["7b2cdfb9317dd1d230a4894a6a4b5b87478f2526"], "node": "be8694a73e6d71fc9ee1e57c9cdd38d069dd15f7", "parents": ["e200fd6c2c8a336c4f61197f2d81ccf3a9ff81d1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2052232 - Make onFirstResult a regular controller notification. r=mbeier\n\nUrlbarChild::receiveMessage singled out onQueryResults so it could run the\ninput's onFirstResult content-side and swallow the results when the input took\nthe query over. That rule now lives in one place for both transports: the parent\ncontroller fires onFirstResult as a plain notification (the input registers as a\ncontroller listener for it), and the child controller decides which results\nstill have a consumer.\n\nDeciding that needs an identity for the query, so UrlbarQueryContext gets an id\nthat survives the actor boundary. The child controller keeps the id of the query\nwhose results still have a consumer and drops anything older. When the input\ntakes over -- entering search mode and restarting the query asynchronously --\nthere is no newer query yet to supersede the running one, so discarding its\nresults means moving that mark past it.\n\nBehavior-neutral except on the message path, where results of a query that a\nnewer one had already superseded could still reach the view; they are dropped\nnow.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317062\n", "files": ["browser/actors/UrlbarChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarParentController.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarQueryContext.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/UrlbarTestUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_impressionCaps.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/quicksuggest/unit/test_quicksuggest_merino.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/unit/test_result_highlights.js"], "git_node": "3663c4b6e17f65689b0cb469d669ff8c6be3ad63", "git_parents": ["2076d07e4e5b5e0873f7b42ac354835879872809"], "node": "34c8fb566d14bc7d40217c96289f86a0aa2f4d09", "parents": ["be8694a73e6d71fc9ee1e57c9cdd38d069dd15f7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062075 - Move the pixelSizeFor helpers into android-components. r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nThese wrap a call that every project makes, but they were written in Fenix, so nobody else could reach\nthem. Move them next to the other extensions on the same receivers and leave the behaviour alone; the\nlint check that recommends them stays restricted to Fenix for now.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317360\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/main/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/android/content/Context.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/main/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/android/view/View.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/android/content/ContextTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/ktx/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/ktx/android/view/ViewTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/utils/src/main/java/mozilla/components/support/utils/ext/Fragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/support/utils/src/test/java/mozilla/components/support/utils/ext/FragmentTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/addons/AddonPopupBaseFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/BaseBrowserFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/browser/store/BrowserScreenMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/collections/CollectionsListAdapter.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/menu/MenuDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/ToolbarsIntegration.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/toolbar/gestures/ToolbarHorizontalGesturesHandler.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/Context.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/Fragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ext/View.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/extension/WebExtensionPromptFeature.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/library/history/HistoryFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/PreferenceFragmentExtensions.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/ToolbarShortcutPreference.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/account/AccountSettingsFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/sitepermissions/SitePermissionsManagePhoneFeatureFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/TabManagementFragment.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/Settings.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/utils/ToolbarPopupWindow.kt"], "git_node": "f93be6aa9dd1456bb53c940b44a1424cb9e10b84", "git_parents": ["3663c4b6e17f65689b0cb469d669ff8c6be3ad63"], "node": "e5392fc4c4d9f903085b95ad7e0ccc46940cf01c", "parents": ["34c8fb566d14bc7d40217c96289f86a0aa2f4d09"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062075 - Apply the pixelSizeFor lint check to every Android project. r=android-reviewers,twhite\n\nNow that the helpers live in android-components the check no longer has any reason to only look at Fenix\ncode, so drop the package restriction and convert the call sites it finds elsewhere. Two projects also\ncarried configuration switching the check off, which never did anything because the restriction had\nalready excluded them, so remove that too.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317361\n", "files": ["mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/icons/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/icons/BrowserIcons.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/menu/BrowserMenu.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/menu/view/DynamicWidthRecyclerView.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu2/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/menu2/adapter/DecorativeTextMenuCandidateViewHolder.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/menu2/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/menu2/adapter/icons/DrawableMenuIconViewHolders.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/thumbnails/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/thumbnails/storage/ThumbnailStorage.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/toolbar/BrowserToolbar.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/toolbar/display/OriginView.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/browser/toolbar/src/main/java/mozilla/components/browser/toolbar/edit/EditToolbar.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/feature/app-links/src/main/java/mozilla/components/feature/app/links/SimpleRedirectDialogFragment.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/tooling/lint/src/main/java/mozilla/components/tooling/lint/PixelSizeForDetector.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/tooling/lint/src/test/java/mozilla/components/tooling/lint/PixelSizeForDetectorTest.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/components/ui/tabcounter/src/main/java/mozilla/components/ui/tabcounter/TabCounterView.kt", "mobile/android/android-components/lint.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/lint.xml", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/open/OpenWithFragment.kt", "mobile/android/focus-android/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/focus/shortcut/IconGenerator.kt"], "git_node": "3ab45eaf89cf73cb19e3fd73876c1d47b823edae", "git_parents": ["f93be6aa9dd1456bb53c940b44a1424cb9e10b84"], "node": "82892fefcf7f8553a4add83fb5b33aaf98b2937d", "parents": ["e5392fc4c4d9f903085b95ad7e0ccc46940cf01c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan VanderMeulen \u003crvandermeulen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062108 - Build the win32 onnxruntime toolchain for x86. r=firefox-build-system-reviewers,sylvestre\n\nvs-setup.sh selects the compiler, INCLUDE and LIB from $TARGET, which the x86 task never set, so the\nbuild fell back to the x64 toolchain and shipped a 64-bit onnxruntime.dll to 32-bit Firefox.\nCMAKE_SYSTEM_PROCESSOR has to be set as well, since with Ninja onnxruntime derives its target platform\nfrom it and would otherwise assemble the amd64 MLAS kernels.\n\nbuild.py's --x86 covered neither and is dropped. It only selects a vcpkg triplet, which we do not use,\nand sets a target architecture on the Visual Studio generator path, which Ninja does not take.\n\ndom/onnx loads the library with PR_LoadLibraryWithFlags rather than linking it, so the wrong\narchitecture never broke the build. It surfaced only as a runtime load failure that MLEngineChild\ncaches as \"no native runtime on this machine\", silently falling back to the wasm backend.\n\nEvery build now has a declared expected architecture, and fails if the result does not match or if\nnone is declared. The win64 task passes its architecture explicitly so it is named rather than an\nunlabelled fall-through.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317379\n", "files": ["taskcluster/kinds/toolchain/onnx.yml", "taskcluster/scripts/misc/build-onnxruntime.sh"], "git_node": "93b9fc49b3badf527a361d9721c5d3e5beb021e3", "git_parents": ["3ab45eaf89cf73cb19e3fd73876c1d47b823edae"], "node": "23f70321a2661ed3a0022ffc91c62bf1bc0ecc11", "parents": ["82892fefcf7f8553a4add83fb5b33aaf98b2937d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061027 - Update metadata for clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https.sub.html.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317436\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/clipboard-apis/permissions-policy/clipboard-read/clipboard-read-enabled-by-permissions-policy.tentative.https.sub.html.ini"], "git_node": "4c8823e0bc0f3c98685ac53887e89f8067df9157", "git_parents": ["93b9fc49b3badf527a361d9721c5d3e5beb021e3"], "node": "223836d854e67fd9be419963aa30b6eec6984b26", "parents": ["23f70321a2661ed3a0022ffc91c62bf1bc0ecc11"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049408 - Implement Memories Evolution Step in Scheduler r=cmurray,ai-platform-reviewers,tetchart,thasan,jlewis\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313491\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/Memories.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesSchedulers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesSchedulers.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Memories.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/services/MemoryStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/services/tests/xpcshell/test_MemoryStore.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "cf1cf3341965bf7756542219fec85ec07c4c895c", "git_parents": ["4c8823e0bc0f3c98685ac53887e89f8067df9157"], "node": "c79d7094cda7c74c4d1dd28b9661dee1345b4662", "parents": ["223836d854e67fd9be419963aa30b6eec6984b26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055869 - Check for cycles in AppendChildrenToNewParent tree op r=dom-core-reviewers,hsivonen\n\nA customized built-in element reaction (attributeChangedCallback) can reparent\nthe new parent below one of those children in between, so the append builds a\ncyclic DOM, causing stack exhaustion.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313727\n", "files": ["parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/tests/custom-elements/append-children-to-new-parent-cycle.html"], "git_node": "d37f7da4d11d1dd15f4f3876aade1260d4b55503", "git_parents": ["cf1cf3341965bf7756542219fec85ec07c4c895c"], "node": "8c246057c21dc28f6eecf957b513b4050578b2bf", "parents": ["c79d7094cda7c74c4d1dd28b9661dee1345b4662"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060748 - Add ifdef MOZ_THUNDERBIRD workaround for drag+drop regression. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317105\n", "files": ["widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp"], "git_node": "feb525e6430405759beb4369d09b759b6b7fad10", "git_parents": ["d37f7da4d11d1dd15f4f3876aade1260d4b55503"], "node": "0248cd290208246a03ae162732ef779bd0391a38", "parents": ["8c246057c21dc28f6eecf957b513b4050578b2bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2029965 - Add customelementregistry attribute r=hsivonen\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311862\n", "files": ["dom/xml/nsXMLContentSink.cpp", "parser/html/javasrc/AttributeName.java", "parser/html/nsHtml5AttributeName.cpp", "parser/html/nsHtml5AttributeName.h", "parser/html/nsHtml5TreeOperation.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/scoped-custom-element-registry-customelementregistry-attribute-in-xhtml.xhtml.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/scoped-custom-element-registry-customelementregistry-attribute.html.ini", "xpcom/ds/HTMLAtoms.py"], "git_node": "8080752a00f5f6dc2ea7aa26826cc2f52fb03a85", "git_parents": ["feb525e6430405759beb4369d09b759b6b7fad10"], "node": "44477184b797cd76a4a2343dd20134ad4a5607b8", "parents": ["0248cd290208246a03ae162732ef779bd0391a38"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csledru@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No bug - Suggest pulling from origin/main when the local checkout is stale in AGENTS.md r=ai4dev-reviewers,suhaib DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314973\n", "files": ["AGENTS.md"], "git_node": "2801729c0b930d9d713620a9b4d28e2f892b6808", "git_parents": ["8080752a00f5f6dc2ea7aa26826cc2f52fb03a85"], "node": "6cc3a9fd8d6ab97333d9b4b83a452a42c73596fd", "parents": ["44477184b797cd76a4a2343dd20134ad4a5607b8"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062203 - Guard null popup frame in WaylandPopupGetPositionFromLayout (Coverity CID 1690877) r=stransky,gtk-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317479\n", "files": ["widget/gtk/nsWindowWayland.cpp"], "git_node": "4769777b1a40e2fe2baeef07d5e9230c8f32aff6", "git_parents": ["2801729c0b930d9d713620a9b4d28e2f892b6808"], "node": "0cac2569c871f800afd9c1711627dd1ce322e394", "parents": ["6cc3a9fd8d6ab97333d9b4b83a452a42c73596fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062203 - Guard null primary frame in HTMLInputElement::FinishRangeThumbDrag (Coverity CID 1447443) r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317476\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLInputElement.cpp"], "git_node": "6f44608478eb8e1927cf897b0b42817083d0676d", "git_parents": ["4769777b1a40e2fe2baeef07d5e9230c8f32aff6"], "node": "5614015449b1d5c2da8dece60d355543358296b4", "parents": ["0cac2569c871f800afd9c1711627dd1ce322e394"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Christopher DiPersio \u003ccdipersio@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2049403 - Add Memories Attribute Update on Use r=cmurray,ai-security-reviewers,jlewis,tetchart\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316343\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatConversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatConversation.js"], "git_node": "6bfcc78c4efbcc7156207192f1daa6e9002cfa50", "git_parents": ["6f44608478eb8e1927cf897b0b42817083d0676d"], "node": "19e30516560055fc2a3ea7d8fff52bdb3afe6cdb", "parents": ["5614015449b1d5c2da8dece60d355543358296b4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062204 - Guard browser-parent count against overflow before increment (Coverity CID 1532568) r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nsBrowserParentCount is int32_t, so the \u003c= INT32_MAX assertion was always\ntrue. Use \u003c INT32_MAX so it actually catches overflow before the ++.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317475\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp"], "git_node": "fff856dbc132b369216e1c6ae9886539541dd81f", "git_parents": ["6bfcc78c4efbcc7156207192f1daa6e9002cfa50"], "node": "0e9094edbbdfda6028afc84055744d2fa305c1b2", "parents": ["19e30516560055fc2a3ea7d8fff52bdb3afe6cdb"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062204 - Reject empty plugin version in GMPParent::ParseVersion (Coverity CID 1640424) r=media-playback-reviewers,padenot\n\nAn empty version string yields zero fragments, making the final\nversion \u003c\u003c (4 - 0) * 16 a shift of 64 on a uint64_t (undefined behavior).\nBail out when no fragments were parsed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317473\n", "files": ["dom/media/gmp/GMPParent.cpp"], "git_node": "fd90ef9c023deb5dca35a90d74f78aee945f000d", "git_parents": ["fff856dbc132b369216e1c6ae9886539541dd81f"], "node": "9285a2b5d0e5d82ac449dd54b7b6a47fba500389", "parents": ["0e9094edbbdfda6028afc84055744d2fa305c1b2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062204 - Compute box-shadow spread distance in floating point (Coverity CID 1447688) r=layout-reviewers,dshin\n\nshadowSpread / oneDevPixel divided two nscoord (int) values, truncating\nsub-device-pixel spread to whole pixels before the Float cast, so\nfractional spread was dropped from the rounded-corner clip geometry.\nCast to Float before dividing.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317471\n", "files": ["layout/painting/nsCSSRendering.cpp"], "git_node": "094bd9034f96157834de34e164756dd0693bf072", "git_parents": ["fd90ef9c023deb5dca35a90d74f78aee945f000d"], "node": "e993e8e8e196c6bb339bb1ee1ae9e747b9df38f2", "parents": ["9285a2b5d0e5d82ac449dd54b7b6a47fba500389"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062180 - Null-check TimelineManager before deref in GetNamedProgressTimeline (Coverity CID 1699955) r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\ntimelineManager is null when the document has no pres context. It was\ncorrectly null-checked in the first operand of the condition, but the\nsecond operand, e == aDocument-\u003eGetDocumentElement(), can be true on its\nown and the body then dereferenced it unconditionally.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317427\n", "files": ["layout/style/nsAnimationManager.cpp"], "git_node": "920fb6bb6f574c423bafcf7527f732bbbf199f0d", "git_parents": ["094bd9034f96157834de34e164756dd0693bf072"], "node": "392a1ac714f42a9f67fa374f6c9da89f66bf8e8d", "parents": ["e993e8e8e196c6bb339bb1ee1ae9e747b9df38f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2049403 - Add Memories Attribute Update on Use r=cmurray,ai-security-reviewers,jlewis,tetchart\" for causing conflicts while backing out Bug 2049408\n\nThis reverts commit 6bfcc78c4efbcc7156207192f1daa6e9002cfa50.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/modules/ChatConversation.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/xpcshell/test_ChatConversation.js"], "git_node": "163bb462a1f0fcfc1b589153c5467467fb712d14", "git_parents": ["920fb6bb6f574c423bafcf7527f732bbbf199f0d"], "node": "0f219a735a5040850fb942bd75a3bd9853f9a251", "parents": ["392a1ac714f42a9f67fa374f6c9da89f66bf8e8d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2049408 - Implement Memories Evolution Step in Scheduler r=cmurray,ai-platform-reviewers,tetchart,thasan,jlewis\" for causing bc failures @ browser_MemoriesManager This reverts commit cf1cf3341965bf7756542219fec85ec07c4c895c.\n", "files": ["browser/components/aiwindow/models/Utils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/Memories.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesConstants.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesManager.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/memories/MemoriesSchedulers.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/browser/browser_MemoriesSchedulers.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_Memories.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/models/tests/xpcshell/test_MemoriesManager.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/services/MemoryStore.sys.mjs", "browser/components/aiwindow/services/tests/xpcshell/test_MemoryStore.js", "browser/components/aiwindow/ui/test/browser/head.js"], "git_node": "f086dd5b0a5884115b99a6f0e1af6c8e8c423791", "git_parents": ["163bb462a1f0fcfc1b589153c5467467fb712d14"], "node": "5615760e379d7f4b2885e6cef8898cb45c63f9e6", "parents": ["0f219a735a5040850fb942bd75a3bd9853f9a251"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1998984 - Don't set result action labels in the new searchbar. r=mbeier\n\nThe searchbar hid action labels, and the title separator that precedes them,\nfrom a stylesheet it shares with the address bar. Deciding this in the view\nkeeps searchbar-specific rules out of the shared stylesheet and avoids fetching\nstrings that are never shown. The action element itself is still created for\nevery row, so its consumers don't have to handle its absence.\n\nThis should be visually neutral for the searchbar. Worth verifying: with no\naction label a row doesn't get `has-action`, so the pre-existing\n`:not([has-action], [has-url], [restyled-search])` rule is what hides both the\nempty action element and the title separator. That leans on searchbar rows\nnever having a URL, which holds for the providers the searchbar runs.\n\nDynamic rows get their action element, and its text, from the provider's view\ntemplate instead, so `has-action` needs the same gate there; the test covers a\nsearchbar dynamic result whose template declares an action. The address bar and\nthe smartbar keep taking the same path as before, so the change there is a\nno-op.\n\nReland with a proton fix. Gating `has-action` isn't enough on its own: proton\nscoped the rule that hides the action to\n`\u003e .urlbarView-row-inner \u003e .urlbarView-no-wrap \u003e`, and a dynamic row's action\nelement is attached straight to the row inner by the view template, so the rule\nnever reached it and the template's action text stayed visible. Nova's\nequivalent rule was already a descendant selector; proton now matches it. The\n`#searchbar-new` rule this patch removes was a descendant selector too, which\nis why the gap only opened once it was gone.\n\nNote the local default is nova, so this only reproduces with\n`--setpref browser.nova.enabled=false`.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315046\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/searchbar/browser_searchbar_actionLabels.js", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-nova.css", "browser/themes/shared/urlbar/view-proton.css"], "git_node": "fca1efcadb9d142b1ed274f91011e8d8157fa6b8", "git_parents": ["f086dd5b0a5884115b99a6f0e1af6c8e8c423791"], "node": "1e704c6738f494b411bce8840fcabc790f704e8b", "parents": ["5615760e379d7f4b2885e6cef8898cb45c63f9e6"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786376917, "git_changesets": ["d8a6fae09cac3a413b2b5be0698a4ba914bbcf16