tabs to inactive\" section r=android-reviewers,android-l10n-reviewers,jonalmeida,parker\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317095\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/values/strings.xml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/res/xml/tabs_preferences.xml"], "git_node": "82c59bae4797723a7c15cf5c370df489decb03be", "git_parents": ["d5e85c9f681047547ef0d555c37b7b99c9238cb0"], "node": "d594fd7436110015f86bb0cb7666ce9316780825", "parents": ["9b00bd6166b12b8f7ac569b53d890b82382beb21"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tim Huang \u003ctihuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055973 - Suppress the warning message of nsUrlClassifierRealTimeLookupHandler::StartRealTimeLookup(). r=dimi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315943\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/url-classifier/nsUrlClassifierDBService.cpp"], "git_node": "8e0c8d5be81778fc8d9ccb4c5747bea2c18674eb", "git_parents": ["82c59bae4797723a7c15cf5c370df489decb03be"], "node": "d1d81090795f0685de119738f316ae3dceb1e558", "parents": ["d594fd7436110015f86bb0cb7666ce9316780825"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Olli Pettay \u003cOlli.Pettay@helsinki.fi\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061968 - Remove some legacy GC/CC/Editor/XHR telemetry probes which have glean counterparts, r=chutten\n\nThis is not trying to fix the rather major issue with many glean probes that they don't report content and parent process numbers separately.\nThe old probes used to report that automatically.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317258\n", "files": ["dom/base/CCGCScheduler.cpp", "dom/metrics.yaml", "editor/libeditor/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json", "toolkit/components/telemetry/histogram-allowlists.json", "xpcom/metrics.yaml"], "git_node": "310178e08e06211e68414924d1e03fd3ef92b8ab", "git_parents": ["8e0c8d5be81778fc8d9ccb4c5747bea2c18674eb"], "node": "f3ac4698025a975e8707c5acae13e987343cb6e0", "parents": ["d1d81090795f0685de119738f316ae3dceb1e558"], "tags": []}, {"author": "DonalMe \u003c76789979+DonalMe@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062264 - Change the dry-runs for merge day to run on Wednesday r=releng-reviewers,bhearsum,Eijebong DONTBUILD\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317532\n", "files": [".cron.yml"], "git_node": "0241796683c399847b76c0f5296dd0db11c59d21", "git_parents": ["310178e08e06211e68414924d1e03fd3ef92b8ab"], "node": "f307421cb6290a97c570dcee89461e52a0f57e22", "parents": ["f3ac4698025a975e8707c5acae13e987343cb6e0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Justin Link \u003cjlink@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058361: Deliver image progress notifications per-observer to improve cache locality r=tnikkel\n\nSyncNotifyInternal previously walked the observer list once per progress\nflag, re-resolving each observer's weak reference and re-AddRef'ing each\nproxy and its listener on every pass. On Speedometer 3.1 NewsSite-Next this\nshowed up as a hot, DRAM-bound imgINotificationObserver::AddRef because the\nlistener's cache lines were fetched, evicted, and re-fetched once per flag.\n\nInterchange the loops so we iterate the observers a single time and deliver\nevery notification implied by the progress delta to each observer before\nmoving to the next. Each observer is resolved and refcounted once, and all\nof its notifications land back-to-back while its cache lines are hot. The\nrelative order of notifications delivered to any given observer is unchanged.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315694\n", "files": ["image/ProgressTracker.cpp"], "git_node": "362aa1c3d9a8a2d348b4cbfc9bb8bf27d0db1f4b", "git_parents": ["0241796683c399847b76c0f5296dd0db11c59d21"], "node": "06f2ae15273e3770159441390bfa8ca834056a77", "parents": ["f307421cb6290a97c570dcee89461e52a0f57e22"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nikki Sharpley \u003cnsharpley@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058595 - Fix perma failing browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_sync.js r=skhamis,desktop-theme-reviewers,Juliana\n\nThe failing test revealed an accessibility issue in focusing the undo button in the disabled button. This restructures the buttons to be siblings.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316348\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_sync.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/webext-glue/metrics/runtime-metrics-153.json", "browser/themes/shared/customizableui/panelUI-shared.css"], "git_node": "bf01fb8a81818cfca02171071562eb1c113c2552", "git_parents": ["362aa1c3d9a8a2d348b4cbfc9bb8bf27d0db1f4b"], "node": "a94e1afc968566a8f9f1f877fab9b6cf95669113", "parents": ["06f2ae15273e3770159441390bfa8ca834056a77"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062205 - Guard end-iterator deref in RemoteTextureMap::GetRemoteTexture (Coverity CID 1602334) r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nThe else branch dereferenced the find() result in a MOZ_ASSERT even\nwhen the lookup failed (it == end()). Only assert when the iterator is\nvalid.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317469\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/RemoteTextureMap.cpp"], "git_node": "32efbb5fed1020fb493d2d83cfc3c8a4139fd0e4", "git_parents": ["bf01fb8a81818cfca02171071562eb1c113c2552"], "node": "9bddd564faebfebf45bd3138f30dbfd1a9d1c334", "parents": ["a94e1afc968566a8f9f1f877fab9b6cf95669113"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062207 - Avoid endianness-dependent 64-bit timestamp read in WebGL GetParameter (Coverity CID 1459593) r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nfGetIntegerv wrote a 32-bit GLint into the address of a uint64_t,\nlanding in the wrong half on big-endian. Read into a GLint temporary\nand assign instead.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317467\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/WebGLContextState.cpp"], "git_node": "2678e723dabcb7d98c6c89ef9b4b687674fe3e73", "git_parents": ["32efbb5fed1020fb493d2d83cfc3c8a4139fd0e4"], "node": "7599a6127a50df5a34437af2f27e5a3f17f715e4", "parents": ["9bddd564faebfebf45bd3138f30dbfd1a9d1c334"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew Halberstadt \u003cahal@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2033838 - Add head_git_repository to remaining test params, r=taskgraph-reviewers,releng-reviewers,bhearsum\n\nThis param is set via the per-project parameters in decision.py.\nTherefore we should add it to any test param that references one of\nthose projects.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317113\n", "files": ["taskcluster/test/params/autoland-cron-android-l10n-import.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/autoland-cron-l10n-bumper.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/autoland-onpush-backstop.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/autoland-onpush.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-promote-android.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-promote-devedition-partials.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-promote-devedition.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-promote-firefox-partials.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-promote-firefox.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-push-android.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-push-devedition.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-push-firefox-partials.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-push-firefox.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-ship-android.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-ship-devedition.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-ship-firefox-partials.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-ship-firefox.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mb-to-release-merge-automation.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mc-android-nightly.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mc-bump-main-merge-automation.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mc-cron-system-symbols.yml", "taskcluster/test/params/mc-des