d8697593f679b4ed8ba864a33e91336891", "ed892d0b5aa12553516ffb7bad106487a2e60dad", "f11e4b9775b2d823603bd48d510aeefe0631a5c2", "470cbd2f15141751671756268066ffc3c791d27b", "cd138927aae91bf4e89e3ee676b496c4c1da2aaf", "85130ba192d9f4bdf63e57502cb23fb31f95f7ca"], "user": "sstanca@mozilla.com"}, "45070": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging ee9f2b2aedc3c58347d66ca8d7b9f92ef1df3f53 with FIREFOX_140_14_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "59ea4a5c7538b88878e3e47cd9e4db83793e9693", "git_parents": ["f3f9ea76c92fb90bbbb5157144908eb099a1931c"], "node": "82f4ac5f446631fa67bbe94e19ab864e0e793eaa", "parents": ["7a7d4e52e6b8f59850c6d7ff18970a1f67153ed3"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786488595, "git_changesets": ["59ea4a5c7538b88878e3e47cd9e4db83793e9693"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45071": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@lando.moz.tools\u003e", "branch": "tags-unified", "desc": "No bug - Tagging bdb74c45c2e1e3fe593fbf3c5ca6d2ab2046ef08 with FIREFOX_153_1_0esr_BUILD1 a=tagging CLOSED TREE DONTBUILD", "files": [".hgtags"], "git_node": "949294dd653999b876f1ca77531e88e46ba0c723", "git_parents": ["59ea4a5c7538b88878e3e47cd9e4db83793e9693"], "node": "9115a99ccd6afface83db6ea44239ae4cdd2af9e", "parents": ["82f4ac5f446631fa67bbe94e19ab864e0e793eaa"], "tags": []}], "date": 1786490327, "git_changesets": ["949294dd653999b876f1ca77531e88e46ba0c723"], "user": "ffxbld@lando.moz.tools"}, "45072": {"changesets": [{"author": "Matthew Gaudet \u003cmgaudet@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060082 - Contain blast radius of failures after MacroAssembler OOM during code-generation r=iain\n\nLet's say you OOM while you're code-generating instruction A, no point in trying to code-generate\ninstruction B which follows, doubly so if you trip an assertion which was only violated\nbecause of OOM earlier.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317676\n", "files": ["js/src/jit/CodeGenerator.cpp"], "git_node": "99345c6a1e381c41522adce8e7cd49c823145d99", "git_parents": ["cd138927aae91bf4e89e3ee676b496c4c1da2aaf"], "node": "0e2fc567670ec0496c214a232cdf4d90938d38f4", "parents": ["67d10c3a9b5979e72544b61df9a240a95ab19f26"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062330 - Keep a cancel from suppressing a running query's results. r=daleharvey\n\nBug 2060933 held a query back until the engine store is populated and made\ncancelQuery bump the query id, so a held-back query wouldn't be dispatched after\nthe fact. But that id is also what notify() filters results by, and a cancel\nsays nothing about the query those results belong to: the view cancels for\nreasons of its own, one of them being that it closes when a superseded query\nreports finished. On the message path the live query's results are in flight by\nthen, so they get dropped and the view never opens -- reopening the view right\nafter a blur hangs, perma-failing\nbrowser_glean_telemetry_abandonment_groups.js on the tier-2 uipc variant.\n\nSo the gate gets its own flag and the id goes back to meaning only what it did\nbefore: which query the results still have a consumer for. The gate had no test\nof its own; the new one pins it.\n\nWorth knowing: the view still closes on a superseded query's QUERY_FINISHED,\nsince notify() filters results only -- Bug 2062284. Reopening here rides on the\nlive query's results already being in flight, so that fix would mask this one;\nthe cancel shouldn't poison the filter either way.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317610\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-search/browser_engineStoreQueryGate.js"], "git_node": "ff845bb1673e7181650c6e49f5dd023630a09d0a", "git_parents": ["99345c6a1e381c41522adce8e7cd49c823145d99"], "node": "f8a69b3923405c1bbcd886e75748a77af83bd91e", "parents": ["0e2fc567670ec0496c214a232cdf4d90938d38f4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062284 - Keep a superseded query's end from reaching the view. r=daleharvey\n\nBug 2052232 taught the child controller to drop the result notifications of a\nquery older than the one it last started. That query's end still gets through,\nand the view reads it against state the dropped results never filled: having\nseen no results for the query, onQueryFinished concludes it produced nothing,\ncloses the view, and so cancels the query that superseded it. Over the message\npath the parent runs a round trip behind, so a query the input has already\nreplaced routinely still has an end to report. onQueryCancelled shields the view\nfrom it, but only while that query is still running; one that completed on its\nown reports straight to a view tracking a newer query, and the address bar goes\nquiet until the next keystroke.\n\nOnly the end is dropped. The rest of the lifecycle carries the per-query state\nthe listeners reset, and the newer query resets it again when it starts.\nWithholding QUERY_STARTED as well would leave the view's \"this query produced\nresults\" flag set from the previous query, which mis-steers that same\nonQueryFinished branch and, through it, exposure telemetry.\n\nDropping the end does leave that query's stale-row timer armed, and firing it\nboth removes stale rows and accepts tentative exposures, so arming the timer now\ncancels any outlived one.\n\nWorth checking: superseded is keyed on the last query started here, not on the\nmark below it, which the input also moves when it discards the running query's\nresults. That query is still the one the listeners track, so it still has to see\nits own end -- Bug 2062366 covers the view acting on that end before the input's\nrestart lands.\n\nThe test drives the notifications directly rather than racing the transport, so\nit covers both paths.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317634\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarView.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_supersededQueryNotifications.js"], "git_node": "50b01df111ae760dee9964992b1bfaa64278b05e", "git_parents": ["ff845bb1673e7181650c6e49f5dd023630a09d0a"], "node": "0f5ec75b2252ebdfaf25740cdbca01dc32073c6b", "parents": ["f8a69b3923405c1bbcd886e75748a77af83bd91e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048793 - Use CheckLoadURIWithPrincipal before loading object/embed content. r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317041\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsObjectLoadingContent.cpp"], "git_node": "e99d23fb258f75e2b88ae715847d1d0bb67ab6c9", "git_parents": ["50b01df111ae760dee9964992b1bfaa64278b05e"], "node": "2baf72dba83ae727b8bfff3adfad078d74b13091", "parents": ["0f5ec75b2252ebdfaf25740cdbca01dc32073c6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048793 - Use CheckLoadURIWithPrincipal for client.navigate(). r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317042\n", "files": ["dom/clients/manager/ClientNavigateOpChild.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/service-workers/service-worker/windowclient-navigate.https.html.ini"], "git_node": "b1810fa41e41d639632815054d7ad7a2cb81c54b", "git_parents": ["e99d23fb258f75e2b88ae715847d1d0bb67ab6c9"], "node": "b2b8cd5fecf65fad300554fcb73bf9c905be480e", "parents": ["2baf72dba83ae727b8bfff3adfad078d74b13091"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2048793 - Check more URLs in nsDocShellLoadState. r=nika,Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D312495\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/tabs/browser_new_tab_in_privilegedabout_process_pref.js", "docshell/base/nsDocShellLoadState.cpp", "docshell/test/browser/browser_browsing_context_discarded.js"], "git_node": "6ad4f1d17c396be61a017272a496add3910e7d4b", "git_parents": ["b1810fa41e41d639632815054d7ad7a2cb81c54b"], "node": "12f0ef62c249140593c60c461f1c46d5c3773aa9", "parents": ["b2b8cd5fecf65fad300554fcb73bf9c905be480e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jamie Nicol \u003cjnicol@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062579 - Report unity-webgl subtest results as higher-is-better scores. r=perftest-reviewers,kshampur\n\nRather than incorrectly reporting them as lower-is-better millisecond\ndurations.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317782\n", "files": ["testing/perfdocs/generated/raptor.md", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/benchmarks/unity-webgl-desktop.toml", "testing/raptor/raptor/tests/benchmarks/unity-webgl-mobile.toml"], "git_node": "9991d18fdd849843918ab34f343453699e0769a8", "git_parents": ["6ad4f1d17c396be61a017272a496add3910e7d4b"], "node": "b46dd0d45710224a22c5419e544e349b12b3b625", "parents": ["12f0ef62c249140593c60c461f1c46d5c3773aa9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ted Campbell \u003ctcampbell@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2044409 - Filter slider updates while Accessibility shouldUseAutoSize is false r=ohall\n\nThe engine code doesn't allow setting a fontSizeFactor when auto-sizing is enabled. We previously tried to disable the Slider that updates the size factor in order to prevent update messages, but the disable doesn't take effect until next recomposition. As a result we see crashes in monkey testing which adds noise even if it is highly unlikely for a normal user to hit.\n\nPull request: https://github.com/mozilla-firefox/firefox/pull/325\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/settings/AccessibilityFragment.kt"], "git_node": "28ea41d95d545fc0f2d10928c0589ca37099364e", "git_parents": ["9991d18fdd849843918ab34f343453699e0769a8"], "node": "4b0e791613a4ac2204d6da26dcf77f6a24ef22b7", "parents": ["b46dd0d45710224a22c5419e544e349b12b3b625"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060903 - Move the urlbar tip-type enums to UrlbarShared. r=daleharvey\n\nA behavior-neutral move of the two tip-type enums, so that code which has to\nrun in a content process can name a tip type without importing a provider.\nUrlbarShared is the single source of truth: the providers don't re-export the\nenums, and their consumers name them where they are defined.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317580\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderInterventions.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarProviderSearchTips.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/UrlbarUtils.sys.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_interventions.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_searchTips.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_searchTips_interaction.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_updateAsk.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_updateRefresh.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_updateRestart.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/browser_updateWeb.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/head.js", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser-tips/suppress-tips/browser_suppressTips.js"], "git_node": "6e31889d917bee4559c04dfd33736f3adfd17491", "git_parents": ["28ea41d95d545fc0f2d10928c0589ca37099364e"], "node": "4d91b51cc41cb6c6bba5670aa47842878f1102bd", "parents": ["4b0e791613a4ac2204d6da26dcf77f6a24ef22b7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Diego Escalante \u003cdescalante@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059278 - Invalidate style container queries that use units dependent on writing mode axis. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317140\n", "files": ["servo/components/style/data.rs", "servo/components/style/invalidation/element/restyle_hints.rs", "servo/components/style/matching.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/cascade.rs", "servo/components/style/properties/computed_value_flags.rs", "servo/components/style/stylesheets/container_rule.rs", "servo/components/style/values/specified/length.rs", "testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-conditional/container-queries/style-query-registered-custom-root-relative-units-change.html.ini"], "git_node": "740f4a1e8c755a629bc8d2673769dd28c1d7f342", "git_parents": ["6e31889d917bee4559c04dfd33736f3adfd17491"], "node": "db7d667eaf10b02e38898ed46db62205c201840f", "parents": ["4d91b51cc41cb6c6bba5670aa47842878f1102bd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Support ping test callbacks across JS and C++, including artifact builds r=TravisLong,chumphreys\n\nInstead of storing ping test callbacks by id, store them by name.\nIt means that on every call to Submit on a C++ Ping object, we do a\nlinear scan of all ping names. But at time of writing there are only 48\nof them, so this is fast enough.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D314766\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/bindings/GleanPings.cpp", "toolkit/components/glean/bindings/private/Ping.cpp", "toolkit/components/glean/bindings/private/Ping.h", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/js_pings.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/js_pings_h.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/docs/user/instrumentation_tests.md", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/xpcshell/test_JOG.js"], "git_node": "e6b2150e330e5bf9a1392590a18d5b733b977b7c", "git_parents": ["740f4a1e8c755a629bc8d2673769dd28c1d7f342"], "node": "6b8ba46f200891a08688b8ae4173b41c485a0166", "parents": ["db7d667eaf10b02e38898ed46db62205c201840f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Unskip browser_page_load_event_telemetry.js in artifact builds now that JS tests of C++ ping submission work r=robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315074\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser_page_load_event_telemetry.js"], "git_node": "cc92d16f2b1e940bda30633ed602737eab8a4cd9", "git_parents": ["e6b2150e330e5bf9a1392590a18d5b733b977b7c"], "node": "4a7b9cec06cb0db2825bd064da28c8076938ecc4", "parents": ["6b8ba46f200891a08688b8ae4173b41c485a0166"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - unskip test_fog_complex_object_works, test_labeled_metrics_test_get_value_works in artifact r=chumphreys\n\nThey both now work!\n(The former since bug 1883857, the latter since Glean SDK v67.2.0)\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315075\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/glean/tests/xpcshell/test_Glean.js"], "git_node": "a00fe709e4bb69b276eb9de888cc5fa93e84e44d", "git_parents": ["cc92d16f2b1e940bda30633ed602737eab8a4cd9"], "node": "30784c44f9a8ed8cbc263b937c9fc18d36fd0edd", "parents": ["4a7b9cec06cb0db2825bd064da28c8076938ecc4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js, test_UsageReporting.js on artifact as they now work r=gstoll\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315076\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "38e44362a60e442d351500f0d936637934cf75ca", "git_parents": ["a00fe709e4bb69b276eb9de888cc5fa93e84e44d"], "node": "1ea5b9a9c9940b22b2878947d855758bb9755fff", "parents": ["30784c44f9a8ed8cbc263b937c9fc18d36fd0edd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_new_profile.js, test_new_profile_ping_sent.js on artifact as they now work r=dmcintosh,jhirsch\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315077\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_new_profile.js", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "ccaafcbc941ce9eac04215d8acb7a3bc3eb8e011", "git_parents": ["38e44362a60e442d351500f0d936637934cf75ca"], "node": "b4c91339ea9a3e0c6ba02f83f68b050d7a76fd6b", "parents": ["1ea5b9a9c9940b22b2878947d855758bb9755fff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_content_decoding_error_telemetry.js on artifact because it is now supported r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315086\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "77a01dfb1f3f9fd8624192a85b91fd123c3248ff", "git_parents": ["ccaafcbc941ce9eac04215d8acb7a3bc3eb8e011"], "node": "90842aef3497aef9229622937c630b5ec53b108b", "parents": ["b4c91339ea9a3e0c6ba02f83f68b050d7a76fd6b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Unskip child_cause_hang.js on artifact because it is now supported r=florian\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315087\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/backgroundhangmonitor/tests/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "3e2692580ffe212c50db332de8422eb59588b497", "git_parents": ["77a01dfb1f3f9fd8624192a85b91fd123c3248ff"], "node": "e20a97a87501fdcc59a28b32d27f9b8079016a8b", "parents": ["90842aef3497aef9229622937c630b5ec53b108b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Chris H-C \u003cchutten@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_ext_urlclassifier on artifact because it is now supported r=extension-reviewers,robwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315088\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "58d8be611352f564f69d1dcea12322393d58f472", "git_parents": ["3e2692580ffe212c50db332de8422eb59588b497"], "node": "c54f62ec14e1e15299506a961d60c38c1d405b55", "parents": ["e20a97a87501fdcc59a28b32d27f9b8079016a8b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1575369 - Consume the sidebar panel load message in browser_ext_sidebarAction_incognito.js and re-enable it, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nsidebar_action.open_at_install defaults to true, so installing the test extension\nmakes sidebarAction's build() call SidebarController.show() in the already open\nnon-private window. The panel loads and sends a \"sidebar\" message that this test,\nunlike every other browser_ext_sidebarAction*.js test, never consumed. The\nmessage was therefore still queued when the file-level cleanup in\nExtensionTestUtils asserts the message queue is empty.\n\nWait for that message and assert the sidebar really is open in the non-private\nwindow, so the now-meaningful empty-queue assertion also covers the case that\nmatters for this test: the private window must not load the extension panel.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317517\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser-sidebar.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_sidebarAction_incognito.js"], "git_node": "2f3265d7e92db9a81f158c6588d3a7301e6fd40e", "git_parents": ["58d8be611352f564f69d1dcea12322393d58f472"], "node": "16d3e49e25d8ce27f3d14f179ca96697591409f6", "parents": ["c54f62ec14e1e15299506a961d60c38c1d405b55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Florian Qu\u00e8ze \u003cflorian@queze.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062187 - Wait for the extension popup's content to be focused before clicking in browser_ext_autocompletepopup.js, and re-enable the test, r=extension-reviewers,rpl.\n\nA click only opens an input's datalist popup when the input is already\nfocused (nsFormFillController::MouseDown -\u003e ShowPopup does nothing until\nfocusin has made the input the controlled element). The test relied on its\nfirst synthesized click doing the focusing, but the focus of a freshly\nopened popup panel's browser reaches the extension process asynchronously:\nwhen the two clicks are dispatched before it arrives, neither opens the\npopup and the test hangs on promisePopupShown until it times out.\n\nWait for content focus in testDatalist, as the about:addons case already\ndid.\n\nThe test was disabled outright by `disabled = \"bug 1438663\"`, which names\nthe same focus race in a different file; that race is what this fixes, so\nthe annotation goes.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317518\n", "files": ["browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/extensions/test/browser/browser_ext_autocompletepopup.js"], "git_node": "8616b3b29121ab3964099d398319a766b09bd11f", "git_parents": ["2f3265d7e92db9a81f158c6588d3a7301e6fd40e"], "node": "93ec75696ffd0c164e6ba09c5834b6d37801ffb6", "parents": ["16d3e49e25d8ce27f3d14f179ca96697591409f6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2018913 - Part 1: Add ImportNodeOptions dictionary and cross-document registry validation for importNode r=dom-core-reviewers,webidl,edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313455\n", "files": ["dom/base/CustomElementRegistry.cpp", "dom/base/CustomElementRegistry.h", "dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/base/Document.h", "dom/base/DocumentOrShadowRoot.cpp", "dom/base/DocumentOrShadowRoot.h", "dom/base/Element.cpp", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.cpp", "dom/base/ShadowRoot.h", "dom/base/nsINode.cpp", "dom/base/nsINode.h", "dom/webidl/Document.webidl", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/CustomElementRegistry-upgrade.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/Document-importNode-cross-document.window.js.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/Document-importNode.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/Element-innerHTML.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/custom-elements/registries/global.window.js.ini"], "git_node": "eff4a4960f500febf54e8b3f24c6343eda51505d", "git_parents": ["8616b3b29121ab3964099d398319a766b09bd11f"], "node": "804f268a054c10aa8174cbf2dbea374df8412179", "parents": ["93ec75696ffd0c164e6ba09c5834b6d37801ffb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Vincent Hilla \u003cvhilla@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062584 - Remove Telemetry for ScreenWakeLock. r=dom-core-reviewers,TravisLong,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317793\n", "files": ["dom/power/WakeLockSentinel.cpp", "dom/power/WakeLockSentinel.h", "dom/power/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/glean/metrics_index.py", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "a628b0c0e23f7f76c03e578a6d920ba90abee8ce", "git_parents": ["eff4a4960f500febf54e8b3f24c6343eda51505d"], "node": "88b02c3820d4727973e3d13cba7e201a13c14db2", "parents": ["804f268a054c10aa8174cbf2dbea374df8412179"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Cosmin Sabou \u003ccsabou@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_ext_urlclassifier on artifact because it is now supported r=extension-reviewers,robwu\" for causing failures on test_glean_parser_js.\n\nThis reverts commit 58d8be611352f564f69d1dcea12322393d58f472.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - Unskip child_cause_hang.js on artifact because it is now supported r=florian\"\n\nThis reverts commit 3e2692580ffe212c50db332de8422eb59588b497.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_content_decoding_error_telemetry.js on artifact because it is now supported r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\"\n\nThis reverts commit 77a01dfb1f3f9fd8624192a85b91fd123c3248ff.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_new_profile.js, test_new_profile_ping_sent.js on artifact as they now work r=dmcintosh,jhirsch\"\n\nThis reverts commit ccaafcbc941ce9eac04215d8acb7a3bc3eb8e011.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - Unskip test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js, test_UsageReporting.js on artifact as they now work r=gstoll\"\n\nThis reverts commit 38e44362a60e442d351500f0d936637934cf75ca.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - unskip test_fog_complex_object_works, test_labeled_metrics_test_get_value_works in artifact r=chumphreys\"\n\nThis reverts commit a00fe709e4bb69b276eb9de888cc5fa93e84e44d.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - Unskip browser_page_load_event_telemetry.js in artifact builds now that JS tests of C++ ping submission work r=robwu\"\n\nThis reverts commit cc92d16f2b1e940bda30633ed602737eab8a4cd9.\n\nRevert \"Bug 1974314 - Support ping test callbacks across JS and C++, including artifact builds r=TravisLong,chumphreys\"\n\nThis reverts commit e6b2150e330e5bf9a1392590a18d5b733b977b7c.\n", "files": ["dom/base/test/browser_page_load_event_telemetry.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/backgroundhangmonitor/tests/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/extensions/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/components/glean/bindings/GleanPings.cpp", "toolkit/components/glean/bindings/private/Ping.cpp", "toolkit/components/glean/bindings/private/Ping.h", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/js_pings.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/build_scripts/glean_parser_ext/templates/js_pings_h.jinja2", "toolkit/components/glean/docs/user/instrumentation_tests.md", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/xpcshell/test_Glean.js", "toolkit/components/glean/tests/xpcshell/test_JOG.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_ThirdPartyModulesPing.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/test_new_profile.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/tests/unit/xpcshell.toml", "toolkit/profile/test/xpcshell/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "004e28be6b64750350e4a48d350bd7024013b7a8", "git_parents": ["a628b0c0e23f7f76c03e578a6d920ba90abee8ce"], "node": "6aeff52a896ef71ef4f54e3f03ab64657a7158a3", "parents": ["88b02c3820d4727973e3d13cba7e201a13c14db2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061801 - Get principal from dragContent if it doesn't come from a remote process. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317134\n", "files": ["dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "dom/ipc/BrowserParent.cpp", "widget/nsDragServiceProxy.cpp"], "git_node": "8da281da3beb7f604c8557af67816d97dcaf6100", "git_parents": ["004e28be6b64750350e4a48d350bd7024013b7a8"], "node": "b17d58776a0721ac008cba431fceaf126fe461bf", "parents": ["6aeff52a896ef71ef4f54e3f03ab64657a7158a3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Jakobi \u003cajakobi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021952 - Report an APZC scrolled by a handed-off gesture as being in a scrolling gesture. r=hiro,botond,layout-reviewers\n\nWhen a scroll gesture is handed off to an ancestor APZC, the repaint\nrequests of the actually-scrolling ancestor carried\nmIsInScrollingGesture=false, so the main thread would re-snap it\nmid-gesture. Track the handoff in a new mScrolledByHandedOffGesture flag,\nclear it on the whole handoff chain when the gesture ends, and include the\nflag in the repaint request deduplication so flag-only changes reach the\nmain thread.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310837\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/InputBlockState.h", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/src/OverscrollHandoffState.h"], "git_node": "ac087e3220d3d2d10e880bd55123fbe577f9aa4f", "git_parents": ["8da281da3beb7f604c8557af67816d97dcaf6100"], "node": "99c78106228f1ab3b6b8a2b21da76adc986506ce", "parents": ["b17d58776a0721ac008cba431fceaf126fe461bf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Jakobi \u003cajakobi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021952 - Consider scrolling gesture state for early return when requesting content repaint r=hiro,botond\n\nRequestContentRepaint() early-returns when the request being built matches\nthe last painted metrics, to avoid sending redundant repaints. The dedup\ncomparison did not include IsInScrollingGesture(), so a request that differs\nfrom the previous one only in its scrolling-gesture flag was dropped and the\nmain thread never learned the gesture state had changed.\n\nAdd IsInScrollingGesture() to the comparison so a flag-only transition (in\nparticular the gesture-end true-\u003efalse transition) is no longer swallowed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D306183\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/src/AsyncPanZoomController.cpp", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/APZTestCommon.h", "gfx/layers/apz/test/gtest/TestPanning.cpp"], "git_node": "5c5dc848e545f04b3216a283288ad56680b84dc8", "git_parents": ["ac087e3220d3d2d10e880bd55123fbe577f9aa4f"], "node": "3b60ec2d45a0c45233d41cda714bac1e4cd3cc82", "parents": ["99c78106228f1ab3b6b8a2b21da76adc986506ce"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Jakobi \u003cajakobi@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2021952 - Add a mochitest for not re-snapping an ancestor scroll container during a handed-off pan gesture. r=ajakobi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D309496\n", "files": ["gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/helper_scroll_snap_not_resnap_on_descendant_overflow_change.html", "gfx/layers/apz/test/mochitest/test_group_scroll_snap.html"], "git_node": "b48764995b13e8210943a7a55678447046f8c506", "git_parents": ["5c5dc848e545f04b3216a283288ad56680b84dc8"], "node": "f2d7361473823429c51ef4e7b564ee15cd62144b", "parents": ["3b60ec2d45a0c45233d41cda714bac1e4cd3cc82"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061864 - Measure how often we recover from a stale tab drag. r=tabbrowser-reviewers,nsharpley\n\nThe reports behind this bug are spread over three platform bugs and a pile of\nduplicates, none of which say how common the broken state actually is. Counting\nrecoveries does, and since the counter rides the same ping as client_info and\ngfx.linux_window_protocol, it splits by OS and by Wayland vs X11 for free.\n\nThe labels keep the causes apart, which matters because they call for different\nfixes: a drag session that outlived its drag, where the user has to click before\nanything recovers; a session that was already gone while moving-tab mode stayed\non, which the watchdog clears within a second; and, in the _after_drop variants,\na drop that did reach us whose animation left moving-tab mode stuck, which is\nours to fix and would otherwise inflate the platform numbers.\n\nWorth checking: the drop deadline is cleared when moving-tab mode ends, so a\ncompleted drop can't get the next drag labelled _after_drop. The third test\ncovers that and fails without the reset. It overrides the reduced motion media\nquery rather than gReduceMotion, because the drop waits on a transition the\nstylesheet only defines under no-preference, and overriding only the script side\nleaves the drop waiting for a transition that never runs.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317761\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/content/drag-and-drop.js", "browser/components/tabbrowser/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_stale_drag_session.js"], "git_node": "9cede4ecf1bd33b0f32a84c1d5b7d20025fd0df5", "git_parents": ["b48764995b13e8210943a7a55678447046f8c506"], "node": "3fd2494e5c5bfc721d09a094eae3b4c89dbde54d", "parents": ["f2d7361473823429c51ef4e7b564ee15cd62144b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandra Borovova \u003caborovova@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061955 - Enable \"layout.css.grid-subgrid-baselines.enabled\" preference for css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/ tests. r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317492\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/meta/css/css-grid/grid-lanes/subgrid/grid-subgridded-to-grid-lanes/baseline/__dir__.ini"], "git_node": "8897b191941499c45ba5f4cfa9908a23afcf2cb0", "git_parents": ["9cede4ecf1bd33b0f32a84c1d5b7d20025fd0df5"], "node": "2bebae8151b8f43db0b6d5dc86fce2a97014406f", "parents": ["3fd2494e5c5bfc721d09a094eae3b4c89dbde54d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053068 - Don't dim titlebar text when inactive r=Dre,emilio,desktop-theme-reviewers,hjones\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316711\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_tokens.scss", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/nova/tokens-figma-theme.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-platform.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/dist/tokens-shared.css", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/nova-export-clean-variables.json", "toolkit/themes/shared/design-system/src/tokens/components/toolbox.nova.tokens.json"], "git_node": "e178d7d42c58a8191719e893b82a3d4a4d147954", "git_parents": ["8897b191941499c45ba5f4cfa9908a23afcf2cb0"], "node": "4adc03b1cddf486b7cde52dbecc321afa049844c", "parents": ["2bebae8151b8f43db0b6d5dc86fce2a97014406f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Striemer \u003cmstriemer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053746 - Fix touch padding in the toolbar r=desktop-theme-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D3167