eba324eadb33c553d772b008d73"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Zoya \u003czfatima@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053832 - updated nav3 version and make tabgroup key use lastEntry r=android-reviewers,jdelorenzo\n\nAdded tests for checking unique keys\nAdded equals and hashCode, as Scene.kt requires and as DialogScene and SinglePaneScene do. With a test to csonfirm\nrebased\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317081\n", "files": ["gradle/libs.versions.toml", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/compose/navigation/BottomSheetScene.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/compose/navigation/BottomSheetSceneStrategyTest.kt"], "git_node": "0c5136e1f6cf1e090de58f5c9a419c0d647dc5f6", "git_parents": ["07acc85a743a10c90489276fa6e3358ea1a53a9e"], "node": "a29ea7b5185de7376101de7bff6cabd4094c28fd", "parents": ["f4aa4d6782c7832157f3662c54b4a22f73994728"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062621 - Add fallback shim for Add/Edit dialog background color. r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317844\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/styles/nova/_TopSites.scss"], "git_node": "15cbd388feda8aeb143c5c5393f5a146a60fc67d", "git_parents": ["0c5136e1f6cf1e090de58f5c9a419c0d647dc5f6"], "node": "7151679b8deb9bf34ff10cb762a50c6dd482b08b", "parents": ["a29ea7b5185de7376101de7bff6cabd4094c28fd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Thayer \u003cdothayer@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062358 - Remove SCRIPT_PRELOADER_REQUESTS probe r=arai,chutten\n\nI am not familiar with anyone caring about this probe, so I'm filing\nthis to remove this. I'm also looking for input as to whether we\nshould just remove the related probes for wait time and mainthread\nrecompile.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317680\n", "files": ["js/xpconnect/loader/ScriptPreloader.cpp", "js/xpconnect/metrics.yaml", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "e0c04d5775c5edced6839c9a316c8eeab0428c0b", "git_parents": ["15cbd388feda8aeb143c5c5393f5a146a60fc67d"], "node": "a2e762e3aee4d48ddba5a5eb12cbe1f12d968dd5", "parents": ["7151679b8deb9bf34ff10cb762a50c6dd482b08b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060788 - Test that Happy Eyeballs revalidates a stale DNS answer r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nSeed a short-TTL A record by driving one connection through Happy\nEyeballs, let it age into the grace period, then answer the name with a\nworking address. The stale address is raced first and its connection is\nrefused; Happy Eyeballs revalidates with a cache-bypassing lookup, races\nthe address that comes back, and the request succeeds on it.\n\nServing a stale entry also makes the resolver renew it in the\nbackground, and that renewal alone is enough to reach the working\naddress: it updates the shared host record, so a lookup landing after it\nsees the new address, and the test would pass with or without the\nrevalidation. DNS therefore goes through the TRR server, whose answers\ncan be delayed: the revalidated answer is held back until Happy Eyeballs\nhas consumed the stale one and failed to connect to it. TRR_ONLY mode\nkeeps native resolution, which answers 127.0.0.1 for everything in TRR\ntests, out of the picture as well.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317011\n", "files": ["netwerk/test/unit/test_happy_eyeballs_optimistic_dns.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "e89e5e69b9fbea67dff91b4a57dbafd4214f46ef", "git_parents": ["e0c04d5775c5edced6839c9a316c8eeab0428c0b"], "node": "e59249982dd28be0d560a6a1f7eecf3fa42cc042", "parents": ["a2e762e3aee4d48ddba5a5eb12cbe1f12d968dd5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060788 - Revalidate stale DNS answers in Happy Eyeballs r=necko-reviewers,kershaw\n\nFirefox already serves DNS answers from a cache entry's grace period\n(stale-while-revalidate). This teaches Happy Eyeballs to notice when an\nanswer was served stale and race it immediately while revalidating with\na fresh, cache-bypassing lookup, then race the revalidated answer too.\n\n- Expose nsIDNSAddrRecord::fromStaleCache and\n  nsIDNSByTypeRecord::fromStaleCache, both backed by nsHostRecord's\n  existing grace-period check (CheckExpiration == EXP_GRACE), rather than\n  reasoning from the record's ttl and lastUpdate: lastUpdate only moves\n  when the address set changes, so a repeatedly refreshed but stable host\n  would otherwise look perpetually stale. The check lives on the shared\n  nsHostRecord base, so AddrHostRecord and TypeHostRecord inherit it\n  instead of each carrying their own copy.\n- Plumb happy-eyeballs v0.11.0's stale/allow_stale API through the FFI\n  glue and the C++ driver. Output::SendDnsQuery carries allow_stale;\n  when the state machine revalidates a stale answer (allow_stale=false)\n  the driver adds RESOLVE_BYPASS_CACHE to force a fresh lookup. The stale\n  entry is left in place so concurrent consumers can keep using it while\n  the revalidation is in flight.\n- happy_eyeballs_process_dns_response_{a,aaaa,https} carry the stale flag\n  into Input::DnsResult, so both address and HTTPS/SVCB answers report\n  fromStaleCache and are revalidated when served stale.\n\nThe DNSRecord and IPCTypeRecord IPC structs carry the flag too, sampled\nwhen the lookup completes: the receiving side holds no expiration times of\nits own, so it cannot recompute grace status, and ttl plus lastUpdate is\nexactly the reasoning rejected above.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317012\n", "files": ["netwerk/dns/DNSByTypeRecord.h", "netwerk/dns/DNSRequestChild.cpp", "netwerk/dns/DNSRequestParent.cpp", "netwerk/dns/PDNSRequestParams.ipdlh", "netwerk/dns/nsDNSService2.cpp", "netwerk/dns/nsHostRecord.cpp", "netwerk/dns/nsHostRecord.h", "netwerk/dns/nsIDNSByTypeRecord.idl", "netwerk/dns/nsIDNSRecord.idl", "netwerk/protocol/http/ConnectionEstablisher.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/ConnectionEstablisher.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/HappyEyeballsConnectionAttempt.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/http/HappyEyeballsConnectionAttempt.h", "netwerk/protocol/http/happy_eyeballs_glue/src/lib.rs"], "git_node": "59fb478277e272821518d3250584a0a97f8d5b13", "git_parents": ["e89e5e69b9fbea67dff91b4a57dbafd4214f46ef"], "node": "8c40d01877d1c80e9384271050cddea5cfe9b7f1", "parents": ["e59249982dd28be0d560a6a1f7eecf3fa42cc042"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Max Inden \u003cmail@max-inden.de\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060788 - Surface stale and revalidation state in Happy Eyeballs profiler markers r=necko-reviewers,jesup\n\nThe Happy Eyeballs DNS profiler markers now record two facts introduced\nby Optimistic DNS: whether a query was a cache-bypassing revalidation of\na stale answer (allow_stale=false), and whether the answer it received\nwas served from a stale (past-TTL, grace-period) cache entry. This makes\nthe revalidation flow visible when profiling a connection.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317089\n", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/happy_eyeballs_glue/src/lib.rs", "netwerk/protocol/http/happy_eyeballs_glue/src/profiler.rs"], "git_node": "4c7abb49797f298dcfec56bbe7e6afd16da1ac5c", "git_parents": ["59fb478277e272821518d3250584a0a97f8d5b13"], "node": "920a2b7bbc6cca3ff02c2780955aae59a4aafce9", "parents": ["8c40d01877d1c80e9384271050cddea5cfe9b7f1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "munawiki \u003c73450925+munawiki@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2055309 - Restore WebVTT processing state when cue rendering throws. r=alwu\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315691\n", "files": ["dom/media/webvtt/test/mochitest/mochitest.toml", "dom/media/webvtt/test/mochitest/test_webvtt_process_cues_exception.html", "dom/media/webvtt/vtt.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "d25517baca1efb2f456989b1f181b3bc2c8667f7", "git_parents": ["4c7abb49797f298dcfec56bbe7e6afd16da1ac5c"], "node": "e9df57b5544124bebbfac39120b763d290d15640", "parents": ["920a2b7bbc6cca3ff02c2780955aae59a4aafce9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Maxx Crawford \u003cmcrawford@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061740 - Move widgets and the content feed into a full-width band below the Nova grid r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317605\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/Base.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Base/_Grid.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/CustomizeMenu/CustomizeMenu.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamAdmin/DiscoveryStreamAdmin.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase/DiscoveryStreamBase.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamBase/_DiscoveryStreamBase.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/CardGrid/_CardGrid.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/CardSections/_CardSections.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/Highlights/_Highlights.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/Navigation/_Navigation.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/DiscoveryStreamComponents/SectionFollowButton/SectionFollowButton.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Search/_Search.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/Widgets.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/WidgetsSidebar.jsx", "browser/extensions/newtab/content-src/components/Widgets/_Widgets.scss", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/jest/content-src/components/Base.test.jsx"], "git_node": "1dcf57b59e7ade14569d10a00b585991c0e493a9", "git_parents": ["d25517baca1efb2f456989b1f181b3bc2c8667f7"], "node": "4c07e5e7887a3974627a584dff15fc65e43a24e4", "parents": ["e9df57b5544124bebbfac39120b763d290d15640"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Serban Stanca \u003csstanca@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 1498271 - Don't wrap long lines in nsXHTMLContentSerializer if OutputDisallowLineBreaking is passed. r=edgar\" for causing mochitests-plain failures in test_copypaste.xhtml.\n\nThis reverts commit b945dad6f469d2aad29759a4291c46dfc51002f4.\n", "files": ["dom/serializers/nsXHTMLContentSerializer.cpp", "dom/serializers/tests/mochitest/copypaste.js", "dom/serializers/tests/mochitest/test_copypaste.html"], "git_node": "bfb362d9666d067b96b479fa3a717e8e720e7093", "git_parents": ["1dcf57b59e7ade14569d10a00b585991c0e493a9"], "node": "bde45b1dff2b3df9b3609f2b2fcabb3a07ebe098", "parents": ["4c07e5e7887a3974627a584dff15fc65e43a24e4"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Katherine Ye \u003ckye@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062219 - Store text overflow marker string in a RefPtr. r=dshin,layout-reviewers,emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317630\n", "files": ["layout/generic/TextOverflow.cpp"], "git_node": "53756688f4c03eebadc05bf3907ff3bb12747cd1", "git_parents": ["bfb362d9666d067b96b479fa3a717e8e720e7093"], "node": "1355b20fd8bef5facf0146e144bd27b95b88ee55", "parents": ["bde45b1dff2b3df9b3609f2b2fcabb3a07ebe098"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sylvestre Ledru \u003csylvestre@debian.org\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062227 - Remove static from mozilla::detail::ComputeGrowth to fix -Wunused-template with clang 23 r=sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317444\n", "files": ["mfbt/Vector.h"], "git_node": "ab8defc34da0934cdf9aaf19aecc16da4a4c2e56", "git_parents": ["53756688f4c03eebadc05bf3907ff3bb12747cd1"], "node": "39f000e410edaf94fa1450a32385f7c9fd24ab84", "parents": ["1355b20fd8bef5facf0146e144bd27b95b88ee55"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061299 - Crashtest. r=firefox-style-system-reviewers,dshin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317808\n", "files": ["testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/document-metadata/the-style-element/crashtests/style-with-title-mutations-while-parsing.xhtml"], "git_node": "7ff4539c35305359764a81f3b88be1d6ac3f8938", "git_parents": ["ab8defc34da0934cdf9aaf19aecc16da4a4c2e56"], "node": "e0f8f1ce232a995ebc36dc58cfa26328cf843fc5", "parents": ["39f000e410edaf94fa1450a32385f7c9fd24ab84"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060396 - Remove OSToolbarButtonPressed and related code. r=mac-reviewers,mstange\n\nI did the digging, and this seems to come from bug 363415, and then\nmorphed shape in multiple ways, but mostly through refactors like\nbug 743975.\n\nBut I don't think macOS titlebars have a \"toolbar\" button anymore. And\nI'm pretty sure even if we reached this code this wouldn't work as\nexpected, since nsIWebBrowserChrome::SetChromeFlags implementations\ndon't do much (clean up for that incoming).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316127\n", "files": ["widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm", "widget/nsIWidgetListener.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.h"], "git_node": "06e2e4f07d857835b3c0bb8df054af8311b929a6", "git_parents": ["7ff4539c35305359764a81f3b88be1d6ac3f8938"], "node": "d8d2efb042bd2c5449f724b04bfde301b3f2208f", "parents": ["e0f8f1ce232a995ebc36dc58cfa26328cf843fc5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alex Hochheiden \u003cahochheiden@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062118 - Batch paths passed to VCS commands so they fit a Windows command line r=ahal,firefox-build-system-reviewers,sergesanspaille\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317386\n", "files": ["python/mach/mach/test/python.toml", "python/mach/mach/test/test_batch_paths.py", "python/mach/mach/util.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/base.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/git.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/jj.py", "python/mozversioncontrol/mozversioncontrol/repo/mercurial.py"], "git_node": "3a8a1cc26afc21d463d6760af76ad3f98ec33c87", "git_parents": ["06e2e4f07d857835b3c0bb8df054af8311b929a6"], "node": "97bc64c5d7ac893fe172a677a6b4f985ba2a33be", "parents": ["d8d2efb042bd2c5449f724b04bfde301b3f2208f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060396 - Remove toggletoolbar attribute support. r=places-reviewers,mak\n\nI did more digging and this seems to be basically dead code. It seems\nolder versions of OSX had some sort of toolbar control button? But it's\ndocumented to have no effect at all nowadays:\n\nhttps://developer.apple.com/documentation/appkit/nswindow/showstoolbarbutton\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316133\n", "files": ["browser/components/places/content/places.xhtml", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.h", "widget/cocoa/nsCocoaWindow.mm", "widget/nsIWidget.h", "xpfe/appshell/AppWindow.cpp"], "git_node": "f9a9af7cd0d262ca6ffb4b110b0cd153c9b97a77", "git_parents": ["3a8a1cc26afc21d463d6760af76ad3f98ec33c87"], "node": "2eab102c0d6bd27ba00da80548f5e7ece006a85b", "parents": ["97bc64c5d7ac893fe172a677a6b4f985ba2a33be"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Irene Ni \u003cini@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060908 - Create initial JSON dump of Remote settings sections layouts for cold startup. r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317640\n", "files": ["services/settings/dumps/main/moz.build", "services/settings/dumps/main/newtab-section-layouts.json", "services/settings/dumps/main/newtab-sections-ordering.json"], "git_node": "de08c2ddb2ed978e0445b12ac241b1cb30ecd3df", "git_parents": ["f9a9af7cd0d262ca6ffb4b110b0cd153c9b97a77"], "node": "77cca24d6afafb16fc8fcc451772d7899db495cc", "parents": ["2eab102c0d6bd27ba00da80548f5e7ece006a85b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "scottdowne \u003csdowne@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062473 - Expand newtab's list of region and locales for content support r=ini\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317697\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/ActivityStream.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "58f7f739096247571c0f5a2588c69644f2a14008", "git_parents": ["de08c2ddb2ed978e0445b12ac241b1cb30ecd3df"], "node": "4d220e79160d4c5346c24dce78bfb2ac49459a83", "parents": ["77cca24d6afafb16fc8fcc451772d7899db495cc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Hirsch \u003cohai@6a68.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2028725 - Gracefully handle missing avatars r=mossop,janerik\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D291785\n", "files": ["browser/components/profiles/SelectableProfile.sys.mjs", "browser/components/profiles/metrics.yaml", "browser/components/profiles/tests/browser/browser_custom_avatar_test.js", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Events.yaml"], "git_node": "dcfdd3addd312208cc1b30300d5a3f9910e8fedb", "git_parents": ["58f7f739096247571c0f5a2588c69644f2a14008"], "node": "16d792abbab35e2f661774498c6906cd29d5c218", "parents": ["4d220e79160d4c5346c24dce78bfb2ac49459a83"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Nicolas Grunbaum \u003cngrunbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2042789 - move stats reports into WebrtcGlobalStatsHistory;r=bwc\n\nThere were several spots were we were making unintentional copies of the stats reports as they were added to the stats history.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316119\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/WebrtcGlobalInformation.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/WebrtcGlobalStatsHistory.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/WebrtcGlobalStatsHistory.h"], "git_node": "e3fdc132d7179dad6fdd59132e6f714eeece4d14", "git_parents": ["dcfdd3addd312208cc1b30300d5a3f9910e8fedb"], "node": "ee9c677934088dee92ee5d2338834aa05821530c", "parents": ["16d792abbab35e2f661774498c6906cd29d5c218"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061530: Replace MWasmLoadField::mightAlias. r=jseward\n\nThe whole way of checking if two different MaybeRefTypes might have\nvalues in common was a) overly focused on structs for some reason, and\nb) a buggy copy of RefType::castPossible. The logic is equivalent: do\ntwo types have any possible values in common? For casts this tells us if\nthe cast will always fail, and for GC object stores/loads it tells us if\ntwo operations are guaranteed to work on different values.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317715\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/bug2061530.js", "js/src/jit/MIR-wasm.cpp", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmTypeDef.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmValType.h"], "git_node": "feae414057520e0084687bb675e275a06832dd10", "git_parents": ["e3fdc132d7179dad6fdd59132e6f714eeece4d14"], "node": "677c83ceaf3d61e3df556943dc95b7740a193d18", "parents": ["ee9c677934088dee92ee5d2338834aa05821530c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061530: Also do struct alias analysis on OOL loads. r=jseward\n\nWhen looking at this with fresh eyes, I realized that it actually would\nrefuse to do this analysis for out-of-line struct fields, because it\nonly checked if the base had a ref type, and the data pointer never\nwill. But the data pointer has its own MIRType, and the load is always\nan MWasmLoadField, so we can just follow it back one more step to the\nbase struct.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317716\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/gc/bug2061530.js", "js/src/jit/MIR.cpp"], "git_node": "93b8e827120f7e1e569c39d2506b6177e22a6e4d", "git_parents": ["feae414057520e0084687bb675e275a06832dd10"], "node": "e58973555370d70007fb6809bfc54f7754e58c4e", "parents": ["677c83ceaf3d61e3df556943dc95b7740a193d18"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057012 - Fix broken code fence and improve documentation for OPEN_PREFERENCES_PAGE and OPEN_ABOUT_PAGE . r=omc-reviewers,sachung\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317562\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/index.md"], "git_node": "6ef10230966034694380761c2cdc2490d3f89fe5", "git_parents": ["93b8e827120f7e1e569c39d2506b6177e22a6e4d"], "node": "30991b4a8908d030a5a72b65e8d95c6e1c6b1f92", "parents": ["e58973555370d70007fb6809bfc54f7754e58c4e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Release Engineering Landoscript \u003crelease+landoscript@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug - Bumping Firefox l10n changesets r=release a=l10n-bump DONTBUILD CLOSED TREE\n\nach -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\naf -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nan -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nar -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nast -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\naz -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbe -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbg -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbn -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbo -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbqi -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbr -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbrx -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nbs -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nca -\u003e 6b1e09fba2de375d8f3132ee8f1fa1367e23035a\nca-va