Columns extension and its associated tests, which were left over from the previous tab grid implementation.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317826\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ext/Context.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ext/ContextKtTest.kt"], "git_node": "dac8f964959550b86753441dc4202c0550083d7c", "git_parents": ["36993ce83e4672ba7cf4199419fb18fb35353582"], "node": "9e061989129dfe863cd4c7ab84d91ad6697528de", "parents": ["c29997519ecbab77c055b3f7e81ee902db60a31a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062395 - r=keithamus\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317612\n", "files": ["dom/html/HTMLDialogElement.cpp"], "git_node": "e4f081f669d0857c3fb6cb02a1d6d35a88dbaeaa", "git_parents": ["dac8f964959550b86753441dc4202c0550083d7c"], "node": "378f0181c6d526f38030a42a6b483183d84071ea", "parents": ["9e061989129dfe863cd4c7ab84d91ad6697528de"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062400 - r=edgar,dom-core-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317658\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsFocusManager.cpp"], "git_node": "2b72978c26c40f8e66ea6574ea9148f2fe1c65e1", "git_parents": ["e4f081f669d0857c3fb6cb02a1d6d35a88dbaeaa"], "node": "40955ba120131072152be81bedf501e543e5d775", "parents": ["378f0181c6d526f38030a42a6b483183d84071ea"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062419 - Use strong pointers in more places in editor module. r=masayuki\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317657\n", "files": ["editor/libeditor/EditorBase.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditSubActionHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditor.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLEditorDeleteHandler.cpp", "editor/libeditor/HTMLTableEditor.cpp"], "git_node": "d3433e9ef340e41591f47b1d357149fe0ab2d072", "git_parents": ["2b72978c26c40f8e66ea6574ea9148f2fe1c65e1"], "node": "051b4164c81ec75f00ee2a3fc6769a4bcc9ac01e", "parents": ["40955ba120131072152be81bedf501e543e5d775"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062404 - r=emilio\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317660\n", "files": ["dom/ipc/BrowserChild.cpp", "dom/view-transitions/ViewTransition.cpp"], "git_node": "1422ee71ee2557efb979da352a10ac82b4f5936a", "git_parents": ["d3433e9ef340e41591f47b1d357149fe0ab2d072"], "node": "e24dcf43aad694c70212ff33b277c5d58e21d081", "parents": ["051b4164c81ec75f00ee2a3fc6769a4bcc9ac01e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Rebecca King \u003crking@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061873 - Update Mozilla VPN link and description when not active - r=fluent-reviewers,bolsson\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317866\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/appmenu-viewcache.inc.xhtml", "browser/base/content/browser-sync.js", "browser/base/content/test/sync/browser_sync.js", "browser/locales/en-US/browser/appmenu.ftl"], "git_node": "cca67e0dae21c168e747dbe06cf2902958735584", "git_parents": ["1422ee71ee2557efb979da352a10ac82b4f5936a"], "node": "2c4bf381be0727bb044ccebabcaa34a3914dccb5", "parents": ["e24dcf43aad694c70212ff33b277c5d58e21d081"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062469 - Make a separate protocol handler for web sockets. r=necko-reviewers,valentin\n\nA web socket channel currently also serves as the protocol handler.\nThis is bad because a protocol handler should be a singleton that is\naccessed via do_getService(). This patch adds a new WebSocketProtocolHandler\nclass as a protocol handler. The handler is used for wss or ws depending on\nthe bool that is passed in. The constructor always creates a new instance,\nso this should be accessed via do_getService(), not do_createInstance().\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317687\n", "files": ["dom/push/PushServiceWebSocket.sys.mjs", "dom/websocket/WebSocket.cpp", "netwerk/build/components.conf", "netwerk/build/nsNetModule.cpp", "netwerk/build/nsNetModule.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/BaseWebSocketChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/BaseWebSocketChannel.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannel.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannelChild.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketChannelParent.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketProtocolHandler.cpp", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/WebSocketProtocolHandler.h", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/moz.build", "netwerk/protocol/websocket/nsIWebSocketProtocolHandler.idl", "netwerk/test/fuzz/TestWebsocketFuzzing.cpp", "netwerk/test/httpserver/NodeServer.sys.mjs", "netwerk/test/unit/head_websocket.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_dns_proxy_bypass.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_happy_eyeballs_websocket_https_rr.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_trr_https_fallback.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_websocket_offline.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_websocket_protocol_handler.js", "netwerk/test/unit/test_websocket_with_h3_active.js", "netwerk/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "0e27dfcbeabe8ad2ebf3bc312a3c3fa4f281d2e7", "git_parents": ["cca67e0dae21c168e747dbe06cf2902958735584"], "node": "52a7abbd920fefeccdea33bc2d48d4d5365d8003", "parents": ["2c4bf381be0727bb044ccebabcaa34a3914dccb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Delia Pop \u003cdpop@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062943 - Migrate 3 SettingsSearchTest UI tests to the efficiency framework r=jajohnson\n\nConvert the three @SmokeTest cases from ui/SettingsSearchTest onto the ui/efficiency\nframework and annotate the legacy methods with @Converted:\n\n- verifySearchShortcutChangesAreReflectedInSearchSelectorMenuTest (TestRail 2203340)\n- verifyCustomSearchEngineCanBeAddedFromSearchEngineMenuTest (TestRail 2203309)\n- verifyShowSearchSuggestionsToggleTest (TestRail 233588)\n\nAdds the SettingsSearchManageShortcuts and SettingsSearchAddSearchEngine page objects\nand selectors, search-selector-menu and awesomebar-suggestion selectors, a\nSearchBarComponent -\u003e HomePage dismiss edge, and reachability cases for the new pages.\n\nverifyShowSearchSuggestionsToggleTest depends on live DuckDuckGo suggestions (no mock in\nthe efficiency BaseTest, as in the legacy test) so it carries the same network flakiness.\nReachability suite: 42 cases, 0 failed, 0 skipped.\n\nAll new UI tests successfully passed 50x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=78096  | Try ]]\nAll efficiency UI test successfully passed 1x on Firebase. [[ https://treeherder.mozilla.org/jobs?repo=try&landoInstance=lando-prod-2025&landoCommitID=78094 | Try ]]\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318102\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/SettingsSearchTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/devtools/NavigationReachabilityParameterizedTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/helpers/PageContext.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SearchBarComponent.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSearchAddSearchEnginePage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/pageObjects/SettingsSearchManageShortcutsPage.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SearchBarSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSearchAddSearchEngineSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSearchDefaultSearchEngineSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSearchManageShortcutsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSearchSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/selectors/SettingsSelectors.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/ui/efficiency/tests/SettingsSearchTest.kt"], "git_node": "3d62831035f7cac62b0e53d62c8446a26feed5ec", "git_parents": ["0e27dfcbeabe8ad2ebf3bc312a3c3fa4f281d2e7"], "node": "8462b3a16b94ff5723a88d74eb1dc14a79ea9334", "parents": ["52a7abbd920fefeccdea33bc2d48d4d5365d8003"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emma Zuehlcke \u003cemz@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059768 - Add tests for BounceTrackingProtection under per-site container association. r=baku,timhuang\n\nBug 2052136 retargets a top level navigation to a site bound to a container into\na new tab in that container. This splits one extended navigation across two\ntabs, and so across two BounceTrackingStates and two per-container stores: the\nrecord stays with the tab the load started in and is filed under that tab's\nOriginAttributes, while the load commits in another container.\n\nThe container is also re-decided on each redirect and sticks once it changes, so\na chain redirecting through a bound site carries every later hop into that\ncontainer. A tracker bound to nothing can collect state there, in a container\nBTP never classifies it against, and a purge leaves that state behind.\n\nThe fix, which turns the todo() expectations into real assertions, is\ntracked in Bug 2058145.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315686\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser.toml", "toolkit/components/antitracking/bouncetrackingprotection/test/browser/browser_bouncetracking_siteContainer.js"], "git_node": "665ee94a7372a366d92af831774fd28f2374a36a", "git_parents": ["3d62831035f7cac62b0e53d62c8446a26feed5ec"], "node": "ed1e8d795aa6c88240a8f1c0684116ec72d7f054", "parents": ["8462b3a16b94ff5723a88d74eb1dc14a79ea9334"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@eqrion.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2013619 - Add test. r=yury\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D284741\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/bug2013619.js"], "git_node": "0413e191789ee37598b1c16e20aed5a29cede11a", "git_parents": ["665ee94a7372a366d92af831774fd28f2374a36a"], "node": "f7ab55af7719ad7d3510fdd5a0937bd72c88727d", "parents": ["ed1e8d795aa6c88240a8f1c0684116ec72d7f054"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062313, part 1 - Clean up function properties in timermanager. r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317563\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/timermanager/UpdateTimerManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/timermanager/tests/unit/consumerNotifications.js"], "git_node": "d39e0be5fbd1f5b19d7bab7e154eec54a43d4488", "git_parents": ["0413e191789ee37598b1c16e20aed5a29cede11a"], "node": "e045156458488cfbfe727a888b36c9f40b3669b0", "parents": ["f7ab55af7719ad7d3510fdd5a0937bd72c88727d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Andrew McCreight \u003ccontinuation@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062313, part 2 - Add validation and a direct call in UpdateTimerManager. r=Gijs\n\nAn indirect call like this makes it hard to understand what is going on,\nand perhaps provides a window for an attacker to do something weird. Also\nwhile we're here, do some basic checking for the component ID, both as\na slight hardening measure and to give better error feedback.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317564\n", "files": ["toolkit/components/timermanager/UpdateTimerManager.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/timermanager/nsIUpdateTimerManager.idl"], "git_node": "2a8f8c3f5a8ebae3886cdbb96527b83598708fb1", "git_parents": ["d39e0be5fbd1f5b19d7bab7e154eec54a43d4488"], "node": "94fe6e1872555b58ef1192821352c0cdd4002da7", "parents": ["e045156458488cfbfe727a888b36c9f40b3669b0"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062448 - Give BrowserTestUtils.waitForMutationCondition a default timeout and message. r=firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,Gijs\n\nwaitForMutationCondition only settles when its condition passes, so a condition\nthat never becomes true hangs the test until the harness kills it, with nothing\nin the log naming the wait. Tests have been reaching for waitForCondition\ninstead, or hand-rolling bounded wrappers of their own.\n\nThis gives it the failure behavior waitForCondition already has: a timeout, a\nmessage naming the wait, and rejection if the test finishes while the wait is\nstill pending. The timeout defaults to 10s, well under the 45s browser-chrome\ntask timeout. Infinity opts out of it; 0 doesn't, so a miscomputed timeout fails\nfast rather than hanging. Callers that pass no message get one built from the\ncall site and the source of checkFn.\n\nThe 10s default comes out of try runs at 60s, 30s, 20s and 10s across opt,\ndebug, asan and tsan, which turned up a single wait that legitimately needs\nlonger; it's opted out later in this stack.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317817\n", "files": ["testing/mochitest/BrowserTestUtils/BrowserTestUtils.sys.mjs", "testing/mochitest/tests/browser/browser_BrowserTestUtils.js"], "git_node": "ebc0dd2d1e2d5af1a59bba0f8212c65f83ed8791", "git_parents": ["2a8f8c3f5a8ebae3886cdbb96527b83598708fb1"], "node": "34bbca735319c39ae07012b089f73e90a5de6db3", "parents": ["94fe6e1872555b58ef1192821352c0cdd4002da7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062448 - Let the sidebar tools resize wait run as long as it needs. r=sfoster\n\nresetToolsHeight waits for the tools to stop overflowing after resizeTools has\nshrunk them, and resizeTools walks the splitter down a frame at a time. Under\ntsan that walk runs past a minute, so the bound waitForMutationCondition now\napplies by default cut the wait short where it used to just take a while.\n\nA longer bound is no help: measured against tsan the wait wants more than 60s and\nthe harness gives up on the test at 120s, so anything that fits between the two is\na guess that turns into an intermittent. Opt this wait out and let the harness be\nthe thing that gives up. The eight callers all go through this helper, so this is\nthe only place that needs it.\n\nThe underlying slowness is worth its own look - a resize this expensive to drive\nis a lot of test runtime for what it checks - but that is a bigger change than\nunblocking the default.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317819\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_tools_overflow.js"], "git_node": "ec7814618b53cba7a6ca9b0717d70b59b687f817", "git_parents": ["ebc0dd2d1e2d5af1a59bba0f8212c65f83ed8791"], "node": "cd6bea08a94840527b7297b8e3d876443754508c", "parents": ["34bbca735319c39ae07012b089f73e90a5de6db3"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062448 - Watch for the tab strip leaving moving-tab mode instead of polling for it. r=nsharpley,tabbrowser-reviewers\n\nThe stale drag tests polled for the movingtab attribute because\nwaitForMutationCondition had no way to fail. It does now, so observe the\nattribute the check reads: the wait ends on the mutation that clears it, and a\nrecovery that never happens fails with the message naming what was expected\nrather than after fifty quiet retries.\n\nThe three waits collapse into one helper alongside assertNotMovingTab. The\nreduced-motion wait stays a waitForCondition - gReduceMotion is a script global\nwith no mutation behind it.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317853\n", "files": ["browser/components/tabbrowser/test/browser/dragdrop/browser_stale_drag_session.js"], "git_node": "139ef68b2c4db3f84a6acfe2ea650df522629acb", "git_parents": ["ec7814618b53cba7a6ca9b0717d70b59b687f817"], "node": "fd12604f193a2900f41f02e4069b4fba8dc3feb5", "parents": ["cd6bea08a94840527b7297b8e3d876443754508c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@eqrion.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1883944 - wasm: Add test. r=yury\n\nDepends on D204280\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D204419\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/exnref/bug1883944.js"], "git_node": "6aa3853678861e9e0db7851b765a4000057b9911", "git_parents": ["139ef68b2c4db3f84a6acfe2ea650df522629acb"], "node": "d6e0ebb84606c9d0cca2c8298e637e59d2ef3913", "parents": ["fd12604f193a2900f41f02e4069b4fba8dc3feb5"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@eqrion.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1928645 - wasm: Add test. r=jseward\n\nDepends on D228245\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D228246\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/regress/bug1928645.js"], "git_node": "2e344d817fc85785b78d565a710a100ab74f316f", "git_parents": ["6aa3853678861e9e0db7851b765a4000057b9911"], "node": "6b6097f6ee0fbe8408ed59e1c6b873ec638cdf27", "parents": ["d6e0ebb84606c9d0cca2c8298e637e59d2ef3913"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ryan Hunt \u003crhunt@eqrion.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1957086 - Add test. r=yury\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D243531\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/regress/bug1957086.js"], "git_node": "d9e63b902fdd42e981cb34cfc77836b4623554f8", "git_parents": ["2e344d817fc85785b78d565a710a100ab74f316f"], "node": "da3fcd1bd96b07589800315df6ba27bdccafd75b", "parents": ["6b6097f6ee0fbe8408ed59e1c6b873ec638cdf27"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045043 - Part 62 - Fixup final classes using _FINAL cycle collecting isupports macro in dom/media r=smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318058\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCIceCandidate.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCIceCandidatePair.h", "dom/media/webspeech/synth/speechd/SpeechDispatcherService.cpp"], "git_node": "0b8e483660a67e4cf6bef9ee8f8358b9c014435b", "git_parents": ["d9e63b902fdd42e981cb34cfc77836b4623554f8"], "node": "9cfebc038fe4496d0f936cf470179f422678bc31", "parents": ["da3fcd1bd96b07589800315df6ba27bdccafd75b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045043 - Part 63 - Fixup final classes using _FINAL cycle collecting isupports macro in dom/webscheduling r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318059\n", "files": ["dom/base/TextInputProcessor.h"], "git_node": "ba151850104aa46cce7315b3f9c48e8c1d25b9d3", "git_parents": ["0b8e483660a67e4cf6bef9ee8f8358b9c014435b"], "node": "03bb40aaea57157b2f1f49fffa495f18dd6f866f", "parents": ["9cfebc038fe4496d0f936cf470179f422678bc31"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045043 - Part 64 - Fixup final classes using _FINAL cycle collecting isupports macro in dom/webscheduling r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318060\n", "files": ["dom/webscheduling/WebTaskScheduler.h"], "git_node": "a3f4b154889adb849cf6a3b53bc66625dd4745ca", "git_parents": ["ba151850104aa46cce7315b3f9c48e8c1d25b9d3"], "node": "6fbb82ab854cd3b8af6ac0c9bdb002c232e6731e", "parents": ["03bb40aaea57157b2f1f49fffa495f18dd6f866f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2045043 - Part 65 - Fixup final classes using _FINAL cycle collecting isupports macro in dom/webtransport r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318061\n", "files": ["dom/webtransport/api/WebTransportSendGroup.h"], "git_node": "0d00f7fa7f1938fcf488cc25b1a12724c4cb7be0", "git_parents": ["a3f4b154889adb849cf6a3b53bc66625dd4745ca"], "node": "5cc65c2599dd9787f822e9b7ebda10ea4e56a8ec", "parents": ["6fbb82ab854cd3b8af6ac0c9bdb002c232e6731e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Sudiaman \u003cjsudiaman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2057872 - Skip browser_BrowserWindowTracker_minimize.js on Linux 22.04 when running Wayland. r=Gijs\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317813\n", "files": ["browser/modules/test/browser/browser.toml"], "git_node": "d9293313aaa8bab8789d277e29b6ebec329d4cb3", "git_parents": ["0d00f7fa7f1938fcf488cc25b1a12724c4cb7be0"], "node": "541b110fe509a97d4258e118a6f2a17496731da1", "parents": ["5cc65c2599dd9787f822e9b7ebda10ea4e56a8ec"], "tags": []}, {"author": "serge-sans-paille \u003csguelton@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062577 - Properly list hunspell in our license file r=sylvestre\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317807\n", "files": ["toolkit/content/license.html"], "git_node": "c555fd074b6f91b3264ec6d4b022aa1bda3d5149", "git_parents": ["d9293313aaa8bab8789d277e29b6ebec329d4cb3"], "node": "b5b03e3618aa8162ea33579e951d73c8b39022cf", "parents": ["541b110fe509a97d4258e118a6f2a17496731da1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Kalen Lu \u003ckalenblu@icloud.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2059339 - Add scrollbar gutter to autocomplete dropdown panel. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,sfoster,dimi\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317136\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/autocomplete.css"], "git_node": "0a85514135aad94a06e8d04351e395d4e30bab05", "git_parents": ["c555fd074b6f91b3264ec6d4b022aa1bda3d5149"], "node": "1054226da7b80fe52d2a9937a5367c6d701d1336", "parents": ["b5b03e3618aa8162ea33579e951d73c8b39022cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056635: Allow ascribing (sub resource) to resources. r=rhunt\n\nThe component model allows you to ascribe the (sub resource) bound to an\nexported resource type, in case a component wants to pretend that two\nresource type exports are actually different types. This is unlikely to\nbe exercised in practice but is the only (?) case right now where we\nreject a valid component (outside of our current scope requirements).\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313255\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/components/exports.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/components/resources.js", "js/src/wasm/WasmComponent.cpp", "js/src/wasm/WasmComponent.h", "js/src/wasm/WasmValidate.cpp"], "git_node": "9e524bd4150c30ead649c6e4ce5dc55a9fc85efd", "git_parents": ["0a85514135aad94a06e8d04351e395d4e30bab05"], "node": "c2d272161d05ac7613007b26c2e53415bcea1691", "parents": ["1054226da7b80fe52d2a9937a5367c6d701d1336"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053447 - Part 1: Create a LaunchOnLogin interface for macOS. r=hsohaney\n\nImplement a macOS interface for adding Login Items (aka LaunchOnLogin) and make a wrapper for LaunchOnLogin that calls the correct OS version.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313482\n", "files": ["browser/components/shell/nsIMacShellService.idl", "browser/components/shell/nsMacShellService.mm", "toolkit/modules/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/LaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/MacOSLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/UnsupportedLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/moz.build", "toolkit/modules/moz.build", "tools/@types/generated/lib.gecko.darwin.d.ts"], "git_node": "6d18ba53d5f9b3c19d4d2aa6156fccb39e0199a5", "git_parents": ["9e524bd4150c30ead649c6e4ce5dc55a9fc85efd"], "node": "544a69b3be17d097d7a409071ce701a739dfb7f2", "parents": ["c2d272161d05ac7613007b26c2e53415bcea1691"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053447: Part 2 - Port the existing LaunchOnLogin code.r=hsohaney\n\nPort the WindowsDefaultLaunchOnLogin to use the new generic LaunchOnLogin interface\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313483\n", "files": ["browser/app/profile/firefox.js", "browser/components/BrowserComponents.manifest", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/DefaultLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/moz.build", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/tests/test_DefaultLaunchOnLogin.js", "browser/components/defaultlaunchonlogin/tests/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/DefaultWindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/moz.build", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/tests/test_DefaultWindowsLaunchOnLogin.js", "browser/components/defaultwindowslaunchonlogin/tests/xpcshell.toml", "browser/components/moz.build"], "git_node": "8df867ed8f7b35901811417f5dafd4821470d4eb", "git_parents": ["6d18ba53d5f9b3c19d4d2aa6156fccb39e0199a5"], "node": "1464cca7523a401d7cefb6d3d31923be6506dcad", "parents": ["544a69b3be17d097d7a409071ce701a739dfb7f2"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053447: Part 3 - Update Launch on Login pref to use new API.r=tgiles\n\nUse the new LaunchOnLogin API to determine if LoL is supported and call the correct OS implementation\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313484\n", "files": ["browser/components/preferences/main.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_windows_launch_on_login.js", "browser/components/preferences/tests/browser_windows_launch_on_login_msix.js"], "git_node": "913a5d3241f676e77b2a549c20dad5307790c193", "git_parents": ["8df867ed8f7b35901811417f5dafd4821470d4eb"], "node": "b1cd88bc52ab8436ba6245325f67a4a2b5f96e10", "parents": ["1464cca7523a401d7cefb6d3d31923be6506dcad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053447: Part 4 - Update rest of LaunchOnLogin code to use new API.r=omc-reviewers,firefox-desktop-core-reviewers ,aminomancer\n\nPort ASRouter and telemetry code to new LaunchOnLogin API\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313485\n", "files": ["browser/base/content/test/performance/browser_startup.js", "browser/components/StartupTelemetry.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouterTargeting.sys.mjs", "browser/components/shell/StartupOSIntegration.sys.mjs", "browser/components/tests/unit/test_startupTelemetry_launchOnLoginState.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/schemas/SpecialMessageActionSchemas/test/browser/browser_sma_launch_on_login.js"], "git_node": "0b434d30a1b242d1ad8920247967bc0ef3c89fb1", "git_parents": ["913a5d3241f676e77b2a549c20dad5307790c193"], "node": "1ef229f106094efc1111207b611aab9a87a4c97d", "parents": ["b1cd88bc52ab8436ba6245325f67a4a2b5f96e10"], "tags": []}, {"author": "iain holmes \u003ciholmes@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2053447: Part 5 - Update for enterprise policies.r=mkaply\n\nUpdate to support the DisableLaunchOnLogin enterprise policy\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316049\n", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.sys.mjs", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_disable_launch_on_login.js", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/LaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/UnsupportedLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs", "toolkit/modules/launchonlogin/WindowsLaunchOnLogin.sys.mjs"], "git_node": "b261b48eda5c11bb45c4fbdd32f20a20d5613496", "git_parents": ["0b434d30a1b242d1ad8920247967bc0ef3c89fb1"], "node": "468c79acc5d271fd20c5ad5149941cea95ee8c7c", "parents": ["1ef229f106094efc1111207b611aab9a87a4c97d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Byron Campen \u003cdocfaraday@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1858557: Prevent GC of RTCDataChannel until its PeerConnection is GC-able. r=jib\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313888\n", "files": ["dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/PeerConnectionImpl.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannel.cpp", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannel.h", "dom/media/webrtc/jsapi/RTCDataChannelDeclarations.h", "testing/web-platform/meta/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-GC.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/webrtc/RTCDataChannel-GC.html"], "git_node": "4c74a6aed3707a4613e6a999521e8ade1591819b", "git_parents": ["b261b48eda5c11bb45c4fbdd32f20a20d5613496"], "node": "d792a61d72555a5118dda79b428ba6fae3f24fc1", "parents": ["468c79acc5d271fd20c5ad5149941cea95ee8c7c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Aaron Train \u003caaron.train@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062368 - Add new interaction factory CI task (tae-arm-interaction) r=ajoltan\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318126\n", "files": ["mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-tae-interaction-tests.yml", "mobile/android/test_infra/flank-configs/fenix/arm-tae-tests.yml", "taskcluster/kinds/ui-test-apk/kind.yml"], "git_node": "a6a5285434d4f4d6b35dd14449e90c9a46a3f973", "git_parents": ["4c74a6aed3707a4613e6a999521e8ade1591819b"], "node": "94e9c7769d69c3f7da9dd9180780f6e7bc8da825", "parents": ["d792a61d72555a5118dda79b428ba6fae3f24fc1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062743 - Let a scroll container say how far one line scrolls it. r=layout-reviewers,firefox-style-system-reviewers,emilio\n\nA line comes out of the scroll container's font metrics. That is the wrong unit\nfor a list of uniformly sized items, where a wheel notch moves a fraction of an\nitem and stops mid-item. The vertical tab strip is the case in point\n(bug 2062682).\n\n-moz-line-scroll-amount is chrome-only, not animatable, and takes one length\nthat applies to both axes, so a consumer varies it per orientation rather than\nsetting two values on one element. auto keeps the font-derived amount, and\nmousewheel.min_line_scroll_amount still floors the result.\n\nGetLineScrollAmount() is the single source for both scrolling paths --\nEventStateManager::GetScrollAmount() on the main thread, ScrollMetadata via\nnsLayoutUtils::ComputeScrollMetadata() for APZ -- so this needs no APZ or IPC\nchange, and arrow keys and scrollbar arrow buttons follow the wheel along with\nDOM_DELTA_LINE. APZ picks the value up on paint, so a change that triggered no\npaint would leave it on the old amount until the next one.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318048\n", "files": ["devtools/server/actors/animation-type-longhand.js", "dom/base/use_counter_metrics.yaml", "layout/generic/ScrollContainerFrame.cpp", "layout/style/GenerateCSSProperties.py", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.cpp", "layout/style/nsStyleStruct.h", "layout/style/test/test_non_content_accessible_properties.html", "servo/components/style/properties/longhands.toml", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/meta/css/css-overflow/moz-line-scroll-amount.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/mozilla/tests/css/css-overflow/moz-line-scroll-amount.html"], "git_node": "479acac11e9f8a688f61000a9a55cbcec6415b74", "git_parents": ["a6a5285434d4f4d6b35dd14449e90c9a46a3f973"], "node": "99b48e220ba8e341d3f971a3d518fd9e21255545", "parents": ["94e9c7769d69c3f7da9dd9180780f6e7bc8da825"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Keith Cirkel \u003ckeithamus@users.noreply.github.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062282 - Close unrelated auto popovers when dialog inside hint opens r=dom-core-reviewers,smaug\n\nThis updates these algorithms to match the spec changes proposed in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/12764\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317541\n", "files": ["dom/base/Document.cpp", "dom/events/EventStateManager.cpp", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/popovers/popover-hint-dialog-dismisses-unrelated-auto.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/meta/html/semantics/popovers/popover-top-layer-nesting-hints.html.ini", "testing/web-platform/tests/html/semantics/popovers/popover-top-layer-nesting-hints.html"], "git_node": "9943a4850587124c6e8aaf03d8323be9892320dd", "git_parents": ["479acac11e9f8a688f61000a9a55cbcec6415b74"], "node": "c117f10a967f499060a0042436c115c3ae9dee9e", "parents": ["99b48e220ba8e341d3f971a3d518fd9e21255545"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061352 - Handle eSetSelection for EditContext. r=masayuki\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317152\n", "files": ["dom/base/nsDOMWindowUtils.cpp", "dom/events/ContentEventHandler.cpp", "dom/html/EditContext.cpp", "dom/html/EditContext.h", "dom/interfaces/base/nsIDOMWindowUtils.idl", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/mochitest.toml", "editor/libeditor/tests/edit-context/test_editcontext_set_selection.html"], "git_node": "2be91e0f50a8c13c4d7c9f0c7226213fc81c1ad2", "git_parents": ["9943a4850587124c6e8aaf03d8323be9892320dd"], "node": "8ec3378d4f333b24839c402d2de67bb3f68ccf0a", "parents": ["c117f10a967f499060a0042436c115c3ae9dee9e"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Leo Tenenbaum \u003cltenenbaum@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061801 - Part 2: Remove #ifdef MOZ_THUNDERBIRD guard for drag+drop principal. r=edgar\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318117\n", "files": ["widget/nsBaseDragService.cpp"], "git_node": "bcdbeb94680f2099f31ddbd7d7c5bdd77338cf48", "git_parents": ["2be91e0f50a8c13c4d7c9f0c7226213fc81c1ad2"], "node": "871390f0256c2b5686a8719a59a7bd3215b51912", "parents": ["8ec3378d4f333b24839c402d2de67bb3f68ccf0a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062988: Do not show the profile-missing dialogs in headless mode. r=gsvelto\n\nProfileMissingDialog() and ProfileEncryptionMismatchDialog() put up a modal alert. Nothing can dismiss a modal in headless mode, so a failure to select a profile turns into an indefinite hang in AppWindow::ShowModal() rather than an error exit. ProfileLockedDialog() already prints to stderr and returns in that case, so do the same in these two.\n\nThis does not change what makes profile selection fail, only how the failure is reported.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318131\n", "files": ["toolkit/xre/nsAppRunner.cpp"], "git_node": "6f83e9a015b801cee78794c71f5905e1b9438ec1", "git_parents": ["bcdbeb94680f2099f31ddbd7d7c5bdd77338cf48"], "node": "4eab4bfbfaf21fe3a41047b441f1f16de28f983d", "parents": ["871390f0256c2b5686a8719a59a7bd3215b51912"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Tom Schuster \u003ctschuster@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062533 - Remove telemetry probes for comparing images/audio/video loads against mixed content upgraded loads. r=freddyb,necko-reviewers,janerik,valentin\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317734\n", "files": ["dom/security/metrics.yaml", "netwerk/protocol/http/nsHttpChannel.cpp", "toolkit/components/telemetry/Histograms.json"], "git_node": "f4e11e7b3eed9df9bbfa38b13e19cb94243d22a1", "git_parents": ["6f83e9a015b801cee78794c71f5905e1b9438ec1"], "node": "fbdb3cb33d3b1173c503522b3916b7c939f3edb1", "parents": ["4eab4bfbfaf21fe3a41047b441f1f16de28f983d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ifeanyi Chima \u003cchimaifeanyi29@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047956 - Folder shortcuts should show a plain folder icon r=jsudiaman\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D311681\n", "files": ["browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-bookmark-list.css", "browser/components/sidebar/sidebar-bookmarks.mjs", "browser/components/sidebar/tests/browser/browser_bookmarks_sidebar.js"], "git_node": "e165441fa6e5513739bc62d4595ed585c5f0a2d5", "git_parents": ["f4e11e7b3eed9df9bbfa38b13e19cb94243d22a1"], "node": "ec7da48f2c28d59061e7dc7a983e83e1853adae7", "parents": ["fbdb3cb33d3b1173c503522b3916b7c939f3edb1"], "tags": []}, {"author": "D\u00e3o Gottwald \u003cdao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062366 - Cancel the query whose results the input discards. r=mbeier\n\nThe input discards the running query's results as it enters search mode from a\nkeyword heuristic result, since the query is about to be restarted in that mode.\nThat query's end still reached the listeners, and the view read it against state\nthe discarded results never filled: having seen none of them, it concluded the\nquery produced nothing, cleared the rows and, with search mode not in place yet,\nclosed -- cancelling the restart it was waiting for, and sending a zero-prefix\nexposure out on the way. Search mode is applied asynchronously, waiting on the\nengine store with the restart scheduled off that, so that window is real; over\nthe message path it is a round trip wide.\n\nThe discard now tells the listeners what holds for them either way: no further\nresults are coming. The view keeps the rows, drops its stale-row timer, and\nwaits for the restart to repopulate. The query's end is withheld the way a\nsuperseded query's is, since nobody is waiting for it either, which collapses\nthe separate id Bug 2062284 added back into one.\n\nWorth checking: the restart still cancels the query in the parent, so the\nlisteners can see that cancellation too.\n\nThe test drives the notifications directly rather than racing the transport, so\nit covers both paths.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317802\n", "files": ["browser/components/urlbar/content/SmartbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarChildController.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarInput.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/content/UrlbarShared.mjs", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser.toml", "browser/components/urlbar/tests/browser/browser_discardedQueryNotifications.js"], "git_node": "95401d412231e882d22cf1f416e152322d1b96cd", "git_parents": ["e165441fa6e5513739bc62d4595ed585c5f0a2d5"], "node": "c1a97d340fec70338d78352fb3b678bb18e72378", "parents": ["ec7da48f2c28d59061e7dc7a983e83e1853adae7"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Meg Viar \u003clmegviar@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058841 - Add on-train block lists for allow lists extendable via remote settings r=aminomancer,omc-reviewers\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D315287\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/modules/ASRouter.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/unit/ASRouter.test.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/MessagingSystemAllowlists.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/MessagingSystemBlocklists.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/SpecialMessageActions.sys.mjs", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/test/unit/test_MessagingSystemAllowlists.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/test/unit/test_MessagingSystemBlocklists.js", "toolkit/components/messaging-system/lib/test/unit/xpcshell.toml"], "git_node": "012a96bf0eab2a7e125f8cadf7fb188e64ad95d9", "git_parents": ["95401d412231e882d22cf1f416e152322d1b96cd"], "node": "623d6bf024e81d0be247e409e37156c05c1f51b9", "parents": ["c1a97d340fec70338d78352fb3b678bb18e72378"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Stephen A Pohl \u003cspohl@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1737953: Fill notched screens in native fullscreen by opting out of display safe area compatibility mode on macOS. r=mac-reviewers,bradwerth\n\nOn built-in displays with a camera housing (the \"notch\"), Firefox was running in the display safe area compatibility mode because it never set NSPrefersDisplaySafeAreaCompatibilityMode to NO. In native fullscreen that gave the content a frame that did not match the usable region, which showed up as letterboxing, most visibly for aspect-ratio-preserving fullscreen video, which ended up with borders on all sides.\n\nSetting NSPrefersDisplaySafeAreaCompatibilityMode to NO opts out of that mode so the content fills the full area below the notch. The menu bar strip at the very top stays drawn black by the system while the menu bar is hidden, which matches other native-fullscreen apps such as Safari; macOS does not let a standard-fullscreen app draw into that strip.\n\nOn displays without a notch this change is inert.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310868\n", "files": ["browser/app/macbuild/Contents/Info.plist.in"], "git_node": "9467ca68d97b8e29a21f2449c7d1cc3377baf3c9", "git_parents": ["012a96bf0eab2a7e125f8cadf7fb188e64ad95d9"], "node": "432eaa043d1f03eed5995cb536884908dac5cb9c", "parents": ["623d6bf024e81d0be247e409e37156c05c1f51b9"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2054657: Add Posix compliance check for special characters. r=dom-storage-reviewers,asuth\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D313256\n", "files": ["dom/filesystem/FileSystemSecurity.cpp"], "git_node": "470cb2351696c7ae5aa839c5500c932dcf76039e", "git_parents": ["9467ca68d97b8e29a21f2449c7d1cc3377baf3c9"], "node": "ee18190f85280dd78041206c4b24e9133e1782dd", "parents": ["432eaa043d1f03eed5995cb536884908dac5cb9c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Alexandru Marc \u003camarc@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2013619 - Add test. r=yury\" for causing sm bustages @ bug2013619.js\n\nThis reverts commit 0413e191789ee37598b1c16e20aed5a29cede11a.\n", "files": ["js/src/jit-test/tests/debug/bug2013619.js"], "git_node": "e05d76aea0fda32f9d19c8c1c13584707dcef9f7", "git_parents": ["470cb2351696c7ae5aa839c5500c932dcf76039e"], "node": "1b5b155b04205a74095b0942ed1cabb21fe46c2d", "parents": ["ee18190f85280dd78041206c4b24e9133e1782dd"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Emilio Cobos \u00c1lvarez \u003cemilio@crisal.io\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061822 - Remove counter-productive rule. r=desktop-theme-reviewers,tgiles\n\nMenulists have a reasonable min-height nowadays.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317150\n", "files": ["browser/themes/shared/preferences/preferences.css"], "git_node": "ff9f73a2e04f6f9383f2dc73e522c4d44a201089", "git_parents": ["e05d76aea0fda32f9d19c8c1c13584707dcef9f7"], "node": "356ab6d721f452784d8c1feafd073dae947eb27a", "parents": ["1b5b155b04205a74095b0942ed1cabb21fe46c2d"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jari Jalkanen \u003cjjalkanen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2058964 - Enqueue all origins for cache flush on fresh storage.sqlite. r=dom-storage-reviewers,hsingh\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316854\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp"], "git_node": "2625840af879eff0f1ab8b7905995fbef5248d85", "git_parents": ["ff9f73a2e04f6f9383f2dc73e522c4d44a201089"], "node": "bfe395755a93498df7c1388a4bb54799910a392c", "parents": ["356ab6d721f452784d8c1feafd073dae947eb27a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Ben Visness \u003cbvisness@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062344: Ship the Compact Import Section proposal. r=rhunt\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317930\n", "files": ["js/moz.configure", "js/src/jit-test/etc/wasm/generate-spectests/config.toml", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/binary.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/directiveless/features.js", "js/src/jit-test/tests/wasm/spec/compact-import-section/directives.txt", "modules/libpref/init/StaticPrefList.yaml"], "git_node": "641f57705c146b3527a1f954e257f7d0bc929cb2", "git_parents": ["2625840af879eff0f1ab8b7905995fbef5248d85"], "node": "7a300e8a703b136da9a72106fd5b1a1773a0d21b", "parents": ["bfe395755a93498df7c1388a4bb54799910a392c"], "tags": []}, {"author": "andyh \u003candhuang@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2056987 - Add optional dismiss_action for infobar. r=omc-reviewers,mimi\n\nAdd an optional dismiss_action to the infobar template that dispatches a SMA(via dispatchUserAction, with MULTI_ACTION support) when the user dismisses the infobar with the X button. It fires only on explicit dismiss, not on tab/window close.\n\nTesting:\n1. Open about:asrouter. Add a dismiss_action to an\n   infobar message's content, Show it,\n    click the X, and confirm the action fires\n   (e.g. OPEN_URL opens a tab).\n2. Re-show and click a button instead of the X:\n    confirm the action does NOT fire.\n3. Re-show as type \"tab\" and close the tab with\n    Ctrl+W or Cmd+W:\n    confirm the action does NOT fire.\n4. ./mach test .../browser_asrouter_infobar.js --headless\n   ./mach test .../browser_asrouter_universal_infobar.js --headless\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316934\n", "files": ["browser/components/asrouter/content-src/schemas/MessagingExperiment.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/content-src/templates/CFR/templates/InfoBar.schema.json", "browser/components/asrouter/modules/InfoBar.sys.mjs", "browser/components/asrouter/tests/browser/browser_asrouter_infobar.js"], "git_node": "3afbb2f45387a07b4cccf7e890683c33c5ac8b71", "git_parents": ["641f57705c146b3527a1f954e257f7d0bc929cb2"], "node": "6a3dd9664edd923c5d0fa30214d35bc1eaadce5f", "parents": ["7a300e8a703b136da9a72106fd5b1a1773a0d21b"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Hansheng Zhao \u003chzhao@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062806 - Back out changeset d5f7230f4124 (Bug 2057317) for crashing the ads-client context-id provider off-main-thread. r=mconley\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318001\n", "files": ["browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsClient.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/lib/AdsFeed.sys.mjs", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsClient.js", "browser/extensions/newtab/test/xpcshell/test_AdsFeed.js"], "git_node": "6d632db954de913942991f2cc6122f334e30c51e", "git_parents": ["3afbb2f45387a07b4cccf7e890683c33c5ac8b71"], "node": "5a641207abbcf476c4ac35a201812d92208e0bb6", "parents": ["6a3dd9664edd923c5d0fa30214d35bc1eaadce5f"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Niklas Baumgardner \u003cnbaumgardner@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062726 - Add explicit px to screenshots overlay style setter. r=sfoster\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317882\n", "files": ["browser/components/screenshots/ScreenshotsOverlayChild.sys.mjs", "browser/components/screenshots/tests/browser/browser_test_element_picker.js"], "git_node": "f2d32c3b7cb17b7e536dbc10fe27791f5912f523", "git_parents": ["6d632db954de913942991f2cc6122f334e30c51e"], "node": "770c1fad7382840080b1afadb206d2059365af52", "parents": ["5a641207abbcf476c4ac35a201812d92208e0bb6"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jared Hirsch \u003cohai@6a68.net\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2062683 - Add Wrexham to topsites r=thecount\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D317928\n", "files": ["browser/components/topsites/content/tippytop/favicons/wrexham.png", "browser/components/topsites/content/tippytop/images/wrexham@2x.png", "browser/components/topsites/content/tippytop/top_sites.json"], "git_node": "3b1576e9e967199f79380923f642a792684eacb0", "git_parents": ["f2d32c3b7cb17b7e536dbc10fe27791f5912f523"], "node": "2cf74a26ee5d62fe532a1f49bf88b76bc8f45afe", "parents": ["770c1fad7382840080b1afadb206d2059365af52"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Jonathan Kew \u003cjkew@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2060963 - Try to avoid recreating fontgroup in offscreen canvas worker if relevant attributes haven't changed. r=gfx-reviewers,lsalzman\n\nEventually we should use a (thread-safe version of) nsFontCache or similar, but as an interim\nmitigation, this addresses the case where a site simply repeats the same `ctx.font = ...` setting\nbefore every individual fillText or measureText call. We don't need to create a new fontGroup\nin that case, if the user font set hasn't changed.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318101\n", "files": ["dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.cpp", "dom/canvas/CanvasRenderingContext2D.h"], "git_node": "ffcea9b5575f7ad4fecd3f11c21f5e02194f1d94", "git_parents": ["3b1576e9e967199f79380923f642a792684eacb0"], "node": "bb7c3b76975330539573ebad5103c097e9362b9a", "parents": ["2cf74a26ee5d62fe532a1f49bf88b76bc8f45afe"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Gabriel Luong \u003cgabriel.luong@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2061753 - Always open a new tab when tapping on the Add button in the navigation bar r=android-reviewers,petru\n\n- The \"+\" button should always open a new tab in Homepage as New Tab.\n- This also applies for the the New Tab toolbar menu items.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D318014\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/store/HomeToolbarStoreBuilder.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddleware.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/home/toolbar/BrowserToolbarMiddlewareTest.kt"], "git_node": "23c8a34ea52d2bd33684bc23ca602507fd43cf98", "git_parents": ["ffcea9b5575f7ad4fecd3f11c21f5e02194f1d94"], "node": "8c66c43da155010fced2513a38884733a31be82a", "parents": ["bb7c3b76975330539573ebad5103c097e9362b9a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Julie De Lorenzo \u003cjdelorenzo@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2010687:  Add a fade to swipe to dismiss and update to Compose3 r=android-reviewers,007\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D316611\n", "files": ["mobile/android/fenix/app/src/androidTest/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/TabGridTabItemTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/compose/SwipeToDismissBox2.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabgroups/TabGroupCard.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/SharedTabItemUi.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/TabGridTabItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/TabListTabItem.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabpage/TabLayout.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/app/src/test/java/org/mozilla/fenix/tabstray/ui/tabitems/SharedTabItemUiTest.kt", "mobile/android/fenix/config/detekt-baseline.xml"], "git_node": "4346bfe9551e902908f3b9a6c2224f704fca40e0", "git_parents": ["23c8a34ea52d2bd33684bc23ca602507fd43cf98"], "node": "8287a4d71e170f1be694f05bfd464ee8d296a7ff", "parents": ["8c66c43da155010fced2513a38884733a31be82a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Joe Bowser \u003cjbowser@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 2047023 - Add mochitest-browser-chrome-ml-models for real-model ML tests r=ai-platform-reviewers,taskgraph-reviewers,thasan,ahal,gregtatum,nordzilla\n\nReal ML models can only run under `./mach perftest` today because the\nmozperftest MLServices layer is what allowlists RS + model-hub hosts via\nnetwork.socket.allowed_nonlocal_domains. That's the wrong tool for\ncorrectness regression tests.\n\nnsSocketTransport::ShouldBlockAddress() reads that pref at runtime per\nconnection, so a per-manifest `prefs = [...]` is enough to reach\nmodel-hub.mozilla.org from a plain mochitest \u2014 no hook, no env vars.\n\nAdds browser_models.toml carrying the RS + model-hub subset of\nMLServices.ALLOWED_HOSTS behind subsuite=ml-models, plus two tests: a\nsanity check (HEAD + Range GET GGUF magic) to keep the bypass covered,\nand a real SmolLM2 chat exercising native llama.cpp.\n\nThe corresponding taskcluster task runs Linux opt only, on\nmozilla-central plus try.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D310941\n", "files": ["python/mozbuild/mozbuild/schedules.py", "taskcluster/kinds/mochitest/kind.yml", "taskcluster/test_configs/test-sets.yml", "testing/mochitest/mach_test_package_commands.py", "testing/mozbase/moztest/moztest/resolve.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/linux_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/mac_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/configs/unittests/win_unittest.py", "testing/mozharness/mach_commands.py", "testing/mozharness/scripts/desktop_unittest.py", "toolkit/components/ml/moz.build", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser_models/browser_ml_smollm2_chat.js", "toolkit/components/ml/tests/browser_models/browser_models.toml"], "git_node": "82f8b264b4f80569796626fa811e96162fbd20c3", "git_parents": ["4346bfe9551e902908f3b9a6c2224f704fca40e0"], "node": "819658346905c0d349a31ae3bfbb1932c593940b", "parents": ["8287a4d71e170f1be694f05bfd464ee8d296a7ff"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Sandor Molnar \u003csmolnar@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Revert \"Bug 2058964 - Enqueue all origins for cache flush on fresh storage.sqlite. r=dom-storage-reviewers,hsingh\" for causing xpc failures @ test_temporary_storage.js\n\nThis reverts commit 2625840af879eff0f1ab8b7905995fbef5248d85.\n", "files": ["dom/quota/ActorsParent.cpp"], "git_node": "65d4295a4b